ch\n\nDrawer app:\nfirst tap → launch\n\nGesture detector non deve rubare i tap.\n\n==================================================\n14. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nCLOCK_TICK:\n\n- app tap accepted\n- Drawer open accepted\n- Drawer close accepted\n\nUna volta.\n\nNO haptic durante MOVE.\n\n==================================================\n15. CORE FILES\n==================================================\n\nRidurre il core a pochi owner chiari.\n\nTarget indicativo:\n\nMachinaCore.kt\nHomeScreen.kt\nAppDrawer.kt\nAppCatalog.kt\nLauncherPreferences.kt\nLauncherActions.kt\nAppVisuals.kt\nMachinaDesign.kt\n\nNon creare framework.\n\n==================================================\n16. CORE STATE OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nHomeSnapshot:\none owner\n\nLauncherSurface:\none owner\n\nCatalog:\none owner\n\nPersistence:\none owner\n\n==================================================\n17. REMOVE DEAD NAVIGATION CODE\n==================================================\n\nRimuovere:\n\nhorizontal navigation helpers\nold back swipe\nold predictive imitation\nold left/right state\nold route transitions\nunused Back handlers\n\n==================================================\n18. SYSTEM NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nSystem Home gesture:\nANDROID OWNED\n\nSystem Overview:\nANDROID OWNED\n\nMachina non li simula.\n\n==================================================\n19. SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nSettings:\nNOT IN CORE\n\nVerrà aggiunta dopo come feature separata.\n\n==================================================\n20. FIRST RUN\n==================================================\n\nFirst Run:\nNOT IN CORE\n\nVerrà aggiunta dopo come feature separata.\n\n==================================================\n21. REGRESSION\n==================================================\n\nP1:\n8 manual\n\nP2:\n8 manual\n\nDock:\n5\n\nHomeSnapshot:\nunchanged\n\nMaterial Stretch:\npreserved\n\nWallpaper/dim/border/shadow:\npreserved\n\n==================================================\n22. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA SIMPLE LAUNCHER CORE COMPLETE\n\nCore surfaces:\n<HOME/APP_DRAWER>\n\nHome root Back:\n<NO_OP/OTHER>\n\nDrawer Back:\n<HOME/OTHER>\n\nSwipe UP:\n<HOME_TO_DRAWER/FAILED>\n\nSwipe DOWN:\n<DRAWER_TO_HOME/FAILED>\n\nLeft navigation actions:\n<numero>\n\nRight navigation actions:\n<numero>\n\nHorizontal state writes:\n<numero>\n\nVertical gesture owners:\n<numero>\n\nHorizontal gesture owners:\n<numero>\n\nMaterial Stretch preserved:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1:\n<numero>\n\nP2:\n<numero>\n\nDock:\n<numero>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nFiles modified:\n<numero>\n\nFiles removed:\n<numero>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:237:{"session_id":"01a0116c-fa49-7f00-b48a-3282b9c83a05","ts":1787168592,"text":"CORE FIX — MACHINA HOME MUST NOT EXPOSE SYSTEM BACK EDGE\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nDEVICE EVIDENCE:\n\nOn HOME ROOT a LEFT edge gesture currently shows\nthe Android/SystemUI circular Back affordance.\n\nThis is WRONG for the desired launcher Home behavior.\n\nDO NOT modify visual design.\nDO NOT add animations.\nDO NOT modify Material Stretch.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL CORE NAVIGATION CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nHOME:\nUP -> APP_DRAWER\nDOWN -> NO_OP\nLEFT -> NO_OP\nRIGHT -> NO_OP\nBACK -> NO_OP\n\nAPP_DRAWER:\nDOWN -> HOME\nBACK -> HOME\n\nNo other core navigation.\n\n==================================================\n1. REMOVE HORIZONTAL MACHINA NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nSearch entire project for every horizontal gesture path.\n\nRemove any Machina:\n\nswipeLeft\nswipeRight\nhorizontal route\nhorizontal Home state\nhorizontal navigation\nback-by-horizontal-swipe\n\nExpected:\n0.\n\n==================================================\n2. HOME ROOT SYSTEM EDGE EXCLUSION\n==================================================\n\nWhile HOME root is visible:\n\nuse the supported Android\nsystemGestureExclusionRects mechanism\non the actual full-screen root View.\n\nPurpose:\n\nLEFT/RIGHT edge gestures must NOT enter\nthe system Back gesture recognizer over the Home surface.\n\nTherefore SystemUI must not show the circular Back arrow.\n\n==================================================\n3. ACTUAL ROOT VIEW\n==================================================\n\nApply exclusion to the actual View covering the display.\n\nDo NOT apply it only to:\n\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\ninner container\n\nThe screenshot proves that system Back is still winning\nat the display edge.\n\n==================================================\n4. FULL HEIGHT LATERAL EDGES\n==================================================\n\nHome exclusion must cover the usable LEFT/RIGHT edge\nvertically across the Home interaction surface.\n\nRespect Android limits and mandatory system gesture regions.\n\nDO NOT exclude the bottom mandatory Home/Overview gesture.\n\n==================================================\n5. BOTTOM GESTURES\n==================================================\n\nBottom system navigation remains Android-owned.\n\nDo NOT exclude:\n\nHOME gesture\nOverview\nQuick Switch\n\n==================================================\n6. APP DRAWER\n==================================================\n\nAPP_DRAWER remains part of launcher core.\n\nVertical navigation:\n\nHOME --UP--> DRAWER\nDRAWER --DOWN--> HOME\n\nBack while DRAWER:\nHOME\n\n==================================================\n7. BACKHANDLER\n==================================================\n\nKeep exactly:\n\nHOME BackHandler = NO_OP\n\nDRAWER BackHandler = HOME\n\nNo PredictiveBackHandler.\n\nNo custom Back animation.\n\n==================================================\n8. MATERIAL STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nKEEP existing approved Material Stretch implementation.\n\nDo not connect it to Android Back.\n\nDo not rewrite it.\n\n==================================================\n9. NO HORIZONTAL ANIMATION\n==================================================\n\nLEFT/RIGHT on HOME:\n\nno route\nno offset\nno alpha\nno scale\nno container shrink\nno state write\n\nIf Material Stretch naturally responds through the\napproved Home interaction layer, keep it.\n\nOtherwise NO visual reaction is preferable to a Back arrow.\n\n==================================================\n10. REMOVE CURRENT WRONG EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nThe screenshot shows the Home/container changing geometry\nwhile the System Back arrow appears.\n\nAudit this path.\n\nThere must NOT be two simultaneous owners:\n\nSystem Back\n+\nMachina horizontal motion\n\nTarget:\nboth horizontal motion/navigation owners = 0 on HOME.\n\n==================================================\n11. EXCLUSION LIFECYCLE\n==================================================\n\nHOME enters:\ninstall lateral exclusion.\n\nHOME leaves for DRAWER/feature:\nupdate/remove exclusion according to destination contract.\n\nActivity destroyed:\nclear ownership naturally.\n\nOne owner only.\n\nNo polling.\n\n==================================================\n12. SETTINGS/FUTURE FEATURE CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nFuture Settings/Changelog:\n\ndo NOT inherit Home lateral exclusion.\n\nThose screens need normal Android Back.\n\nHOME:\nlauncher exclusion ON\n\nFEATURE PAGE:\nlauncher exclusion OFF\n\n==================================================\n13. STATIC AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nReport:\n\nsystemGestureExclusionRects owners\nrect dimensions\nroot View dimensions\nmandatorySystemGestureInsets\n\nConfirm the exclusion is installed on the full-screen root,\nnot the inner Machina panel.\n\n==================================================\n14. DEVICE CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nHOME ROOT:\n\nLEFT edge:\nSystem Back arrow = MUST NOT APPEAR\n\nRIGHT edge:\nSystem Back arrow = MUST NOT APPEAR\n\nUP:\nAPP DRAWER\n\nDOWN from DRAWER:\nHOME\n\nBottom system gesture:\nunchanged\n\n==================================================\n15. DO NOT TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nPATCH001 Material Stretch\nPATCH003 Visual Tokens\nwallpaper\ndim\nborder\nshadow\nP1\nP2\nDock\ncatalog\npersistence\nR8\n\n==================================================\n16. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA TRUE LAUNCHER ROOT INPUT COMPLETE\n\nCore surfaces:\nHOME / APP_DRAWER\n\nHOME UP:\n<APP_DRAWER/FAILED>\n\nDRAWER DOWN:\n<HOME/FAILED>\n\nHOME LEFT navigation:\n<0/FAILED>\n\nHOME RIGHT navigation:\n<0/FAILED>\n\nHOME Back:\n<NO_OP/FAILED>\n\nDRAWER Back:\n<HOME/FAILED>\n\nSystem gesture exclusion owners:\n<numero>\n\nExclusion applied to full-screen root:\n<YES/NO>\n\nLeft edge excluded:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRight edge excluded:\n<YES/NO>\n\nBottom mandatory gesture excluded:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHorizontal Machina motion owners:\n<numero>\n\nPredictiveBackHandler:\n<numero>\n\nMaterial Stretch modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH003 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nDEVICE TEST REQUIRED:\nYES"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:238:{"session_id":"01a0116c-fa49-7f00-b48a-3282b9c83a05","ts":1787168921,"text":"FASE: MACHINA — RESTORE /opt OPERATIONAL WORKSPACE\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/Machina\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nTIMEZONE:\nEurope/Rome\n\nOBIETTIVO\n\nRicostruire una struttura operativa stabile in /opt.\n\nOgni build deve:\n\n1. usare /opt/Android/Machina/project come unica working copy\n2. generare timestamp Europe/Rome\n3. eseguire build\n4. creare output session\n5. copiare APK\n6. salvare build.log\n7. calcolare SHA-256\n8. creare snapshot ESATTO del source usato\n9. collegare logicamente snapshot e build con stesso ID\n10. non installare APK\n11. non usare adb\n\n==================================================\n1. DIRECTORIES\n==================================================\n\nGarantire:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n/opt/Android/Machina/outputs\n/opt/Android/Machina/snapshots\n/opt/Android/Machina/checkpoints\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs\n/opt/Android/Machina/logs\n/opt/Android/Machina/reports\n/opt/Android/Machina/tmp\n/opt/Android/Machina/private\n\nPermissions normali e coerenti con l'utente/build environment.\n\nNON creare nuovamente:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/builds\n\n==================================================\n2. SINGLE CONTROL SCRIPT\n==================================================\n\nUsare come unico controller:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl\n\nSupportare almeno:\n\nprojectctl build\nprojectctl status\nprojectctl snapshot\nprojectctl checkpoint\nprojectctl latest\n\nNon creare controller paralleli.\n\n==================================================\n3. EUROPE/ROME TIMESTAMP\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nNON dipendere dal timezone della shell.\n\nOgni session ID deve essere calcolato esplicitamente con:\n\nTZ=Europe/Rome\n\nFormato:\n\nYYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS\n\nEsempio:\n\n2026-08-19_21-35-42\n\nUsare lo STESSO BUILD_ID per output e snapshot.\n\n==================================================\n4. BUILD SESSION\n==================================================\n\nPer:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\ncreare:\n\nBUILD_ID=\"$(TZ=Europe/Rome date '+%Y-%m-%d_%H-%M-%S')\"\n\nOUTPUT_DIR=\n/opt/Android/Machina/outputs/$BUILD_ID\n\nSNAPSHOT_DIR=\n/opt/Android/Machina/snapshots/$BUILD_ID\n\nLOG=\n/opt/Android/Machina/logs/build-$BUILD_ID.log\n\n==================================================\n5. BUILD SOURCE\n==================================================\n\nBuild sempre da:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nMai build da snapshot/checkpoint.\n\nUsare la pipeline Gradle già valida del progetto.\n\nNON cambiare:\n\nGradle versions\nAGP\nR8\nruntime\nKotlin\n\nQuesta fase riguarda solo workspace/build orchestration.\n\n==================================================\n6. BUILD LOG\n==================================================\n\nCatturare stdout + stderr completi.\n\nIl comando deve continuare a essere visibile nel terminale\ne contemporaneamente scritto nel log.\n\nUsare comportamento equivalente a:\n\n... 2>&1 | tee \"$LOG\"\n\nPreservare correttamente exit status tramite pipefail.\n\n==================================================\n7. BUILD FAILURE\n==================================================\n\nSe Gradle/build FALLISCE:\n\ncreare comunque OUTPUT_DIR con:\n\nbuild.log\nBUILD_INFO.txt\n\nBUILD_INFO:\n\nStatus: FAILED\nBuild ID\nEurope/Rome timestamp\nproject path\nexit code\n\nNON creare un falso SUCCESS snapshot.\n\nNON copiare APK vecchi come se fossero nuovi.\n\nSTOP.\n\n==================================================\n8. APK DISCOVERY\n==================================================\n\nDopo SUCCESS:\n\nindividuare SOLO APK prodotti/aggiornati dalla build corrente.\n\nPreferire percorsi ufficiali:\n\nproject/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/\nproject/app/build/outputs/apk/release/\n\nNon pescare APK storici da outputs/.\n\n==================================================\n9. COPY APK\n==================================================\n\nCopiare nell'OUTPUT_DIR mantenendo nomi chiari:\n\napp-debug.apk\n\nse presente.\n\nRelease:\n\napp-release.apk\noppure\napp-release-unsigned.apk\n\nsecondo ciò che produce realmente la pipeline.\n\nNON rinominare unsigned come signed.\n\n==================================================\n10. BUILD INFO\n==================================================\n\nCreare:\n\n$OUTPUT_DIR/BUILD_INFO.txt\n\nContenuto:\n\nProject: Machina\nBuild ID: <id>\nTimezone: Europe/Rome\nLocal Timestamp: <ISO/local>\nProject Path: /opt/Android/Machina/project\nBuild Status: SUCCESS\nDebug APK: <YES/NO>\nRelease APK: <YES/NO>\nGit Commit: <hash oppure N/A>\nGit Dirty: <YES/NO oppure N/A>\nR8 Release: <ON/OFF/UNKNOWN>\n\nSnapshot:\n/opt/Android/Machina/snapshots/<BUILD_ID>\n\n==================================================\n11. SHA256 OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nCreare:\n\n$OUTPUT_DIR/SHA256SUMS.txt\n\nHash di:\n\nAPK\nbuild.log\nBUILD_INFO.txt\n\nUsare sha256sum.\n\n==================================================\n12. SNAPSHOT AFTER SUCCESS\n==================================================\n\nDopo build SUCCESS creare snapshot del SOURCE\nche ha prodotto la build.\n\nDestination:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/snapshots/$BUILD_ID\n\nSnapshot archive:\n\nproject.tar.gz\n\n==================================================\n13. SNAPSHOT CONTENT\n==================================================\n\nSnapshot deve includere il progetto sorgente ma NON\nspazzatura rigenerabile.\n\nIncludere:\n\napp/src\nGradle files\ngradle wrapper/config\nproguard/r8 rules\nmanifest\nresources\nscripts appartenenti al progetto\nFROZEN/contract docs presenti nel project\n\nEscludere:\n\n.gradle/\n**/build/\ntmp/\nlocal caches\n*.apk\n*.aab\nlarge generated reports se esterni al source\n\nNON includere:\n\nkeystore\n.jks\nprivate keys\npassword\ncredentials\nprivate/\n\n==================================================\n14. SNAPSHOT INFO\n==================================================\n\nCreare:\n\n$SNAPSHOT_DIR/SNAPSHOT_INFO.txt\n\nContenuto:\n\nProject: Machina\nSnapshot ID: <BUILD_ID>\nTimezone: Europe/Rome\nSource: /opt/Android/Machina/project\nAssociated Output:\n/opt/Android/Machina/outputs/<BUILD_ID>\nBuild Status: SUCCESS\nArchive: project.tar.gz\nGit Commit: <hash/N-A>\nGit Dirty: <YES/NO/N-A>\n\n==================================================\n15. SNAPSHOT HASH\n==================================================\n\nCreare:\n\n$SNAPSHOT_DIR/SHA256SUMS.txt\n\ncon hash di:\n\nproject.tar.gz\nSNAPSHOT_INFO.txt\n\n==================================================\n16. ATOMICITY\n==================================================\n\nNon lasciare sessioni apparentemente complete durante build.\n\nPreferire:\n\noutputs/.working-$BUILD_ID\nsnapshots/.working-$BUILD_ID\n\ne rinominare alle directory finali SOLO al completamento.\n\nOppure usare marker:\n\nBUILD_IN_PROGRESS\nBUILD_SUCCESS\n\nScelta semplice e robusta.\n\n==================================================\n17. LATEST POINTER\n==================================================\n\nMantenere symlink:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/outputs/latest\n→ ultimo build SUCCESS\n\ne:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/snapshots/latest\n→ snapshot associato\n\nAggiornare atomicamente.\n\nNON puntare latest a build fallita.\n\n==================================================\n18. PROJECTCTL LATEST\n==================================================\n\nprojectctl latest\n\ndeve mostrare:\n\nBuild ID\nTimestamp Europe/Rome\nAPK paths\nAPK sizes\nSHA-256\nSnapshot path\n\n==================================================\n19. PROJECTCTL STATUS\n==================================================\n\nprojectctl status\n\ndeve mostrare:\n\nProject exists\nGradle wrapper/status\nlatest successful build\nlatest snapshot\nlatest checkpoint\ndisk usage:\n\nproject\noutputs\nsnapshots\ncheckpoints\n\n==================================================\n20. MANUAL SNAPSHOT\n==================================================\n\nprojectctl snapshot\n\ncrea snapshot indipendente con timestamp Europe/Rome:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/snapshots/manual-<timestamp>/\n\nNON esegue build.\n\nSpecificare:\n\nBuild association: NONE\n\n==================================================\n21. CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nprojectctl checkpoint <name>\n\ncrea:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/checkpoints/\n<timestamp>-<sanitized-name>/\n\ne archive:\n\n<timestamp>-<sanitized-name>.tar.gz\n\nInclude:\n\nsource snapshot\ndocs correnti\nlatest BUILD_INFO\nlatest APK metadata\n\nNO private keys.\n\n==================================================\n22. CHECKPOINT SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nNON cancellare checkpoint automaticamente.\n\nNON fare retention automatica sui checkpoints.\n\nSono backup manuali importanti.\n\n==================================================\n23. OUTPUT RETENTION\n==================================================\n\nNON eliminare output automaticamente in questa fase.\n\nPrima voglio una struttura affidabile.\n\nCleanup/retention verrà deciso separatamente.\n\n==================================================\n24. TMP\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/tmp\n\npuò contenere soltanto temporanei.\n\nprojectctl può pulire file temporanei appartenenti\nalla sessione corrente dopo SUCCESS.\n\n==================================================\n25. PRIVATE\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/private\n\ndestinato a:\n\nR8 mapping\nprivate build metadata\nfuture signing material references\n\nNON copiare private/ dentro:\n\noutputs\nsnapshots\ncheckpoints\n\nsalvo mapping.txt se un checkpoint PRIVATE viene\nesplicitamente richiesto in futuro.\n\n==================================================\n26. BUILD NUMBER COLLISION\n==================================================\n\nSe due build partono nello stesso secondo:\n\nNON sovrascrivere.\n\nSe directory BUILD_ID esiste:\n\naggiungere:\n\n-01\n-02\n...\n\noppure micro/epoch suffix.\n\nMai rm -rf una sessione esistente.\n\n==================================================\n27. TIME VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nOgni build deve stampare:\n\nSystem timezone:\n<value>\n\nMachina build timezone:\nEurope/Rome\n\nMachina local timestamp:\n<value>\n\nVerificare con:\n\nTZ=Europe/Rome date\n\n==================================================\n28. PROJECTCTL HARDENING\n==================================================\n\nScript shell:\n\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\nquotare tutte le path.\n\nUsare trap per errori dove utile.\n\nNo eval.\n\nNo parsing fragile di ls.\n\nUsare find/stat/readlink.\n\n==================================================\n29. NO SOURCE MUTATION\n==================================================\n\nprojectctl build non deve:\n\ngit reset\ngit clean\nsed source\nmodify Gradle\nmodify manifest\nmodify Kotlin\n\nBuild controller è read-only sul source,\nsalvo normali output Gradle dentro build/.\n\n==================================================\n30. VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nEseguire una build reale tramite:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nPoi controllare:\n\noutputs/<ID> exists\nsnapshots/<ID> exists\n\nstesso ID.\n\nAPK exists.\n\nBUILD_INFO exists.\n\nproject.tar.gz exists.\n\nSHA256SUMS valid.\n\nlatest symlinks valid.\n\n==================================================\n31. TEST HASH\n==================================================\n\nEseguire:\n\nsha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt\n\nin:\n\noutput session\nsnapshot session\n\nPASS.\n\n==================================================\n32. TEST SNAPSHOT\n==================================================\n\nEseguire:\n\ntar -tzf project.tar.gz >/dev/null\n\nPASS.\n\n==================================================\n33. NO ADB\n==================================================\n\nADB:\nNO\n\nAPK installation:\nNO\n\n==================================================\nFINAL OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA /opt OPERATIONAL WORKSPACE READY\n\nRoot:\n/opt/Android/Machina\n\nProject:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nTimezone:\nEurope/Rome\n\nprojectctl:\n<path>\n\nLatest Build ID:\n<value>\n\nLatest Output:\n<path>\n\nLatest Debug APK:\n<path/N-A>\n\nLatest Release APK:\n<path/N-A>\n\nLatest Snapshot:\n<path>\n\nOutput SHA256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSnapshot SHA256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSnapshot archive validation:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nOutputs latest symlink:\n<path>\n\nSnapshots latest symlink:\n<path>\n\nBuild:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nADB used:\nNO\n\nAPK installed:\nNO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:239:{"session_id":"01a0116c-fa49-7f00-b48a-3282b9c83a05","ts":1787169850,"text":"FASE: MACHINA — FINAL IMMUTABLE /opt WORKSPACE\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/Machina\n\nTIMEZONE:\nEurope/Rome\n\nOBIETTIVO\n\nCreare una struttura operativa DEFINITIVA.\n\nDOPO QUESTA FASE:\nNON rinominare directory.\nNON spostare outputs.\nNON reintrodurre builds/.\nNON cambiare naming scheme.\nNON creare controller paralleli.\n\n==================================================\n1. FINAL DIRECTORY CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nUse exactly:\n\nproject/\noutputs/\nsnapshots/\ncheckpoints/\ncache/\nlogs/\ndocs/\nreports/\ntmp/\nprivate/\n\nNo other top-level operational directories unless explicitly approved.\n\n==================================================\n2. CACHE CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\ncache/gradle\ncache/android\ncache/kotlin\ncache/r8\ncache/projectctl\n\nCache is:\n\n- reusable\n- deletable\n- never authoritative\n- never included in snapshots\n- never included in checkpoints unless explicitly requested\n\n==================================================\n3. GRADLE CACHE\n==================================================\n\nprojectctl must export:\n\nGRADLE_USER_HOME=/opt/Android/Machina/cache/gradle\n\nbefore every Gradle invocation.\n\nDo not use random per-build Gradle homes.\n\n==================================================\n4. BUILD CACHE\n==================================================\n\nPreserve normal Gradle incremental/build cache behavior.\n\nDo NOT run:\n\ngradle clean\n\nfor every build.\n\nDefault:\n\nincremental build.\n\nAdd explicit command:\n\nprojectctl clean-build\n\nonly when a clean rebuild is intentionally required.\n\n==================================================\n5. PROJECT BUILD DIRECTORY\n==================================================\n\nKeep normal generated Gradle directories under:\n\nproject/.gradle/\nproject/app/build/\n\nThese are working build caches/artifacts only.\n\nThey are NOT final outputs.\n\nDo not archive them in snapshots.\n\n==================================================\n6. TIMESTAMP\n==================================================\n\nAll operational IDs use:\n\nTZ=Europe/Rome\n\nFormat:\n\nYYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS\n\nSame BUILD_ID for:\n\noutputs/<ID>\nsnapshots/<ID>\nlogs/build-<ID>.log\n\n==================================================\n7. BUILD COMMAND\n==================================================\n\nprojectctl build\n\nmust:\n\n- use incremental Gradle build\n- preserve cache\n- build project\n- collect current APKs\n- write log\n- write metadata\n- write hashes\n- create associated snapshot\n- update latest symlinks\n\nNo adb.\nNo install.\n\n==================================================\n8. CLEAN BUILD COMMAND\n==================================================\n\nprojectctl clean-build\n\nmust:\n\n- run controlled project clean\n- NOT delete shared cache/gradle\n- build again\n- produce normal timestamped output/snapshot\n\n==================================================\n9. CACHE CLEAN COMMAND\n==================================================\n\nprojectctl cache-clean\n\nmust require explicit execution.\n\nIt may clean:\n\ncache/projectctl\nsafe temporary caches\n\nDo NOT automatically wipe Gradle dependency cache.\n\nAdd optional:\n\nprojectctl cache-clean --all\n\nfor deliberate full cache deletion.\n\n==================================================\n10. TMP\n==================================================\n\ntmp/ is ephemeral.\n\nprojectctl may remove only its own temporary files.\n\nNever use tmp as final artifact storage.\n\n==================================================\n11. OUTPUT SESSION\n==================================================\n\noutputs/<BUILD_ID>/\n\ncontains only:\n\nAPK artifacts\nBUILD_INFO.txt\nbuild.log\nSHA256SUMS.txt\n\nOptional:\n\nmapping/reference metadata links\n\nNo source copy.\nNo Gradle cache.\nNo private keys.\n\n==================================================\n12. SNAPSHOT SESSION\n==================================================\n\nsnapshots/<BUILD_ID>/\n\ncontains:\n\nproject.tar.gz\nSNAPSHOT_INFO.txt\nSHA256SUMS.txt\n\nSnapshot exclusions:\n\n.git caches if unnecessary\n.gradle/\n**/build/\ncache/\ntmp/\noutputs/\nsnapshots/\ncheckpoints/\nprivate/\n*.apk\n*.aab\n*.jks\n*.keystore\n\n==================================================\n13. CHECKPOINT CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\ncheckpoints/\n\nmanual only.\n\nprojectctl checkpoint <name>\n\ncreates immutable checkpoint bundle.\n\nNever auto-delete.\n\nNever use checkpoint as working tree.\n\n==================================================\n14. PRIVATE CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nprivate/\n\ncontains only sensitive artifacts.\n\nExamples:\n\nprivate/signing/\nprivate/mapping/\n\nPermissions restrictive where possible.\n\nNever copy private/ into:\n\noutputs\nsnapshots\nreports\ndocs\n\n==================================================\n15. MAPPING\n==================================================\n\nR8 mapping output may be copied to:\n\nprivate/mapping/<BUILD_ID>/\n\nand referenced by BUILD_INFO.\n\nDo not package mapping in APK.\n\n==================================================\n16. LATEST\n==================================================\n\nMaintain:\n\noutputs/latest\nsnapshots/latest\n\nOnly point to last SUCCESSFUL build.\n\nUse atomic symlink replacement.\n\n==================================================\n17. BUILD FAILURE\n==================================================\n\nFailed build:\n\ndo not update latest.\n\nDo not reuse previous APK.\n\nWrite failed session metadata/log.\n\nNo snapshot marked SUCCESS.\n\n==================================================\n18. NO AUTOMATIC DELETION\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT automatically delete:\n\noutputs\nsnapshots\ncheckpoints\n\nRetention policy will be a separate future decision.\n\n==================================================\n19. DISK STATUS\n==================================================\n\nprojectctl status\n\nshows:\n\nproject size\nGradle cache size\noutputs size\nsnapshots size\ncheckpoints size\nprivate size\nlatest build ID\nlatest snapshot ID\n\n==================================================\n20. PROJECTCTL COMMANDS\n==================================================\n\nFinal supported commands:\n\nprojectctl build\nprojectctl clean-build\nprojectctl status\nprojectctl latest\nprojectctl snapshot\nprojectctl checkpoint <name>\nprojectctl cache-status\nprojectctl cache-clean\nprojectctl cache-clean --all\n\nNo duplicate aliases unless necessary.\n\n==================================================\n21. SHELL HARDENING\n==================================================\n\nprojectctl:\n\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\nNo eval.\nNo ls parsing.\nQuote paths.\nUse find/stat/readlink.\nUse mktemp under tmp/.\nUse traps for incomplete sessions.\n\n==================================================\n22. LOCK FILE\n==================================================\n\nPrevent simultaneous builds.\n\nUse:\n\ncache/projectctl/build.lock\n\nwith flock.\n\nIf build already active:\nfail clearly.\n\nDo not allow two projectctl build sessions to mutate Gradle outputs simultaneously.\n\n==================================================\n23. ATOMIC SESSION\n==================================================\n\nBuild into:\n\noutputs/.working-<ID>\n\nSnapshot into:\n\nsnapshots/.working-<ID>\n\nRename to final only after success/validation.\n\n==================================================\n24. SOURCE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nprojectctl must never:\n\ngit reset\ngit clean\ncheckout\nsed source\nrewrite Kotlin\nrewrite Manifest\nrewrite Gradle\n\nexcept commands explicitly designed to modify project in future.\n\n==================================================\n25. VALIDATE CACHE USAGE\n==================================================\n\nRun two consecutive builds.\n\nBuild #2 should reuse Gradle cache/incremental state.\n\nDocument:\n\nbuild 1 duration\nbuild 2 duration\n\nDo not make speed a PASS requirement,\nonly verify cache paths are reused.\n\n==================================================\n26. FINAL DOCUMENT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\ndocs/MACHINA_OPT_WORKSPACE_CONTRACT.md\n\nThis document becomes authoritative.\n\nInclude:\n\ndirectory map\ncache contract\nbuild lifecycle\nsnapshot lifecycle\ncheckpoint lifecycle\nprivate data rules\ncleanup rules\ntimezone rule\nnaming rule\nrecovery procedure\n\n==================================================\n27. FREEZE\n==================================================\n\nCreate marker:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/WORKSPACE_FROZEN\n\nContents:\n\nWorkspace Contract Version: 1\nTimezone: Europe/Rome\nController: /opt/Android/Machina/projectctl\nWorking Copy: /opt/Android/Machina/project\nDo not restructure without explicit migration.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA FINAL /opt WORKSPACE READY\n\nWorkspace contract:\nVERSION 1\n\nRoot:\n/opt/Android/Machina\n\nWorking copy:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nGradle cache:\n/opt/Android/Machina/cache/gradle\n\nBuild lock:\n/opt/Android/Machina/cache/projectctl/build.lock\n\nTimezone:\nEurope/Rome\n\nLatest output:\n<path>\n\nLatest snapshot:\n<path>\n\nIncremental build cache:\n<ENABLED/FAILED>\n\nBuild #1:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nBuild #2:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot validation:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nOutput hashes:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nWorkspace frozen marker:\n<path>\n\nContract:\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_OPT_WORKSPACE_CONTRACT.md\n\nADB used:\nNO\n\nAPK installed:\nNO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:240:{"session_id":"01a0116c-fa49-7f00-b48a-3282b9c83a05","ts":1787171273,"text":"FASE: MACHINA HOME — PAUSED CORE FULL AUDIT\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nSTATUS:\nPAUSED\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nREAD-ONLY AUDIT.\n\nNON modificare:\n- Kotlin\n- Manifest\n- Gradle\n- resources\n- docs esistenti\n- projectctl\n- build configuration\n\nNON applicare fix.\nNON fare refactor.\nNON rimuovere codice.\nNON aggiungere feature.\n\nObiettivo:\ncapire con precisione lo stato reale del core prima di riprenderne lo sviluppo.\n\n==================================================\n1. SOURCE INVENTORY\n==================================================\n\nInventaria tutto il progetto.\n\nRiporta:\n\n- Kotlin files\n- Kotlin LOC\n- composables\n- classes\n- objects\n- data classes\n- enums/sealed types\n- interfaces\n- extension functions\n- resources\n- dependencies production\n- Manifest components\n\nClassifica ogni file:\n\nCORE\nFEATURE\nINFRASTRUCTURE\nLEGACY\nUNKNOWN\n\n==================================================\n2. CORE DEFINITION — OBSERVED, NOT ASSUMED\n==================================================\n\nNon partire dal contratto teorico precedente.\n\nDetermina dal codice reale quali componenti formano oggi:\n\n- Home\n- Fav\n- P1\n- P2\n- Dock\n- App Drawer\n- App catalog\n- persistence\n- launch pipeline\n- motion/input\n\nRiporta eventuali discrepanze rispetto al design desiderato.\n\n==================================================\n3. HOME STATE MODEL\n==================================================\n\nTrova tutti gli state che controllano la Home.\n\nInventaria:\n\nmutableStateOf\nmutableIntStateOf\nmutableFloatStateOf\nStateFlow\nMutableStateFlow\nLiveData\nremember\nrememberSaveable\nderivedStateOf\n\nPer ogni state:\n\nFILE\nOWNER\nPURPOSE\nPERSISTENT/TEMPORARY\nWRITERS\nREADERS\n\nSegnala:\n\nduplicate state\nderived state persisted inutilmente\nstate con ownership ambigua\n\n==================================================\n4. HOME SNAPSHOT\n==================================================\n\nVerifica se esiste davvero un HomeSnapshot unico.\n\nControlla:\n\nP1 size\nP2 size\nDock size\n\nTarget desiderato:\n\nP1 = 8\nP2 = 8\nDock = 5\n\nRiporta:\n\n- source of truth\n- normalization\n- temporary empty states\n- partial snapshot paths\n- refresh behavior\n\n==================================================\n5. PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nAudit completo LauncherPreferences / storage.\n\nVerifica:\n\nP1 8\nP2 8\nDock 5\nexplicit empty\nlegacy migration\nicon shape\nobsolete preferences\nold feature keys\n\nSegnala:\n\n- write during composition\n- repeated migration\n- per-slot write loops\n- destructive repair\n- malformed data crash path\n\n==================================================\n6. APP CATALOG\n==================================================\n\nAudit AppCatalog.\n\nVerifica:\n\n- source APIs\n- package enumeration\n- callbacks\n- profiles\n- refresh triggers\n- refresh onResume\n- main-thread work\n- generation/cancellation\n- stale result protection\n- listener registration/cleanup\n\nClassifica:\n\nGOOD\nRISK\nBUG\nDEAD\n\n==================================================\n7. LAUNCH PIPELINE\n==================================================\n\nTraccia:\n\nP1 tap\nP2 tap\nDock tap\nDrawer tap\n\nfino a launch.\n\nRiporta:\n\n- number of launch paths\n- duplicate clickable owners\n- debounce/locks\n- failed launch handling\n- first-touch blockers\n\n==================================================\n8. INPUT / GESTURE INVENTORY\n==================================================\n\nCerca TUTTI:\n\npointerInput\nscrollable\ndraggable\ndetectDragGestures\ndetectVerticalDragGestures\ndetectHorizontalDragGestures\nawaitPointerEventScope\nBackHandler\nPredictiveBackHandler\nsystemGestureExclusionRects\nnestedScroll\noverscroll\nclickable\ncombinedClickable\n\nPer ciascuno:\n\nFILE\nOWNER\nAXIS\nCONSUMES EVENTS\nSTATE WRITES\nVISUAL WRITES\n\n==================================================\n9. SYSTEM GESTURE MODEL\n==================================================\n\nAudit separatamente:\n\nLEFT system Back\nRIGHT system Back\nBOTTOM Home\nOverview\nQuick Switch\n\nRiporta:\n\n- app interception\n- gesture exclusion\n- BackHandler ownership\n- Predictive Back participation\n- custom gesture emulation\n\nTarget desiderato NON va imposto.\n\nDescrivere comportamento reale.\n\n==================================================\n10. APP DRAWER\n==================================================\n\nVerifica se App Drawer esiste realmente oggi.\n\nRiporta:\n\n- implementation file\n- state owner\n- open path\n- close path\n- Back behavior\n- swipe behavior\n- catalog source\n- separate cache/state\n- search/suggestions/recents residual code\n\nClassificare:\n\nCLEAN\nOVERCOMPLEX\nBROKEN\nPARTIAL\nABSENT\n\n==================================================\n11. MATERIAL STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nAudit PATCH 001 reale.\n\nVerifica:\n\n- exact Compose/Foundation API\n- number of OverscrollEffect instances\n- input source\n- actual delta consumption\n- horizontal/vertical behavior\n- duplicate custom motion\n- old spring/wobble leftovers\n\nNon assumere che il doc PATCH 001 corrisponda ancora al runtime.\n\n==================================================\n12. ANIMATION INVENTORY\n==================================================\n\nCerca:\n\nanimate*\nAnimatable\nspring\ntween\nkeyframes\nAnimatedVisibility\nAnimatedContent\nCrossfade\ngraphicsLayer\nalpha\nscale\ntranslation\n\nClassifica:\n\nSYSTEM\nMATERIAL\nCORE\nFEATURE\nLEGACY\nUNEXPECTED\n\n==================================================\n13. WINDOW / THEME\n==================================================\n\nAudit:\n\nTheme.Machina\nTheme.Machina.Starting\nSplashScreen\npostSplashScreenTheme\nwindowShowWallpaper\nwindowBackground\nwindowIsTranslucent\nedge-to-edge\nsystem bars\ncontrast enforcement\n\nDescrivere il percorso:\n\nsystem wallpaper\n→ Window\n→ Compose root\n→ dim\n→ Home\n\n==================================================\n14. SPLASH\n==================================================\n\nVerifica lo stato reale:\n\nTheme.SplashScreen\ninstallSplashScreen()\nicon\nbackground\npostSplashScreenTheme\n\nSegnala:\n\ndouble splash\nopaque intermediate frame\ncustom delay\ncustom SplashActivity\n\n==================================================\n15. VISUAL PATCH\n==================================================\n\nAudit PATCH 003 reale.\n\nVerifica:\n\n- border\n- dim\n- shadow\n- color tokens\n- hardcoded duplicates\n- alpha paths\n- full-screen coverage\n\nNon modificarla.\n\n==================================================\n16. SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nLe Settings erano state rimosse.\n\nVerifica se esistono ancora:\n\nsettings routes\nsettings composables\nMaterial icons dependency\nRoleManager UI\nDynamic Color\nsettings-only strings/resources\nicon-shape setter adapters\n\nClassifica:\n\nREMOVED\nPARTIAL RESIDUE\nSTILL ACTIVE\n\n==================================================\n17. FIRST RUN\n==================================================\n\nVerifica se esiste già codice first-run.\n\nCerca:\n\nfirst_run\nonboarding\nchangelog\nRoleManager prompt\nlogo bounce\nstartup state\n\nClassifica:\n\nABSENT\nPARTIAL\nACTIVE\n\n==================================================\n18. LIFECYCLE\n==================================================\n\nAudit:\n\nonCreate\nonStart\nonResume\nonPause\nonStop\nonDestroy\n\ne Compose lifecycle effects.\n\nRiporta:\n\n- state resets\n- catalog refresh\n- cache clear\n- snapshot clear\n- listener setup\n- listener cleanup\n- repeated initialization\n\n==================================================\n19. THREADING / COROUTINES\n==================================================\n\nInventaria:\n\nCoroutineScope\nlaunch\nasync\nwithContext\nDispatchers\nExecutor\nThread\nHandler\nrunBlocking\n\nSegnala:\n\nmain-thread PackageManager work\nblocking IO\nraw threads\nscope leaks\nunstructured coroutines\n\n==================================================\n20. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nCerca:\n\nPackageManager enumeration in composition\nicon loading in recomposition\nbitmap decoding\nwallpaper decoding\nrepeated sorting\nlarge allocations\ncache misses\ncache clears\nunbounded lists\n\nClassifica:\n\nCONFIRMED\nLIKELY\nPOSSIBLE\nNOT_FOUND\n\n==================================================\n21. CRASH PATHS\n==================================================\n\nCerca:\n\n!!\nlist[index]\nfirst()\nsingle()\nlateinit\nunsafe casts\nIllegalStateException\nActivityNotFoundException\nSecurityException\nCancellationException misuse\nConcurrentModificationException risks\n\nRiporta solo path realmente plausibili.\n\n==================================================\n22. ERROR HANDLING\n==================================================\n\nAudit:\n\ncatch(Throwable)\ncatch(Exception)\nsilent catches\nLog spam\nfallback logic\n\nClassifica qualità.\n\n==================================================\n23. MANIFEST\n==================================================\n\nRiporta:\n\nactivities\nservices\nreceivers\nproviders\npermissions\nqueries\nintent filters\nHOME\nDEFAULT\nLAUNCHER\nexported\nlaunchMode\ntaskAffinity\nexcludeFromRecents\n\nSegnala componenti residui non necessari.\n\n==================================================\n24. DEPENDENCIES\n==================================================\n\nRiporta tutte le production dependencies.\n\nPer ciascuna:\n\nUSED\nLIKELY_UNUSED\nCONFIRMED_UNUSED\nUNKNOWN\n\nNON rimuoverle.\n\n==================================================\n25. R8\n==================================================\n\nVerifica:\n\ndebug minify\ndebug shrinkResources\nrelease minify\nrelease shrinkResources\nfull mode\nkeep rules\ndontwarn\ndontobfuscate\ndontoptimize\ndontshrink\n\nRiporta eventuali regole troppo ampie.\n\n==================================================\n26. APK BUILD\n==================================================\n\nEseguire solo build di verifica:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nNessuna installazione.\n\nRiporta:\n\nDebug build\nRelease/R8 build se projectctl la produce\nAPK paths\nsizes\nSHA-256\n\n==================================================\n27. APK STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nSul build più recente:\n\nZIP validation\nDEX size\nresource size\nnative libs\nimages\npadding\n\nVerificare che il vecchio problema da ~25 MiB di padding\nnon sia tornato.\n\n==================================================\n28. CORE COMPLEXITY METRICS\n==================================================\n\nCalcola:\n\nKotlin LOC\nKotlin files\nstate owners\ngesture/input owners\nCompose effects\nlisteners\ncallbacks\nanimation owners\ncatalog refresh paths\nlaunch paths\n\n==================================================\n29. DEAD CODE\n==================================================\n\nClassificare:\n\nCONFIRMED DEAD\nLIKELY DEAD\nACTIVE\nUNKNOWN\n\nNON eliminare.\n\n==================================================\n30. ARCHITECTURE SCORE\n==================================================\n\nDare score 0-10 con motivazione breve:\n\nCore simplicity\nState ownership\nInput architecture\nLifecycle\nPersistence\nCatalog\nPerformance\nReliability\nPatchability\nMaintainability\n\n==================================================\n31. BUG/RISK PRIORITY\n==================================================\n\nCreare:\n\nP0 — confirmed blocker\nP1 — serious risk\nP2 — cleanup/complexity\nP3 — cosmetic/non-critical\n\nOgni item deve includere:\n\nFILE\nSYMBOL\nWHY\nRECOMMENDED DIRECTION\n\nNON implementare fix.\n\n==================================================\n32. WHAT TO KEEP\n==================================================\n\nElencare le parti che meritano di essere congelate così come sono.\n\nSolo evidenza reale.\n\n==================================================\n33. WHAT TO REBUILD\n==================================================\n\nElencare le parti che sarebbe più sicuro ricostruire\ninvece di continuare a patchare.\n\n==================================================\n34. MINIMUM GOOD CORE\n==================================================\n\nProporre, sulla base del codice osservato, la struttura minima\nche potrebbe diventare Machina Core V2.\n\nNO implementazione.\n\n==================================================\n35. CREATE AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nCreare:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_PAUSED_CORE_FULL_AUDIT.md\n\n==================================================\nFINAL OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PAUSED CORE FULL AUDIT COMPLETE\n\n=== SIZE ===\nKotlin files: <n>\nKotlin LOC: <n>\nCore files: <n>\nFeature files: <n>\nDead/legacy files: <n>\n\n=== STATE ===\nMutable state owners: <n>\nDuplicate state owners: <n>\nHomeSnapshot owners: <n>\nPartial snapshot paths: <n>\n\n=== INPUT ===\nClickable owners: <n>\nGesture owners: <n>\nHorizontal gesture owners: <n>\nVertical gesture owners: <n>\nBackHandlers: <n>\nGesture exclusion owners: <n>\nOverscrollEffect owners: <n>\n\n=== CORE ===\nP1 slots: <n>\nP2 slots: <n>\nDock slots: <n>\nApp Drawer: <CLEAN/OVERCOMPLEX/BROKEN/PARTIAL/ABSENT>\n\n=== LIFECYCLE ===\nCatalog refresh-on-resume paths: <n>\nSnapshot clear paths: <n>\nListener leak paths: <n>\nMain-thread heavy paths: <n>\n\n=== RELIABILITY ===\nConfirmed crash paths: <n>\nFirst-touch blockers: <n>\nRace/stale-result risks: <n>\nMalformed persistence crash paths: <n>\n\n=== LEGACY ===\nSettings state: <value>\nFirst Run state: <value>\nDead feature paths: <n>\nLegacy motion paths: <n>\n\n=== BUILD ===\nDebug: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8 Release: <SUCCESS/FAILED/N-A>\nAPK size: <value>\nAPK padding: <value>\nZIP validation: <PASS/FAIL>\n\n=== SCORES ===\nCore simplicity: <0-10>\nState ownership: <0-10>\nInput architecture: <0-10>\nLifecycle: <0-10>\nPersistence: <0-10>\nCatalog: <0-10>\nPerformance: <0-10>\nReliability: <0-10>\nPatchability: <0-10>\nMaintainability: <0-10>\n\n=== PRIORITY ===\nP0: <n>\nP1: <n>\nP2: <n>\nP3: <n>\n\nKEEP:\n<short list>\n\nREBUILD:\n<short list>\n\nRecommended next action:\n<ONE concise recommendation>\n\nProject modified:\nNO\n\nAudit:\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_PAUSED_CORE_FULL_AUDIT.md"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:241:{"session_id":"01a01bb8-a362-7412-9ff8-6a60394d0a09","ts":1787172187,"text":"FASE: MACHINA HOME — CORE V2 CLEAN BASELINE\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nSTATUS:\nREBUILD CORE BASELINE\n\nOBIETTIVO\n\nCreare un Core V2 minimale e stabile per Machina Home.\n\nNESSUNA FEATURE.\n\nIl Core deve essere utilizzabile anche se la directory features/\nnon esiste.\n\n==================================================\n1. CORE RUNTIME\n==================================================\n\nVisible runtime:\n\n- Home\n- Fav\n- P1\n- P2\n- Dock\n\nP1:\n8 slot manuali\n\nP2:\n8 slot manuali\n\nDock:\n5 slot manuali\n\nNient'altro.\n\n==================================================\n2. REMOVE FROM CORE\n==================================================\n\nIl Core NON deve contenere:\n\n- Settings\n- Search\n- App Drawer\n- First Run\n- Changelog\n- Dynamic Color\n- Material Stretch\n- custom gestures\n- wobble\n- animation engine\n- weather\n- clock/date\n- media\n- suggestions\n- recents\n- onboarding\n- RoleManager UI\n\n==================================================\n3. CORE FILE TARGET\n==================================================\n\nPreferire una struttura piccola:\n\ncore/\n  MachinaCore.kt\n  HomeSnapshot.kt\n\ncatalog/\n  AppCatalog.kt\n\nstorage/\n  LauncherPreferences.kt\n\nactions/\n  LauncherActions.kt\n\nui/home/\n  HomeScreen.kt\n  HomePanels.kt\n\nui/common/\n  AppVisuals.kt\n\nui/design/\n  MachinaDesign.kt\n\nMainActivity.kt\n\nNon creare framework.\n\n==================================================\n4. HOME SNAPSHOT\n==================================================\n\nUna sola source visuale:\n\nHomeSnapshot(\n    p1 = exactly 8,\n    p2 = exactly 8,\n    dock = exactly 5\n)\n\nUI legge solo snapshot.\n\nMai snapshot parziale.\n\n==================================================\n5. STATE OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nHomeSnapshot:\n1 owner\n\nCatalog:\n1 owner\n\nPersistence:\nLauncherPreferences\n\nLaunch:\nLauncherActions\n\nUI:\nread-only state\n\nNessun duplicato.\n\n==================================================\n6. PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nPersistenza core solo:\n\nP1[0..7]\nP2[0..7]\nDock[0..4]\n\nExplicit empty:\npreserved.\n\nNo auto-fill.\n\nNo suggested.\n\nNo random replacement.\n\n==================================================\n7. SAFE NORMALIZATION\n==================================================\n\nQuando si legge lo storage:\n\nP1 -> exactly 8\nP2 -> exactly 8\nDock -> exactly 5\n\nMalformed entry:\nsafe unresolved/empty.\n\nMai IndexOutOfBounds.\n\n==================================================\n8. APP CATALOG\n==================================================\n\nCatalog serve solo a:\n\n- enumerate launchable apps\n- resolve saved identities\n- label\n- icon\n- react to package changes\n\nNo ranking.\nNo Search.\nNo suggestions.\nNo recents.\n\n==================================================\n9. THREADING\n==================================================\n\nPackage enumeration:\noff main thread.\n\nOne refresh owner.\n\nNo thread storm.\n\nNo full catalog refresh on every onResume.\n\n==================================================\n10. STALE REFRESH PROTECTION\n==================================================\n\nOld refresh result must not replace newer result.\n\nUse:\n\ngeneration counter\nor equivalent simple cancellation.\n\n==================================================\n11. HOME LIFECYCLE\n==================================================\n\nHome -> app -> Home:\n\ndo not:\n\nclear snapshot\nclear slots\nclear catalog\nreset defaults\nrerun migrations\n\nFirst frame on return:\nprevious valid snapshot available.\n\n==================================================\n12. APP LAUNCH\n==================================================\n\nSingle path:\n\nAppCell\n→ LauncherActions.launch(app)\n\nP1/P2/Dock share it.\n\nNo duplicate launch handlers.\n\n==================================================\n13. FIRST TAP\n==================================================\n\nEach app cell:\n\none clickable.\n\nNo root pointerInput.\nNo gesture overlay.\nNo interaction lock.\nNo debounce blocking first tap.\n\n1 tap = 1 launch.\n\n==================================================\n14. FAILED LAUNCH\n==================================================\n\nHandle locally:\n\nActivityNotFoundException\nSecurityException\n\nNo Home crash.\n\n==================================================\n15. UNINSTALLED APP\n==================================================\n\nSaved app disappears:\n\nslot becomes unresolved safely.\n\nDo NOT replace with another app.\n\nIf app returns:\nidentity may resolve again.\n\n==================================================\n16. BACK CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nHOME ROOT:\n\nBack = NO_OP\n\nUse one supported BackHandler.\n\nNo finish.\nNo task manipulation.\nNo navigation.\nNo animation.\n\n==================================================\n17. SYSTEM GESTURES\n==================================================\n\nCore does NOT implement:\n\nLEFT swipe\nRIGHT swipe\nUP swipe\nDOWN swipe\n\nSystem Home/Overview:\nAndroid owned.\n\nFeature patches can add interaction later.\n\n==================================================\n18. WALLPAPER\n==================================================\n\nWallpaper:\nAndroid system only.\n\nMaintain:\n\nwindowShowWallpaper = true\n\nNo wallpaper picker.\nNo bitmap decoder.\nNo WallpaperManager setter.\n\n==================================================\n19. HOME VISUAL\n==================================================\n\nKeep current approved simple appearance if possible:\n\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nDo not add visual feature architecture yet.\n\nNo custom animations.\n\n==================================================\n20. ICONS\n==================================================\n\nOne icon rendering path.\n\nP1/P2/Dock use same resolver.\n\nNo separate caches per panel.\n\n==================================================\n21. CACHE\n==================================================\n\nSmall bounded in-memory icon cache if already necessary.\n\nDo not retain Activity context.\n\nApplication context only for long-lived services/cache.\n\n==================================================\n22. COMPOSE EFFECTS\n==================================================\n\nMinimize:\n\nLaunchedEffect\nDisposableEffect\nSideEffect\n\nEvery effect needs clear lifecycle reason.\n\nNo writes during composition.\n\n==================================================\n23. MAINACTIVITY\n==================================================\n\nMainActivity responsibilities only:\n\n- install splash if currently required\n- edge-to-edge/window setup\n- create core owner\n- render Home\n\nNo feature routing.\n\n==================================================\n24. MANIFEST\n==================================================\n\nKeep correct launcher:\n\nMAIN\nHOME\nDEFAULT\n\nexported = true\n\nNo unnecessary activities/services/receivers/providers.\n\n==================================================\n25. REMOVE LEGACY CORE PATHS\n==================================================\n\nIdentify and remove confirmed runtime legacy from old core:\n\n- Drawer\n- Settings\n- FirstRun\n- Search\n- old motion\n- old gestures\n- feature routing\n- suggested apps\n- recents\n\nOnly after call-site verification.\n\n==================================================\n26. FEATURE BOUNDARY PREPARATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate ONLY one minimal future hook contract.\n\nExample:\n\ninterface MachinaPatch {\n    @Composable\n    fun Content(core: MachinaCoreApi)\n}\n\nBut do NOT connect any patch yet if it complicates Core V2.\n\nPrefer even simpler:\n\nCore V2 first.\nPatch bridge next phase.\n\n==================================================\n27. CORE API\n==================================================\n\nIf needed expose minimal read-only API:\n\ninterface MachinaCoreApi {\n    val snapshot: HomeSnapshot\n    fun launchApp(app: LaunchableApp)\n}\n\nNo mutable storage access.\n\n==================================================\n28. HARDENING\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\npartial snapshot paths = 0\nsnapshot clear on resume = 0\ncatalog refresh on every resume = 0\nduplicate click owners = 0\nglobal input locks = 0\nmain-thread heavy scans = 0\nconfirmed listener leaks = 0\nconfirmed crash paths = 0\n\n==================================================\n29. R8 FRIENDLY\n==================================================\n\nNo reflection.\nNo dynamic plugin loading.\nNo broad keep rules.\n\n==================================================\n30. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS if configured.\n\nNO adb.\nNO install.\n\n==================================================\n31. CORE AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_CORE_V2_AUDIT.md\n\nSections:\n\nArchitecture\nState Ownership\nSnapshot\nCatalog\nPersistence\nLaunch\nInput\nLifecycle\nThreading\nManifest\nDependencies\nHardening\nRemaining Risks\n\n==================================================\n32. CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nIf build + audit SUCCESS:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint core-v2-baseline\n\nDo not delete old checkpoints.\n\n==================================================\nSUCCESS CRITERIA\n==================================================\n\nVisible runtime:\nHome/Fav/P1/P2/Dock\n\nP1:\n8\n\nP2:\n8\n\nDock:\n5\n\nFeature runtime paths:\n0\n\nHome Back:\nNO_OP\n\nCustom gestures:\n0\n\nCustom animations:\n0\n\nSnapshot owners:\n1\n\nCatalog owners:\n1\n\nLaunch paths:\n1\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n0\n\nSnapshot clear on resume:\n0\n\nMain-thread catalog scans:\n0\n\nConfirmed crash paths:\n0\n\nDebug build:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA CORE V2 BASELINE COMPLETE\n\nCore files: <numero>\nCore Kotlin LOC: <numero>\n\nP1: <numero>\nP2: <numero>\nDock: <numero>\n\nHomeSnapshot owners: <numero>\nCatalog owners: <numero>\nLaunch paths: <numero>\n\nFeature runtime paths: <numero>\nCustom gesture owners: <numero>\nCustom animation owners: <numero>\n\nHome Back: <NO_OP/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot clear on resume: <numero>\nCatalog refresh-on-resume: <numero>\nFirst-touch blockers: <numero>\nMain-thread heavy paths: <numero>\nConfirmed crash paths: <numero>\n\nDebug build: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8 release: <SUCCESS/FAILED/N-A>\n\nCheckpoint: <path>\n\nAudit:\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_CORE_V2_AUDIT.md\n\nADB used: NO\nAPK installed: NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:242:{"session_id":"01a01bb8-a362-7412-9ff8-6a60394d0a09","ts":1787173354,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — LAUNCHER INTERACTION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCORE V2 checkpoint\n2026-08-19_22-49-30-core-v2-baseline\n\nCORE STATUS:\nFROZEN\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRipristinare come UNA SOLA PATCH:\n\n1. comportamento corretto della Home launcher ai bordi LEFT/RIGHT\n2. Material/Android Stretch effect già approvato\n3. nessuna navigazione orizzontale\n\nNON modificare la logica Core V2.\n\n==================================================\n1. PATCH LOCATION\n==================================================\n\nCreare soltanto:\n\npatches/launcher_interaction/\n    LauncherInteractionPatch.kt\n\nPreferire UN SOLO FILE.\n\n==================================================\n2. CORE INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nConsentito:\n\nUN SOLO hook nel punto root della Home.\n\nConcetto:\n\nLauncherInteractionPatch.Attach {\n    HomeContent(...)\n}\n\noppure equivalente minimale.\n\nCore files touched:\nMAX 1\n\nCore logic changed:\n0\n\n==================================================\n3. HOME ROOT BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nHOME ROOT:\n\nLEFT:\nNO navigation\n\nRIGHT:\nNO navigation\n\nBACK:\nNO_OP\n\nLa Home non deve avere una pagina precedente.\n\n==================================================\n4. SYSTEM BACK AFFORDANCE\n==================================================\n\nProblema device confermato:\n\nsulla Home compare la grossa icona/freccia Back\ndi Android SystemUI.\n\nLa patch deve applicare il comportamento launcher-root\nnecessario affinché LEFT/RIGHT sulla Home non vengano\npresentati come normale Back applicativo.\n\nUsare API Android supportate.\n\nNON creare freccia custom.\n\nNON imitare SystemUI.\n\n==================================================\n5. GESTURE EXCLUSION\n==================================================\n\nSe necessario usare:\n\nsystemGestureExclusionRects\n\nSOLTANTO sulla Home root.\n\nOwner:\n1\n\nScope:\nsolo bordi laterali necessari.\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nNON escludere la gesture inferiore Android.\n\nHome / Overview / Quick Switch dal bordo inferiore:\nANDROID OWNED.\n\n==================================================\n6. MATERIAL STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nRipristinare l'effetto che era stato approvato\nprima del Core V2.\n\nUsare Compose Foundation / Material overscroll APIs.\n\nPreferenza:\n\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\nModifier.overscroll(...)\n\ncon corretta sorgente di gesture/scroll se richiesta.\n\nNON implementare:\n\ncustom spring\ncustom wobble\ncustom scale\ncustom fade\ncustom alpha\ncustom translation\n\n==================================================\n7. FULL HOME SURFACE\n==================================================\n\nIl Material Stretch deve appartenere alla superficie Home\nnel suo complesso.\n\nNon creare motion separato per:\n\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nUn solo visual effect owner.\n\n==================================================\n8. LEFT / RIGHT RESULT\n==================================================\n\nSwipe LEFT:\n\n- NO back arrow\n- NO navigation\n- NO state change\n- Material Stretch response\n\nSwipe RIGHT:\n\nstesso comportamento speculare.\n\n==================================================\n9. CORE DATA HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nLa patch NON può scrivere:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nP1\nP2\nDock\nAppCatalog\nLauncherPreferences\n\nPersistent writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n10. INPUT SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nLa patch non deve interferire con normali tap.\n\nP1:\nfirst tap launch\n\nP2:\nfirst tap launch\n\nDock:\nfirst tap launch\n\nTouch sotto touchSlop:\nnon diventa gesture.\n\n==================================================\n11. BACK\n==================================================\n\nHome BackHandler:\nKEEP NO_OP\n\nNon aggiungere:\n\nPredictiveBackHandler\nfinish()\nmoveTaskToBack()\ncustom Back animation\n\n==================================================\n12. WALLPAPER\n==================================================\n\nNon modificare:\n\nwindowShowWallpaper\nwindowBackground\ndim\nborder\nshadow\n\n==================================================\n13. PATCH REMOVABILITY\n==================================================\n\nEliminando:\n\npatches/launcher_interaction/\n\n+\nil singolo hook\n\ndeve tornare esattamente Core V2.\n\n==================================================\n14. PATCH AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nCreare:\n\ndocs/PATCH_001_V2_LAUNCHER_INTERACTION.md\n\nRiportare:\n\nfiles added\ncore files touched\ngesture exclusion owner\nMaterial overscroll owner\nstate writes\npersistence writes\nrollback\n\n==================================================\n15. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nSUCCESS\n==================================================\n\nCore logic modified:\nNO\n\nCore files touched:\n<= 1\n\nPatch files:\n1 preferred\n\nLEFT navigation:\n0\n\nRIGHT navigation:\n0\n\nSystem Back affordance on Home:\nEXPECTED HIDDEN\n\nMaterial Stretch:\nYES\n\nCustom motion engine:\n0\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nPersistence writes:\n0\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n0\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 001 V2 LAUNCHER INTERACTION COMPLETE\n\nPatch files: <n>\nCore files touched: <n>\n\nLauncher-root exclusion owner: <n>\nMaterial Stretch owner: <n>\n\nLEFT navigation actions: <n>\nRIGHT navigation actions: <n>\n\nHomeSnapshot writes: <n>\nPersistence writes: <n>\n\nCustom spring paths: <n>\nCustom fade paths: <n>\nCustom scale paths: <n>\n\nFirst-touch blockers: <n>\n\nDebug build: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8 release: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nCore V2 checksum changed by logic:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPatch:\ndocs/PATCH_001_V2_LAUNCHER_INTERACTION.md"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:244:{"session_id":"01a01bdb-3823-7351-9e08-7afaedf44feb","ts":1787173772,"text":"Aggiorniamo il piano del progetto.\n\nCONTESTO\n\nCodex è già aperto e sta lavorando dentro:\n\n/opt/Android/Delta\n\nQuesta directory deve diventare il progetto operativo del nuovo:\n\nHacie Icon Pack\n\nNON creare:\n\n/opt/projects/HacieIconPack\n\nNON spostare ancora la directory.\n\nMantieni come project root:\n\n/opt/Android/Delta\n\nBRANDING NUOVO\n\nNome app:\n\nHacie Icon Pack\n\nApplication ID:\n\nit.gaetano.hacieiconpack\n\nNome progetto/logico:\n\nHacieIconPack\n\nOBIETTIVO\n\nRicostruire da zero una base Android minimale per Hacie Icon Pack dentro:\n\n/opt/Android/Delta\n\nPrima però fai un PRE-CHECK.\n\nPRE-CHECK OBBLIGATORIO\n\n1. mostra:\n   pwd\n2. verifica che il path corrente sia:\n   /opt/Android/Delta\n3. mostra:\n   ls -la\n4. verifica se esiste già un repository Git\n5. mostra:\n   git status --short\n   git rev-parse HEAD\n   solo se Git è già presente\n6. verifica se la directory contiene già file/progetti\n\nIMPORTANTE\n\nSe /opt/Android/Delta NON è vuota:\n\nNON cancellare nulla.\nNON sovrascrivere nulla.\nNON eseguire rm.\nNON fare git clean.\nNON fare git reset.\n\nPrima mostra cosa contiene e fermati se c'è materiale non chiaramente ricostruibile.\n\nSe invece è vuota o contiene soltanto una struttura nuova chiaramente destinata a questo progetto, continua.\n\nARCHITETTURA\n\nHacie Icon Pack deve essere una semplice app Android personale per GrapheneOS.\n\nRequisiti:\n\n- Kotlin\n- Gradle Kotlin DSL\n- Material 3\n- una sola MainActivity\n- nessun drawer\n- nessuna griglia\n- nessuna ricerca\n- nessun catalogo runtime\n- nessun servizio\n- nessun receiver\n- nessun provider\n- nessun worker\n- nessun job\n- nessun alarm\n- nessuna rete\n- nessuna telemetry\n- nessun analytics\n- nessun account\n- nessun permesso Android non necessario\n\nZERO-IDLE\n\nActivity = 1\nService = 0\nReceiver = 0\nProvider = 0\nPermissions = 0\n\nUI\n\nMostrare:\n\nHacie Icon Pack\n\nIcone incluse: 0\n\nVersione: 0.1.0\n\nIcon pack personale per GrapheneOS\n\nSupportare:\n\n- edge-to-edge\n- Material 3\n- dynamic color\n- light/dark\n\nICON PACK\n\nPreparare:\n\napp/src/main/assets/appfilter.xml\napp/src/main/assets/drawable.xml\n\napp/src/main/res/xml/appfilter.xml\napp/src/main/res/xml/drawable.xml\n\napp/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/\n\nLe coppie XML assets/res devono essere byte-identiche.\n\nInizialmente:\n\n0 mapping\n0 drawable applicativi\n\nINVENTORY\n\nCreare:\n\ninventory/grapheneos-apps.yaml\n\nPer ora vuoto/minimale.\n\nNon inventare package.\n\nVALIDATOR\n\nCreare:\n\ntools/validate-iconpack.sh\n\nControlli minimi:\n\n- XML assets/res identici\n- drawable dichiarati esistenti\n- nessun mapping verso asset mancante\n- nessun drawable duplicato\n- conteggio asset\n- zero componenti background\n- zero permessi\n\nVERSIONE\n\nversionCode = 1\nversionName = 0.1.0\n\nSDK\n\nPreferire:\n\ncompileSdk = 36\ntargetSdk = 36\nminSdk >= 35\n\nsolo se gli SDK sono già disponibili localmente.\n\nJava toolchain:\n\npreferire JDK 21 con bytecode Java/Kotlin 17 se compatibile.\n\nTIMESTAMP\n\nOgni:\n\n- APK\n- report\n- snapshot\n- artifact\n\ndeve usare:\n\nTZ=Europe/Rome\n\nFormato 12 ore con AM/PM.\n\nBUILD\n\nDopo bootstrap:\n\n1. validator\n2. zero-idle audit\n3. solo:\n   :app:assembleDebug\n\nNON fare release.\nNON installare APK.\n\nARTIFACT\n\nSalva sotto:\n\n/opt/Android/Delta/artifacts/\n\ne report sotto:\n\n/opt/Android/Delta/reports/\n\nNome esempio:\n\nHacieIconPack-debug-19-08-2026_11-15-00-PM.apk\n\nGIT\n\nSe il repository non esiste ancora:\n\ninizializza Git locale.\n\nNON configurare remote.\n\nSe tutto passa crea un solo commit:\n\nbootstrap Hacie Icon Pack\n\nOUTPUT\n\nSe tutto passa stampa:\n\nHACIE REBUILD FASE 1 COMPLETATA\n\nPoi mostra:\n\n- project root\n- application ID\n- versionCode\n- versionName\n- compileSdk\n- targetSdk\n- minSdk\n- Activity\n- Service\n- Receiver\n- Provider\n- permissions\n- validator\n- zero-idle\n- build result\n- APK path\n- APK size\n- APK SHA256\n- report path\n- Git HEAD\n- conferma nessuna installazione\n- conferma nessuna build release\n\nSe trovi materiale esistente non chiaramente ricostruibile stampa:\n\nHACIE REBUILD BLOCCATA — DIRECTORY NON VUOTA\n\ne mostra soltanto cosa contiene.\n\nNON cancellare nulla.\n\nPoi fermati."}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:245:{"session_id":"01a01bb8-a362-7412-9ff8-6a60394d0a09","ts":1787175961,"text":"FASE: MACHINA CORE V2 — ANDROID PROCESS CACHE POLICY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nOBIETTIVO\n\nDocumentare nel contratto del Core V2 che la gestione\ndel processo cached appartiene ad Android.\n\nNON aggiungere codice runtime.\nNON aggiungere Service.\nNON aggiungere WakeLock.\nNON aggiungere cache manager.\nNON modificare lifecycle.\n\n==================================================\n1. UPDATE CORE CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nAggiornare:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_CORE_CONTRACT.md\n\nAggiungere la sezione:\n\n## Android Process Cache Policy\n\nTesto:\n\n- Android owns process caching and process residency.\n- Machina does not attempt to keep its process alive.\n- Machina does not use foreground/background services,\n  wakelocks, alarms, polling, or process-priority tricks\n  to remain resident.\n- If Android keeps the Machina process cached,\n  existing valid in-memory state may be reused naturally.\n- Machina must not depend on process survival for correctness.\n- If Android terminates the process, the Home must be able\n  to reconstruct its persistent state correctly on the next start.\n- Persistent state remains the source of truth for data that\n  must survive process death.\n- Android memory/process policy must not be overridden by Machina.\n\n==================================================\n2. CORE STATUS\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\nCORE V2 = STABLE CANDIDATE\n\nThis is a policy/documentation update only.\n\n==================================================\n3. STATIC VERIFY\n==================================================\n\nConfirm current core contains no:\n\nforeground service used for residency\nbackground service used for residency\nWakeLock\nkeep-alive loop\nperiodic polling used to keep process active\nprocess priority manipulation\n\nDo not modify code if count is already zero.\n\n==================================================\n4. NO BUILD REQUIRED IF DOC-ONLY\n==================================================\n\nIf only documentation changes:\n\nBuild:\nNOT REQUIRED\n\nIf any project source unexpectedly changes:\nSTOP and report it.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA ANDROID PROCESS CACHE POLICY ADDED\n\nCore contract updated: <YES/NO>\n\nRuntime files modified: <numero>\nLifecycle files modified: <numero>\n\nKeep-alive services: <numero>\nWakeLock paths: <numero>\nResidency polling paths: <numero>\nProcess-priority tricks: <numero>\n\nCore status:\nSTABLE CANDIDATE\n\nRuntime behavior changed:\nNO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:246:{"session_id":"01a01bb8-a362-7412-9ff8-6a60394d0a09","ts":1787176184,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — FAV EXPANSION / SEARCH SLOT PREPARATION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCORE V2 STABLE CANDIDATE\n\nCORE POLICY:\nDO NOT MODIFY CORE LOGIC\n\nPATCH TYPE:\nFEATURE_PATCH\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAggiungere un solo comportamento:\n\nSWIPE UP sulla Home\n→ Fav sale\n→ il container Home si allunga verso l'alto\n→ compare uno spazio libero tra Fav e P1/P2\n→ P1/P2/Dock NON cambiano posizione\n→ quello spazio sarà usato da una futura Search patch\n\nPer ora:\nNO SEARCH\nNO KEYBOARD\nNO INPUT\nNO RESULTS\nNO SETTINGS\n\n==================================================\n1. PATCH LOCATION\n==================================================\n\nCreare:\n\npatches/fav_expansion/\n    FavExpansionPatch.kt\n\nPreferire:\n1 solo file patch.\n\n==================================================\n2. SINGLE CORE HOOK\n==================================================\n\nLa patch deve entrare nel core con UN SOLO hook.\n\nEsempio concettuale:\n\nFavExpansionPatch.Attach(\n    content = {\n        HomeContent(...)\n    }\n)\n\noppure equivalente minimale.\n\nCore files touched:\nMAX 1\n\nCore logic modified:\n0\n\n==================================================\n3. HOME GEOMETRY CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nHOME BASE:\n\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nposizioni approvate.\n\nQuando espansa:\n\nFav sale verso l'alto.\n\nIl container principale aumenta altezza verso l'alto.\n\nP1:\nFIXED\n\nP2:\nFIXED\n\nDock:\nFIXED\n\nBottom anchor:\nFIXED\n\n==================================================\n4. IMPORTANT — DO NOT MOVE EVERYTHING\n==================================================\n\nNON traslare l'intera Home.\n\nNON muovere:\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\ninsieme a Fav.\n\nLa geometria corretta è:\n\nbottom of Upper/container:\nFIXED\n\ntop of Upper/container:\nmoves UP\n\nFav:\nattached to top section\n\nP1/P2:\nremain anchored near bottom of Upper\n\n==================================================\n5. SEARCH SLOT\n==================================================\n\nDurante expansion deve comparire uno spazio libero:\n\nbetween Fav and P1/P2\n\nQuesto spazio NON contiene ancora nulla.\n\nDefinirlo come:\n\nSearchSlot\n\nsolo come area geometrica vuota.\n\nNO Search feature.\n\n==================================================\n6. SEARCH SLOT SIZE\n==================================================\n\nCalcolare lo spazio in modo responsivo.\n\nNon hardcodare coordinate Pixel-specifiche.\n\nUsare:\n\navailableHeight\nsystem insets\nFav height\nP1/P2 height\nspacing\nDock bounds\n\nTarget:\n\nSearchSlot deve avere abbastanza spazio\nper una futura search bar + risultati compatti.\n\n==================================================\n7. HOME STATES\n==================================================\n\nUsare SOLO due stati patch-locali:\n\nCOLLAPSED\nEXPANDED\n\nNessun altro state.\n\nCore HomeSnapshot:\nUNCHANGED.\n\n==================================================\n8. STATE OWNER\n==================================================\n\nPatch state owner:\n1\n\nPersistenza:\n0\n\nLo stato expanded/collapsed è transient.\n\nRitorno da altra app:\npreferenza iniziale:\nCOLLAPSED\n\nNON modificare persistence core.\n\n==================================================\n9. SWIPE UP\n==================================================\n\nDa COLLAPSED:\n\nvalid swipe UP\n→ EXPANDED\n\nUna sola azione.\n\n==================================================\n10. SWIPE DOWN\n==================================================\n\nDa EXPANDED:\n\nvalid swipe DOWN\n→ COLLAPSED\n\nDa COLLAPSED:\n\nswipe DOWN\n→ NO_OP\n\n==================================================\n11. LEFT / RIGHT\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\nNO_OP\n\nRIGHT:\nNO_OP\n\nNessuna navigazione.\n\nNessun state change.\n\nNessuna animazione orizzontale.\n\n==================================================\n12. GESTURE OWNER\n==================================================\n\nUn solo gesture owner verticale nella patch.\n\nCore custom gesture owners:\n0\n\nPatch gesture owners:\n1\n\n==================================================\n13. INPUT SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nTouch sotto touchSlop:\nnon è swipe.\n\nP1/P2/Dock taps:\nfirst tap works.\n\nNessun full-screen pointer overlay che blocca i click.\n\n==================================================\n14. MOTION\n==================================================\n\nUsare motion semplice e unico.\n\nPreferenza iniziale:\n\nCompose Material/standard motion,\nsenza custom wobble.\n\nAnimare una sola proprietà geometrica:\n\nUpper top\noppure\nUpper height bottom-anchored.\n\nNO:\n\nalpha\nscale\ntranslationX\ncrossfade\nchild animations\nDock animation\n\n==================================================\n15. ANIMATION OWNER\n==================================================\n\nPatch animation owners:\n1\n\nCore animation owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n16. MATERIAL FEEL\n==================================================\n\nUsare preset Compose/Material standard.\n\nPreferire:\n\nspring(\n    dampingRatio = Spring.DampingRatioNoBouncy,\n    stiffness = Spring.StiffnessMedium\n)\n\nNiente custom float finché non serve.\n\n==================================================\n17. FAV\n==================================================\n\nFav deve restare identico visualmente.\n\nNon cambiare:\n\ncolor\nborder\nshadow\ntext\nicon\n\nSolo posizione verticale derivata dal container.\n\n==================================================\n18. P1 / P2\n==================================================\n\nP1/P2 devono restare:\n\nsame size\nsame icon size\nsame grid\nsame spacing\nsame y-position\n\ndurante expansion.\n\n==================================================\n19. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock:\ncompletely fixed.\n\nNo movement.\n\nNo resize.\n\n==================================================\n20. SEARCH SLOT VISUAL\n==================================================\n\nPer ora:\n\nSearchSlot:\ntransparent / empty\n\nNo border.\nNo background.\nNo placeholder.\nNo text.\n\nServe soltanto a validare la geometria.\n\n==================================================\n21. WINDOW / WALLPAPER\n==================================================\n\nNON modificare:\n\nwindowShowWallpaper\nwindow background\ndim\nborder\nshadow\nsystem bars\n\n==================================================\n22. BACK\n==================================================\n\nHOME COLLAPSED:\nBack = NO_OP\n\nHOME EXPANDED:\nBack = COLLAPSED\n\nQuesto è l'unico Back utile introdotto dalla patch.\n\nNon uscire dal launcher.\n\n==================================================\n23. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nCLOCK_TICK:\n\non accepted COLLAPSED → EXPANDED\nonce\n\non accepted EXPANDED → COLLAPSED\nonce\n\nNO haptic during MOVE.\n\n==================================================\n24. NO SEARCH YET\n==================================================\n\nAbsolutely no:\n\nTextField\nBasicTextField\nkeyboard\nfocus requester\nsearch results\npackage search\nweb search\nsettings search\nhidden apps search\n\nSearch will be PATCH 002 V2 later.\n\n==================================================\n25. NO FEATURE COUPLING\n==================================================\n\nPatch cannot access:\n\nLauncherPreferences\nAppCatalog internals\nHomeSnapshot writers\nP1/P2/Dock storage\n\n==================================================\n26. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nRemoving:\n\npatches/fav_expansion/\n\n+\nthe single core hook\n\nmust restore exact Core V2.\n\n==================================================\n27. PATCH DOC\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\ndocs/PATCH_001_V2_FAV_EXPANSION.md\n\nInclude:\n\npurpose\ngeometry\nstate owner\ngesture owner\nanimated property\ncore files touched\npersistence\nrollback\nbuild results\n\n==================================================\n28. DEVICE TARGET\n==================================================\n\nOn Pixel:\n\nBASE:\nFav/P1/P2/Dock exactly as Core V2.\n\nSwipe UP:\nFav rises.\nUpper extends upward.\nEmpty SearchSlot appears.\nP1/P2 stay fixed.\nDock stays fixed.\n\nSwipe DOWN:\nreturns exactly to baseline.\n\nNo bounce.\nNo flash.\nNo multi-touch issue.\nNo second/third tap requirement.\n\n==================================================\n29. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nSUCCESS CRITERIA\n==================================================\n\nCore logic modified:\nNO\n\nCore files touched:\n<= 1\n\nPatch files:\n1 preferred\n\nPatch state owners:\n1\n\nPatch gesture owners:\n1\n\nPatch animation owners:\n1\n\nSearch paths:\n0\n\nKeyboard paths:\n0\n\nP1 movement:\n0\n\nP2 movement:\n0\n\nDock movement:\n0\n\nHorizontal navigation:\n0\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n0\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nPersistence writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 001 V2 FAV EXPANSION COMPLETE\n\nPatch files: <n>\nCore files touched: <n>\n\nState owners: <n>\nGesture owners: <n>\nAnimation owners: <n>\n\nAnimated property: <value>\n\nCollapsed state height: <value>\nExpanded state height: <value>\nSearchSlot height: <value>\n\nFav movement: <dp>\nP1 movement: <dp>\nP2 movement: <dp>\nDock movement: <dp>\n\nSearch paths: <n>\nKeyboard paths: <n>\n\nHomeSnapshot writes: <n>\nPersistence writes: <n>\n\nFirst-touch blockers: <n>\nFlash regression: <NONE/FOUND>\n\nDebug build: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8 release: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPatch doc:\ndocs/PATCH_001_V2_FAV_EXPANSION.md\n\nADB used: NO\nAPK installed: NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:247:{"session_id":"01a01bb8-a362-7412-9ff8-6a60394d0a09","ts":1787178009,"text":"REFERENCE IMAGE:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/references/fav-ui-reference.png\n\nUSE ONLY AS VISUAL REFERENCE.\n\nDO NOT recreate the image.\nDO NOT infer fake exact measurements from pixels.\nDO NOT replace the reference with generated artwork.\n\nUse it only to match:\n\n- container proportions\n- dark surface tone\n- corner radius feeling\n- gaps between Fav / main container / Dock\n- Dock height/proportion\n- border subtlety\n- icon spacing\n- overall visual density\n\nPATCH REQUEST:\n\n1. Keep current working Fav Expansion behavior.\n2. Raise Fav Apps further when expanded.\n3. Keep P1/P2/Dock fixed.\n4. Adjust main container + Dock appearance toward the supplied reference.\n5. Do not modify Core V2 state/persistence/catalog/launch paths.\n6. Do not add Search yet.\n7. Do not change gesture logic except expansion travel if required.\n8. Keep this as a patch-only visual/geometric change.\n\nREFERENCE PATH:\n/opt/Android/Machina/references/fav-ui-reference.png"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:248:{"session_id":"01a01bb8-a362-7412-9ff8-6a60394d0a09","ts":1787178559,"text":"REFERENCE IMAGE:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/references/fav-ui-reference.png\n\nUSE ONLY AS VISUAL REFERENCE.\n\nDO NOT recreate the image.\nDO NOT infer fake exact measurements from pixels.\nDO NOT replace the reference with generated artwork.\n\nUse it only to match:\n\n- container proportions\n- dark surface tone\n- corner radius feeling\n- gaps between Fav / main container / Dock\n- Dock height/proportion\n- border subtlety\n- icon spacing\n- overall visual density\n\nPATCH REQUEST:\n\n1. Keep current working Fav Expansion behavior.\n2. Raise Fav Apps further when expanded.\n3. Keep P1/P2/Dock fixed.\n4. Adjust main container + Dock appearance toward the supplied reference.\n5. Do not modify Core V2 state/persistence/catalog/launch paths.\n6. Do not add Search yet.\n7. Do not change gesture logic except expansion travel if required.\n8. Keep this as a patch-only visual/geometric change.\n\nREFERENCE PATH:\n/opt/Android/Machina/references/fav-ui-reference.png"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:251:{"session_id":"01a01bb8-a362-7412-9ff8-6a60394d0a09","ts":1787180096,"text":"FASE: MACHINA PATCH VALIDATION GATE\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nOBIETTIVO\n\nValidare la patch Fav/Search Pull già implementata.\n\nNON aggiungere feature.\nNON cambiare UI.\nNON cambiare motion.\nNON cambiare haptic.\nNON cambiare Core V2.\n\n==================================================\n1. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nEseguire:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n2. DEVICE TEST REQUIRED\n==================================================\n\nSul Pixel verificare manualmente:\n\nA. SWIPE UP\n- pull segue il dito\n- settle morbido\n- Fav sale correttamente\n- Search area appare correttamente\n- keyboard solo dopo EXPANDED\n- CONFIRM x1\n\nB. SWIPE DOWN\n- clear focus\n- keyboard chiusa\n- pull segue il dito\n- settle verso COLLAPSED\n- CONFIRM x1\n\nC. STATIC ELEMENTS\n- P1 movement = 0\n- P2 movement = 0\n- Dock movement = 0\n\nD. INPUT\n- P1 first tap = PASS\n- P2 first tap = PASS\n- Dock first tap = PASS\n- Search result first tap = PASS\n\nE. REGRESSIONS\n- no flash\n- no double touch\n- no crash\n- no keyboard layout jump\n- no horizontal navigation\n- no repeated haptic during MOVE\n\n==================================================\n3. STOP GATE\n==================================================\n\nSe QUALSIASI test device fallisce:\n\nNON fare cleanup/refactor.\n\nNON convalidare.\n\nRiportare:\n\nPATCH DEVICE VALIDATION FAILED\n\ncon causa precisa.\n\n==================================================\n4. STATIC AUDIT — ONLY IF DEVICE PASS\n==================================================\n\nSe test device PASS:\n\naudit della patch.\n\nVerificare:\n\n- state owners\n- gesture owners\n- animation owners\n- haptic owners\n- focus owners\n- IME owners\n- AppCatalog access\n- HomeSnapshot writes\n- persistence writes\n- duplicate listeners\n- duplicate effects\n- obsolete helpers\n- dead imports\n- dead state\n- dead callbacks\n\n==================================================\n5. CORE PROTECTION\n==================================================\n\nConfermare:\n\nCore V2 logic modified:\nNO\n\nHomeSnapshot semantics changed:\nNO\n\nP1/P2/Dock persistence changed:\nNO\n\nAppCatalog owner changed:\nNO\n\nLauncherActions changed:\nNO\n\n==================================================\n6. MOTION HEALTH\n==================================================\n\nTarget:\n\nvertical pull owners:\n1\n\nexpansion progress owners:\n1\n\nsettle spring owners:\n1\n\ncustom damping/stiffness floats:\n0\n\nhorizontal motion owners:\n0\n\nduplicate Animatable:\n0\n\n==================================================\n7. HAPTIC HEALTH\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nTarget:\n\nhaptic owners:\n1\n\nEXPAND:\n1\n\nCOLLAPSE:\n1\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\nCANCEL:\n0\n\nduplicate haptic:\n0\n\nVIBRATE permission:\nNO\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH HEALTH\n==================================================\n\nHistory:\nmemory-only\n\nMax:\n3\n\nDataStore:\n0\n\nSharedPreferences for search history:\n0\n\nRoom:\n0\n\nPackageManager query per keystroke:\n0\n\nNew AppCatalog owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n9. IME / FOCUS HEALTH\n==================================================\n\nFocusRequester owners:\n1 preferred\n\nKeyboard controller owners:\n1 preferred\n\nIME opens only after accepted EXPANDED:\nYES\n\nIME partial-pull paths:\n0\n\nLayout jump paths:\n0\n\n==================================================\n10. CLEANUP\n==================================================\n\nSolo se confermato dead:\n\nremove:\n- unused imports\n- unused helpers\n- duplicate callbacks\n- dead state\n- legacy motion code\n- abandoned search code\n\nNON fare cosmetic refactor.\n\nNON rinominare architettura sana.\n\n==================================================\n11. PATCH BOUNDARY\n==================================================\n\nLa patch deve restare rimovibile.\n\nRemoving patch files + single hook:\nCore V2 builds and runs.\n\n==================================================\n12. CODE QUALITY CHECK\n==================================================\n\nClassificare:\n\nSTATE OWNERSHIP:\nPASS/FAIL\n\nINPUT OWNERSHIP:\nPASS/FAIL\n\nMOTION:\nPASS/FAIL\n\nHAPTIC:\nPASS/FAIL\n\nIME:\nPASS/FAIL\n\nSEARCH:\nPASS/FAIL\n\nCORE ISOLATION:\nPASS/FAIL\n\nROLLBACK:\nPASS/FAIL\n\n==================================================\n13. FINAL BUILD\n==================================================\n\nDopo cleanup:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n14. PATCH DOC\n==================================================\n\nAggiornare/creare:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nPATCH_VALIDATED_FAV_SEARCH_PULL.md\n\nContiene:\n\nDevice validation\nArchitecture\nState ownership\nGesture ownership\nMotion\nHaptic\nIME\nSearch history\nCore isolation\nCleanup\nRollback\nBuild results\n\n==================================================\n15. CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nSolo se TUTTO PASS:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint fav-search-pull-validated\n\n==================================================\nFINAL OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH FAV/SEARCH PULL VALIDATION COMPLETE\n\nDevice validation:\n<PASS/FAILED>\n\nCore V2 logic modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nState owners:\n<n>\n\nGesture owners:\n<n>\n\nAnimation owners:\n<n>\n\nHaptic owners:\n<n>\n\nExpansion progress owners:\n<n>\n\nHorizontal motion owners:\n<n>\n\nIME partial-pull paths:\n<n>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n<n>\n\nMOVE haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nSearch history storage:\n<MEMORY_ONLY/OTHER>\n\nSearch history max:\n<n>\n\nNew AppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n<n>\n\nDead code removed:\n<n>\n\nCode quality:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nCheckpoint:\n<path/N-A>\n\nPatch audit:\n<path>\n\nADB used:\nNO\n\nAPK installed:\nNO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:253:{"session_id":"01a01bb8-a362-7412-9ff8-6a60394d0a09","ts":1787180630,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — SWIPE UP/DOWN MOTION RETUNE ONLY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCurrent PATCH 001 V2 Fav Expansion\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nCambiare SOLO l'animazione swipe UP/DOWN.\n\nNON modificare:\n\n- Core V2\n- Fav final geometry\n- SearchSlot geometry\n- P1 position\n- P2 position\n- Dock position\n- expansion state model\n- expansion progress owner\n- gesture owner count\n- haptic CONFIRM\n- persistence\n- HomeSnapshot\n- left/right behavior\n\n==================================================\n1. CURRENT PROBLEM\n==================================================\n\nCurrent vertical swipe behavior is functionally correct\nbut visually different from the previously preferred motion.\n\nPatch only the motion feel.\n\n==================================================\n2. KEEP DIRECT PULL\n==================================================\n\nDuring swipe:\n\ncontainer/Fav must follow the finger continuously.\n\nUP:\nprogress increases\n\nDOWN:\nprogress decreases\n\nDo NOT revert to:\ngesture -> toggle -> animation\n\n==================================================\n3. ONE PROGRESS\n==================================================\n\nKeep exactly one:\n\nexpansionProgress 0f..1f\n\n0f:\nCOLLAPSED\n\n1f:\nEXPANDED\n\nNo second progress.\nNo second Animatable.\n\n==================================================\n4. PULL FEEL\n==================================================\n\nMake the drag feel softer/heavier.\n\nDo not map raw drag 1:1 if current result feels too rigid.\n\nUse a small resistance factor only during direct drag.\n\nPreferred starting point:\n\ndrag response about 0.88x\n\nDo not affect final geometry.\n\n==================================================\n5. RELEASE\n==================================================\n\nAt release:\n\nuse existing:\nposition + velocity\n\nto choose target:\n\nCOLLAPSED\nor\nEXPANDED\n\nNo fixed-duration tween.\n\n==================================================\n6. SETTLE\n==================================================\n\nUse a softer official Compose spring preset.\n\nPreferred first test:\n\nSpring.DampingRatioLowBouncy\n+\nSpring.StiffnessMediumLow\n\nIf StiffnessMediumLow is unavailable in installed Compose:\n\nuse:\nSpring.StiffnessLow\n\nor nearest official preset.\n\nDo NOT hardcode custom damping/stiffness numbers unless required.\n\n==================================================\n7. TARGET FEEL\n==================================================\n\nDesired motion:\n\n- soft\n- slightly elastic\n- one subtle settle\n- no aggressive bounce\n- no abrupt stop\n- no rubber-band feel\n- no visible oscillation\n\n==================================================\n8. UP/DOWN SYMMETRY\n==================================================\n\nUP and DOWN must use the same motion language.\n\nUP:\nsoft pull + settle expanded\n\nDOWN:\nsoft pull + settle collapsed\n\nNo different animation engine per direction.\n\n==================================================\n9. NO OVERSHOOT GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nFinal progress bounds:\n\n0f..1f\n\nDo not let Fav/container visually overshoot far beyond\ncollapsed/expanded bounds.\n\nSmall spring settle is enough.\n\n==================================================\n10. INTERRUPTIBLE\n==================================================\n\nIf user starts a new drag while settle is running:\n\nstop current settle\ncontinue from current visual progress\n\nNo jump to old target first.\n\n==================================================\n11. NO EXTRA MOTION\n==================================================\n\nDo not add:\n\nalpha\nfade\nscale\ncrossfade\nAnimatedVisibility\ngraphicsLayer translationX\nblur\nparallax\nchild animations\n\n==================================================\n12. P1/P2/DOCK LOCK\n==================================================\n\nP1 movement:\n0\n\nP2 movement:\n0\n\nDock movement:\n0\n\nAlways.\n\n==================================================\n13. SEARCH SLOT LOCK\n==================================================\n\nSearchSlot final collapsed/expanded dimensions:\nUNCHANGED.\n\nOnly motion between those states changes.\n\n==================================================\n14. HAPTIC LOCK\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nExactly once when target state is accepted.\n\nMOVE haptic:\n0\n\nCANCEL haptic:\n0\n\n==================================================\n15. INPUT SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nTouch below touchSlop:\nnormal tap.\n\nP1/P2/Dock:\nfirst tap unchanged.\n\nNo new pointer layer.\n\n==================================================\n16. LEFT/RIGHT\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\nNO_OP\n\nRIGHT:\nNO_OP\n\nNo horizontal motion added.\n\n==================================================\n17. CODE-SECURITY POLICY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\n\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nCore isolation PASS\nInput ownership PASS\nMotion ownership PASS\nHaptic ownership PASS\nDebug build PASS\nR8 release PASS\n\n==================================================\n18. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 001 V2 SWIPE MOTION RETUNE COMPLETE\n\nCore logic modified: <NO/YES>\n\nGesture owners: <n>\nExpansion progress owners: <n>\nAnimation owners: <n>\n\nDrag resistance: <value>\n\nOld damping: <value>\nOld stiffness: <value>\n\nNew damping: <value>\nNew stiffness: <value>\n\nCustom spring constants: <n>\n\nUP pull: <YES/NO>\nDOWN pull: <YES/NO>\n\nInterruptible settle: <YES/NO>\n\nP1 movement: <dp>\nP2 movement: <dp>\nDock movement: <dp>\n\nSearchSlot geometry changed: <NO/YES>\n\nHaptic changed: <NO/YES>\nMOVE haptic paths: <n>\n\nHorizontal motion owners: <n>\nFirst-touch regression: <NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security: <PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug build: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8 release: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nDEVICE VALIDATION REQUIRED:\nYES"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:254:{"session_id":"01a01bb8-a362-7412-9ff8-6a60394d0a09","ts":1787181305,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — REDUCE MOTION AMPLITUDE ONLY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRidurre l'intensità visiva dello swipe UP/DOWN.\n\nNON rendere l'animazione più lenta.\nNON cambiare geometria finale.\nNON cambiare gesture ownership.\nNON cambiare haptic.\nNON cambiare P1/P2/Dock.\n\n==================================================\n1. KEEP CURRENT SPEED\n==================================================\n\nMantieni:\n\n- current release timing\n- current velocity handling\n- current state thresholds\n\nNon allungare la durata.\n\n==================================================\n2. REDUCE DRAG RESPONSE\n==================================================\n\nRidurre quanto il container segue il dito.\n\nSe ora è circa 0.72–0.88:\n\ntarget iniziale:\n\n0.55f–0.60f\n\nPreferred:\n0.58f\n\nQuindi il gesto resta reattivo,\nma il movimento visivo è più contenuto.\n\n==================================================\n3. REDUCE SETTLE AMPLITUDE\n==================================================\n\nUsare:\n\nSpring.DampingRatioNoBouncy\nSpring.StiffnessMedium\n\nNessun bounce visibile.\n\nIl settle deve solo accompagnare\ngli ultimi pochi dp verso il target.\n\n==================================================\n4. NO EXTRA OVERSHOOT\n==================================================\n\nOvershoot:\n0 preferred.\n\nNiente elasticità evidente.\n\n==================================================\n5. FINAL POSITIONS\n==================================================\n\nCOLLAPSED:\nUNCHANGED\n\nEXPANDED:\nUNCHANGED\n\nFav deve comunque raggiungere\nla posizione finale approvata.\n\nSi riduce solo la quantità di movimento percepita\ndurante il pull.\n\n==================================================\n6. FULL-CONTAINER SWIPE DOWN\n==================================================\n\nMantieni anche la correzione hitbox:\n\nswipe DOWN deve funzionare su tutto il container\nFav/SearchSlot/P1/P2,\n\nnon solo sull'ultima riga di P2.\n\nVertical gesture owners:\n1\n\n==================================================\n7. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nKEEP:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\n1 volta su transition accepted.\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 001 V2 REDUCED MOTION COMPLETE\n\nDrag response: <value>\n\nFinal geometry changed: NO\nTiming changed: NO\nVelocity logic changed: NO\n\nOvershoot: <0/other>\n\nSwipe DOWN full container: <YES/NO>\n\nP1 movement: 0\nP2 movement: 0\nDock movement: 0\n\nFirst-touch regression: <NONE/FOUND>\n\nDebug build: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8 release: <SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:255:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787194630,"text":"PATCH 002 V2 — HOME VISUAL GEOMETRY MATCH\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nREFERENCE:\n/opt/Android/Machina/references/home-ui-reference.png\n\nBASE:\nCore V2 STABLE CANDIDATE\n+ PATCH 001 V2 Fav Expansion\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\n==================================================\nOBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nMatch the visual language of the supplied reference image:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/references/home-ui-reference.png\n\nONLY use the image as visual reference.\n\nDO NOT recreate the screenshot.\nDO NOT copy its icons.\nDO NOT copy its wallpaper.\nDO NOT invent exact measurements from screenshot pixels.\n\nMatch the visible design characteristics:\n\n- dark container color\n- subtle borders\n- rounded corners\n- spacing/gaps\n- container proportions\n- Dock proportions\n- visual density\n- consistent padding\n\n==================================================\n1. PATCH SCOPE\n==================================================\n\nThis is VISUAL ONLY.\n\nDO NOT modify:\n\n- Core V2 logic\n- HomeSnapshot\n- AppCatalog\n- LauncherPreferences\n- LauncherActions\n- P1 slots\n- P2 slots\n- Dock slots\n- Fav Expansion state\n- swipe UP/DOWN recognition\n- expansion progress\n- haptic CONFIRM\n- animation spring\n- SearchSlot behavior\n\n==================================================\n2. REFERENCE CHARACTER\n==================================================\n\nThe supplied image shows:\n\n- very dark neutral surfaces\n- rounded rectangular containers\n- consistent radius language\n- narrow but visible gaps between sections\n- minimal/light outlining\n- flat surfaces\n- compact visual density\n- separate Dock surface\n- generous icon breathing room\n\nUse these characteristics.\n\n==================================================\n3. SINGLE VISUAL OWNER\n==================================================\n\nCreate one patch-local visual token owner.\n\nPreferred:\n\npatches/home_visual/\n    HomeVisualPatch.kt\n\nor equivalent existing patch architecture.\n\nAvoid spreading hardcoded values across Home composables.\n\n==================================================\n4. CONTAINER COLOR\n==================================================\n\nMain containers should use one shared dark-neutral surface tone.\n\nDo not use pure black unless the reference/available current\ndesign makes it necessary.\n\nTarget feel:\n\nnear-black\nneutral\nslightly separated from wallpaper\n\nFav may use its own wallpaper/visual treatment later,\nbut its structural surface must remain coherent.\n\n==================================================\n5. BORDERS\n==================================================\n\nReference has very subtle edge definition.\n\nUse:\n\nthin\nlow-contrast\nconsistent stroke\n\nTarget baseline:\n\napproximately 1dp visual stroke\n\nbut use the smallest value that visually matches\nthe supplied reference on-device.\n\nDo NOT use:\n\nbright outline\nwhite border\ndouble border\nglow\nheavy shadow\n\n==================================================\n6. CORNER LANGUAGE\n==================================================\n\nAll major containers should share one rounded-corner family.\n\nInclude:\n\nFav\nP1 container\nP2 container\nDock\n\nDo NOT give each panel unrelated radii.\n\nReference feel:\nlarge soft rounding,\nnot pill-shaped.\n\n==================================================\n7. GAP SYSTEM\n==================================================\n\nCreate one spacing/token system.\n\nRequired relationships:\n\nFav → P1:\nclear compact gap\n\nP1 → P2:\nsame or visually related gap\n\nP2 → Dock:\nslightly more separation if needed\n\nOuter horizontal margin:\nconsistent\n\nDo not use arbitrary per-container spacing.\n\n==================================================\n8. FAV POSITION\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 001 already controls Fav expansion.\n\nDO NOT rewrite that behavior.\n\nVisual patch may only adjust:\n\n- Fav surface shape\n- border\n- padding\n- color treatment\n- internal spacing\n\nFav expansion geometry/state:\nLOCKED.\n\n==================================================\n9. P1 / P2\n==================================================\n\nMaintain:\n\nP1 = 8\nP2 = 8\n\nIcon positions:\nsemantically unchanged.\n\nDo not change slot identities.\n\nAdjust only:\n\n- internal padding\n- row/column breathing room\n- container radius\n- surface color\n- border\n\nIcons must not feel cramped.\n\n==================================================\n10. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock should visually match the reference:\n\n- independent dark rounded surface\n- same radius family\n- compact vertical height\n- consistent horizontal padding\n- evenly spaced 5 icons\n- subtle border\n- no heavy elevation\n\nDock state/launch behavior:\nUNCHANGED.\n\n==================================================\n11. SHADOW\n==================================================\n\nReference is predominantly flat.\n\nPrefer:\n\nno shadow\nor extremely subtle shadow only if current Machina design\nrequires separation from wallpaper.\n\nDo not combine strong border + strong shadow.\n\n==================================================\n12. WALLPAPER\n==================================================\n\nSystem wallpaper handling:\nUNCHANGED.\n\nDo NOT:\n\nset wallpaper\ndecode new wallpaper\nadd wallpaper picker\nchange windowShowWallpaper\n\nThis patch concerns Home surfaces only.\n\n==================================================\n13. DIM\n==================================================\n\nExisting wallpaper dim:\nUNCHANGED unless current visual token is part of the patch.\n\nDo not animate dim.\n\nNo alpha changes during swipe.\n\n==================================================\n14. ICONS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT replace app artwork.\n\nKeep existing icon resolver.\n\nOnly adjust layout around icons if necessary.\n\nNo icon-pack logic changes.\n\n==================================================\n15. TYPOGRAPHY\n==================================================\n\nFav title/subtitle should retain current semantics.\n\nOnly adjust spacing/weight if needed to better match reference.\n\nDo not add:\nclock\ndate\nextra labels\nnew decorative text.\n\n==================================================\n16. SEARCH SLOT\n==================================================\n\nThe expanded empty area for future Search remains intact.\n\nDo not implement Search in this patch.\n\nDo not fill SearchSlot.\n\nDo not alter its behavior.\n\n==================================================\n17. MOTION LOCK\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 001 swipe motion:\nUNCHANGED.\n\nNo new:\n\nAnimatable\nspring\ntween\nfade\nscale\ntranslation\nAnimatedVisibility\n\nAnimation owners added:\n0\n\n==================================================\n18. HAPTIC LOCK\n==================================================\n\nExisting:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nUNCHANGED.\n\nNew haptic owners:\n0.\n\n==================================================\n19. TOKENIZATION\n==================================================\n\nPrefer patch-local tokens for:\n\nContainerColor\nBorderColor\nBorderWidth\nCornerRadius\nSectionGap\nOuterMargin\nContainerPadding\nDockPadding\n\nOne source of truth.\n\n==================================================\n20. CORE BOUNDARY\n==================================================\n\nCore logic touched:\n0\n\nCore UI hook:\nmax 1 if required by current patch architecture.\n\nNo direct writes to:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nLauncherPreferences\nAppCatalog\n\n==================================================\n21. REFERENCE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT derive \"exact\" dp values from raw screenshot pixels.\n\nInstead:\n\n1. inspect current layout\n2. use reference for proportions/visual relationships\n3. choose Android dp/sp values that reproduce the same feel\n4. document chosen values\n\n==================================================\n22. DEVICE TARGET\n==================================================\n\nOn Pixel:\n\nContainers should visibly resemble reference in:\n\n- rounding\n- darkness\n- border subtlety\n- spacing\n- density\n\nBut Core V2 behavior must be unchanged.\n\n==================================================\n23. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nValidate:\n\nCore isolation:\nPASS\n\nNew state owners:\n0\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nNew animation owners:\n0\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nNew persistence:\n0\n\nDirect HomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n24. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n25. PATCH DOC\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nPATCH_002_V2_HOME_VISUAL_GEOMETRY.md\n\nDocument:\n\n- reference path\n- selected tokens\n- files touched\n- core files touched\n- before/after values\n- rollback\n- code-security result\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 002 V2 HOME VISUAL GEOMETRY COMPLETE\n\nReference:\n/opt/Android/Machina/references/home-ui-reference.png\n\nVisual token owners: <n>\n\nContainer color: <value>\nBorder color: <value>\nBorder width: <value>\nCorner radius: <value>\n\nOuter margin: <value>\nFav → P1 gap: <value>\nP1 → P2 gap: <value>\nP2 → Dock gap: <value>\n\nP1 padding: <value>\nP2 padding: <value>\n\nDock height: <value>\nDock horizontal padding: <value>\nDock vertical padding: <value>\n\nP1 movement: 0\nP2 movement: 0\nDock movement: 0\n\nFav Expansion geometry changed: <NO/YES>\nSwipe motion changed: <NO/YES>\nHaptic changed: <NO/YES>\n\nNew state owners: <n>\nNew gesture owners: <n>\nNew animation owners: <n>\nNew persistence paths: <n>\n\nCore logic modified: <NO/YES>\nCore files touched: <n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPatch doc:\ndocs/PATCH_002_V2_HOME_VISUAL_GEOMETRY.md\n\nDEVICE VALIDATION REQUIRED:\nYES"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:256:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787202481,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — USE DEFAULT PIXEL / FOUNDATION VERTICAL MOTION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nPer swipe UP/DOWN usare il comportamento Foundation/Material\nstandard disponibile nella versione Compose installata.\n\nNON usare più spring custom per simulare il Pixel.\n\n==================================================\n1. KEEP EXISTING GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nNON modificare:\n\n- Fav collapsed bounds\n- Fav expanded bounds\n- SearchSlot\n- P1\n- P2\n- Dock\n- HomeSnapshot\n- persistence\n- haptic\n\nCambiare SOLO input/motion pipeline verticale.\n\n==================================================\n2. USE FOUNDATION SCROLL MOTION\n==================================================\n\nPreferire:\n\nModifier.scrollableArea(...)\n\nse compatibile con la struttura corrente.\n\nAltrimenti:\n\nModifier.scrollable(\n    state = ...,\n    orientation = Orientation.Vertical,\n    flingBehavior = ScrollableDefaults.flingBehavior(),\n    overscrollEffect = rememberOverscrollEffect()\n)\n\nsecondo API realmente disponibile.\n\n==================================================\n3. DEFAULT FLING\n==================================================\n\nUsare:\n\nScrollableDefaults.flingBehavior()\n\nNON:\n\nspring(...)\ntween(...)\ncustom decay\ncustom velocity curve\n\n==================================================\n4. DEFAULT OVERSCROLL\n==================================================\n\nUsare:\n\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\n\ndal LocalOverscrollFactory corrente.\n\nQuesto deve fornire il comportamento stretch standard\ndella piattaforma/Compose.\n\nNo custom wobble.\n\n==================================================\n5. SINGLE VERTICAL STATE\n==================================================\n\nMantenere un solo expansion progress:\n\n0f = collapsed\n1f = expanded\n\nLa scrollable state modifica solo questo progress.\n\nNo second Animatable.\n\n==================================================\n6. DRAG CONSUMPTION\n==================================================\n\nUP:\nconsume delta verso EXPANDED\n\nDOWN:\nconsume delta verso COLLAPSED\n\nIl container deve seguire il gesto in modo naturale.\n\nNon applicare coefficienti artificiali tipo:\n\n0.58\n0.72\n0.88\n\nse non strettamente richiesti.\n\nPartire dal comportamento Foundation reale.\n\n==================================================\n7. EDGE BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nQuando progress raggiunge:\n\n0f\noppure\n1f\n\nil delta residuo può alimentare\nrememberOverscrollEffect().\n\nQuindi al limite:\nMaterial stretch standard.\n\n==================================================\n8. RELEASE\n==================================================\n\nAl rilascio usare il default fling behavior.\n\nLa decisione collapsed/expanded può continuare a usare\nla soglia logica esistente,\n\nma il movimento deve derivare dal comportamento\nFoundation standard, non da una custom spring.\n\n==================================================\n9. FULL CONTAINER INPUT\n==================================================\n\nVertical gesture/input owner deve coprire:\n\nFav\nSearchSlot\nP1\nP2\n\nnon solo una parte di P2.\n\nOwner:\n1\n\nDock:\nfixed/outside.\n\n==================================================\n10. MATERIAL DEFAULT ONLY\n==================================================\n\nTarget:\n\ncustom spring paths = 0\ncustom tween paths = 0\ncustom damping constants = 0\ncustom stiffness constants = 0\ncustom drag-response constants = 0\n\nDefault fling owner = 1\nOverscrollEffect owner = 1\n\n==================================================\n11. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nKEEP:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nUna volta su transition accepted.\n\nMOVE:\n0.\n\n==================================================\n12. P1/P2/DOCK\n==================================================\n\nP1 movement:\n0\n\nP2 movement:\n0\n\nDock movement:\n0\n\n==================================================\n13. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nNo Core logic changes.\n\nNo new persistence.\n\nNo new lifecycle owner.\n\nNo new catalog owner.\n\n==================================================\n14. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 001 V2 DEFAULT FOUNDATION MOTION COMPLETE\n\nCompose Foundation version:\n<value>\n\nVertical primitive:\n<SCROLLABLE_AREA/SCROLLABLE/OTHER>\n\nDefault fling:\n<YES/NO>\n\nOverscroll API:\n<value>\n\nLocalOverscrollFactory used:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCustom spring paths:\n<n>\n\nCustom tween paths:\n<n>\n\nCustom damping/stiffness constants:\n<n>\n\nCustom drag-response constants:\n<n>\n\nVertical input owners:\n<n>\n\nSwipe DOWN full container:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nHaptic:\n<CONFIRM/OTHER>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:257:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787202970,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — FAV Z-ORDER / ANCHOR FIX ONLY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nKEEP:\n- default Foundation vertical motion\n- ScrollableDefaults.flingBehavior()\n- rememberOverscrollEffect()\n- haptic CONFIRM\n- P1/P2/Dock positions\n- SearchSlot\n- Core V2\n\nPROBLEM\n\nDuring swipe UP, Fav Apps rises underneath / behind\nthe main container.\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFav must always remain visually ABOVE the main container.\n\n==================================================\n1. Z ORDER\n==================================================\n\nFav:\ntop visual layer\n\nMain container:\nbelow Fav\n\nUse proper Compose drawing order / zIndex if required.\n\nDo NOT solve with alpha.\n\n==================================================\n2. ANCHOR\n==================================================\n\nFav top position may move upward.\n\nFav bottom must remain logically connected to SearchSlot.\n\nThe main container must extend beneath it,\nnot cover it.\n\n==================================================\n3. EXPANDED LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nCOLLAPSED:\n\nFav\nsmall gap\nP1/P2\n\nEXPANDED:\n\nFav moved further UP\nlarger SearchSlot below Fav\nP1/P2 unchanged\n\n==================================================\n4. NO OVERLAP\n==================================================\n\nAt every expansionProgress value:\n\nFav bounds must not be obscured by:\n- P1 container\n- P2 container\n- parent background\n- clipping layer\n\nOverlap/clipping paths:\n0\n\n==================================================\n5. CLIPPING\n==================================================\n\nAudit parent modifiers:\n\nclip()\nclipToBounds()\ngraphicsLayer(clip = true)\n\nIf a parent clips Fav during upward movement,\nmove clipping to the correct child/container.\n\nDo not remove clipping required for rounded surfaces.\n\n==================================================\n6. DRAW ORDER\n==================================================\n\nPreferred:\n\nBackground\n→ Main container\n→ P1/P2\n→ SearchSlot\n→ Fav\n\nor equivalent structure where Fav is drawn last/on top.\n\n==================================================\n7. MOTION LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nvertical gesture pipeline\nfling\noverscroll\nvelocity\nthreshold\nanimation timing\n\nMotion feeling:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n8. STATIC ELEMENTS\n==================================================\n\nP1 movement:\n0\n\nP2 movement:\n0\n\nDock movement:\n0\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH SLOT\n==================================================\n\nSearchSlot grows BELOW Fav.\n\nFav must never move \"inside\" the SearchSlot visually.\n\n==================================================\n10. OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA FAV ANCHOR FIX COMPLETE\n\nFav z-order: <TOP/FAILED>\nFav clipping paths: <n>\nFav overlap with main container: <NONE/FOUND>\n\nMotion changed: NO\n\nP1 movement: 0\nP2 movement: 0\nDock movement: 0\n\nDebug build: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8 release: <SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:258:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787203262,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — FAV REAL LAYOUT POSITION FIX\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nPROBLEM\n\nDuring swipe UP, Fav visually moves upward\nbut ends up underneath / inside the main container.\n\nPrevious zIndex/clipping fix did not solve it.\n\nROOT CAUSE TO VERIFY\n\nFav is likely being moved using visual offset/translation\ninstead of real layout geometry.\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFav must move through REAL layout positioning.\n\nDo NOT visually translate Fav over a fixed layout.\n\n==================================================\n1. AUDIT CURRENT FAV MOTION\n==================================================\n\nFind every use affecting Fav:\n\noffset(...)\nabsoluteOffset(...)\ngraphicsLayer.translationY\ntranslationY\nModifier.layout\nplaceRelative\nplace\npadding driven by progress\n\nReport exact current implementation.\n\n==================================================\n2. FORBID VISUAL TRANSLATION\n==================================================\n\nFav vertical movement must NOT use:\n\ngraphicsLayer.translationY\ntranslationY\nvisual-only offset\n\nTarget:\nvisual translation paths for Fav = 0\n\n==================================================\n3. REAL LAYOUT MODEL\n==================================================\n\nUse one real layout structure:\n\nTOP:\nFav\n\nMIDDLE:\nSearchSlot / expandable spacer\n\nBOTTOM:\nP1/P2 fixed section\n\nDuring expansion:\n\nFav top moves upward through actual layout coordinates\n\nSearchSlot height increases\n\nP1/P2 position stays fixed\n\n==================================================\n4. BOTTOM ANCHOR\n==================================================\n\nAnchor the P1/P2 section to its existing bottom position.\n\nExpansion must be calculated upward from that fixed anchor.\n\nConcept:\n\nfixedBottom = current P1/P2 bottom\n\nexpandedTop =\nfixedBottom\n- P1P2Height\n- SearchSlotExpandedHeight\n- FavHeight\n- gaps\n\ncollapsedTop =\nfixedBottom\n- P1P2Height\n- SearchSlotCollapsedHeight\n- FavHeight\n- gaps\n\n==================================================\n5. FAV AND SEARCH SLOT\n==================================================\n\nFav and SearchSlot must be siblings in the same real layout flow.\n\nFav must NOT be drawn inside the P1/P2 container bounds.\n\nStructure conceptually:\n\nColumn / custom Layout:\n\nFav\nSpacer(SearchSlotHeight)\nP1\nP2\n\nwith bottom anchoring for the whole upper group.\n\n==================================================\n6. NO OVERLAP BY CONSTRUCTION\n==================================================\n\nDo not rely on zIndex to prevent overlap.\n\nGeometry itself must guarantee:\n\nFav.bottom <= SearchSlot.top/bounds relationship\nSearchSlot.bottom <= P1.top\n\nAt every progress value.\n\n==================================================\n7. P1/P2 FIXED\n==================================================\n\nP1 y-position:\nconstant\n\nP2 y-position:\nconstant\n\nDuring full progress 0f..1f:\n\ndelta P1 = 0dp\ndelta P2 = 0dp\n\n==================================================\n8. DOCK FIXED\n==================================================\n\nDock:\ncompletely outside this layout animation.\n\ndelta Dock = 0dp\n\n==================================================\n9. PROGRESS\n==================================================\n\nKeep the existing single expansion progress.\n\nDo NOT add state.\n\nprogress 0f:\ncollapsed geometry\n\nprogress 1f:\nexpanded geometry\n\nUse progress to interpolate SearchSlot/layout dimensions,\nnot visual translation.\n\n==================================================\n10. DEFAULT FOUNDATION MOTION LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nScrollableDefaults.flingBehavior()\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\nvertical input owner\nvelocity handling\ntouch slop\nhaptic CONFIRM\n\nThe motion feel is already approved.\n\n==================================================\n11. PARENT SIZE\n==================================================\n\nEnsure the parent has enough real height for expanded state.\n\nIf current parent height is fixed to collapsed bounds,\nmake the actual upper layout height expansion-aware.\n\nDo not draw Fav outside parent bounds.\n\n==================================================\n12. CLIP\n==================================================\n\nAfter real layout correction:\n\nFav must remain inside valid parent bounds.\n\nNo need for clipping hacks.\n\nRounded clipping applies only to the visual Fav card itself.\n\n==================================================\n13. HIT TESTING\n==================================================\n\nBecause Fav now moves via layout:\n\nits touch bounds must move with it.\n\nNo invisible old hitbox.\n\nNo translated visual / stale clickable mismatch.\n\n==================================================\n14. SEARCH SLOT\n==================================================\n\nSearchSlot is the element that changes size.\n\nCollapsed:\nsmall/zero reserved area\n\nExpanded:\nlarger area\n\nFav remains above it.\n\nP1 begins after it.\n\n==================================================\n15. STATIC ASSERTIONS\n==================================================\n\nAt progress:\n\n0.0\n0.25\n0.50\n0.75\n1.0\n\nverify bounds:\n\nFav\nSearchSlot\nP1\nP2\n\nFor every sample:\n\nFav overlap P1 = false\nFav overlap P2 = false\nSearchSlot overlap P1 = false\n\n==================================================\n16. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nNo core state writes.\nNo persistence writes.\nNo new gesture owner.\nNo new animation owner.\nNo new lifecycle owner.\n\n==================================================\n17. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA FAV REAL LAYOUT FIX COMPLETE\n\nPrevious Fav motion implementation:\n<OFFSET/TRANSLATION/LAYOUT/OTHER>\n\nFav visual translation paths after:\n<n>\n\nFav real layout positioning:\n<YES/NO>\n\nExpansion changes SearchSlot/layout size:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1 delta:\n<dp>\n\nP2 delta:\n<dp>\n\nDock delta:\n<dp>\n\nFav overlap at progress 0.00:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFav overlap at progress 0.25:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFav overlap at progress 0.50:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFav overlap at progress 0.75:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFav overlap at progress 1.00:\n<YES/NO>\n\nTouch bounds follow Fav:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFoundation motion changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHaptic changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:259:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787203658,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — FAV MUST BE FIXED / EXPAND BELOW ONLY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nPROBLEM\n\nFav moves upward during swipe UP\nand ends up underneath/inside the container.\n\nTHIS IS WRONG.\n\nFINAL REQUIRED BEHAVIOR\n\nFav position:\nFIXED ALWAYS.\n\nDuring swipe UP:\n\nFav does NOT move.\n\nOnly the expandable area BELOW Fav changes height.\n\n==================================================\n1. REMOVE ALL FAV MOTION\n==================================================\n\nFind and remove every progress-driven modification of Fav:\n\noffset\ntranslationY\ngraphicsLayer.translationY\nanimated top\nanimated padding\nanimated y placement\nprogress-derived position\n\nTarget:\n\nFav y-position writes from expansion = 0\n\n==================================================\n2. FAV FIXED ANCHOR\n==================================================\n\nFav top:\nconstant\n\nFav bottom:\nconstant\n\nFav bounds:\nidentical at progress:\n\n0.0\n0.25\n0.50\n0.75\n1.0\n\n==================================================\n3. EXPANSION OWNER\n==================================================\n\nOnly this area changes:\n\nSearchSlot / expandable spacer BELOW Fav.\n\nprogress 0f:\nsmall/minimum height\n\nprogress 1f:\nexpanded height\n\n==================================================\n4. P1/P2/DOCK\n==================================================\n\nP1:\nfixed\n\nP2:\nfixed\n\nDock:\nfixed\n\nTherefore the expandable area must grow into the available\nspace between Fav and P1.\n\n==================================================\n5. LAYOUT MODEL\n==================================================\n\nUse real layout:\n\nFav [FIXED]\n\nExpandableSearchSlot [ANIMATED HEIGHT]\n\nP1 [FIXED]\nP2 [FIXED]\n\nDock [FIXED OUTSIDE]\n\nDo NOT move Fav to create SearchSlot.\n\n==================================================\n6. PARENT GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nIf there is not enough room:\n\nthe parent/container must extend upward/downward appropriately\nWITHOUT changing Fav coordinates.\n\nDo not solve by translating Fav.\n\n==================================================\n7. SWIPE MOTION\n==================================================\n\nKeep existing approved Foundation vertical motion.\n\nSwipe UP:\nincreases SearchSlot height.\n\nSwipe DOWN:\ndecreases SearchSlot height.\n\nFav coordinates:\nunchanged.\n\n==================================================\n8. MATERIAL MOTION\n==================================================\n\nKEEP current:\n\nFoundation vertical primitive\nScrollableDefaults.flingBehavior()\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\n\nDo not change motion feel.\n\n==================================================\n9. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nKEEP:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nOne accepted transition = one feedback.\n\n==================================================\n10. TOUCH BOUNDS\n==================================================\n\nFav touch bounds:\nconstant.\n\nP1/P2/Dock:\nconstant.\n\nNo stale or translated hitbox.\n\n==================================================\n11. STATIC ASSERTIONS\n==================================================\n\nMeasure bounds at progress:\n\n0.00\n0.25\n0.50\n0.75\n1.00\n\nRequired:\n\nFav.top:\nIDENTICAL\n\nFav.bottom:\nIDENTICAL\n\nP1.top:\nIDENTICAL\n\nP2.top:\nIDENTICAL\n\nDock.top:\nIDENTICAL\n\nOnly SearchSlot height changes.\n\n==================================================\n12. REMOVE OLD WRONG LOGIC\n==================================================\n\nDelete confirmed old paths whose purpose was:\n\nFav rises on expand\nFav follows progress vertically\nFav translation\nFav top interpolation\n\nDo not leave compatibility code.\n\n==================================================\n13. CORE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nCore logic modified:\nNO\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nPersistence writes:\n0\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nNew state owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n14. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA FAV FIXED EXPANSION COMPLETE\n\nFav progress-driven position paths removed: <n>\n\nFav.top progress 0.00: <value>\nFav.top progress 0.25: <value>\nFav.top progress 0.50: <value>\nFav.top progress 0.75: <value>\nFav.top progress 1.00: <value>\n\nFav position invariant:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearchSlot animated height:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1 position invariant:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP2 position invariant:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock position invariant:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFoundation motion changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHaptic changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:260:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787204020,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — EXPANSION MAX-BOUND FIX\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nCURRENT GOOD STATE:\n\nFav position:\nFIXED\n\nP1:\nFIXED\n\nP2:\nFIXED\n\nDock:\nFIXED\n\nOnly SearchSlot/container height changes.\n\nPROBLEM:\n\nDuring swipe UP the expandable container reaches/passes\na lower visual limit.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nClamp expansion to the real available space.\n\n==================================================\n1. REAL MAX HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nCalculate:\n\nmaxSearchSlotHeight\n\nfrom actual layout bounds.\n\nConcept:\n\navailableSpace =\nP1.top\n- Fav.bottom\n- requiredGap\n\nSearchSlot height must never exceed availableSpace.\n\n==================================================\n2. NO HARDCODED SCREEN COORDINATES\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT use:\n\nPixel-specific y coordinates\nscreen-height magic numbers\nfixed absolute bottom values\n\nUse measured layout bounds / constraints.\n\n==================================================\n3. CLAMP PROGRESS\n==================================================\n\nExpansion progress:\n\n0f..1f\n\nMapped height:\n\nlerp(\n    collapsedSearchSlotHeight,\n    maxSearchSlotHeight,\n    progress\n)\n\nAlways clamp result.\n\n==================================================\n4. LOWER LIMIT\n==================================================\n\nSearchSlot.bottom must always remain ABOVE P1.top\nwith the approved gap.\n\nRequired:\n\nSearchSlot.bottom + gap <= P1.top\n\nat every progress value.\n\n==================================================\n5. FAV FIXED\n==================================================\n\nFav.top:\nconstant\n\nFav.bottom:\nconstant\n\nNo movement.\n\n==================================================\n6. P1/P2/DOCK FIXED\n==================================================\n\nP1 delta:\n0dp\n\nP2 delta:\n0dp\n\nDock delta:\n0dp\n\n==================================================\n7. OVERSCROLL\n==================================================\n\nMaterial/overscroll may visually stretch slightly at the edge,\nbut actual layout height must remain clamped.\n\nDo not let overscroll mutate real SearchSlot bounds.\n\n==================================================\n8. SWIPE DOWN\n==================================================\n\nCollapse from anywhere in valid vertical gesture area.\n\nHeight reduces back toward collapsed target.\n\nNo negative height.\n\n==================================================\n9. DEVICE-SAFE INSETS\n==================================================\n\nRespect:\n\nstatus bar\ndisplay cutout\nnavigation gesture area\n\nDo not let expanded container enter forbidden system UI bounds.\n\n==================================================\n10. STATIC ASSERTIONS\n==================================================\n\nAt progress:\n\n0.00\n0.25\n0.50\n0.75\n1.00\n\nreport:\n\nFav.bottom\nSearchSlot.top\nSearchSlot.bottom\nP1.top\ngap\n\nRequired:\n\noverlap = 0\n\n==================================================\n11. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nNo Core logic changes.\nNo new state owner.\nNo new gesture owner.\nNo persistence.\nNo HomeSnapshot writes.\n\n==================================================\n12. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA SEARCH SLOT MAX-BOUND FIX COMPLETE\n\nMax available height: <dp>\nCollapsed height: <dp>\nExpanded height: <dp>\n\nFav position invariant: <YES/NO>\nP1 position invariant: <YES/NO>\nP2 position invariant: <YES/NO>\nDock position invariant: <YES/NO>\n\nSearchSlot overlap P1: <NONE/FOUND>\nSystem inset violation: <NONE/FOUND>\n\nMotion changed: <NO/YES>\nHaptic changed: <NO/YES>\n\nDebug build: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8 release: <SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:261:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787204473,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — CONTAINER ABOVE WALLPAPER FIX\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nPROBLEM\n\nDuring expansion, the Fav/Search container visually goes\nunder the wallpaper layer.\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFix only visual layer ordering / parent clipping.\n\nDO NOT change:\n- Core V2 logic\n- expansion progress\n- swipe UP/DOWN behavior\n- Foundation motion\n- haptic\n- P1/P2/Dock positions\n- SearchSlot max height\n- wallpaper source\n\n==================================================\n1. FINAL DRAW ORDER\n==================================================\n\nRequired layer order:\n\n1. SYSTEM WALLPAPER\n2. PATCH003 wallpaper dim overlay\n3. Main Home surfaces\n4. P1/P2\n5. SearchSlot / expandable container\n6. Fav\n7. interactive foreground content\n\nWallpaper must always be the lowest layer.\n\n==================================================\n2. AUDIT CURRENT LAYERS\n==================================================\n\nFind:\n\nBox\nSurface\ndrawBehind\ndrawWithContent\nbackground\nzIndex\ngraphicsLayer\nclip\nclipToBounds\n\nReport which layer currently owns:\n\n- wallpaper visibility\n- dim\n- Home container\n- SearchSlot\n- Fav\n\n==================================================\n3. WALLPAPER MUST NOT OVERDRAW UI\n==================================================\n\nNo draw call related to wallpaper/dim may happen\nafter Home content drawing.\n\nIf using drawWithContent:\n\ncontent must be drawn AFTER wallpaper/dim background,\nnot before.\n\nPrefer:\n\nbackground/dim\n→ content\n\nnot:\n\ncontent\n→ wallpaper/dim\n\n==================================================\n4. EXPANDABLE CONTAINER LAYER\n==================================================\n\nSearchSlot/container must remain in normal foreground layout.\n\nDo not place it inside:\n\nwallpaper Box\nbackground drawing layer\nbehind-content modifier\n\n==================================================\n5. Z-ORDER\n==================================================\n\nIf explicit zIndex is needed:\n\nWallpaper/dim:\nlowest\n\nMain container:\nabove wallpaper\n\nSearchSlot:\nabove main container\n\nFav:\ntop of expansion group\n\nUse minimal zIndex values.\n\nDo not create many arbitrary layers.\n\n==================================================\n6. CLIPPING\n==================================================\n\nAudit parent clipping.\n\nSearchSlot/Fav must not be clipped by the wallpaper/background parent.\n\nRounded clipping should apply only to the visual container\nthat actually needs rounded corners.\n\n==================================================\n7. REAL LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\nFav fixed\nP1 fixed\nP2 fixed\nDock fixed\n\nOnly SearchSlot height changes.\n\nNo offset/translation workaround.\n\n==================================================\n8. WALLPAPER CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nSystem wallpaper remains:\n\nwindowShowWallpaper = true\n\nPATCH003 dim remains static.\n\nDo NOT:\n- duplicate wallpaper bitmap\n- create local wallpaper layer\n- add Image filling screen\n- change window background\n\n==================================================\n9. STATIC ASSERTION\n==================================================\n\nAt progress:\n\n0.00\n0.25\n0.50\n0.75\n1.00\n\nverify:\n\nSearchSlot visible above wallpaper = YES\nFav visible above wallpaper = YES\nP1/P2 visible above wallpaper = YES\n\nWallpaper overdraw over Home UI = NO\n\n==================================================\n10. MOTION LOCK\n==================================================\n\nFoundation vertical motion:\nUNCHANGED\n\nScrollableDefaults.flingBehavior():\nUNCHANGED\n\nrememberOverscrollEffect():\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n11. HAPTIC LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCONFIRM haptic:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n12. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nNo new state.\nNo new gesture owner.\nNo new animation owner.\nNo persistence changes.\nNo HomeSnapshot writes.\nNo core logic changes.\n\n==================================================\n13. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA WALLPAPER LAYER FIX COMPLETE\n\nWallpaper layer owner:\n<value>\n\nDim layer owner:\n<value>\n\nSearchSlot layer:\n<value>\n\nFav layer:\n<value>\n\nWallpaper overdraw paths:\n<n>\n\nSearchSlot below wallpaper paths:\n<n>\n\nFav below wallpaper paths:\n<n>\n\nClipping conflicts:\n<n>\n\nMotion changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHaptic changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1 movement:\n0\n\nP2 movement:\n0\n\nDock movement:\n0\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:262:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787204825,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — GLOBAL MICRO SWIPE FEEDBACK\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRimuovere completamente il movimento geometrico del container.\n\nNessun elemento deve:\n\n- salire\n- scendere\n- cambiare altezza\n- cambiare top/bottom\n- cambiare posizione\n\nGli swipe devono produrre soltanto\nun piccolo feedback Material globale.\n\n==================================================\n1. FINAL GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nFav:\nFIXED\n\nSearchSlot:\nFIXED\n\nP1:\nFIXED\n\nP2:\nFIXED\n\nDock:\nFIXED\n\nMain container:\nFIXED\n\nProgress-driven layout movement:\n0\n\n==================================================\n2. REMOVE VERTICAL EXPANSION\n==================================================\n\nRimuovere dalla patch:\n\n- Fav vertical movement\n- SearchSlot height animation\n- container height animation\n- top interpolation\n- bottom interpolation\n- expanded/collapsed geometry movement\n\nSe esistono state usati solo per questo:\nrimuoverli.\n\n==================================================\n3. GLOBAL SWIPE RESPONSE\n==================================================\n\nGli swipe:\n\nUP\nDOWN\nLEFT\nRIGHT\n\nnon navigano e non cambiano layout.\n\nProducono solo un piccolo feedback visivo\nsulla superficie Home.\n\n==================================================\n4. MATERIAL / FOUNDATION FEEL\n==================================================\n\nUsare la stessa famiglia di feedback Material/Foundation\ngià approvata.\n\nPreferire:\n\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\n\ncon una source di gesture corretta.\n\nNON creare:\n\ncustom spring\ncustom wobble\ncustom scale animation\ncustom translation\n\n==================================================\n5. MICRO RESPONSE\n==================================================\n\nL'effetto deve essere molto contenuto.\n\nTarget:\n\n- percepibile\n- breve\n- morbido\n- nessuna grande deformazione\n- nessun movimento del layout\n\nDeve sembrare un piccolo \"touch\" della superficie.\n\n==================================================\n6. FULL DISPLAY / GLOBAL OWNER\n==================================================\n\nUn solo owner globale della Home.\n\nIl feedback deve poter partire da:\n\nFav\nSearchSlot\nP1\nP2\n\nsenza creare gesture owner separati.\n\nDock può restare escluso se serve per preservare i tap.\n\n==================================================\n7. NO LAYOUT WRITES\n==================================================\n\nDurante swipe:\n\nFav bounds writes = 0\nSearchSlot bounds writes = 0\nP1 bounds writes = 0\nP2 bounds writes = 0\nDock bounds writes = 0\nContainer bounds writes = 0\n\n==================================================\n8. NO NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nUP:\nNO navigation\n\nDOWN:\nNO navigation\n\nLEFT:\nNO navigation\n\nRIGHT:\nNO navigation\n\nHome remains Home.\n\n==================================================\n9. TAP SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nTouch sotto touchSlop:\ntap normale.\n\nP1:\nfirst tap launch\n\nP2:\nfirst tap launch\n\nDock:\nfirst tap launch\n\nFav:\nnormal interaction\n\nNo global overlay that consumes DOWN immediately.\n\n==================================================\n10. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nUsare:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nSolo quando uno swipe viene realmente accettato.\n\nUna volta.\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\nCANCEL:\n0\n\n==================================================\n11. NO SEARCH BEHAVIOR YET\n==================================================\n\nSearch UI:\nNOT IMPLEMENTED in this patch.\n\nSearchSlot:\nstatic placeholder only.\n\nNo keyboard.\nNo focus.\nNo history.\n\n==================================================\n12. REMOVE OLD MOTION\n==================================================\n\nRimuovere tutti i confirmed legacy paths relativi a:\n\nvertical expansion\nFav offset\nSearchSlot animated height\ncontainer growth\nspring settle\nexpanded/collapsed layout state\n\nNon lasciare compatibility code.\n\n==================================================\n13. STATE TARGET\n==================================================\n\nPatch state owners:\n0 preferred\n\nSe serve solo stato transient per gesture:\n1 massimo\n\nNo persistent state.\n\n==================================================\n14. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nCore logic modified: NO\nHomeSnapshot writes: 0\nPersistence writes: 0\nNew catalog owners: 0\nNew lifecycle owners: 0\nDuplicate gesture owners: 0\nFirst-touch blockers: 0\n\n==================================================\n15. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 001 V2 GLOBAL MICRO SWIPE COMPLETE\n\nFav movement: 0\nSearchSlot movement: 0\nP1 movement: 0\nP2 movement: 0\nDock movement: 0\nContainer movement: 0\n\nLayout animation owners: <n>\nGlobal swipe owners: <n>\n\nUP navigation: 0\nDOWN navigation: 0\nLEFT navigation: 0\nRIGHT navigation: 0\n\nMaterial/Foundation feedback:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCustom spring paths: <n>\nCustom translation paths: <n>\nCustom scale paths: <n>\n\nHaptic:\n<CONFIRM/OTHER>\n\nMOVE haptic paths: <n>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCore logic modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:263:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787205327,"text":"TEST PATCH — STATIC CONTAINER EXPANSION ONLY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2 + current visual patches\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nProvare SOLO una geometria Home con container più lungo.\n\nNO swipe.\nNO gesture.\nNO animation.\nNO haptic change.\nNO Search logic yet.\n\n==================================================\n1. STATIC EXPANSION\n==================================================\n\nAllungare staticamente il container Home verso l'alto\nper creare più spazio tra Fav e P1.\n\nFav:\nFIXED\n\nP1:\nFIXED\n\nP2:\nFIXED\n\nDock:\nFIXED\n\n==================================================\n2. SEARCH SLOT\n==================================================\n\nAumentare staticamente lo spazio destinato alla futura Search.\n\nSearchSlot:\nVISIBLE AS EMPTY SPACE ONLY\n\nNO:\nTextField\nkeyboard\nhistory\nresults\nfocus\n\n==================================================\n3. NO MOTION\n==================================================\n\nTemporaneamente disabilitare SOLO per questo test:\n\nswipe UP\nswipe DOWN\nvertical draggable\nfling\noverscroll-driven expansion\n\nDo not delete implementation permanently.\n\nUse a reversible test flag/local branch if possible.\n\n==================================================\n4. NO ELEMENT MOVEMENT\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nFav delta = 0dp\nP1 delta = 0dp\nP2 delta = 0dp\nDock delta = 0dp\n\nOnly container/SearchSlot available area changes.\n\n==================================================\n5. TARGET\n==================================================\n\nAumentare lo spazio in modo chiaramente visibile,\nma senza arrivare sotto Fav o sovrapporre P1.\n\nPreferire inizialmente:\n\n+48dp rispetto all'attuale SearchSlot\n\nIf current layout constraints make this invalid,\nuse the maximum safe increase and report it.\n\n==================================================\n6. VISUALS\n==================================================\n\nKeep unchanged:\n\ncontainer color\nborder\ncorner radius\ngaps\nDock style\nsystem wallpaper\ndim\nshadow\n\n==================================================\n7. CORE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nNo changes to:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nAppCatalog\nLauncherPreferences\nLauncherActions\nslot counts\nlifecycle\n\n==================================================\n8. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA STATIC CONTAINER EXPANSION TEST READY\n\nPrevious SearchSlot height: <dp>\nTest SearchSlot height: <dp>\nIncrease: <dp>\n\nFav movement: <dp>\nP1 movement: <dp>\nP2 movement: <dp>\nDock movement: <dp>\n\nSwipe UP active: NO\nSwipe DOWN active: NO\nAnimation active: NO\n\nOverlap detected: <NONE/FOUND>\nCore logic modified: <NO/YES>\n\nDebug build: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8 release: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nTEST ONLY:\nYES"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:265:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787205671,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — FAV LIFT ONLY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2 STABLE CANDIDATE\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nImplementare UNA SOLA funzione:\n\nSWIPE UP\n→ Fav sale rispetto a P1\n→ aumenta il gap Fav → P1\n\nNient'altro.\n\nNO Search.\nNO swipe DOWN.\nNO wallpaper animation.\nNO Settings.\nNO container resize complesso.\n\n==================================================\n1. FIXED ELEMENTS\n==================================================\n\nP1:\nFIXED\n\nP2:\nFIXED\n\nDock:\nFIXED\n\nFav:\nunico elemento che può muoversi verticalmente.\n\n==================================================\n2. SWIPE UP\n==================================================\n\nUn solo gesture owner verticale.\n\nDa stato BASE:\n\nswipe UP valido\n→ Fav sale.\n\nLEFT:\nNO_OP\n\nRIGHT:\nNO_OP\n\nDOWN:\nNO_OP per questa prima versione.\n\n==================================================\n3. FAV TRAVEL\n==================================================\n\nFav deve salire di poco.\n\nStarting target:\n24dp\n\nSe sul device è troppo:\nridurre.\n\nSe è troppo poco:\naumentare in una patch successiva.\n\nNON superare 32dp nella baseline.\n\n==================================================\n4. REAL LAYOUT POSITION\n==================================================\n\nFav deve cambiare posizione reale nel layout.\n\nNON usare:\n\ngraphicsLayer.translationY\nvisual-only translation\nalpha tricks\n\nTouch bounds devono seguire Fav.\n\n==================================================\n5. GAP\n==================================================\n\nFav → P1 gap:\n\nBASE:\ncurrent value\n\nAFTER UP:\ncurrent value + Fav travel\n\nP1 non deve spostarsi.\n\n==================================================\n6. MOTION\n==================================================\n\nDurante drag:\n\nFav segue il dito verticalmente.\n\nRelease:\n\nusa comportamento Compose/Foundation standard.\n\nPreferire:\n\nScrollableDefaults.flingBehavior()\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\n\noppure primitive Foundation equivalenti disponibili.\n\nNO custom spring.\nNO custom tween.\nNO custom damping/stiffness.\n\n==================================================\n7. STATE\n==================================================\n\nUn solo state patch-local:\n\nBASE\nLIFTED\n\noppure progress 0f..1f.\n\nNon aggiungere altro.\n\nPersistence:\n0\n\n==================================================\n8. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nQuando BASE → LIFTED viene accettato:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nUna volta.\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\nCANCEL:\n0\n\n==================================================\n9. FIRST TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nTouch sotto touchSlop:\ntap normale.\n\nP1/P2/Dock:\nfirst tap unchanged.\n\nFav:\ntouch bounds corretti dopo il lift.\n\n==================================================\n10. CORE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nNo writes to:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nLauncherPreferences\nAppCatalog\nP1/P2/Dock state\n\nCore logic modified:\nNO\n\n==================================================\n11. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nNew gesture owners:\n1 max\n\nNew animation owners:\n1 max\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nPersistence writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n12. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 001 V2 FAV LIFT COMPLETE\n\nFav travel:\n<dp>\n\nFav real-layout movement:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nFav→P1 gap before:\n<dp>\n\nFav→P1 gap after:\n<dp>\n\nVertical gesture owners:\n<n>\n\nSwipe UP:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSwipe DOWN:\n<NO/YES>\n\nLEFT actions:\n<n>\n\nRIGHT actions:\n<n>\n\nHaptic:\n<CONFIRM/OTHER>\n\nMOVE haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCore logic modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:266:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787205851,"text":"FASE: MACHINA — MINI CODE AUDIT\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nSCOPE:\nCore V2\n+ PATCH 001 V2 Fav Lift\n\nMODE:\nREAD-ONLY\n\nNON modificare:\n- Kotlin\n- Manifest\n- Gradle\n- resources\n- docs\n- projectctl\n\nNON fare cleanup.\nNON fare refactor.\nNON applicare fix.\n\nOBIETTIVO\n\nVerificare rapidamente che il codice resti semplice,\nisolato e sano prima di continuare.\n\n==================================================\n1. CORE BOUNDARY\n==================================================\n\nVerificare:\n\nCore logic modified by PATCH 001:\nNO preferred\n\nCore files touched:\n<= 1\n\nPatch files:\nminimal\n\nDirect writes from patch to:\nHomeSnapshot = 0\nLauncherPreferences = 0\nAppCatalog internals = 0\nP1/P2/Dock state = 0\n\n==================================================\n2. STATE OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nRiporta:\n\nHomeSnapshot owners\nCatalog owners\nFav Lift state owners\nExpansion/progress owners\n\nTarget:\n\nHomeSnapshot = 1\nCatalog = 1\nFav Lift state = 1\nDuplicate state = 0\n\n==================================================\n3. INPUT\n==================================================\n\nCerca:\n\npointerInput\ndraggable\nscrollable\nclickable\ncombinedClickable\nBackHandler\n\nTarget:\n\nvertical Fav gesture owner = 1\nduplicate gesture owner = 0\nP1/P2/Dock duplicate clickable = 0\nfirst-touch blocker = 0\n\n==================================================\n4. MOTION\n==================================================\n\nVerificare:\n\nFav motion owners\nAnimatable\nspring\ntween\ngraphicsLayer.translationY\noffset/translation paths\n\nTarget:\n\n1 motion owner max\n\nNo duplicate animation paths.\n\nSegnalare se Fav usa visual-only translation\nanziché layout reale.\n\n==================================================\n5. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nVerificare:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nTarget:\n\naccepted UP = 1\nMOVE = 0\nCANCEL = 0\nduplicate haptic path = 0\n\nNo:\nVibrator\nVibrationEffect\nVIBRATE permission\n\n==================================================\n6. GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nConfermare:\n\nFav movement only\n\nP1 delta = 0\nP2 delta = 0\nDock delta = 0\n\nFav touch bounds follow visual bounds:\nYES\n\nNo overlap/clipping risk.\n\n==================================================\n7. LIFECYCLE\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 001 deve introdurre:\n\nnew lifecycle owner = 0\nnew listener = 0\nnew onResume path = 0\nnew persistence = 0\n\nCore:\n\nsnapshot clear on resume = 0\ncatalog refresh on resume = 0\n\n==================================================\n8. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nVerificare:\n\nmain-thread heavy paths = 0\nbitmap decode during gesture = 0\nPackageManager calls during gesture = 0\nallocation-heavy frame path = 0 confirmed\n\n==================================================\n9. ERROR / CRASH CHECK\n==================================================\n\nCerca nella patch/core touched:\n\n!!\nunsafe index\nunsafe cast\ncatch(Throwable)\nunbounded coroutine\nlateinit misuse\n\nRiporta solo rischi plausibili.\n\n==================================================\n10. DEAD / LEGACY PATHS\n==================================================\n\nCerca eventuali residui:\n\nold Fav expansion\nold SearchSlot animation\nold container growth\nold swipe down path\nold motion retune\nlegacy wobble\n\nNON rimuoverli.\n\nConta e segnala.\n\n==================================================\n11. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nNon fare una nuova build se l'ultima build debug + R8\nè già SUCCESS e il source non è cambiato.\n\nSe source è cambiato dopo l'ultima build:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA MINI CODE AUDIT COMPLETE\n\nCore files touched by patch: <n>\nPatch files: <n>\n\nHomeSnapshot owners: <n>\nCatalog owners: <n>\nFav Lift state owners: <n>\nDuplicate state owners: <n>\n\nVertical gesture owners: <n>\nDuplicate gesture owners: <n>\nFirst-touch blockers: <n>\n\nMotion owners: <n>\nVisual-only Fav translation paths: <n>\nDuplicate animation paths: <n>\n\nHaptic owners: <n>\nMOVE haptic paths: <n>\nDuplicate haptic paths: <n>\n\nP1 movement: <dp>\nP2 movement: <dp>\nDock movement: <dp>\n\nLifecycle owners added: <n>\nPersistence writes added: <n>\nMain-thread heavy paths: <n>\n\nConfirmed crash paths: <n>\nLegacy motion paths: <n>\n\nCore isolation:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nInput safety:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nMotion ownership:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nHaptic ownership:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nOverall:\n<PASS / REVIEW_REQUIRED>\n\nBuild:\n<UNCHANGED_SUCCESS / SUCCESS / FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:267:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787206088,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — RESTORE CONTAINER BASELINE + MATERIAL MOTION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nDEVICE EVIDENCE:\ncurrent swipe UP moves the entire main container upward.\nThis is wrong.\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\n1. restore main container to the original approved baseline position\n2. keep P1/P2/Dock fixed\n3. restore Material/Foundation swipe motion\n4. remove geometry drift caused by swipe progress\n\n==================================================\n1. BASELINE GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nThe current Core V2 baseline position is authoritative.\n\nRestore:\n\nMain container top\nMain container bottom\nP1 position\nP2 position\nDock position\n\nto their original baseline coordinates/layout constraints.\n\nDo NOT derive a new baseline from current expanded state.\n\n==================================================\n2. NO CONTAINER TRANSLATION\n==================================================\n\nRemove any swipe-progress-driven:\n\ntranslationY\noffset\ngraphicsLayer.translationY\nanimated top\nanimated bottom\nanimated parent position\n\nfor the whole main container.\n\nTarget:\n\nmain container movement = 0dp\n\n==================================================\n3. FAV\n==================================================\n\nFav must remain inside the main Home geometry correctly.\n\nNo drawing under wallpaper.\nNo leaving parent bounds.\nNo container lift.\n\nIf Fav has a small approved local response,\nit must stay within its own bounds.\n\n==================================================\n4. P1 / P2\n==================================================\n\nP1:\n0dp movement\n\nP2:\n0dp movement\n\nAlways.\n\n==================================================\n5. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock:\n0dp movement\n\nNo resize.\nNo vertical shift.\n\n==================================================\n6. MATERIAL / FOUNDATION MOTION\n==================================================\n\nRestore the approved standard Compose/Foundation motion.\n\nPrefer current available APIs:\n\nScrollableDefaults.flingBehavior()\n\n+\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\n\nor the equivalent already validated in this project.\n\nDo NOT emulate with:\n\ncustom spring constants\ncustom tween\ncustom wobble\ncustom translation\ncustom scale\n\n==================================================\n7. SWIPE EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nSwipe UP/DOWN should produce only the standard Material/Foundation\nsurface response.\n\nThe visual effect may deform/stretch subtly,\nbut it must NOT change actual layout geometry.\n\n==================================================\n8. FULL HOME SURFACE\n==================================================\n\nUse one motion owner for the Home surface.\n\nNo separate motion owners for:\n\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\n==================================================\n9. LAYOUT VS EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nActual layout bounds:\nSTATIC\n\nMaterial overscroll visual effect:\nTRANSIENT\n\nDo not use overscroll progress as layout position.\n\n==================================================\n10. LEFT / RIGHT\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\nNO navigation\n\nRIGHT:\nNO navigation\n\nKeep current launcher contract.\n\n==================================================\n11. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nOnly once on accepted interaction if still required.\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\n==================================================\n12. FIRST TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nP1 first tap:\nPASS\n\nP2 first tap:\nPASS\n\nDock first tap:\nPASS\n\nNo full-screen pointer overlay consuming taps.\n\n==================================================\n13. REMOVE LEGACY MOTION PATHS\n==================================================\n\nAudit and remove confirmed old paths responsible for:\n\ncontainer lift\nFav lift\nlayout height animation\nprogress-driven y position\nold custom spring motion\n\nDo not leave duplicate motion engines.\n\n==================================================\n14. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nCore logic modified:\nNO\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nPersistence writes:\n0\n\nGesture owners:\n1 max\n\nMotion owners:\n1\n\nDuplicate animation paths:\n0\n\n==================================================\n15. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA CONTAINER BASELINE + MATERIAL MOTION RESTORED\n\nMain container movement:\n<dp>\n\nFav movement:\n<dp>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nLayout bounds driven by swipe:\n<NO/YES>\n\nFoundation motion owner:\n<n>\n\nDefault fling:\n<YES/NO>\n\nMaterial overscroll:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCustom spring paths:\n<n>\n\nCustom translation paths:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate motion paths:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nDEVICE VALIDATION REQUIRED:\nYES"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:268:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787206886,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — LIGHTER MATERIAL SWIPE EFFECT\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRendere più leggero e discreto il feedback Material\nsu swipe UP/DOWN.\n\nNON modificare:\n\n- layout\n- container position\n- Fav position\n- P1/P2/Dock\n- gesture ownership\n- haptic\n- Core V2\n\n==================================================\n1. KEEP FOUNDATION MOTION\n==================================================\n\nKEEP:\n\nScrollableDefaults.flingBehavior()\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\n\nNo custom spring.\nNo custom tween.\nNo custom translation.\n\n==================================================\n2. REDUCE VISUAL INTENSITY\n==================================================\n\nIl feedback deve essere:\n\n- più corto visivamente\n- meno deformato\n- meno evidente\n- morbido\n- quasi impercettibile\n\nTarget:\nmicro-stretch, non elasticità evidente.\n\n==================================================\n3. DO NOT CHANGE SPEED\n==================================================\n\nNon rallentare.\n\nNon allungare la durata.\n\nRidurre soltanto l'ampiezza percepita.\n\n==================================================\n4. NO LAYOUT RESPONSE\n==================================================\n\nContainer movement:\n0dp\n\nFav movement:\n0dp\n\nP1 movement:\n0dp\n\nP2 movement:\n0dp\n\nDock movement:\n0dp\n\n==================================================\n5. GLOBAL EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nUn solo effetto sulla Home surface.\n\nNo effect separati per Fav/P1/P2.\n\n==================================================\n6. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nKEEP:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nDo not change haptic strength or implementation.\n\n==================================================\n7. DEVICE FEEL\n==================================================\n\nDesired:\n\nswipe\n→ very small Material response\n→ immediate natural settle\n\nNo visible wobble.\nNo large stretch.\nNo bounce.\n\n==================================================\n8. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nCore logic modified:\nNO\n\nNew animation owners:\n0\n\nDuplicate motion paths:\n0\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA LIGHT MATERIAL MOTION COMPLETE\n\nLayout movement: 0dp\nMaterial motion owner: <n>\n\nVisual intensity:\n<REDUCED/FAILED>\n\nSpeed changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCustom animation paths:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:269:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787207193,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — MINIMAL TOUCH RESPONSE ONLY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRidurre il motion a UNA SOLA micro-animazione\nlegata al touch/swipe.\n\nIl feedback deve essere minimo.\n\nNON deve sembrare:\n- bounce\n- wobble\n- stretch evidente\n- slide\n- container movement\n\n==================================================\n1. LAYOUT LOCK\n==================================================\n\nMain container:\n0dp movement\n\nFav:\n0dp movement\n\nP1:\n0dp movement\n\nP2:\n0dp movement\n\nDock:\n0dp movement\n\nSearchSlot:\n0dp movement\n\n==================================================\n2. ONE MOTION OWNER\n==================================================\n\nMotion owners:\n1\n\nNo child-specific animations.\n\nNo separate Fav/P1/P2/Dock motion.\n\n==================================================\n3. TOUCH RESPONSE\n==================================================\n\nQuando viene riconosciuto un touch/swipe valido:\n\napplicare soltanto una micro-risposta visiva\nalla Home surface.\n\nTarget:\nmolto piccola.\n\nNon deve cambiare realmente posizione.\n\n==================================================\n4. PREFERRED EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nPreferire Foundation/Material overscroll standard\nse può essere reso sufficientemente discreto.\n\nSe l'effetto standard disponibile è troppo ampio:\n\nNON aggiungere una seconda animation engine.\n\nUsare invece una sola micro-deformazione locale\ncon ampiezza estremamente limitata.\n\n==================================================\n5. MAX VISUAL RESPONSE\n==================================================\n\nTarget visivo:\n\ncirca 1–2% massimo.\n\nNiente 5–10%.\n\nDeve essere percepibile soprattutto sotto il dito,\nnon osservabile come animazione dell'intera Home.\n\n==================================================\n6. DIRECTION\n==================================================\n\nUP:\nmicro response verso UP\n\nDOWN:\nmicro response verso DOWN\n\nLEFT:\nmicro response verso LEFT\n\nRIGHT:\nmicro response verso RIGHT\n\nMa:\n\nnavigation = 0\nlayout movement = 0\n\n==================================================\n7. RELEASE\n==================================================\n\nAl rilascio:\n\nritorno immediato e morbido allo stato neutro.\n\nUn solo settle.\n\nNo oscillazione.\n\n==================================================\n8. NO CUSTOM SPRING STACK\n==================================================\n\nCustom spring engines:\n0 preferred\n\nCustom tween chains:\n0\n\nMultiple Animatable:\n0\n\nAnimatedVisibility:\n0\n\nCrossfade:\n0\n\n==================================================\n9. NO ALPHA FLASH\n==================================================\n\nNon modificare:\n\nalpha\nvisibility\nwallpaper dim\ncontainer opacity\n\nFlash paths:\n0\n\n==================================================\n10. TOUCH SLOP\n==================================================\n\nTap normale:\nnon deve diventare swipe.\n\nP1/P2/Dock:\nfirst tap works.\n\nNo full-screen pointer block.\n\n==================================================\n11. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nUna sola volta quando l'interazione viene accettata.\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\nCANCEL:\n0\n\n==================================================\n12. CORE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nCore logic modified:\nNO\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nPersistence writes:\n0\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nDuplicate gesture owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n13. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA MINIMAL TOUCH MOTION COMPLETE\n\nMotion owners: <n>\n\nLayout movement:\n0dp\n\nFav movement:\n0dp\n\nP1 movement:\n0dp\n\nP2 movement:\n0dp\n\nDock movement:\n0dp\n\nMaximum visual response:\n<value>\n\nDirectional micro response:\n<YES/NO>\n\nAlpha paths:\n<n>\n\nCustom animation engines:\n<n>\n\nHaptic:\n<CONFIRM/OTHER>\n\nMOVE haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:270:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787207455,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — REAL PIXEL STRETCH OVERSCROLL\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRiprodurre il vero comportamento Pixel/Android\ndi stretch overscroll.\n\nNON simulare il Pixel con:\n- spring custom\n- scale custom\n- translation\n- wobble\n- touch animation\n- container movement\n\n==================================================\n1. REAL SCROLL PIPELINE\n==================================================\n\nLa superficie Home interessata deve usare una vera\nprimitive Foundation scrollable.\n\nPreferire API correnti:\n\nscrollableArea(...)\n\noppure, se non adatta alla versione installata:\n\nscrollable(\n    orientation = Orientation.Vertical,\n    state = ...,\n    flingBehavior = ScrollableDefaults.flingBehavior(),\n    overscrollEffect = rememberOverscrollEffect()\n)\n\nUsare l'API realmente supportata dalla Compose Foundation\ninstallata.\n\n==================================================\n2. PIXEL EFFECT SOURCE\n==================================================\n\nUsare:\n\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\n\nche deve provenire dal corrente:\n\nLocalOverscrollFactory\n\nNON creare un OverscrollEffect custom.\n\n==================================================\n3. DEFAULT FLING\n==================================================\n\nUsare:\n\nScrollableDefaults.flingBehavior()\n\nper la curva naturale Foundation.\n\nNo custom fling.\n\n==================================================\n4. IMPORTANT\n==================================================\n\nLo stretch deve ricevere solo il delta NON CONSUMATO\ndallo scroll.\n\nPipeline reale:\n\npointer input\n→ scrollable\n→ normal consumption\n→ remaining delta\n→ OverscrollEffect\n→ stretch\n→ release\n\nNon inviare arbitrariamente tutto il drag\nall'effetto.\n\n==================================================\n5. HOME GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nLa Home NON deve realmente spostarsi.\n\nFav:\n0dp permanent movement\n\nP1:\n0dp permanent movement\n\nP2:\n0dp permanent movement\n\nDock:\n0dp permanent movement\n\nMain container:\n0dp permanent movement\n\nStretch è un effetto grafico transitorio,\nnon una modifica layout.\n\n==================================================\n6. UP / DOWN\n==================================================\n\nSwipe UP:\nquando raggiunge il limite della superficie scrollabile\n→ Pixel stretch\n\nSwipe DOWN:\nstesso comportamento sul limite opposto.\n\nIl ritorno è gestito dall'OverscrollEffect.\n\n==================================================\n7. NO CUSTOM SETTLE\n==================================================\n\nRemove from this path:\n\nspring(...)\ntween(...)\nAnimatable settle\ncustom resistance factors\ncustom drag factors\n\nTarget:\n\ncustom motion engine = 0\n\n==================================================\n8. NO MANUAL MICRO EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nRimuovere il precedente tentativo:\n\nmicro scale\nmicro translation\ncustom touch response\n\nNon sovrapporre due effetti.\n\n==================================================\n9. EFFECT SCOPE\n==================================================\n\nUn solo overscroll owner per la superficie Home.\n\nNon uno per:\n\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\n==================================================\n10. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock resta statico.\n\nSe necessario, escluderlo dalla superficie stretch\nper mantenere il launcher più stabile.\n\n==================================================\n11. TAP SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nTouch sotto touchSlop:\n\nP1/P2/Dock click normali.\n\nFirst tap:\nPASS.\n\n==================================================\n12. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nNON usare haptic durante lo stretch.\n\nLo stretch Pixel non deve essere accompagnato\nda CONFIRM durante MOVE.\n\nEventuali haptic di azioni reali restano separati.\n\n==================================================\n13. AUDIT INSTALLED API\n==================================================\n\nPrima di implementare, riportare:\n\nCompose Foundation version\nscrollableArea availability\nscrollable overload used\nOverscrollEffect API used\nLocalOverscrollFactory provider\n\nNon assumere vecchie API.\n\n==================================================\n14. STATIC TARGET\n==================================================\n\nOverscrollEffect owners:\n1\n\nDefault fling owners:\n1\n\nCustom spring paths:\n0\n\nCustom tween paths:\n0\n\nCustom scale paths:\n0\n\nCustom translation paths:\n0\n\nLayout movement:\n0\n\n==================================================\n15. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA REAL PIXEL STRETCH COMPLETE\n\nCompose Foundation:\n<version>\n\nScrollable primitive:\n<value>\n\nLocalOverscrollFactory:\n<value>\n\nrememberOverscrollEffect:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDefault fling:\n<YES/NO>\n\nReal unconsumed-delta pipeline:\n<YES/NO>\n\nUP edge stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDOWN edge stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nOverscroll owners:\n<n>\n\nCustom spring paths:\n<n>\n\nCustom scale paths:\n<n>\n\nCustom translation paths:\n<n>\n\nFav permanent movement:\n<dp>\n\nP1 permanent movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 permanent movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock permanent movement:\n<dp>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:272:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787208106,"text":"PATCH FIX — STATIC HOME + 4-DIRECTION MICRO MATERIAL OVERSCROLL\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nLa Home deve restare geometricamente IMMOBILE.\n\nSWIPE:\nUP\nDOWN\nLEFT\nRIGHT\n\ndeve produrre solo un piccolo feedback Material/Foundation.\n\nNON deve spostare:\n- main container\n- Fav\n- P1\n- P2\n- Dock\n- SearchSlot\n\n==================================================\n1. ABSOLUTE GEOMETRY LOCK\n==================================================\n\nRequired permanent deltas:\n\nMain container:\n0dp\n\nFav:\n0dp\n\nP1:\n0dp\n\nP2:\n0dp\n\nDock:\n0dp\n\nSearchSlot:\n0dp\n\nNo position changes before/during/after swipe.\n\n==================================================\n2. REMOVE ALL LAYOUT MOTION\n==================================================\n\nRemove every swipe-driven:\n\noffset()\nabsoluteOffset()\ntranslationX\ntranslationY\ngraphicsLayer translation\nanimated top\nanimated bottom\nanimated width/height\nlayout interpolation\npadding interpolation\n\nTarget:\nlayout-motion paths = 0\n\n==================================================\n3. ONE GLOBAL VISUAL EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nUse ONE transient visual response owner\nfor the Home surface.\n\nPreferred:\n\nFoundation/Material OverscrollEffect\n\nwith:\n\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\n\nand the real scroll/overscroll pipeline supported\nby the installed Compose Foundation version.\n\nDo NOT create separate effects for:\n\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\n==================================================\n4. FOUR DIRECTIONS\n==================================================\n\nUP:\nsmall top-edge Material stretch\n\nDOWN:\nsmall bottom-edge Material stretch\n\nLEFT:\nsmall left-edge Material stretch\n\nRIGHT:\nsmall right-edge Material stretch\n\nAll four:\nNO navigation\nNO state mutation\nNO layout movement\n\n==================================================\n5. HORIZONTAL PIPELINE\n==================================================\n\nHorizontal LEFT/RIGHT must use a real Foundation\nhorizontal scroll/overscroll source.\n\nDo not fake it with translationX.\n\nUse:\n\nOrientation.Horizontal\n\nwith default Foundation behavior.\n\n==================================================\n6. VERTICAL PIPELINE\n==================================================\n\nVertical UP/DOWN:\n\nOrientation.Vertical\n\nwith the same Material/Foundation effect family.\n\nNo Fav expansion.\nNo container expansion.\n\n==================================================\n7. ONE MATERIAL LANGUAGE\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nScrollableDefaults.flingBehavior()\n\n+\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\n\nor the exact current Foundation equivalents.\n\nNo:\ncustom spring\ncustom tween\ncustom wobble\ncustom scale animation\ncustom fade\n\n==================================================\n8. EFFECT INTENSITY\n==================================================\n\nKeep the effect very small.\n\nTarget feel:\n\n- subtle\n- short\n- Pixel-like\n- edge-local\n- no obvious bounce\n- no visible container displacement\n\n==================================================\n9. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock is part of the static Home geometry.\n\nDock coordinates:\nalways fixed.\n\nIf including Dock in the visual stretch makes it\nlook like it moves:\n\napply the effect only to the upper Home surface\nwhile keeping Dock completely outside the effect.\n\nPreferred device result:\nDock appears perfectly stable.\n\n==================================================\n10. NO BACK/NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\n0 navigation\n\nRIGHT:\n0 navigation\n\nUP:\n0 navigation\n\nDOWN:\n0 navigation\n\nThis patch is only visual feedback.\n\n==================================================\n11. TOUCH SLOP\n==================================================\n\nNormal taps must remain taps.\n\nP1:\nfirst tap works\n\nP2:\nfirst tap works\n\nDock:\nfirst tap works\n\nNo full-screen pointer layer that consumes DOWN early.\n\n==================================================\n12. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nKeep existing:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nOnly once on an accepted swipe gesture.\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\nCANCEL:\n0\n\n==================================================\n13. ALPHA\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT animate:\n\nalpha\nwallpaper dim\nvisibility\ncontainer opacity\n\nAlpha motion paths:\n0\n\n==================================================\n14. CORE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nCore logic modified:\nNO\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nPersistence writes:\n0\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nDuplicate gesture owners:\n0\n\nDuplicate motion owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n15. STATIC DEVICE CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nWhile finger moves:\n\nMain container bounds:\nunchanged\n\nDock bounds:\nunchanged\n\nP1/P2 bounds:\nunchanged\n\nOnly the Material overscroll rendering changes transiently.\n\n==================================================\n16. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA STATIC 4-WAY MATERIAL MOTION COMPLETE\n\nLayout motion paths:\n<n>\n\nMain container movement:\n<dp>\n\nFav movement:\n<dp>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nVertical overscroll owner:\n<n>\n\nHorizontal overscroll owner:\n<n>\n\nUP stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDOWN stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nLEFT stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRIGHT stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHorizontal navigation:\n<n>\n\nVertical navigation:\n<n>\n\nCustom spring paths:\n<n>\n\nCustom translation paths:\n<n>\n\nAlpha motion paths:\n<n>\n\nHaptic:\n<CONFIRM/OTHER>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:273:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787208364,"text":"PATCH FIX — REDUCE 4-WAY MATERIAL EFFECT INTENSITY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nKEEP:\n- static Home geometry\n- Dock fixed\n- Fav fixed\n- P1/P2 fixed\n- 4-direction support\n- Foundation/Material overscroll\n- haptic CONFIRM\n- touch behavior\n- no navigation\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRidurre leggermente l'intensità visiva del micro-effetto.\n\nNON rallentare.\nNON cambiare timing.\nNON cambiare layout.\nNON cambiare gesture logic.\n\nTARGET\n\nCurrent effect:\ntoo visible\n\nNew effect:\nabout 20–30% lighter visually\n\nDesired feel:\n- very subtle\n- short\n- edge-local\n- Pixel-like\n- no obvious stretch\n- no bounce\n\nIf current implementation exposes an intensity/amplitude parameter:\nreduce only that parameter.\n\nIf Foundation default does NOT expose intensity directly:\nDO NOT add a second custom animation engine.\n\nPrefer the smallest supported adjustment available in the current\nOverscrollEffect / OverscrollFactory implementation.\n\nDO NOT introduce:\n- custom translation\n- custom scale\n- custom spring\n- custom tween\n- alpha animation\n\nREQUIRED\n\nMain container movement: 0dp\nFav movement: 0dp\nP1 movement: 0dp\nP2 movement: 0dp\nDock movement: 0dp\n\nUP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT:\nstill active\n\nOUTPUT\n\nMACHINA MATERIAL MICRO EFFECT REDUCED\n\nPrevious intensity: <value/DEFAULT>\nNew intensity: <value/DEFAULT_ADJUSTED>\n\nVisual reduction: <value>\n\nGeometry changed: NO\nTiming changed: NO\nGesture logic changed: NO\nHaptic changed: NO\n\nCustom motion added: 0\n\nFirst-touch regression: <NONE/FOUND>\n\nDebug build: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8 release: <SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:274:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787208649,"text":"PATCH FIX — SWIPE-ONLY MATERIAL EFFECT / EXCLUDE UP\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nApplicare una micro animazione Material SOLO agli swipe:\n\nLEFT\nRIGHT\nDOWN\n\nSWIPE UP:\nNO visual animation\n\nNormal tap/touch:\nNO animation\n\n==================================================\n1. TOUCH MUST NOT ANIMATE\n==================================================\n\nSimple DOWN/UP tap:\nNO visual response\n\nP1 tap:\nlaunch only\n\nP2 tap:\nlaunch only\n\nDock tap:\nlaunch only\n\nFav tap:\nnormal interaction only\n\nNo animation before touchSlop.\n\n==================================================\n2. GESTURE GATE\n==================================================\n\nWait until swipe is actually recognized.\n\nOnly after touchSlop + direction lock:\n\nLEFT:\nMaterial micro effect\n\nRIGHT:\nMaterial micro effect\n\nDOWN:\nMaterial micro effect\n\nUP:\nNO visual effect\n\n==================================================\n3. SWIPE UP RESERVED\n==================================================\n\nUP is reserved for future launcher behavior.\n\nFor now:\n\nUP animation paths = 0\nUP layout movement = 0\nUP navigation = 0\n\nDo not consume it with the visual motion system\nunless required only for direction classification.\n\n==================================================\n4. STATIC HOME\n==================================================\n\nMain container movement:\n0dp\n\nFav movement:\n0dp\n\nP1 movement:\n0dp\n\nP2 movement:\n0dp\n\nDock movement:\n0dp\n\nSearchSlot movement:\n0dp\n\n==================================================\n5. MATERIAL EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nUse existing approved Material/Foundation overscroll family.\n\nKeep it subtle.\n\nNo:\ncustom spring\ncustom tween\ncustom translation\ncustom scale\ncustom alpha\ncustom wobble\n\n==================================================\n6. LEFT / RIGHT\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\nmicro Material edge response only\n\nRIGHT:\nmicro Material edge response only\n\nNavigation:\n0\n\nState writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n7. DOWN\n==================================================\n\nDOWN:\nmicro Material response only\n\nNo container movement.\nNo collapse.\nNo route/state change.\n\n==================================================\n8. UP\n==================================================\n\nUP:\nvisual Material response = NONE\n\nNo stretch.\nNo bounce.\nNo fade.\nNo haptic for visual motion.\n\n==================================================\n9. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nUse existing:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nOnly when a valid LEFT/RIGHT/DOWN swipe is accepted,\nif haptic is still desired for gesture confirmation.\n\nTap:\n0\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\nUP:\n0\n\nCANCEL:\n0\n\n==================================================\n10. ONE GESTURE OWNER\n==================================================\n\nOne direction classifier/gesture owner.\n\nNo separate owners for each direction.\n\n==================================================\n11. FIRST-TOUCH SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nTap below touchSlop:\nchild click wins.\n\nFirst tap P1/P2/Dock:\nPASS.\n\n==================================================\n12. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nCore logic modified:\nNO\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nPersistence writes:\n0\n\nDuplicate gesture owners:\n0\n\nDuplicate motion owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA SWIPE-ONLY MATERIAL MOTION COMPLETE\n\nTap animation paths: <n>\n\nLEFT animation:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRIGHT animation:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDOWN animation:\n<YES/NO>\n\nUP animation:\n<NO/YES>\n\nMain container movement:\n<dp>\n\nFav movement:\n<dp>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nGesture owners:\n<n>\n\nMotion owners:\n<n>\n\nHaptic on tap:\n<n>\n\nHaptic on MOVE:\n<n>\n\nHaptic on UP:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:275:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787208973,"text":"PATCH FIX — ULTRA-SHORT BACK-SWIPE ANIMATION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nImplementare una vera animazione swipe laterale,\nmolto corta e molto contenuta.\n\nNon è un semplice feedback touch.\n\nDeve ricordare un leggerissimo gesto \"back\",\nsenza navigazione.\n\n==================================================\n1. ACTIVE DIRECTIONS\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\nYES\n\nRIGHT:\nYES\n\nDOWN:\noptional same micro language\n\nUP:\nNO animation\n\n==================================================\n2. NO TOUCH ANIMATION\n==================================================\n\nTap normale:\nNO animation\n\nAnimazione parte solo dopo:\n\ntouchSlop\n+\ndirection lock\n+\nvalid swipe\n\n==================================================\n3. MAX TRAVEL\n==================================================\n\nIl movimento deve essere estremamente piccolo.\n\nTarget iniziale:\n\nLEFT/RIGHT visual travel:\n2dp max\n\nHard max:\n3dp\n\nDOWN visual travel:\n1.5–2dp max\n\nUP:\n0dp\n\n==================================================\n4. BACK-SWIPE FEEL\n==================================================\n\nDurante LEFT/RIGHT:\n\nla superficie cede appena nella direzione dello swipe.\n\nNon deve sembrare:\n\nslide\npage transition\noverscroll grande\nrubber band\nwobble\n\nDeve sembrare solo una tensione laterale minima.\n\n==================================================\n5. RETURN\n==================================================\n\nAl release:\n\nritorno immediato e morbido a 0.\n\nUn solo settle.\n\nNo oscillazione.\n\nNo overshoot visibile.\n\n==================================================\n6. GEOMETRY LOCK\n==================================================\n\nActual layout:\n\nMain container = fixed\nFav = fixed\nP1 = fixed\nP2 = fixed\nDock = fixed\nSearchSlot = fixed\n\nNon cambiare bounds reali.\n\n==================================================\n7. VISUAL-ONLY TRANSFORM\n==================================================\n\nSe serve una trasformazione transient:\n\napplicarla solo al layer visuale Home superiore.\n\nNon modificare layout coordinates.\n\nDock:\npreferibilmente completamente esclusa dall'effetto.\n\n==================================================\n8. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock movement:\n0dp\n\nDock transform:\n0 preferred\n\nLa Dock deve sembrare totalmente ferma.\n\n==================================================\n9. LEFT / RIGHT SYMMETRY\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\nmax -2dp visual response\n\nRIGHT:\nmax +2dp visual response\n\nStesso timing.\nStessa curva.\nStessa intensità.\n\n==================================================\n10. DOWN\n==================================================\n\nDOWN:\n\nmicro risposta max 1.5–2dp.\n\nNessuna espansione/collapse.\n\nNessun layout state.\n\n==================================================\n11. UP RESERVED\n==================================================\n\nUP:\n\nanimation paths = 0\nvisual movement = 0\nhaptic = 0\n\nLascia UP libero per funzione futura.\n\n==================================================\n12. MOTION CURVE\n==================================================\n\nUsare un settle molto corto.\n\nPreferire una singola animation primitive.\n\nNo stack di:\n\nspring + overscroll + tween.\n\nOne owner only.\n\nSe serve spring:\n\nNoBouncy\n+\nMedium/MediumHigh stiffness\n\nma niente custom float finché non necessario.\n\n==================================================\n13. NO MATERIAL STRETCH LARGE EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nNon usare il grande stretch overscroll Pixel\nse produce deformazione evidente.\n\nQuesto path deve essere più ristretto.\n\nTarget:\nback-swipe micro motion.\n\n==================================================\n14. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nSolo una volta su swipe LEFT/RIGHT/DOWN accettato.\n\nTap:\n0\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\nUP:\n0\n\n==================================================\n15. NO ALPHA\n==================================================\n\nAlpha animation:\n0\n\nWallpaper dim animation:\n0\n\nVisibility changes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n16. INPUT SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nFirst tap:\n\nP1 PASS\nP2 PASS\nDock PASS\n\nNo gesture owner consuming tap before touchSlop.\n\n==================================================\n17. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nCore logic modified:\nNO\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nPersistence writes:\n0\n\nMotion owners:\n1\n\nGesture owners:\n1\n\nDuplicate motion:\n0\n\n==================================================\n18. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA ULTRA-SHORT BACK-SWIPE MOTION COMPLETE\n\nLEFT max visual travel: <dp>\nRIGHT max visual travel: <dp>\nDOWN max visual travel: <dp>\nUP visual travel: <dp>\n\nActual layout movement: <dp>\n\nDock movement: <dp>\n\nMotion owners: <n>\nGesture owners: <n>\n\nAlpha animation paths: <n>\nOvershoot: <value>\n\nHaptic:\n<CONFIRM/OTHER>\n\nMOVE haptic paths: <n>\nUP haptic paths: <n>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCore logic modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug build:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:276:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787209384,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — STATIC HOME / SUBTLE MATERIAL STRETCH\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2 STABLE CANDIDATE\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nImplementare un solo comportamento motion sulla Home:\n\nLEFT  -> subtle Material/Android stretch\nRIGHT -> subtle Material/Android stretch\nDOWN  -> subtle Material/Android stretch\nUP    -> RESERVED, nessuna animazione\n\nLa Home NON deve muoversi realmente.\n\nNessuna navigazione.\nNessun Back.\nNessun edge indicator.\nNessun fade.\n\n==================================================\n1. FINAL MOTION CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\nMaterial stretch only\n\nRIGHT:\nMaterial stretch only\n\nDOWN:\nMaterial stretch only\n\nUP:\nNO visual motion\nNO navigation\nNO haptic\n\nTAP:\nNO motion\n\n==================================================\n2. HOME GEOMETRY HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nActual layout bounds must remain unchanged.\n\nMain container:\n0dp movement\n\nFav:\n0dp movement\n\nP1:\n0dp movement\n\nP2:\n0dp movement\n\nDock:\n0dp movement\n\nSearchSlot:\n0dp movement\n\nNo swipe may change:\ntop\nbottom\nheight\nwidth\npadding\noffset\nlayout position\n\n==================================================\n3. NO BACK UI\n==================================================\n\nHome root has no previous destination.\n\nDo NOT add:\n\nback arrow\nedge indicator\nchevron\npredictive destination\nback animation\nBack navigation\n\nHome Back behavior remains:\nNO_OP\n\n==================================================\n4. REMOVE LEGACY MOTION\n==================================================\n\nAudit and remove confirmed old runtime paths for:\n\nFav lift\ncontainer expansion\ncontainer translation\nSearchSlot animated height\nvertical layout interpolation\ncustom micro translation\ncustom 2dp back motion\ncustom wobble\ncustom spring motion\ncustom alpha/fade motion\n\nDo not leave parallel motion engines.\n\n==================================================\n5. ONE MOTION OWNER\n==================================================\n\nHome motion owners:\n1\n\nNo separate motion owner for:\n\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\nSearchSlot\n\n==================================================\n6. ONE GESTURE OWNER\n==================================================\n\nUse one gesture/direction owner for Home.\n\nIt must classify only after touchSlop.\n\nBefore touchSlop:\nchild taps remain untouched.\n\nAfter direction lock:\n\nLEFT\nRIGHT\nDOWN\nUP\n\nDirection remains locked until release/cancel.\n\n==================================================\n7. TAP SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nSimple tap:\n\nno animation\nno haptic from this patch\nno gesture state transition\n\nRequired:\n\nP1 first tap -> launch\nP2 first tap -> launch\nDock first tap -> launch\n\nNo full-screen DOWN consumption.\n\n==================================================\n8. MATERIAL / FOUNDATION IMPLEMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nUse real Compose Foundation overscroll behavior.\n\nPrefer the APIs available in the installed Compose version:\n\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\n\nand the appropriate Foundation scroll/overscroll pipeline.\n\nUse:\nLocalOverscrollFactory\n\nwhen provided by the installed Foundation version.\n\nDo NOT build a custom Pixel-like effect.\n\n==================================================\n9. REAL OVERSCROLL PIPELINE\n==================================================\n\nThe visual stretch must receive real unconsumed gesture delta.\n\nConceptual pipeline:\n\ngesture\n-> touchSlop\n-> direction lock\n-> scroll delta\n-> normal consumption\n-> unconsumed delta\n-> OverscrollEffect\n-> transient stretch\n-> release\n\nDo not map gesture delta to layout position.\n\n==================================================\n10. HORIZONTAL\n==================================================\n\nLEFT/RIGHT must use the proper horizontal Foundation\nscroll/overscroll source.\n\nOrientation:\nHorizontal\n\nLEFT:\nsubtle left-edge stretch\n\nRIGHT:\nsubtle right-edge stretch\n\nHorizontal navigation actions:\n0\n\nPersistent state writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n11. DOWN\n==================================================\n\nDOWN must use the vertical Foundation overscroll source.\n\nOrientation:\nVertical\n\nOnly DOWN is allowed to trigger the visual effect.\n\nNo collapse.\nNo layout state.\nNo container movement.\n\n==================================================\n12. UP RESERVED\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nUP must remain free for a future launcher function.\n\nTherefore:\n\nUP stretch paths:\n0\n\nUP navigation paths:\n0\n\nUP haptic paths:\n0\n\nUP state writes:\n0\n\nThe motion system may classify UP only to ignore it.\n\n==================================================\n13. MATERIAL STRETCH INTENSITY\n==================================================\n\nEffect must be subtle.\n\nDesired feel:\n\n- short\n- restrained\n- Pixel-like\n- edge-local\n- no obvious bounce\n- no visible page movement\n- no large deformation\n\nUse the smallest supported Foundation/Material adjustment\navailable without introducing a second custom animation engine.\n\nIf default OverscrollEffect exposes no supported intensity control:\n\nKEEP default Foundation effect.\n\nDo NOT emulate lower intensity with:\ntranslation\nscale\nalpha\ncustom spring\n\n==================================================\n14. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock must appear completely static.\n\nPreferred:\n\nDock outside the overscroll visual layer.\n\nRequired:\n\nDock visual movement:\n0\n\nDock actual movement:\n0\n\nDock click behavior:\nunchanged\n\n==================================================\n15. UPPER HOME SURFACE\n==================================================\n\nApply the transient effect only to the Home surface that contains:\n\nFav\nSearchSlot\nP1\nP2\n\nif this is required to keep Dock perfectly stable.\n\nStill:\n\nactual bounds remain static.\n\n==================================================\n16. NO CUSTOM TRANSFORMS\n==================================================\n\nTarget runtime:\n\ncustom translationX paths = 0\ncustom translationY paths = 0\ncustom scale paths = 0\ncustom alpha paths = 0\ncustom fade paths = 0\ncustom spring paths = 0\ncustom tween paths = 0\ncustom wobble paths = 0\n\n==================================================\n17. NO LAYOUT ANIMATION\n==================================================\n\nNo:\n\nanimateDpAsState for geometry\nAnimatedContent\nAnimatedVisibility\nCrossfade\nanimated height\nanimated padding\nprogress-driven layout\n\nLayout animation owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n18. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nUse Android hardware-adaptive haptic only for accepted\nswipe gestures:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nAllowed:\n\nLEFT accepted -> CONFIRM x1\nRIGHT accepted -> CONFIRM x1\nDOWN accepted -> CONFIRM x1\n\nNot allowed:\n\nUP -> 0\ntap -> 0\nMOVE -> 0\nCANCEL -> 0\n\nNo:\n\nVibrator\nVibratorManager\nVibrationEffect\ncustom duration\ncustom waveform\n\nNo VIBRATE permission added for this patch.\n\n==================================================\n19. WALLPAPER / VISUALS\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT modify:\n\nwindowShowWallpaper\nwindowBackground\nwallpaper dim\ncontainer color\nborder\nshadow\ncorner radius\nsystem bars\n\nNo opacity animation.\n\n==================================================\n20. CORE DATA HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nPatch writes to:\n\nHomeSnapshot = 0\nP1 state = 0\nP2 state = 0\nDock state = 0\nLauncherPreferences = 0\nAppCatalog internals = 0\n\nNew persistence:\n0\n\n==================================================\n21. LIFECYCLE\n==================================================\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nNew onResume paths:\n0\n\nNew listeners:\n0 preferred\n\nNo polling.\n\nNo keep-alive.\n\n==================================================\n22. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nDuring gesture:\n\nPackageManager calls = 0\nbitmap decode = 0\nnetwork = 0\ndisk IO = 0\n\nAvoid per-frame heavy allocation.\n\n==================================================\n23. PROCESS CACHE POLICY\n==================================================\n\nUnchanged:\n\nAndroid owns process caching.\n\nPatch must not add:\n\nService\nWakeLock\nkeep-alive\nprocess priority tricks\n\n==================================================\n24. PATCH LOCATION\n==================================================\n\nKeep implementation isolated.\n\nPreferred:\n\npatches/home_motion/\n    HomeMotionPatch.kt\n\nOne file preferred if maintainable.\n\nCore hook:\nMAX 1\n\n==================================================\n25. PATCH REMOVABILITY\n==================================================\n\nRemoving:\n\npatches/home_motion/\n\n+\nsingle hook\n\nmust restore exact Core V2 behavior.\n\nNo residual state.\nNo residual persistence.\nNo residual Manifest changes.\n\n==================================================\n26. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nCore isolation:\nPASS\n\nState ownership:\nPASS\n\nInput ownership:\nPASS\n\nMotion ownership:\nPASS\n\nHaptic ownership:\nPASS\n\nLifecycle:\nPASS\n\nPerformance:\nPASS\n\nRollback:\nPASS\n\n==================================================\n27. STATIC AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nSearch project for:\n\noffset(\nabsoluteOffset(\ntranslationX\ntranslationY\ngraphicsLayer\nanimateDpAsState\nAnimatable\nspring(\ntween(\nAnimatedVisibility\nAnimatedContent\nCrossfade\nalpha\nBackHandler\nPredictiveBackHandler\n\nClassify every relevant hit.\n\nNo old layout-motion path may remain active.\n\n==================================================\n28. DEVICE TEST\n==================================================\n\nPixel device:\n\nA. TAP\n\nP1 first tap:\nPASS\n\nP2 first tap:\nPASS\n\nDock first tap:\nPASS\n\nNo visual animation on simple tap.\n\nB. LEFT\n\nsmall Material stretch:\nYES\n\nnavigation:\nNO\n\nHome movement:\nNO\n\nDock movement:\nNO\n\nC. RIGHT\n\nsame as LEFT.\n\nD. DOWN\n\nsmall Material stretch:\nYES\n\nHome movement:\nNO\n\nDock movement:\nNO\n\nE. UP\n\nvisual animation:\nNO\n\nnavigation:\nNO\n\nstate change:\nNO\n\nF. REGRESSION\n\nflash:\nNONE\n\nmulti-touch requirement:\nNONE\n\nfirst-touch bug:\nNONE\n\ncrash:\nNONE\n\n==================================================\n29. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\nSnapshot/hash validation:\nPASS\n\n==================================================\n30. PATCH DOC\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nPATCH_001_V2_STATIC_MATERIAL_STRETCH.md\n\nDocument:\n\nPurpose\nCore hook\nGesture owner\nMotion owner\nOverscroll API\nDirection contract\nHaptic contract\nCore isolation\nStatic audit\nDevice validation\nRollback\nBuild results\n\n==================================================\n31. VALIDATION STATUS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT mark VALIDATED from static analysis alone.\n\nInitial status after successful build:\n\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\nOnly after device PASS:\n\nrun code-security validation\nrebuild\nR8\ncheckpoint\n\nThen status may become:\n\nVALIDATED\n\n==================================================\nFINAL OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 001 V2 STATIC MATERIAL STRETCH COMPLETE\n\n=== CORE ===\n\nCore logic modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore files touched:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n<n>\n\nPersistence writes:\n<n>\n\n=== GEOMETRY ===\n\nMain container movement:\n<dp>\n\nFav movement:\n<dp>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nSearchSlot movement:\n<dp>\n\nLayout animation owners:\n<n>\n\n=== INPUT ===\n\nGesture owners:\n<n>\n\nTap animation paths:\n<n>\n\nLEFT active:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRIGHT active:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDOWN active:\n<YES/NO>\n\nUP active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHorizontal navigation actions:\n<n>\n\nVertical navigation actions:\n<n>\n\n=== MOTION ===\n\nCompose Foundation version:\n<value>\n\nOverscrollEffect:\n<value>\n\nLocalOverscrollFactory:\n<value>\n\nHorizontal overscroll source:\n<value>\n\nVertical overscroll source:\n<value>\n\nReal unconsumed-delta pipeline:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCustom spring paths:\n<n>\n\nCustom tween paths:\n<n>\n\nCustom translation paths:\n<n>\n\nCustom scale paths:\n<n>\n\nCustom alpha/fade paths:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate motion owners:\n<n>\n\n=== HAPTIC ===\n\nHaptic:\n<CONFIRM/OTHER>\n\nLEFT haptic:\n<n>\n\nRIGHT haptic:\n<n>\n\nDOWN haptic:\n<n>\n\nUP haptic:\n<n>\n\nTap haptic:\n<n>\n\nMOVE haptic:\n<n>\n\nVIBRATE permission added:\n<NO/YES>\n\n=== SECURITY ===\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n<n>\n\nNew persistence:\n<n>\n\nMain-thread heavy paths:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nRollback:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\n=== BUILD ===\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot validation:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPatch status:\n<DEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED/FAILED>\n\nPatch doc:\ndocs/PATCH_001_V2_STATIC_MATERIAL_STRETCH.md\n\nADB used:\nNO\n\nAPK installed:\nNO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:277:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787211843,"text":"PATCH 001 V2 — SENSITIVE HOME INTERACTION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2 STABLE CANDIDATE\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nCreare un solo layer di interazione Home che gestisca:\n\n1. LEFT / RIGHT\n   -> subtle Material stretch\n   -> NO system Back arrow\n   -> NO navigation\n\n2. TOUCH COMMANDS\n   -> hardware-adaptive Pixel haptic\n   -> performHapticFeedback(CONFIRM)\n\n3. SWIPE UP / DOWN\n   -> espansione/collasso reale del container\n   -> NO Material stretch\n   -> max expanded height ≈ 60% del display utile\n   -> gesture-threshold haptic una sola volta\n\n==================================================\n1. ONE INTERACTION OWNER\n==================================================\n\nUn solo owner:\n\nHomeInteractionPatch\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- direction classification\n- lateral gesture exclusion\n- horizontal Material stretch\n- vertical expansion progress\n- haptic dispatch\n\nNo duplicate gesture engines.\n\n==================================================\n2. CORE DATA LOCK\n==================================================\n\nNO writes to:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nP1\nP2\nDock\nAppCatalog internals\nLauncherPreferences slot state\n\nPersistent writes:\n0\n\nCore lifecycle changes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n3. LEFT / RIGHT — LAUNCHER ROOT\n==================================================\n\nWhile HOME ROOT is visible:\n\nLEFT:\nMaterial stretch only\n\nRIGHT:\nMaterial stretch only\n\nNavigation:\n0\n\nState changes:\n0\n\nBack destination:\nNONE\n\n==================================================\n4. NO EDGE BACK ARROW\n==================================================\n\nUse Android supported system-gesture exclusion\non the Home root lateral regions.\n\nPreferred Compose API if available:\n\nModifier.systemGestureExclusion(...)\n\nor View.setSystemGestureExclusionRects / ViewCompat equivalent.\n\nPurpose:\n\nLEFT/RIGHT interaction belongs to Machina Home,\nnot Android Back.\n\nDo NOT exclude bottom Home/Overview gesture region.\n\n==================================================\n5. LATERAL EXCLUSION SCOPE\n==================================================\n\nExclusion must be:\n\n- HOME ROOT only\n- lateral only\n- minimum region necessary\n- lifecycle/layout safe\n\nWhen Home root is not visible:\nclear/remove exclusion.\n\nDo not apply globally to future Settings/subpages.\n\n==================================================\n6. LEFT / RIGHT MATERIAL EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nUse real Compose Foundation overscroll family.\n\nPrefer:\n\nrememberOverscrollEffect()\n\nwith a real horizontal scroll/overscroll source.\n\nNo:\n\ncustom translationX\ncustom spring\ncustom scale\ncustom alpha\ncustom edge arrow\n\nContainer actual bounds:\nunchanged.\n\nDock:\nunchanged.\n\n==================================================\n7. LEFT / RIGHT RESULT\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\nsmall Material stretch\nno arrow\nno Back\nno navigation\n\nRIGHT:\nsame\n\nRelease:\nnatural Material return.\n\n==================================================\n8. TAP / TOUCH COMMAND HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nFor accepted user commands:\n\nApp launch\nFav command\nSearch result command\nfuture explicit action\n\nuse:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nExactly once per accepted command.\n\n==================================================\n9. TOUCH HAPTIC RULES\n==================================================\n\nTap that performs no command:\n0\n\nPointer DOWN:\n0\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\nCancelled action:\n0\n\nDuplicate haptic:\n0\n\nDo NOT use:\n\nVibrator\nVibratorManager\nVibrationEffect\ncustom duration\ncustom waveform\n\nDo NOT add VIBRATE permission.\n\n==================================================\n10. VERTICAL EXPANSION\n==================================================\n\nUP and DOWN have a DIFFERENT motion contract.\n\nThey must NOT use Material stretch.\n\nUP:\nexpand container\n\nDOWN:\ncollapse container\n\n==================================================\n11. VERTICAL PULL\n==================================================\n\nUse one vertical drag owner.\n\nDuring drag:\n\ncontainer expansionProgress follows finger.\n\nprogress:\n\n0f = collapsed\n1f = expanded\n\nNo second Animatable.\n\nNo horizontal coupling.\n\n==================================================\n12. EXPANDED HEIGHT TARGET\n==================================================\n\nExpanded container must use approximately:\n\n60% of available display height\n\nNOT raw physical screen height.\n\nUse actual usable/root constraints after relevant\nsystem insets.\n\nConcept:\n\nexpandedHeight =\navailableHomeHeight * 0.60f\n\n==================================================\n13. SAFE CLAMP\n==================================================\n\nHard clamp:\n\ncollapsedHeight <= currentHeight <= expandedHeight\n\nNever exceed expandedHeight.\n\nNever move underneath wallpaper layer.\nNever pass root bounds.\nNever enter mandatory bottom gesture region.\n\n==================================================\n14. REAL LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nUP/DOWN may change ONLY the intended container height.\n\nDo NOT translate the entire Home.\n\nNo:\n\nroot translationY\ngraphicsLayer translationY\nvisual-only offset for layout\n\nUse real constrained layout height.\n\n==================================================\n15. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock stays completely fixed.\n\nDock:\n\nposition delta = 0dp\nheight delta = 0dp\n\nExpanded container must stop above Dock using\nreal measured/constraint relationship.\n\n==================================================\n16. P1 / P2\n==================================================\n\nPreferred:\n\nP1/P2 retain their established anchor positions\ninside the Home composition.\n\nDo not animate each grid independently.\n\nNo independent P1/P2 motion owner.\n\n==================================================\n17. FAV / SEARCH AREA\n==================================================\n\nExpansion creates usable space for:\n\nFav\nfuture Search\nfuture results\n\nbut this patch does NOT implement Search logic.\n\nSearch paths:\n0\n\nKeyboard paths:\n0\n\n==================================================\n18. UP / DOWN MOTION\n==================================================\n\nUP/DOWN must NOT use Material OverscrollEffect.\n\nInstead use:\n\ndirect drag progress\n+\nsingle bounded settle to target\n\nDo not stack:\noverscroll + spring + tween.\n\n==================================================\n19. SETTLE\n==================================================\n\nUse one standard Compose settle primitive.\n\nPrefer official spring preset only.\n\nTarget feel:\n\n- direct during drag\n- short settle\n- no large bounce\n- no overshoot beyond bounds\n\nNo arbitrary per-device magic durations.\n\n==================================================\n20. THRESHOLD HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nFor UP/DOWN gesture threshold:\n\nuse:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.GESTURE_THRESHOLD_ACTIVATE\n)\n\nwhen available on current API.\n\nTrigger:\nonce when gesture becomes eligible to complete\nEXPAND or COLLAPSE.\n\nIf user crosses back below threshold before release,\noptional:\n\nGESTURE_THRESHOLD_DEACTIVATE\n\nonly if it improves behavior and remains one-to-one.\n\nDo NOT fire haptic continuously.\n\n==================================================\n21. FINAL STATE HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT also fire CONFIRM for the same vertical gesture\nif threshold haptic already communicated acceptance.\n\nVertical gesture:\none semantic haptic path only.\n\nAvoid:\nthreshold haptic + CONFIRM duplicate.\n\n==================================================\n22. RELEASE DECISION\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nprogress\n+\nvertical velocity\n\nto decide:\n\nCOLLAPSED\nor\nEXPANDED.\n\nNo arbitrary route/state transitions.\n\n==================================================\n23. DOWN FROM COLLAPSED\n==================================================\n\nIf already COLLAPSED:\n\nDOWN:\nNO geometry change\nNO Material stretch\nNO haptic\n\n==================================================\n24. UP FROM EXPANDED\n==================================================\n\nIf already EXPANDED:\n\nUP:\nNO additional geometry\nNO Material stretch\nNO haptic\n\n==================================================\n25. INPUT ARBITRATION\n==================================================\n\nBefore touchSlop:\nnormal child click owns interaction.\n\nAfter touchSlop:\nlock dominant axis.\n\nHorizontal:\nLEFT/RIGHT stretch path.\n\nVertical:\nUP/DOWN container path.\n\nNever run both.\n\n==================================================\n26. FIRST TOUCH SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nP1 first tap:\nPASS\n\nP2 first tap:\nPASS\n\nDock first tap:\nPASS\n\nFav first command:\nPASS\n\nNo full-screen handler consumes initial DOWN.\n\n==================================================\n27. MATERIAL VS VERTICAL CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nSTRICT:\n\nLEFT/RIGHT:\nMaterial stretch\n\nUP/DOWN:\ncontainer expansion/collapse\n\nNever:\n\nUP/DOWN Material stretch\n\nNever:\n\nLEFT/RIGHT geometry expansion\n\n==================================================\n28. ALPHA / WALLPAPER\n==================================================\n\nNo:\n\nfade\nalpha animation\nwallpaper opacity animation\ndim animation\nvisibility animation\n\nWallpaper remains Android-owned.\n\n==================================================\n29. BOTTOM SYSTEM GESTURES\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT exclude:\n\nsystem Home\nOverview\nQuick Switch\n\nBottom mandatory gesture region:\nAndroid-owned.\n\n==================================================\n30. HAPTIC API FALLBACK\n==================================================\n\nIf GESTURE_THRESHOLD_ACTIVATE is not available\non the runtime/API compatibility path:\n\nfallback to:\n\nHapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n\nonce at accepted vertical transition.\n\nDocument fallback.\n\nDo not use raw vibrator APIs.\n\n==================================================\n31. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nDuring gesture:\n\ndisk IO = 0\nPackageManager work = 0\nbitmap decode = 0\nnetwork = 0\n\nAvoid allocation-heavy per-frame work.\n\n==================================================\n32. PATCH BOUNDARY\n==================================================\n\nPreferred:\n\npatches/home_interaction/\n    HomeInteractionPatch.kt\n\nOne file preferred if maintainable.\n\nCore integration:\none hook maximum.\n\n==================================================\n33. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nRemove:\n\npatches/home_interaction/\n\n+\nsingle hook\n\n=> exact Core V2 behavior.\n\nNo residual manifest/persistence/state changes.\n\n==================================================\n34. STATIC SECURITY AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nRequired target:\n\ngesture owners = 1\naxis classifiers = 1\nhorizontal overscroll owners = 1\nvertical expansion owners = 1\nhaptic dispatch owners = 1\n\nHomeSnapshot writes = 0\npersistence writes = 0\nnew lifecycle owners = 0\nduplicate input owners = 0\nfirst-touch blockers = 0\n\n==================================================\n35. DEVICE TEST\n==================================================\n\nPIXEL DEVICE\n\nLEFT:\n- no Back arrow\n- small Material stretch\n- no navigation\n- container geometry unchanged\n\nRIGHT:\nsame\n\nTAP APP:\n- one command\n- one CONFIRM haptic\n- one launch\n\nUP:\n- container follows finger\n- no Material stretch\n- threshold haptic once\n- settles expanded\n- max height ~60% usable display\n- Dock fixed\n\nDOWN:\n- container follows finger\n- no Material stretch\n- threshold haptic once\n- settles collapsed\n- Dock fixed\n\nREPEAT:\n- no flash\n- no multi-touch requirement\n- no duplicate haptic\n- no crash\n\n==================================================\n36. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\nSnapshot/hash:\nPASS\n\n==================================================\n37. PATCH DOC\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\ndocs/PATCH_001_V2_SENSITIVE_HOME_INTERACTION.md\n\nDocument:\n\n- gesture ownership\n- systemGestureExclusion API\n- horizontal Material implementation\n- vertical expansion implementation\n- 60% height calculation\n- haptic semantics\n- core isolation\n- rollback\n- device validation\n- code-security\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 001 V2 SENSITIVE HOME INTERACTION COMPLETE\n\n=== INPUT ===\n\nGesture owners: <n>\nAxis classifiers: <n>\n\nLEFT: <YES/NO>\nRIGHT: <YES/NO>\nUP: <YES/NO>\nDOWN: <YES/NO>\n\nFirst-touch blockers: <n>\n\n=== SYSTEM GESTURES ===\n\nGesture exclusion API: <value>\nHome-root exclusion owners: <n>\n\nLeft Back arrow expected: <HIDDEN/FAILED>\nRight Back arrow expected: <HIDDEN/FAILED>\n\nBottom mandatory gesture excluded: <NO/YES>\n\n=== HORIZONTAL ===\n\nMaterial overscroll owner: <n>\nLEFT navigation: <n>\nRIGHT navigation: <n>\n\nContainer movement LEFT/RIGHT: <dp>\nDock movement LEFT/RIGHT: <dp>\n\n=== VERTICAL ===\n\nVertical expansion owners: <n>\n\nCollapsed height: <dp>\nExpanded height: <dp>\nUsable display percentage: <value>\n\nUP Material stretch paths: <n>\nDOWN Material stretch paths: <n>\n\nRoot translation paths: <n>\nDock movement UP/DOWN: <dp>\n\n=== HAPTIC ===\n\nCommand haptic: <CONFIRM/OTHER>\nGesture threshold haptic: <GESTURE_THRESHOLD_ACTIVATE/CONFIRM_FALLBACK/OTHER>\n\nTap-command haptic count: <n>\nVertical MOVE haptic paths: <n>\nDuplicate haptic paths: <n>\n\nRaw Vibrator paths: <n>\nVIBRATE permission added: <NO/YES>\n\n=== CORE ===\n\nCore logic modified: <NO/YES>\nCore files touched: <n>\n\nHomeSnapshot writes: <n>\nPersistence writes: <n>\nNew lifecycle owners: <n>\n\n=== SECURITY ===\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nRollback:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\n=== BUILD ===\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8 release:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot validation:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPatch status:\n<DEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED/FAILED>\n\nPatch doc:\ndocs/PATCH_001_V2_SENSITIVE_HOME_INTERACTION.md"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:278:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787212917,"text":"PATCH FIX — VERTICAL CONTAINER EXPANSION / NO MATERIAL STRETCH\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2\n+ current sensitive interaction patch\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nUP/DOWN control only the real Home container expansion.\n\nUP:\nexpand container\n\nDOWN:\ncollapse container\n\nNO Material Stretch on UP/DOWN.\n\nExpanded geometry:\n\n- Fav reaches the top area inside the container\n- a larger empty space appears between Fav and P1\n- P1 remains fixed\n- P2 remains fixed\n- Dock remains fixed\n\nLEFT/RIGHT Material Stretch:\nKEEP UNCHANGED.\n\n==================================================\n1. DIRECTION CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\nMaterial Stretch\n\nRIGHT:\nMaterial Stretch\n\nUP:\ncontainer expansion only\n\nDOWN:\ncontainer collapse only\n\nNever mix the two systems.\n\n==================================================\n2. VERTICAL MATERIAL STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nUP OverscrollEffect paths:\n0\n\nDOWN OverscrollEffect paths:\n0\n\nVertical Material stretch:\nDISABLED\n\nHorizontal Material stretch:\nPRESERVED\n\n==================================================\n3. REAL CONTAINER GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nUP/DOWN must operate on actual layout geometry.\n\nNo visual-only:\n\ntranslationY\ngraphicsLayer translation\noffset trick\nscale\nalpha\n\nThe container's real bounds change.\n\n==================================================\n4. EXPANDED HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nTarget expanded container height:\n\napproximately 60% of usable Home display height.\n\nUse actual layout constraints and system insets.\n\nDo NOT use raw screen pixel magic numbers.\n\nFormula concept:\n\nexpandedHeight =\nusableHomeHeight * 0.60f\n\nClamp to valid parent bounds.\n\n==================================================\n5. COLLAPSED HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nKeep the current approved collapsed container geometry.\n\nDo not redesign baseline Home.\n\n==================================================\n6. FAV POSITION\n==================================================\n\nCOLLAPSED:\n\nFav remains in current baseline location.\n\nDuring expansion:\n\nFav moves within the container toward its TOP internal anchor.\n\nEXPANDED:\n\nFav top =\ncontainer top + approved internal top padding\n\nFav must NOT:\n\n- exit container\n- draw under wallpaper\n- overlap container border\n- be translated outside real layout bounds\n\n==================================================\n7. FAV REAL LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nFav movement must use real layout positioning.\n\nDo NOT use:\n\ngraphicsLayer.translationY\ntranslationY\nvisual-only offset\n\nIts touch bounds must follow its visual position.\n\n==================================================\n8. P1 POSITION\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nP1 should remain at its approved baseline Y position.\n\nUP expansion must NOT lift P1.\n\nP1 delta:\n0dp\n\n==================================================\n9. P2 POSITION\n==================================================\n\nP2:\nsame baseline position.\n\nP2 delta:\n0dp\n\n==================================================\n10. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock is completely outside vertical expansion.\n\nDock position:\nfixed\n\nDock height:\nfixed\n\nDock delta:\n0dp\n\n==================================================\n11. SEARCH GAP\n==================================================\n\nThe expansion creates a real empty region between:\n\nFav.bottom\nand\nP1.top\n\nCall it:\n\nSearchSlot\n\nFor now:\n\nSearchSlot contains NOTHING.\n\nNo Search.\nNo TextField.\nNo keyboard.\nNo history.\n\n==================================================\n12. EXPANDED SEARCH SLOT\n==================================================\n\nWhen fully expanded:\n\nFav is near container top.\n\nP1 remains fixed.\n\nTherefore:\n\nSearchSlotHeight =\nP1.top\n- Fav.bottom\n- approved gaps\n\nThis is the space future Search will use.\n\n==================================================\n13. COLLAPSED SEARCH SLOT\n==================================================\n\nWhen collapsed:\n\nSearchSlot returns to its small/minimum baseline gap.\n\nNo overlap.\n\nNo negative size.\n\n==================================================\n14. EXPANSION PROGRESS\n==================================================\n\nUse one patch-local progress:\n\n0f = collapsed\n1f = expanded\n\nOnly one owner.\n\nNo duplicate expansion state.\n\n==================================================\n15. SWIPE UP\n==================================================\n\nAfter touchSlop and vertical direction lock:\n\nUP:\n\nprogress follows finger toward 1f.\n\nContainer height increases.\n\nFav moves toward top anchor.\n\nP1/P2/Dock remain fixed.\n\n==================================================\n16. SWIPE DOWN\n==================================================\n\nWhen expanded/partially expanded:\n\nDOWN:\n\nprogress follows finger toward 0f.\n\nContainer returns toward baseline.\n\nFav returns to baseline location.\n\nP1/P2/Dock remain fixed.\n\n==================================================\n17. DIRECT PULL\n==================================================\n\nDuring vertical drag:\n\nuse direct bounded progress.\n\nDo NOT use Material OverscrollEffect.\n\nNo rubber-band beyond geometry limits.\n\n==================================================\n18. LIMITS\n==================================================\n\nHard clamp:\n\nprogress:\n0f..1f\n\nContainer height:\ncollapsedHeight..expandedHeight\n\nFav bounds:\nalways inside container\n\nSearchSlot:\nnever overlaps P1\n\n==================================================\n19. RELEASE\n==================================================\n\nAt release:\n\nuse progress + vertical velocity\n\nto select:\n\nCOLLAPSED\nor\nEXPANDED.\n\nUse one standard Compose settle primitive.\n\nNo multiple animation engines.\n\n==================================================\n20. SETTLE\n==================================================\n\nUse a restrained official Compose spring preset.\n\nTarget:\n\n- short\n- no visible bounce\n- no overshoot outside bounds\n- no Material stretch\n\nDo not add arbitrary custom timing unless required.\n\n==================================================\n21. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nVertical threshold:\n\nuse:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.GESTURE_THRESHOLD_ACTIVATE\n)\n\nonce when expansion/collapse becomes committed.\n\nIf unavailable:\nCONFIRM fallback once.\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\nNo duplicate final CONFIRM for same gesture.\n\n==================================================\n22. LEFT / RIGHT LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT modify working LEFT/RIGHT implementation.\n\nLEFT:\nMaterial Stretch\nno Back arrow\nno navigation\n\nRIGHT:\nsame\n\nHorizontal geometry writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n23. AXIS ARBITRATION\n==================================================\n\nOne classifier.\n\nHorizontal dominant:\nLEFT/RIGHT Material path\n\nVertical dominant:\nUP/DOWN expansion path\n\nNever execute both for one gesture.\n\n==================================================\n24. TOUCH SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nBefore touchSlop:\nchildren receive normal taps.\n\nP1 first tap:\nPASS\n\nP2 first tap:\nPASS\n\nDock first tap:\nPASS\n\nNo root DOWN consumption.\n\n==================================================\n25. LAYER ORDER\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nsystem wallpaper\n→ dim/background\n→ container\n→ P1/P2/SearchSlot\n→ Fav foreground content\n\nExpanded Fav must remain above the container background,\nbut inside container bounds.\n\n==================================================\n26. NO WALLPAPER BUG\n==================================================\n\nAt progress:\n\n0.00\n0.25\n0.50\n0.75\n1.00\n\nverify:\n\nFav under wallpaper:\nNO\n\nContainer under wallpaper:\nNO\n\nFav outside container:\nNO\n\nSearchSlot overlap P1:\nNO\n\n==================================================\n27. NO ALPHA MOTION\n==================================================\n\nUP/DOWN:\n\nalpha animation = 0\nfade = 0\nwallpaper dim animation = 0\n\nOnly geometry changes.\n\n==================================================\n28. CORE ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nLauncherPreferences writes:\n0\n\nAppCatalog writes:\n0\n\nP1/P2/Dock state writes:\n0\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nPersistence:\n0\n\n==================================================\n29. PATCH BOUNDARY\n==================================================\n\nKeep all vertical expansion logic inside the interaction patch.\n\nCore hook:\nno additional hooks.\n\nDo not spread expansion code into P1/P2/Dock composables.\n\n==================================================\n30. STATIC BOUNDS AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nReport at progress:\n\n0.00\n0.25\n0.50\n0.75\n1.00\n\nfor:\n\nContainer.top\nContainer.bottom\nFav.top\nFav.bottom\nSearchSlot.height\nP1.top\nP2.top\nDock.top\n\nRequired invariants:\n\nP1.top constant\nP2.top constant\nDock.top constant\n\nFav stays inside container.\n\n==================================================\n31. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA VERTICAL CONTAINER EXPANSION COMPLETE\n\n=== HORIZONTAL ===\n\nLEFT Material Stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRIGHT Material Stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nLeft/Right implementation modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\n=== VERTICAL ===\n\nUP Material Stretch paths:\n<n>\n\nDOWN Material Stretch paths:\n<n>\n\nVertical expansion owner:\n<n>\n\nCollapsed container height:\n<dp>\n\nExpanded container height:\n<dp>\n\nExpanded usable display percentage:\n<value>\n\nFav top collapsed:\n<dp>\n\nFav top expanded:\n<dp>\n\nFav inside container:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearchSlot collapsed height:\n<dp>\n\nSearchSlot expanded height:\n<dp>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nVertical root translation paths:\n<n>\n\n=== HAPTIC ===\n\nVertical haptic:\n<GESTURE_THRESHOLD_ACTIVATE/CONFIRM_FALLBACK/OTHER>\n\nMOVE haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate vertical haptic paths:\n<n>\n\n=== SAFETY ===\n\nFav under wallpaper:\n<NO/YES>\n\nContainer under wallpaper:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearchSlot overlap P1:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCore logic modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nDEVICE VALIDATION REQUIRED:\nYES"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:279:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787213276,"text":"FASE: MACHINA — PATCH 001 V2 FINAL VALIDATION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nPATCH:\nPATCH 001 V2 — SENSITIVE HOME INTERACTION\n\nDEVICE TEST:\nPASS\n\nCORE V2:\nSTABLE CANDIDATE / FROZEN FOR THIS VALIDATION\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nNON cambiare:\n- motion\n- gesture sensitivity\n- LEFT/RIGHT Material Stretch\n- edge exclusion\n- haptic\n- UI\n- geometry\n- P1/P2/Dock\n- Core V2 behavior\n\nQuesta fase è VALIDATION ONLY.\n\n==================================================\n1. APPLY CODE SECURITY POLICY\n==================================================\n\nApplicare:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nSe il documento non esiste:\nSTOP\n\nNon inventare una policy sostitutiva.\n\n==================================================\n2. PATCH BOUNDARY AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nVerificare:\n\nCore logic writes from patch = 0\nHomeSnapshot writes = 0\nLauncherPreferences writes = 0\nAppCatalog internal writes = 0\n\nNew persistence = 0\nNew lifecycle owners = 0\n\n==================================================\n3. INPUT AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nVerificare:\n\ngesture owners = 1 preferred\naxis classifier owners = 1 preferred\nduplicate pointer owners = 0\nfirst-touch blockers = 0\n\nLEFT/RIGHT:\nMaterial Stretch\n\nSystem Back arrow:\nexcluded on Home root\n\nNo unintended navigation.\n\n==================================================\n4. MOTION AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nVerificare che non siano rimasti path legacy attivi:\n\ncustom wobble\nduplicate spring\nduplicate overscroll\ntranslation hacks\nalpha/fade motion\nold Fav/container motion\n\nNon rimuovere nulla se non è CONFIRMED DEAD.\n\nSe serve una modifica runtime per superare l'audit:\nSTOP.\n\nQuesta validazione non deve cambiare il feeling già approvato.\n\n==================================================\n5. HAPTIC AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nVerificare uso di:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(...)\n\nNo raw Vibrator path unless explicitly required.\n\nNo duplicate haptic for one accepted command.\n\nNo continuous MOVE haptic.\n\nNo unnecessary VIBRATE permission.\n\n==================================================\n6. LIFECYCLE / PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nPatch must add:\n\nonResume refresh paths = 0\nkeep-alive paths = 0\nWakeLock paths = 0\npolling paths = 0\n\nGesture path must perform:\n\ndisk IO = 0\nPackageManager work = 0\nnetwork = 0\nbitmap decode = 0\n\n==================================================\n7. SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nreflection unnecessary = 0\ndynamic code loading = 0\nembedded credentials = 0\nbroad R8 keep rules added by patch = 0\n\n==================================================\n8. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nDocument exact rollback:\n\npatch files\n+\nsingle integration hook\n\nRemoving those must restore Core V2.\n\nRollback:\nPASS/FAIL\n\n==================================================\n9. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 release = SUCCESS\nsnapshot validation = PASS\nSHA-256 validation = PASS\n\nNO adb.\nNO install.\n\n==================================================\n10. FINAL STATUS\n==================================================\n\nOnly if ALL gates PASS:\n\nPATCH 001 V2 status:\nVALIDATED\n\nThen freeze patch behavior.\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nPATCH_001_V2_SENSITIVE_HOME_INTERACTION.md\n\nAdd:\n\nSTATUS: VALIDATED\nDEVICE: PASS\nCODE_SECURITY: PASS\nDEBUG: PASS\nR8: PASS\nROLLBACK: PASS\n\n==================================================\n11. CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nOnly after validation PASS:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint patch-001-sensitive-validated\n\n==================================================\n12. DO NOT CONTINUE\n==================================================\n\nAfter checkpoint:\n\nSTOP.\n\nDo not implement Search.\nDo not implement another patch.\nDo not refactor Core.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 001 V2 VALIDATION COMPLETE\n\nDevice validation: PASS\n\nCore logic modified by validation: <NO/YES>\nPatch runtime modified by validation: <NO/YES>\n\nCore writes: <n>\nHomeSnapshot writes: <n>\nPersistence writes: <n>\n\nGesture owners: <n>\nDuplicate input owners: <n>\nFirst-touch blockers: <n>\n\nMotion owners: <n>\nLegacy active motion paths: <n>\nDuplicate motion paths: <n>\n\nHaptic owners: <n>\nMOVE haptic paths: <n>\nDuplicate haptic paths: <n>\n\nLifecycle owners added: <n>\nKeep-alive paths: <n>\nMain-thread heavy gesture paths: <n>\n\nCode-security: <PASS/FAIL>\nRollback: <PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug build: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8 release: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nSnapshot validation: <PASS/FAIL>\nSHA-256 validation: <PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\n<VALIDATED/FAILED>\n\nCheckpoint:\n<path/N-A>\n\nADB used: NO\nAPK installed: NO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:280:{"session_id":"01a01d19-caa0-7921-a3ec-211c73fb2cc5","ts":1787213357,"text":"cat > /opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md <<'EOF'\n# MACHINA PATCH CODE SECURITY POLICY\n\nStatus: ACTIVE\nApplies to: ALL Machina feature patches\nCore target: Machina Core V2\n\n## 1. Core isolation\n\n- Core logic must remain unchanged unless a patch explicitly declares a core migration.\n- Maximum one declared integration hook into the core.\n- Direct writes to HomeSnapshot: 0\n- Direct writes to P1/P2/Dock state: 0\n- Direct writes to LauncherPreferences core slot storage: 0\n- Direct writes to AppCatalog internals: 0\n- Patch rollback must restore the previous validated core/runtime.\n\n## 2. State ownership\n\n- Every new mutable state has one clear owner.\n- Duplicate state owners are forbidden.\n- Global mutable state is forbidden unless explicitly justified.\n- Persistence must be explicitly declared.\n- Transient UI state must not leak into Core persistence.\n\n## 3. Input safety\n\n- One gesture owner per interaction domain.\n- No duplicate pointer handlers.\n- No full-screen handler may consume DOWN before touch slop without necessity.\n- P1/P2/Dock first-touch behavior must remain valid.\n- No accidental multi-touch requirement.\n- Horizontal and vertical gesture ownership must be deterministic.\n\n## 4. Lifecycle safety\n\n- No unnecessary lifecycle owner may be introduced.\n- No listener leak.\n- No refresh storm.\n- No state reset on every onResume.\n- No keep-alive behavior.\n- Listener registration and cleanup must be deterministic.\n\n## 5. Threading\n\n- Heavy PackageManager work must not run on the main thread.\n- No raw Thread unless explicitly justified.\n- Coroutine ownership must be clear.\n- Stale asynchronous results must not overwrite newer state.\n\n## 6. Motion\n\n- One motion owner per feature.\n- Duplicate motion engines are forbidden.\n- Legacy animation paths must not remain active in parallel.\n- No custom alpha/fade/translation/scale path unless explicitly required by the patch.\n- Prefer Android/Compose/Material platform primitives over emulation.\n- Layout geometry must not be mutated by visual-only motion unless the feature explicitly requires real geometry changes.\n\n## 7. Haptic\n\n- Prefer View.performHapticFeedback(...).\n- Do not use raw Vibrator/VibrationEffect unless explicitly required.\n- No haptic during continuous MOVE unless feature semantics explicitly require it.\n- One accepted command or gesture must not trigger duplicate haptics.\n- Do not add android.permission.VIBRATE unless genuinely necessary.\n\n## 8. Data / cache\n\n- Reuse existing AppCatalog and core data sources.\n- No PackageManager scan per keystroke or gesture.\n- Cache must be bounded.\n- Android owns process caching.\n- Patches must not add Service, WakeLock, polling, alarms, or process-priority tricks to remain resident.\n\n## 9. Error handling\n\n- catch(Throwable) is forbidden unless explicitly justified.\n- Local failures must not crash the Home.\n- Missing/uninstalled apps must fail safely.\n- Malformed optional patch data must degrade safely.\n- Silent failure paths should be minimized and documented.\n\n## 10. Security / hardening\n\n- No unnecessary reflection.\n- No dynamic code loading.\n- No embedded credentials or secrets.\n- No broad R8 keep rules without justification.\n- No private keys or signing secrets in source, snapshots, docs, outputs, or checkpoints.\n- Release minify/shrink/obfuscation must remain enabled where configured.\n\n## 11. Performance\n\nDuring gesture/input/render hot paths:\n\n- disk IO = 0\n- network = 0\n- PackageManager heavy work = 0\n- bitmap decode = 0\n- avoid heavy per-frame allocation\n\nIdle Home should not poll or perform continuous work.\n\n## 12. Patch rollback\n\nEvery patch document must state:\n\n- files added\n- files modified\n- core hook\n- state introduced\n- persistence introduced\n- lifecycle ownership\n- rollback procedure\n\nRemoving patch files plus the declared hook must restore the previous validated baseline.\n\n## 13. Validation gate\n\nA patch may be marked VALIDATED only when all applicable gates pass:\n\n- DEVICE TEST: PASS\n- STATIC AUDIT: PASS\n- CORE ISOLATION: PASS\n- INPUT SAFETY: PASS\n- STATE OWNERSHIP: PASS\n- LIFECYCLE: PASS\n- MOTION OWNERSHIP: PASS\n- HAPTIC OWNERSHIP: PASS\n- CODE SECURITY: PASS\n- DEBUG BUILD: SUCCESS\n- R8 RELEASE BUILD: SUCCESS\n- SNAPSHOT/HASH VALIDATION: PASS\n- ROLLBACK: PASS\n- CHECKPOINT: CREATED\n\nIf any required gate fails:\n\nPATCH STATUS = NOT VALIDATED\n\nDo not build additional feature patches on top until the failure is understood or explicitly waived.\n\n## 14. Validation must not change approved behavior\n\nThe validation phase is not a feature-development phase.\n\nIf runtime behavior must change to pass validation:\n\nSTOP.\n\nReport the issue and require a separate corrective patch.\n\n## 15. Core process-cache policy\n\n- Android owns process caching and residency.\n- Machina does not attempt to keep its process alive.\n- Valid in-memory state may be reused naturally while the process survives.\n- Correctness must not depend on process survival.\nEOF"}
