/root/.codex/history.jsonl:290:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787217777,"text":"PATCH 002 V2 — FIX SEARCH SLOT + FORCE SEARCH BAR VISIBLE\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2\n+ PATCH 001 V2 [VALIDATED / FROZEN]\n+ current PATCH 002 Search Bar UI\n\nPROBLEM FROM DEVICE:\n\n- Fav → P1 spacing exists but is still too small\n- Search bar is NOT visible\n- PATCH 001 behavior must remain untouched\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\n1. Increase real space between Fav and P1\n2. Render Search bar visibly inside that space\n3. Keep P1/P2/Dock fixed\n4. Do not modify gestures/motion from PATCH 001\n\n==================================================\n1. PATCH 001 HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 001 files modified:\n0\n\nLEFT/RIGHT Material Stretch:\nUNCHANGED\n\ngesture exclusion:\nUNCHANGED\n\nhaptic:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n2. INCREASE SEARCH SLOT\n==================================================\n\nIncrease the real layout space between:\n\nFav.bottom\nand\nP1.top\n\nTarget first device test:\n\nSearchSlot height:\n72dp minimum\n\nPreferred available range:\n72dp–96dp\n\nDo NOT move P1.\n\nIf space is insufficient:\nextend only the upper container area,\nnot P1/P2/Dock.\n\n==================================================\n3. FIXED ELEMENTS\n==================================================\n\nP1 movement:\n0dp\n\nP2 movement:\n0dp\n\nDock movement:\n0dp\n\nFav should remain in its current approved position\nunless only internal container top padding requires adjustment.\n\n==================================================\n4. SEARCH BAR MUST BE COMPOSED\n==================================================\n\nThe Search bar must be actually present in SearchSlot.\n\nDo NOT gate it behind a visibility state for this test.\n\nTEMPORARY DEVICE-VALIDATION MODE:\n\nSearch bar:\nALWAYS VISIBLE\n\nThis is intentional so we can validate layout/UI first.\n\nNo swipe dependency yet.\n\n==================================================\n5. SEARCH BAR UI\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nmagnifier icon on left\nBasicTextField\nsingle underline\n\nLayout concept:\n\n[ magnifier ]  cursor/input\n────────────────────────────\n\nNO:\npill\ncard\nfilled background\nouter border\nshadow\n\n==================================================\n6. SEARCH POSITION\n==================================================\n\nPlace Search bar vertically centered\ninside SearchSlot.\n\nKeep enough padding above/below.\n\nSuggested:\n\nhorizontal padding:\n8–12dp\n\nvertical available space:\n~72dp minimum\n\n==================================================\n7. MAGNIFIER\n==================================================\n\nMaterial Search icon:\n\n18–20dp\n\nColor:\ncurrent onSurface/onSurfaceVariant token\n\n==================================================\n8. UNDERLINE\n==================================================\n\nSingle line only:\n\n~1dp\n\nFull remaining width.\n\nUse subtle Material contrast.\n\nNo additional box outline.\n\n==================================================\n9. INPUT\n==================================================\n\nBasicTextField:\n\nsingleLine = true\n\nCursor:\nvisible\n\nenabled:\ntrue\n\nfocusable:\ntrue\n\nDo not use alpha 0.\n\nDo not use zero height.\n\n==================================================\n10. FOCUS FOR TEST\n==================================================\n\nFor this test:\n\nSearch bar visible immediately.\n\nDo NOT auto-open keyboard on Home entry.\n\nKeyboard opens when user taps field.\n\nReason:\nfirst validate the bar is visible and correctly placed.\n\n==================================================\n11. NO AUTO IME YET\n==================================================\n\nTemporarily disable:\n\nautomatic FocusRequester trigger\nautomatic keyboardController.show()\n\nKeep those helpers if needed,\nbut do not fire them automatically.\n\nThis removes focus/IME as a variable while validating layout.\n\n==================================================\n12. BOUNDS AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nReport actual runtime/layout bounds:\n\nFav.bottom\nSearchSlot.top\nSearchSlot.bottom\nSearchBar.top\nSearchBar.bottom\nP1.top\n\nRequired:\n\nFav.bottom < SearchBar.top\nSearchBar.bottom < P1.top\n\nNo clipping.\n\n==================================================\n13. Z ORDER\n==================================================\n\nSearch bar must be above:\n\ncontainer background\n\nand below/independent of Fav/P1 foreground.\n\nNo wallpaper overdraw.\n\nNo clipping parent.\n\n==================================================\n14. NO SEARCH ENGINE\n==================================================\n\nStill DO NOT implement:\n\napp filtering\nresults\nhistory\nweb search\nsystem settings search\n\nThis fix is UI/layout only.\n\n==================================================\n15. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nNew motion owners:\n0\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nPersistence writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n16. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 002 SEARCH BAR VISIBILITY FIX COMPLETE\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearchSlot height:\n<dp>\n\nFav → P1 gap:\n<dp>\n\nSearch bar composed:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearch bar visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nBasicTextField bounds:\n<value>\n\nMagnifier visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nUnderline visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nAuto focus enabled:\n<NO/YES>\n\nKeyboard auto-open:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nClipping risk:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nZ-order risk:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:291:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787218498,"text":"PATCH 002 V2 — IME + VISIBILITY + AXIS ISOLATION FIX\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2\n+ PATCH 001 V2 Sensitive Home Interaction [VALIDATED/FROZEN]\n+ PATCH 002 V2 Search Bar UI\n\nDEVICE BUGS CONFIRMED:\n\n1. IME/keyboard opening compresses or shifts Home layout\n2. Search bar is visible without requiring swipe UP\n3. LEFT/RIGHT incorrectly collapse/retract Fav\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFix ONLY PATCH 002.\n\nPATCH 001 must remain byte/behavior unchanged.\n\n==================================================\n1. PATCH 001 HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT MODIFY:\n\nPATCH 001 files\nLEFT Material Stretch\nRIGHT Material Stretch\nedge exclusion\nPATCH 001 haptic\nhorizontal gesture classifier\n\nPATCH 001 regression allowed:\nNONE\n\n==================================================\n2. SEARCH VISIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nSearch bar must NOT be always visible.\n\nRequired:\n\nCOLLAPSED:\nSearch bar = HIDDEN\n\nEXPANDED after valid SWIPE UP:\nSearch bar = VISIBLE\n\nSWIPE DOWN:\nSearch bar = HIDDEN\n\nNo other gesture changes visibility.\n\n==================================================\n3. PATCH 002 VERTICAL ONLY\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 002 gesture logic must react ONLY to dominant vertical drag.\n\nUP:\nexpand/reveal Search\n\nDOWN:\ncollapse/hide Search\n\nLEFT:\nIGNORED BY PATCH 002\n\nRIGHT:\nIGNORED BY PATCH 002\n\n==================================================\n4. AXIS LOCK\n==================================================\n\nAfter touchSlop:\n\nif abs(deltaX) > abs(deltaY):\nPATCH 002 must not mutate any state.\n\nReturn horizontal interaction to PATCH 001.\n\nif abs(deltaY) > abs(deltaX):\nPATCH 002 may process UP/DOWN.\n\nNo mixed-axis handling.\n\n==================================================\n5. LEFT / RIGHT MUST NOT CHANGE FAV\n==================================================\n\nDuring LEFT or RIGHT swipe:\n\nFav expansion state:\nUNCHANGED\n\nSearch visibility:\nUNCHANGED\n\nSearchSlot height:\nUNCHANGED\n\nContainer geometry:\nUNCHANGED\n\nPATCH 002 haptic:\n0\n\n==================================================\n6. FIX IME LAYOUT BUG\n==================================================\n\nCurrent device screenshot shows keyboard opening\ncauses the Home/container to be compressed or repositioned.\n\nDo not let IME resize the Home geometry.\n\nAudit:\n\nWindowSoftInputMode\nimePadding()\nWindowInsets.ime\nwindowInsetsPadding()\nnavigationBarsPadding()\nconsumeWindowInsets()\nenableEdgeToEdge()\n\n==================================================\n7. IME STRATEGY\n==================================================\n\nPreferred behavior:\n\nKeyboard overlays lower screen area.\n\nHome geometry above it remains unchanged.\n\nDo NOT animate or recompute:\n\ncontainer height\nFav position\nP1 position\nP2 position\nDock position\n\nbased on IME height.\n\n==================================================\n8. DO NOT USE IME FOR HOME SIZE\n==================================================\n\nSearch/Fav expanded geometry must be calculated from\nnormal Home layout constraints,\n\nNOT from:\n\navailable height after IME\nWindowInsets.ime bottom\nkeyboard height\n\nIME presence must not change expansion bounds.\n\n==================================================\n9. REMOVE IME-DRIVEN PADDING\n==================================================\n\nIf current Search/Home root uses:\n\nModifier.imePadding()\n\nand this moves/compresses the whole Home:\n\nremove it from the Home layout.\n\nApply IME handling only to the Search input layer\nif necessary.\n\nDo not globally pad P1/P2/Dock for IME.\n\n==================================================\n10. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock baseline position:\nfixed.\n\nWhen IME opens:\n\nDo NOT move Dock upward.\n\nIt is acceptable for keyboard to visually cover\nlower Home content while Search is active.\n\nDo not reflow Home to keep Dock visible.\n\n==================================================\n11. P1 / P2\n==================================================\n\nWhen keyboard opens:\n\nP1 y delta = 0dp\nP2 y delta = 0dp\n\nNo resize.\n\nNo scroll-to-fit.\n\n==================================================\n12. FAV\n==================================================\n\nWhen keyboard opens:\n\nFav y delta = 0dp\n\nFav bounds:\nunchanged from expanded state.\n\n==================================================\n13. SEARCH FOCUS\n==================================================\n\nAfter UP expansion is accepted:\n\nSearch becomes visible\n→ requestFocus()\n→ keyboard.show()\n\nDo not request focus during partial drag.\n\n==================================================\n14. SEARCH COLLAPSE\n==================================================\n\nOn valid DOWN:\n\n1. clear Search focus\n2. hide keyboard\n3. Search bar hidden\n4. expansion state collapsed\n\nLEFT/RIGHT do NONE of these.\n\n==================================================\n15. BACK\n==================================================\n\nWhile Search is visible/focused:\n\nBack:\nclear focus\nhide keyboard\ncollapse Search\n\nHome collapsed:\nexisting Core/PATCH001 Back contract unchanged.\n\nDo not add duplicate BackHandler.\n\n==================================================\n16. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 002 haptic only for accepted vertical state changes.\n\nUP accepted:\none GESTURE_THRESHOLD_ACTIVATE\nor existing fallback\n\nDOWN accepted:\none\n\nLEFT:\n0\n\nRIGHT:\n0\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\nTyping:\n0\n\n==================================================\n17. SEARCH BAR UI\n==================================================\n\nKeep current approved UI:\n\nmagnifier left\nBasicTextField\nsingle underline\n\nNo design change.\n\n==================================================\n18. SEARCH SLOT\n==================================================\n\nKeep current approved SearchSlot dimensions\nunless required only to eliminate clipping.\n\nDo not redesign spacing in this fix.\n\n==================================================\n19. STATE OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 002 state owners:\n1\n\nNo duplicate expanded state.\nNo duplicate query state.\n\nHorizontal state writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n20. STATIC DEVICE CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nCOLLAPSED:\n\nSearch hidden\nkeyboard hidden\n\nSWIPE UP:\n\nSearch visible\ncursor active\nkeyboard opens\nFav/P1/P2/Dock geometry stays correct\n\nLEFT while expanded:\n\nPATCH001 Material Stretch only\nSearch stays expanded\nFav does not retract\nkeyboard stays according to current focus\n\nRIGHT while expanded:\n\nsame\n\nSWIPE DOWN:\n\nkeyboard hides\nSearch hides\ncollapse\n\n==================================================\n21. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nPATCH 001 files modified = 0\nCore logic modified = 0\n\nHomeSnapshot writes = 0\nPersistence writes = 0\n\nDuplicate gesture owners = 0\nDuplicate BackHandlers = 0\nFirst-touch blockers = 0\n\n==================================================\n22. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 002 IME / AXIS FIX COMPLETE\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearch visible collapsed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearch visible after UP:\n<YES/NO>\n\nLEFT changes Fav/Search state:\n<NO/YES>\n\nRIGHT changes Fav/Search state:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHorizontal PATCH002 state writes:\n<n>\n\nKeyboard shifts Fav:\n<NO/YES>\n\nKeyboard shifts P1:\n<NO/YES>\n\nKeyboard shifts P2:\n<NO/YES>\n\nKeyboard shifts Dock:\n<NO/YES>\n\nGlobal imePadding paths:\n<n>\n\nAuto focus after accepted UP:\n<YES/NO>\n\nKeyboard auto-open:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDOWN hides keyboard/Search:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDuplicate gesture owners:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate BackHandlers:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nLEFT/RIGHT PATCH001 regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:292:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787221399,"text":"PATCH 002 V2 — SEARCH SPACING / COLLAPSED GAP FIX\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2\n+ PATCH 001 V2 [VALIDATED / FROZEN]\n+ current PATCH 002 Search Bar UI\n\nDEVICE REFERENCE:\n- expanded/search screenshot: Search works\n- collapsed screenshot: unused empty Search space remains\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\n1. When EXPANDED:\n   increase spacing between Fav and Search bar.\n\n2. When COLLAPSED:\n   remove the unused SearchSlot completely.\n   No empty reserved area between Fav and P1.\n\nDO NOT modify PATCH 001.\n\n==================================================\n1. PATCH 001 LOCK\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 001 files modified:\n0\n\nLEFT/RIGHT Material Stretch:\nUNCHANGED\n\nhaptic:\nUNCHANGED\n\ngesture exclusion:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n2. EXPANDED LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nWhen Search is visible:\n\nFav\n↓\nlarger intentional gap\n↓\nSearch bar\n↓\nsmall controlled gap\n↓\nP1\n\nIncrease Fav → Search spacing.\n\nStarting target:\n\nFav bottom → Search content:\n24dp\n\nAllow:\n20–28dp\n\nUse one token.\n\nDo not hardcode multiple paddings.\n\n==================================================\n3. SEARCH BAR\n==================================================\n\nKeep current design exactly:\n\nmagnifier left\ncursor/input\nsingle underline\n\nNo pill.\nNo card.\nNo additional border.\n\n==================================================\n4. SEARCH → P1 GAP\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT leave a large unused area below Search.\n\nAfter underline:\n\nuse only normal section spacing.\n\nTarget:\n12–16dp\n\nThen P1 begins.\n\n==================================================\n5. COLLAPSED LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nWhen Search is hidden:\n\nSearchSlot height:\n0dp\n\nSearch bar:\nNOT COMPOSED\n\nSearch underline:\nNOT COMPOSED\n\nSearch padding:\n0dp\n\nReserved Search space:\n0dp\n\n==================================================\n6. COLLAPSED FAV → P1\n==================================================\n\nCollapsed Home must return to the normal compact layout:\n\nFav\n↓\nnormal section gap\n↓\nP1\n\nTarget visual gap:\nsame family used by existing Home panels.\n\nNo large empty black region.\n\n==================================================\n7. IMPORTANT GEOMETRY MODEL\n==================================================\n\nThe Search space exists ONLY while expanded.\n\nCOLLAPSED:\n\nFav\nnormal gap\nP1\nP2\n\nEXPANDED:\n\nFav\n24dp approx gap\nSearch\n12–16dp approx gap\nP1\nP2\n\n==================================================\n8. NO INVISIBLE SPACER\n==================================================\n\nSearch hidden must not leave:\n\nSpacer(SearchSlotHeight)\nempty Box\nfixed minHeight\nreserved weight\ninvisible BasicTextField bounds\nalpha=0 Search container\n\nTarget:\n\nhidden Search layout footprint = 0dp\n\n==================================================\n9. EXPANSION\n==================================================\n\nUse existing PATCH 002 UP/DOWN state.\n\nUP:\nallocate Search layout space\n\nDOWN:\nremove Search layout space completely\n\nDo not add another gesture owner.\n\n==================================================\n10. IME\n==================================================\n\nKeep current IME fix.\n\nKeyboard must not create additional permanent spacing.\n\nWhen keyboard closes:\nlayout returns to correct expanded/collapsed geometry.\n\n==================================================\n11. LEFT / RIGHT\n==================================================\n\nLEFT/RIGHT must never:\n\ncollapse Search\nchange SearchSlot height\nchange Fav vertical state\n\nPATCH 002 horizontal state writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n12. STATE\n==================================================\n\nKeep existing PATCH 002 state owner.\n\nNo new state.\n\nNo persistence.\n\n==================================================\n13. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\nNO\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nNew motion owners:\n0\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nPersistence writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n14. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 002 SEARCH SPACING FIX COMPLETE\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nEXPANDED:\n\nFav → Search gap:\n<dp>\n\nSearch → P1 gap:\n<dp>\n\nSearch visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCOLLAPSED:\n\nSearch visible:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearchSlot height:\n<dp>\n\nReserved hidden Search space:\n<dp>\n\nFav → P1 gap:\n<dp>\n\nInvisible Search layout footprint:\n<dp>\n\nLEFT changes Search state:\n<NO/YES>\n\nRIGHT changes Search state:\n<NO/YES>\n\nIME regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:293:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787233251,"text":"PATCH 002 V2 — DOUBLE SEARCH SPACE + RESULTS ABOVE BAR\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2\n+ PATCH 001 V2 [VALIDATED / FROZEN]\n+ current PATCH 002 Search Bar UI\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\n1. In EXPANDED state:\n   double the current Search area approximately.\n\n2. Results area must be ABOVE the Search bar.\n\n3. Search bar remains near the bottom of SearchSlot,\n   directly above P1.\n\n4. In COLLAPSED state:\n   SearchSlot footprint returns to 0dp.\n\nDO NOT modify PATCH 001.\n\n==================================================\n1. EXPANDED SEARCH SLOT SIZE\n==================================================\n\nCurrent SearchSlot is too small.\n\nIncrease expanded SearchSlot to approximately:\n\n2x current effective height.\n\nIf current effective SearchSlot is ~72–96dp:\n\ntarget initial expanded range:\n144–192dp\n\nUse available real layout constraints.\n\nDo NOT exceed safe space above P1.\n\n==================================================\n2. LAYOUT ORDER\n==================================================\n\nInside expanded SearchSlot use this exact order:\n\nResultsArea\nSearchBar\n\nNOT:\n\nSearchBar\nResultsArea\n\n==================================================\n3. RESULTS AREA\n==================================================\n\nResultsArea occupies the upper portion of SearchSlot.\n\nSearch bar stays anchored toward bottom of SearchSlot.\n\nResultsArea:\n\n- transparent background\n- no card\n- no border\n- no shadow\n- compact vertical list later\n\nFor now it may be empty if Search engine is not active yet.\n\n==================================================\n4. SEARCH BAR POSITION\n==================================================\n\nSearch bar:\n\nnear bottom of SearchSlot\n\nStructure:\n\nResultsArea\nSpacer/minimum gap\nSearchBar\n\nThen:\nnormal small gap\nP1\n\n==================================================\n5. FAV → RESULTS GAP\n==================================================\n\nFav must have a comfortable gap above results.\n\nTarget baseline:\n\nFav bottom → ResultsArea top:\n~20–24dp\n\nUse one spacing token.\n\n==================================================\n6. RESULTS → SEARCH BAR GAP\n==================================================\n\nUse compact spacing:\n\n~8–12dp\n\nDo not waste vertical area.\n\n==================================================\n7. SEARCH BAR → P1 GAP\n==================================================\n\nKeep small controlled gap:\n\n~12–16dp\n\nP1 remains fixed.\n\n==================================================\n8. COLLAPSED STATE\n==================================================\n\nWhen Search is closed:\n\nSearchSlot height:\n0dp\n\nResultsArea:\nNOT COMPOSED\n\nSearchBar:\nNOT COMPOSED\n\nReserved Search space:\n0dp\n\nFav → P1 returns to normal compact gap.\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH RESULT PLACEMENT CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nFuture PATCH 003 Search Engine must render results\nONLY into ResultsArea.\n\nResults must never appear below SearchBar.\n\n==================================================\n10. MAX RESULT ROWS\n==================================================\n\nDesign target for later:\n\n3 compact result rows visible\nwithout moving P1.\n\nIf more:\ninternal scroll inside ResultsArea.\n\nDo not move Home geometry.\n\n==================================================\n11. P1/P2/DOCK LOCK\n==================================================\n\nP1 movement:\n0dp\n\nP2 movement:\n0dp\n\nDock movement:\n0dp\n\n==================================================\n12. PATCH 001 LOCK\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\nNO\n\nLEFT/RIGHT Material Stretch:\nUNCHANGED\n\nedge handling:\nUNCHANGED\n\nhaptic:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n13. IME\n==================================================\n\nKeyboard must not resize SearchSlot geometry.\n\nExpanded SearchSlot dimensions are independent\nof IME height.\n\nNo imePadding on whole Home root.\n\n==================================================\n14. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nNew motion owners:\n0\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nPersistence writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n15. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 002 DOUBLE SEARCH SPACE COMPLETE\n\nExpanded SearchSlot height:\n<dp>\n\nPrevious SearchSlot height:\n<dp>\n\nExpansion ratio:\n<value>\n\nFav → Results gap:\n<dp>\n\nResultsArea height:\n<dp>\n\nResults → SearchBar gap:\n<dp>\n\nSearchBar → P1 gap:\n<dp>\n\nResults above SearchBar:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCollapsed SearchSlot height:\n<dp>\n\nReserved hidden Search space:\n<dp>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nIME regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:294:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787233795,"text":"PATCH 004 V2 — MATERIAL 3 SETTINGS SHELL\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2\n+ PATCH 001 VALIDATED/FROZEN\n+ PATCH 002 current\n+ PATCH 003 future/search-engine compatible\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nFROZEN\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAdd a complete Material 3 Settings shell with\nmain categories and sub-categories.\n\nThis phase creates navigation/UI structure only.\n\nDo NOT modify Core behavior yet.\n\n==================================================\n1. PATCH LOCATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\npatches/settings/\n    SettingsPatch.kt\n\nIf necessary:\nSettingsModel.kt\n\nPrefer max 2 files initially.\n\n==================================================\n2. SETTINGS ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nProvide one explicit Settings entry point.\n\nDo NOT put Settings logic inside MainActivity.\n\nDo NOT modify Core navigation architecture.\n\nUse one patch hook.\n\n==================================================\n3. MAIN SETTINGS SCREEN\n==================================================\n\nMaterial 3.\n\nUse:\n\n- compact top app bar\n- category rows\n- small explicit icons\n- title\n- optional short subtitle\n- chevron/end indicator\n\nNo giant cards.\n\nNo oversized spacing.\n\n==================================================\n4. CATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nCreate these main categories:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nInteraction\nSystem\nAbout\n\n==================================================\n5. APPEARANCE\n==================================================\n\nSub-categories/placeholders:\n\nIcon shape\nDynamic color\nSurface style\nBorders and corners\nWallpaper dim\n\nNo runtime changes yet unless already supported safely.\n\n==================================================\n6. HOME\n==================================================\n\nSub-categories/placeholders:\n\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\nLayout spacing\n\nNo slot mutation in this phase.\n\n==================================================\n7. SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nSub-categories/placeholders:\n\nSearch behavior\nSearch sources\nHistory\nKeyboard and focus\n\nCompatible with PATCH 002 / PATCH 003.\n\nDo not duplicate Search state.\n\n==================================================\n8. INTERACTION\n==================================================\n\nSub-categories/placeholders:\n\nHaptic\nLEFT / RIGHT\nUP / DOWN\nMotion\n\nDo not modify PATCH 001.\n\nShow current values read-only if easily available.\n\n==================================================\n9. SYSTEM\n==================================================\n\nInclude:\n\nSet as default Home\nApp info\n\nOptional:\nrelevant permissions/system destinations.\n\nUse supported Android Intents / RoleManager only.\n\nNo hidden API.\n\n==================================================\n10. ABOUT\n==================================================\n\nInclude:\n\nApp version\nBuild information\nChangelog\nPatch status\nLicenses\n\n==================================================\n11. PATCH STATUS\n==================================================\n\nShow active patch information:\n\nCore V2\nPATCH 001\nPATCH 002\nfuture PATCH 003\nPATCH 004\n\nPrefer read-only metadata.\n\nDo not parse arbitrary source files at runtime.\n\n==================================================\n12. NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nSettings root\n→ category\n→ sub-category\n\nBack:\nsub-category → category\ncategory → Settings root\nSettings root → Home\n\nUse one navigation owner local to PATCH 004.\n\n==================================================\n13. MATERIAL 3\n==================================================\n\nUse Material 3 components.\n\nPrefer:\n\nListItem\nHorizontalDivider\nSwitch where relevant\nRadioButton where relevant\nSlider only where truly needed\n\nDynamic Color support may be added later.\n\n==================================================\n14. ICONS\n==================================================\n\nSmall explicit Material icons.\n\nDo not add large icon dependency if existing Material icons\nalready cover requirements.\n\n==================================================\n15. STATE\n==================================================\n\nThis phase:\n\nnavigation state only.\n\nNo duplicate Core state.\n\nNo HomeSnapshot writes.\n\nNo P1/P2/Dock writes.\n\n==================================================\n16. PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nNo new setting persistence until individual options are implemented.\n\nDo not add placeholder keys.\n\n==================================================\n17. CORE ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 002 modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 003 modified:\nNO\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nLauncherPreferences writes:\n0 for this phase\n\n==================================================\n18. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nUse existing semantic haptic policy for accepted commands.\n\nDo not create a second global haptic system.\n\n==================================================\n19. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nSettings should be lazy/cheap.\n\nNo package scan.\n\nNo wallpaper decode.\n\nNo continuous polling.\n\n==================================================\n20. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nRemoving settings patch + hook:\n\nHome continues exactly as before.\n\n==================================================\n21. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n22. PATCH DOC\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\ndocs/PATCH_004_V2_SETTINGS.md\n\nDocument:\n\n- categories\n- navigation\n- state ownership\n- core isolation\n- future settings wiring\n- rollback\n- code-security\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 004 V2 SETTINGS SHELL COMPLETE\n\nMain categories:\n<n>\n\nSub-categories:\n<n>\n\nNavigation owners:\n<n>\n\nNew persistence:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n<n>\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 003 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nMaterial 3:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDynamic color runtime:\n<NOT_YET/YES/NO>\n\nSet default Home action:\n<YES/NO>\n\nPatch status screen:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:295:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787234226,"text":"PATCH 004 V2 — SETTINGS ENTRY ICON\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2\n+ PATCH 001 FROZEN\n+ PATCH 002\n+ Settings PATCH 004\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAdd one Settings icon inside the Fav header.\n\nPOSITION:\n\nFav header:\n\nFav. apps                         [settings icon]\nApps 16\n\n==================================================\n1. POSITION\n==================================================\n\nSettings icon:\n\n- right side of Fav\n- aligned with \"Fav. apps\" title\n- inside Fav bounds\n- vertically centered against title row\n\nDo not increase Fav height.\n\nDo not move Fav.\nDo not move Search.\nDo not move P1/P2/Dock.\n\n==================================================\n2. ICON\n==================================================\n\nUse Material Settings icon.\n\nPreferred visual size:\n20dp\n\nTouch target:\nminimum 48dp\n\nIcon must look small,\nwhile touch area remains accessible.\n\n==================================================\n3. STYLE\n==================================================\n\nUse current Fav foreground color.\n\nNo:\n\n- circular background\n- card\n- border\n- shadow\n- label\n- badge\n\nOnly the Settings glyph.\n\n==================================================\n4. HEADER LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nUse a real header Row:\n\nRow(\n    title area -> weight(1f)\n    settings action -> fixed touch target\n)\n\nLeft:\n\nFav. apps\nApps 16\n\nRight:\n\nSettings icon\n\nAvoid absolute coordinates.\n\n==================================================\n5. ACTION\n==================================================\n\nSingle tap:\n\nopen PATCH 004 Settings.\n\nOne tap = one action.\n\nNo long-press behavior.\n\n==================================================\n6. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nOn accepted Settings tap use existing policy:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nExactly once.\n\nNo raw Vibrator.\n\n==================================================\n7. GESTURE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nSettings touch target must not interfere with:\n\nPATCH 001 LEFT/RIGHT\nPATCH 002 UP/DOWN\nSearch\nFav gesture detection\n\nSimple tap:\nSettings wins.\n\nSwipe exceeding touchSlop:\nexisting gesture owner wins according to current arbitration.\n\n==================================================\n8. PATCH OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nThe Settings action belongs to PATCH 004.\n\nDo not put Settings navigation logic into Core.\n\nPrefer one PATCH 004 entry callback/hook.\n\n==================================================\n9. HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 001 behavior:\nUNCHANGED\n\nPATCH 002 behavior:\nUNCHANGED\n\nCore logic:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP1/P2/Dock:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n10. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nNew persistence:\n0\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n11. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA SETTINGS ENTRY ICON COMPLETE\n\nSettings icon:\n<YES/NO>\n\nVisual size:\n<dp>\n\nTouch target:\n<dp>\n\nPosition:\n<FAV_HEADER_RIGHT/OTHER>\n\nFav height changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nHaptic:\n<CONFIRM/OTHER>\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:296:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787234608,"text":"PATCH 004 V2 — SETTINGS SIMPLIFICATION / SYSTEM TYPOGRAPHY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2\n+ PATCH 001 FROZEN\n+ PATCH 002\n+ current PATCH 004 Settings\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRefactor Settings UI only.\n\nCurrent Settings are too complex and visually inconsistent.\n\nMake them:\n\n- simpler\n- fewer categories\n- fewer sub-categories\n- system/Material typography\n- explicit category icons\n- compact spacing\n- consistent text sizing\n\nDO NOT modify Core behavior.\nDO NOT modify PATCH 001.\nDO NOT modify PATCH 002.\n\n==================================================\n1. TYPOGRAPHY\n==================================================\n\nUse Android/Material 3 system typography.\n\nDo NOT use custom fonts.\n\nUse MaterialTheme.typography only.\n\nPreferred mapping:\n\nScreen title:\ntitleLarge\n\nCategory title:\ntitleMedium or bodyLarge\n\nSubtitle:\nbodyMedium\n\nSecondary metadata:\nbodySmall\n\nKeep one consistent scale across all Settings screens.\n\nNo oversized headers.\n\n==================================================\n2. ROOT CATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nUse exactly:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nSystem\nAbout\n\nTotal:\n5\n\nNo additional root categories.\n\n==================================================\n3. CATEGORY ICONS\n==================================================\n\nEvery root category MUST have a meaningful Material icon.\n\nSuggested:\n\nAppearance:\nPalette / Tune\n\nHome:\nHome\n\nSearch:\nSearch\n\nSystem:\nSettings / Android\n\nAbout:\nInfo\n\nIcon size:\n20–24dp\n\nTouch row:\nminimum 48dp height.\n\n==================================================\n4. APPEARANCE\n==================================================\n\nOnly:\n\nIcon shape\nDynamic color\n\nDo NOT add:\nsurface style\nborder tuning\nradius tuning\nwallpaper dim controls\nadvanced appearance options\n\n==================================================\n5. HOME\n==================================================\n\nOnly:\n\nLayout\nHaptic & gestures\n\nLayout may later contain:\nFav / P1 / P2 / Dock spacing\n\nDo not expose many individual toggles now.\n\n==================================================\n6. SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nOnly:\n\nSearch behavior\nHistory\n\nDo not expose:\nranking\nproviders\nkeyboard internals\ndebug options\n\n==================================================\n7. SYSTEM\n==================================================\n\nOnly:\n\nSet as default Home\nApp info\n\nUse supported Android APIs/intents.\n\n==================================================\n8. ABOUT\n==================================================\n\nOnly:\n\nVersion\nChangelog\n\nOptional:\nLicenses if already required.\n\nDo not expose internal patch/debug details to normal users.\n\n==================================================\n9. ROW DESIGN\n==================================================\n\nUse compact Material 3 ListItem-style rows.\n\nEach root row:\n\n[icon] Category title        >\n\nOptional subtitle:\nmax one short line.\n\nNo giant cards.\n\nNo large decorative backgrounds.\n\n==================================================\n10. DIVIDERS\n==================================================\n\nUse subtle HorizontalDivider between logical groups only.\n\nDo not put thick borders around every row.\n\n==================================================\n11. SPACING\n==================================================\n\nKeep compact:\n\nscreen horizontal padding:\n16–20dp\n\nrow vertical rhythm:\nMaterial standard\n\ncategory-to-category gap:\nsmall\n\nNo large empty zones.\n\n==================================================\n12. TOP APP BAR\n==================================================\n\nUse compact Material 3 TopAppBar.\n\nTitle:\nSettings\n\nSystem typography only.\n\nNo custom font size.\n\n==================================================\n13. SUBCATEGORY NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nRoot\n→ one small sub-page\n→ setting rows\n\nDo not create deep navigation.\n\nMaximum depth:\n2 levels from Settings root.\n\n==================================================\n14. ICON CONSISTENCY\n==================================================\n\nAll category icons:\n\nsame size\nsame optical weight\nsame tint family\n\nUse current Material onSurface/onSurfaceVariant tokens.\n\n==================================================\n15. DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nIf Dynamic Color is not yet wired safely:\n\nshow the option but keep it disabled/read-only\nor mark as Coming soon.\n\nDo NOT change runtime theme in this refactor unless already supported.\n\n==================================================\n16. HOME LAYOUT OPTION\n==================================================\n\nKeep as one entry:\n\nLayout\n\nDo not create separate root entries for:\n\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nThose can live inside Layout later.\n\n==================================================\n17. HAPTIC / GESTURES\n==================================================\n\nOne subcategory only:\n\nHaptic & gestures\n\nDo not expose internal PATCH 001 implementation details.\n\n==================================================\n18. SEARCH HISTORY\n==================================================\n\nIf PATCH 003 not yet active:\n\nHistory entry can remain placeholder/read-only.\n\nDo not add persistence in this refactor.\n\n==================================================\n19. SYSTEM FONT POLICY\n==================================================\n\nNo bundled fonts.\nNo custom Typeface.\nNo font asset.\n\nUse system/Material typography exclusively.\n\n==================================================\n20. PATCH OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 004 owns:\n\nSettings UI\nSettings navigation\nSettings category icons\n\nIt must not modify:\nCore\nPATCH 001\nPATCH 002\n\n==================================================\n21. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nNew persistence:\n0 preferred\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nGesture owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n22. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 004 SETTINGS SIMPLIFIED\n\nRoot categories:\n5\n\nAppearance entries:\n<n>\n\nHome entries:\n<n>\n\nSearch entries:\n<n>\n\nSystem entries:\n<n>\n\nAbout entries:\n<n>\n\nSystem/Material typography:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCustom fonts:\n<n>\n\nRoot category icons:\n<n>\n\nMax navigation depth:\n<n>\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nNew persistence:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:297:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787235053,"text":"PATCH 004 V2 — SETTINGS VISUAL REFINEMENT + DEFAULT DYNAMIC COLOR\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\ncurrent PATCH 004 Settings\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nFROZEN\n\nDO NOT modify PATCH 002 behavior.\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRefine Settings visually using the cleaner structure\nfrom the previous Settings version.\n\nRequirements:\n\n1. Dynamic Color enabled by default for Settings\n2. smaller category icons\n3. compact system typography\n4. cleaner Material 3 hierarchy\n5. fewer visual containers/cards\n6. consistent spacing and alignment\n\n==================================================\n1. DYNAMIC COLOR DEFAULT\n==================================================\n\nApply Android Material 3 Dynamic Color to SETTINGS by default\nwhen supported by the device/API.\n\nUse current Android/Material APIs.\n\nPreferred:\n\ndynamicDarkColorScheme(context)\ndynamicLightColorScheme(context)\n\naccording to system appearance.\n\nFallback:\nexisting Machina Material color scheme.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDynamic Color scope for this phase:\nSETTINGS ONLY.\n\nDo NOT modify Home/PATCH001/PATCH002 colors.\n\n==================================================\n2. NO USER TOGGLE YET\n==================================================\n\nDynamic Color is default Settings behavior.\n\nDo not add persistence or a toggle yet.\n\nSettings Dynamic Color state:\nplatform-derived.\n\nPersistence:\n0.\n\n==================================================\n3. TYPOGRAPHY\n==================================================\n\nUse only:\n\nMaterialTheme.typography\n\nNo custom Typeface.\nNo bundled fonts.\n\nScreen title:\ntitleLarge\n\nCategory title:\nbodyLarge or titleMedium\n\nCategory subtitle:\nbodySmall/bodyMedium\n\nKeep sizes consistent.\n\n==================================================\n4. ROOT STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nKeep exactly 5 root categories:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nSystem\nAbout\n\nNo extra root sections.\n\n==================================================\n5. CATEGORY ICONS\n==================================================\n\nUse the previous Material icon set:\n\nAppearance:\nPalette\n\nHome:\nHome\n\nSearch:\nSearch\n\nSystem:\nSettings\n\nAbout:\nInfo\n\nICON VISUAL SIZE:\n18dp\n\nTouch target belongs to the row,\nnot the icon.\n\nDo NOT wrap icons in:\n\ncircle\npill\ncard\ncolored tile\n\n==================================================\n6. ICON ALIGNMENT\n==================================================\n\nAll icons:\n\nsame 18dp size\nsame horizontal position\nsame tint family\nsame optical alignment\n\nUse:\nonSurfaceVariant\n\nor appropriate Material token.\n\n==================================================\n7. ROW LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nEach root category row:\n\n18dp icon\n12–16dp horizontal gap\ntext column\noptional end chevron\n\nText column:\n\ntitle\nshort subtitle\n\nNo oversized vertical padding.\n\n==================================================\n8. CATEGORY SUBTITLES\n==================================================\n\nUse short summaries:\n\nAppearance:\nIcon shape · Dynamic color\n\nHome:\nLayout · Haptic & gestures\n\nSearch:\nBehavior · History\n\nSystem:\nDefault Home · App info\n\nAbout:\nVersion · Changelog\n\nKeep one line only.\n\n==================================================\n9. REMOVE LARGE CARDS\n==================================================\n\nRoot Settings should NOT look like a grid of cards.\n\nPrefer:\n\nflat Material surface\nListItem-style rows\nsubtle dividers\n\nNo heavy:\nborders\nshadows\ncontainer backgrounds per item\n\n==================================================\n10. SURFACE\n==================================================\n\nUse Material 3 Dynamic Color surface tokens:\n\nbackground\nsurface\nsurfaceContainer\nonSurface\nonSurfaceVariant\n\nDo not hardcode colorful values.\n\n==================================================\n11. TOP APP BAR\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nTopAppBar\n\nCompact.\n\nTitle:\nSettings\n\nBack button:\nsmall Material ArrowBackRounded if Settings is a subpage.\n\nNo custom large header.\n\n==================================================\n12. SPACING\n==================================================\n\nRoot horizontal padding:\n16dp\n\nTop/bottom screen rhythm:\nMaterial standard\n\nRow height:\ncompact but accessible\n\nInter-section gap:\nsmall.\n\n==================================================\n13. DIVIDERS\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nHorizontalDivider\n\nonly where helpful.\n\nVery subtle.\n\nNo divider after every row if unnecessary.\n\n==================================================\n14. APPEARANCE\n==================================================\n\nKeep only:\n\nIcon shape\nDynamic color\n\nDynamic color entry may display:\n\nOn · System colors\n\nRead-only for now.\n\n==================================================\n15. HOME\n==================================================\n\nKeep only:\n\nLayout\nHaptic & gestures\n\nDo not expose internal patch controls.\n\n==================================================\n16. SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nKeep only:\n\nSearch behavior\nHistory\n\nIf Search engine/history not active yet:\nshow current status cleanly,\ndo not create fake persistence.\n\n==================================================\n17. SYSTEM\n==================================================\n\nKeep only:\n\nSet as default Home\nApp info\n\nUse supported Android APIs/intents.\n\n==================================================\n18. ABOUT\n==================================================\n\nKeep only:\n\nVersion\nChangelog\n\nOptional:\nLicenses only if already present.\n\n==================================================\n19. SUBPAGE DESIGN\n==================================================\n\nSubpages use the same design language:\n\nsmall icons where useful\nsystem typography\nflat rows\ndynamic color\nno giant cards\n\nMaximum navigation depth:\n2.\n\n==================================================\n20. SETTINGS ENTRY ICON\n==================================================\n\nKeep Settings icon in Fav header.\n\nVisual size:\n20dp max\n\nNo surrounding circle/card.\n\nDo not move Fav geometry.\n\n==================================================\n21. PATCH ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 002 behavior modified:\nNO\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nNew persistence:\n0\n\n==================================================\n22. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nDynamic Color implementation:\nno reflection\nno hidden APIs\n\n==================================================\n23. DEVICE TARGET\n==================================================\n\nOn Pixel:\n\nSettings should visually feel native to current Android/Material 3:\n\n- system typography\n- dynamic system colors\n- compact rows\n- small icons\n- clean spacing\n- no unnecessary cards\n- consistent hierarchy\n\n==================================================\n24. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 004 SETTINGS VISUAL REFINEMENT COMPLETE\n\nDynamic Color:\n<ENABLED_DEFAULT/FALLBACK/FAILED>\n\nDynamic Color scope:\n<SETTINGS_ONLY/OTHER>\n\nCustom fonts:\n<n>\n\nRoot categories:\n<n>\n\nRoot category icons:\n<n>\n\nCategory icon size:\n<dp>\n\nLarge per-row cards:\n<n>\n\nMaterial typography:\n<YES/NO>\n\nAppearance entries:\n<n>\n\nHome entries:\n<n>\n\nSearch entries:\n<n>\n\nSystem entries:\n<n>\n\nAbout entries:\n<n>\n\nSettings Fav icon:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 behavior modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nNew persistence:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:298:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787235180,"text":"FASE: MACHINA — LEGACY SETTINGS VISUAL RECOVERY AUDIT\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/Machina\n\nREAD ONLY.\n\nOBIETTIVO\n\nTrovare la versione precedente di Settings che aveva\nil design particolare approvato.\n\nNON ripristinare codice.\nNON modificare progetto corrente.\nNON modificare PATCH 004.\n\nCercare in:\n\ncheckpoints/\nsnapshots/\ndocs/\nproject history disponibile\n\nIdentificare:\n\n1. vecchi Settings composables\n2. icone utilizzate\n3. icon resource/vector names\n4. dimensioni icone\n5. typography\n6. category layout\n7. row/container shapes\n8. spacing\n9. colors\n10. dividers/borders\n11. navigation style\n12. eventuali elementi grafici particolari\n\nConfrontare con PATCH 004 corrente.\n\nIMPORTANTE\n\nSeparare:\n\nLEGACY VISUAL DESIGN\nda\nLEGACY SETTINGS LOGIC\n\nVogliamo recuperare SOLO il visual design.\n\nNon recuperare:\n\nvecchia persistence\nvecchia navigation architecture\nvecchi gesture handlers\nvecchio state management\nvecchie feature obsolete\n\nOUTPUT\n\nMACHINA LEGACY SETTINGS VISUAL AUDIT\n\nBest legacy source:\n<checkpoint/snapshot/path>\n\nSettings files found:\n<paths>\n\nLegacy icon set:\n<list>\n\nLegacy icon sizes:\n<values>\n\nLegacy typography:\n<values>\n\nLegacy category layout:\n<description>\n\nLegacy surface/container style:\n<description>\n\nLegacy spacing:\n<values>\n\nLegacy colors:\n<values>\n\nUnique visual elements:\n<list>\n\nCurrent PATCH004 differences:\n<short list>\n\nVisual elements safe to restore:\n<list>\n\nLegacy logic that must NOT return:\n<list>\n\nProject modified:\nNO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:299:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787235471,"text":"FASE: MACHINA — RESTORE LEGACY SETTINGS VISUAL ASSETS\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/Machina\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nMODE:\nREAD ONLY FIRST\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRecuperare dal vecchio backup:\n\n1. il set di icone Settings che era già approvato\n2. il layout/visual design del vecchio Settings\n3. eventuali vector drawable/resource originali\n4. dimensioni, spacing, shapes e hierarchy\n\nNON recuperare la vecchia logica Settings.\n\n==================================================\n1. SEARCH SOURCES\n==================================================\n\nCercare in:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/checkpoints/\n/opt/Android/Machina/snapshots/\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\n\ne qualunque backup legacy già presente sotto /opt/Android/Machina.\n\nTrovare la versione Settings precedente alla semplificazione attuale.\n\n==================================================\n2. FIND ICON ASSETS\n==================================================\n\nCercare:\n\nres/drawable/\nres/drawable-anydpi/\nres/drawable-nodpi/\nImageVector definitions\nMaterial icon references\ncustom vectors\n\nRiportare esattamente:\n\n- filename\n- resource name\n- vector path source\n- dimensions\n- tint behavior\n- category association\n\n==================================================\n3. FIND LEGACY SETTINGS UI\n==================================================\n\nIndividuare:\n\nSettings composable\ncategory rows\nsub-category rows\ntop bar\nback icon\ndividers\ncontainers\nshapes\nspacing\ntypography\n\n==================================================\n4. CLASSIFY\n==================================================\n\nPer ogni elemento:\n\nRESTORE_VISUAL\nKEEP_CURRENT_LOGIC\nDO_NOT_RESTORE\n\n==================================================\n5. DO NOT RESTORE\n==================================================\n\nNON riportare:\n\nlegacy persistence\nlegacy navigation framework\nlegacy state owners\nold Back handlers\nold gesture code\nold lifecycle code\nold Dynamic Color implementation\nobsolete Settings options\n\n==================================================\n6. TARGET PATCH\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 004 current architecture remains owner.\n\nRestore into PATCH 004 only:\n\n- legacy category icons\n- legacy Settings row visual language\n- legacy spacing\n- legacy shapes\n- legacy icon sizing\n- legacy distinctive hierarchy\n\nDynamic Color:\nkeep current SETTINGS_ONLY implementation.\n\n==================================================\n7. OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA LEGACY SETTINGS VISUAL RECOVERY AUDIT\n\nBest backup source:\n<path>\n\nLegacy Settings file:\n<path>\n\nLegacy icon assets:\n<list>\n\nLegacy category icons:\nAppearance -> <resource>\nHome -> <resource>\nSearch -> <resource>\nSystem -> <resource>\nAbout -> <resource>\n\nLegacy icon sizes:\n<values>\n\nLegacy row layout:\n<description>\n\nLegacy corner radius:\n<value>\n\nLegacy spacing:\n<values>\n\nLegacy typography:\n<values>\n\nLegacy dividers/borders:\n<description>\n\nSafe visual assets to restore:\n<list>\n\nLegacy logic NOT to restore:\n<list>\n\nCurrent project modified:\nNO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:300:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787235643,"text":"FASE: MACHINA — RESTORE LEGACY SETTINGS VISUAL INTO PATCH 004\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBACKUP SOURCE:\n<INSERIRE QUI IL PATH TROVATO DA CODEX>\n\nCURRENT OWNER:\nPATCH 004 V2 SETTINGS\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 002:\nUNCHANGED\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRipristinare dal backup il vecchio Settings che visivamente\nera approvato, mantenendo l'architettura PATCH 004 attuale.\n\nRESTORE ONLY:\n\n- category icons\n- icon dimensions\n- row layout\n- spacing\n- shapes\n- borders/dividers\n- typography hierarchy\n- distinctive visual details\n- Settings top bar/back treatment\n\nDO NOT RESTORE:\n\n- legacy Settings state\n- legacy persistence\n- legacy navigation engine\n- legacy gesture handlers\n- legacy Back handlers\n- old lifecycle code\n- obsolete settings options\n- old feature coupling\n\n==================================================\n1. BACKUP IS VISUAL REFERENCE\n==================================================\n\nTreat backup Settings implementation as authoritative\nfor VISUAL DESIGN only.\n\nDo not copy entire files blindly.\n\nExtract only the pieces needed to reproduce the old look.\n\n==================================================\n2. ICONS\n==================================================\n\nRestore the exact old Settings icons found in backup.\n\nPrefer original vector drawables/resources\nif they still build correctly.\n\nPreserve:\n\n- resource names where practical\n- intrinsic size\n- optical proportions\n- tint behavior\n\nDo not replace them with generic Material icons\nunless a legacy asset is missing/broken.\n\n==================================================\n3. SETTINGS ROOT\n==================================================\n\nRecreate the old root visual layout inside PATCH 004.\n\nUse the same:\n\n- icon placement\n- category spacing\n- row height\n- typography hierarchy\n- corner treatment\n- separators\n- visual density\n\nKeep current simplified category count if desired,\nbut make them LOOK like the old Settings.\n\n==================================================\n4. CATEGORY SET\n==================================================\n\nKeep current simplified functional structure:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nSystem\nAbout\n\nUse the old icon/design language for those categories.\n\nMap legacy icons to current categories\naccording to meaning.\n\n==================================================\n5. TYPOGRAPHY\n==================================================\n\nIf old Settings used system/Material typography:\nrestore same mapping.\n\nIf old Settings hardcoded font sizes:\ntranslate them to the nearest MaterialTheme.typography\ntoken while preserving the same visual scale.\n\nNo custom font files.\n\n==================================================\n6. DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nKeep current Dynamic Color behavior:\n\nSETTINGS ONLY\nenabled by default where supported.\n\nDo not restore old hardcoded color system\nif it conflicts with current Dynamic Color.\n\nInstead map legacy surfaces to:\n\nsurface\nsurfaceContainer\nsurfaceContainerHigh\nonSurface\nonSurfaceVariant\noutlineVariant\n\nPreserve legacy layout/shapes,\nmodernize only color source.\n\n==================================================\n7. BACK BUTTON\n==================================================\n\nRestore old Settings Back visual if it was distinctive.\n\nBut behavior remains current PATCH 004 navigation.\n\nNo legacy BackHandler code.\n\n==================================================\n8. SUB-CATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nUse the old visual treatment for subcategory rows too.\n\nKeep few subcategories:\n\nAppearance\n- Icon shape\n- Dynamic color\n\nHome\n- Layout\n- Haptic & gestures\n\nSearch\n- Search behavior\n- History\n\nSystem\n- Set as default Home\n- App info\n\nAbout\n- Version\n- Changelog\n\nNo deeper nesting.\n\n==================================================\n9. SETTINGS ENTRY FROM FAV\n==================================================\n\nKeep current Settings icon entry inside Fav.\n\nIf old backup had a better matching settings glyph,\nuse that visual asset.\n\nDo not move Fav geometry.\n\n==================================================\n10. RESOURCE RESTORE\n==================================================\n\nCopy only required legacy visual assets into current project.\n\nExamples:\n\ndrawable vectors\nicons\nshape resources\ndimension tokens if genuinely useful\n\nDo not copy:\n\nold manifests\nold Gradle\nold Kotlin feature logic\nold preferences XML\nobsolete resources unrelated to Settings\n\n==================================================\n11. NO CORE CONTAMINATION\n==================================================\n\nCore files modified:\n0\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n0\n\nPATCH 002 behavior modified:\n0\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nLauncherPreferences core writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n12. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nRun code-security policy after restore.\n\nSpecifically verify:\n\nlegacy state owners imported:\n0\n\nlegacy gesture owners imported:\n0\n\nlegacy BackHandlers imported:\n0\n\nlegacy lifecycle owners imported:\n0\n\nlegacy persistence paths imported:\n0\n\n==================================================\n13. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n14. DEVICE VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nOn Pixel:\n\n- Settings visually matches old backup\n- icons match old version\n- spacing/shapes feel like old version\n- Dynamic Color applies correctly\n- navigation still current/new\n- no old logic returns\n- Home/PATCH001/PATCH002 regressions = NONE\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA LEGACY SETTINGS VISUAL RESTORED\n\nBackup source:\n<path>\n\nLegacy icons restored:\n<n>\n\nLegacy visual resources restored:\n<n>\n\nLegacy Kotlin logic copied:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n0\n\nCurrent PATCH 004 navigation preserved:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDynamic Color preserved:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRoot categories:\n<n>\n\nSubcategories:\n<n>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 behavior modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nLegacy persistence imported:\n<n>\n\nLegacy gesture owners imported:\n<n>\n\nLegacy BackHandlers imported:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:301:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787236016,"text":"PATCH 004 V2 — MACHINA SETTINGS\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nCORE V2:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nVALIDATED / FROZEN\n\nPATCH 002:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nPATCH 003:\nNO DEPENDENCY REQUIRED\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nCreare il Settings definitivo di Machina usando:\n\n- visual design recuperato dal vecchio backup\n- vecchie icone approvate\n- architettura nuova e isolata\n- Material 3\n- Dynamic Color attivo di default SOLO nei Settings\n- poche categorie\n- poche sottocategorie\n- navigazione semplice\n\nNON riportare la vecchia logica Settings.\n\n==================================================\n1. PATCH OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 004 owns only:\n\n- Settings entry\n- Settings UI\n- Settings navigation\n- Settings visual assets\n- Settings-specific state/actions\n\nCore logic:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n2. LEGACY VISUAL\n==================================================\n\nUse the previously located backup as the visual source\nof truth.\n\nRestore:\n\n- legacy category icons\n- legacy icon proportions\n- row layout\n- spacing\n- distinctive shapes\n- dividers/borders\n- typography hierarchy\n- back-button visual treatment\n- overall visual density\n\nDO NOT copy entire old Settings Kotlin files blindly.\n\n==================================================\n3. NEW ARCHITECTURE\n==================================================\n\nKeep current PATCH 004 architecture.\n\nDo NOT restore:\n\n- old persistence\n- old state management\n- old navigation framework\n- old Back handlers\n- old gesture handlers\n- old lifecycle code\n- obsolete options\n\nTarget:\n\nLEGACY VISUAL\n+\nNEW CLEAN LOGIC\n\n==================================================\n4. SETTINGS ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nFav header:\n\nFav. apps                      [Settings icon]\n\nSettings icon:\nuse the approved legacy glyph if available.\n\nVisual size:\napproximately 18–20dp\n\nTouch target:\n>= 48dp\n\nNo circle/card/background around icon unless that was\npart of the approved legacy visual.\n\nOne tap:\nopen Settings.\n\n==================================================\n5. ROOT CATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nKeep only:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nSystem\nAbout\n\nExactly 5 root categories.\n\n==================================================\n6. APPEARANCE\n==================================================\n\nOnly:\n\nIcon shape\nDynamic color\n\n==================================================\n7. HOME\n==================================================\n\nOnly:\n\nLayout\nHaptic & gestures\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nOnly:\n\nSearch behavior\nHistory\n\nIf search engine/history is not active yet:\nshow safe status/placeholder only.\n\nDo not invent runtime settings.\n\n==================================================\n9. SYSTEM\n==================================================\n\nOnly:\n\nSet as default Home\nApp info\n\nUse supported Android APIs.\n\nHome role:\nRoleManager.ROLE_HOME\n\nDo not duplicate role backend unnecessarily.\n\n==================================================\n10. ABOUT\n==================================================\n\nOnly:\n\nVersion\nChangelog\n\nOptional:\nLicenses only if already required/present.\n\n==================================================\n11. NAVIGATION DEPTH\n==================================================\n\nMaximum:\n\nSettings root\n→ Category\n→ Sub-page/action\n\nNo deeper navigation.\n\n==================================================\n12. LEGACY ICONS\n==================================================\n\nUse exact recovered legacy icons where safe.\n\nDo NOT replace them with generic Material icons\nif original assets are available and valid.\n\nAll category icons:\n\n- same optical family\n- small\n- clean\n- aligned consistently\n\nDo not enlarge them.\n\n==================================================\n13. TYPOGRAPHY\n==================================================\n\nNo custom font files.\n\nUse system / MaterialTheme typography.\n\nPreserve legacy visual proportions using nearest\nMaterial typography tokens.\n\nPreferred:\n\nSettings title:\ntitleLarge\n\nCategory:\nbodyLarge / titleMedium\n\nSubtitle:\nbodySmall / bodyMedium\n\nNo oversized text.\n\n==================================================\n14. DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nDynamic Color:\nON BY DEFAULT\n\nScope:\nSETTINGS ONLY\n\nUse:\n\ndynamicDarkColorScheme(context)\ndynamicLightColorScheme(context)\n\nwhen supported.\n\nFallback:\ncurrent Machina Material scheme.\n\nNo persistence required.\n\nNo toggle required in this phase.\n\n==================================================\n15. DYNAMIC COLOR + LEGACY VISUAL\n==================================================\n\nLegacy layout/style remains.\n\nReplace old hardcoded theme colors where necessary with\nMaterial 3 tokens:\n\nbackground\nsurface\nsurfaceContainer\nsurfaceContainerHigh\nonSurface\nonSurfaceVariant\noutlineVariant\nprimary\n\nDo not destroy the legacy visual identity.\n\n==================================================\n16. ROOT SCREEN STYLE\n==================================================\n\nSettings should feel distinctive, not generic.\n\nUse:\n\n- recovered icon language\n- compact rows\n- controlled spacing\n- flat/clean surfaces\n- subtle dividers\n- legacy shapes where appropriate\n\nAvoid:\n\n- giant Material cards\n- oversized category blocks\n- excessive whitespace\n- generic Settings clone appearance\n\n==================================================\n17. CATEGORY ROW\n==================================================\n\nConcept:\n\n[legacy icon]  Category\n               short subtitle                    >\n\nUse the same rhythm throughout.\n\n==================================================\n18. BACK\n==================================================\n\nSettings root:\nBack → Home\n\nCategory:\nBack → Settings root\n\nSubpage:\nBack → Category\n\nUse current PATCH 004 navigation owner.\n\nDo NOT restore legacy BackHandler architecture.\n\n==================================================\n19. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nAccepted Settings commands use the existing Machina policy:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nOne action:\none haptic.\n\nNo raw Vibrator.\n\nNo MOVE haptic.\n\n==================================================\n20. CORE / PATCH LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 002 behavior modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 003 modified:\nNO\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nP1/P2/Dock writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n21. PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nDo not create placeholder preferences.\n\nOnly persist a setting when it actually controls\na real implemented feature.\n\nThis visual/settings-shell phase should preferably add:\n\nnew persistence = 0\n\n==================================================\n22. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nSettings opening must not trigger:\n\nPackageManager full scan\nwallpaper decode\nnetwork\ncontinuous polling\nHome catalog reload\n\n==================================================\n23. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nRemoving PATCH 004 + its single entry hook:\n\nHome\nPATCH 001\nPATCH 002\nPATCH 003\n\nmust continue normally.\n\n==================================================\n24. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nCore isolation PASS\nState ownership PASS\nNavigation ownership PASS\nHaptic ownership PASS\nLifecycle PASS\nRollback PASS\n\nLegacy logic accidentally restored:\n0\n\n==================================================\n25. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8 release:\nSUCCESS\n\nSnapshot:\nPASS\n\nSHA-256:\nPASS\n\n==================================================\n26. DOCUMENT\n==================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nPATCH_004_V2_SETTINGS.md\n\nInclude:\n\n- backup source used\n- visual assets restored\n- categories\n- navigation\n- Dynamic Color implementation\n- legacy logic explicitly NOT restored\n- core isolation\n- rollback\n- build results\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 004 V2 SETTINGS COMPLETE\n\nBackup source:\n<path>\n\nLegacy icons restored:\n<n>\n\nLegacy visual resources restored:\n<n>\n\nLegacy Kotlin logic restored:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n0\n\nRoot categories:\n<n>\n\nSub-category entries:\n<n>\n\nDynamic Color:\n<ENABLED_DEFAULT/FALLBACK/FAILED>\n\nDynamic Color scope:\n<SETTINGS_ONLY/OTHER>\n\nCustom fonts:\n<n>\n\nSettings entry icon:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSettings icon size:\n<dp>\n\nNavigation owners:\n<n>\n\nMax navigation depth:\n<n>\n\nNew persistence:\n<n>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 behavior modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 003 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n<n>\n\nLegacy BackHandlers imported:\n<n>\n\nLegacy gesture owners imported:\n<n>\n\nLegacy lifecycle owners imported:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nRollback:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\nPatch doc:\ndocs/PATCH_004_V2_SETTINGS.md"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:302:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787236381,"text":"FASE: MACHINA — PATCH 004 V2 FINAL VALIDATION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nPATCH:\nPATCH 004 V2 — SETTINGS\n\nDEVICE TEST:\nPASS\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nVALIDATED / FROZEN\n\nPATCH 002:\nUNCHANGED\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nVALIDATION ONLY.\n\nNON modificare:\n- Settings visual\n- Settings navigation\n- legacy icon assets\n- Dynamic Color\n- category structure\n- Fav Settings entry icon\n- Core\n- PATCH 001\n- PATCH 002\n\n==================================================\n1. APPLY SECURITY POLICY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\n==================================================\n2. PATCH BOUNDARY\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nCore writes = 0\nHomeSnapshot writes = 0\nP1/P2/Dock writes = 0\nPATCH 001 modifications = 0\nPATCH 002 behavior modifications = 0\n\n==================================================\n3. LEGACY SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nVerify recovered backup contributed only approved visual assets/layout.\n\nTarget:\n\nlegacy persistence imported = 0\nlegacy gesture owners imported = 0\nlegacy lifecycle owners imported = 0\nlegacy BackHandler architecture imported = 0\n\n==================================================\n4. SETTINGS OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nSettings navigation owner = 1\nDynamic Color owner = 1\nSettings entry action owner = 1\nduplicate Settings state = 0\n\n==================================================\n5. DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nDynamic Color = SETTINGS ONLY\n\nNo Home theme mutation.\n\nNo PATCH 001/002 color mutation.\n\nFallback color scheme exists.\n\n==================================================\n6. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nUse existing semantic policy:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(...)\n\nNo raw Vibrator.\nNo duplicate command haptic.\nNo MOVE haptic.\n\n==================================================\n7. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nOpening Settings must trigger:\n\nPackageManager full scan = 0\nnetwork = 0\nwallpaper decode = 0\npolling = 0\n\n==================================================\n8. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nVerify exact rollback:\n\nremove PATCH 004 files\n+\nsingle Settings entry hook/assets\n\n=> previous Home baseline works unchanged.\n\nRollback = PASS required.\n\n==================================================\n9. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 release = SUCCESS\nSnapshot validation = PASS\nSHA-256 validation = PASS\n\n==================================================\n10. DOCUMENT\n==================================================\n\nUpdate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nPATCH_004_V2_SETTINGS.md\n\nAdd:\n\nSTATUS: VALIDATED\nDEVICE: PASS\nCODE_SECURITY: PASS\nROLLBACK: PASS\nDEBUG: SUCCESS\nR8: SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n11. CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nOnly if ALL PASS:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint patch-004-settings-validated\n\n==================================================\n12. STOP\n==================================================\n\nAfter checkpoint:\n\nSTOP.\n\nDo not start another patch.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 004 V2 VALIDATION COMPLETE\n\nDevice validation:\nPASS\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 behavior modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nLegacy persistence imported:\n<n>\n\nLegacy gesture owners imported:\n<n>\n\nLegacy lifecycle owners imported:\n<n>\n\nLegacy BackHandlers imported:\n<n>\n\nSettings navigation owners:\n<n>\n\nDynamic Color scope:\n<SETTINGS_ONLY/OTHER>\n\nDuplicate Settings state:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nRollback:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot validation:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256 validation:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\n<VALIDATED/FAILED>\n\nCheckpoint:\n<path/N-A>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:303:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787236761,"text":"FASE: PATCH 004 — REMOVE PLACEHOLDERS / KEEP APPROVED UI\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nPreservare ESATTAMENTE il Settings visuale approvato.\n\nRimuovere soltanto testo tecnico/placeholder come:\n\nPATCH 004\npatch status\nimplementation placeholder\nfuture patch\ndebug labels\ninternal architecture descriptions\n\nNON modificare:\n- icone\n- layout\n- spacing\n- typography\n- Dynamic Color\n- category structure\n- navigation\n- Fav Settings icon\n\n==================================================\n1. ROOT / SUBPAGE TEXT\n==================================================\n\nOgni voce Settings deve mostrare solo testo utente finale.\n\nNO riferimenti a:\nPATCH 001\nPATCH 002\nPATCH 003\nPATCH 004\nCore V2\nruntime owner\nplaceholder implementation\ndebug status\n\n==================================================\n2. CURRENT NON-FUNCTIONAL OPTIONS\n==================================================\n\nSe una voce non ha ancora una funzione reale:\n\nNON fingere che sia operativa.\n\nPreferire uno dei due comportamenti:\n\nA. row visibile ma disabled con subtitle breve:\n\"Not available yet\"\n\noppure\n\nB. rimuovere temporaneamente la row.\n\nPreferred:\nB, se la categoria resta comunque sensata.\n\n==================================================\n3. KEEP ONLY REAL / USEFUL ITEMS\n==================================================\n\nPer ora mostrare solo voci che hanno senso reale.\n\nEsempio:\n\nAppearance\n- Icon shape        [solo se funziona]\n- Dynamic color     [se realmente attivo]\n\nHome\n- Haptic & gestures [solo se esiste azione/config reale]\n\nSystem\n- Set as default Home\n- App info\n\nAbout\n- Version\n- Changelog         [se esiste contenuto reale]\n\nRimuovere ogni voce finta/placeholder.\n\n==================================================\n4. NO NEW SETTINGS LOGIC\n==================================================\n\nQuesta fase NON deve implementare nuove opzioni.\n\nServe solo a trasformare la shell approvata\nin una UI pulita e presentabile.\n\n==================================================\n5. DEVICE UI LOCK\n==================================================\n\nSettings visual:\nUNCHANGED\n\nLegacy icons:\nUNCHANGED\n\nDynamic Color:\nUNCHANGED\n\nSpacing:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n6. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nDebug: SUCCESS\nR8: SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 004 SETTINGS SHELL CLEANUP COMPLETE\n\nPlaceholder/debug strings removed: <n>\nPATCH-number user-visible strings remaining: <n>\n\nFunctional Settings rows: <n>\nDisabled placeholder rows: <n>\n\nVisual design changed: <NO/YES>\n\nDynamic Color changed: <NO/YES>\n\nDebug: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nUI_APPROVED_FUNCTIONAL_INCOMPLETE"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:304:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787236910,"text":"FASE: PATCH 004 V2 — SETTINGS FUNCTIONAL WIRING\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCurrent PATCH 004 Settings UI\n\nSTATUS:\nVISUAL UI APPROVED\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nVALIDATED / FROZEN\n\nPATCH 002:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nMantenere ESATTAMENTE il Settings visuale approvato\ne collegare le voci a funzioni reali.\n\nREMOVE all user-visible development text:\n\nPATCH 001\nPATCH 002\nPATCH 003\nPATCH 004\nCore V2\nplaceholder\ndebug status\nimplementation notes\n\nThe user must see only product-facing Settings.\n\n==================================================\n1. VISUAL HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT change:\n\nlegacy icons\nicon sizes\nrow layout\nspacing\ntypography\nDynamic Color\nshapes\ndividers\nnavigation appearance\nSettings entry icon in Fav\n\nThis phase is FUNCTIONAL WIRING ONLY.\n\n==================================================\n2. KEEP SETTINGS SMALL\n==================================================\n\nFinal functional structure:\n\nAPPEARANCE\n- Icon shape\n- Dynamic color\n\nHOME\n- Layout\n- Haptic & gestures\n\nSEARCH\n- Search behavior\n- History\n\nSYSTEM\n- Set as default Home\n- App info\n\nABOUT\n- Version\n- Changelog\n\nNo additional categories.\n\n==================================================\n3. APPEARANCE — ICON SHAPE\n==================================================\n\nConnect Icon shape to the existing Machina icon rendering\ncapability if it already exists.\n\nProvide only supported shapes actually implemented.\n\nExample only if supported:\n\nSystem\nCircle\nRounded square\nSquircle\n\nDo NOT create fake options.\n\nSelection must immediately update Machina icon rendering.\n\nPersist selected shape using PATCH 004-owned preference/state,\nor reuse an existing safe icon-shape preference if already present.\n\nDo NOT mutate P1/P2/Dock identities.\n\n==================================================\n4. APPEARANCE — DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nDynamic Color already applies to Settings.\n\nExpose a real switch:\n\nDynamic color\n[ON/OFF]\n\nDefault:\nON\n\nON:\nuse Android dynamic color when supported.\n\nOFF:\nuse Machina fallback Settings color scheme.\n\nScope:\nSETTINGS ONLY for now.\n\nPersist this preference.\n\nDo NOT change Home colors.\n\n==================================================\n5. HOME — LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nLayout page must be useful but minimal.\n\nFor this first functional version expose only values\nthat already have safe runtime support.\n\nPreferred:\n\nFav / Home spacing\nor other existing layout token that can be safely adjusted.\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nDo NOT expose arbitrary P1/P2/Dock positioning if this would\nbreak validated geometry.\n\nIf no safe layout control currently exists:\n\nshow read-only current layout information\ninstead of implementing dangerous mutation.\n\n==================================================\n6. HOME — HAPTIC & GESTURES\n==================================================\n\nExpose only safe controls.\n\nHAPTIC:\n\nSwitch:\nHaptic feedback\n\nDefault:\nON\n\nON:\nexisting performHapticFeedback paths enabled.\n\nOFF:\nMachina command/patch haptics suppressed.\n\nDo not change Android system haptics.\n\nGESTURES:\n\nShow current gesture configuration.\n\nDo NOT allow changing PATCH 001 validated LEFT/RIGHT behavior\nyet unless an existing safe abstraction already supports it.\n\nPreferred baseline:\n\nLEFT / RIGHT:\nMaterial Stretch\nread-only\n\nUP / DOWN:\ncurrent PATCH 002 behavior\nread-only\n\n==================================================\n7. HAPTIC SINGLE SOURCE\n==================================================\n\nDo not add separate haptic toggles in every patch.\n\nCreate/use one minimal Machina preference/API:\n\nhapticEnabled\n\nPATCH 001 / PATCH 002 / PATCH 004 command haptic paths\nread this value.\n\nDo NOT duplicate haptic state owners.\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH — SEARCH BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 002 currently owns Search bar/reveal UI.\n\nDo not duplicate query/focus/IME state.\n\nExpose only implemented behavior.\n\nPossible real setting:\n\nAuto-open keyboard\n[ON/OFF]\n\nDefault:\nON\n\nON:\naccepted Search reveal requests focus + keyboard.\n\nOFF:\nSearch reveals but keyboard opens only after field tap.\n\nPersist preference.\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH — HISTORY\n==================================================\n\nIf Search history engine is NOT implemented yet:\n\nDO NOT show fake controls.\n\nPreferred:\n\nremove History row temporarily.\n\nIf in-memory history already exists:\n\nshow:\n\nHistory\nIn memory · cleared when Android ends the process\n\nOptional action:\nClear history\n\nNo disk persistence for Search history.\n\n==================================================\n10. SYSTEM — SET AS DEFAULT HOME\n==================================================\n\nMake functional.\n\nUse:\n\nRoleManager.ROLE_HOME\n\nwhere supported.\n\nTap:\nopen the Android-supported Home role request/selection flow.\n\nIf Machina is already default Home:\n\nshow status:\nDefault Home\n\nDo not repeatedly prompt.\n\nNo hidden APIs.\n\n==================================================\n11. SYSTEM — APP INFO\n==================================================\n\nMake functional.\n\nOpen Android application details for Machina using:\n\nSettings.ACTION_APPLICATION_DETAILS_SETTINGS\n\nwith Machina package URI.\n\nNo custom App Info screen.\n\n==================================================\n12. ABOUT — VERSION\n==================================================\n\nRead actual application metadata.\n\nShow:\n\nversionName\nversionCode\n\nDo not hardcode version strings.\n\n==================================================\n13. ABOUT — CHANGELOG\n==================================================\n\nCreate a user-facing Changelog source owned by PATCH 004.\n\nDo NOT expose internal patch audit text.\n\nChangelog must contain only understandable product changes.\n\nExample structure:\n\nCurrent version\n\n- Improved Home interactions\n- Added Search interface\n- Added Settings\n- Improved haptic feedback\n- Visual refinements\n\nUse only features actually present in current build.\n\n==================================================\n14. REMOVE DEVELOPMENT TEXT\n==================================================\n\nSearch all user-visible Settings strings for:\n\nPATCH\nCore V2\nVALIDATED\nFROZEN\nruntime\nowner\nhook\nplaceholder\ndebug\n\nExpected user-visible occurrences:\n0\n\nInternal docs may retain these terms.\n\n==================================================\n15. SETTINGS PREFERENCES\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 004 may persist ONLY real user settings.\n\nInitial allowed persisted settings:\n\ndynamicColorEnabled\nhapticEnabled\nsearchAutoKeyboard\niconShape (only if truly implemented)\n\nNo placeholder keys.\n\n==================================================\n16. PREFERENCE OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nUse one Settings preference owner.\n\nDo not scatter SharedPreferences/DataStore access\nthrough composables.\n\nIf LauncherPreferences already provides a safe general\npreference mechanism, evaluate reuse.\n\nDo NOT contaminate P1/P2/Dock slot persistence.\n\n==================================================\n17. DEFAULT VALUES\n==================================================\n\nDynamic Color:\nON\n\nHaptic:\nON\n\nSearch auto keyboard:\nON\n\nIcon shape:\ncurrent existing behavior\n\nDo not reset values on app restart.\n\n==================================================\n18. SETTINGS STATE\n==================================================\n\nUI state should derive from preference state.\n\nNo duplicated mutable copies unless required for Compose.\n\nOne source of truth per setting.\n\n==================================================\n19. IMMEDIATE APPLY\n==================================================\n\nWhen a user changes a setting:\n\napply immediately where safe.\n\nNo Save button.\n\nNo Apply screen.\n\nMaterial switch/selection updates directly.\n\n==================================================\n20. HAPTIC ON SETTINGS COMMAND\n==================================================\n\nIf hapticEnabled == true:\n\naccepted Settings action:\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nonce.\n\nChanging hapticEnabled from ON -> OFF:\n\ndo not require an extra vibration after it has been disabled.\n\n==================================================\n21. CORE PROTECTION\n==================================================\n\nCore logic:\nUNCHANGED\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nP1/P2/Dock identities:\nUNCHANGED\n\nAppCatalog:\nUNCHANGED\n\nLauncherActions:\nUNCHANGED except reuse, not duplication.\n\n==================================================\n22. PATCH 001 PROTECTION\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change PATCH 001 motion implementation.\n\nOnly permitted integration:\n\nread hapticEnabled through the minimal shared preference/API\nif required.\n\nLEFT/RIGHT Material Stretch behavior:\nUNCHANGED\n\nedge handling:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n23. PATCH 002 PROTECTION\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change PATCH 002 geometry.\n\nPermitted integration:\n\nread searchAutoKeyboard\nread hapticEnabled\n\nNo gesture redesign.\n\nNo SearchSlot redesign.\n\n==================================================\n24. SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nNo reflection.\nNo hidden APIs.\nNo dynamic code loading.\nNo credentials.\nNo broad R8 keep rules.\n\nSettings intents must be explicit/safe.\n\n==================================================\n25. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nOpening Settings:\n\nPackageManager full enumeration = 0\nnetwork = 0\nwallpaper decode = 0\npolling = 0\n\nPreference reads must be lightweight.\n\n==================================================\n26. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 004 remains removable.\n\nRemoving PATCH 004:\n\nCore + PATCH 001 + PATCH 002 still work with their\nsafe defaults.\n\nShared preference/API integration must have safe default values\nif Settings UI is absent.\n\n==================================================\n27. CODE SECURITY GATE\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md.\n\nVerify:\n\nSettings preference owners = 1\nduplicate state owners = 0\nnew lifecycle owners = 0\nHomeSnapshot writes = 0\nplaceholder preference keys = 0\nuser-visible PATCH/debug strings = 0\n\n==================================================\n28. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot validation = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n29. DEVICE STATUS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT mark VALIDATED automatically.\n\nAfter build:\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\nTest on Pixel:\n\n- Settings visual unchanged\n- Dynamic Color switch works\n- Haptic switch works\n- Search keyboard option works\n- Icon shape works if exposed\n- Set default Home works\n- App info opens Android Settings\n- Version is real\n- Changelog contains no development terminology\n- Home regressions = NONE\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 004 FUNCTIONAL SETTINGS COMPLETE\n\nVisual design changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUser-visible PATCH/debug strings:\n<n>\n\nFunctional settings:\n<n>\n\nSettings preference owners:\n<n>\n\nPersisted keys:\n<list>\n\nDynamic Color:\n<FUNCTIONAL/FAILED>\n\nDynamic Color default:\n<ON/OFF>\n\nIcon shape:\n<FUNCTIONAL/NOT_EXPOSED/FAILED>\n\nHaptic toggle:\n<FUNCTIONAL/FAILED>\n\nHaptic default:\n<ON/OFF>\n\nSearch auto-keyboard:\n<FUNCTIONAL/FAILED>\n\nSearch auto-keyboard default:\n<ON/OFF>\n\nSearch history:\n<FUNCTIONAL/NOT_EXPOSED>\n\nSet default Home:\n<FUNCTIONAL/FAILED>\n\nApp info:\n<FUNCTIONAL/FAILED>\n\nVersion:\n<RUNTIME_METADATA/HARDCODED>\n\nChangelog:\n<USER_FACING/FAILED>\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n<n>\n\nPATCH 001 behavior changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 geometry changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\n<DEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:305:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787237358,"text":"PATCH 004 FIX — STATUS BAR SAFE INSETS\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nSettings must never place interactive/content UI\nunder the Android status bar.\n\nKEEP:\n- edge-to-edge window configuration\n- Dynamic Color\n- current Settings visual design\n- current icons\n- current navigation\n\n==================================================\n1. TOP INSETS\n==================================================\n\nSettings root must respect:\n\nWindowInsets.statusBars\n\nUse appropriate Compose inset handling, for example:\n\nstatusBarsPadding()\n\nor\n\nwindowInsetsPadding(WindowInsets.statusBars)\n\nApply it to the Settings top-level content/app-bar region.\n\n==================================================\n2. TOP APP BAR\n==================================================\n\nTopAppBar must begin BELOW the status bar safe inset.\n\nNo title/icon/button may overlap:\n\n- clock\n- signal icons\n- battery\n- cutout area\n\n==================================================\n3. DO NOT DOUBLE-PAD\n==================================================\n\nAudit existing:\n\nstatusBarsPadding()\nsafeDrawingPadding()\nwindowInsetsPadding()\nScaffold contentWindowInsets\nTopAppBar windowInsets\n\nTarget:\none coherent owner.\n\nAvoid double top padding.\n\n==================================================\n4. SUBPAGES\n==================================================\n\nAll Settings subpages must use the same inset policy.\n\nRoot:\nsafe\n\nCategory:\nsafe\n\nSubpage:\nsafe\n\n==================================================\n5. HOME UNCHANGED\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change Home edge-to-edge behavior.\n\nThis fix is PATCH 004 Settings only.\n\n==================================================\n6. BOTTOM INSETS\n==================================================\n\nSettings should also respect navigation/gesture bottom inset\nfor scrollable content.\n\nNo Settings row hidden under gesture navigation area.\n\n==================================================\n7. OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 004 STATUS BAR INSET FIX COMPLETE\n\nStatus bar overlap:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nTop inset owner:\n<value>\n\nDouble top padding:\n<NO/YES>\n\nRoot Settings safe:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSubpages safe:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHome modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:306:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787237516,"text":"PATCH 004 V2 — SETTINGS NETWORK PARTICLES BACKGROUND\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\ncurrent PATCH 004 Settings\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 002:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAdd a subtle animated background to Settings only.\n\nVisual:\n\n- small circular particles\n- very thin connecting lines\n- particles move slowly\n- nearby particles connect\n- background remains quiet and elegant\n- Settings content stays fully readable\n\n==================================================\n1. SCOPE\n==================================================\n\nAnimation scope:\nSETTINGS ONLY\n\nDo NOT apply to Home.\n\nDo NOT modify:\n- Home wallpaper\n- PATCH 001 motion\n- PATCH 002 Search\n- Core\n\n==================================================\n2. VISUAL STYLE\n==================================================\n\nParticles:\n\n- small circles\n- roughly 2–4dp visual diameter\n- low contrast\n- soft Material/Dynamic Color tint\n\nLines:\n\n- very thin\n- low alpha\n- only between nearby particles\n- no thick web\n- no glow\n\n==================================================\n3. PARTICLE COUNT\n==================================================\n\nKeep low.\n\nTarget:\n~12–20 particles on phone portrait.\n\nDo not create hundreds of nodes.\n\n==================================================\n4. MOTION\n==================================================\n\nMovement must be:\n\n- slow\n- continuous\n- subtle\n- non-distracting\n\nNo bounce.\nNo abrupt direction changes.\nNo flashing.\n\nParticles drift gently.\n\n==================================================\n5. CONNECTION RULE\n==================================================\n\nConnect two particles only if distance is below\na fixed visual threshold.\n\nKeep max connections bounded.\n\nDo not evaluate an unbounded graph.\n\n==================================================\n6. DRAWING\n==================================================\n\nPrefer one Compose Canvas/background owner.\n\nOne animation owner.\n\nDo not create one Composable/Animatable per particle.\n\nPreferred:\nsingle draw loop/state model.\n\n==================================================\n7. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nCritical:\n\n- no allocations per frame where avoidable\n- no bitmap decode\n- no network\n- no PackageManager work\n- no disk IO\n- no coroutine per particle\n- no unbounded O(n²) with large n\n\nWith <=20 particles, bounded pair checks are acceptable.\n\n==================================================\n8. DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nUse current Settings Dynamic Color tokens.\n\nPreferred:\n\nparticles:\nonSurfaceVariant / primary with very low alpha\n\nlines:\noutlineVariant / onSurfaceVariant with very low alpha\n\nDo NOT hardcode bright neon colors.\n\n==================================================\n9. ALPHA\n==================================================\n\nKeep background subtle.\n\nSuggested starting point:\n\nparticle alpha:\n~0.18–0.28\n\nline alpha:\n~0.06–0.12\n\nTune visually on Pixel.\n\n==================================================\n10. CONTENT LAYER\n==================================================\n\nLayer order:\n\nDynamic Color background\n→ particle network animation\n→ Settings UI content\n\nSettings text/icons remain above animation.\n\n==================================================\n11. STATUS BAR\n==================================================\n\nAnimation may draw behind the status bar background,\nbut interactive Settings content must still respect\nstatusBars insets.\n\nDo not move content under system icons.\n\n==================================================\n12. TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nBackground animation must be completely non-interactive.\n\nNo pointerInput.\nNo gesture owner.\nNo touch interception.\n\nSettings rows/toggles keep normal first-touch behavior.\n\n==================================================\n13. ACCESSIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nRespect reduced-motion / animator scale when possible.\n\nIf system animations are disabled/reduced:\nshow static particle background or pause motion.\n\n==================================================\n14. LIFECYCLE\n==================================================\n\nAnimate only while Settings is visible.\n\nWhen Settings leaves composition:\nanimation stops naturally.\n\nNo background service.\nNo keep-alive.\nNo global animation scope.\n\n==================================================\n15. RANDOMNESS\n==================================================\n\nInitial particle placement may be pseudo-random.\n\nPrefer stable seed per Settings session\nto avoid layout flashing/reseeding every recomposition.\n\nDo not persist positions.\n\n==================================================\n16. BOUNDS\n==================================================\n\nParticles stay inside Settings background bounds.\n\nWrap or softly reverse direction at edges.\n\nNo particles escaping canvas.\n\n==================================================\n17. SETTINGS UI LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nlegacy Settings icons\ncategory layout\ntypography\nDynamic Color behavior\nspacing\nnavigation\nfunctional Settings wiring\n\nOnly add background layer.\n\n==================================================\n18. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0 preferred\n\nNew persistence:\n0\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 002 modified:\nNO\n\n==================================================\n19. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 004 NETWORK PARTICLES BACKGROUND COMPLETE\n\nParticle count:\n<n>\n\nParticle diameter:\n<dp>\n\nConnection threshold:\n<value>\n\nAnimation owners:\n<n>\n\nGesture owners added:\n<n>\n\nParticles alpha:\n<value>\n\nLines alpha:\n<value>\n\nDynamic Color used:\n<YES/NO>\n\nReduced-motion handling:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSettings content modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:307:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787238044,"text":"PATCH 004 FIX — REAL ANIMATED NETWORK PARTICLES\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nReplace any static wallpaper/background asset used for\nNETWORK PARTICLES with a REAL animated particle network.\n\nNO image wallpaper.\nNO bitmap background.\nNO static decorative asset.\n\n==================================================\n1. REAL ANIMATION\n==================================================\n\nUse one Compose Canvas.\n\nParticles are generated in memory.\n\nEach particle has:\n\n- x\n- y\n- velocityX\n- velocityY\n\nParticles move continuously while Settings is visible.\n\n==================================================\n2. CONNECTIONS\n==================================================\n\nDraw thin lines between nearby particles.\n\nConnection appears only when distance < threshold.\n\nLine alpha decreases with distance.\n\n==================================================\n3. PARTICLES\n==================================================\n\nTarget:\n\n14–18 particles\n\nDiameter:\n2–3dp\n\nMotion:\nslow\n\nNo bounce animation.\n\nParticles drift naturally.\n\n==================================================\n4. EDGE BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nWhen particle reaches canvas boundary:\n\nsoftly reverse velocity\nor wrap to opposite edge.\n\nNo sudden teleport visible if possible.\n\n==================================================\n5. ONE ANIMATION LOOP\n==================================================\n\nUse one animation owner only.\n\nPreferred:\n\nwithFrameNanos / frame clock\n\nor equivalent Compose animation loop.\n\nDO NOT create:\n\nAnimatable per particle\ncoroutine per particle\nComposable per particle\n\n==================================================\n6. FRAME UPDATE\n==================================================\n\nEach frame:\n\ndeltaTime\n→ update particle positions\n→ request redraw\n\nMovement must be time-based,\nnot frame-count based.\n\n==================================================\n7. NO WALLPAPER\n==================================================\n\nRemove/disable any NETWORK PARTICLES implementation using:\n\nImage\npainterResource\nBitmap\ndrawable wallpaper\nbackground image\n\nExpected static wallpaper assets added for this feature:\n0\n\n==================================================\n8. LAYER ORDER\n==================================================\n\nSettings background color\n→ animated network Canvas\n→ Settings UI content\n\nCanvas:\nnon-interactive.\n\n==================================================\n9. DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nParticles/lines should use Settings Dynamic Color.\n\nSuggested:\n\nparticles:\nprimary/onSurfaceVariant low alpha\n\nlines:\noutlineVariant low alpha\n\nNo hardcoded neon colors.\n\n==================================================\n10. INTENSITY\n==================================================\n\nKeep subtle.\n\nInitial target:\n\nparticle alpha:\n~0.22\n\nline max alpha:\n~0.10\n\nLine fades toward 0 as distance approaches threshold.\n\n==================================================\n11. SPEED\n==================================================\n\nVery slow movement.\n\nTarget order:\na few dp per second,\nnot fast floating dots.\n\nAvoid distracting motion.\n\n==================================================\n12. CONNECTION THRESHOLD\n==================================================\n\nUse a moderate threshold derived from canvas size/density.\n\nDo not connect every particle to every other visually.\n\nKeep web sparse.\n\n==================================================\n13. SETTINGS ONLY\n==================================================\n\nAnimation active only while Settings is composed.\n\nLeaving Settings:\nanimation loop stops.\n\nHome:\nunchanged.\n\n==================================================\n14. STATUS BAR\n==================================================\n\nCanvas may draw behind Settings background/status region.\n\nBut Settings content still respects status bar insets.\n\n==================================================\n15. TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nCanvas must not intercept touch.\n\nGesture owners added:\n0\n\nPointer input:\n0\n\n==================================================\n16. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nNo allocation-heavy per-frame objects if avoidable.\n\nReuse particle list.\n\nNo network.\nNo disk IO.\nNo bitmap decode.\n\nParticle count must remain bounded.\n\n==================================================\n17. REDUCED MOTION\n==================================================\n\nIf system animations are disabled/reduced:\n\nfreeze particles\nor reduce movement to zero.\n\nKeep static dots/lines if desired.\n\n==================================================\n18. SETTINGS VISUAL LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nSettings icons\nSettings typography\nSettings spacing\nDynamic Color\nnavigation\nfunctional settings\nFav Settings entry\n\nOnly replace static background implementation with animation.\n\n==================================================\n19. SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 002 modified:\nNO\n\nNew persistence:\n0\n\nNew lifecycle owner:\n0 preferred\n\n==================================================\n20. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA REAL NETWORK PARTICLES ANIMATION COMPLETE\n\nStatic wallpaper/image paths:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n0\n\nCanvas animation:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticle count:\n<n>\n\nAnimation owners:\n<n>\n\nPer-particle Animatable:\n<n>\n\nPer-particle coroutines:\n<n>\n\nParticle movement:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDynamic connections:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDistance-based line alpha:\n<YES/NO>\n\nGesture owners added:\n<n>\n\nReduced-motion support:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSettings UI changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:308:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787238253,"text":"PATCH 004 V2 — FUNCTIONAL SETTINGS COMPLETE\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\ncurrent PATCH 004 visual approved\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nVALIDATED / FROZEN\n\nPATCH 002:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nKeep the approved Settings visual unchanged.\n\nAdd real working settings behind the existing categories.\n\nRemove every fake/placeholder row.\n\nDo not expose options that have no functional backend.\n\n==================================================\n1. APPEARANCE\n==================================================\n\nFunctional options:\n\nA. Icon shape\n\nOnly expose shapes already supported by Machina.\n\nExamples if supported:\n- System\n- Circle\n- Rounded\n- Squircle\n\nPersist:\niconShape\n\nApply immediately.\n\nDo not change slot identities.\n\nB. Dynamic Color\n\nSwitch:\nON/OFF\n\nDefault:\nON\n\nScope:\nSettings only\n\nON:\nAndroid dynamic color\n\nOFF:\nMachina fallback scheme\n\nPersist:\ndynamicColorEnabled\n\n==================================================\n2. HOME\n==================================================\n\nFunctional options:\n\nA. Haptic feedback\n\nSwitch:\nON/OFF\n\nDefault:\nON\n\nControls Machina app haptic only.\n\nUse:\nperformHapticFeedback(...)\n\nDo not change system haptic settings.\n\nPersist:\nhapticEnabled\n\nB. Home spacing\n\nExpose only if the current layout has a safe tokenized value.\n\nPrefer:\nCompact\nDefault\nRelaxed\n\nDo NOT expose arbitrary dp slider.\n\nPersist:\nhomeSpacingMode\n\nIf safe runtime support is absent:\ndo not show this row.\n\nC. Gesture status\n\nRead-only status:\n\nLEFT / RIGHT:\nMaterial Stretch\n\nUP / DOWN:\ncurrent behavior\n\nDo not make validated PATCH 001 behavior user-editable yet.\n\n==================================================\n3. SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nFunctional options:\n\nA. Auto-open keyboard\n\nSwitch:\nON/OFF\n\nDefault:\nON\n\nON:\nSearch reveal requests focus + keyboard\n\nOFF:\nSearch reveals, keyboard opens only on field tap\n\nPersist:\nsearchAutoKeyboard\n\nB. Search history\n\nIf PATCH 003 history is active:\n\nshow:\nHistory size\nClear history\n\nIf PATCH 003 is not active:\ndo not show fake History controls.\n\nC. Search sources\n\nOnly if corresponding backends exist:\n\nApps\nSystem Settings\nWeb\n\nUse switches only for implemented sources.\n\nNo fake providers.\n\n==================================================\n4. SYSTEM\n==================================================\n\nA. Set as default Home\n\nFunctional.\n\nUse:\nRoleManager.ROLE_HOME\n\nShow current state:\n\nDefault Home\nor\nSet as default\n\nB. App info\n\nFunctional.\n\nOpen:\nSettings.ACTION_APPLICATION_DETAILS_SETTINGS\n\nfor Machina package.\n\nC. Battery optimization\n\nOptional only if useful.\n\nPrefer opening Android system screen,\nnot implementing custom battery management.\n\n==================================================\n5. ABOUT\n==================================================\n\nA. Version\n\nRead actual:\n\nversionName\nversionCode\n\nNo hardcoded version.\n\nB. Changelog\n\nUser-facing only.\n\nNo:\nPATCH 001\nPATCH 002\nCore V2\nVALIDATED\nFROZEN\ninternal audit terminology\n\nC. Licenses\n\nShow only if licenses screen/resource already exists.\n\n==================================================\n6. SETTINGS PREFERENCE OWNER\n==================================================\n\nCreate/use one Settings preference owner.\n\nAllowed keys only:\n\ndynamicColorEnabled\niconShape\nhapticEnabled\nhomeSpacingMode\nsearchAutoKeyboard\nsearchAppsEnabled\nsearchSettingsEnabled\nsearchWebEnabled\n\nOnly create a key if its setting is actually implemented.\n\nNo placeholder preferences.\n\n==================================================\n7. DEFAULTS\n==================================================\n\ndynamicColorEnabled:\ntrue\n\nhapticEnabled:\ntrue\n\nsearchAutoKeyboard:\ntrue\n\niconShape:\ncurrent existing behavior\n\nhomeSpacingMode:\ncurrent approved geometry\n\nSearch source defaults:\nenabled for every implemented source.\n\n==================================================\n8. IMMEDIATE APPLY\n==================================================\n\nNo Save button.\n\nToggle/selection:\napply immediately.\n\nUI derives from single source of truth.\n\n==================================================\n9. VISUAL HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nlegacy icons\nnetwork particles animation\ncategory layout\ntypography\nspacing\nshapes\nDynamic Color visual language\nFav Settings icon\n\n==================================================\n10. REMOVE NON-FUNCTIONAL ROWS\n==================================================\n\nAudit every current Settings row.\n\nClassify:\n\nFUNCTIONAL\nREAD_ONLY_USEFUL\nPLACEHOLDER\n\nRemove every PLACEHOLDER row.\n\nUser-visible placeholder rows:\n0\n\n==================================================\n11. REMOVE INTERNAL TEXT\n==================================================\n\nUser-facing occurrence count must be 0 for:\n\nPATCH\nCore V2\nFROZEN\nVALIDATED\nruntime owner\nhook\nimplementation\nplaceholder\n\n==================================================\n12. HAPTIC INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nOne shared setting:\n\nhapticEnabled\n\nPATCH 001 / PATCH 002 / PATCH 004 should consume\nthe same preference/API.\n\nDo not create duplicate haptic state.\n\nIf OFF:\nMachina haptic paths suppressed.\n\nMotion/gestures continue normally.\n\n==================================================\n13. SEARCH INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 002 geometry:\nUNCHANGED\n\nOnly permitted integration:\n\nsearchAutoKeyboard\nand implemented Search-source settings.\n\nNo geometry mutation from Settings.\n\n==================================================\n14. CORE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nP1/P2/Dock identity writes:\n0\n\nAppCatalog owner changes:\n0\n\nCore lifecycle changes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n15. PATCH 001 SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nLEFT/RIGHT Material Stretch:\nUNCHANGED\n\nEdge exclusion:\nUNCHANGED\n\nOnly hapticEnabled read is permitted.\n\n==================================================\n16. PATCH 002 SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nSearch reveal geometry:\nUNCHANGED\n\nOnly preference reads permitted.\n\n==================================================\n17. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nSettings preference owners = 1\nduplicate setting owners = 0\nplaceholder preference keys = 0\nuser-visible debug strings = 0\nnew lifecycle owners = 0\nHomeSnapshot writes = 0\n\n==================================================\n18. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\nSnapshot:\nPASS\n\nSHA-256:\nPASS\n\n==================================================\n19. DEVICE TEST\n==================================================\n\nOn Pixel verify:\n\nDynamic Color toggle:\nworks\n\nIcon shape:\nworks if exposed\n\nHaptic toggle:\nworks\n\nSearch auto-keyboard:\nworks\n\nSearch source toggles:\nwork if exposed\n\nSet default Home:\nworks\n\nApp info:\nworks\n\nVersion:\nreal\n\nChangelog:\nuser-facing\n\nNetwork particles:\nstill animated\n\nSettings visual:\nunchanged\n\nHome regressions:\nNONE\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 004 FUNCTIONAL SETTINGS COMPLETE\n\nCurrent Settings rows:\n<n>\n\nFunctional rows:\n<n>\n\nRead-only useful rows:\n<n>\n\nPlaceholder rows:\n<n>\n\nUser-visible internal/debug strings:\n<n>\n\nPreference owner:\n<n>\n\nPersisted keys:\n<list>\n\nDynamic Color:\n<FUNCTIONAL/FAILED>\n\nIcon shape:\n<FUNCTIONAL/NOT_EXPOSED/FAILED>\n\nHaptic:\n<FUNCTIONAL/FAILED>\n\nHome spacing:\n<FUNCTIONAL/NOT_EXPOSED/FAILED>\n\nSearch auto keyboard:\n<FUNCTIONAL/FAILED>\n\nSearch sources:\n<list>\n\nSearch history:\n<FUNCTIONAL/NOT_EXPOSED>\n\nDefault Home:\n<FUNCTIONAL/FAILED>\n\nApp info:\n<FUNCTIONAL/FAILED>\n\nVersion:\n<RUNTIME/FAILED>\n\nChangelog:\n<USER_FACING/FAILED>\n\nNetwork particles regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nPATCH 001 behavior changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 geometry changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:309:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787238379,"text":"PATCH 004 FIX — REMOVE STATIC WALLPAPER / ENABLE REAL PARTICLE CANVAS\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nPROBLEM\n\nSettings still shows the previous static wallpaper/background.\nNo visible animated network particles.\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRemove the static Settings wallpaper path and make the real\nanimated particle Canvas the active Settings background.\n\nDO NOT modify:\n- Settings layout\n- Settings icons\n- typography\n- Dynamic Color\n- categories\n- navigation\n- functional settings\n- Core\n- PATCH 001\n- PATCH 002\n\n==================================================\n1. AUDIT CURRENT BACKGROUND\n==================================================\n\nFind every Settings background path:\n\nImage(...)\npainterResource(...)\nBitmap\ndrawable resource\nbackground(...)\ndrawBehind(...)\nCanvas\nparticle implementation\n\nReport which one is actually active at runtime.\n\n==================================================\n2. REMOVE STATIC WALLPAPER FROM SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nSettings must NOT render any background image.\n\nTarget:\n\nSettings Image wallpaper paths = 0\nSettings bitmap background paths = 0\n\nDo not remove Android Home wallpaper behavior.\n\nThis applies only to PATCH 004 Settings.\n\n==================================================\n3. REAL PARTICLE CANVAS\n==================================================\n\nUse one animated Compose Canvas behind Settings content.\n\nLayer order:\n\nMaterial/Dynamic Color surface\n→ AnimatedParticleNetwork Canvas\n→ Settings content\n\nCanvas must be actually composed in the Settings root.\n\n==================================================\n4. PARTICLE MODEL\n==================================================\n\nUse approximately:\n\n16 particles\n\nEach particle owns:\n\nx\ny\nvx\nvy\n\nSmall circle:\n2–3dp\n\nNo bitmap particles.\n\n==================================================\n5. REAL FRAME ANIMATION\n==================================================\n\nUse one frame loop:\n\nwithFrameNanos\n\nor current Compose equivalent.\n\nEvery frame:\n\ncalculate delta time\nupdate x/y\nredraw\n\nParticle positions must visibly change over time.\n\nDo not use a static generated list only.\n\n==================================================\n6. MOVEMENT\n==================================================\n\nMovement:\n\nslow but clearly visible when watching for a few seconds.\n\nDo not make velocity so low that animation appears static.\n\nInitial target:\n\napproximately 6–12dp per second.\n\nTune after Pixel test.\n\n==================================================\n7. CONNECTION LINES\n==================================================\n\nFor particles within connection threshold:\n\ndraw line.\n\nLine alpha decreases with distance.\n\nConnections must change as particles move.\n\nNo fixed/static line graph.\n\n==================================================\n8. EDGES\n==================================================\n\nParticles remain inside canvas.\n\nAt edges:\nsoft reverse velocity preferred.\n\nNo off-screen accumulation.\n\n==================================================\n9. COLOR\n==================================================\n\nUse current Settings Dynamic Color scheme.\n\nParticles:\nprimary/onSurfaceVariant low alpha.\n\nLines:\noutlineVariant/onSurfaceVariant lower alpha.\n\nNo wallpaper colors.\n\n==================================================\n10. VISIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nMake animation visible enough to validate.\n\nFor first device test:\n\nparticle alpha:\n~0.30\n\nline max alpha:\n~0.14\n\nAfter confirming it works,\nwe can reduce intensity.\n\n==================================================\n11. NO CONTENT BACKGROUND HIDING CANVAS\n==================================================\n\nAudit Settings root surfaces.\n\nDo NOT place a fully opaque full-screen Surface ABOVE\nthe particle Canvas.\n\nIf Settings content uses Surface:\n\neither:\n- particle Canvas belongs inside that Surface background stack\nor\n- content container uses transparent background where appropriate.\n\nDynamic Color base background stays behind particles.\n\n==================================================\n12. STATUS BAR\n==================================================\n\nParticle Canvas may extend behind system status background.\n\nSettings content continues respecting status bar insets.\n\n==================================================\n13. NON-INTERACTIVE\n==================================================\n\nParticle background:\n\npointerInput = 0\nclickable = 0\ngesture owners = 0\n\nIt must never block Settings controls.\n\n==================================================\n14. LIFECYCLE\n==================================================\n\nAnimation runs only while Settings root is composed/visible.\n\nLeaving Settings:\nframe loop cancels with composition.\n\nNo service.\nNo global scope.\nNo keep-alive.\n\n==================================================\n15. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nParticle count bounded:\n<= 20\n\nNo:\nnetwork\ndisk IO\nbitmap decode\nper-particle coroutine\nper-particle Animatable\n\nOne owner only.\n\n==================================================\n16. STATIC WALLPAPER ASSETS\n==================================================\n\nDo not necessarily delete historical resource files yet.\n\nBut runtime references from Settings to static wallpaper:\n0\n\nIf asset is confirmed PATCH004-only and dead:\nreport it before removal.\n\n==================================================\n17. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 002 modified:\nNO\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nNew persistence:\n0\n\n==================================================\n18. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA SETTINGS PARTICLE ANIMATION RUNTIME FIX COMPLETE\n\nActive Settings background before:\n<STATIC_IMAGE/CANVAS/OTHER>\n\nStatic wallpaper runtime paths after:\n<n>\n\nParticle Canvas composed:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFrame loop active:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticle count:\n<n>\n\nParticle positions change over time:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDynamic connection lines:\n<YES/NO>\n\nOpaque layer hiding Canvas:\n<NO/YES>\n\nParticle speed:\n<value>\n\nParticle alpha:\n<value>\n\nLine alpha:\n<value>\n\nGesture owners added:\n<n>\n\nSettings UI changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
