e a fully opaque full-screen Surface ABOVE\nthe particle Canvas.\n\nIf Settings content uses Surface:\n\neither:\n- particle Canvas belongs inside that Surface background stack\nor\n- content container uses transparent background where appropriate.\n\nDynamic Color base background stays behind particles.\n\n==================================================\n12. STATUS BAR\n==================================================\n\nParticle Canvas may extend behind system status background.\n\nSettings content continues respecting status bar insets.\n\n==================================================\n13. NON-INTERACTIVE\n==================================================\n\nParticle background:\n\npointerInput = 0\nclickable = 0\ngesture owners = 0\n\nIt must never block Settings controls.\n\n==================================================\n14. LIFECYCLE\n==================================================\n\nAnimation runs only while Settings root is composed/visible.\n\nLeaving Settings:\nframe loop cancels with composition.\n\nNo service.\nNo global scope.\nNo keep-alive.\n\n==================================================\n15. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nParticle count bounded:\n<= 20\n\nNo:\nnetwork\ndisk IO\nbitmap decode\nper-particle coroutine\nper-particle Animatable\n\nOne owner only.\n\n==================================================\n16. STATIC WALLPAPER ASSETS\n==================================================\n\nDo not necessarily delete historical resource files yet.\n\nBut runtime references from Settings to static wallpaper:\n0\n\nIf asset is confirmed PATCH004-only and dead:\nreport it before removal.\n\n==================================================\n17. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 002 modified:\nNO\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nNew persistence:\n0\n\n==================================================\n18. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA SETTINGS PARTICLE ANIMATION RUNTIME FIX COMPLETE\n\nActive Settings background before:\n<STATIC_IMAGE/CANVAS/OTHER>\n\nStatic wallpaper runtime paths after:\n<n>\n\nParticle Canvas composed:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFrame loop active:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticle count:\n<n>\n\nParticle positions change over time:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDynamic connection lines:\n<YES/NO>\n\nOpaque layer hiding Canvas:\n<NO/YES>\n\nParticle speed:\n<value>\n\nParticle alpha:\n<value>\n\nLine alpha:\n<value>\n\nGesture owners added:\n<n>\n\nSettings UI changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:311:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787238825,"text":"PATCH 004 FIX — INCREASE PARTICLE VISIBILITY ONLY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nKeep the current animated network particles implementation.\n\nIncrease ONLY visual visibility.\n\nDO NOT change:\n- particle count\n- movement speed\n- connection logic\n- Settings layout\n- Dynamic Color behavior\n- gestures\n- lifecycle\n- Core\n- PATCH 001\n- PATCH 002\n\n==================================================\n1. PARTICLES\n==================================================\n\nCurrent particles are almost invisible.\n\nIncrease particle alpha.\n\nTarget:\n\nparticle alpha:\n~0.42\n\nAllowed:\n0.38–0.46\n\nKeep diameter unchanged unless absolutely necessary.\n\n==================================================\n2. LINES\n==================================================\n\nIncrease connection line visibility slightly.\n\nTarget:\n\nline max alpha:\n~0.20\n\nAllowed:\n0.16–0.22\n\nDistance-based fade:\nKEEP.\n\n==================================================\n3. COLOR SOURCE\n==================================================\n\nKeep Dynamic Color tokens.\n\nPrefer:\n\nparticles:\nprimary / onSurfaceVariant\n\nlines:\noutlineVariant / onSurfaceVariant\n\nDo not hardcode white/neon.\n\n==================================================\n4. NO HEAVY EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT add:\n\nglow\nblur\nshadow\nthicker strokes\nlarger particles\nfaster motion\n\nThe network should still remain background decoration.\n\n==================================================\n5. CONTENT READABILITY\n==================================================\n\nSettings text/icons must remain dominant.\n\nIf contrast becomes too strong:\nreduce only line alpha first.\n\n==================================================\n6. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PARTICLE VISIBILITY INCREASED\n\nParticle alpha:\n<value>\n\nLine max alpha:\n<value>\n\nParticle size changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nParticle speed changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nConnection logic changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSettings UI changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:312:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787239079,"text":"PATCH 005 V2 — APP SLOT EDITOR\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\ncurrent validated Machina baseline\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nFROZEN\n\nDO NOT modify existing patch behavior.\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAllow user to manually assign installed applications to:\n\nP1 = 8 slots\nP2 = 8 slots\nDock = 5 slots\n\nusing one common interaction model.\n\n==================================================\n1. INTERACTION\n==================================================\n\nNORMAL TAP on assigned slot:\nlaunch app exactly as today.\n\nLONG PRESS:\nopen App Picker for that specific slot.\n\nEmpty slot:\ntap or long press may open App Picker.\n\nPrefer:\nlong press everywhere for consistency.\n\n==================================================\n2. ONE SLOT EDITOR\n==================================================\n\nUse one implementation for:\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nDo NOT create separate editors.\n\nConcept:\n\neditSlot(\n    target = P1/P2/DOCK,\n    index = n\n)\n\n==================================================\n3. APP PICKER\n==================================================\n\nShow installed launchable apps using EXISTING AppCatalog.\n\nDo NOT create another PackageManager scanner.\n\nPicker:\n\n- app icon\n- app label\n- compact list/grid\n- alphabetical\n- searchable if simple\n\n==================================================\n4. ICONS\n==================================================\n\nUse existing Machina AppVisuals/icon resolver.\n\nSelected app must look exactly like apps already shown\non Home.\n\nNo duplicate icon cache.\n\n==================================================\n5. ASSIGN\n==================================================\n\nSelecting an app:\n\nwrite only the selected slot identity.\n\nExamples:\n\nP1[3] = selected app\nP2[6] = selected app\nDock[1] = selected app\n\nDo not rebuild the entire HomeSnapshot manually.\n\nUse the existing safe persistence/state API.\n\n==================================================\n6. REMOVE\n==================================================\n\nProvide:\n\nRemove from Home\n\nfor occupied slots.\n\nResult:\n\nslot = explicit empty\n\nDo NOT auto-fill another app.\n\n==================================================\n7. EXPLICIT EMPTY\n==================================================\n\nPreserve Core V2 contract:\n\nempty means intentionally empty.\n\nNo suggestions.\nNo automatic replacement.\nNo random app.\n\n==================================================\n8. PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nAssignments MUST survive process death/reboot.\n\nUse existing LauncherPreferences slot persistence.\n\nDo NOT create PATCH-specific duplicate slot storage.\n\n==================================================\n9. HOME SNAPSHOT\n==================================================\n\nAfter valid assignment/removal:\n\nupdate through the existing Core owner/API.\n\nHomeSnapshot owner remains:\n1\n\nPATCH 005 must not become another snapshot owner.\n\n==================================================\n10. SLOT COUNTS\n==================================================\n\nHard contract:\n\nP1:\nexactly 8\n\nP2:\nexactly 8\n\nDock:\nexactly 5\n\nPATCH 005 cannot change these counts.\n\n==================================================\n11. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nLong press accepted:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.LONG_PRESS\n)\n\nApp assignment accepted:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nRemove accepted:\nCONFIRM\n\nRespect global Machina hapticEnabled setting if present.\n\n==================================================\n12. GESTURE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nLong press must coexist with PATCH 001/PATCH 002 gestures.\n\nNormal swipe:\nmust NOT open picker.\n\nLong press without meaningful drag:\nopens picker.\n\nFirst normal tap:\nstill launches app.\n\nNo duplicate clickable owners.\n\n==================================================\n13. APP PICKER NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nPicker may be:\n\nMaterial 3 modal bottom sheet\n\npreferred.\n\nDo not create a new Activity.\n\nBack:\nclose picker.\n\nHome remains underneath.\n\n==================================================\n14. PICKER SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nOptional simple local search:\n\nfilter existing AppCatalog in memory.\n\nNo PackageManager scan per character.\n\nNo network.\n\n==================================================\n15. DUPLICATES\n==================================================\n\nAllow same app in multiple panels unless current Core contract\nexplicitly forbids it.\n\nDo not invent uniqueness restrictions.\n\n==================================================\n16. UNINSTALLED APP\n==================================================\n\nIf assigned app is later uninstalled:\n\nkeep existing Core V2 behavior.\n\nSlot becomes unresolved/empty safely.\n\nDo not automatically replace it.\n\n==================================================\n17. PATCH BOUNDARY\n==================================================\n\nPreferred:\n\npatches/slot_editor/\n    SlotEditorPatch.kt\n\nOne common editor.\n\nMinimal integration bridge into existing AppCell interaction.\n\n==================================================\n18. CORE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nCore slot counts:\nUNCHANGED\n\nAppCatalog owner:\nUNCHANGED\n\nHomeSnapshot owner:\nUNCHANGED\n\nLaunch path:\nUNCHANGED\n\nPATCH 001:\nUNCHANGED\n\nPATCH 002:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n19. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md.\n\nTarget:\n\nnew AppCatalog owners = 0\nnew HomeSnapshot owners = 0\nduplicate slot persistence = 0\nfirst-touch blockers = 0\nmain-thread PackageManager scans = 0\nnew lifecycle owners = 0\n\n==================================================\n20. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 005 APP SLOT EDITOR COMPLETE\n\nEditable P1 slots: <n>\nEditable P2 slots: <n>\nEditable Dock slots: <n>\n\nSlot editor owners: <n>\nApp picker owners: <n>\n\nNew AppCatalog owners: <n>\nNew HomeSnapshot owners: <n>\n\nDuplicate persistence paths: <n>\n\nLong press:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRemove action:\n<YES/NO>\n\nExplicit empty preserved:\n<YES/NO>\n\nAssignments persistent:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1/P2/Dock counts changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nNormal first tap regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nPATCH 001 regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nPATCH 002 regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:316:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787240025,"text":"PATCH 004 V2 — COMPACT TOP-DOWN SETTINGS PANEL\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nReplace current Settings presentation.\n\nSettings must open:\n\nFROM TOP OF DISPLAY\n→ slide downward\n→ compact height\n→ remain attached to top edge\n\nNOT from bottom.\n\n==================================================\n1. PRESENTATION\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT use:\n\nModalBottomSheet\nBottomSheetScaffold\nbottom-sheet motion\n\nUse a custom top-attached Settings panel\nor equivalent Compose layout.\n\nInitial state:\nHIDDEN\n\nOpen:\npanel descends from top edge\n\nClose:\npanel retracts upward\n\n==================================================\n2. SIZE\n==================================================\n\nPanel must be compact.\n\nTarget initial maximum height:\n\n~30–35% of usable display height\n\nDo NOT fill most of screen.\n\nPreferred first test:\n32%\n\nWidth:\nfull available width\nwith normal horizontal margins if current design requires them.\n\n==================================================\n3. TOP ANCHOR\n==================================================\n\nPanel top is anchored to top display safe area.\n\nRespect:\n\nstatus bar inset\ndisplay cutout\n\nInteractive content starts BELOW system status bar.\n\nDo not draw buttons/text underneath clock/battery.\n\n==================================================\n4. MOTION\n==================================================\n\nOpening:\n\ntop edge\n→ short downward reveal\n\nClosing:\n\nreverse upward.\n\nUse one motion owner.\n\nPrefer standard Compose animation.\n\nNo bounce.\nNo overshoot.\nNo large spring.\n\nTarget:\nshort, precise, restrained.\n\n==================================================\n5. HOME\n==================================================\n\nHome remains visible underneath.\n\nDo NOT:\n\nmove Home\nresize Home\nmove Fav\nmove P1/P2\nmove Dock\n\nSettings panel overlays Home.\n\n==================================================\n6. PANEL VISUAL\n==================================================\n\nKeep approved PATCH 004 design:\n\n- legacy icons\n- Dynamic Color\n- system typography\n- network-particle animation\n- functional settings\n\nOnly presentation changes.\n\n==================================================\n7. CONTENT\n==================================================\n\nBecause panel is compact:\n\nshow Settings root compactly.\n\nIf content exceeds panel height:\n\ninternal vertical scroll.\n\nDo NOT increase panel height automatically.\n\n==================================================\n8. CATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nKeep current small category set.\n\nCompact rows.\n\nAvoid large subtitles or excessive whitespace.\n\n==================================================\n9. SUBCATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nOpening a category:\n\nreuse SAME top panel.\n\nReplace its content internally.\n\nDo NOT open:\n\nnew sheet\nnew fullscreen screen\nnested overlay\n\n==================================================\n10. CLOSE\n==================================================\n\nClose by:\n\n- Back from Settings root\n- tap outside panel\n- upward swipe on panel\n\nDo NOT close because of LEFT/RIGHT Home gestures.\n\n==================================================\n11. TOUCH ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nWhile panel is open:\n\ntouches inside panel:\nSettings-owned\n\ntouch outside:\nmay dismiss panel\n\nPATCH 001 Home gestures must not activate through panel.\n\n==================================================\n12. PARTICLES\n==================================================\n\nNetwork particles remain inside panel bounds only.\n\nDo not animate behind entire Home.\n\n==================================================\n13. SCRIM\n==================================================\n\nUse minimal scrim.\n\nVery light/dark subtle overlay only.\n\nDo not heavily darken Home.\n\nNo custom wallpaper dim animation.\n\n==================================================\n14. SETTINGS ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nFav Settings icon:\n\ntap\n→ panel descends from top.\n\nExisting icon unchanged.\n\n==================================================\n15. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nOpen accepted:\nCONFIRM x1\n\nClose:\noptional CONFIRM x1 only if consistent with current policy.\n\nNo haptic during drag/MOVE.\n\n==================================================\n16. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md.\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 002 modified:\nNO\n\nNew persistence:\n0\n\nGesture owners:\n1 panel-specific max\n\n==================================================\n17. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA COMPACT TOP SETTINGS PANEL COMPLETE\n\nPresentation:\n<TOP_DOWN_PANEL/OTHER>\n\nPanel max height:\n<percentage/dp>\n\nStatus bar respected:\n<YES/NO>\n\nOpen from top:\n<YES/NO>\n\nClose upward:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHome movement:\n<dp>\n\nFav movement:\n<dp>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nInternal scroll:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSettings visual changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nParticle background contained in panel:\n<YES/NO>\n\nPATCH 001 regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nPATCH 002 regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:317:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787240503,"text":"PATCH 007 V2 — FIRST RUN USAGE-BASED AUTOFILL\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nSolo durante la prima configurazione di Machina:\n\n1. chiedere facoltativamente Usage Access\n2. leggere l'utilizzo recente delle app\n3. ordinare le app realmente launchable\n4. riempire automaticamente:\n\nDock = top 5\nP1   = next 8\nP2   = next 8\n\n5. salvare gli slot usando la persistence Core già esistente\n6. NON riordinare più automaticamente dopo il primo setup\n\n==================================================\n1. USER CONSENT\n==================================================\n\nFirst Run screen:\n\n\"Organizza automaticamente le app più usate\"\n\nActions:\n\n[Usa app più usate]\n[Salta]\n\nIf user chooses autofill:\n\ncheck Usage Access.\n\nIf unavailable/not granted:\nopen supported Android screen:\n\nSettings.ACTION_USAGE_ACCESS_SETTINGS\n\nDo not force permission.\n\n==================================================\n2. PERMISSION\n==================================================\n\nManifest may declare:\n\nandroid.permission.PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS\n\nbut access still requires explicit user grant.\n\nNo hidden API.\nNo accessibility service.\nNo background surveillance.\n\n==================================================\n3. DATA SOURCE\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nUsageStatsManager.queryAndAggregateUsageStats(...)\n\nor equivalent stable UsageStatsManager API available\nfor current Android target.\n\nTime window:\n\nprefer last 30 days.\n\nIntersect usage packages with EXISTING AppCatalog.\n\nOnly launchable apps already known by Machina\nmay enter Dock/P1/P2.\n\n==================================================\n4. SCORE\n==================================================\n\nKeep scoring simple and deterministic.\n\nUse only stable usage information such as:\n\n- totalTimeInForeground\n- lastTimeUsed\n\nConceptual score:\n\nusageScore =\nforegroundTimeWeight\n+\nrecencyWeight\n\nDo NOT add ML.\n\nDo NOT use cloud processing.\n\nDo NOT upload usage data.\n\n==================================================\n5. RECENCY\n==================================================\n\nRecent use should matter so an app heavily used months ago\ndoes not dominate forever.\n\nUse a bounded recency component based on lastTimeUsed.\n\nDocument exact formula.\n\n==================================================\n6. EXCLUSIONS\n==================================================\n\nExclude:\n\n- Machina itself\n- non-launchable packages\n- unresolved packages\n- duplicate package entries\n- apps with no usable catalog entry\n\nDo not hardcode personal app names.\n\n==================================================\n7. ASSIGNMENT\n==================================================\n\nAfter sorting descending by score:\n\nDock:\nrank 1..5\n\nP1:\nrank 6..13\n\nP2:\nrank 14..21\n\nTotal maximum:\n21 apps.\n\n==================================================\n8. FEWER THAN 21 APPS\n==================================================\n\nIf fewer launchable/used apps exist:\n\nfill available ranks.\n\nRemaining slots:\nexplicit empty.\n\nDo NOT insert random apps.\n\n==================================================\n9. TIES\n==================================================\n\nDeterministic tie break:\n\n1. score\n2. most recent lastTimeUsed\n3. app label alphabetical\n\nSame data must produce same layout.\n\n==================================================\n10. FIRST RUN ONLY\n==================================================\n\nAutofill runs only when:\n\ninitial Home setup has not been completed.\n\nAfter successful initialization:\n\nmark:\nusageAutofillCompleted = true\n\nNever automatically reorder an established Home.\n\n==================================================\n11. EXISTING USER LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nIf any meaningful P1/P2/Dock layout already exists:\n\nDO NOT overwrite automatically.\n\nRequire an explicit user action if re-autofill is ever\nadded later.\n\n==================================================\n12. PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nUse EXISTING Core slot persistence.\n\nDo NOT create another Dock/P1/P2 database.\n\nHomeSnapshot owner remains unchanged.\n\nPATCH 007 calculates assignments;\nCore persistence stores them.\n\n==================================================\n13. NO CONTINUOUS MONITORING\n==================================================\n\nAfter initial fill:\n\nUsageStats polling = 0\n\nBackground services = 0\nWorkManager periodic jobs = 0\nalarms = 0\nWakeLocks = 0\n\nMachina does not continuously profile app usage.\n\n==================================================\n14. PRIVACY\n==================================================\n\nUsage information stays on-device.\n\nNo network requests.\n\nNo telemetry.\n\nNo logs containing detailed usage history in release builds.\n\n==================================================\n15. FALLBACK\n==================================================\n\nIf Usage Access is denied:\n\nFirst Run continues normally.\n\nOptions:\n\n- keep slots empty/default\n- user fills slots manually using PATCH 005\n\nNo blocking setup.\n\n==================================================\n16. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nAccepted autofill action:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nonce.\n\nNo haptic while ranking.\n\n==================================================\n17. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nUsage query:\none-time only.\n\nRun aggregation outside gesture/render hot path.\n\nNo repeated query per slot.\n\nNo PackageManager enumeration duplicate:\nreuse AppCatalog.\n\n==================================================\n18. SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 004 System/Home may later expose:\n\n\"Organizza app più usate\"\n\nbut DO NOT implement automatic periodic sorting.\n\nIf exposed:\nexplicit manual action only.\n\n==================================================\n19. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nnew AppCatalog owners = 0\nnew HomeSnapshot owners = 0\nduplicate slot persistence = 0\ncontinuous monitoring paths = 0\nnetwork paths = 0\nusage-data logging paths = 0\n\n==================================================\n20. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 007 FIRST RUN USAGE AUTOFILL COMPLETE\n\nUsageStats API:\n<value>\n\nUsage Access declaration:\n<YES/NO>\n\nUser grant required:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRanking window:\n<days>\n\nRanking formula:\n<description>\n\nLaunchable catalog reused:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock assigned:\n<n>/5\n\nP1 assigned:\n<n>/8\n\nP2 assigned:\n<n>/8\n\nDeterministic tie-break:\n<YES/NO>\n\nExisting layout overwrite protection:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRuns after first setup:\n<NO/YES>\n\nContinuous monitoring:\n<NO/YES>\n\nNew AppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nNew HomeSnapshot owners:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate persistence:\n<n>\n\nNetwork:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:318:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787241053,"text":"PATCH 007 V2 — FIRST RUN USAGE-BASED AUTOFILL\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nSolo durante la prima configurazione di Machina:\n\n1. chiedere facoltativamente Usage Access\n2. leggere l'utilizzo recente delle app\n3. ordinare le app realmente launchable\n4. riempire automaticamente:\n\nDock = top 5\nP1   = next 8\nP2   = next 8\n\n5. salvare gli slot usando la persistence Core già esistente\n6. NON riordinare più automaticamente dopo il primo setup\n\n==================================================\n1. USER CONSENT\n==================================================\n\nFirst Run screen:\n\n\"Organizza automaticamente le app più usate\"\n\nActions:\n\n[Usa app più usate]\n[Salta]\n\nIf user chooses autofill:\n\ncheck Usage Access.\n\nIf unavailable/not granted:\nopen supported Android screen:\n\nSettings.ACTION_USAGE_ACCESS_SETTINGS\n\nDo not force permission.\n\n==================================================\n2. PERMISSION\n==================================================\n\nManifest may declare:\n\nandroid.permission.PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS\n\nbut access still requires explicit user grant.\n\nNo hidden API.\nNo accessibility service.\nNo background surveillance.\n\n==================================================\n3. DATA SOURCE\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nUsageStatsManager.queryAndAggregateUsageStats(...)\n\nor equivalent stable UsageStatsManager API available\nfor current Android target.\n\nTime window:\n\nprefer last 30 days.\n\nIntersect usage packages with EXISTING AppCatalog.\n\nOnly launchable apps already known by Machina\nmay enter Dock/P1/P2.\n\n==================================================\n4. SCORE\n==================================================\n\nKeep scoring simple and deterministic.\n\nUse only stable usage information such as:\n\n- totalTimeInForeground\n- lastTimeUsed\n\nConceptual score:\n\nusageScore =\nforegroundTimeWeight\n+\nrecencyWeight\n\nDo NOT add ML.\n\nDo NOT use cloud processing.\n\nDo NOT upload usage data.\n\n==================================================\n5. RECENCY\n==================================================\n\nRecent use should matter so an app heavily used months ago\ndoes not dominate forever.\n\nUse a bounded recency component based on lastTimeUsed.\n\nDocument exact formula.\n\n==================================================\n6. EXCLUSIONS\n==================================================\n\nExclude:\n\n- Machina itself\n- non-launchable packages\n- unresolved packages\n- duplicate package entries\n- apps with no usable catalog entry\n\nDo not hardcode personal app names.\n\n==================================================\n7. ASSIGNMENT\n==================================================\n\nAfter sorting descending by score:\n\nDock:\nrank 1..5\n\nP1:\nrank 6..13\n\nP2:\nrank 14..21\n\nTotal maximum:\n21 apps.\n\n==================================================\n8. FEWER THAN 21 APPS\n==================================================\n\nIf fewer launchable/used apps exist:\n\nfill available ranks.\n\nRemaining slots:\nexplicit empty.\n\nDo NOT insert random apps.\n\n==================================================\n9. TIES\n==================================================\n\nDeterministic tie break:\n\n1. score\n2. most recent lastTimeUsed\n3. app label alphabetical\n\nSame data must produce same layout.\n\n==================================================\n10. FIRST RUN ONLY\n==================================================\n\nAutofill runs only when:\n\ninitial Home setup has not been completed.\n\nAfter successful initialization:\n\nmark:\nusageAutofillCompleted = true\n\nNever automatically reorder an established Home.\n\n==================================================\n11. EXISTING USER LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nIf any meaningful P1/P2/Dock layout already exists:\n\nDO NOT overwrite automatically.\n\nRequire an explicit user action if re-autofill is ever\nadded later.\n\n==================================================\n12. PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nUse EXISTING Core slot persistence.\n\nDo NOT create another Dock/P1/P2 database.\n\nHomeSnapshot owner remains unchanged.\n\nPATCH 007 calculates assignments;\nCore persistence stores them.\n\n==================================================\n13. NO CONTINUOUS MONITORING\n==================================================\n\nAfter initial fill:\n\nUsageStats polling = 0\n\nBackground services = 0\nWorkManager periodic jobs = 0\nalarms = 0\nWakeLocks = 0\n\nMachina does not continuously profile app usage.\n\n==================================================\n14. PRIVACY\n==================================================\n\nUsage information stays on-device.\n\nNo network requests.\n\nNo telemetry.\n\nNo logs containing detailed usage history in release builds.\n\n==================================================\n15. FALLBACK\n==================================================\n\nIf Usage Access is denied:\n\nFirst Run continues normally.\n\nOptions:\n\n- keep slots empty/default\n- user fills slots manually using PATCH 005\n\nNo blocking setup.\n\n==================================================\n16. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nAccepted autofill action:\n\nperformHapticFeedback(\n    HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM\n)\n\nonce.\n\nNo haptic while ranking.\n\n==================================================\n17. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nUsage query:\none-time only.\n\nRun aggregation outside gesture/render hot path.\n\nNo repeated query per slot.\n\nNo PackageManager enumeration duplicate:\nreuse AppCatalog.\n\n==================================================\n18. SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 004 System/Home may later expose:\n\n\"Organizza app più usate\"\n\nbut DO NOT implement automatic periodic sorting.\n\nIf exposed:\nexplicit manual action only.\n\n==================================================\n19. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nnew AppCatalog owners = 0\nnew HomeSnapshot owners = 0\nduplicate slot persistence = 0\ncontinuous monitoring paths = 0\nnetwork paths = 0\nusage-data logging paths = 0\n\n==================================================\n20. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 007 FIRST RUN USAGE AUTOFILL COMPLETE\n\nUsageStats API:\n<value>\n\nUsage Access declaration:\n<YES/NO>\n\nUser grant required:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRanking window:\n<days>\n\nRanking formula:\n<description>\n\nLaunchable catalog reused:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock assigned:\n<n>/5\n\nP1 assigned:\n<n>/8\n\nP2 assigned:\n<n>/8\n\nDeterministic tie-break:\n<YES/NO>\n\nExisting layout overwrite protection:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRuns after first setup:\n<NO/YES>\n\nContinuous monitoring:\n<NO/YES>\n\nNew AppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nNew HomeSnapshot owners:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate persistence:\n<n>\n\nNetwork:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:319:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787241165,"text":"PATCH 003 V2 — SEARCH ENGINE + RESULTS + HISTORY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2\n+ PATCH 001 [VALIDATED/FROZEN]\n+ PATCH 002 Search Bar / Reveal\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 002:\nGEOMETRY / GESTURES / IME FROZEN\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nMake the existing PATCH 002 Search fully functional.\n\nPATCH 003 owns ONLY:\n\n- search filtering\n- results\n- result ranking\n- search history\n- result actions\n\nPATCH 002 continues to own:\n\n- Search bar\n- query input\n- SearchSlot\n- UP/DOWN reveal\n- focus\n- keyboard\n- geometry\n\n==================================================\n1. RESULTS POSITION\n==================================================\n\nResults MUST render ABOVE SearchBar.\n\nExact structure:\n\nFav\n\nResultsArea\n\nSearchBar\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nNever render results below SearchBar.\n\n==================================================\n2. QUERY SOURCE\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 003 consumes PATCH 002 query.\n\nDo NOT create another editable query owner.\n\nQuery owners:\n1 total.\n\nPATCH 002 remains source of truth.\n\n==================================================\n3. APP SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nSearch installed launchable apps using EXISTING AppCatalog.\n\nNo new AppCatalog.\n\nNo PackageManager enumeration while typing.\n\nMatch:\n\n1. exact label\n2. label starts with query\n3. label contains query\n\nCase-insensitive.\n\n==================================================\n4. RESULTS\n==================================================\n\nShow compact app results.\n\nEach row:\n\nexisting Machina app icon\napp label\n\nOptional:\nshort secondary information only if useful.\n\nNo cards.\nNo heavy borders.\n\n==================================================\n5. RESULT LIMIT\n==================================================\n\nInitially show max:\n\n5 results\n\nResultsArea scrolls internally if required.\n\nP1/P2/Dock:\n0dp movement.\n\n==================================================\n6. ICONS\n==================================================\n\nUse the SAME icon resolver as Home.\n\nNo second icon cache.\n\nNo original-icon regression.\n\n==================================================\n7. APP ACTION\n==================================================\n\nTap result:\n\n1. save confirmed query to history\n2. perform accepted-command haptic\n3. launch using existing LauncherActions\n4. clear/hide Search according to existing PATCH 002 contract\n\nOne tap:\none launch.\n\n==================================================\n8. HISTORY\n==================================================\n\nHistory max:\n\n3\n\nStorage:\n\nMEMORY_ONLY\n\nNo:\nDataStore\nSharedPreferences\nRoom\nfile\n\nHistory intentionally lives only while Android keeps\nthe Machina process alive.\n\n==================================================\n9. HISTORY UPDATE\n==================================================\n\nStore only confirmed searches.\n\nDo NOT store every typed character.\n\nConfirmed means:\n\n- app result selected\n- IME search submitted\n- future web/settings result selected\n\n==================================================\n10. HISTORY ORDER\n==================================================\n\nMost recent first.\n\nDeduplicate.\n\nExample:\n\ncamera\nchat\ncamera\n\nbecomes:\n\ncamera\nchat\n\nwith camera moved to first position.\n\n==================================================\n11. EMPTY QUERY\n==================================================\n\nWhen Search is open and query is empty:\n\nshow History above SearchBar.\n\nMaximum:\n3 rows.\n\nIf history empty:\nResultsArea remains visually empty.\n\nDo NOT show random apps.\n\n==================================================\n12. HISTORY ROW\n==================================================\n\nCompact:\n\nhistory icon\nquery text\n\nTap:\n\nset PATCH 002 query to selected history value\nkeep Search focused\nupdate results immediately\n\nDo NOT launch automatically from history tap.\n\n==================================================\n13. LIVE SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nWhile typing:\n\nfilter existing in-memory catalog immediately.\n\nNo network.\nNo disk.\nNo PackageManager scan.\n\nFor current catalog size:\nno debounce unless measurement proves necessary.\n\n==================================================\n14. IME SEARCH ACTION\n==================================================\n\nKeyboard Search/Done action:\n\ntrim query.\n\nIf non-empty:\nadd query to history.\n\nIf there is an exact/obvious single app result:\nDO NOT auto-launch unless explicitly designed.\n\nPreferred:\nkeep results visible.\n\n==================================================\n15. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nUse existing global Machina haptic policy.\n\nIf hapticEnabled:\n\nresult selected:\nperformHapticFeedback(CONFIRM)\n\nhistory selected:\nperformHapticFeedback(CONFIRM)\n\nIME confirmed:\nCONFIRM once\n\nTyping:\n0\n\nScrolling:\n0\n\nResult appearance:\n0\n\n==================================================\n16. SEARCH HISTORY CACHE POLICY\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nHistory is process-memory state.\n\nIf Android keeps Machina process cached:\nhistory survives naturally.\n\nIf Android kills process:\nhistory = empty.\n\nThis is intentional.\n\nDo NOT add process keep-alive.\n\n==================================================\n17. PROCESS SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nNo:\n\nService\nWakeLock\nWorkManager\nalarm\npolling\nprocess priority manipulation\n\nSearch correctness must not depend on process survival.\n\n==================================================\n18. SEARCH RESULTS + USAGE AUTOFILL\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 007 usage ranking must NOT affect Search ranking.\n\nSearch ranking remains deterministic text matching.\n\nUsageStats must not be queried while searching.\n\nNo coupling between Search and first-run autofill.\n\n==================================================\n19. OPTIONAL SYSTEM SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nIf desired and already safely implemented:\n\nsupport a small curated set:\n\nWi-Fi\nBluetooth\nDisplay\nBattery\nApps\nAccessibility\nPrivacy/Security\n\nOnly documented Android Settings intents.\n\nThese results also appear ABOVE SearchBar.\n\nDo not implement hidden APIs.\n\n==================================================\n20. OPTIONAL WEB ACTION\n==================================================\n\nFor non-empty query optionally show:\n\nSearch web for \"<query>\"\n\nUse external browser ACTION_VIEW.\n\nNo WebView.\nNo network request from Machina.\n\n==================================================\n21. RESULT TYPE ORDER\n==================================================\n\nPreferred:\n\nApp exact matches\nApp prefix matches\nApp contains matches\nSystem Settings matches\nWeb action\n\nKeep ranking simple.\n\n==================================================\n22. PATCH 002 HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT change:\n\nSearchSlot dimensions\nFav → Search spacing\nSearchBar → P1 spacing\nUP/DOWN gesture behavior\nIME geometry handling\nLEFT/RIGHT arbitration\n\nPATCH 003 only fills ResultsArea.\n\n==================================================\n23. PATCH 001 HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nLEFT Material Stretch:\nUNCHANGED\n\nRIGHT Material Stretch:\nUNCHANGED\n\nNo edge Back arrow regression.\n\n==================================================\n24. FIRST TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nResult:\nfirst tap works.\n\nP1:\nfirst tap works.\n\nP2:\nfirst tap works.\n\nDock:\nfirst tap works.\n\nResults list must not intercept touches outside ResultsArea.\n\n==================================================\n25. ERROR SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nApp removed between result generation and tap:\nsafe failure.\n\nActivityNotFoundException:\nsafe.\n\nSecurityException:\nsafe.\n\nNo Search failure crashes Home.\n\n==================================================\n26. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nPer query:\n\nPackageManager calls = 0\ndisk IO = 0\nnetwork = 0\nUsageStats queries = 0\nbitmap decode = 0\n\nUse existing catalog/icon state.\n\n==================================================\n27. STATE OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 002:\nquery owner = 1\n\nPATCH 003:\nhistory owner = 1\nderived results owner/state = max 1 if required\n\nNew query owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n28. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nNew AppCatalog owners = 0\nNew HomeSnapshot owners = 0\nPersistence writes = 0\nGesture owners added = 0\nBackHandlers added = 0\nLifecycle owners added = 0\nFirst-touch blockers = 0\n\n==================================================\n29. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nRemoving PATCH 003:\n\nSearchBar/reveal from PATCH 002 still works.\n\nOnly:\n\nresults\nhistory\nsearch actions\n\ndisappear.\n\nCore/PATCH001/PATCH002 remain valid.\n\n==================================================\n30. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 003 SEARCH ENGINE COMPLETE\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 geometry modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nQuery owners:\n<n>\n\nHistory owners:\n<n>\n\nHistory max:\n<n>\n\nHistory storage:\n<MEMORY_ONLY/OTHER>\n\nApp search:\n<YES/NO>\n\nResults above SearchBar:\n<YES/NO>\n\nMax visible results:\n<n>\n\nNew AppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nPackageManager calls while typing:\n<n>\n\nUsageStats calls while typing:\n<n>\n\nIcon resolver:\n<SHARED/OTHER>\n\nSystem Settings results:\n<YES/NO>\n\nWeb action:\n<YES/NO>\n\nGesture owners added:\n<n>\n\nBackHandlers added:\n<n>\n\nPersistence writes:\n<n>\n\nTyping haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nPATCH 001 regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nPATCH 002 geometry regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:320:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787241687,"text":"PATCH 004 V2 — TEMPORARY DEVELOPMENT STATUS SUMMARY\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\ncurrent PATCH 004 Settings\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAdd one temporary developer-facing summary page inside Settings.\n\nThis page is for development only.\n\nAt final release it must be easy to:\n- hide\nor\n- remove completely\n\nDO NOT modify:\n- Core behavior\n- PATCH 001\n- PATCH 002\n- Settings visual language\n- functional Settings behavior\n\n==================================================\n1. SETTINGS ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nAdd one temporary row under About:\n\nDevelopment status\n\nIcon:\nsmall existing legacy/info/developer-style icon\n\nSubtitle:\nCurrent Core / Patch state\n\nThis row must follow the existing approved Settings visual style.\n\n==================================================\n2. DEVELOPMENT STATUS PAGE\n==================================================\n\nShow a compact summary:\n\nCORE V2\nStatus: FROZEN\n\nPATCH 001\nSensitive Home Interaction\nStatus: VALIDATED / FROZEN\n\nPATCH 002\nFav Reveal + Search Bar UI\nStatus: IMPLEMENTED / VALIDATION REQUIRED\n\nPATCH 003\nSearch Engine + Results + History\nStatus: PLANNED\n\nPATCH 004\nSettings\nStatus: IMPLEMENTED / VALIDATION REQUIRED\n\nPATCH 005\nApp Slot Editor\nStatus: IMPLEMENTED / VALIDATION REQUIRED\n\nPATCH 006\nOverlay / Panel Presentation Cleanup\nStatus: PLANNED / PARTIAL\n\nPATCH 007\nFirst Run Usage Autofill\nStatus: PLANNED\n\n==================================================\n3. VISUAL STYLE\n==================================================\n\nKeep compact.\n\nEach item:\n\npatch number\nshort name\nstatus\n\nNo large cards.\n\nPrefer:\n\nsmall status indicator\ntitle\none-line subtitle\n\nUse existing legacy Settings icons/tokens.\n\n==================================================\n4. STATUS VISUALS\n==================================================\n\nUse Dynamic Color / Material tokens.\n\nSuggested semantic mapping:\n\nVALIDATED / FROZEN\n-> primary / positive-looking token\n\nVALIDATION REQUIRED\n-> tertiary / warning-neutral token\n\nPLANNED\n-> onSurfaceVariant\n\nREJECTED\n-> error\n\nDo not hardcode neon colors.\n\n==================================================\n5. NO RUNTIME INTROSPECTION\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT scan source files at runtime.\n\nDo NOT parse docs/checkpoints at runtime.\n\nUse one small PATCH 004 development metadata structure.\n\nExample concept:\n\nPatchStatus(\n    id,\n    name,\n    state\n)\n\n==================================================\n6. SOURCE OF TRUTH\n==================================================\n\nKeep the metadata in one PATCH 004 development-only file/object.\n\nNo duplicated status strings across screens.\n\n==================================================\n7. RELEASE FLAG\n==================================================\n\nAdd one simple build/config flag:\n\nSHOW_DEVELOPMENT_STATUS\n\nDevelopment:\ntrue\n\nFinal public release:\nfalse\n\nWhen false:\n\n- Development status row hidden\n- Development status page unreachable\n- no visual gap remains\n\n==================================================\n8. PREFERRED BUILD BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nPrefer compile-time/build configuration if already available.\n\nDo not add a complex feature-flag framework.\n\nIf BuildConfig is suitable:\n\nSHOW_DEVELOPMENT_STATUS = true\n\nor equivalent minimal implementation.\n\n==================================================\n9. RELEASE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nDevelopment status must never expose:\n\nfilesystem paths\nprivate keys\nSHA hashes\ninternal usernames\ndevice identifiers\ndebug logs\nsecrets\n\nOnly show:\n\nCore/Patch number\nhuman-readable name\nstatus\n\n==================================================\n10. NO PATCH BEHAVIOR CONTROL\n==================================================\n\nThis page is READ-ONLY.\n\nDo NOT allow:\n\nenable patch\ndisable patch\nrollback patch\nedit status\nrun build\nrun checkpoint\n\nIt is only a summary.\n\n==================================================\n11. ABOUT PAGE\n==================================================\n\nSuggested order:\n\nVersion\nChangelog\nDevelopment status\n\nKeep Licenses if already present.\n\n==================================================\n12. OPTIONAL COUNTS\n==================================================\n\nAt top of Development status page show:\n\nValidated: <n>\nValidation required: <n>\nPlanned: <n>\n\nCompute from the local metadata list.\n\n==================================================\n13. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nNew persistence:\n0\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nNew lifecycle owners:\n0\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n14. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA TEMP DEVELOPMENT STATUS SETTINGS COMPLETE\n\nDevelopment status row:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDevelopment status page:\n<YES/NO>\n\nPatch entries:\n<n>\n\nValidated count:\n<n>\n\nValidation-required count:\n<n>\n\nPlanned count:\n<n>\n\nRuntime source scanning:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSensitive/internal paths exposed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nRelease hide flag:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSettings visual changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:321:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787241933,"text":"PATCH 002 + PATCH 004 — SEARCH SPACE INCREASE + PARTICLE BACKGROUND REUSE\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2\n+ PATCH 001 [VALIDATED/FROZEN]\n+ current PATCH 002 Search UI\n+ current PATCH 004 Settings with animated network particles\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nFROZEN\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\n1. Increase vertical Search area by moving Fav further upward\n   ONLY in PATCH 002 expanded state.\n\n2. Keep P1/P2/Dock fixed.\n\n3. Reuse the existing animated network-particles background\n   from PATCH 004 inside the expanded Search area.\n\nDO NOT modify PATCH 001.\n\n==================================================\n1. EXPANDED FAV POSITION\n==================================================\n\nCurrent expanded Fav position is still too low.\n\nRaise Fav further upward in EXPANDED state.\n\nStarting target:\n\nadditional lift from current expanded position:\n~24dp\n\nAllowed test range:\n20–32dp\n\nDo NOT change collapsed Fav position.\n\n==================================================\n2. FIXED ELEMENTS\n==================================================\n\nP1 movement:\n0dp\n\nP2 movement:\n0dp\n\nDock movement:\n0dp\n\nSearch area increase must come from Fav moving upward,\nnot from shifting P1/P2/Dock.\n\n==================================================\n3. SEARCH AREA\n==================================================\n\nExpanded Search area must become large enough for:\n\n- results area\n- search bar\n- comfortable spacing\n\nTarget layout:\n\nFav\n\n[ animated results/background area ]\n\n[ results ]\n\n🔍 query________________\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\n==================================================\n4. SEARCH AREA HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nIncrease SearchSlot based on real measured space.\n\nDo not hardcode absolute screen coordinates.\n\nExpanded SearchSlot should use:\n\nP1.top\n- Fav.bottom\n- approved gaps\n\nNo overlap.\n\n==================================================\n5. FAV REAL LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nFav must remain inside valid Home/container bounds.\n\nDo NOT use:\n\ngraphicsLayer.translationY\nvisual-only translation\nstale hitbox offset\n\nUse real layout positioning.\n\nFav touch bounds must follow visual bounds.\n\n==================================================\n6. COLLAPSED STATE\n==================================================\n\nCollapsed:\n\nFav returns exactly to baseline position.\n\nSearchSlot:\n0dp or approved minimal footprint.\n\nNo empty reserved space.\n\n==================================================\n7. PARTICLE BACKGROUND REUSE\n==================================================\n\nReuse the existing PATCH 004 animated network-particles implementation.\n\nDO NOT duplicate the algorithm.\n\nExtract/reuse one shared visual component if necessary:\n\nAnimatedParticleNetwork(...)\n\nor equivalent.\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH PARTICLE SCOPE\n==================================================\n\nParticles appear ONLY when Search is expanded.\n\nDraw them only inside SearchSlot/ResultsArea.\n\nDo NOT apply particles to:\n\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\nfull Home background\n\n==================================================\n9. PARTICLE VISUAL\n==================================================\n\nUse same animation language as Settings:\n\n- small moving dots\n- thin dynamic connection lines\n- Dynamic Color aware\n- bounded particle count\n- one animation loop\n- no wallpaper bitmap\n\nFor Search:\nslightly lower intensity than Settings preferred.\n\nSuggested:\n\nparticle alpha:\n~0.30–0.36\n\nline max alpha:\n~0.14–0.18\n\n==================================================\n10. PARTICLE LAYER ORDER\n==================================================\n\nSearchSlot background\n→ AnimatedParticleNetwork\n→ Search results\n→ Search bar\n\nParticles must remain behind text/icons/input.\n\n==================================================\n11. PARTICLE TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nParticle layer:\n\npointerInput = 0\nclickable = 0\ngesture owners = 0\n\nMust never block Search or Home input.\n\n==================================================\n12. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nReuse one bounded particle model.\n\nNo:\n\ncoroutine per particle\nAnimatable per particle\nbitmap decode\nnetwork\ndisk IO\n\nAnimation runs only while Search expanded.\n\n==================================================\n13. PATCH 004 SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nSettings particle animation:\nUNCHANGED visually.\n\nIf extracting shared component:\n\nPATCH 004 must continue using same behavior.\n\nNo Settings regression.\n\n==================================================\n14. PATCH 002 VERTICAL BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nKeep existing UP/DOWN gesture owner.\n\nUP:\nexpand\nraise Fav\nshow Search\nshow particles\n\nDOWN:\nhide keyboard\nhide Search\nstop particle animation\nreturn Fav baseline\n\nNo new gesture owner.\n\n==================================================\n15. LEFT / RIGHT\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 001 remains sole owner.\n\nLEFT:\nMaterial Stretch unchanged\n\nRIGHT:\nMaterial Stretch unchanged\n\nPATCH 002 state writes on horizontal gesture:\n0\n\n==================================================\n16. IME\n==================================================\n\nKeep current IME fix.\n\nKeyboard must not alter:\n\nFav expanded position\nSearchSlot height\nP1/P2/Dock positions\n\n==================================================\n17. SEARCH RESULTS\n==================================================\n\nIf PATCH 003 is not yet active:\n\nResultsArea may stay empty over animated background.\n\nDo NOT invent fake results.\n\nIf PATCH 003 is active:\nresults render above SearchBar and above particle Canvas.\n\n==================================================\n18. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nPATCH 001 modified = 0\nCore modified = 0\n\nNew gesture owners = 0\nNew persistence = 0\nHomeSnapshot writes = 0\n\nDuplicate particle animation owners = 0 preferred\nShared particle visual owner = 1 preferred\n\n==================================================\n19. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA SEARCH SPACE + PARTICLE BACKGROUND UPDATE COMPLETE\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nFav additional expanded lift:\n<dp>\n\nFav collapsed position changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nExpanded SearchSlot height:\n<dp>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nSearch overlap P1:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nParticle component reused:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDuplicate particle engines:\n<n>\n\nSearch particle alpha:\n<value>\n\nSearch line alpha:\n<value>\n\nParticle gesture owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings particle regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nLEFT/RIGHT regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nIME regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:322:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787242447,"text":"PATCH 002/004 FIX — SEARCH PARTICLE NETWORK FULL SLOT + VISIBILITY + SPEED\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nCore V2\n+ PATCH 001 [VALIDATED/FROZEN]\n+ current PATCH 002 Search UI\n+ current shared network-particles component from PATCH 004\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nImprove ONLY the animated particle network used inside\nthe expanded Search area.\n\nCURRENT DEVICE ISSUES:\n\n1. connection lines are barely visible\n2. particle motion feels too slow\n3. animation does not visually fill the full area between Fav and P1\n\nDO NOT modify:\n\n- PATCH 001\n- Search gesture ownership\n- Search bar design\n- P1/P2/Dock positions\n- Core\n- Search engine logic\n\n==================================================\n1. FULL SEARCH SLOT COVERAGE\n==================================================\n\nAnimatedParticleNetwork must fill the ENTIRE expanded area:\n\nfrom:\n\nFav.bottom + approved gap\n\nto:\n\nP1.top - approved gap\n\nWidth:\nfull SearchSlot width.\n\nNo small centered Canvas.\nNo fixed-height particle sub-area.\n\nUse:\n\nModifier.fillMaxSize()\n\ninside the real SearchSlot/ResultsArea bounds\nor equivalent constraint-driven sizing.\n\n==================================================\n2. SEARCH SLOT AS AUTHORITATIVE BOUNDS\n==================================================\n\nCanvas bounds must derive from actual SearchSlot.\n\nDo NOT use:\n\nfixed 96dp canvas\nfixed particle area height\nscreen-coordinate magic values\n\nReport:\n\nSearchSlot height\nCanvas height\n\nRequired:\n\nCanvas height == SearchSlot usable visual height\n\n==================================================\n3. RESULTS / SEARCH BAR LAYERING\n==================================================\n\nLayer order:\n\nSearchSlot base\n→ Particle Canvas FULL SLOT\n→ ResultsArea\n→ SearchBar\n\nParticle network may animate behind both ResultsArea\nand SearchBar if readability remains good.\n\nDo not clip it to only the result rows.\n\n==================================================\n4. LINE VISIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nCurrent lines are too faint.\n\nIncrease line max alpha.\n\nStarting target:\n\nline max alpha:\n0.26\n\nAllowed test range:\n0.22–0.30\n\nDistance fade:\nKEEP\n\nAt connection threshold:\nalpha approaches 0.\n\nAt short distance:\nline should be clearly visible but still background-level.\n\n==================================================\n5. LINE WIDTH\n==================================================\n\nIf current stroke is extremely thin:\n\ntarget:\n~0.8dp–1.0dp\n\nDo not exceed 1dp baseline.\n\nNo glow.\nNo shadow.\n\n==================================================\n6. PARTICLE VISIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nKeep particles slightly stronger than lines.\n\nTarget:\n\nparticle alpha:\n0.44–0.50\n\nPreferred:\n0.46\n\nParticle diameter:\nkeep current unless below ~2dp.\n\nPreferred:\n2.5–3dp\n\n==================================================\n7. MOTION SPEED\n==================================================\n\nCurrent movement is too slow.\n\nIncrease velocity moderately.\n\nTarget:\n\n~12–20dp/sec\n\nPreferred first test:\n~16dp/sec average visual speed\n\nDo NOT make them dart around.\n\nMovement should remain:\nsmooth\ncontinuous\ncalm\nclearly animated\n\n==================================================\n8. VELOCITY VARIATION\n==================================================\n\nDo not give every particle identical speed/direction.\n\nUse a small bounded variation.\n\nExample conceptual range:\n\n0.75x .. 1.25x base speed\n\nStable per-particle velocity during session.\n\nNo random velocity reset every frame.\n\n==================================================\n9. CONNECTION DENSITY\n==================================================\n\nEnsure enough visible connections.\n\nIf threshold is currently too small:\n\nincrease moderately.\n\nTarget:\neach particle typically has a few nearby connections,\nnot zero and not a dense complete graph.\n\nKeep particle count bounded.\n\n==================================================\n10. PARTICLE COUNT\n==================================================\n\nIf full SearchSlot looks too empty:\n\nincrease only slightly.\n\nPreferred:\n16–20 particles\n\nHard max:\n24\n\nDo not solve visibility with huge particle counts.\n\n==================================================\n11. EDGE COVERAGE\n==================================================\n\nParticles should use the full slot:\n\ntop\nmiddle\nbottom\nleft\nright\n\nDo not initialize all points near center.\n\nInitial positions:\ndistributed across entire Canvas.\n\n==================================================\n12. EDGE BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nKeep particles inside bounds.\n\nSoft velocity reversal at edges preferred.\n\nNo visible teleport.\n\n==================================================\n13. DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nKeep Dynamic Color-derived colors.\n\nBut choose tokens with sufficient contrast.\n\nPreferred:\n\nparticles:\nprimary or onSurface\n\nlines:\nonSurfaceVariant / primary\n\nwith explicit low alpha.\n\nDo not use outlineVariant if it becomes too faint on device.\n\n==================================================\n14. READABILITY\n==================================================\n\nSearch text/results must remain dominant.\n\nIf network becomes too strong:\n\nfirst reduce line alpha slightly.\n\nDo NOT add opaque backgrounds over the whole SearchSlot.\n\n==================================================\n15. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nOne shared Canvas animation owner.\n\nNo per-particle coroutine.\nNo per-particle Animatable.\n\nParticle count <= 24.\n\nNo disk/network/bitmap work during animation.\n\n==================================================\n16. SETTINGS REUSE\n==================================================\n\nIf shared component is used by Settings too:\n\nsupport presentation parameters:\n\nparticleAlpha\nlineAlpha\nspeed\nparticleCount\n\nSearch may use a slightly stronger/faster preset.\n\nDo NOT fork/copy the animation implementation.\n\nOne shared network engine.\n\n==================================================\n17. SEARCH PRESET\n==================================================\n\nPreferred Search preset:\n\nparticleCount:\n18\n\nparticleAlpha:\n0.46\n\nlineMaxAlpha:\n0.26\n\nlineWidth:\n~0.9dp\n\naverageSpeed:\n~16dp/sec\n\n==================================================\n18. SETTINGS PRESET\n==================================================\n\nKeep Settings visually close to current approved version.\n\nDo not automatically apply Search's stronger values\nto Settings unless explicitly parameterized.\n\n==================================================\n19. GEOMETRY LOCK\n==================================================\n\nFav position:\ncurrent approved expanded position\n\nP1 movement:\n0dp\n\nP2 movement:\n0dp\n\nDock movement:\n0dp\n\nSearchSlot geometry:\nUNCHANGED except Canvas now fills it correctly.\n\n==================================================\n20. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nNew persistence:\n0\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\nNO\n\nDuplicate particle engines:\n0 preferred\n\n==================================================\n21. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA SEARCH PARTICLE NETWORK TUNED\n\nSearchSlot height:\n<dp>\n\nParticle Canvas height:\n<dp>\n\nCanvas fills SearchSlot:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticle count:\n<n>\n\nParticle alpha:\n<value>\n\nLine max alpha:\n<value>\n\nLine width:\n<dp>\n\nAverage particle speed:\n<value>\n\nConnection threshold:\n<value>\n\nDynamic connections visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSettings particle behavior changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:323:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787243069,"text":"PATCH 000 — PATCH REORGANIZATION / BASELINE NORMALIZATION\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/Machina\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nMODE:\nSTRUCTURAL REORGANIZATION\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\n==================================================\n0. HARD BACKUP GATE\n==================================================\n\nBEFORE ANY SOURCE MODIFICATION:\n\nVerify a checkpoint exists with label:\n\nbefore-patch-reorganization\n\nIf it does NOT exist:\nSTOP.\n\nRecord exact checkpoint path.\n\nThis checkpoint is the rollback source of truth.\n\n==================================================\n1. OBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nReorganize the current Machina patch layer into clear,\nsingle-responsibility patches.\n\nDO NOT change runtime behavior.\n\nDO NOT redesign UI.\n\nDO NOT retune motion.\n\nDO NOT change slot contents.\n\nDO NOT add new features.\n\nThis phase only:\n\n- separates existing responsibilities\n- renames/restructures patch files where necessary\n- removes confirmed duplicate ownership\n- updates patch documentation/status\n- preserves current device-visible behavior\n\n==================================================\n2. CORE\n==================================================\n\nCore V2:\nFROZEN\n\nDo NOT modify Core logic.\n\nHomeSnapshot:\nUNCHANGED\n\nAppCatalog:\nUNCHANGED\n\nLauncherPreferences:\nUNCHANGED\n\nLauncherActions:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP1 = 8\nP2 = 8\nDock = 5\n\n==================================================\n3. FINAL PATCH MAP\n==================================================\n\nNormalize project toward this structure:\n\nPATCH 001\nSensitive Home Interaction\n\nPATCH 002\nSearch Container Reveal\n\nPATCH 003\nSearch Engine\n\nPATCH 004\nSearch Network Animation\n\nPATCH 005\nSettings Visual\n\nPATCH 006\nSettings Functionality\n\nPATCH 007\nApp Slot Editor\n\nPATCH 008\nFirst Install Autofill\n\n==================================================\n4. PATCH 001 — SENSITIVE HOME INTERACTION\n==================================================\n\nOwns ONLY:\n\n- LEFT Material Stretch\n- RIGHT Material Stretch\n- system Back edge exclusion on Home\n- base gesture arbitration\n- approved interaction haptic infrastructure\n\nStatus:\n\nVALIDATED / FROZEN\n\nDo NOT modify its behavior.\n\n==================================================\n5. PATCH 002 — SEARCH CONTAINER REVEAL\n==================================================\n\nOwns ONLY:\n\n- UP reveal\n- DOWN collapse\n- SearchSlot geometry\n- Fav expanded position\n- Search bar shell\n- focus / IME reveal behavior\n\nMust NOT own:\n\n- search algorithm\n- results\n- history\n- particle animation\n- Settings\n\n==================================================\n6. PATCH 003 — SEARCH ENGINE\n==================================================\n\nOwns ONLY:\n\n- query processing\n- app filtering\n- ranking\n- results\n- history MEMORY_ONLY\n- system setting search actions\n- optional web action\n\nMust NOT own:\n\n- SearchSlot geometry\n- UP/DOWN gesture\n- particle drawing\n- IME layout\n\nIf not implemented:\nmark PLANNED.\n\nDo not implement it during PATCH 000.\n\n==================================================\n7. PATCH 004 — SEARCH NETWORK ANIMATION\n==================================================\n\nOwns ONLY:\n\n- animated particle Canvas inside Search area\n- moving dots\n- dynamic connection lines\n- animation parameters\n\nNo touch.\nNo query.\nNo geometry ownership.\n\nIf currently embedded in another patch:\nextract structurally WITHOUT changing appearance.\n\n==================================================\n8. PATCH 005 — SETTINGS VISUAL\n==================================================\n\nOwns ONLY:\n\n- approved legacy Settings appearance\n- legacy icons\n- typography/layout\n- Dynamic Color presentation\n- top-down Settings panel\n- Settings particle visual background\n\nNo actual preference/backend logic.\n\n==================================================\n9. PATCH 006 — SETTINGS FUNCTIONALITY\n==================================================\n\nOwns ONLY real Settings functionality:\n\n- preference owner\n- switches\n- haptic enabled\n- Dynamic Color enabled\n- icon shape\n- Search auto-keyboard\n- Set default Home\n- App info\n- Version\n- Changelog\n- temporary Development Status\n\nNo Settings visual redesign.\n\n==================================================\n10. PATCH 007 — APP SLOT EDITOR\n==================================================\n\nOwns ONLY:\n\n- long press slot editing\n- App Picker\n- assign/remove P1/P2/Dock apps\n\nMust reuse:\n\nAppCatalog\nCore slot persistence\nexisting icon resolver\n\nNo duplicate slot storage.\n\n==================================================\n11. PATCH 008 — FIRST INSTALL AUTOFILL\n==================================================\n\nOwns ONLY first-install initialization.\n\nDock semantic slots:\n\n0 = default Phone\n1 = default Messages/SMS\n2 = default Browser\n3 = default Music\n4 = default Mail/Email\n\nP1:\ntop 8 usage-ranked apps excluding Dock apps\n\nP2:\nnext 8 usage-ranked apps excluding Dock apps\n\nIf not implemented:\nmark PLANNED.\n\nDo NOT implement during PATCH 000.\n\n==================================================\n12. IMPORTANT — NO FEATURE DEVELOPMENT\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 000 must NOT add missing behavior.\n\nIf a target patch does not yet exist:\n\ncreate documentation/status entry only.\n\nDo not write speculative runtime code.\n\n==================================================\n13. FILE STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nPreferred:\n\npatches/\n  sensitive_home/\n  search_reveal/\n  search_engine/\n  search_animation/\n  settings_visual/\n  settings_functional/\n  slot_editor/\n  first_install/\n\nDo not force one file per directory if existing code\nwould become less clear.\n\nClarity > artificial file count.\n\n==================================================\n14. OWNERSHIP AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nFor every runtime capability identify exactly one owner:\n\nLEFT/RIGHT gesture\nUP/DOWN gesture\nSearch geometry\nquery state\nSearch results\nSearch history\nSearch particle animation\nSettings navigation\nSettings visual\nSettings preferences\nslot editor\nslot persistence\nfirst-install autofill\nhaptic preference\n\nReport duplicates before removing them.\n\n==================================================\n15. REMOVE DUPLICATES\n==================================================\n\nRemove only CONFIRMED duplicate/dead paths.\n\nExamples:\n\n- second query owner\n- duplicate particle engine\n- duplicate haptic state\n- duplicate Settings preference storage\n- obsolete Search geometry path\n- abandoned gesture handler\n\nIf uncertain:\nKEEP and report.\n\n==================================================\n16. PATCH DEPENDENCIES\n==================================================\n\nDocument dependencies explicitly.\n\nPreferred:\n\n001 -> Core\n\n002 -> Core + 001 interaction boundary\n\n003 -> 002 + Core AppCatalog/LauncherActions\n\n004 -> 002 visual slot\n\n005 -> Core Home entry only\n\n006 -> 005 + minimal shared preference API\n\n007 -> Core AppCatalog + Core persistence\n\n008 -> Core AppCatalog + Core persistence + UsageStats\n\nNo circular dependency.\n\n==================================================\n17. PATCH STATUS\n==================================================\n\nUpdate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/PATCH_STATUS.md\n\nAllowed states:\n\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\nIMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\nPLANNED\nREJECTED\n\nDo not guess statuses.\n\nUse evidence from current code/docs/checkpoints.\n\n==================================================\n18. DEVELOPMENT STATUS SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nUpdate temporary Settings Development Status page\nto use the normalized numbering.\n\nKeep read-only.\n\nDo not expose filesystem paths/checkpoint hashes to user UI.\n\n==================================================\n19. HISTORICAL DOCS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT delete old patch documentation.\n\nMove/mark superseded documents if necessary.\n\nHistorical rejected experiments remain traceable.\n\n==================================================\n20. RUNTIME PARITY\n==================================================\n\nBefore/after expected visible behavior must be identical.\n\nRequired:\n\nHome geometry:\nUNCHANGED\n\nLEFT/RIGHT behavior:\nUNCHANGED\n\nSearch reveal:\nUNCHANGED\n\nSearch UI:\nUNCHANGED\n\nSettings visual:\nUNCHANGED\n\nParticles:\nUNCHANGED\n\nApp Picker:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP1/P2/Dock contents:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n21. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nCore writes added = 0\nHomeSnapshot owners = 1\nAppCatalog owners = 1\nslot persistence owners = 1\n\nduplicate gesture owners = 0\nduplicate query owners = 0\nduplicate particle engines = 0\nduplicate Settings preference owners = 0\n\nnew lifecycle owners = 0 preferred\n\n==================================================\n22. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nAfter reorganization:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 release = SUCCESS\nSnapshot validation = PASS\nSHA-256 validation = PASS\n\n==================================================\n23. POST-REORGANIZATION CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nOnly if:\n\nruntime parity PASS\ncode-security PASS\nDebug PASS\nR8 PASS\nsnapshot/hash PASS\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint patch-layout-normalized\n\n==================================================\n24. ROLLBACK TEST\n==================================================\n\nDocument:\n\nPRE checkpoint:\nbefore-patch-reorganization\n\nPOST checkpoint:\npatch-layout-normalized\n\nIf regression appears on device:\n\nrollback source =\nPRE checkpoint\n\n==================================================\n25. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nPATCH_000_REORGANIZATION.md\n\nInclude:\n\n- pre-checkpoint\n- old patch map\n- normalized patch map\n- files moved\n- files renamed\n- ownership changes\n- duplicate paths removed\n- dependencies\n- runtime parity\n- rollback procedure\n- final build/checkpoint\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 000 REORGANIZATION COMPLETE\n\nPre-backup checkpoint:\n<path>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nRuntime behavior intentionally changed:\nNO\n\nPatch map:\n\n001: <name/status>\n002: <name/status>\n003: <name/status>\n004: <name/status>\n005: <name/status>\n006: <name/status>\n007: <name/status>\n008: <name/status>\n\nFiles moved:\n<n>\n\nFiles renamed:\n<n>\n\nConfirmed duplicate paths removed:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot owners:\n<n>\n\nAppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nSlot persistence owners:\n<n>\n\nGesture ownership conflicts:\n<n>\n\nQuery ownership conflicts:\n<n>\n\nParticle engine duplicates:\n<n>\n\nSettings preference owner duplicates:\n<n>\n\nCircular patch dependencies:\n<n>\n\nRuntime parity:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPost-normalization checkpoint:\n<path/N-A>\n\nRollback source:\n<path>\n\nPATCH 000 STATUS:\n<VALIDATED_STRUCTURE/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:324:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787243152,"text":"FASE: PATCH 000 — POST CHECKPOINT VERIFY\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/Machina\n\nMODE:\nREAD ONLY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nVerify the already-created post-reorganization checkpoint.\n\nDo not modify source.\nDo not build unless source changed after checkpoint.\nDo not create another checkpoint.\n\nReport:\n\n1. exact latest checkpoint path\n2. patch directories currently present\n3. PATCH_STATUS.md mapping\n4. Core files modified by reorganization\n5. runtime patch ownership\n6. duplicate gesture/query/particle/settings owners\n7. build associated with checkpoint\n8. snapshot/hash status if recorded\n\nEXPECTED PATCH MAP:\n\n001 Sensitive Home Interaction\n002 Search Container Reveal\n003 Search Engine\n004 Search Network Animation\n005 Settings Visual\n006 Settings Functionality\n007 App Slot Editor\n008 First Install Autofill\n\nOUTPUT:\n\nMACHINA POST-REORGANIZATION CHECKPOINT VERIFIED\n\nCheckpoint:\n<path>\n\nPatch map normalized:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nOwnership conflicts:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate runtime paths:\n<n>\n\nPATCH_STATUS synchronized:\n<YES/NO>\n\nBuild status:\n<value>\n\nSnapshot/hash:\n<value>\n\nStructural baseline:\n<VALID/REVIEW_REQUIRED>\n\nProject modified:\nNO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:325:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787243279,"text":"PATCH 000 — REAL PATCH NORMALIZATION\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/Machina\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nPRE-REORGANIZATION CHECKPOINT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/checkpoints/\n2026-08-20_16-35-44-patch-004-settings-validated\n\nMODE:\nSTRUCTURAL REORGANIZATION\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nIMPORTANT\n\nThe previous audit confirmed that PATCH 000 has NOT yet\nbeen performed.\n\nThis checkpoint is now the official rollback source.\n\nDO NOT create another PRE checkpoint.\n\n==================================================\n1. OBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nNormalize existing patch code into this permanent map:\n\n001 — Sensitive Home Interaction\n002 — Search Container Reveal\n003 — Search Engine\n004 — Search Network Animation\n005 — Settings Visual\n006 — Settings Functionality\n007 — App Slot Editor\n008 — First Install Autofill\n\nNO feature development.\n\nNO visual changes.\n\nNO runtime behavior changes.\n\n==================================================\n2. CURRENT LEGACY DIRECTORIES\n==================================================\n\nAudit current directories including:\n\nhome_interaction\nsearch_bar\nsearch_engine\nsettings\nslot_editor\nusage_autofill\n\nand legacy directories such as:\n\nfav_expansion\nfav_lift\nfav_search\nhome_visual\netc.\n\nClassify each:\n\nACTIVE\nDEAD\nSUPERSEDED\nHISTORICAL_ONLY\n\nDo not delete uncertain code.\n\n==================================================\n3. TARGET DIRECTORY MAP\n==================================================\n\nNormalize toward:\n\npatches/\n  001_sensitive_home/\n  002_search_reveal/\n  003_search_engine/\n  004_search_animation/\n  005_settings_visual/\n  006_settings_functional/\n  007_slot_editor/\n  008_first_install/\n\nDirectory numbering must now remain permanent.\n\n==================================================\n4. PATCH 001\n==================================================\n\nSource from current:\n\nhome_interaction\n\nOwn only:\n\nLEFT/RIGHT Material Stretch\nedge Back exclusion\ngesture arbitration\nbase haptic interaction\n\nStatus:\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\n\nBehavior:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n5. PATCH 002\n==================================================\n\nNormalize current Search/Fav reveal code.\n\nOwn only:\n\nUP/DOWN Search reveal\nFav expanded geometry\nSearchSlot\nSearch bar shell\nFocus / IME\n\nMust NOT contain:\n\nsearch algorithm\nhistory\nparticle animation\nSettings\n\n==================================================\n6. PATCH 003\n==================================================\n\nNormalize existing:\n\nsearch_engine\n\nOwn:\n\nquery processing\nresults\nhistory\napp filtering\nsystem/web actions if already implemented\n\nDo NOT add missing functionality.\n\nIf incomplete:\nstatus = IMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\nor PLANNED according to actual runtime evidence.\n\n==================================================\n7. PATCH 004\n==================================================\n\nExtract Search network animation into:\n\n004_search_animation\n\nOwn only:\n\nAnimatedParticleNetwork\nSearch particle presentation/configuration\n\nNo gesture.\nNo Search algorithm.\nNo geometry owner.\n\nIf shared particle engine is also used by Settings,\nkeep ONE reusable visual implementation and clearly\ndocument ownership/library boundary.\n\nDo not duplicate particle engine.\n\n==================================================\n8. PATCH 005\n==================================================\n\nSplit current Settings visual responsibility into:\n\n005_settings_visual\n\nOwn:\n\nlegacy icons\nSettings layout\ntypography\nDynamic Color visual theme\ntop-down panel\nSettings network visual presentation\n\nNO preference backend.\n\n==================================================\n9. PATCH 006\n==================================================\n\nExtract Settings functional/backend responsibility into:\n\n006_settings_functional\n\nOwn:\n\nSettings preference owner\nON/OFF switches\nicon shape preference\nhaptic preference\nSearch preferences\ndefault Home\nApp info\nVersion\nChangelog\ntemporary Development Status\n\nDo not redesign Settings.\n\n==================================================\n10. PATCH 007\n==================================================\n\nNormalize current:\n\nslot_editor\n\nOwn:\n\nP1/P2/Dock editor\nApp Picker\nassign/remove action\n\nReuse Core persistence.\n\n==================================================\n11. PATCH 008\n==================================================\n\nNormalize:\n\nusage_autofill\n\nOwn first-install initialization only.\n\nTarget semantic Dock contract:\n\nDock[0] = default Phone\nDock[1] = default Messages/SMS\nDock[2] = default Browser\nDock[3] = default Music\nDock[4] = default Mail/Email\n\nP1:\ntop 8 usage-ranked non-Dock apps\n\nP2:\nnext 8\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT implement missing logic during PATCH 000.\n\nOnly move existing implementation and document gaps.\n\n==================================================\n12. LEGACY DIRECTORIES\n==================================================\n\nAfter ownership is resolved:\n\nconfirmed DEAD/SUPERSEDED runtime code:\nremove from active source tree.\n\nHistorical docs:\nKEEP.\n\nIf useful, move historical patch documentation under:\n\ndocs/history/\n\nDo not delete development history unnecessarily.\n\n==================================================\n13. OWNERSHIP INVARIANTS\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHomeSnapshot owners = 1\nAppCatalog owners = 1\nslot persistence owners = 1\nquery owners = 1\nparticle engines = 1\nSettings preference owners = 1\n\nGesture ownership conflicts = 0\n\nCircular patch dependencies = 0\n\n==================================================\n14. NO CORE CHANGE\n==================================================\n\nCore logic:\nNO CHANGE\n\nP1 = 8\nP2 = 8\nDock = 5\n\nLauncherActions:\nUNCHANGED\n\nHomeSnapshot semantics:\nUNCHANGED\n\nAppCatalog semantics:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n15. RUNTIME PARITY\n==================================================\n\nBefore/after:\n\nHome:\nIDENTICAL\n\nLEFT/RIGHT:\nIDENTICAL\n\nSearch reveal:\nIDENTICAL\n\nSearch bar:\nIDENTICAL\n\nSettings:\nIDENTICAL\n\nSettings particles:\nIDENTICAL\n\nSearch particles:\nIDENTICAL\n\nApp Picker:\nIDENTICAL\n\nP1/P2/Dock assignments:\nIDENTICAL\n\n==================================================\n16. CREATE PATCH STATUS\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/PATCH_STATUS.md\n\nColumns:\n\nPatch\nName\nRuntime\nDevice\nSecurity\nBuild\nCheckpoint\nStatus\n\nAllowed statuses:\n\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\nIMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\nPLANNED\nREJECTED\n\nPopulate from evidence only.\n\n==================================================\n17. PATCH 000 DOCUMENT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/PATCH_000_REORGANIZATION.md\n\nRecord:\n\nPRE checkpoint\nold directory map\nnew directory map\nfiles moved\nfiles removed\nownership map\nstatuses\ndependency graph\nruntime parity\nrollback procedure\n\n==================================================\n18. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 release = SUCCESS\nSnapshot validation = PASS\nSHA-256 validation = PASS\n\n==================================================\n19. POST CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nOnly after all PASS:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint patch-layout-normalized\n\n==================================================\n20. FINAL VERIFY\n==================================================\n\nVerify target directories exist:\n\n001_sensitive_home\n002_search_reveal\n003_search_engine\n004_search_animation\n005_settings_visual\n006_settings_functional\n007_slot_editor\n008_first_install\n\nLegacy active runtime directories remaining:\n0 preferred\n\nAny retained legacy directory must be explained.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 000 NORMALIZATION COMPLETE\n\nPRE checkpoint:\n<path>\n\nPatch directories before:\n<list>\n\nPatch directories after:\n<list>\n\n001:\n<status>\n\n002:\n<status>\n\n003:\n<status>\n\n004:\n<status>\n\n005:\n<status>\n\n006:\n<status>\n\n007:\n<status>\n\n008:\n<status>\n\nFiles moved:\n<n>\n\nFiles removed as confirmed dead:\n<n>\n\nLegacy runtime directories remaining:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot owners:\n<n>\n\nAppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nQuery owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nSettings preference owners:\n<n>\n\nGesture ownership conflicts:\n<n>\n\nCircular dependencies:\n<n>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nRuntime parity:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH_STATUS created:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPOST checkpoint:\n<path/N-A>\n\nRollback source:\n/opt/Android/Machina/checkpoints/\n2026-08-20_16-35-44-patch-004-settings-validated\n\nPATCH 000 STATUS:\n<VALIDATED_STRUCTURE/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:326:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787243791,"text":"FASE: PATCH 002 — SEARCH CONTAINER REVEAL VALIDATION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASELINE:\nPATCH 000 normalized structure\n\nPATCH:\n002_search_reveal\n\nSTATUS:\nIMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply:\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nValidare PATCH 002 così com'è oggi.\n\nPATCH 002 owns only:\n\n- swipe UP reveal\n- swipe DOWN collapse\n- SearchSlot geometry\n- Fav expanded position\n- Search bar shell\n- focus / IME behavior\n\nDO NOT add:\n\n- search results\n- history\n- particle animation\n- Settings\n- new gestures\n- new persistence\n\n==================================================\n1. DEVICE CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nVerify current runtime behavior matches:\n\nCOLLAPSED:\n- Search hidden\n- SearchSlot footprint minimal/zero\n- Fav baseline position\n- P1/P2/Dock baseline positions\n\nSWIPE UP:\n- Search area reveals\n- Fav reaches approved expanded position\n- Search bar becomes visible\n- P1 movement = 0dp\n- P2 movement = 0dp\n- Dock movement = 0dp\n- focus/IME behavior works\n- no LEFT/RIGHT regression\n\nSWIPE DOWN:\n- keyboard hides\n- Search collapses\n- Fav returns baseline\n- P1/P2/Dock remain fixed\n\n==================================================\n2. PATCH 001 HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nPATCH 001 files modified = 0\n\nLEFT Material Stretch:\nUNCHANGED\n\nRIGHT Material Stretch:\nUNCHANGED\n\nedge Back exclusion:\nUNCHANGED\n\nPATCH 001 haptic:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n3. OWNERSHIP AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nvertical reveal owner = 1\nSearchSlot geometry owner = 1\nSearch query/UI owner = 1\nfocus owner = 1\nIME owner = 1\n\nDuplicate owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n4. AXIS ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 002 must only react to vertical interaction.\n\nLEFT:\nno PATCH002 state mutation\n\nRIGHT:\nno PATCH002 state mutation\n\nTarget:\n\nhorizontal PATCH002 writes = 0\n\n==================================================\n5. SEARCH SLOT BOUNDS\n==================================================\n\nReport actual collapsed/expanded geometry:\n\nFav.bottom\nSearchSlot.top\nSearchSlot.bottom\nSearchBar.top\nSearchBar.bottom\nP1.top\n\nRequired:\n\nSearchBar inside SearchSlot\nSearchSlot does not overlap P1\nFav remains inside Home bounds\n\n==================================================\n6. IME SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nVerify keyboard does NOT shift:\n\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nTarget:\n\nkeyboard shifts Fav = NO\nkeyboard shifts P1 = NO\nkeyboard shifts P2 = NO\nkeyboard shifts Dock = NO\n\nAudit:\n\nimePadding\nWindowInsets.ime\nwindowInsetsPadding\nroot resize behavior\n\n==================================================\n7. FOCUS\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nrequestFocus only after accepted reveal\nkeyboard show reachable\nno focus request during partial drag\nno immediate clearFocus/reset path\n\n==================================================\n8. BACK\n==================================================\n\nWhile Search is active:\n\nBack:\n- clear focus\n- hide keyboard\n- collapse Search\n\nHome collapsed:\nexisting Core/PATCH001 Back contract preserved\n\nDuplicate BackHandlers:\n0\n\n==================================================\n9. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nVerify existing PATCH 002 haptic path.\n\nTarget:\n\naccepted UP = 1\naccepted DOWN = 1\nMOVE = 0\nLEFT = 0\nRIGHT = 0\nduplicate haptic = 0\n\nUse current hardware-adaptive API only.\n\n==================================================\n10. FIRST TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nP1 first tap = PASS\nP2 first tap = PASS\nDock first tap = PASS\nSearch field first tap = PASS\n\nFirst-touch blockers = 0\n\n==================================================\n11. NO SEARCH ENGINE COUPLING\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 002 must NOT own:\n\nAppCatalog filtering\nresults\nhistory\nweb search\nSettings search\nUsageStats\n\nThese belong elsewhere.\n\n==================================================\n12. NO PARTICLE COUPLING\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 002 must not own the particle engine.\n\nIt may expose SearchSlot bounds/content hook for PATCH 004,\nbut particle owner remains separate.\n\n==================================================\n13. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nHomeSnapshot writes = 0\nPersistence writes = 0\nNew AppCatalog owners = 0\nNew lifecycle owners = 0\nKeep-alive paths = 0\nMain-thread heavy gesture paths = 0\n\n==================================================\n14. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nRemoving:\n\n002_search_reveal\n\n+\nits declared integration hook\n\nmust restore:\n\nCore + PATCH 001\n\nwithout Search reveal.\n\nRollback:\nPASS required.\n\n==================================================\n15. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n16. DEVICE GATE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT mark VALIDATED from static analysis alone.\n\nIf current device behavior has already been tested and all points\nabove are confirmed PASS, record DEVICE = PASS.\n\nOtherwise:\n\nDEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\n==================================================\n17. CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nOnly if:\n\nDEVICE PASS\nCODE_SECURITY PASS\nROLLBACK PASS\nDEBUG PASS\nR8 PASS\nSNAPSHOT PASS\nSHA-256 PASS\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint patch-002-search-reveal-validated\n\nThen status:\n\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 002 SEARCH REVEAL VALIDATION COMPLETE\n\nDevice:\n<PASS/PENDING/FAILED>\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nVertical reveal owners:\n<n>\n\nSearchSlot geometry owners:\n<n>\n\nQuery/UI owners:\n<n>\n\nFocus owners:\n<n>\n\nIME owners:\n<n>\n\nHorizontal PATCH002 writes:\n<n>\n\nFav movement collapsed→expanded:\n<dp>\n\nP1 movement:\n<dp>\n\nP2 movement:\n<dp>\n\nDock movement:\n<dp>\n\nSearch overlap P1:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nKeyboard shifts Fav:\n<NO/YES>\n\nKeyboard shifts P1:\n<NO/YES>\n\nKeyboard shifts P2:\n<NO/YES>\n\nKeyboard shifts Dock:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDuplicate BackHandlers:\n<n>\n\nMOVE haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n<n>\n\nPersistence writes:\n<n>\n\nParticle engine owners inside PATCH002:\n<n>\n\nSearch engine paths inside PATCH002:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nRollback:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\n<VALIDATED_FROZEN / IMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED / FAILED>\n\nCheckpoint:\n<path/N-A>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:327:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787243963,"text":"FASE: PATCH 003 — SEARCH ENGINE VALIDATION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASELINE:\nPATCH 000 normalized structure\n\nPATCH:\n003_search_engine\n\nSTATUS:\nIMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\n\nPATCH 002:\nSEARCH REVEAL OWNER / DO NOT MODIFY GEOMETRY\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply:\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nValidare PATCH 003 così com'è oggi.\n\nPATCH 003 owns only:\n\n- query processing\n- app filtering\n- result ranking\n- results\n- history MEMORY_ONLY\n- optional Android Settings results\n- optional Web action\n- result actions/haptic\n\nPATCH 003 must NOT own:\n\n- UP/DOWN reveal\n- SearchSlot geometry\n- Fav movement\n- focus/IME geometry\n- Home gestures\n- particle animation\n\n==================================================\n1. QUERY OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nquery source owners total = 1\n\nPATCH 003 must consume the query state exposed by PATCH 002\nor the normalized shared Search UI contract.\n\nDo not create a second editable query source.\n\nDuplicate query owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n2. APP SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nUse EXISTING AppCatalog only.\n\nRequired:\n\nnew AppCatalog owners = 0\nPackageManager scan per keystroke = 0\n\nSearch launchable apps by:\n\n1. exact label match\n2. label startsWith query\n3. label contains query\n\nCase-insensitive.\n\nNormalize:\ntrim whitespace.\n\n==================================================\n3. DETERMINISTIC RANKING\n==================================================\n\nRanking must be stable.\n\nPreferred order:\n\nexact matches\nprefix matches\ncontains matches\n\nThen:\nalphabetical by label.\n\nNo UsageStats ranking.\nNo ML.\nNo recent-app ranking.\n\n==================================================\n4. RESULTS POSITION\n==================================================\n\nResults render ONLY inside the ResultsArea supplied by PATCH 002.\n\nRequired order:\n\nFav\nResultsArea\nSearchBar\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nResults below SearchBar:\n0\n\nPATCH 003 geometry writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\n5. RESULT LIMIT\n==================================================\n\nUse compact results.\n\nPreferred:\nmax 5 visible app results.\n\nIf more:\ninternal ResultsArea scroll.\n\nDo NOT move:\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\n==================================================\n6. ICONS\n==================================================\n\nUse existing Home icon resolver/AppVisuals.\n\nNo new icon cache.\n\nNo PackageManager drawable lookup per result render\nif shared visual resolver already exists.\n\nIcon resolver duplication:\n0\n\n==================================================\n7. APP RESULT ACTION\n==================================================\n\nTap app result:\n\n1. accepted command\n2. add confirmed query to history\n3. haptic if globally enabled\n4. launch through existing LauncherActions\n5. return Search according to PATCH 002 contract\n\nOne tap:\none launch.\n\nDo not create another launch implementation.\n\n==================================================\n8. HISTORY\n==================================================\n\nHistory maximum:\n3\n\nStorage:\nMEMORY_ONLY\n\nNo:\nDataStore\nSharedPreferences\nRoom\nfile storage\n\nHistory owner:\n1\n\n==================================================\n9. HISTORY PROCESS POLICY\n==================================================\n\nIf Android keeps Machina process cached:\nhistory survives naturally.\n\nIf Android kills process:\nhistory becomes empty.\n\nThis is intentional.\n\nDo not force process residency.\n\n==================================================\n10. HISTORY WRITE RULE\n==================================================\n\nStore only confirmed, non-empty searches.\n\nValid triggers:\n\n- app result selected\n- IME Search/Done confirmed\n- System Settings result selected\n- Web action selected\n\nDo NOT store:\neach keystroke\nfocus\nresult appearance\n\n==================================================\n11. HISTORY NORMALIZATION\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nmax 3\nmost recent first\ndeduplicate\ntrim whitespace\n\nIf existing query selected again:\nmove to first position.\n\n==================================================\n12. EMPTY QUERY\n==================================================\n\nWhen query is empty:\n\nshow up to 3 history rows.\n\nIf history empty:\nResultsArea remains empty.\n\nDo NOT show:\nrandom apps\nrecommended apps\nrecent apps\n\n==================================================\n13. HISTORY ROW ACTION\n==================================================\n\nTap history row:\n\n- populate current Search query\n- keep Search open/focused\n- recompute results\n\nDo NOT auto-launch an app.\n\n==================================================\n14. LIVE FILTERING\n==================================================\n\nWhile typing:\n\nfilter in-memory AppCatalog.\n\nTarget hot path:\n\nPackageManager = 0\ndisk IO = 0\nnetwork = 0\nUsageStats = 0\nbitmap decode = 0\n\nNo debounce/coroutine unless measured need exists.\n\n==================================================\n15. IME ACTION\n==================================================\n\nIME Search/Done:\n\ntrim query.\n\nIf non-empty:\nstore in history.\n\nDo NOT auto-launch first result by default.\n\nKeep Search/results visible.\n\n==================================================\n16. SYSTEM SETTINGS RESULTS\n==================================================\n\nIf already implemented, validate curated results only.\n\nExamples:\n\nWi-Fi\nBluetooth\nDisplay\nBattery\nApps\nAccessibility\nPrivacy/Security\n\nUse documented Settings intents.\n\nNo hidden APIs.\nNo reflection.\n\nIf not implemented:\ndo NOT implement during validation.\nReport as NOT_IMPLEMENTED.\n\n==================================================\n17. WEB ACTION\n==================================================\n\nIf already implemented:\n\nshow one action for non-empty query:\n\nSearch web for \"<query>\"\n\nUse external browser via safe ACTION_VIEW HTTPS flow.\n\nNo WebView.\nNo network request from Machina.\n\nIf not implemented:\nreport NOT_IMPLEMENTED.\n\n==================================================\n18. ERROR SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nHandle safely:\n\nuninstalled app\nActivityNotFoundException\nSecurityException\nunresolvable Settings action\nno browser\n\nSearch failure must not crash Home.\n\nConfirmed crash paths:\n0\n\n==================================================\n19. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nUse shared Machina haptic preference/API.\n\nIf enabled:\n\napp result selected:\nCONFIRM x1\n\nhistory selected:\nCONFIRM x1\n\nsystem result selected:\nCONFIRM x1\n\nweb result selected:\nCONFIRM x1\n\nIME confirmed:\nmax 1\n\nNo haptic:\n\ntyping\nscroll\nresult appearance\nfocus\nMOVE\n\nDuplicate haptic:\n0\n\n==================================================\n20. PATCH 002 HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 003 must not change:\n\nSearchSlot dimensions\nFav expanded position\nUP/DOWN reveal\nSearchBar visual\nIME layout behavior\nLEFT/RIGHT arbitration\n\nPATCH 002 geometry modifications:\n0\n\n==================================================\n21. PATCH 001 HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nLEFT Material Stretch:\nUNCHANGED\n\nRIGHT Material Stretch:\nUNCHANGED\n\nedge Back exclusion:\nUNCHANGED\n\nPATCH 001 files modified:\n0\n\n==================================================\n22. PARTICLE ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 003 must not own:\n\nAnimatedParticleNetwork\nparticle Canvas\nparticle velocity\nline rendering\n\nParticle engine owners inside PATCH 003:\n0\n\n==================================================\n23. FIRST TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\napp result first tap = PASS\nhistory first tap = PASS\nP1 first tap = PASS\nP2 first tap = PASS\nDock first tap = PASS\n\nResults hitbox must remain inside ResultsArea.\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n0\n\n==================================================\n24. STATE OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nExpected:\n\nquery owner = 1 total\nhistory owner = 1\nresults derivation owner = <=1\n\nDuplicate mutable result state:\n0 preferred\n\nNo global mutable search singleton unless already normalized\nand justified.\n\n==================================================\n25. NO PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nSearch history persistence writes:\n0\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nLauncherPreferences writes:\n0\n\nPATCH 003 must not own persistent Home data.\n\n==================================================\n26. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nAudit hot path for:\n\nmain-thread heavy work\nPackageManager calls\ndisk access\nnetwork\nUsageStats\nrepeated icon resolution\n\nTarget all:\n0 except lightweight in-memory filtering/render.\n\n==================================================\n27. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nRemoving:\n\n003_search_engine\n\n+\nits declared Search results integration hook\n\nmust leave:\n\nCore\nPATCH 001\nPATCH 002 Search bar/reveal\n\nworking normally.\n\nOnly Search results/history/actions disappear.\n\nRollback:\nPASS required.\n\n==================================================\n28. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md.\n\nRequired:\n\nNew AppCatalog owners = 0\nNew HomeSnapshot owners = 0\nNew gesture owners = 0\nNew lifecycle owners = 0\nBackHandlers added = 0\nPersistence writes = 0\nFirst-touch blockers = 0\n\n==================================================\n29. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n30. DEVICE TEST\n==================================================\n\nOn Pixel verify:\n\nA. EMPTY QUERY\n- history shown if present\n- max 3\n- no random apps\n\nB. TYPE QUERY\n- results appear above SearchBar\n- ranking sensible\n- icons correct\n- P1/P2/Dock do not move\n\nC. APP RESULT\n- first tap works\n- app launches\n- query enters history\n\nD. HISTORY\n- previous query shown\n- tap restores query\n- results refresh\n- no automatic launch\n\nE. LEFT/RIGHT\n- PATCH 001 behavior unchanged\n\nF. UP/DOWN / IME\n- PATCH 002 behavior unchanged\n\nG. REGRESSIONS\n- crash NONE\n- first-touch bug NONE\n- geometry jump NONE\n- duplicate haptic NONE\n\n==================================================\n31. CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nOnly if:\n\nDEVICE PASS\nCODE_SECURITY PASS\nROLLBACK PASS\nDEBUG PASS\nR8 PASS\nSNAPSHOT PASS\nSHA-256 PASS\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint patch-003-search-engine-validated\n\nThen:\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 003 SEARCH ENGINE VALIDATION COMPLETE\n\nDevice:\n<PASS/PENDING/FAILED>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 001 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 geometry modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nQuery owners:\n<n>\n\nHistory owners:\n<n>\n\nHistory max:\n<n>\n\nHistory storage:\n<MEMORY_ONLY/OTHER>\n\nApp search:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRanking:\n<EXACT_PREFIX_CONTAINS/OTHER>\n\nResults above SearchBar:\n<YES/NO>\n\nMax visible results:\n<n>\n\nNew AppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nPackageManager calls while typing:\n<n>\n\nUsageStats calls while typing:\n<n>\n\nIcon resolver:\n<SHARED/OTHER>\n\nSystem Settings results:\n<YES/NO/NOT_IMPLEMENTED>\n\nWeb action:\n<YES/NO/NOT_IMPLEMENTED>\n\nParticle engine owners:\n<n>\n\nGesture owners added:\n<n>\n\nBackHandlers added:\n<n>\n\nPersistence writes:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n<n>\n\nMOVE/typing haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n<n>\n\nConfirmed crash paths:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nRollback:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\n<VALIDATED_FROZEN / IMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED / FAILED>\n\nCheckpoint:\n<path/N-A>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:328:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787244513,"text":"FASE: PATCH 005 — SETTINGS VISUAL VALIDATION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nPATCH:\n005_settings_visual\n\nSTATUS:\nIMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\n\nPATCH 002:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nPATCH 003:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nPATCH 004:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nValidare SOLO il visual Settings già approvato.\n\nDo not add functionality.\nDo not modify switches/preferences.\nDo not redesign.\n\nVERIFY:\n\n1. Legacy icons restored and consistent.\n2. System/Material typography only.\n3. Dynamic Color presentation works.\n4. Top-down Settings panel remains compact.\n5. Status bar safe inset respected.\n6. Network particles visible and animated.\n7. No static wallpaper fallback.\n8. Category/subcategory layout unchanged.\n9. P1/P2/Dock/Home unaffected.\n10. No touch interception from particle Canvas.\n\nREQUIRED:\n\nCore modified = NO\nPATCH001 modified = NO\nPATCH002 modified = NO\nPATCH003 modified = NO\nPATCH004 modified = NO\n\nNew persistence = 0\nNew gesture owners = 0\nHomeSnapshot writes = 0\n\nBUILD:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\nDEVICE TEST:\n\n- Settings opens correctly\n- visual matches approved version\n- icons correct\n- Dynamic Color correct\n- particles visible\n- lines visible\n- status bar overlap = NONE\n- top panel size correct\n- Settings rows readable/clickable\n- Home regressions = NONE\n\nIF DEVICE PASS:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint patch-005-settings-visual-validated\n\nUpdate PATCH_STATUS.md:\n\n005 Settings Visual\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\n\nOUTPUT:\n\nMACHINA PATCH 005 SETTINGS VISUAL VALIDATION COMPLETE\n\nDevice: <PASS/PENDING/FAILED>\nLegacy icons: <PASS/FAIL>\nMaterial typography: <PASS/FAIL>\nDynamic Color visual: <PASS/FAIL>\nTop panel: <PASS/FAIL>\nStatus bar safe: <PASS/FAIL>\nParticle animation: <PASS/FAIL>\nStatic wallpaper paths: <n>\nGesture owners added: <n>\nPersistence writes: <n>\nCore modified: <NO/YES>\nCode-security: <PASS/FAIL>\nRollback: <PASS/FAIL>\nDebug: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nR8: <SUCCESS/FAILED>\nSnapshot: <PASS/FAIL>\nSHA-256: <PASS/FAIL>\nPATCH STATUS:\n<VALIDATED_FROZEN / IMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED / FAILED>\nCheckpoint:\n<path/N-A>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:329:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787244957,"text":"FASE: PATCH 006 — SETTINGS FUNCTIONALITY VALIDATION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nPATCH:\n006_settings_functional\n\nSTATUS:\nIMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\n\nPATCH 002:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nPATCH 003:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nPATCH 004:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nPATCH 005:\nSETTINGS VISUAL OWNER / DO NOT REDESIGN\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply:\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nValidare PATCH 006 così com'è oggi.\n\nPATCH 006 owns only:\n\n- Settings preference owner\n- real ON/OFF switches\n- Dynamic Color preference\n- haptic preference\n- Search auto-keyboard preference\n- icon-shape preference if truly implemented\n- default Home action\n- App info action\n- version information\n- changelog\n- temporary Development Status metadata\n\nPATCH 006 must NOT own:\n\n- Settings visual layout\n- legacy icons\n- Settings particle drawing\n- Search geometry\n- Search algorithm\n- Home gestures\n- P1/P2/Dock slot editing\n\n==================================================\n1. SETTINGS PREFERENCE OWNER\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nSettings preference owners = 1\n\nAll persisted Settings values must go through one owner.\n\nNo direct preference access scattered across composables.\n\nDuplicate preference owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n2. ALLOWED SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nAudit only actually implemented settings.\n\nExpected candidates:\n\ndynamicColorEnabled\nhapticEnabled\nsearchAutoKeyboard\niconShape\nhomeSpacingMode\nsearchAppsEnabled\nsearchSettingsEnabled\nsearchWebEnabled\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo not require every key to exist.\n\nOnly implemented real features may have persisted keys.\n\nPlaceholder preference keys:\n0\n\n==================================================\n3. DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nIf implemented:\n\nSwitch works:\nYES\n\nDefault:\nON\n\nScope:\nSETTINGS ONLY unless explicitly documented otherwise.\n\nON:\nAndroid dynamic color\n\nOFF:\nMachina fallback Settings scheme\n\nPersist:\nYES\n\nHome color mutation:\nNO\n\n==================================================\n4. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nIf implemented:\n\nSwitch:\nON/OFF\n\nDefault:\nON\n\nOne shared state:\n\nhapticEnabled\n\nConsumers may include:\nPATCH 001\nPATCH 002\nPATCH 006\nother explicit action patches\n\nDo not duplicate haptic preference state.\n\nOFF:\nMachina haptic calls suppressed\n\nMotion/gesture behavior:\nunchanged\n\n==================================================\n5. SEARCH AUTO-KEYBOARD\n==================================================\n\nIf implemented:\n\nDefault:\nON\n\nON:\nPATCH 002 reveal requests focus + keyboard\n\nOFF:\nSearch reveals but keyboard waits for user tap\n\nPATCH 002 geometry:\nUNCHANGED\n\nOnly preference read is allowed.\n\n==================================================\n6. ICON SHAPE\n==================================================\n\nIf exposed:\n\nverify backend is real.\n\nDo NOT show fake choices.\n\nEach option must change actual Machina icon rendering.\n\nPersist:\nYES\n\nNo slot identity mutation.\n\nIf backend does not exist:\nstatus = NOT_EXPOSED\n\n==================================================\n7. HOME SPACING\n==================================================\n\nIf exposed:\n\nmust use safe predefined tokens only.\n\nPreferred:\nCompact\nDefault\nRelaxed\n\nDo NOT expose arbitrary raw dp slider if it can break\nvalidated Home geometry.\n\nIf backend unsafe/incomplete:\nstatus = NOT_EXPOSED\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH SOURCE TOGGLES\n==================================================\n\nIf Search providers are actually implemented:\n\nApps\nSystem Settings\nWeb\n\nshow real toggles.\n\nIf provider not implemented:\ndo not show fake switch.\n\nPATCH 003 query/ranking logic must remain unchanged except\nfor reading enabled-source preference.\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH HISTORY SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nHistory is MEMORY_ONLY.\n\nDo not create disk persistence.\n\nIf Clear history action exists:\nmust call PATCH 003 history owner through explicit bridge.\n\nDo not create a second history store.\n\n==================================================\n10. DEFAULT HOME\n==================================================\n\nMust be functional.\n\nUse supported Android:\n\nRoleManager.ROLE_HOME\n\nor existing HomeRoleAction backend.\n\nDo not duplicate role-management implementation.\n\nIf already default:\nshow correct status.\n\nNo hidden API.\n\n==================================================\n11. APP INFO\n==================================================\n\nMust open Android application details:\n\nSettings.ACTION_APPLICATION_DETAILS_SETTINGS\n\npackage:\nMachina package\n\nNo custom App Info implementation required.\n\n==================================================\n12. VERSION\n==================================================\n\nRead runtime application metadata:\n\nversionName\nversionCode\n\nNo hardcoded version.\n\n==================================================\n13. CHANGELOG\n==================================================\n\nUser-facing only.\n\nNo internal terminology such as:\n\nPATCH 001\nPATCH 002\nCore V2\nVALIDATED\nFROZEN\nowner\nhook\ncheckpoint\nruntime audit\n\nChangelog must describe product changes only.\n\n==================================================\n14. DEVELOPMENT STATUS\n==================================================\n\nTemporary development page may exist.\n\nRequired:\n\nread-only\ncompile/config hide flag available\nno filesystem paths\nno SHA hashes\nno secrets\nno device IDs\n\nFinal release:\nmust be easy to hide/remove.\n\n==================================================\n15. USER-VISIBLE DEBUG TEXT\n==================================================\n\nSearch Settings UI strings for:\n\nPATCH\nCore V2\nVALIDATED\nFROZEN\nhook\nruntime owner\nplaceholder\nimplementation detail\n\nOutside Development Status page:\nexpected occurrences = 0\n\n==================================================\n16. PATCH 005 HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 006 must NOT redesign:\n\nSettings layout\nlegacy icons\ntop panel\nparticles\ntypography\nspacing\ncategory visuals\n\nPATCH 005 visual modifications:\n0\n\n==================================================\n17. PATCH 001 HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nOnly permitted integration:\nread hapticEnabled if already wired.\n\nLEFT/RIGHT Material Stretch:\nUNCHANGED\n\ngesture exclusion:\nUNCHANGED\n\nNo motion changes.\n\n==================================================\n18. PATCH 002 HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nPermitted reads:\n\nsearchAutoKeyboard\nhapticEnabled\n\nDo not modify:\n\nSearchSlot geometry\nFav position\nUP/DOWN gesture\nIME layout strategy\n\n==================================================\n19. PATCH 003 HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nPermitted reads:\n\nenabled Search sources\n\nPermitted action:\nclear history through owner bridge if implemented\n\nDo not create duplicate query/history owners.\n\n==================================================\n20. STATE OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nExpected:\n\nSettings preference owner = 1\nDynamic Color state owner = 1\nHaptic state owner = 1\nSearch auto-keyboard owner = 1\n\nNo duplicate mutable copies as independent sources of truth.\n\n==================================================\n21. PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nPersistence is allowed ONLY for real user settings.\n\nDo NOT persist:\n\nSearch history\nparticle positions\ngesture transient state\nquery\nHomeSnapshot duplicates\n\n==================================================\n22. FIRST TOUCH / ACTION SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nEach Settings command:\n\none tap\n→ one action\n\nNo duplicate callbacks.\n\nNo repeated Activity launch.\n\nNo accidental haptic duplication.\n\n==================================================\n23. HAPTIC ON SETTINGS ACTIONS\n==================================================\n\nIf hapticEnabled:\n\naccepted Settings command:\nCONFIRM x1\n\nTyping/scroll/MOVE:\n0\n\nTurning haptic OFF:\nmust not immediately trigger a second duplicate vibration.\n\n==================================================\n24. SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nNo reflection.\nNo hidden APIs.\nNo dynamic code loading.\nNo embedded credentials.\nNo broad R8 keep rules.\n\nSettings intents:\nsafe and documented.\n\n==================================================\n25. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nOpening Settings:\n\nPackageManager full enumeration = 0\nnetwork = 0\nwallpaper decode = 0\nUsageStats = 0\npolling = 0\n\nPreference reads:\nlightweight only.\n\n==================================================\n26. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nRemoving:\n\n006_settings_functional\n\nmust leave PATCH 005 visual Settings shell intact.\n\nCore + other patches continue with safe defaults.\n\nRollback:\nPASS required.\n\n==================================================\n27. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nSettings preference owners = 1\nduplicate setting owners = 0\nplaceholder keys = 0\nHomeSnapshot writes = 0\nnew lifecycle owners = 0\nfirst-touch blockers = 0\n\n==================================================\n28. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n29. DEVICE TEST\n==================================================\n\nOn Pixel verify all implemented controls only.\n\nA. Dynamic Color\n- toggle works\n- persists\n- only Settings changes if scoped Settings-only\n\nB. Haptic\n- ON works\n- OFF suppresses Machina haptic\n- gestures still work\n\nC. Search auto keyboard\n- ON works\n- OFF works\n- no Search geometry change\n\nD. Icon shape\n- works if exposed\n- actual Home icons update\n\nE. Default Home\n- Android Home-role flow works\n- current status correct\n\nF. App info\n- Android App info opens\n\nG. Version\n- real metadata displayed\n\nH. Changelog\n- user-facing only\n\nI. Development Status\n- read-only\n- no sensitive paths/data\n\nJ. REGRESSIONS\n- PATCH005 visual unchanged\n- PATCH001 motion unchanged\n- PATCH002 geometry unchanged\n- PATCH003 search unchanged\n- no crashes\n- no first-touch bug\n\n==================================================\n30. CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nOnly if:\n\nDEVICE PASS\nCODE_SECURITY PASS\nROLLBACK PASS\nDEBUG PASS\nR8 PASS\nSNAPSHOT PASS\nSHA-256 PASS\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint patch-006-settings-functional-validated\n\nThen:\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 006 SETTINGS FUNCTIONALITY VALIDATION COMPLETE\n\nDevice:\n<PASS/PENDING/FAILED>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 001 behavior modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 002 geometry modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 003 state ownership modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 005 visual modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSettings preference owners:\n<n>\n\nPersisted keys:\n<list>\n\nPlaceholder preference keys:\n<n>\n\nDynamic Color:\n<FUNCTIONAL/NOT_IMPLEMENTED/FAILED>\n\nDynamic Color scope:\n<SETTINGS_ONLY/OTHER/N-A>\n\nHaptic:\n<FUNCTIONAL/NOT_IMPLEMENTED/FAILED>\n\nSearch auto-keyboard:\n<FUNCTIONAL/NOT_IMPLEMENTED/FAILED>\n\nIcon shape:\n<FUNCTIONAL/NOT_EXPOSED/FAILED>\n\nHome spacing:\n<FUNCTIONAL/NOT_EXPOSED/FAILED>\n\nSearch source toggles:\n<list/NONE>\n\nSearch history clear:\n<FUNCTIONAL/NOT_EXPOSED>\n\nDefault Home:\n<FUNCTIONAL/FAILED>\n\nApp info:\n<FUNCTIONAL/FAILED>\n\nVersion:\n<RUNTIME_METADATA/FAILED>\n\nChangelog:\n<USER_FACING/FAILED>\n\nDevelopment status:\n<READ_ONLY/HIDDEN/NOT_IMPLEMENTED/FAILED>\n\nUser-visible debug strings outside dev page:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate setting owners:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nRollback:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\n<VALIDATED_FROZEN / IMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED / FAILED>\n\nCheckpoint:\n<path/N-A>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:330:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787245801,"text":"FASE: PATCH 008 — FIRST INSTALL AUTOFILL VALIDATION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nPATCH:\n008_first_install\n\nSTATUS:\nIMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001:\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\n\nPATCH 002:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nPATCH 003:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nPATCH 004:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nPATCH 005:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nPATCH 006:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nPATCH 007:\nDO NOT MODIFY\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply:\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nValidare PATCH 008 così com'è oggi.\n\nPATCH 008 owns only:\n\n- first-install slot initialization\n- semantic Dock resolution\n- usage-based P1/P2 ranking\n- one-time completion marker\n- safe fallback if Usage Access unavailable\n\nPATCH 008 must NOT own:\n\n- manual slot editing\n- continuous usage monitoring\n- Search ranking\n- Home gestures\n- Settings visual\n- AppCatalog\n- HomeSnapshot\n- duplicate slot persistence\n\n==================================================\n1. FIRST RUN ONLY\n==================================================\n\nAutofill must run only when initial setup is not yet complete.\n\nRequired:\n\nfirst-run marker owner = 1\n\nAfter successful setup:\n\nmark autofill complete.\n\nLater launches:\nNO automatic reordering.\n\n==================================================\n2. EXISTING LAYOUT PROTECTION\n==================================================\n\nIf P1/P2/Dock already contain a meaningful user layout:\n\nDO NOT overwrite automatically.\n\nExisting layout protection:\nPASS required.\n\nIf user explicitly resets/re-runs in future:\nthat must be a separate action.\n\n==================================================\n3. DOCK CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nDock is NOT usage-ranked.\n\nRequired semantic slots:\n\nDock[0] = default Phone\nDock[1] = default Messages/SMS\nDock[2] = default Browser\nDock[3] = default Music\nDock[4] = default Mail/Email\n\nUse current Android-supported role/default-handler resolution.\n\n==================================================\n4. PHONE\n==================================================\n\nResolve default Phone app using supported Android role/default APIs.\n\nPrefer:\n\nRoleManager.ROLE_DIALER\n\nor existing safe backend.\n\nNo hardcoded package names.\n\nIf unresolved:\nleave Dock[0] empty.\n\n==================================================\n5. MESSAGES / SMS\n==================================================\n\nResolve default SMS/Messages app.\n\nPrefer:\n\nRoleManager.ROLE_SMS\n\nor supported equivalent.\n\nNo hardcoded Google Messages package.\n\nIf unresolved:\nleave Dock[1] empty.\n\n==================================================\n6. BROWSER\n==================================================\n\nResolve default Browser app.\n\nPrefer supported Android default-browser role/API.\n\nNo hardcoded Chrome package.\n\nIf unresolved:\nleave Dock[2] empty.\n\n==================================================\n7. MUSIC\n==================================================\n\nResolve a default Music-capable app safely.\n\nUse supported intent/default-handler resolution for audio/media.\n\nDo NOT hardcode YouTube Music/Spotify/etc.\n\nOnly choose a launchable app that can reasonably handle music/audio.\n\nIf no reliable default can be determined:\nleave Dock[3] empty.\n\nDo not pick random installed music app.\n\n==================================================\n8. MAIL / EMAIL\n==================================================\n\nResolve default Email-capable app using supported mail intent resolution.\n\nNo hardcoded Gmail package.\n\nIf no reliable default exists:\nleave Dock[4] empty.\n\n==================================================\n9. DOCK DUPLICATE PROTECTION\n==================================================\n\nResolved semantic Dock apps should be unique where possible.\n\nIf same package resolves for two semantic roles:\n\nkeep the most authoritative role\nand leave conflicting slot empty unless a safe alternative exists.\n\nDo not invent arbitrary replacement.\n\n==================================================\n10. USAGE ACCESS\n==================================================\n\nP1/P2 ranking may use:\n\nUsageStatsManager\n\nRequired:\n\nandroid.permission.PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS\ndeclaration if needed\n\nUser must grant Usage Access manually through Android Settings.\n\nNo bypass.\nNo accessibility-service workaround.\n\n==================================================\n11. USAGE ACCESS FLOW\n==================================================\n\nIf Usage Access is not granted:\n\ndo NOT block first-run completion.\n\nBehavior:\n\n- semantic Dock may still be resolved\n- P1/P2 remain empty or use safe existing default behavior\n- user may fill manually via PATCH 007\n\nNo crash.\n\n==================================================\n12. USAGE WINDOW\n==================================================\n\nValidate actual configured window.\n\nPreferred target:\nlast 30 days\n\nDo not change during validation.\n\nReport exact value.\n\n==================================================\n13. APP SOURCE\n==================================================\n\nUsageStats packages must be intersected with EXISTING AppCatalog.\n\nOnly launchable Machina catalog entries may be assigned.\n\nRequired:\n\nnew AppCatalog owners = 0\n\nNo independent full app scanner.\n\n==================================================\n14. USAGE RANKING\n==================================================\n\nP1/P2 ranking only.\n\nExclude:\n\n- Machina itself\n- all Dock-assigned packages\n- non-launchable apps\n- unresolved packages\n- duplicate packages\n\n==================================================\n15. SCORE\n==================================================\n\nValidate current deterministic scoring formula.\n\nPreferred components:\n\n- total foreground time\n- recency / lastTimeUsed\n\nNo ML.\nNo cloud.\nNo remote ranking.\n\nDocument exact current formula.\n\n==================================================\n16. DETERMINISM\n==================================================\n\nSame usage data must produce same result.\n\nTie break preferred:\n\n1. score descending\n2. lastTimeUsed descending\n3. label ascending\n\nReport actual tie-break.\n\n==================================================\n17. P1 ASSIGNMENT\n==================================================\n\nAfter exclusions and sorting:\n\nP1:\nfirst 8 ranked apps\n\nExactly 8 slots max.\n\nIf fewer:\nremaining slots explicit empty.\n\n==================================================\n18. P2 ASSIGNMENT\n==================================================\n\nP2:\nnext 8 ranked apps\n\nExactly 8 slots max.\n\nIf fewer:\nremaining slots explicit empty.\n\n==================================================\n19. DOCK + P1/P2 TOTAL\n==================================================\n\nMaximum automatic assignments:\n\nDock:\n5\n\nP1:\n8\n\nP2:\n8\n\nTotal:\n21\n\nNo slot count change.\n\n==================================================\n20. SLOT PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nUse existing Core slot persistence only.\n\nRequired:\n\nslot persistence owners total = 1\n\nPATCH 008 must not create:\n\nSharedPreferences duplicate slot map\nDataStore duplicate slot map\nRoom duplicate slot store\n\n==================================================\n21. HOMESNAPSHOT\n==================================================\n\nHomeSnapshot owner remains:\n1\n\nPATCH 008 supplies assignments through existing safe API.\n\nNew HomeSnapshot owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n22. MANUAL EDITOR PROTECTION\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 007 remains sole manual editor.\n\nPATCH 008 must not modify manual slot-edit behavior.\n\nOnce initial autofill is complete:\nPATCH 007 becomes authoritative for user changes.\n\n==================================================\n23. NO CONTINUOUS MONITORING\n==================================================\n\nAfter first-run initialization:\n\nUsageStats polling:\n0\n\nWorkManager periodic jobs:\n0\n\nService:\n0\n\nForeground service:\n0\n\nWakeLock:\n0\n\nAlarm:\n0\n\nBackground ranking:\n0\n\n==================================================\n24. SEARCH ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 003 Search ranking must remain text-based.\n\nUsageStats must NOT influence Search results.\n\nUsageStats calls while Search active:\n0\n\n==================================================\n25. PRIVACY\n==================================================\n\nUsage data remains on-device.\n\nRequired:\n\nnetwork upload = 0\ntelemetry upload = 0\nusage-history release logging = 0\n\nDo not store detailed usage history.\n\nOnly persist resulting slot assignments and completion state.\n\n==================================================\n26. COMPLETION STATE\n==================================================\n\nPersist only the minimal marker necessary:\n\nfirstInstallAutofillCompleted\nor existing equivalent.\n\nDo not persist raw usage scores/history.\n\n==================================================\n27. USER CHOICE\n==================================================\n\nIf first-run UI exposes choice:\n\n\"Organizza automaticamente\"\n\nand\n\n\"Salta\"\n\nboth paths must complete setup safely.\n\nSkip:\nno Usage Access required.\n\n==================================================\n28. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nIf user explicitly confirms autofill and global haptic is enabled:\n\nCONFIRM x1\n\nNo haptic per assigned app.\nNo ranking haptic.\nNo MOVE haptic.\n\n==================================================\n29. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nUsageStats query:\none-time during initialization.\n\nDo not run on render/gesture hot path.\n\nNo repeated PackageManager scans.\n\nNo bitmap decode during ranking.\n\n==================================================\n30. ERROR SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nHandle safely:\n\nUsageStats unavailable\nUsage Access denied\ndefault role unresolved\npackage uninstalled during setup\nempty usage data\nless than 16 ranked apps\nmissing Music/Mail default\n\nNo crash.\n\n==================================================\n31. ROLLBACK\n==================================================\n\nRemoving:\n\n008_first_install\n\nmust leave:\n\nCore\nPATCH001–007\n\nworking normally.\n\nOnly automatic first-install slot population disappears.\n\nExisting user slot assignments remain valid.\n\nRollback:\nPASS required.\n\n==================================================\n32. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nnew AppCatalog owners = 0\nnew HomeSnapshot owners = 0\nduplicate slot persistence = 0\ncontinuous monitoring paths = 0\nnetwork paths = 0\nusage-data logging paths = 0\nnew lifecycle owners = 0 preferred\n\n==================================================\n33. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n34. DEVICE TEST\n==================================================\n\nOn Pixel test using a clean first-run state.\n\nA. DOCK\n\nVerify:\n\nDock[0] -> default Phone\nDock[1] -> default SMS/Messages\nDock[2] -> default Browser\nDock[3] -> default Music if safely resolved\nDock[4] -> default Email if safely resolved\n\nNo hardcoded package substitution.\n\nB. USAGE ACCESS GRANTED\n\nVerify:\n\nP1 = top 8 eligible usage-ranked apps\nP2 = next 8\n\nDock apps excluded from P1/P2.\n\nC. USAGE ACCESS DENIED\n\nVerify:\n\nsetup continues\nDock still resolves where possible\nP1/P2 safe/empty\nno crash\n\nD. SECOND LAUNCH\n\nVerify:\n\nno automatic reorder\nno UsageStats re-query for autofill\nmanual PATCH007 edits preserved\n\nE. PROCESS / REBOOT\n\nVerify:\n\nassigned slots persist\ncompletion marker persists\nno rerun\n\nF. REGRESSIONS\n\nPATCH001–007:\nunchanged\n\nHome:\nno crash\nno first-touch regression\nno slot-count change\n\n==================================================\n35. CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nOnly if:\n\nDEVICE PASS\nCODE_SECURITY PASS\nROLLBACK PASS\nDEBUG PASS\nR8 PASS\nSNAPSHOT PASS\nSHA-256 PASS\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint patch-008-first-install-validated\n\nThen:\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nVALIDATED_FROZEN\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 008 FIRST INSTALL VALIDATION COMPLETE\n\nDevice:\n<PASS/PENDING/FAILED>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH001-007 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nFirst-run owners:\n<n>\n\nAutofill completion marker:\n<value>\n\nExisting-layout overwrite protection:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nUsageStats API:\n<value>\n\nUsage Access required:\n<YES/NO>\n\nUsage window:\n<value>\n\nRanking formula:\n<value>\n\nTie-break:\n<value>\n\nDock Phone:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY/FAILED>\n\nDock Messages:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY/FAILED>\n\nDock Browser:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY/FAILED>\n\nDock Music:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY/FAILED>\n\nDock Mail:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY/FAILED>\n\nP1 assigned:\n<n>/8\n\nP2 assigned:\n<n>/8\n\nDock packages excluded from ranking:\n<YES/NO>\n\nNew AppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nNew HomeSnapshot owners:\n<n>\n\nSlot persistence owners:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate slot persistence:\n<n>\n\nContinuous UsageStats monitoring:\n<NO/YES>\n\nWorkManager paths:\n<n>\n\nService/keep-alive paths:\n<n>\n\nNetwork/telemetry paths:\n<n>\n\nUsage-data logging paths:\n<n>\n\nSecond-launch automatic reorder:\n<NO/YES>\n\nManual PATCH007 edits preserved:\n<YES/NO>\n\nConfirmed crash paths:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nRollback:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\n<VALIDATED_FROZEN / IMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED / FAILED>\n\nCheckpoint:\n<path/N-A>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:331:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787245911,"text":"PATCH 008 FIX — SEMANTIC DOCK RESOLVERS\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nPATCH:\n008_first_install\n\nCURRENT STATUS:\nFAILED\n\nFAILURE REASON:\nDock currently uses top-5 UsageStats ranking.\nRequired semantic Dock contract is missing.\n\nKEEP UNCHANGED:\n- first-run only behavior\n- existing-layout protection\n- UsageStats ranking for P1/P2\n- completion marker\n- Core slot persistence\n- PATCH 007 manual editing\n- no continuous monitoring\n- code-security behavior\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nReplace usage-ranked Dock with semantic default-app resolution:\n\nDock[0] = Phone\nDock[1] = Messages/SMS\nDock[2] = Browser\nDock[3] = Music\nDock[4] = Mail/Email\n\nThen exclude every resolved Dock package from P1/P2 usage ranking.\n\n==================================================\n1. DOCK MUST NOT USE USAGE RANKING\n==================================================\n\nRemove current logic:\n\nrankedApps.take(5) -> Dock\n\nDock assignments must be resolved independently.\n\nUsage ranking starts only AFTER semantic Dock packages\nare collected/excluded.\n\n==================================================\n2. PHONE RESOLVER\n==================================================\n\nPreferred source:\n\nRoleManager.ROLE_DIALER\n\nResolve current role holder.\n\nValidate result against existing AppCatalog:\n- package exists\n- launchable\n\nIf no valid holder:\nDock[0] = empty\n\nNo hardcoded package.\n\n==================================================\n3. SMS / MESSAGES RESOLVER\n==================================================\n\nPreferred:\n\nRoleManager.ROLE_SMS\n\nResolve current role holder.\n\nValidate against AppCatalog.\n\nIf unavailable:\nDock[1] = empty\n\nNo hardcoded Google Messages.\n\n==================================================\n4. BROWSER RESOLVER\n==================================================\n\nPreferred:\n\nRoleManager.ROLE_BROWSER\n\nResolve current role holder when supported.\n\nFallback only if needed:\nresolve default handler for a normal HTTPS VIEW intent\nwithout presenting chooser.\n\nValidate selected package against AppCatalog.\n\nIf no unambiguous default:\nDock[2] = empty\n\nNo hardcoded Chrome.\n\n==================================================\n5. MUSIC RESOLVER\n==================================================\n\nAndroid has no equivalent universal \"default music app\" role.\n\nUse a conservative resolver.\n\nPreferred strategy:\n\n1. build a standard audio/media intent appropriate for opening\n   playable audio content\n2. ask PackageManager for the DEFAULT resolved activity\n3. accept only if resolution is unambiguous and package is launchable\n4. validate package against AppCatalog\n\nDo NOT:\n- choose first installed music app\n- usage-rank music apps\n- hardcode Spotify/YouTube Music/etc.\n\nIf no trustworthy default:\nDock[3] = empty\n\n==================================================\n6. MAIL / EMAIL RESOLVER\n==================================================\n\nAndroid may not expose a universal email role.\n\nUse a conservative email default-handler resolution.\n\nPreferred:\nstandard mailto: intent / email-capable intent.\n\nResolve DEFAULT handler only.\n\nAccept only if:\n- unambiguous\n- launchable\n- present in AppCatalog\n\nDo NOT hardcode Gmail.\n\nIf unresolved:\nDock[4] = empty\n\n==================================================\n7. ROLE / DEFAULT RESOLVER OWNER\n==================================================\n\nCreate one PATCH008 semantic resolver owner.\n\nConcept:\n\nSemanticDockResolver\n\nMethods conceptually:\n\nresolvePhone()\nresolveSms()\nresolveBrowser()\nresolveMusic()\nresolveMail()\n\nDo not scatter PackageManager/RoleManager logic.\n\n==================================================\n8. CATALOG VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nEvery resolved package must be intersected with EXISTING AppCatalog.\n\nNew AppCatalog owners:\n0\n\nIf semantic resolver returns package not launchable by Machina:\ntreat as unresolved.\n\n==================================================\n9. DUPLICATES\n==================================================\n\nBuild semantic Dock in fixed slot order:\n\nPhone\nSMS\nBrowser\nMusic\nMail\n\nTrack packages already used.\n\nIf a later semantic resolver returns a package already occupying\nanother Dock slot:\n\nlater slot = empty\n\nDo not invent alternate candidates during this patch.\n\n==================================================\n10. P1/P2 EXCLUSION\n==================================================\n\nAfter semantic Dock resolution:\n\ndockPackages =\nall non-empty resolved Dock package names\n\nUsage-ranked candidate list must exclude:\n\n- Machina package\n- non-launchable packages\n- dockPackages\n- duplicates\n\nRequired:\nDock packages excluded from ranking = YES\n\n==================================================\n11. P1 / P2 ASSIGNMENT\n==================================================\n\nAfter exclusion:\n\nP1 = ranked candidates 0..7\nP2 = ranked candidates 8..15\n\nNo Dock assignment from usage ranking.\n\nKeep existing scoring formula unchanged.\n\n==================================================\n12. NO USAGE FALLBACK FOR DOCK\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nIf a semantic Dock slot cannot be resolved:\n\nleave it EMPTY.\n\nDo NOT fill it with next usage-ranked app.\n\nThis preserves semantic meaning.\n\n==================================================\n13. FIRST-RUN SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\n- first run only\n- no overwrite of meaningful existing layout\n- completion marker\n- manual PATCH007 edits preserved\n\nNo behavior change outside initial autofill.\n\n==================================================\n14. PERMISSIONS\n==================================================\n\nSemantic Dock resolution must NOT require Usage Access.\n\nUsage Access is only for P1/P2 ranking.\n\nTherefore:\n\nDock can populate even when Usage Access is denied.\n\n==================================================\n15. API SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nUse supported public Android APIs only.\n\nNo hidden APIs.\nNo reflection.\nNo package-name assumptions.\n\nGuard APIs by SDK level where required.\n\n==================================================\n16. ERROR HANDLING\n==================================================\n\nEach resolver must fail locally.\n\nOne unresolved role must not abort all autofill.\n\nExample:\n\nPhone resolved\nSMS resolved\nBrowser resolved\nMusic empty\nMail empty\n\nis a valid result.\n\nNo crash.\n\n==================================================\n17. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md.\n\nTarget:\n\nnew AppCatalog owners = 0\nnew HomeSnapshot owners = 0\nduplicate persistence = 0\ncontinuous monitoring = 0\nnetwork = 0\nhardcoded semantic package names = 0\n\n==================================================\n18. BUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 008 SEMANTIC DOCK FIX COMPLETE\n\nDock source:\n<SEMANTIC_RESOLVERS/FAILED>\n\nPhone resolver:\n<ROLE_DIALER/OTHER>\nPhone:\n<package/EMPTY>\n\nMessages resolver:\n<ROLE_SMS/OTHER>\nMessages:\n<package/EMPTY>\n\nBrowser resolver:\n<ROLE_BROWSER/DEFAULT_INTENT/OTHER>\nBrowser:\n<package/EMPTY>\n\nMusic resolver:\n<DEFAULT_AUDIO_HANDLER/OTHER>\nMusic:\n<package/EMPTY>\n\nMail resolver:\n<DEFAULT_MAIL_HANDLER/OTHER>\nMail:\n<package/EMPTY>\n\nHardcoded semantic package names:\n<n>\n\nSemantic resolver owners:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate Dock packages:\n<n>\n\nDock derived from UsageStats:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock packages excluded from P1/P2 ranking:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1 ranking formula changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP2 ranking formula changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUsage Access required for Dock:\n<NO/YES>\n\nExisting-layout protection:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSecond-launch automatic reorder:\n<NO/YES>\n\nNew AppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nNew HomeSnapshot owners:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate persistence:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nIMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:332:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787247692,"text":"PATCH 009 V2 — HOME CONTAINER / P1-P2 VISUAL REWORK\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nBASE:\nPATCH 000 normalized structure\nPATCH 001–008 read-only unless explicitly required\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nSTATUS:\nIMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply:\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nCorreggere SOLO il layout Home visivo.\n\nTarget finale:\n\n- Fav Apps dentro il container principale\n- Search dentro il container principale\n- P1 dentro il container principale\n- P2 dentro il container principale\n- Dock FUORI dal container principale\n- P1 e P2 mantengono la loro altezza approvata\n- Dock mantiene la sua altezza approvata\n- il container principale NON deve occupare quasi tutto il display\n- colori / bordi / angoli / gap devono richiamare lo screen di riferimento approvato\n- colore interno più scuro e uniforme\n\nDO NOT modify:\n- Core data\n- AppCatalog\n- HomeSnapshot semantics\n- slot counts\n- Search algorithm\n- UsageStats\n- PATCH 001 motion\n- PATCH 003 ranking/history\n- PATCH 007 slot editor\n- PATCH 008 autofill logic\n\n==================================================\n1. FINAL STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nVisual order top -> bottom:\n\nFav Apps\n\nSearch area / Search animation / results\n\nP1\n\nP2\n\nEND OF MAIN CONTAINER\n\nGAP\n\nDock\n\nThe Dock MUST NOT be inside the main container.\n\n==================================================\n2. MAIN CONTAINER\n==================================================\n\nThe main Home container contains ONLY:\n\n- Fav Apps\n- Search\n- P1\n- P2\n\nIt must NOT contain Dock.\n\nUse one rounded outer container.\n\nTarget visual:\n\ndark charcoal / near-black\nslightly darker than current internal cards\n\nSuggested family:\nsurface / surfaceContainerLowest / equivalent current Machina token\n\nDo not hardcode bright colors.\n\n==================================================\n3. MAIN CONTAINER WIDTH\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT take the whole display width.\n\nPreferred:\n\n~84–90% of usable screen width\n\nStart target:\n88%\n\nCentered horizontally.\n\nKeep symmetric side margins.\n\n==================================================\n4. MAIN CONTAINER HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nCurrent Home height is too large.\n\nReduce total vertical footprint.\n\nThe container must wrap its content.\n\nDo NOT use:\nfillMaxHeight()\nweight() that forces full-screen vertical occupation\nfixed percentage of whole display unless required as max clamp\n\nPreferred:\nwrap content + bounded maxHeight\n\n==================================================\n5. MAIN CONTAINER SHAPE\n==================================================\n\nOuter corner radius:\n\n~26–30dp\n\nPreferred first test:\n28dp\n\nBorder:\n\n1dp subtle\n\nUse current Machina outline / outlineVariant family.\n\nNo thick border.\n\nNo glow.\n\n==================================================\n6. MAIN CONTAINER INNER PADDING\n==================================================\n\nUse compact consistent padding.\n\nPreferred:\n\nhorizontal:\n14–16dp\n\ntop:\n14–16dp\n\nbottom:\n14–16dp\n\nDo not stack multiple independent paddings.\n\n==================================================\n7. SECTION GAP\n==================================================\n\nUse consistent vertical gap between:\n\nFav -> Search\nSearch -> P1\nP1 -> P2\n\nPreferred:\n12–16dp\n\nStart:\n14dp\n\nNo huge blank areas.\n\n==================================================\n8. FAV APPS CARD\n==================================================\n\nFav Apps remains the first section.\n\nMake it visually more substantial vertically,\nbut not excessively tall.\n\nTarget:\n\ncurrent height + modest increase\n\nPreferred:\n+12–20%\n\nDo NOT make Fav Apps a giant header.\n\nKeep:\ntitle\nApps count\nSettings icon\ncurrent approved background/visual identity\n\nFav Apps internal corner radius:\nsame family as P1/P2.\n\n==================================================\n9. FAV APPS POSITION\n==================================================\n\nFav Apps must sit near the top inside the main container.\n\nDo NOT vertically center the whole module.\n\nNo large blank area above Fav.\n\n==================================================\n10. SEARCH AREA\n==================================================\n\nSearch stays between Fav and P1.\n\nSearch animation/results area may use available space,\nbut must not push P1/P2 downward beyond approved positions.\n\nSearch bar itself:\nkeep current approved visual.\n\nSearch results/history:\nPATCH 003-owned.\n\nSearch network animation:\nPATCH 004-owned.\n\nPATCH 009 only provides/layouts the space.\n\n==================================================\n11. P1\n==================================================\n\nP1 height:\nKEEP current approved height.\n\nDo NOT enlarge P1.\n\nDo NOT shrink P1.\n\nUse same rounded visual style as screen reference.\n\nP1:\ndark internal surface\nsubtle 1dp border\nsame radius family\n\nIf P1 has apps:\nkeep existing 2x4 grid.\n\nIf P1 is empty:\nshow empty-state content.\n\n==================================================\n12. P2\n==================================================\n\nP2 height:\nEXACTLY SAME AS P1.\n\nP2 visual:\nsame as P1.\n\nNo independent height calculation.\n\n==================================================\n13. EMPTY P1/P2 STATE\n==================================================\n\nWhen P1 or P2 is empty, show:\n\nsmall outline cube/box icon\n\nthen:\n\n\"No apps in this section\"\n\nthen smaller secondary text:\n\n\"Add your favorite apps to access them quickly.\"\n\nKeep content centered within section.\n\nDo NOT show empty state if apps are present.\n\n==================================================\n14. EMPTY STATE ICON\n==================================================\n\nUse the approved small cube/box visual.\n\nSize:\n~28–32dp\n\nLow contrast:\nonSurfaceVariant / equivalent\n\nNo large decorative icon.\n\n==================================================\n15. EMPTY STATE TYPOGRAPHY\n==================================================\n\nPrimary:\nbodyLarge / equivalent\n\nSecondary:\nbodySmall / bodyMedium\n\nSystem/Material typography only.\n\nNo oversized empty-state text.\n\n==================================================\n16. P1 / P2 INTERNAL SPACING\n==================================================\n\nKeep internal top/bottom padding compact:\n\n~10–12dp\n\nGrid when populated:\nunchanged.\n\nDo not change icon sizes through PATCH 009 unless necessary\nto preserve current visual.\n\n==================================================\n17. DOCK OUTSIDE MAIN CONTAINER\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL.\n\nDock MUST render as a separate rounded module below\nthe main container.\n\nStructure:\n\nMAIN CONTAINER\n[ Fav / Search / P1 / P2 ]\n\ngap\n\nDOCK MODULE\n\nDo NOT nest Dock inside main container.\n\n==================================================\n18. DOCK GAP\n==================================================\n\nGap between main container and Dock:\n\n~16–20dp\n\nPreferred:\n18dp\n\nClearly visually separated.\n\n==================================================\n19. DOCK MODULE\n==================================================\n\nDock uses its own dark rounded background.\n\nWidth:\nsame visual family as main container,\nbut it may be slightly narrower if current layout expects it.\n\nPreferred:\nsame centered alignment.\n\nCorner radius:\nsame family ~24–28dp.\n\nBorder:\n1dp subtle.\n\n==================================================\n20. DOCK HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nCurrent Dock height:\nKEEP approved compact height.\n\nDo NOT increase it.\n\nDock must look like a compact bottom bar,\nnot a third content card.\n\n==================================================\n21. DOCK ICONS\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n5 slots\n\nDo NOT change:\nslot logic\nsemantic Dock mapping\nmanual editor behavior\n\nPATCH 009 only controls container presentation.\n\n==================================================\n22. DOCK EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT show giant empty-state text inside Dock.\n\nIf Dock is empty:\nprefer compact empty slots / existing slot presentation.\n\nDock remains visually compact.\n\n==================================================\n23. COLORS\n==================================================\n\nTarget visual from reference:\n\nOuter main container:\nvery dark charcoal\n\nP1/P2:\nslightly lighter/different dark surface\n\nDock:\ndark independent surface\n\nBorders:\nsubtle gray / outlineVariant\n\nAvoid:\npure black boxes with no separation\nbright borders\nlarge transparency shifts\n\n==================================================\n24. ROUNDED CORNERS\n==================================================\n\nUse consistent corner family:\n\nMain outer container:\n28dp approx\n\nFav:\n22–24dp\n\nP1:\n22–24dp\n\nP2:\n22–24dp\n\nDock:\n24–28dp\n\nSearch:\nkeep current approved radius\n\nDo not mix many unrelated radii.\n\n==================================================\n25. NO FULL-SCREEN CONTAINER\n==================================================\n\nHard requirement:\n\nMain Home container must NOT touch:\n\nstatus bar\nleft screen edge\nright screen edge\nnavigation gesture area\n\nIt must remain a centered module.\n\n==================================================\n26. STATUS / NAV SAFE AREA\n==================================================\n\nRespect:\n\nstatusBars\nnavigationBars / gesture inset\n\nNo content under system status icons.\n\nNo Dock under gesture bar.\n\n==================================================\n27. KEYBOARD / IME\n==================================================\n\nWhen keyboard opens:\n\nP1 height:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP2 height:\nUNCHANGED\n\nDock height:\nUNCHANGED\n\nMain container should not permanently remeasure into an\noversized or compressed shape.\n\nKeep existing PATCH 002 IME strategy.\n\n==================================================\n28. PATCH 001 LOCK\n==================================================\n\nLEFT/RIGHT Material Stretch:\nUNCHANGED\n\nNo gesture changes.\n\nNo haptic changes.\n\n==================================================\n29. PATCH 002 LOCK\n==================================================\n\nSearch reveal behavior:\nUNCHANGED\n\nPATCH 009 may consume current SearchSlot dimensions,\nbut must not become a second reveal owner.\n\n==================================================\n30. PATCH 003 LOCK\n==================================================\n\nSearch ranking:\nUNCHANGED\n\nHistory:\nUNCHANGED\n\nResults:\nUNCHANGED\n\nPATCH 009 only provides visual bounds.\n\n==================================================\n31. PATCH 004 LOCK\n==================================================\n\nSearch network animation:\nUNCHANGED\n\nPATCH 009 only provides the full Search visual area.\n\nNo new particle engine.\n\n==================================================\n32. PATCH 007 LOCK\n==================================================\n\nLong press / App Picker:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP1/P2/Dock interaction hitboxes must still match visuals.\n\n==================================================\n33. PATCH 008 LOCK\n==================================================\n\nFirst-install assignment:\nUNCHANGED\n\nDock semantic logic:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP1/P2 usage ranking:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n34. OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 009 owns only:\n\nHome visual container composition\nsection spacing\nsection surface shape/color\nP1/P2 empty-state visual\nDock separation from main container\n\nIt owns NO data.\n\n==================================================\n35. STATE\n==================================================\n\nNew persistent state:\n0\n\nNew gesture state:\n0\n\nNew HomeSnapshot writes:\n0\n\nNew AppCatalog owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n36. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nNo:\nnetwork\nPackageManager scan\nUsageStats\ndisk IO\nbitmap decode\n\nLayout-only patch.\n\n==================================================\n37. STATIC AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nVerify no accidental use of:\n\nfillMaxHeight on main container\nweight forcing full-height Home\nDock nested inside main container\nduplicate P1/P2 sizing logic\n\nRequired:\n\nP1/P2 shared height token:\n1\n\nDock outside main container:\nYES\n\n==================================================\n38. DEVICE TEST\n==================================================\n\nPixel device:\n\nA. MAIN CONTAINER\n- centered\n- not full width\n- not full height\n- Fav/Search/P1/P2 inside\n- rounded border correct\n\nB. P1/P2\n- same height\n- same visual\n- compact\n- no resize regression\n\nC. EMPTY STATE\n- cube visible\n- text visible\n- centered\n- no oversized content\n\nD. DOCK\n- outside main container\n- compact\n- separate gap\n- 5 slots intact\n\nE. SEARCH\n- Search remains between Fav and P1\n- animation/results still work\n\nF. GESTURES\n- PATCH001 unchanged\n- PATCH002 unchanged\n\nG. REGRESSIONS\n- no overlap\n- no clipping\n- no first-touch bug\n- no keyboard layout break\n\n==================================================\n39. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n40. STATUS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT auto-freeze before device test.\n\nAfter build:\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nIMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 009 HOME CONTAINER REWORK COMPLETE\n\nMain container width:\n<value>\n\nMain container height behavior:\n<WRAP_CONTENT/BOUNDED/OTHER>\n\nMain container radius:\n<dp>\n\nMain container border:\n<value>\n\nFav height:\n<dp>\n\nFav height change:\n<value>\n\nSearch inside main container:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1 height:\n<dp>\n\nP2 height:\n<dp>\n\nP1/P2 same height:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1 empty-state:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP2 empty-state:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock inside main container:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock module height:\n<dp>\n\nDock gap from main container:\n<dp>\n\nDock slot count changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearch logic changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH001 behavior changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH002 behavior changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH003 behavior changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH004 engine changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH007 logic changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH008 logic changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHomeSnapshot writes:\n<n>\n\nNew persistence:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\n<IMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:333:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787248704,"text":"PATCH 009 — HOME UI V2 / CONTAINER & SPACING REVISION\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nPATCH:\n009_home_ui_v2\n\nSTATUS:\nIMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\nCORE:\nFROZEN\n\nPATCH 001–008:\nREAD ONLY / DO NOT MODIFY\n\nMANDATORY:\nApply:\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/MACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nImplement Home UI V2 exactly with this structure:\n\n1. Fav. apps\n2. Search bar\n3. P1\n4. P2\n5. Dock OUTSIDE the Home container\n\nMain requirement:\n\nFav. apps + Search + P1 + P2\nmust live inside ONE centered Home container.\n\nDock must stay outside that container.\n\nDo NOT make the Home container fill the whole display.\n\n==================================================\n1. HOME CONTAINER\n==================================================\n\nCreate one centered rounded Home container containing:\n\n- Fav. apps\n- Search bar\n- P1\n- P2\n\nDock:\noutside.\n\nDo NOT include Dock inside the Home container.\n\n==================================================\n2. HOME CONTAINER STYLE\n==================================================\n\nMatch the approved reference style.\n\nHome container:\n\ncolor:\ndark / slightly lighter than Dock\n\nPreferred starting token:\n#0F0F11\n\nborder:\n1dp subtle\n\nPreferred:\n#1C1C1E\n\ncorner radius:\n24dp\n\nhorizontal width:\napproximately 88–90% of available Home width\n\nDo NOT use full display width.\n\nDo NOT use full display height.\n\n==================================================\n3. OUTER POSITION\n==================================================\n\nKeep Home container visually centered.\n\nUse real layout constraints.\n\nNo absolute screen coordinates.\n\nRespect:\n\nstatus bar\nnavigation bar / gesture inset\n\nDo not push Home under system bars.\n\n==================================================\n4. INTERNAL PADDING\n==================================================\n\nHome container internal padding:\n\n16dp left\n16dp right\n16dp top\n16dp bottom\n\nUse one shared spacing token.\n\n==================================================\n5. INTERNAL GAP\n==================================================\n\nGap between internal sections:\n\nFav -> Search:\n16dp\n\nSearch -> P1:\n16dp\n\nP1 -> P2:\n16dp\n\nUse one shared gap token.\n\nAvoid large unused vertical space.\n\n==================================================\n6. FAV APPS HEADER\n==================================================\n\nFav remains first section.\n\nKeep:\n\nFav. apps title\nApps count\nSettings icon\nexisting Fav visual background / animation\n\nFav section:\n\nrounded corners:\n24dp\n\nsame border family as Home container\n\nsame dark color family\n\nFav must be slightly taller than current compact version,\nbut NOT huge.\n\nPreferred target:\nincrease current Fav visual height moderately,\napproximately +20–30%.\n\nDo NOT use 60% of screen.\n\n==================================================\n7. FAV CONTENT\n==================================================\n\nTitle:\nFav. apps\n\nSubtitle:\nApps <count>\n\nSettings icon:\nright aligned\n\nKeep existing typography scale.\n\nDo not enlarge title excessively.\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH BAR\n==================================================\n\nSearch stays between Fav and P1.\n\nKeep current Search behavior.\n\nDo NOT change PATCH 002/003 logic.\n\nVisual:\n\nsearch icon left\ninput\ncurrent underline / current approved shell\n\nUse full internal Home-container width.\n\nSearch must not create an extra giant empty area.\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH ANIMATION\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 004 Search animation remains unchanged.\n\nParticle/network animation may render in the Search area\naccording to current implementation.\n\nPATCH 009 must NOT own the particle engine.\n\nParticle engine owners added:\n0\n\n==================================================\n10. P1\n==================================================\n\nP1 remains the SAME functional size as current P1.\n\nDo NOT vertically stretch P1 just because Home container changes.\n\nStyle:\n\ndark section\nrounded 24dp\nsubtle 1dp border\nsame family as reference\n\nTitle:\nP1\nleft aligned.\n\n==================================================\n11. P2\n==================================================\n\nP2 must match P1 exactly.\n\nSame:\n\nheight\npadding\ncorner radius\nborder\nbackground\ngrid geometry\n\nP1 height == P2 height\n\n==================================================\n12. P1/P2 APP GRID\n==================================================\n\nWhen populated:\n\n2 rows x 4 columns\n\n8 slots each.\n\nDo not change:\n\nslot count\nicon resolver\nslot persistence\nlaunch behavior\nPATCH 007 editor behavior\n\n==================================================\n13. P1/P2 EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nWhen P1 or P2 is empty, show:\n\noutline cube / square icon\n\nthen:\n\n\"No apps in this section\"\n\nthen smaller secondary text:\n\n\"Add your favorite apps to access\nthem quickly.\"\n\nKeep centered content.\n\nDo not alter section height.\n\n==================================================\n14. EMPTY STATE STYLE\n==================================================\n\nEmpty icon:\napproximately 28–32dp\n\nPrimary empty text:\nbodyMedium / medium emphasis\n\nSecondary text:\nbodySmall\nonSurfaceVariant\n\nNo giant illustration.\n\nNo card inside card.\n\n==================================================\n15. DOCK OUTSIDE CONTAINER\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nDock must be COMPLETELY OUTSIDE Home container.\n\nStructure:\n\n[ Home container:\n    Fav\n    Search\n    P1\n    P2\n]\n\ngap\n\n[ Dock ]\n\nDock must never be clipped by Home container.\n\n==================================================\n16. HOME → DOCK GAP\n==================================================\n\nUse controlled gap:\n\napproximately 16–20dp\n\nPreferred:\n20dp\n\nNo excessive empty region.\n\n==================================================\n17. DOCK STYLE\n==================================================\n\nDock owns its own background.\n\nColor:\nslightly darker than Home container\n\nPreferred starting token:\n#0A0A0C\n\nCorner radius:\n24dp\n\nBorder:\nsame subtle family\n\nHorizontal width:\naligned visually with Home container\n\nPadding:\n12dp top/bottom\n12–16dp left/right\n\n==================================================\n18. DOCK GRID\n==================================================\n\nDock:\n\n1 row\n5 columns\n\nKeep current 5 slots.\n\nDo not change semantic/default app behavior from PATCH 008.\n\nDo not change PATCH 007 editing.\n\n==================================================\n19. DOCK ICONS\n==================================================\n\nKeep current Dock icon size unless actual clipping requires\na tiny adjustment.\n\nPreferred:\nsame current size.\n\nDo NOT make Dock icons huge.\n\n==================================================\n20. TOTAL HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nCurrent issue:\nHome became too tall.\n\nReduce total vertical footprint.\n\nTarget:\n\nFav + Search + P1 + P2 container\nshould occupy only the required content height.\n\nNo Spacer(weight()) that stretches Home vertically.\n\nNo fillMaxHeight() for the Home module.\n\nAvoid:\n\nheightIn(min = huge)\nweight(1f)\nfull-screen Column expansion\n\nunless strictly necessary.\n\n==================================================\n21. REAL MEASURED LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nUse wrap-content / measured section heights.\n\nPreferred concept:\n\nHomeContainer\n    wrapContentHeight()\n\nFav:\nfixed/tuned height\n\nSearch:\ncurrent fixed height\n\nP1:\ncurrent approved fixed height\n\nP2:\nsame as P1\n\nDock:\ncurrent compact height\n\n==================================================\n22. NO FULL DISPLAY PANEL\n==================================================\n\nHome container must NOT look like a fullscreen sheet.\n\nExpected wallpaper remains clearly visible:\n\nabove Home\nleft/right margins\nbetween Home and Dock where applicable\nbelow Dock/navigation area\n\n==================================================\n23. COLOR CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nUse a consistent hierarchy:\n\nFav / P1 / P2:\ndark surface family\n\nHome outer container:\ndark base\n\nDock:\nslightly darker\n\nNo bright surfaces.\n\nNo large transparency changes.\n\nKeep existing visual language.\n\n==================================================\n24. CORNER CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nUse consistent corner family.\n\nHome outer:\n24dp\n\nFav:\n24dp\n\nP1:\n24dp\n\nP2:\n24dp\n\nDock:\n24dp\n\nDo not create random radii.\n\n==================================================\n25. BORDER CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nUse subtle consistent border:\n\n~1dp\n\nSame visual family across:\n\nHome container\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nDo not use thick outlines.\n\n==================================================\n26. SEARCH COLLAPSED / EXPANDED\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change Search behavior.\n\nPATCH 009 changes visual container/layout only.\n\nUP/DOWN:\nPATCH 002 remains owner.\n\nSearch engine:\nPATCH 003 remains owner.\n\nSearch animation:\nPATCH 004 remains owner.\n\n==================================================\n27. P1 / P2 POSITION\n==================================================\n\nDo not redesign their functional geometry.\n\nTarget:\n\nP1 movement caused by Search interaction:\n0dp relative to its approved anchored behavior\n\nP2:\nsame existing behavior\n\nPATCH 009 must not add motion ownership.\n\n==================================================\n28. DOCK POSITION\n==================================================\n\nDock does not join Search expansion.\n\nDock movement from PATCH 009:\n0dp during Search gesture.\n\nDock remains independently placed below Home container.\n\n==================================================\n29. TOUCH SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nDo not add new input layer.\n\nNew gesture owners:\n0\n\nP1 first tap:\nPASS\n\nP2 first tap:\nPASS\n\nDock first tap:\nPASS\n\nSettings icon:\nPASS\n\nSearch field:\nPASS\n\nLong press slot editor:\nPASS\n\n==================================================\n30. PATCH OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 009 owns ONLY:\n\n- Home UI V2 container composition\n- section spacing\n- visual section surfaces\n- empty-state presentation\n- Dock external placement\n\nPATCH 009 does NOT own:\n\ngestures\nSearch logic\nSearch animation\nSettings\nslot editing\nUsageStats\nslot persistence\nAppCatalog\n\n==================================================\n31. CORE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nHomeSnapshot owner:\nUNCHANGED\n\nAppCatalog owner:\nUNCHANGED\n\nLauncherPreferences:\nUNCHANGED\n\nLauncherActions:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP1 = 8\nP2 = 8\nDock = 5\n\n==================================================\n32. PATCH 001–008 LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo not modify behavior of:\n\n001_sensitive_home\n002_search_reveal\n003_search_engine\n004_search_animation\n005_settings_visual\n006_settings_functional\n007_slot_editor\n008_first_install\n\nIf a visual integration hook is required:\nkeep it minimal and document it.\n\n==================================================\n33. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nRequired:\n\nnew gesture owners = 0\nnew persistence = 0\nnew AppCatalog owners = 0\nnew HomeSnapshot owners = 0\nnew lifecycle owners = 0\nduplicate slot state = 0\n\n==================================================\n34. DEVICE TARGET\n==================================================\n\nExpected visual order:\n\nFav. apps\n↓ 16dp\n\nSearch\n↓ 16dp\n\nP1\n↓ 16dp\n\nP2\n\nEND HOME CONTAINER\n\n↓ 20dp\n\nDock\n\nDock is NOT inside Home container.\n\n==================================================\n35. STATIC GEOMETRY REPORT\n==================================================\n\nReport:\n\nHome container width\nHome container height\n\nFav height\nSearch height\nP1 height\nP2 height\nDock height\n\nFav → Search gap\nSearch → P1 gap\nP1 → P2 gap\nHome → Dock gap\n\nRequired:\n\nP1 height == P2 height\n\nDock inside Home container:\nNO\n\n==================================================\n36. EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nP1 empty:\nicon + text visible\n\nP2 empty:\nicon + text visible\n\nDock empty:\ndo NOT add P1/P2-style empty message unless already required.\n\nKeep Dock compact even if empty.\n\n==================================================\n37. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nSUCCESS\n\nSnapshot:\nPASS\n\nSHA-256:\nPASS\n\n==================================================\n38. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nPATCH_009_HOME_UI_V2.md\n\nDocument:\n\n- visual reference contract\n- Home container membership\n- Dock external placement\n- dimensions\n- gap tokens\n- colors\n- borders\n- radii\n- empty state\n- patch dependencies\n- rollback\n\n==================================================\n39. STATUS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT mark validated automatically.\n\nAfter build:\n\nPATCH STATUS:\nIMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\nDevice validation required.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA PATCH 009 HOME UI V2 COMPLETE\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPATCH 001–008 behavior modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHome container width:\n<dp/%>\n\nHome container height:\n<dp>\n\nFav height:\n<dp>\n\nSearch height:\n<dp>\n\nP1 height:\n<dp>\n\nP2 height:\n<dp>\n\nDock height:\n<dp>\n\nP1 == P2 height:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFav → Search gap:\n<dp>\n\nSearch → P1 gap:\n<dp>\n\nP1 → P2 gap:\n<dp>\n\nHome → Dock gap:\n<dp>\n\nHome corner radius:\n<dp>\n\nFav corner radius:\n<dp>\n\nP1 corner radius:\n<dp>\n\nP2 corner radius:\n<dp>\n\nDock corner radius:\n<dp>\n\nDock inside Home container:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock has independent background:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHome fills full display:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1 empty state:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP2 empty state:\n<YES/NO>\n\nNew gesture owners:\n<n>\n\nNew persistence:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot owners added:\n<n>\n\nAppCatalog owners added:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nSearch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nSlot-editor regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH STATUS:\n<IMPLEMENTED_VALIDATION_REQUIRED/FAILED>\n\nPatch doc:\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/PATCH_009_HOME_UI_V2.md"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:334:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787249329,"text":"MACHINA V3 — CORE/UI DECOUPLING MIGRATION\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/Machina\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRetire the current PATCH 00x runtime architecture.\n\nReassemble Machina using:\n\nCORE V3\n+\nUI V3\n+\nindependent feature modules\n\nThe old PATCH 001–009 model must no longer be the runtime\narchitecture after migration.\n\n==================================================\n0. BACKUP GATE\n==================================================\n\nBEFORE MODIFYING SOURCE:\n\nRun current build:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\nThen create:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint pre-core-v3-ui-v3-migration\n\nIf checkpoint fails:\nSTOP.\n\nRecord exact checkpoint path.\n\n==================================================\n1. DO NOT DELETE OLD PATCHES YET\n==================================================\n\nMove existing normalized patch sources out of active runtime.\n\nCurrent:\n\npatches/\n  001_sensitive_home\n  002_search_reveal\n  003_search_engine\n  004_search_animation\n  005_settings_visual\n  006_settings_functional\n  007_slot_editor\n  008_first_install\n  009... if present\n\nArchive under:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/archive/legacy_patches_v2/\n\nPreserve:\n\n- source\n- docs\n- status\n- historical checkpoints\n\nDo NOT compile archived patch sources.\n\nDo NOT permanently delete them during this migration.\n\n==================================================\n2. CORE V3\n==================================================\n\nCreate a clean Core V3 namespace.\n\nPreferred structure:\n\napp/src/main/java/it/gaetano/machinahome/core/v3/\n\nCore V3 must contain NO UI presentation logic.\n\n==================================================\n3. CORE V3 — APPCATALOG\n==================================================\n\nOne AppCatalog owner.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- launchable apps snapshot\n- label/package metadata\n- stable catalog access\n\nNo Compose UI.\n\nNo layout dimensions.\n\nNo color/radius/spacing.\n\n==================================================\n4. CORE V3 — HOMESNAPSHOT\n==================================================\n\nOne immutable Home state model.\n\nHard contract:\n\nP1 = 8 slots\nP2 = 8 slots\nDock = 5 slots\n\nConceptually:\n\nHomeSnapshot(\n    p1,\n    p2,\n    dock\n)\n\nNo UI coordinates.\n\nNo dp.\n\nNo animation state.\n\n==================================================\n5. CORE V3 — SLOT REPOSITORY\n==================================================\n\nOne persistence owner.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- load slot assignments\n- write one slot\n- clear one slot\n- first-install initialization state\n\nNo duplicate SharedPreferences/DataStore owners.\n\nUI never writes storage directly.\n\n==================================================\n6. CORE V3 — LAUNCHER ACTIONS\n==================================================\n\nOne action owner for:\n\n- launch app\n- open App info\n- supported external/system intents\n\nSafe error handling:\n\nActivityNotFoundException\nSecurityException\nuninstalled package\n\n==================================================\n7. CORE V3 — APP VISUALS\n==================================================\n\nOne app icon resolver/cache.\n\nUsed by:\n\nHome\nSearch\nApp Picker\n\nNo duplicate icon resolver.\n\n==================================================\n8. CORE V3 — DEFAULT APPS\n==================================================\n\nOne:\n\nDefaultAppsResolver\n\nResolve semantic Dock:\n\nDock[0] Phone\nDock[1] Messages\nDock[2] Browser\nDock[3] Music\nDock[4] Mail\n\nUse public Android APIs only.\n\nNo hardcoded app package names.\n\nIf semantic default cannot be reliably resolved:\n\nslot = empty\n\n==================================================\n9. CORE V3 — FIRST INSTALL\n==================================================\n\nOne:\n\nFirstInstallInitializer\n\nDock:\nsemantic defaults\n\nP1:\ntop 8 eligible usage-ranked apps\n\nP2:\nnext 8 eligible usage-ranked apps\n\nExclude Dock packages.\n\nUsageStats:\nfirst setup only.\n\nNo continuous monitoring.\n\nNo automatic later reorder.\n\n==================================================\n10. UI V3 ROOT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\napp/src/main/java/it/gaetano/machinahome/ui/v3/\n\nUI V3 consumes Core V3 state.\n\nUI V3 must never own slot persistence.\n\n==================================================\n11. HOME UI V3\n==================================================\n\nCreate a clean Home module.\n\nTarget visual hierarchy:\n\nHOME CONTAINER\n├── Fav\n├── SearchArea\n├── P1\n└── P2\n\nOUTSIDE:\nDock\n\nThis is authoritative.\n\n==================================================\n12. HOME CONTAINER\n==================================================\n\nHome container:\n\n- centered\n- compact\n- content-driven height\n- not fullscreen\n- wallpaper visible around it\n\nVisual family based on approved reference.\n\nRecommended baseline:\n\nwidth:\n~88–90%\n\ncorner:\n24dp\n\nouter padding:\n16dp\n\nsection gap:\n12–16dp\n\ndark surface\nsubtle border\n\n==================================================\n13. FAV UI\n==================================================\n\nFav owns presentation only:\n\n- title\n- count\n- Settings icon\n- rounded surface\n- visual background\n\nNo app-data persistence.\n\nNo Search engine.\n\n==================================================\n14. SEARCH AREA UI\n==================================================\n\nSearch area is a UI V3 region.\n\nCollapsed:\n\nheight = 0/minimal\n\nExpanded:\n\ncreates extra area ABOVE P1.\n\nInside expanded SearchArea:\n\nParticle/results area\nSearchBar\n\nSearchBar is at bottom of SearchArea.\n\nP1/P2/Dock remain anchored.\n\n==================================================\n15. SEARCH REVEAL\n==================================================\n\nMove vertical reveal behavior into one UI V3 interaction controller.\n\nUP:\nexpand SearchArea\n\nDOWN:\ncollapse SearchArea\n\nLEFT/RIGHT:\ndo not mutate Search state.\n\nNo old PATCH002 dependency.\n\n==================================================\n16. HOME INTERACTION\n==================================================\n\nMove approved LEFT/RIGHT Material interaction into one V3\nHome interaction module.\n\nPreserve current device-approved behavior.\n\nNo edge Back arrow.\n\nNo duplicate gesture owner.\n\n==================================================\n17. SEARCH ENGINE FEATURE\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nfeatures/search/\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- query processing\n- AppCatalog filtering\n- ranking\n- results\n- history max 3 MEMORY_ONLY\n- optional system/web actions later\n\nNo Search geometry.\n\nNo particle drawing.\n\n==================================================\n18. SEARCH HISTORY\n==================================================\n\nHistory:\n\nmax 3\nmemory only\n\nNo persistence.\n\nProcess death:\nhistory clears.\n\nNo keep-alive.\n\n==================================================\n19. PARTICLE NETWORK FEATURE\n==================================================\n\nCreate one reusable:\n\nAnimatedParticleNetwork\n\nunder:\n\nui/v3/components/\nor\nfeatures/particles/\n\nOne engine.\n\nParameters may differ between:\n\nSearch\nSettings\n\nNo duplicate implementation.\n\n==================================================\n20. SEARCH PARTICLES\n==================================================\n\nSearch particle Canvas fills:\n\nFav/Search upper boundary\nto\nSearchBar top\n\nOnly while Search expanded.\n\nNo touch interception.\n\n==================================================\n21. P1 / P2 UI\n==================================================\n\nP1 and P2:\n\nsame dimensions\n\n8 slots each\n\n2 x 4\n\nsame:\n\nradius\nborder\nbackground\npadding\nicon geometry\n\nEmpty state:\n\nsmall outline cube\n\"No apps in this section\"\n\"Add your favorite apps to access them quickly.\"\n\n==================================================\n22. DOCK UI\n==================================================\n\nDock:\n\nOUTSIDE Home container.\n\n5 slots.\n\nIndependent:\n\nbackground\nborder\ncorner radius\npadding\n\nSlightly darker than Home surfaces.\n\nNo Home container clipping.\n\n==================================================\n23. APP PICKER\n==================================================\n\nCreate UI V3 AppPicker.\n\nOne shared picker for:\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nSlot editing belongs to feature:\n\nfeatures/slot_editor/\n\nLong press:\nopen picker\n\nNormal tap:\nlaunch app\n\n==================================================\n24. SETTINGS UI V3\n==================================================\n\nCreate Settings independent from Home Core.\n\nPreserve approved visual language:\n\n- legacy recovered icons\n- system typography\n- Dynamic Color\n- particle animation\n- compact presentation\n\nNo PATCH numbering in normal user UI.\n\n==================================================\n25. SETTINGS FUNCTIONALITY\n==================================================\n\nSeparate:\n\nfeatures/settings/\n\nOne preference owner.\n\nOnly real settings.\n\nExamples:\n\nhapticEnabled\ndynamicColorEnabled\nsearchAutoKeyboard\niconShape if supported\n\nSystem actions:\n\nDefault Home\nApp info\n\nAbout:\n\nVersion\nChangelog\n\n==================================================\n26. HAPTIC V3\n==================================================\n\nOne semantic haptic service/API.\n\nPrefer:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(...)\n\nGlobal Machina setting:\n\nhapticEnabled\n\nNo raw vibrator paths unless absolutely required.\n\nNo MOVE haptic.\n\n==================================================\n27. STATE OWNERSHIP TARGET\n==================================================\n\nRequired after migration:\n\nAppCatalog owners = 1\n\nHomeSnapshot owners = 1\n\nslot persistence owners = 1\n\napp visual/icon owners = 1\n\nSearch query owners = 1\n\nSearch history owners = 1\n\nHome gesture owners = 1\n\nSearch reveal owners = 1\n\nparticle engines = 1\n\nSettings preference owners = 1\n\n==================================================\n28. NO PATCH 00x RUNTIME\n==================================================\n\nAfter migration:\n\nactive runtime references to:\n\npatches.001...\npatches.002...\n...\npatches.009...\n\nmust be:\n\n0\n\nOld patch code may exist only under archive/history.\n\n==================================================\n29. MAINACTIVITY\n==================================================\n\nMainActivity must become thin.\n\nPreferred:\n\nsetContent {\n    MachinaAppV3(...)\n}\n\nDo not place:\n\nslot logic\nSearch engine\nUsageStats\nSettings backend\n\ninside MainActivity.\n\n==================================================\n30. DEPENDENCY DIRECTION\n==================================================\n\nRequired direction:\n\nUI\n↓\nfeatures/controllers\n↓\nCore V3\n\nCore V3 must never depend on UI V3.\n\nNo circular dependency.\n\n==================================================\n31. V2 DATA MIGRATION\n==================================================\n\nPreserve existing user slot assignments where possible.\n\nCore V3 must read/migrate existing slot persistence.\n\nDo NOT reset existing P1/P2/Dock during V3 upgrade.\n\nFirstInstallInitializer must not run against an established layout.\n\n==================================================\n32. VISUAL BASELINE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT reproduce the rejected PATCH009 screenshot.\n\nUse the approved Home reference as visual guidance.\n\nHard rules:\n\n- compact Home\n- wallpaper visible\n- P1/P2 equal size\n- Dock external\n- Search expanded above P1\n- no fullscreen Home panel\n\n==================================================\n33. CODE SECURITY\n==================================================\n\nApply:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/docs/\nMACHINA_PATCH_CODE_SECURITY_POLICY.md\n\nVerify:\n\nduplicate owners = 0\nCore UI imports = 0\nUI persistence writes = 0\ncontinuous UsageStats monitoring = 0\nnew keep-alive = 0\nfirst-touch blockers = 0\ncircular dependencies = 0\n\n==================================================\n34. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\ndocs/CORE_V3.md\ndocs/UI_V3.md\ndocs/MACHINA_V3_ARCHITECTURE.md\ndocs/V2_TO_V3_MIGRATION.md\n\nArchive old:\n\nPATCH_STATUS.md\n\nas historical V2 status if appropriate.\n\nCreate:\n\ndocs/V3_STATUS.md\n\n==================================================\n35. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n36. STATIC AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nactive PATCH00x runtime references = 0\n\nCore V3 Compose UI imports = 0\n\nUI direct persistence writes = 0\n\nAppCatalog owners = 1\n\nHomeSnapshot owners = 1\n\nslot persistence owners = 1\n\nparticle engines = 1\n\nSettings preference owners = 1\n\ngesture conflicts = 0\n\ncircular dependencies = 0\n\n==================================================\n37. DEVICE STATUS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT delete archived V2 yet.\n\nDo NOT mark V3 frozen automatically.\n\nStatus after build:\n\nV3_DEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\n==================================================\n38. POST DEVICE VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nAfter Pixel passes:\n\n- Home\n- Search\n- particles\n- Settings\n- Slot Editor\n- first-install logic\n- persistence migration\n\ncreate:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint core-v3-ui-v3-validated\n\nThen:\n\nCORE V3 = FROZEN\nUI V3 = BASELINE_FROZEN\n\nOnly after that may legacy V2 patch source be permanently removed.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA V3 MIGRATION COMPLETE\n\nPRE-V3 checkpoint:\n<path>\n\nLegacy patches archived:\n<n>\n\nActive PATCH00x runtime references:\n<n>\n\nCore V3 files:\n<n>\n\nUI V3 files:\n<n>\n\nFeature modules:\n<list>\n\nCore V3 Compose UI imports:\n<n>\n\nAppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot owners:\n<n>\n\nSlot persistence owners:\n<n>\n\nIcon resolver owners:\n<n>\n\nHome gesture owners:\n<n>\n\nSearch reveal owners:\n<n>\n\nQuery owners:\n<n>\n\nHistory owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nSettings preference owners:\n<n>\n\nExisting V2 slot data preserved:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFirst-install rerun on existing layout:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCircular dependencies:\n<n>\n\nCore modified from V2 semantics:\n<NO/YES + explanation>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nV3 STATUS:\n<V3_DEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED/FAILED>\n\nRollback checkpoint:\n<path>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:335:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787250289,"text":"FASE: MACHINA V3 — PARALLEL CORE + UI REBUILD\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nCURRENT STATE:\nV3 shell visible on device but incomplete.\n\nDEVICE SYMPTOMS:\n\n- Fav visible\n- P1/P2 empty-state visible\n- Dock surface visible but empty\n- Search not present\n- old/runtime feature wiring incomplete\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nBuild Core V3 and UI V3 in PARALLEL,\nwithout deleting working V2 sources yet.\n\nDo not patch the current incomplete UI incrementally.\n\nCreate a clean V3 runtime path.\n\n==================================================\n0. BACKUP\n==================================================\n\nBefore source changes:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nthen:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint pre-v3-parallel-rebuild\n\nIf build/checkpoint fails:\nSTOP.\n\n==================================================\n1. KEEP LEGACY V2 FOR NOW\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT delete current:\n\ncore V2\npatches legacy\nold Home UI\nold Search\nold Settings\nold Slot Editor\n\nThey remain rollback/reference only.\n\nBut V3 must not depend on their presentation code.\n\n==================================================\n2. NEW CORE V3 ROOT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\napp/src/main/java/it/gaetano/machinahome/core/v3/\n\nSuggested modules:\n\nAppCatalogV3.kt\nHomeSnapshotV3.kt\nSlotRepositoryV3.kt\nLauncherActionsV3.kt\nAppVisualsV3.kt\nDefaultAppsResolverV3.kt\nFirstInstallInitializerV3.kt\n\n==================================================\n3. CORE V3 RULE\n==================================================\n\nCore V3 contains:\n\nDATA\nSTATE\nPERSISTENCE\nACTIONS\n\nCore V3 contains NO:\n\nCompose layout\ndp\npadding\ncolors\nradii\nSearch geometry\nparticles\nSettings UI\nDock position\nFav position\n\n==================================================\n4. HOME SNAPSHOT V3\n==================================================\n\nHard contract:\n\nP1 = 8\nP2 = 8\nDock = 5\n\nOne immutable source of truth.\n\nExisting persisted slot data must be migrated/read.\n\nDo not reset current user assignments.\n\n==================================================\n5. SLOT REPOSITORY V3\n==================================================\n\nOne persistence owner.\n\nMust support:\n\nread P1/P2/Dock\nwrite one slot\nclear one slot\nread first-install completion\n\nNo duplicate preference backend.\n\n==================================================\n6. APP CATALOG V3\n==================================================\n\nOne app catalog owner.\n\nExpose launchable apps to:\n\nHome\nSearch\nApp Picker\nFirst Install\n\nNo separate scanners.\n\n==================================================\n7. APP VISUALS V3\n==================================================\n\nOne icon resolver/cache.\n\nUsed by:\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\nSearch results\nApp Picker\n\n==================================================\n8. NEW UI V3 ROOT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\napp/src/main/java/it/gaetano/machinahome/ui/v3/\n\nSuggested:\n\nMachinaHomeV3.kt\nFavSectionV3.kt\nSearchAreaV3.kt\nPanelSectionV3.kt\nDockV3.kt\nEmptyStateV3.kt\nHomeInteractionV3.kt\n\n==================================================\n9. AUTHORITATIVE HOME STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nUI V3 must render:\n\n[ HOME CONTAINER\n    Fav\n    SearchArea\n    P1\n    P2\n]\n\ngap\n\n[ Dock ]\n\nDock is outside Home container.\n\n==================================================\n10. COLLAPSED HOME\n==================================================\n\nCollapsed:\n\nFav\nsmall normal gap\nP1\nsmall normal gap\nP2\n\nSearchArea footprint:\n0/minimal\n\nDock stays below outside container.\n\n==================================================\n11. EXPANDED SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nExpanded:\n\nFav\nlarge SearchArea\n    particle animation\n    results/history\n    SearchBar at bottom\nP1\nP2\n\nDock outside.\n\nCritical:\n\nP1 movement = 0dp\nP2 movement = 0dp\nDock movement = 0dp\n\nExpansion is taken from upper available space.\n\n==================================================\n12. SEARCH BAR\n==================================================\n\nRestore actual Search UI:\n\nmagnifier left\nsingle underline\nquery input\ncursor\nIME\n\nNo pill.\n\nNo filled card unless existing approved design explicitly requires it.\n\n==================================================\n13. SEARCH ENGINE V3\n==================================================\n\nReuse logic conceptually from old Search engine,\nbut connect to V3 contracts.\n\nMust support:\n\napp search\nexact/prefix/contains ranking\nhistory max 3 MEMORY_ONLY\nresults above SearchBar\n\nNo dependency on old PATCH003 package path.\n\n==================================================\n14. PARTICLE NETWORK V3\n==================================================\n\nOne shared engine.\n\nSearch:\nfills full SearchArea.\n\nSettings:\nuses same engine with different visual parameters.\n\nNo duplicate particle implementation.\n\n==================================================\n15. P1/P2\n==================================================\n\nP1/P2:\n\nequal height\n2 x 4 slots\n8 each\n\nIf populated:\nshow icons.\n\nIf empty:\nshow small cube icon +\n\"No apps in this section\" +\nsecondary line.\n\n==================================================\n16. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock:\n\noutside Home container\n5 slots\nown dark background\nrounded corners\ncompact height\n\nIf persisted assignments exist:\nshow them.\n\nIf first-install setup not complete:\nFirstInstallInitializerV3 may populate.\n\n==================================================\n17. FIRST INSTALL V3\n==================================================\n\nDock semantic:\n\n0 Phone\n1 Messages\n2 Browser\n3 Music\n4 Mail\n\nP1:\ntop 8 usage-ranked apps excluding Dock\n\nP2:\nnext 8\n\nNever rerun after established layout.\n\n==================================================\n18. SLOT EDITOR V3\n==================================================\n\nLong press slot:\nopen App Picker.\n\nNormal tap:\nlaunch app.\n\nReuse Core V3 SlotRepository.\n\n==================================================\n19. SETTINGS V3\n==================================================\n\nKeep approved Settings visual.\n\nWire against V3 preference/state APIs.\n\nNo dependency on patch numbering.\n\n==================================================\n20. MAINACTIVITY CUTOVER\n==================================================\n\nMainActivity must have one V3 entry path:\n\nsetContent {\n    MachinaAppV3(...)\n}\n\nDo not run V2 and V3 Home simultaneously.\n\nV2 code remains on disk only until validation.\n\n==================================================\n21. V3 RUNTIME REFERENCES\n==================================================\n\nAfter cutover:\n\nactive references from V3 Home to old:\n\npatches/001...\npatches/002...\n...\npatches/009...\n\nmust be:\n0\n\nLegacy code may remain compiled only if necessary temporarily,\nbut should not be runtime owner.\n\nPreferred:\nexclude/archive after device validation.\n\n==================================================\n22. DEVICE TARGET\n==================================================\n\nOn Pixel V3 must show:\n\n- Fav\n- functional Search\n- P1 populated if data exists\n- P2 populated if data exists\n- Dock populated if data exists\n- same wallpaper\n- compact centered Home\n- Dock external\n- P1/P2 equal size\n\nThe current empty skeleton is NOT acceptable.\n\n==================================================\n23. STATIC OWNERSHIP TARGET\n==================================================\n\nAppCatalog owners = 1\nHomeSnapshot owners = 1\nSlotRepository owners = 1\nIcon resolver owners = 1\nSearch query owners = 1\nSearch history owners = 1\nParticle engines = 1\nSettings preference owners = 1\nGesture conflicts = 0\n\n==================================================\n24. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n25. DEVICE VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nDo not delete legacy V2 yet.\n\nStatus after build:\n\nV3_PARALLEL_DEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED\n\n==================================================\n26. ONLY AFTER PIXEL PASS\n==================================================\n\nAfter full Pixel validation:\n\nmove legacy active code to:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/archive/v2_retired/\n\nThen remove it from compilation.\n\nCreate checkpoint:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl checkpoint core-v3-ui-v3-baseline\n\nOnly then:\n\nCORE V3 = FROZEN\nUI V3 = BASELINE_FROZEN\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA V3 PARALLEL REBUILD COMPLETE\n\nPRE checkpoint:\n<path>\n\nCore V3 files:\n<n>\n\nUI V3 files:\n<n>\n\nActive V3 Home:\n<YES/NO>\n\nOld V2 Home active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nExisting slot data migrated:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearch restored:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1 data visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP2 data visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock data visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock outside Home:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1 == P2 size:\n<YES/NO>\n\nAppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot owners:\n<n>\n\nSlotRepository owners:\n<n>\n\nIcon resolver owners:\n<n>\n\nSearch query owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nLegacy patch runtime references:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSTATUS:\nV3_PARALLEL_DEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:336:{"session_id":"01a01e67-609e-7143-851f-20a717288c4f","ts":1787252516,"text":"MACHINA HOME UI V3 — IMPLEMENT APPROVED REFERENCE\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/Machina/project\n\nREFERENCE:\n/mnt/data/824.png\n\nARCHITECTURE:\n\nCORE V3 = DATA / STATE / ACTIONS\nHOME UI V3 = PRESENTATION\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nUse the supplied reference image as the AUTHORITATIVE\nvisual target.\n\nDo NOT reproduce the current device skeleton.\nDo NOT restore PATCH009 architecture.\n\nImplement this appearance directly in Home UI V3.\n\n==================================================\n1. HARD ARCHITECTURE BOUNDARY\n==================================================\n\nCORE V3 owns:\n\n- AppCatalog\n- HomeSnapshot\n- P1/P2/Dock slot identities\n- persistence\n- LauncherActions\n- AppVisuals\n\nHOME UI V3 owns:\n\n- position\n- size\n- padding\n- gaps\n- colors\n- borders\n- corner radius\n- surfaces\n- empty states\n- visual hierarchy\n\nCore V3 must contain:\n\n0 dp values\n0 colors\n0 Compose layout\n0 corner-radius values\n0 Home geometry\n\n==================================================\n2. AUTHORITATIVE VISUAL STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nRender:\n\n        HOME CONTAINER\n\n    ┌─────────────────────┐\n    │      Fav. apps      │\n    ├─────────────────────┤\n    │       Search        │\n    ├─────────────────────┤\n    │         P1          │\n    ├─────────────────────┤\n    │         P2          │\n    └─────────────────────┘\n\n             GAP\n\n    ┌─────────────────────┐\n    │        DOCK         │\n    └─────────────────────┘\n\nDock is NOT a child of Home container.\n\n==================================================\n3. HOME POSITION\n==================================================\n\nHome module:\n\ncentered horizontally\n\nWidth target:\n~88–90% available screen width\n\nDo NOT:\n\nfillMaxWidth without outer margins\nfillMaxHeight\nuse fullscreen Surface\nstretch vertically using weight(1f)\n\nWallpaper must remain clearly visible around Home.\n\n==================================================\n4. HOME CONTAINER\n==================================================\n\nOne outer Home container wrapping:\n\nFav\nSearch\nP1\nP2\n\nStyle baseline:\n\nbackground:\n#0F0F11 family\n\nborder:\n1dp subtle dark/light outline\n\ncorner radius:\n24dp\n\ninternal padding:\n16dp\n\ncontent-driven height.\n\n==================================================\n5. INTERNAL SPACING\n==================================================\n\nUse one spacing system.\n\nOuter padding:\n16dp\n\nFav -> Search:\n16dp\n\nSearch -> P1:\n16dp\n\nP1 -> P2:\n12–16dp\n\nNo stacked duplicate Spacer/padding values.\n\n==================================================\n6. FAV APPS\n==================================================\n\nFav header is its own rounded internal surface.\n\nContents:\n\nFav. apps\nApps <count>\n\nSettings icon:\nright aligned\n\nUse approved existing typography.\n\nFav background may contain the existing approved\nvisual/particle treatment.\n\nStyle:\n\ncorner radius:\n24dp\n\nsubtle border\n\nsame dark family as reference.\n\n==================================================\n7. FAV HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference proportions.\n\nFav should be compact but visibly substantial.\n\nDo NOT make it as short as the current skeleton.\n\nDo NOT make it enormous.\n\nUse reference 824.png proportions as source of truth.\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nSearch is directly below Fav.\n\nCollapsed/normal visible shell follows current V3 Search state.\n\nApproved visual:\n\nmagnifier left\ntext/input\nsingle underline where applicable\n\nDo NOT turn Search into a generic oversized Material pill\nunless the existing approved implementation already requires it.\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH EXPANSION\n==================================================\n\nWhen Search is expanded:\n\nadditional Search space belongs BETWEEN:\n\nFav\nand\nSearchBar/P1\n\nUse:\n\nparticle network\nresults/history\nSearchBar\n\nRequired ordering:\n\nFav\n↓\nParticle + Results area\n↓\nSearchBar\n↓\nP1\n↓\nP2\n\n==================================================\n10. SEARCH GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nSearch expansion must NOT resize:\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nP1 height delta:\n0dp\n\nP2 height delta:\n0dp\n\nDock height delta:\n0dp\n\nThe upper region expands/repositions as required.\n\n==================================================\n11. P1\n==================================================\n\nP1 is an independent rounded surface INSIDE Home container.\n\nSlots:\n8\n\nGrid:\n4 columns x 2 rows\n\nStyle:\n\ncorner radius:\n24dp\n\nsubtle border\n\ndark surface\n\ninternal padding:\n12dp\n\nDo NOT merge P1 visually with P2.\n\n==================================================\n12. P2\n==================================================\n\nSame contract as P1.\n\nSlots:\n8\n\nGrid:\n4 x 2\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nP1 height == P2 height\n\nP1 width == P2 width\n\nsame:\nbackground\nborder\nradius\npadding\nicon geometry\n\n==================================================\n13. EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nIf P1/P2 contains no assigned apps:\n\nshow centered:\n\nsmall outline cube icon\n\n\"No apps in this section\"\n\n\"Add your favorite apps to access\nthem quickly.\"\n\nUse reference visual hierarchy.\n\nCube:\n~28–32dp\n\nPrimary:\nbodyMedium / medium emphasis\n\nSecondary:\nbodySmall / onSurfaceVariant\n\nNo giant empty-state illustration.\n\n==================================================\n14. POPULATED STATE\n==================================================\n\nWhen slot data exists:\n\nREMOVE empty-state content completely.\n\nRender actual Core V3 slot icons.\n\nDo not show:\n\nApps 0-style placeholder\nempty-state text\ncube\n\nbehind populated grid.\n\n==================================================\n15. DOCK — CRITICAL\n==================================================\n\nDock is completely OUTSIDE Home container.\n\nHierarchy must prove:\n\nHomeContainer(...)\nDock(...)\n\nNOT:\n\nHomeContainer {\n    Dock(...)\n}\n\n==================================================\n16. DOCK POSITION\n==================================================\n\nHome container bottom\n↓\n20dp approximately\n↓\nDock\n\nDock centered horizontally.\n\nWidth:\nsame visual family as Home container.\n\nDo not attach Dock to navigation bar.\n\n==================================================\n17. DOCK STYLE\n==================================================\n\nIndependent background.\n\nSlightly darker than Home container.\n\nStarting family:\n#0A0A0C\n\nCorner radius:\n24dp\n\nBorder:\nsubtle 1dp\n\nPadding:\n~12dp\n\nSlots:\n5\n\nOne row.\n\n==================================================\n18. DOCK DATA\n==================================================\n\nDock consumes Core V3 slot state.\n\nIf Core contains assignments:\nicons MUST appear.\n\nDo NOT render an empty black Dock merely because\nfirst-install initialization has not run.\n\nExisting persisted assignments take priority.\n\n==================================================\n19. APP ICONS\n==================================================\n\nAll:\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nuse ONE AppVisualsV3 resolver.\n\nNo separate drawable loading.\n\nNo duplicate icon cache.\n\n==================================================\n20. TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nNormal icon tap:\nLauncherActionsV3\n\nLong press:\nSlotEditor V3\n\nSettings gear:\nSettings V3\n\nSearch:\nSearch V3\n\nNo presentation layer owns persistence.\n\n==================================================\n21. STATUS / NAVIGATION BARS\n==================================================\n\nWallpaper may draw edge-to-edge.\n\nHome content respects safe usable bounds.\n\nDo not position Home under status bar.\n\nDo not position Dock over gesture/navigation indicator.\n\n==================================================\n22. HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nThe reference is compact.\n\nDo NOT stretch Home vertically to consume available screen.\n\nUse measured/content-driven heights.\n\nWallpaper should remain visible:\n\nabove Home\nleft/right\nbetween Home and Dock\nbelow Dock\n\n==================================================\n23. COLORS\n==================================================\n\nReference hierarchy:\n\nwallpaper\n→ dark outer Home\n→ slightly differentiated internal panels\n→ darker external Dock\n\nAvoid:\n\nlight gray\nMaterial default cards\nopaque fullscreen background\n\n==================================================\n24. CORNERS\n==================================================\n\nUse one visual family.\n\nHome outer:\n24dp\n\nFav:\n24dp\n\nP1:\n24dp\n\nP2:\n24dp\n\nDock:\n24dp\n\nSearch:\nexisting approved shape\n\n==================================================\n25. BORDERS\n==================================================\n\nFav/P1/P2/Dock:\n\nsubtle ~1dp outline.\n\nNo thick border.\n\nNo bright white border.\n\n==================================================\n26. PARTICLES\n==================================================\n\nUse ONE existing V3 particle engine.\n\nFav visual:\nmay use configured visual effect if approved.\n\nSearch expanded:\nparticle network fills Search result area.\n\nSettings:\nsame engine, separate preset.\n\nDo not duplicate engine.\n\n==================================================\n27. DATA / UI SEPARATION\n==================================================\n\nHome UI V3 must receive state conceptually like:\n\nHomeUiState(\n    favCount,\n    p1Slots,\n    p2Slots,\n    dockSlots,\n    searchState\n)\n\nUI must not:\n\nread SharedPreferences\nquery PackageManager\nquery UsageStats\nwrite slots directly\n\n==================================================\n28. REMOVE CURRENT SKELETON PATH\n==================================================\n\nThe current device UI shown before this task is NOT the target.\n\nFind the active V3 skeleton Home implementation.\n\nReplace its presentation with this reference implementation.\n\nDo not leave two competing V3 Home composables active.\n\nActive Home UI owners:\n1\n\n==================================================\n29. OLD PATCH UI\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT call old PATCH009 UI.\n\nDo NOT call old PATCH002 layout.\n\nDo NOT use old Settings/Home visual owners.\n\nV3 may reuse extracted generic components only when\nthey have no patch ownership/state.\n\n==================================================\n30. STATIC ASSERTIONS\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nCore V3 Compose presentation imports:\n0\n\nHome UI persistence writes:\n0\n\nHome UI PackageManager calls:\n0\n\nHome UI UsageStats calls:\n0\n\nHome UI owners:\n1\n\nAppVisuals owners:\n1\n\nDock parent == HomeContainer:\nNO\n\nP1/P2 equal dimensions:\nYES\n\n==================================================\n31. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n32. DEVICE VALIDATION TARGET\n==================================================\n\nOn Pixel verify visually against 824.png:\n\nHOME:\n\n- centered\n- compact\n- correct width\n- wallpaper visible\n\nFAV:\n\n- correct proportions\n- Settings icon\n- count\n\nSEARCH:\n\n- correctly positioned\n- expanded Search works\n\nP1/P2:\n\n- same size\n- rounded\n- bordered\n- actual apps when assigned\n- empty state only when empty\n\nDOCK:\n\n- outside Home\n- independent dark surface\n- actual icons when assigned\n\nNo fullscreen container.\n\n==================================================\n33. DO NOT DELETE V2 YET\n==================================================\n\nAfter implementation:\n\ndo NOT delete archived V2/Core V2.\n\nFirst validate this Home UI V3 on Pixel.\n\nOnly after device PASS can legacy runtime files be removed.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA HOME UI V3 REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION COMPLETE\n\nReference:\n824.png\n\nActive Home UI owners:\n<n>\n\nCore V3 presentation imports:\n<n>\n\nHome width:\n<value>\n\nHome height:\n<value>\n\nFav height:\n<value>\n\nSearch collapsed height:\n<value>\n\nSearch expanded height:\n<value>\n\nP1 size:\n<value>\n\nP2 size:\n<value>\n\nP1 == P2:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock size:\n<value>\n\nDock outside Home:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHome → Dock gap:\n<value>\n\nP1 slot count:\n<n>\n\nP2 slot count:\n<n>\n\nDock slot count:\n<n>\n\nExisting P1 data rendered:\n<YES/NO>\n\nExisting P2 data rendered:\n<YES/NO>\n\nExisting Dock data rendered:\n<YES/NO>\n\nEmpty state conditional:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHome UI persistence writes:\n<n>\n\nHome UI PackageManager calls:\n<n>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nOld PATCH009 UI runtime references:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSTATUS:\nV3_DEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
