===================================\n\nWhen Search is expanded:\n\nadditional Search space belongs BETWEEN:\n\nFav\nand\nSearchBar/P1\n\nUse:\n\nparticle network\nresults/history\nSearchBar\n\nRequired ordering:\n\nFav\n↓\nParticle + Results area\n↓\nSearchBar\n↓\nP1\n↓\nP2\n\n==================================================\n10. SEARCH GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nSearch expansion must NOT resize:\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nP1 height delta:\n0dp\n\nP2 height delta:\n0dp\n\nDock height delta:\n0dp\n\nThe upper region expands/repositions as required.\n\n==================================================\n11. P1\n==================================================\n\nP1 is an independent rounded surface INSIDE Home container.\n\nSlots:\n8\n\nGrid:\n4 columns x 2 rows\n\nStyle:\n\ncorner radius:\n24dp\n\nsubtle border\n\ndark surface\n\ninternal padding:\n12dp\n\nDo NOT merge P1 visually with P2.\n\n==================================================\n12. P2\n==================================================\n\nSame contract as P1.\n\nSlots:\n8\n\nGrid:\n4 x 2\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nP1 height == P2 height\n\nP1 width == P2 width\n\nsame:\nbackground\nborder\nradius\npadding\nicon geometry\n\n==================================================\n13. EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nIf P1/P2 contains no assigned apps:\n\nshow centered:\n\nsmall outline cube icon\n\n\"No apps in this section\"\n\n\"Add your favorite apps to access\nthem quickly.\"\n\nUse reference visual hierarchy.\n\nCube:\n~28–32dp\n\nPrimary:\nbodyMedium / medium emphasis\n\nSecondary:\nbodySmall / onSurfaceVariant\n\nNo giant empty-state illustration.\n\n==================================================\n14. POPULATED STATE\n==================================================\n\nWhen slot data exists:\n\nREMOVE empty-state content completely.\n\nRender actual Core V3 slot icons.\n\nDo not show:\n\nApps 0-style placeholder\nempty-state text\ncube\n\nbehind populated grid.\n\n==================================================\n15. DOCK — CRITICAL\n==================================================\n\nDock is completely OUTSIDE Home container.\n\nHierarchy must prove:\n\nHomeContainer(...)\nDock(...)\n\nNOT:\n\nHomeContainer {\n    Dock(...)\n}\n\n==================================================\n16. DOCK POSITION\n==================================================\n\nHome container bottom\n↓\n20dp approximately\n↓\nDock\n\nDock centered horizontally.\n\nWidth:\nsame visual family as Home container.\n\nDo not attach Dock to navigation bar.\n\n==================================================\n17. DOCK STYLE\n==================================================\n\nIndependent background.\n\nSlightly darker than Home container.\n\nStarting family:\n#0A0A0C\n\nCorner radius:\n24dp\n\nBorder:\nsubtle 1dp\n\nPadding:\n~12dp\n\nSlots:\n5\n\nOne row.\n\n==================================================\n18. DOCK DATA\n==================================================\n\nDock consumes Core V3 slot state.\n\nIf Core contains assignments:\nicons MUST appear.\n\nDo NOT render an empty black Dock merely because\nfirst-install initialization has not run.\n\nExisting persisted assignments take priority.\n\n==================================================\n19. APP ICONS\n==================================================\n\nAll:\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nuse ONE AppVisualsV3 resolver.\n\nNo separate drawable loading.\n\nNo duplicate icon cache.\n\n==================================================\n20. TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nNormal icon tap:\nLauncherActionsV3\n\nLong press:\nSlotEditor V3\n\nSettings gear:\nSettings V3\n\nSearch:\nSearch V3\n\nNo presentation layer owns persistence.\n\n==================================================\n21. STATUS / NAVIGATION BARS\n==================================================\n\nWallpaper may draw edge-to-edge.\n\nHome content respects safe usable bounds.\n\nDo not position Home under status bar.\n\nDo not position Dock over gesture/navigation indicator.\n\n==================================================\n22. HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nThe reference is compact.\n\nDo NOT stretch Home vertically to consume available screen.\n\nUse measured/content-driven heights.\n\nWallpaper should remain visible:\n\nabove Home\nleft/right\nbetween Home and Dock\nbelow Dock\n\n==================================================\n23. COLORS\n==================================================\n\nReference hierarchy:\n\nwallpaper\n→ dark outer Home\n→ slightly differentiated internal panels\n→ darker external Dock\n\nAvoid:\n\nlight gray\nMaterial default cards\nopaque fullscreen background\n\n==================================================\n24. CORNERS\n==================================================\n\nUse one visual family.\n\nHome outer:\n24dp\n\nFav:\n24dp\n\nP1:\n24dp\n\nP2:\n24dp\n\nDock:\n24dp\n\nSearch:\nexisting approved shape\n\n==================================================\n25. BORDERS\n==================================================\n\nFav/P1/P2/Dock:\n\nsubtle ~1dp outline.\n\nNo thick border.\n\nNo bright white border.\n\n==================================================\n26. PARTICLES\n==================================================\n\nUse ONE existing V3 particle engine.\n\nFav visual:\nmay use configured visual effect if approved.\n\nSearch expanded:\nparticle network fills Search result area.\n\nSettings:\nsame engine, separate preset.\n\nDo not duplicate engine.\n\n==================================================\n27. DATA / UI SEPARATION\n==================================================\n\nHome UI V3 must receive state conceptually like:\n\nHomeUiState(\n    favCount,\n    p1Slots,\n    p2Slots,\n    dockSlots,\n    searchState\n)\n\nUI must not:\n\nread SharedPreferences\nquery PackageManager\nquery UsageStats\nwrite slots directly\n\n==================================================\n28. REMOVE CURRENT SKELETON PATH\n==================================================\n\nThe current device UI shown before this task is NOT the target.\n\nFind the active V3 skeleton Home implementation.\n\nReplace its presentation with this reference implementation.\n\nDo not leave two competing V3 Home composables active.\n\nActive Home UI owners:\n1\n\n==================================================\n29. OLD PATCH UI\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT call old PATCH009 UI.\n\nDo NOT call old PATCH002 layout.\n\nDo NOT use old Settings/Home visual owners.\n\nV3 may reuse extracted generic components only when\nthey have no patch ownership/state.\n\n==================================================\n30. STATIC ASSERTIONS\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nCore V3 Compose presentation imports:\n0\n\nHome UI persistence writes:\n0\n\nHome UI PackageManager calls:\n0\n\nHome UI UsageStats calls:\n0\n\nHome UI owners:\n1\n\nAppVisuals owners:\n1\n\nDock parent == HomeContainer:\nNO\n\nP1/P2 equal dimensions:\nYES\n\n==================================================\n31. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/Machina/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n32. DEVICE VALIDATION TARGET\n==================================================\n\nOn Pixel verify visually against 824.png:\n\nHOME:\n\n- centered\n- compact\n- correct width\n- wallpaper visible\n\nFAV:\n\n- correct proportions\n- Settings icon\n- count\n\nSEARCH:\n\n- correctly positioned\n- expanded Search works\n\nP1/P2:\n\n- same size\n- rounded\n- bordered\n- actual apps when assigned\n- empty state only when empty\n\nDOCK:\n\n- outside Home\n- independent dark surface\n- actual icons when assigned\n\nNo fullscreen container.\n\n==================================================\n33. DO NOT DELETE V2 YET\n==================================================\n\nAfter implementation:\n\ndo NOT delete archived V2/Core V2.\n\nFirst validate this Home UI V3 on Pixel.\n\nOnly after device PASS can legacy runtime files be removed.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nMACHINA HOME UI V3 REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION COMPLETE\n\nReference:\n824.png\n\nActive Home UI owners:\n<n>\n\nCore V3 presentation imports:\n<n>\n\nHome width:\n<value>\n\nHome height:\n<value>\n\nFav height:\n<value>\n\nSearch collapsed height:\n<value>\n\nSearch expanded height:\n<value>\n\nP1 size:\n<value>\n\nP2 size:\n<value>\n\nP1 == P2:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock size:\n<value>\n\nDock outside Home:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHome → Dock gap:\n<value>\n\nP1 slot count:\n<n>\n\nP2 slot count:\n<n>\n\nDock slot count:\n<n>\n\nExisting P1 data rendered:\n<YES/NO>\n\nExisting P2 data rendered:\n<YES/NO>\n\nExisting Dock data rendered:\n<YES/NO>\n\nEmpty state conditional:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHome UI persistence writes:\n<n>\n\nHome UI PackageManager calls:\n<n>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nOld PATCH009 UI runtime references:\n<n>\n\nCode-security:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSTATUS:\nV3_DEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
