/root/.codex/history.jsonl:381:{"session_id":"01a0241b-790e-77f3-8e38-a3325f95253f","ts":1787328539,"text":"FASE — worm HOME UI REFERENCE FIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nREFERENCE:\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/home-ui-approved.png\n\nCURRENT RESULT:\n\nVisual parity:\nREVIEW_REQUIRED\n\nFav:\nFAIL\n\nSearch:\nPASS\n\nP1/P2 equal:\nYES\n\nDock outside Home:\nYES\n\nLegacy runtime refs:\n0\n\nDebug:\nSUCCESS\n\nR8:\nFAILED\n\nRelease APK size:\n1,553,780 bytes\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFix ONLY the confirmed reference mismatches:\n\n1. restore the \"Apps 0\" count line in Fav\n2. restore wallpapered/background presentation behind Home\n3. diagnose and fix current R8 failure\n\nDo NOT redesign Home.\nDo NOT change Search geometry.\nDo NOT change P1/P2 geometry.\nDo NOT move Dock.\nDo NOT add new architecture layers.\n\n==================================================\n1. FAV COUNT\n==================================================\n\nFav must render:\n\nFav. apps\nApps <count>\n\nCount must come from current Core/Home state.\n\nFor current empty baseline:\n\nApps 0\n\nDo NOT hardcode \"Apps 0\" as permanent text.\n\nExpected concept:\n\nApps ${favCount}\n\nUse the existing approved typography hierarchy.\n\n==================================================\n2. FAV LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\ntitle left\ncount directly below title\nsettings icon right\n\nDo not change Fav outer size unless required only to fit\nthe missing count line without clipping.\n\nNo other Fav redesign.\n\n==================================================\n3. WALLPAPER BACKGROUND\n==================================================\n\nCurrent flat dark shell does NOT match reference.\n\nRestore Home screen presentation so wallpaper remains visible\nbehind the Home module.\n\nImportant:\n\nDo NOT bundle a large raster wallpaper into the APK just to\nmatch the mockup.\n\nPreferred order:\n\n1. transparent/edge-to-edge activity/window background allowing\n   launcher/system wallpaper presentation where appropriate\n\nor\n\n2. existing lightweight approved background mechanism already\n   present in worm\n\nDo NOT add:\n\nlarge PNG/JPG\nGIF\nvideo\nstatic screenshot asset\n\n==================================================\n4. HOME SURFACES\n==================================================\n\nHome/Fav/Search/P1/P2/Dock remain dark surfaces over wallpaper.\n\nDo NOT make the root composable an opaque fullscreen black Surface.\n\nAudit for:\n\nSurface(\n    modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize(),\n    color = darkColor\n)\n\nor equivalent fullscreen opaque background.\n\nIf found:\nmake only the module surfaces opaque/dark,\nnot the entire Home root.\n\n==================================================\n5. EDGE TO EDGE\n==================================================\n\nPreserve system bars and wallpaper visibility.\n\nRoot may use:\n\ntransparent background\n\nwhile Home module remains centered and dark.\n\nDo not move Home under status/navigation bars.\n\n==================================================\n6. NO SIZE REGRESSION\n==================================================\n\nRequired unchanged:\n\nHome compact = YES\nSearch = PASS\nP1/P2 equal = YES\nDock outside Home = YES\n\nP1 dimensions:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP2 dimensions:\nUNCHANGED\n\nDock placement:\nUNCHANGED\n\nSearch placement:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n7. R8 DIAGNOSIS\n==================================================\n\nCurrent:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = FAILED\n\nRun release/R8 task directly and capture the FIRST real failure.\n\nDo not guess.\n\nReport:\n\ntask\nexception/error\nclass/resource involved\nwhether failure is:\n\n- missing class\n- keep rule\n- resource shrinker\n- manifest\n- signing\n- Kotlin/Compose\n- other\n\n==================================================\n8. R8 FIX\n==================================================\n\nApply only the minimal justified fix.\n\nDo NOT add broad rules like:\n\n-keep class ** { *; }\n\nDo NOT disable R8.\n\nDo NOT disable resource shrinking unless proven necessary.\n\nKeep:\n\nminifyEnabled = true\nshrinkResources = true\n\nif currently configured.\n\n==================================================\n9. SIZE GATE\n==================================================\n\nCurrent release size is excellent:\n\n1,553,780 bytes\n\nKeep hard target:\n\n<= 7 MB\n\nAfter fix report new release APK size.\n\nDo not accept a large size regression from adding wallpaper assets.\n\n==================================================\n10. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n11. FINAL REFERENCE CHECK\n==================================================\n\nRe-run:\n\nworm HOME UI FINAL REFERENCE CHECK\n\nExpected:\n\nVisual parity:\nPASS\n\nFav:\nPASS\n\nSearch:\nPASS\n\nP1/P2 equal:\nYES\n\nDock outside Home:\nYES\n\nLegacy runtime refs:\n0\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm HOME UI REFERENCE FIX COMPLETE\n\nFav count source:\n<CORE/OTHER>\n\nFav count rendered:\n<YES/NO>\n\nWallpaper visible behind Home:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFullscreen opaque root removed:\n<YES/NO/N-A>\n\nHome geometry changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearch geometry changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1/P2 geometry changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock position changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nR8 root cause:\n<value>\n\nR8 fix:\n<value>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease APK size:\n<value>\n\nRelease <= 7 MB:\n<YES/NO>\n\nVisual parity:\n<PASS/REVIEW_REQUIRED>\n\nSTATUS:\n<HOME_UI_REFERENCE_VALIDATED / REVIEW_REQUIRED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:382:{"session_id":"01a0241b-790e-77f3-8e38-a3325f95253f","ts":1787329277,"text":"FASE — worm CORE + UI FOUNDATION ONLY\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nBuild ONLY the permanent worm foundation:\n\ncore/\nui/\n\nCore and UI must be developed in parallel.\n\nDO NOT implement optional functionality.\n\nDO NOT create:\npatches/\nfeatures/\nplugins/\nv2/\nv3/\n\n==================================================\nCORE\n==================================================\n\nImplement only:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nHomeSlot\nAppCatalog contract\nSlotRepository contract\nLauncherActions contract\nAppVisuals contract\n\nHard slot contract:\n\nP1 = 8\nP2 = 8\nDock = 5\n\nCore contains NO:\n\nCompose layout\ndp\ncolors\npadding\nanimation\nSearch engine\nSettings\nUsageStats\nplugin code\n\n==================================================\nUI\n==================================================\n\nImplement only:\n\nWormApp\nHome\nFav\nSearch shell\nP1\nP2\nDock\ntheme\nshared visual components\n\nAuthoritative Home structure:\n\nHOME CONTAINER\n├── Fav\n├── Search shell\n├── P1\n└── P2\n\nGAP\n\nDOCK\n\nDock outside Home container.\n\nP1/P2 same dimensions.\n\nUI contains NO:\n\npersistence writes\nPackageManager scans\nUsageStats\nSearch engine\nSettings backend\nplugin logic\n\n==================================================\nEXTENSION CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nPrepare clean interfaces so future optional modules can attach\nwithout rewriting Core/UI.\n\nFuture capabilities may include:\n\nSearch\nSettings\nParticles\nSlot Editor\nFirst Install\nPlugins\n\nBut implement NONE of them now.\n\n==================================================\nARCHITECTURE\n==================================================\n\nAllowed active architecture:\n\ncom/worm/\n  core/\n  ui/\n\nExpected active third-layer directories:\n0\n\nCore -> UI dependencies:\n0\n\nUI direct persistence writes:\n0\n\n==================================================\nBUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\nRelease APK target:\n<= 7 MB\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm CORE + UI FOUNDATION COMPLETE\n\nActive architecture:\n<list>\n\nExpected:\ncore\nui\n\nCore files:\n<n>\n\nUI files:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot owners:\n<n>\n\nSlotRepository owners:\n<n>\n\nHome UI owners:\n<n>\n\nP1 slots:\n<n>/8\n\nP2 slots:\n<n>/8\n\nDock slots:\n<n>/5\n\nCore Compose imports:\n<n>\n\nUI persistence writes:\n<n>\n\nOptional functionality implemented:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n0\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease APK size:\n<value>\n\nSTATUS:\nCORE_UI_FOUNDATION_DEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:383:{"session_id":"01a0241b-790e-77f3-8e38-a3325f95253f","ts":1787329682,"text":"FASE — worm STABLE CORE + REWRITABLE PATCH RUNTIME\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nReorganize worm around:\n\n1. ONE stable Core\n2. ONE runtime entry\n3. all UI/functions implemented as replaceable patches\n4. patches may be rewritten repeatedly until STABLE\n\nCORE must never depend on patches.\n\n==================================================\n1. FINAL ACTIVE ARCHITECTURE\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\napp/src/main/java/com/worm/\n\ncore/\nruntime/\npatches/\nui/\n\nMeaning:\n\ncore/\n= permanent data/state/action foundation\n\nruntime/\n= single patch integration entry\n\npatches/\n= replaceable UI/function implementations\n\nui/\n= generic reusable visual primitives only\n\n==================================================\n2. CORE\n==================================================\n\nCore owns only permanent contracts and state.\n\nCreate/keep:\n\ncore/model/\ncore/catalog/\ncore/persistence/\ncore/actions/\ncore/visuals/\ncore/contracts/\n\nCore responsibilities:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nHomeSlot\nAppCatalog\nSlotRepository\nLauncherActions\nAppVisuals\nstable patch-facing interfaces\n\nHard Home contract:\n\nP1 = 8\nP2 = 8\nDock = 5\n\n==================================================\n3. CORE MUST NOT CONTAIN\n==================================================\n\nCore must contain NO:\n\nCompose Home layout\nSearch UI\nSettings UI\nparticle animation\ngesture implementation\nUsageStats UI\nApp Picker UI\ndp values\ncolors\ncorner radius\nvisual spacing\n\n==================================================\n4. PATCH CONTRACTS\n==================================================\n\nCreate minimal Core contracts required by patches.\n\nExamples conceptually:\n\nHomeStateReader\nSlotEditor\nAppLauncher\nAppCatalogReader\nAppVisualResolver\n\nPatch code talks to Core only through these stable contracts\nwhere practical.\n\nDo not expose persistence implementation directly.\n\n==================================================\n5. SINGLE RUNTIME ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nruntime/WormRuntime.kt\n\nWormRuntime is the ONLY integration point between:\n\nMainActivity\nand\nactive patches.\n\nMainActivity must conceptually become:\n\nsetContent {\n    WormRuntime(...)\n}\n\nor equivalent minimal entry.\n\nMainActivity must not import individual patches.\n\n==================================================\n6. PATCH TREE\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\npatches/home/\npatches/search/\npatches/particles/\npatches/settings/\npatches/slot_editor/\npatches/first_install/\n\nDo not implement all features now.\n\nCreate only the ownership structure/contracts required.\n\n==================================================\n7. HOME PATCH\n==================================================\n\npatches/home/\n\nOwns:\n\nHome UI\nFav\nSearch slot placement\nP1\nP2\nDock\nHome gestures\nHome geometry\n\nMay be rewritten completely without modifying Core.\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH PATCH\n==================================================\n\npatches/search/\n\nOwns:\n\nSearch UI\nquery handling\nresults\nhistory\nIME/focus\nsearch ranking\n\nConsumes Core AppCatalog / LauncherActions.\n\nNo direct slot persistence ownership.\n\n==================================================\n9. PARTICLES PATCH\n==================================================\n\npatches/particles/\n\nOwns:\n\nparticle animation\nnetwork lines\nvisual parameters\n\nNo persistence.\nNo Core state ownership.\n\n==================================================\n10. SETTINGS PATCH\n==================================================\n\npatches/settings/\n\nOwns:\n\nSettings UI\nSettings interaction\nuser-facing preferences\n\nMay communicate with stable SettingsStore contract if later added\nto Core.\n\nNo Home state ownership.\n\n==================================================\n11. SLOT EDITOR PATCH\n==================================================\n\npatches/slot_editor/\n\nOwns:\n\nlong press UI\nApp Picker\nslot-edit interaction\n\nWrites slots only through Core SlotRepository contract.\n\n==================================================\n12. FIRST INSTALL PATCH\n==================================================\n\npatches/first_install/\n\nOwns:\n\nfirst-install initialization flow\nUsageStats ranking\nsemantic Dock resolution orchestration\n\nResulting assignments written through Core.\n\nNo continuous monitoring.\n\n==================================================\n13. PATCH REWRITE POLICY\n==================================================\n\nEvery patch is replaceable.\n\nA patch may be:\n\nrewritten\ndeleted\nrecreated\nredesigned\n\nwithout changing Core contracts.\n\nCore modifications are allowed only if a genuinely missing\nstable capability is proven.\n\nDo not modify Core merely to accommodate one visual experiment.\n\n==================================================\n14. PATCH STATUS\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/PATCH_STATUS.md\n\nAllowed states:\n\nDRAFT\nIMPLEMENTED\nDEVICE_TEST\nSTABLE\nREJECTED\n\nInitial status should reflect actual current state.\n\n==================================================\n15. PATCH VERSIONING\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT use permanent source package names like:\n\npatch001\npatch002\npatch003\n\nUse capability names:\n\nhome\nsearch\nparticles\nsettings\nslot_editor\nfirst_install\n\nDuring iteration use docs/checkpoints for versions.\n\nExample:\n\nhome-r1\nhome-r2\nhome-r3\n\nbut active source remains:\n\npatches/home/\n\n==================================================\n16. CHECKPOINT POLICY\n==================================================\n\nBefore rewriting a patch:\n\nprojectctl checkpoint <patch>-pre-rewrite\n\nAfter device-approved patch:\n\nprojectctl checkpoint <patch>-stable\n\nOnly STABLE patches become reference baselines.\n\n==================================================\n17. PATCH ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nEach patch must have:\n\none owner\nminimal Core contract\nexplicit rollback\nno duplicate state owner\n\nRemoving one optional patch must not corrupt Core.\n\n==================================================\n18. UI SHARED COMPONENTS\n==================================================\n\nui/\n\ncontains only reusable presentation primitives:\n\ntheme\nsurface styles\nicons\nspacing tokens\ngeneric animation helpers\n\nNo Home state.\nNo Search state.\nNo Settings state.\n\n==================================================\n19. DEPENDENCY DIRECTION\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\npatches\n↓\ncore\n\nruntime\n↓\npatches + core\n\nMainActivity\n↓\nruntime\n\nForbidden:\n\ncore → patches\ncore → runtime\ncore → Home UI\n\n==================================================\n20. BUILD SIZE\n==================================================\n\nRelease R8 target:\n\n<= 7 MB\n\nPreferred:\n4–6 MB\n\nDo not compile rejected/archived patch versions.\n\nOnly current active patch implementation is part of APK.\n\n==================================================\n21. ARCHIVE\n==================================================\n\nOld patch revisions must NOT remain in active source sets.\n\nArchive under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/archive/patches/\n\nExample:\n\narchive/patches/home/r1/\narchive/patches/home/r2/\n\nNever compile archive/.\n\n==================================================\n22. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md\ndocs/CORE.md\ndocs/PATCHES.md\ndocs/PATCH_STATUS.md\n\nDocument:\n\n- stable Core boundary\n- runtime entry\n- patch ownership\n- rewrite policy\n- stable gate\n- rollback procedure\n\n==================================================\n23. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm STABLE CORE / PATCH RUNTIME READY\n\nCore owners:\n<list>\n\nRuntime entry:\n<symbol>\n\nMainActivity patch imports:\n<n>\n\nCore -> patch dependencies:\n<n>\n\nPatch directories:\n<list>\n\nActive Home patch:\n<path/N-A>\n\nActive Search patch:\n<path/N-A>\n\nActive Particle patch:\n<path/N-A>\n\nActive Settings patch:\n<path/N-A>\n\nActive Slot Editor patch:\n<path/N-A>\n\nActive First Install patch:\n<path/N-A>\n\nPatch status file:\n<path>\n\nArchived patch code compiled:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease APK size:\n<value>\n\nSTATUS:\nCORE_STABLE_PATCH_RUNTIME_READY"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:384:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787330658,"text":"FASE — UI-001 HOME REFERENCE BASELINE\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI-001\n\nREFERENCE:\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/ui-001/home-approved.png\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nImplement the first replaceable Home UI patch using the supplied\nreference image as the authoritative visual target.\n\nCORE:\nREAD ONLY / STABLE CONTRACT\n\nUI-001 may be rewritten repeatedly until STABLE.\n\nDo NOT modify Core to solve visual mismatches.\n\n==================================================\nREFERENCE CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nMatch the reference for:\n\n- overall Home placement\n- Fav.apps header proportions\n- P1 panel\n- P2 panel\n- Dock external panel\n- rounded corners\n- panel gaps\n- dark surface hierarchy\n- app grid proportions\n- icon spacing\n- compact overall Home height\n\nDo not implement the clock/date area shown in the wallpaper/reference\nunless it is part of worm itself.\n\nTreat background/wallpaper content as environmental reference,\nnot bundled app UI.\n\n==================================================\nSTRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nHOME\n\nFav.apps\n\nP1\n4 x 2\n\nP2\n4 x 2\n\nDOCK\n5 slots\noutside main Home container\n\n==================================================\nFEEDBACK LOOP\n==================================================\n\nAfter each device test classify:\n\nMATCH\nMINOR_MISMATCH\nMAJOR_MISMATCH\n\nRecord concrete mismatch only:\n\n- width\n- height\n- vertical position\n- gap\n- radius\n- border\n- color\n- icon size\n- icon spacing\n- text position\n\nDo not redesign unrelated areas from feedback.\n\n==================================================\nDEBUG REFERENCE\n==================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/UI-001.md\n\nRecord:\n\nreference image\ncurrent revision\ndevice screenshot result\nknown mismatches\nchanges made\nstatus\n\nRevision examples:\n\nUI-001-r1\nUI-001-r2\nUI-001-r3\n\nActive source remains one UI-001 implementation.\n\nOld revisions go to archive, not active source.\n\n==================================================\nSTABLE GATE\n==================================================\n\nUI-001 becomes STABLE only when Pixel comparison is approved.\n\nUntil then:\n\nCore modified = NO\nUI-001 status = DEVICE_TEST\n\n==================================================\nBUILD\n==================================================\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm UI-001 HOME COMPLETE\n\nReference:\n<path>\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nVisual parity:\n<MATCH/MINOR_MISMATCH/MAJOR_MISMATCH>\n\nHome geometry:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nFav:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nP1:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nP2:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDock:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DRAFT/DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:385:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787331715,"text":"FASE — UI-002 MOTION / GESTURE FEEDBACK\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI-002\n\nDEPENDS ON:\nUI-001 Home visual baseline\n\nCORE:\nREAD ONLY / STABLE\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAdd only Home motion/gesture behavior.\n\nDo NOT redesign UI-001.\nDo NOT modify Core.\nDo NOT add Search functionality yet.\n\n==================================================\n1. LEFT SWIPE\n==================================================\n\nHorizontal swipe LEFT:\n\napply Material 3 style stretch/elastic feedback.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- no page navigation\n- no edge arrow\n- no permanent translation\n- release returns smoothly to rest\n- Home structure remains intact\n- P1/P2/Dock keep their normal layout after release\n\n==================================================\n2. RIGHT SWIPE\n==================================================\n\nHorizontal swipe RIGHT:\n\nsame Material 3 stretch/elastic behavior.\n\nRequirements identical to LEFT.\n\nLEFT and RIGHT must feel symmetric.\n\n==================================================\n3. MATERIAL STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nStretch should be:\n\n- soft\n- bounded\n- temporary\n- proportional to drag distance\n- resistant near maximum stretch\n- smoothly returning on release/cancel\n\nDo not use a crude linear translation.\n\nDo not permanently scale app icons independently.\n\nPrefer one Home-surface motion owner.\n\n==================================================\n4. AXIS LOCK\n==================================================\n\nGesture arbitration must distinguish:\n\nhorizontal gesture\nvs\nvertical gesture\n\nAfter axis lock:\n\nLEFT/RIGHT must not trigger UP expansion.\n\nUP must not trigger horizontal stretch.\n\nDuplicate gesture owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n5. SWIPE UP\n==================================================\n\nSwipe UP changes only the space between:\n\nFav.apps\nand\nP1\n\nTarget expansion:\n\n+25% relative to the approved collapsed Home geometry.\n\nThis newly revealed region must remain EMPTY for UI-002.\n\nDo NOT add:\n\nSearch bar\nresults\nhistory\nparticles\nbuttons\ntext\n\nOnly empty space.\n\n==================================================\n6. ANCHORED SECTIONS\n==================================================\n\nDuring UP expansion:\n\nP1:\nmust NOT resize.\n\nP2:\nmust NOT resize.\n\nDock:\nmust NOT resize.\n\nFav:\nkeeps its approved size.\n\nOnly the vertical gap / reveal region between Fav and P1\nis expanded.\n\n==================================================\n7. EXPANDED GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nDefine:\n\ncollapsedRevealHeight = baseline gap\n\nexpandedRevealHeight =\ncollapsedRevealHeight + 25% approved expansion target\n\nUse measured/responsive layout.\n\nDo not derive from hardcoded absolute screen coordinates.\n\nReport exact dp result on current target configuration.\n\n==================================================\n8. RELEASE DECISION\n==================================================\n\nVertical drag should support:\n\ndrag preview\nthen settle to one of:\n\nCOLLAPSED\nEXPANDED\n\nUse a clear threshold.\n\nPreferred:\n\nexpand if progress >= 0.5\nor upward velocity clearly passes threshold.\n\ncollapse otherwise.\n\nDo not leave intermediate state after release.\n\n==================================================\n9. SWIPE DOWN\n==================================================\n\nWhen expanded:\n\nswipe DOWN collapses the empty reveal area.\n\nReturn to exact UI-001 collapsed geometry.\n\nNo permanent spacing drift.\n\n==================================================\n10. MOTION FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nDuring UP/DOWN drag:\n\nanimate reveal height smoothly.\n\nNo Material horizontal stretch effect on vertical movement.\n\nVertical behavior is layout/reveal motion only.\n\n==================================================\n11. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nFor UI-002 use at most one semantic haptic when state is accepted:\n\nCOLLAPSED → EXPANDED:\n1 confirmation haptic\n\nEXPANDED → COLLAPSED:\n1 confirmation haptic\n\nNo haptic during MOVE.\n\nNo repeated vibration while dragging.\n\n==================================================\n12. TOUCH SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nP1 normal taps remain usable\nP2 normal taps remain usable\nDock normal taps remain usable\n\nGesture layer must not create a first-touch blocker.\n\nLong-press behavior, if not implemented yet:\ndo not add it here.\n\n==================================================\n13. SINGLE MOTION OWNER\n==================================================\n\nUI-002 owns Home gesture motion.\n\nExpected:\n\nhorizontal motion owners = 1\nvertical reveal owners = 1\n\nThese may live in one controller.\n\nNo duplicated pointerInput chains competing for the same Home.\n\n==================================================\n14. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nGesture hot path:\n\nno disk IO\nno PackageManager\nno network\nno allocations that grow with MOVE events\nno coroutine per pointer event\n\n==================================================\n15. FEEDBACK LOOP\n==================================================\n\nUse revision states:\n\nUI-002-r1\nUI-002-r2\nUI-002-r3\n...\n\nAfter each Pixel test record:\n\nLEFT:\nPASS / TOO_WEAK / TOO_STRONG / JANK\n\nRIGHT:\nPASS / TOO_WEAK / TOO_STRONG / JANK\n\nUP:\nPASS / TOO_SMALL / TOO_LARGE / WRONG_GEOMETRY\n\nDOWN:\nPASS / FAIL\n\nHAPTIC:\nPASS / TOO_STRONG / DUPLICATED / MISSING\n\n==================================================\n16. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/UI-002.md\n\nRecord:\n\n- current revision\n- horizontal stretch parameters\n- vertical reveal parameters\n- expansion dp\n- threshold\n- haptic behavior\n- device feedback\n- current status\n\n==================================================\n17. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm UI-002 MOTION COMPLETE\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUI-001 geometry modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nLEFT Material stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRIGHT Material stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHorizontal symmetry:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nHorizontal motion owners:\n<n>\n\nVertical reveal owners:\n<n>\n\nCollapsed reveal height:\n<dp>\n\nExpanded reveal height:\n<dp>\n\nExpansion:\n<percent>\n\nExpected:\n25%\n\nP1 resized:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP2 resized:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock resized:\n<NO/YES>\n\nFav resized:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUP settle:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDOWN collapse:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nMOVE haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nAccepted-state haptic:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n<n>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DRAFT/DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:386:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787332719,"text":"FASE — UI-003 WIDTH / HORIZONTAL GEOMETRY\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI-003\n\nDEPENDS ON:\nUI-001 Home visual baseline\nUI-002 Motion / Gesture feedback\n\nCORE:\nREAD ONLY / STABLE\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nIncrease the horizontal width of the Home UI.\n\nMake both:\n\n- main Home container\n- external Dock\n\nvisibly wider than the current approved geometry.\n\nDo NOT change vertical proportions.\nDo NOT change P1/P2 heights.\nDo NOT change motion behavior from UI-002.\nDo NOT modify Core.\n\n==================================================\n1. MAIN HOME WIDTH\n==================================================\n\nIncrease the Home container width.\n\nCurrent geometry:\nuse actual measured current value.\n\nTarget:\nwider than current by a controlled amount.\n\nPreferred starting target:\n\napproximately +6% to +10% relative width\n\nor approximately:\n\n92–94% of usable display width\n\ndepending on current implementation.\n\nDo NOT use full edge-to-edge width.\n\nKeep visible wallpaper margins left/right.\n\n==================================================\n2. DOCK WIDTH\n==================================================\n\nIncrease Dock width proportionally.\n\nDock should visually align with the widened Home container.\n\nPreferred:\n\nDock width ≈ Home container width\n\nor slightly narrower if that matches reference feedback.\n\nDo NOT leave Dock at the old narrow width.\n\n==================================================\n3. HORIZONTAL MARGINS\n==================================================\n\nReduce left/right external margins.\n\nKeep them symmetric.\n\nTarget:\n\nleft margin == right margin\n\nNo hardcoded absolute screen coordinates.\n\nUse responsive constraints.\n\n==================================================\n4. INTERNAL PANELS\n==================================================\n\nFav\nSearch\nP1\nP2\n\nmust expand horizontally with the Home container.\n\nKeep internal padding coherent.\n\nDo NOT keep old narrow fixed widths inside a wider outer shell.\n\n==================================================\n5. P1 / P2 GRID\n==================================================\n\nP1/P2 width increases.\n\nKeep:\n\n8 slots\n4 columns x 2 rows\nsame icon size initially\n\nIncrease horizontal spacing only if needed.\n\nDo NOT enlarge icons automatically just because container is wider.\n\n==================================================\n6. FAV\n==================================================\n\nFav width follows Home width.\n\nKeep:\n\nheight unchanged\ntitle placement unchanged\nsettings icon placement unchanged\n\nOnly horizontal geometry changes.\n\n==================================================\n7. SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nSearch width follows Home width.\n\nKeep:\n\nheight unchanged\nSearch behavior unchanged\nUI-002 reveal unchanged\n\nDo not alter vertical spacing.\n\n==================================================\n8. DOCK ICON GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nDock remains:\n\n5 slots\n1 row\n\nUse the extra horizontal width to improve icon distribution.\n\nKeep icon size unchanged unless clipping/spacing requires\na small adjustment.\n\nTarget:\n\nequal slot spacing\nbalanced left/right padding\n\n==================================================\n9. UI-002 MOTION LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nLEFT Material stretch\nRIGHT Material stretch\nUP +25% reveal\nDOWN collapse\ngesture thresholds\nhaptics\n\nHorizontal width changes must not create gesture regressions.\n\n==================================================\n10. VERTICAL GEOMETRY LOCK\n==================================================\n\nRequired unchanged:\n\nFav height\nSearch height\nP1 height\nP2 height\nDock height\n\nHome vertical position:\nunchanged unless a tiny centering correction is strictly required.\n\n==================================================\n11. WIDTH TOKENS\n==================================================\n\nUse one shared width/margin owner.\n\nAvoid:\n\ndifferent arbitrary widths for Fav/Search/P1/P2.\n\nPreferred:\n\nHome outer width defines all inner widths.\n\nDock uses same responsive width token/fraction.\n\n==================================================\n12. DEVICE FEEDBACK LOOP\n==================================================\n\nRevision examples:\n\nUI-003-r1\nUI-003-r2\nUI-003-r3\n\nAfter each Pixel test record:\n\nHOME WIDTH:\nPASS / TOO_NARROW / TOO_WIDE\n\nDOCK WIDTH:\nPASS / TOO_NARROW / TOO_WIDE\n\nLEFT/RIGHT MARGINS:\nPASS / TOO_LARGE / TOO_SMALL\n\nINNER PANELS:\nPASS / MISALIGNED\n\nICON SPACING:\nPASS / TOO_TIGHT / TOO_WIDE\n\n==================================================\n13. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/UI-003.md\n\nRecord:\n\n- revision\n- old Home width\n- new Home width\n- old Dock width\n- new Dock width\n- external margins\n- internal padding\n- Pixel feedback\n- status\n\n==================================================\n14. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm UI-003 WIDTH COMPLETE\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUI-001 visual behavior modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUI-002 motion behavior modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nOld Home width:\n<dp/%>\n\nNew Home width:\n<dp/%>\n\nHome width increase:\n<percent>\n\nOld Dock width:\n<dp/%>\n\nNew Dock width:\n<dp/%>\n\nDock width increase:\n<percent>\n\nLeft margin:\n<dp>\n\nRight margin:\n<dp>\n\nMargins symmetric:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFav height changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearch height changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1 height changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP2 height changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock height changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1/P2 grid changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock slots:\n<5/OTHER>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DRAFT/DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:387:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787333258,"text":"FASE — UI-004 EDGE / GESTURE ARBITRATION\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI-004\n\nDEPENDS ON:\nUI-001 Home visual baseline\nUI-002 Motion / Gesture feedback\nUI-003 Horizontal geometry\n\nCORE:\nREAD ONLY / STABLE\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRefine launcher gesture behavior.\n\nHard requirements:\n\n1. worm must NOT expose left/right edge Back/Forward behavior\n   from the Home surface.\n\n2. LEFT / RIGHT swipe:\n   Material 3 stretch animation must start from the touched edge.\n\n3. UP swipe:\n   NO Material stretch.\n   Use only vertical reveal/motion + tactile feedback,\n   with a Pixel-like feel.\n\nDo NOT modify Core.\nDo NOT redesign UI.\nDo NOT change UI-003 width geometry.\n\n==================================================\n1. EDGE BACK / FORWARD\n==================================================\n\nOn worm Home:\n\nLEFT edge swipe:\nmust NOT trigger navigation Back.\n\nRIGHT edge swipe:\nmust NOT trigger Forward/navigation behavior.\n\nNo visible edge arrow.\n\nNo launcher page navigation.\n\nNo system-like horizontal history behavior inside worm.\n\nExpected:\n\nedge Back indicator:\nNONE\n\nedge Forward behavior:\nNONE\n\n==================================================\n2. SYSTEM GESTURE ARBITRATION\n==================================================\n\nAudit Android edge gesture handling.\n\nFor the Home interaction surface, prevent worm's own\nhorizontal gesture path from becoming a Back/Forward action.\n\nUse supported Android public APIs only.\n\nDo not use hidden APIs.\n\nDo not globally disable Android navigation outside worm.\n\n==================================================\n3. LEFT SWIPE — MATERIAL 3 STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nSwipe from LEFT toward center:\n\napply Material 3 style stretch.\n\nImportant:\n\nstretch origin must visually begin at LEFT edge.\n\nThe opposite side should feel more anchored.\n\nNo page translation.\n\nNo navigation action.\n\nNo edge arrow.\n\nOn release:\nsmoothly return to rest.\n\n==================================================\n4. RIGHT SWIPE — MATERIAL 3 STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nSwipe from RIGHT toward center:\n\nsame behavior mirrored.\n\nStretch origin:\nRIGHT edge.\n\nLEFT and RIGHT must be symmetric.\n\n==================================================\n5. STRETCH CHARACTER\n==================================================\n\nHorizontal stretch must be:\n\nsoft\nbounded\nelastic\nresistant near limit\nproportional to drag\nsmooth on release\n\nDo not implement as simple linear offset.\n\nDo not independently scale each icon.\n\nPrefer one coherent Home/container deformation owner.\n\n==================================================\n6. EDGE-BASED TRANSFORM\n==================================================\n\nHorizontal visual transformation must preserve edge origin.\n\nConceptually:\n\nLEFT swipe:\ntransform pivot/origin biased to left edge\n\nRIGHT swipe:\ntransform pivot/origin biased to right edge\n\nDo not stretch from center.\n\n==================================================\n7. UP SWIPE — NO MATERIAL STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nUP gesture must NOT trigger horizontal/Material stretch.\n\nUP owns only:\n\nvertical reveal / lift behavior\n+\naccepted-state haptic feedback\n\nHorizontal stretch amount during UP:\n0\n\n==================================================\n8. UP BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nPreserve approved UI-002 vertical behavior:\n\nswipe UP\n→ reveal/expand upper region\n\nCurrent target:\n+25% reveal between Fav.apps and P1\n\nDo not modify that geometry in UI-004.\n\n==================================================\n9. UP HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nWhen UP state is accepted:\n\none tactile confirmation.\n\nTarget feel:\nshort, clean, Pixel-like semantic feedback.\n\nUse supported View.performHapticFeedback(...) path.\n\nPrefer semantic Android haptic constants available on target SDK.\n\nNo raw waveform unless no supported semantic API can satisfy it.\n\nDo not attempt to imitate a specific device motor waveform.\n\n==================================================\n10. DOWN\n==================================================\n\nIf current UI-002 DOWN collapse exists:\n\npreserve it.\n\nDOWN:\nno horizontal Material stretch.\n\nAccepted collapse:\nmay retain one existing semantic haptic if already approved.\n\nDo not introduce new duplicate feedback.\n\n==================================================\n11. NO HAPTIC ON HORIZONTAL MOVE\n==================================================\n\nLEFT/RIGHT Material stretch:\n\nMOVE haptic = 0\n\nDrag haptic = 0\n\nRelease haptic = 0 preferred unless existing approved contract\nexplicitly requires one.\n\nHorizontal feedback is visual.\n\n==================================================\n12. AXIS LOCK\n==================================================\n\nGesture recognition must lock to one axis after threshold.\n\nHorizontal:\n\nabs(dx) > abs(dy)\n→ LEFT/RIGHT stretch owner\n\nVertical:\n\nabs(dy) > abs(dx)\n→ UP/DOWN reveal owner\n\nAfter axis lock:\ndo not switch owners mid-gesture.\n\n==================================================\n13. TOUCH SLOP\n==================================================\n\nUse Android/ViewConfiguration touch slop.\n\nDo not activate stretch on microscopic movement.\n\nDo not trigger UP reveal before intentional vertical drag.\n\nReport actual threshold strategy.\n\n==================================================\n14. DIAGONAL SWIPES\n==================================================\n\nDiagonal gesture must resolve deterministically.\n\nExamples:\n\nstrong horizontal diagonal\n→ horizontal stretch\n\nstrong upward diagonal\n→ vertical reveal\n\nNo simultaneous:\n\nstretch + reveal\n\nRequired simultaneous motion owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n15. FIRST TOUCH SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nGesture layer must not consume normal taps unnecessarily.\n\nRequired:\n\nFav/settings first tap = PASS\nP1 first tap = PASS\nP2 first tap = PASS\nDock first tap = PASS\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n0\n\n==================================================\n16. UI-001 / UI-003 LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nHome width\nDock width\nP1/P2 dimensions\nFav dimensions\ncolors\nborders\nradii\nspacing\n\nUI-004 owns gesture arbitration/motion feedback only.\n\n==================================================\n17. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nNo:\n\nHomeSnapshot changes\nSlotRepository changes\nAppCatalog changes\npersistence changes\n\n==================================================\n18. SINGLE GESTURE OWNER\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHome gesture owner total = 1\n\nHorizontal stretch owner = 1\nVertical reveal owner = 1\n\nThey may live under one Home gesture controller.\n\nDuplicate pointerInput owners:\n0 preferred.\n\n==================================================\n19. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nMOVE hot path:\n\ndisk IO = 0\nnetwork = 0\nPackageManager = 0\nUsageStats = 0\npersistence writes = 0\n\nAvoid allocation-heavy object creation on every pointer event.\n\n==================================================\n20. DEVICE FEEDBACK LOOP\n==================================================\n\nRevision:\n\nUI-004-r1\nUI-004-r2\nUI-004-r3\n...\n\nAfter Pixel test record:\n\nLEFT EDGE:\nPASS\nTOO_WEAK\nTOO_STRONG\nWRONG_ORIGIN\nBACK_TRIGGERED\nJANK\n\nRIGHT EDGE:\nPASS\nTOO_WEAK\nTOO_STRONG\nWRONG_ORIGIN\nNAV_TRIGGERED\nJANK\n\nUP:\nPASS\nSTRETCH_LEAK\nHAPTIC_WEAK\nHAPTIC_STRONG\nHAPTIC_DUPLICATE\nWRONG_GEOMETRY\n\nDIAGONAL:\nPASS\nCONFLICT\n\n==================================================\n21. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/UI-004.md\n\nRecord:\n\nrevision\nedge arbitration\ntouch slop\naxis-lock strategy\nstretch origin behavior\nstretch bounds\nUP haptic API\ndevice feedback\nstatus\n\n==================================================\n22. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm UI-004 EDGE / GESTURE COMPLETE\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUI-001 geometry modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUI-002 reveal geometry modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUI-003 width geometry modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSystem Back arrow from Home:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nForward/navigation horizontal path:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nLEFT stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nLEFT stretch origin:\n<LEFT_EDGE/OTHER>\n\nRIGHT stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRIGHT stretch origin:\n<RIGHT_EDGE/OTHER>\n\nHorizontal symmetry:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nUP Material stretch:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUP reveal preserved:\n<YES/NO>\n\nUP accepted haptic:\n<YES/NO>\n\nUP haptic API:\n<value>\n\nHorizontal MOVE haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nTouch slop:\n<value>\n\nAxis lock:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDiagonal simultaneous motion:\n<NO/YES>\n\nGesture owners:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n<n>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DRAFT/DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:388:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787333738,"text":"FASE — UI+OPTION-005 APP ICON + FIRST INSTALL\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI+OPTION-005\n\nDEPENDS ON:\nUI-001 Home reference\nUI-002 Motion\nUI-003 Width\nUI-004 Gesture arbitration\n\nCORE:\nSTABLE / READ ONLY\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAdd two independent capabilities:\n\n1. a worm application icon treatment\n2. a first-install fullscreen onboarding screen with\n   \"set worm as default Home\"\n\nDo NOT redesign the Home.\nDo NOT modify existing gesture geometry.\nDo NOT modify P1/P2/Dock layout.\n\n==================================================\n1. WORM APP ICON\n==================================================\n\nCreate the worm application icon.\n\nVisual target:\n\n- geometric hexagonal shape\n- hexagon extends visually to/through the outer black boundary\n- strong dark/black outer treatment\n- centered \"X\" symbol\n- minimal\n- monochrome/dark-friendly\n- readable at launcher icon size\n\nThe central X must be clearly centered.\n\nDo not add:\n- text\n- gradients unless necessary\n- detailed illustrations\n- large raster asset\n\nPrefer:\nVectorDrawable / adaptive icon layers.\n\n==================================================\n2. ADAPTIVE ICON\n==================================================\n\nImplement Android adaptive icon correctly.\n\nRequired:\n\nforeground layer:\nhexagon + X\n\nbackground layer:\nblack/dark\n\nSupport launcher masking safely.\n\nThe intended hexagonal graphic should remain visible even when\nAndroid applies circle/squircle/rounded-square icon masks.\n\nDo NOT draw critical parts outside adaptive icon safe zone.\n\n==================================================\n3. ICON FILES\n==================================================\n\nUse standard Android resources.\n\nPreferred structure:\n\nmipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml\nmipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher_round.xml\n\ndrawable/ic_launcher_foreground.xml\nvalues/ic_launcher_background.xml\n\nor equivalent existing project convention.\n\nKeep resource footprint minimal.\n\n==================================================\n4. MANIFEST ICON\n==================================================\n\nApplication manifest must reference the new worm icon.\n\nVerify:\n\nandroid:icon\nandroid:roundIcon\n\nNo legacy Machina icon references.\n\n==================================================\n5. FIRST INSTALL STATE\n==================================================\n\nAdd one minimal first-install state owner.\n\nPurpose:\n\nshow onboarding only until the initial setup is completed.\n\nDo NOT create a large Settings/preferences architecture.\n\nMinimal state only:\n\nfirstInstallCompleted\n\nPersistence:\nsmall and local.\n\nOwner:\n1\n\n==================================================\n6. FIRST INSTALL SCREEN\n==================================================\n\nOn first launch only:\n\nshow a fullscreen onboarding screen.\n\nBackground:\npure black / near-black\n\nFullscreen:\nYES\n\nNo Home panels visible underneath.\n\nNo wallpaper visible.\n\n==================================================\n7. FIRST INSTALL LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nVisual structure:\n\nBLACK FULLSCREEN\n\n        worm logo\n        upper-center / center-top area\n\n        optional short product name:\n        worm\n\n        optional minimal explanatory line\n\n        [ Set as default Home ]\n\n        optional:\n        [ Continue ]\n\nKeep layout extremely minimal.\n\n==================================================\n8. LOGO POSITION\n==================================================\n\nLogo must sit in the upper/central region.\n\nPreferred target:\n\nroughly 30–40% from top of usable display\n\nDo NOT place it directly under status bar.\n\nDo NOT center everything vertically in a generic Material dialog.\n\nThis is a dedicated onboarding screen.\n\n==================================================\n9. LOGO STYLE\n==================================================\n\nReuse worm application mark:\n\nhexagon + centered X\n\nDo NOT duplicate a separate visual identity.\n\nUse vector/code resource.\n\nNo large bitmap.\n\n==================================================\n10. DEFAULT HOME OPTION\n==================================================\n\nPrimary action:\n\n\"Set worm as default Home\"\n\nUse supported Android public APIs.\n\nPreferred:\nRoleManager.ROLE_HOME\n\nIf API/role is available:\n\nlaunch Android system Home-role request.\n\nDo NOT fake a custom default-app picker.\n\nDo NOT use hidden APIs.\n\n==================================================\n11. ROLE STATE\n==================================================\n\nDetect whether worm is already the current/default Home.\n\nIf already default:\n\nshow state such as:\n\n\"worm is your default Home\"\n\nand do not repeatedly request role.\n\n==================================================\n12. ROLE REQUEST RESULT\n==================================================\n\nAfter successful Home role selection:\n\nupdate onboarding UI.\n\nDo NOT automatically mark setup complete before result is known\nunless Android API behavior requires a safe fallback.\n\n==================================================\n13. CONTINUE\n==================================================\n\nProvide a secondary continuation path.\n\nPreferred:\n\nContinue\n\nBehavior:\n\n- user can proceed even if worm is not yet default Home\n- first-install onboarding can be completed intentionally\n\nDo NOT trap user in onboarding.\n\n==================================================\n14. BACK BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nOn first-install screen:\n\nBack must behave predictably.\n\nPreferred:\nallow Android-normal exit/back behavior.\n\nDo not create a permanent Back lock.\n\n==================================================\n15. ONBOARDING COMPLETION\n==================================================\n\nWhen user explicitly continues:\n\nfirstInstallCompleted = true\n\nSubsequent launches:\n\ngo directly to normal worm runtime/Home.\n\nDo NOT show onboarding every launch.\n\n==================================================\n16. RESET / DEBUG\n==================================================\n\nFor development only, document how to reset onboarding state.\n\nDo NOT expose a permanent debug button in production UI.\n\nDocument in:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/UI-OPTION-005.md\n\n==================================================\n17. SINGLE ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nKeep the existing single runtime entry.\n\nConcept:\n\nMainActivity\n↓\nWormRuntime\n↓\nif firstInstallCompleted:\n    active Home patch\nelse:\n    FirstInstallScreen\n\nMainActivity must NOT own onboarding logic.\n\n==================================================\n18. CORE BOUNDARY\n==================================================\n\nDo not change stable Core Home contracts.\n\nAllowed new minimal persistent option:\n\nfirstInstallCompleted\n\nAllowed system action:\n\nrequest Home role\n\nDo not modify:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nP1/P2/Dock\nAppCatalog\nSlotRepository semantics\n\n==================================================\n19. UI-001–004 LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT modify:\n\nHome geometry\nHome width\nDock width\nP1/P2 size\nLEFT/RIGHT stretch\nUP reveal\ngesture thresholds\nexisting haptics\n\n==================================================\n20. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nPrimary accepted button press may use one semantic confirmation haptic.\n\nNo haptic loops.\n\nNo MOVE haptic.\n\nNo repeated vibration while Android role UI opens.\n\n==================================================\n21. SYSTEM BARS\n==================================================\n\nFirst-install screen may draw edge-to-edge black.\n\nRespect safe insets for actual interactive content.\n\nDo not overlap critical controls with:\n\nstatus bar\nnavigation/gesture area\n\n==================================================\n22. SIZE BUDGET\n==================================================\n\nUse vector resources only where practical.\n\nDo NOT add large images.\n\nRelease R8 target remains:\n\n<= 7 MB\n\n==================================================\n23. DEVICE FEEDBACK LOOP\n==================================================\n\nRevision:\n\nUI+OPTION-005-r1\nUI+OPTION-005-r2\nUI+OPTION-005-r3\n\nRecord:\n\nAPP ICON:\nPASS\nHEXAGON_TOO_SMALL\nHEXAGON_TOO_LARGE\nX_OFF_CENTER\nMASKING_BAD\n\nONBOARDING:\nPASS\nLOGO_TOO_HIGH\nLOGO_TOO_LOW\nTOO_EMPTY\nTOO_BUSY\n\nDEFAULT HOME:\nPASS\nROLE_REQUEST_FAIL\nSTATE_NOT_REFRESHED\nREPEATED_REQUEST\n\n==================================================\n24. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/UI-OPTION-005.md\n\nRecord:\n\n- revision\n- icon resource paths\n- adaptive icon geometry\n- onboarding layout\n- Home role API\n- firstInstallCompleted owner\n- device feedback\n- status\n\n==================================================\n25. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm UI+OPTION-005 COMPLETE\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nCore Home contracts modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nApp icon:\n<IMPLEMENTED/FAILED>\n\nAdaptive icon:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHexagon:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCentered X:\n<YES/NO>\n\nLegacy icon refs:\n<n>\n\nFirst-install owners:\n<n>\n\nFirst-install fullscreen:\n<YES/NO>\n\nBackground:\n<BLACK/OTHER>\n\nLogo position:\n<value>\n\nDefault Home action:\n<ROLE_HOME/OTHER>\n\nAlready-default detection:\n<YES/NO>\n\nContinue path:\n<YES/NO>\n\nOnboarding persistent state:\n<value>\n\nRepeated onboarding after completion:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUI-001 geometry modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUI-002 motion modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUI-003 width modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUI-004 gestures modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease APK size:\n<value>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DRAFT/DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:389:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787335457,"text":"FASE — UI+CORE+OPTION-006 INTEGRATED SYSTEM\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI+CORE+OPTION-006\n\nDEPENDS ON:\nUI-001 Home\nUI-002 Motion\nUI-003 Width\nUI-004 Gestures\nUI+OPTION-005 First Install / Icon\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nImplement the next integrated worm layer:\n\n- Settings with glyph categories/subcategories\n- Dynamic Color Settings\n- Settings functionality\n- Changelog\n- Home top-position correction\n- adaptive status-bar appearance\n- Search bar shell\n- richer empty P1/P2 state\n- first-run particle animation\n- usage-ranked P1/P2 initial population\n- semantic Dock population\n- Search options\n- icon style / icon-pack options\n- time/timezone formatting options\n- Fav background/effect options\n\nKeep architecture:\n\ncore/\nruntime/\npatches/\nui/\n\nCore remains the single permanent state/data foundation.\n\n==================================================\n1. SETTINGS — GENERAL\n==================================================\n\nAdd worm Settings.\n\nSettings must NOT use the previous custom black wallpaper.\n\nUse the normal Settings surface/background derived from\nMaterial 3 theme.\n\nWhen Dynamic Color is available:\n\nuse system Dynamic Color.\n\nFallback:\nworm Material color scheme.\n\nNo custom fullscreen black wallpaper in Settings.\n\n==================================================\n2. SETTINGS ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nKeep Settings glyph in Fav.apps header.\n\nTap:\nopen Settings.\n\nUse one Settings navigation owner.\n\n==================================================\n3. SETTINGS VISUAL LANGUAGE\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\n- system font\n- compact Material 3 typography\n- small glyphs\n- categories\n- sub-categories\n- Dynamic Color\n- subtle dividers\n- no oversized cards\n\nEach root category gets a meaningful glyph.\n\n==================================================\n4. SETTINGS ROOT CATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nIcons\nTime\nSystem\nAbout\n\nDo not create dozens of root categories.\n\n==================================================\n5. APPEARANCE\n==================================================\n\nSubcategories/options:\n\nDynamic Color\nFav background\nFav visual effect\nStatus bar appearance\n\n==================================================\n6. DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nSetting:\n\nDynamic Color\nON/OFF\n\nDefault:\nON\n\nON:\nuse Android Dynamic Color where supported.\n\nOFF:\nworm fallback theme.\n\nApply to Settings.\n\nDo not arbitrarily recolor app icons.\n\nPersist through one Settings state owner.\n\n==================================================\n7. STATUS BAR APPEARANCE\n==================================================\n\nAdd setting:\n\nStatus bar icons:\n\nAUTO\nWHITE\nBLACK\n\nAUTO:\nderive light/dark system-bar icon appearance from the current\nwallpaper/system wallpaper colors using supported Android APIs.\n\nPrefer WallpaperManager / WallpaperColors where available.\n\nDo not screenshot/analyze wallpaper pixels continuously.\n\nWHITE:\nforce light/white status-bar icons.\n\nBLACK:\nforce dark/black status-bar icons.\n\nApply through supported WindowInsetsController APIs.\n\nNo hidden API.\n\n==================================================\n8. HOME TOP POSITION\n==================================================\n\nRevisit active Home UI patch geometry.\n\nMove the entire Home module upward.\n\nTarget:\n\nHome container top sits near the top of usable display,\ndirectly BELOW status bar.\n\nKeep a controlled gap.\n\nPreferred starting gap:\n\n12–20dp after status-bar safe inset.\n\nDo NOT overlap status bar.\n\nDo NOT move content behind clock/battery/signal.\n\n==================================================\n9. HOME WIDTH / EXISTING GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nPreserve UI-003 width unless device feedback proves a small\nadjustment is required.\n\nDo NOT undo:\n\nwide Home\nwide Dock\nexternal Dock\nP1/P2 equal geometry\n\n==================================================\n10. SEARCH BAR SHELL\n==================================================\n\nAdd Search bar between:\n\nFav.apps\nand\nP1\n\nVisual requirement:\n\nmagnifier on LEFT\n\neditable/search text area\n\nONE underline only\n\nNo filled Material pill.\n\nNo large card.\n\nNo double border.\n\nStructure:\n\nFav.apps\n\nSearch\n────────────\n\nP1\n\nP2\n\n==================================================\n11. SEARCH BAR SCOPE\n==================================================\n\nIn this patch Search shell must support connection to Search logic,\nbut keep UI ownership separate.\n\nDo not put PackageManager scanning in Search composable.\n\n==================================================\n12. SEARCH SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nCreate Settings → Search.\n\nOptions with switches:\n\nApps\nWeb results\nShortcuts\nHidden apps\nWork profile apps\n\nEach switch must correspond to a real backend capability.\n\nDo NOT expose fake switches.\n\nIf a capability cannot be supported safely/currently:\ndisable row and mark it unavailable internally,\nor omit it.\n\n==================================================\n13. SEARCH — APPS\n==================================================\n\nApps switch:\n\nON:\nsearch launchable apps from Core AppCatalog.\n\nOFF:\nexclude normal app results.\n\nNo PackageManager query per keystroke.\n\n==================================================\n14. SEARCH — WEB\n==================================================\n\nWeb results switch.\n\nPreferred implementation:\n\nshow a final action:\n\nSearch web for \"<query>\"\n\nUse external browser via HTTPS ACTION_VIEW.\n\nDo NOT implement an embedded WebView.\n\nDo NOT make worm itself perform web requests for this baseline.\n\n==================================================\n15. SEARCH — SHORTCUTS\n==================================================\n\nIf supported through public LauncherApps/ShortcutManager APIs:\n\ninclude eligible app shortcuts.\n\nDo not require unrestricted shortcut access.\n\nRespect launcher/default-home capabilities.\n\nIf unsupported:\ndo not fake results.\n\n==================================================\n16. SEARCH — HIDDEN APPS\n==================================================\n\nAdd Core setting/state for user-hidden apps.\n\nHidden app means:\n\nuser explicitly hides it from normal worm surfaces/search.\n\nDo not infer \"hidden\" from Android private/system packages.\n\nProvide stable package identity list.\n\nWhen \"Hidden apps\" Search switch is OFF:\nexclude hidden entries.\n\nWhen ON:\nallow explicitly hidden worm entries to appear in Search.\n\n==================================================\n17. SEARCH — WORK PROFILE\n==================================================\n\nUse supported Android launcher/profile APIs.\n\nPrefer:\n\nLauncherApps\nUserManager / UserHandle\n\nOnly enumerate profiles worm is legitimately allowed to access.\n\nNo privilege escalation.\n\nNo hidden API.\n\nIf work profile unavailable:\nswitch may remain disabled/hidden.\n\n==================================================\n18. P1 / P2 EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nReplace fake placeholder app icons.\n\nWhen P1/P2 contain no apps:\n\nshow ONE small glyph.\n\nPreferred:\noutline square/cube/add-app style glyph.\n\nText:\n\n\"No apps\"\n\nSecondary text:\n\n\"Add apps from Settings\"\n\nor equivalent concise user-facing wording.\n\nNo multiple fake application icons.\n\n==================================================\n19. P1 / P2 EMPTY GLYPH\n==================================================\n\nUse one system/vector glyph.\n\nSmall.\n\nCentered.\n\nNo large illustration.\n\nNo raster asset.\n\n==================================================\n20. FIRST INSTALL PARTICLE NETWORK\n==================================================\n\nUI+OPTION-005 first-install fullscreen screen remains.\n\nAdd animated network particles across the ENTIRE first-install\ndisplay.\n\nLayer order:\n\nblack base\n→ AnimatedParticleNetwork\n→ worm logo\n→ onboarding controls\n\nParticles extend across full screen.\n\nControls stay readable.\n\n==================================================\n21. PARTICLE ENGINE\n==================================================\n\nUse ONE reusable particle engine.\n\nNo duplicate implementation.\n\nParticle model:\n\nsmall moving dots\ndynamic nearby connection lines\ndelta-time movement\none frame owner\n\nNo wallpaper image.\n\nNo bitmap animation.\n\nNo per-particle coroutine.\n\n==================================================\n22. FIRST INSTALL PARTICLE STYLE\n==================================================\n\nFor onboarding:\n\nparticle count:\napproximately 20–28\n\nmovement:\nslow/moderate\n\nlines:\nclearly visible but background-level\n\nUse monochrome/dynamic neutral tones.\n\nNo neon effect.\n\n==================================================\n23. USAGE-BASED P1 / P2 INITIALIZATION\n==================================================\n\nOn FIRST INSTALL only:\n\nif user grants Usage Access:\n\nrank eligible apps by recent usage.\n\nUse supported UsageStatsManager.\n\nSuggested window:\nlast 30 days.\n\nRanking should combine:\n\nforeground usage\n+\nrecency\n\nDeterministic tie-break.\n\n==================================================\n24. P1 ASSIGNMENT\n==================================================\n\nP1:\n\ntop 8 eligible usage-ranked apps\n\nafter excluding Dock packages.\n\n==================================================\n25. P2 ASSIGNMENT\n==================================================\n\nP2:\n\nnext 8 eligible usage-ranked apps\n\nafter excluding Dock packages.\n\n==================================================\n26. DOCK CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nDock contains exactly 5 semantic entries:\n\nDock[0] = Phone\nDock[1] = Messages/SMS\nDock[2] = Browser\nDock[3] = Music\nDock[4] = WhatsApp\n\nDock is NOT usage ranked.\n\n==================================================\n27. PHONE\n==================================================\n\nResolve default Phone using public Android/default-role API.\n\nNo hardcoded Phone package.\n\nIf unresolved:\nslot empty.\n\n==================================================\n28. MESSAGES\n==================================================\n\nResolve default SMS/Messages using public role/default API.\n\nNo hardcoded Google Messages.\n\nIf unresolved:\nslot empty.\n\n==================================================\n29. BROWSER\n==================================================\n\nResolve current default browser using supported Android API /\ndefault HTTPS handler.\n\nIf unresolved:\nslot empty.\n\n==================================================\n30. MUSIC\n==================================================\n\nResolve a reliable default audio/music handler where possible.\n\nNo random music app.\n\nNo usage-ranked fallback.\n\nIf no reliable default:\nslot empty.\n\n==================================================\n31. WHATSAPP\n==================================================\n\nThis slot is explicitly requested to be WhatsApp.\n\nResolve standard WhatsApp only if installed and launchable.\n\nDo NOT replace it with another messaging app automatically.\n\nIf standard WhatsApp is not installed:\nDock[4] = empty.\n\nDocument this as the one explicit product-specific Dock rule.\n\n==================================================\n32. DOCK EXCLUSION\n==================================================\n\nAll non-empty Dock packages MUST be excluded from P1/P2 usage\nranking.\n\nNo duplicates caused by first-install autofill.\n\n==================================================\n33. FIRST INSTALL ONLY\n==================================================\n\nAutomatic population runs once.\n\nAfter established Home:\n\nno automatic P1/P2 reorder.\n\nManual user choices always win.\n\nNo background UsageStats monitoring.\n\n==================================================\n34. ICON SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nCreate Settings → Icons.\n\nOptions:\n\nSystem / Original icons\nIcon pack\n\n==================================================\n35. ORIGINAL ICON MODE\n==================================================\n\nOriginal/System:\n\nuse app's normal icon as resolved by Core AppVisuals.\n\nDo not reshape unless Android's normal icon mask/presentation\nrequires it.\n\n==================================================\n36. ICON PACK MODE\n==================================================\n\nAdd an icon-pack selection contract.\n\nDo not bundle giant icon packs in worm.\n\nDetect compatible installed icon packs only through safe/public\npackage/resource mechanisms.\n\nIf no icon pack is selected:\n\nfallback to Original/System.\n\nPersist selected icon-pack package identity.\n\n==================================================\n37. ICON PACK FAILURE\n==================================================\n\nIf selected pack:\n\nuninstalled\nmissing icon\nbroken resource\n\nfallback per-app to original icon.\n\nNever render blank icon.\n\n==================================================\n38. TIME SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nCreate Settings → Time.\n\nOptions:\n\nTime zone\nTime format\n\n==================================================\n39. TIME ZONE\n==================================================\n\nDefault:\nSystem time zone\n\nOptionally allow selecting another valid zone using java.time\nZoneId IDs.\n\nDo not invent a custom timezone database.\n\nUse system/java.time timezone data.\n\nPersist selected zone only when user overrides System.\n\n==================================================\n40. AM / PM\n==================================================\n\nAdd time format:\n\nSystem\n24-hour\n12-hour AM/PM\n\nSystem:\nfollow Android system preference.\n\n12-hour:\ndisplay AM/PM.\n\n24-hour:\nno AM/PM.\n\n==================================================\n41. TIME UI SCOPE\n==================================================\n\nDo not add a huge clock to Home unless a clock UI already exists\nor later patch requests it.\n\nThis patch creates the setting/state capability.\n\n==================================================\n42. FAV BACKGROUND SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nSettings → Appearance → Fav background\n\nAllow user to choose among implemented lightweight presets.\n\nBaseline:\n\nDefault\nDynamic\nNothing-like effect\n\n==================================================\n43. NOTHING-LIKE EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nImplement an ORIGINAL worm effect inspired by minimal monochrome\ndot/texture aesthetics.\n\nDo not copy proprietary Nothing OS assets.\n\nUse code-generated effect only.\n\nExamples allowed:\n\ndot matrix\nsubtle moving dots\nhigh-contrast monochrome texture\nslow parallax/noise-like procedural pattern\n\nNo copied wallpaper/resource.\n\n==================================================\n44. FAV EFFECT SWITCH\n==================================================\n\nProvide switch:\n\nFav visual effect\nON/OFF\n\nON:\nselected Fav effect active.\n\nOFF:\nplain themed Fav surface.\n\nPersist setting.\n\n==================================================\n45. FAV BACKGROUND OWNER\n==================================================\n\nFav background presentation belongs to UI.\n\nCore stores only selected option/state if persistence is required.\n\nNo bitmap stored in Core.\n\n==================================================\n46. SETTINGS CHANGELOG\n==================================================\n\nAdd Settings → About → Changelog.\n\nUser-facing only.\n\nNo internal patch terminology.\n\nDo NOT display:\n\nUI-001\nUI-002\nPATCH\nruntime owner\ncheckpoint\nR8 audit\nCore implementation details\n\n==================================================\n47. CHANGELOG CONTENT\n==================================================\n\nInitial entries may include only actually implemented product changes:\n\n- new worm Home\n- gesture feedback\n- first-run setup\n- Search\n- Settings\n- icon options\n- initial Home organization\n\nKeep concise.\n\n==================================================\n48. SETTINGS SUBCATEGORY GLYPHS\n==================================================\n\nEvery main Settings category gets one small meaningful glyph.\n\nSuggested semantic mapping:\n\nAppearance → palette/tune\nHome → home\nSearch → search\nIcons → grid/apps\nTime → schedule\nSystem → settings\nAbout → info\n\nUse vector/system icons.\n\nDo not use fake decorative application icons.\n\n==================================================\n49. SINGLE SETTINGS STORE\n==================================================\n\nOne Settings state/persistence owner.\n\nExample real keys only:\n\ndynamicColorEnabled\nstatusBarMode\nsearchAppsEnabled\nsearchWebEnabled\nsearchShortcutsEnabled\nsearchHiddenEnabled\nsearchWorkProfileEnabled\niconMode\niconPackPackage\ntimeZoneMode\ntimeZoneId\ntimeFormat\nfavEffectEnabled\nfavBackgroundMode\n\nNo placeholder keys.\n\n==================================================\n50. SINGLE CORE OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHomeSnapshot owner = 1\nAppCatalog owner = 1\nSlotRepository owner = 1\nAppVisuals owner = 1\nSettingsStore owner = 1\nFirstInstall owner = 1\n\nNo duplicate persistence.\n\n==================================================\n51. UI PATCH COMPATIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nUI-006 may revise prior active UI patches where explicitly requested:\n\nALLOWED:\n\nHome top position\nSearch shell insertion\nP1/P2 empty state\n\nDO NOT regress:\n\nUI-003 width\nDock external placement\nP1/P2 equality\nUI-004 LEFT/RIGHT stretch\nUI-004 edge policy\nUI-002 UP reveal behavior\n\n==================================================\n52. GESTURE CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\nMaterial stretch from left edge.\n\nRIGHT:\nMaterial stretch from right edge.\n\nUP:\nvertical reveal + semantic haptic.\n\nUP:\nNO horizontal stretch.\n\nHome system edge Back/Forward UI:\nnone from worm's own gesture layer.\n\n==================================================\n53. STATUS BAR + WALLPAPER\n==================================================\n\nHome remains wallpaper-aware.\n\nDo not add a custom black Home root.\n\nStatus bar mode AUTO derives appearance from wallpaper/system colors.\n\nSettings uses its own Material/Dynamic Color surface.\n\nFirst-install remains fullscreen black as explicitly designed.\n\n==================================================\n54. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nNo continuous:\n\nUsageStats polling\nwallpaper pixel analysis\nPackageManager scanning\nwork-profile scanning\nshortcut scanning\n\nCache/update through appropriate lifecycle events.\n\nSearch typing hot path uses in-memory catalog/index.\n\n==================================================\n55. PRIVACY\n==================================================\n\nUsageStats:\nlocal only.\n\nHidden-app list:\nlocal only.\n\nSearch history:\nmemory/local according to its explicit later contract.\n\nNo telemetry.\n\nNo network analytics.\n\n==================================================\n56. APK SIZE BUDGET\n==================================================\n\nRelease/R8 target:\n\n<= 7 MB\n\nPreferred:\n4–6 MB.\n\nAvoid:\n\nlarge raster backgrounds\nbundled icon packs\ncustom font packs\nlarge animation dependencies\nduplicate Material icon libraries\n\nUse vectors/procedural Canvas.\n\n==================================================\n57. FEEDBACK REVISIONS\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nUI+CORE+OPTION-006-r1\nUI+CORE+OPTION-006-r2\nUI+CORE+OPTION-006-r3\n...\n\nUntil device-approved.\n\nDo not create multiple active implementations.\n\nOld revisions:\narchive only.\n\n==================================================\n58. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/UI-CORE-OPTION-006.md\n\nDocument:\n\nSettings hierarchy\nSettings keys\nstatus-bar modes\nSearch providers\nicon modes\ntimezone/time-format modes\nFav effects\nfirst-install particles\nusage ranking\nDock semantic resolver\ndevice feedback\nstatus\n\n==================================================\n59. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm UI+CORE+OPTION-006 COMPLETE\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nHomeSnapshot owners:\n<n>\n\nAppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nSettingsStore owners:\n<n>\n\nFirstInstall owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSettings Dynamic Color:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCustom black Settings wallpaper:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSettings root categories:\n<n>\n\nChangelog:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHome top gap:\n<dp>\n\nStatus bar mode:\n<AUTO/WHITE/BLACK>\n\nWallpaper auto appearance:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearch shell:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearch magnifier left:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearch underline count:\n<n>\n\nP1 empty state:\n<GLYPH_TEXT/OTHER>\n\nP2 empty state:\n<GLYPH_TEXT/OTHER>\n\nFirst-install particles:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nP1 usage autofill:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP2 usage autofill:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock Phone:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY>\n\nDock Messages:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY>\n\nDock Browser:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY>\n\nDock Music:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY>\n\nDock WhatsApp:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY>\n\nDock packages excluded from P1/P2:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearch Apps switch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearch Web switch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearch Shortcuts switch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearch Hidden switch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearch Work Profile switch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nOriginal icons:\n<YES/NO>\n\nIcon pack support:\n<YES/NO>\n\nTime zone setting:\n<YES/NO>\n\n12h AM/PM:\n<YES/NO>\n\n24h:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFav background options:\n<list>\n\nFav effect switch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nNothing-like original effect:\n<YES/NO>\n\nUI-003 width regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nUI-004 gesture regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nP1/P2 equality regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nDock external regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease APK size:\n<value>\n\nRelease <= 7 MB:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DRAFT/DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:390:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787342041,"text":"FASE — UI+DEV-007 DEBUG STATUS\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI+DEV-007\n\nTYPE:\nDEVELOPMENT ONLY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAdd a very small developer-only Debug Status screen to worm.\n\nIt must show the simplified patch/test status directly on device.\n\nThis is NOT a user-facing feature.\n\n==================================================\n1. DEBUG ONLY\n==================================================\n\nDebug Status must be available only in DEBUG builds.\n\nPreferred:\n\nBuildConfig.DEBUG\n\nRelease/R8:\n\nDebug Status UI = NOT REACHABLE\n\nDo not create a user setting to enable it.\n\n==================================================\n2. ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nAdd a temporary DEV entry inside Settings:\n\nDebug\n\nSubtitle:\n\nPatch status\n\nOnly visible when:\n\nBuildConfig.DEBUG == true\n\nRelease:\nrow absent completely.\n\n==================================================\n3. DEBUG SCREEN\n==================================================\n\nUse a compact scrollable list.\n\nFormat:\n\nUI-001 — Home\n✓ Home/container\n✓ Fav Apps\n! P1\n✓ P2\n✓ Dock\nSTATUS: DEVICE TEST\n\nUI-002 — Motion\n✓ Left\n✓ Right\n! Up\n✓ Down\n✓ Haptic\nSTATUS: DEVICE TEST\n\netc.\n\nNo large cards.\n\nNo complicated dashboard.\n\n==================================================\n4. STATUS SYMBOLS\n==================================================\n\nUse only:\n\n✓ = OK\n! = BUG\n~ = DA SISTEMARE\n○ = NON TESTATO\n\nKeep them immediately readable.\n\n==================================================\n5. PATCH LIST\n==================================================\n\nShow:\n\nUI-001 — Home\n\nUI-002 — Motion\n\nUI-003 — Width\n\nUI-004 — Gestures\n\nUI+OPTION-005 — First Install\n\nUI+CORE+OPTION-006 — System\n\nUI+DEV-007 — Debug\n\n==================================================\n6. UI-001\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nHome/container\nFav Apps\nP1\nP2\nDock outside container\nGap/borders/corners\n\n==================================================\n7. UI-002\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nSwipe Left\nSwipe Right\nMaterial Stretch\nSwipe Up +25%\nSwipe Down\nHaptic\n\n==================================================\n8. UI-003\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nContainer width\nFav width\nP1/P2 width\nDock width\nSide margins\n\n==================================================\n9. UI-004\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nNo edge Back\nNo edge Forward\nLeft edge Stretch\nRight edge Stretch\nUp without Stretch\nUp Haptic\nDiagonal arbitration\n\n==================================================\n10. UI+OPTION-005\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nHexagon icon\nCentered X\nAdaptive icon\nFirst Install\nLogo\nParticles\nDefault Home\nContinue\n\n==================================================\n11. UI+CORE+OPTION-006\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nSettings\nGlyphs/subcategories\nDynamic Color\nChangelog\nHome/status-bar gap\nStatus bar Auto/White/Black\nSearch bar\nP1/P2 empty state\nP1 usage autofill\nP2 usage autofill\nDock Phone\nDock Messages\nDock Browser\nDock Music\nDock WhatsApp\nSearch Apps\nSearch Web\nSearch Shortcuts\nSearch Hidden\nSearch Work Profile\nOriginal icons\nIcon Pack\nTimezone\n12h/24h\nFav background\nFav effect\n\n==================================================\n12. GLOBAL\n==================================================\n\nAt bottom show:\n\nGLOBAL\n\nCore\nDebug build\nR8\nRelease <= 7 MB\nCrash\nRegressions\n\nKeep concise.\n\n==================================================\n13. DATA MODEL\n==================================================\n\nUse one tiny DEV-only model.\n\nConcept:\n\nDebugPatchStatus(\n    name,\n    items,\n    status\n)\n\nDebugItem(\n    label,\n    state\n)\n\nDo not create persistence for this.\n\n==================================================\n14. NO AUTOMATIC FAKE PASS\n==================================================\n\nImportant:\n\nDo NOT automatically mark device tests as ✓ just because\nstatic analysis/build passed.\n\nDevice-dependent items default to:\n\n○ NON TESTATO\n\nOnly explicitly confirmed results may become:\n\n✓\n!\n~\n\n==================================================\n15. BUILD RESULTS\n==================================================\n\nBuild/static information may be populated from compile-time\ndevelopment metadata if already available.\n\nDo NOT:\n\nexecute shell commands from Android\nread /opt paths from Android runtime\nparse projectctl files on device\n\nNo filesystem coupling.\n\n==================================================\n16. NO SENSITIVE INFORMATION\n==================================================\n\nNever display:\n\nfilesystem paths\ncheckpoint paths\nSHA-256 values\nuser/device IDs\nkeys\nenvironment variables\nlogs containing private information\n\nOnly development status labels.\n\n==================================================\n17. VISUAL\n==================================================\n\nUse current Settings visual language:\n\nsystem font\nDynamic Color\nsmall glyphs\ncompact spacing\n\nDebug screen should still look native to worm.\n\n==================================================\n18. CORE\n==================================================\n\nCore modification:\nNONE preferred.\n\nDebug Status belongs to DEV UI.\n\nNo HomeSnapshot changes.\n\nNo AppCatalog changes.\n\nNo persistence changes.\n\n==================================================\n19. SIZE\n==================================================\n\nKeep implementation tiny.\n\nNo new dependency.\n\nNo image assets.\n\nNo debug dashboard library.\n\n==================================================\n20. RELEASE STRIPPING\n==================================================\n\nVerify release/R8:\n\nDebug Settings row:\nABSENT\n\nDebug screen reachable:\nNO\n\nDebug status data:\nremoved/shrunk where possible\n\nNo release navigation route to Debug.\n\n==================================================\n21. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/UI-DEV-007.md\n\nThis document may contain the development checklist.\n\n==================================================\n22. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\nVerify separately:\n\nDEBUG:\nDebug Status visible\n\nRELEASE:\nDebug Status absent\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm UI+DEV-007 DEBUG STATUS COMPLETE\n\nDebug entry:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDebug-only:\n<YES/NO>\n\nPatch groups:\n<n>\n\nSimplified status list:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDevice tests default NON TESTATO:\n<YES/NO>\n\nNew persistence:\n<n>\n\nNew dependencies:\n<n>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nDebug Status in release:\n<ABSENT/PRESENT>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:391:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787343350,"text":"FASE — UI-002 MATERIAL STRETCH FEEDBACK REWRITE\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI-002\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT / REWRITE\n\nCORE:\nSTABLE / READ ONLY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRewrite UI-002 so LEFT / RIGHT swipes use only the\nMaterial 3 / modern Android stretch-style overscroll feedback.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\n- NO edge Back arrow\n- NO edge Forward behavior\n- NO animation on normal touch/tap\n- NO visual deformation just by touching the display\n- Stretch starts only after a real horizontal swipe is recognized\n- UP gesture is NOT part of this rewrite\n\n==================================================\n1. LEFT SWIPE\n==================================================\n\nSwipe LEFT:\n\napply bounded Material stretch feedback.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- starts only after horizontal drag threshold\n- no edge arrow\n- no Back action\n- no page navigation\n- no permanent translation\n- returns smoothly to rest on release\n\n==================================================\n2. RIGHT SWIPE\n==================================================\n\nSwipe RIGHT:\n\nsame Material stretch behavior mirrored.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- starts only after horizontal drag threshold\n- no edge arrow\n- no Forward/navigation behavior\n- no permanent translation\n- returns smoothly to rest\n\n==================================================\n3. NO TOUCH ANIMATION\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nACTION_DOWN / initial finger contact must produce:\n\nstretch = 0\nscale = 1\ntranslation = 0\nvisual feedback = NONE\n\nDo NOT animate merely because user touches the screen.\n\nAnimation begins only when:\n\nhorizontal movement > touchSlop\nAND horizontal axis wins gesture arbitration.\n\n==================================================\n4. TOUCH SLOP\n==================================================\n\nUse Android ViewConfiguration touchSlop.\n\nBefore threshold:\n\nHome remains visually EXACTLY still.\n\nAfter threshold:\n\nlock gesture to horizontal axis and begin stretch.\n\nDo not use arbitrary 1–2px thresholds.\n\n==================================================\n5. AXIS LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDetermine gesture intent from movement.\n\nHorizontal only when:\n\nabs(dx) > touchSlop\nAND\nabs(dx) > abs(dy)\n\nOnce horizontal is accepted:\n\nlock to horizontal for the gesture.\n\nDo not switch between vertical/horizontal owners mid-drag.\n\n==================================================\n6. MATERIAL STRETCH CHARACTER\n==================================================\n\nTarget feel:\n\nmodern Android / Material elastic overscroll.\n\nMust be:\n\nsoft\nsubtle\nbounded\nnon-linear\nresistant near maximum\nsmooth on release\n\nDo NOT implement:\n\nsimple slide\npage translation\nlarge scale\nbounce animation\nspring that throws Home around\n\n==================================================\n7. LEFT ORIGIN\n==================================================\n\nFor LEFT-directed interaction:\n\nvisual stretch must feel anchored to the appropriate edge,\nnot like the whole Home is simply translated.\n\nNo central scale pulse.\n\n==================================================\n8. RIGHT ORIGIN\n==================================================\n\nMirror LEFT behavior.\n\nLEFT / RIGHT intensity:\nsymmetric.\n\n==================================================\n9. MAXIMUM EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nKeep effect intentionally small.\n\nThe Home must remain recognizably fixed in place.\n\nUse a strict bounded maximum deformation.\n\nDo not let Fav/P1/P2/Dock travel outside their intended\nvisual region.\n\n==================================================\n10. RELEASE\n==================================================\n\nOn finger release/cancel:\n\nreturn stretch to neutral.\n\nReturn must be:\n\nshort\nsmooth\nMaterial-like\n\nNo overshoot required.\n\nNo secondary bounce.\n\n==================================================\n11. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\nno haptic\n\nRIGHT:\nno haptic\n\nMOVE:\nno haptic\n\nTouch:\nno haptic\n\nUI-002 horizontal gesture is VISUAL feedback only.\n\n==================================================\n12. NO EDGE NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nworm Home must not expose its own:\n\nBack arrow\nForward arrow\nhorizontal page navigation\n\nHorizontal swipe result:\nvisual stretch only.\n\n==================================================\n13. SYSTEM GESTURE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nUse supported Android APIs.\n\nDo not globally break system navigation.\n\nDo not introduce hidden APIs.\n\nworm must not draw an edge indicator itself.\n\n==================================================\n14. UI GEOMETRY LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nHome width\nHome height\nFav geometry\nP1 geometry\nP2 geometry\nDock geometry\nspacing\nborders\ncorners\n\nUI-002 owns motion feedback only.\n\n==================================================\n15. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nNo changes to:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nAppCatalog\nSlotRepository\npersistence\nLauncherActions\n\n==================================================\n16. SINGLE MOTION OWNER\n==================================================\n\nHorizontal stretch owners:\n1\n\nDuplicate horizontal pointer owners:\n0\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n0\n\n==================================================\n17. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nGesture MOVE hot path:\n\ndisk IO = 0\nnetwork = 0\nPackageManager = 0\npersistence = 0\nhaptic = 0\n\nAvoid allocating growing objects on every MOVE event.\n\n==================================================\n18. DEVICE FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nUse simplified feedback:\n\nUI-002\n\n[ ] LEFT stretch\n[ ] RIGHT stretch\n[ ] No edge arrow\n[ ] No navigation\n[ ] No animation on touch\n[ ] Stretch starts only after swipe\n[ ] Effect subtle\n[ ] Release smooth\n[ ] First touch unaffected\n\nStatus values:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ DA SISTEMARE\n○ NON TESTATO\n\n==================================================\n19. DEBUG STATUS\n==================================================\n\nUpdate DEV-only Debug Status entry for UI-002 with:\n\nLEFT stretch\nRIGHT stretch\nNo edge\nNo touch animation\nSwipe threshold\nRelease\n\nDefault device state:\n○ NON TESTATO\n\nDo not expose this in release.\n\n==================================================\n20. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nUpdate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/UI-002.md\n\nRecord:\n\nrevision\ntouchSlop strategy\naxis lock\nmaximum deformation\nrelease behavior\ndevice feedback\n\n==================================================\n21. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm UI-002 MATERIAL STRETCH REWRITE COMPLETE\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nLEFT stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRIGHT stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nEdge indicator:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nHorizontal navigation:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nAnimation on ACTION_DOWN:\n<NO/YES>\n\nTouchSlop used:\n<YES/NO>\n\nAxis lock:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nMaximum deformation:\n<value>\n\nRelease:\n<SMOOTH/OTHER>\n\nHorizontal haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nGesture owners:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n<n>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DRAFT/DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:392:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787343904,"text":"FASE — UI-002 EDGE TOUCH MATERIAL STRETCH REWRITE\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI-002\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT / REWRITE\n\nCORE:\nSTABLE / READ ONLY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRifare UI-002 con questo comportamento preciso:\n\nTOCCO VICINO AL BORDO SINISTRO O DESTRO\n→ prepara il feedback Material 3 Stretch\n\nSWIPE ORIZZONTALE DAL BORDO\n→ attiva lo Stretch Material 3 / Android moderno\n\nNESSUNA:\n- freccia edge\n- navigazione Back\n- navigazione Forward\n- pagina precedente/successiva\n- animazione al semplice touch nel centro del display\n\n==================================================\n1. EDGE ZONES\n==================================================\n\nDefinire due zone sensibili:\n\nLEFT EDGE ZONE\nRIGHT EDGE ZONE\n\nUsare una larghezza contenuta.\n\nTarget iniziale:\n~24–32dp dal bordo.\n\nNon rendere tutto il display una edge-zone.\n\n==================================================\n2. SIMPLE TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nSe l'utente tocca il centro della Home:\n\nnessuna animazione.\n\nSe tocca dentro LEFT/RIGHT edge zone:\n\nnon deformare immediatamente tutta la Home.\n\nIl touch deve solo armare il possibile gesto edge.\n\n==================================================\n3. EDGE SWIPE START\n==================================================\n\nQuando:\n\nACTION_DOWN è dentro una edge zone\n\ne\n\nmovimento orizzontale supera touchSlop\n\nallora:\n\nattiva Material Stretch.\n\nLEFT edge:\nstretch con origine dal bordo sinistro.\n\nRIGHT edge:\nstretch con origine dal bordo destro.\n\n==================================================\n4. MATERIAL 3 STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nIl feedback deve sembrare elastic overscroll moderno.\n\nCaratteristiche:\n\n- piccolo\n- morbido\n- elastico\n- non lineare\n- resistente aumentando la distanza\n- limitato\n- nessuna traslazione permanente\n\nNon usare semplice translationX.\n\nNon usare grande scale dell'intera Home.\n\n==================================================\n5. EDGE ORIGIN\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\n\nla deformazione deve essere percepita come proveniente\ndal bordo sinistro.\n\nRIGHT:\n\nstesso comportamento specchiato dal bordo destro.\n\nNon partire dal centro del container.\n\n==================================================\n6. NO EDGE ARROW\n==================================================\n\nNon disegnare:\n\nBack arrow\nForward arrow\nedge indicator\nnavigation chevron\n\nExpected:\n\nEdge visual indicator:\nNONE\n\n==================================================\n7. NO NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nLo swipe LEFT/RIGHT da bordo serve SOLO come feedback visivo.\n\nNon deve:\n\nnavigare\ncambiare pagina\nchiudere Home\naprire Activity\neseguire Back\neseguire Forward\n\n==================================================\n8. TOUCH SLOP\n==================================================\n\nUsare:\n\nViewConfiguration.touchSlop\n\nPrima di superare touchSlop:\n\nstretch = 0\n\nHome geometry:\nimmutata.\n\nDopo soglia:\n\ninizia stretch progressivo.\n\n==================================================\n9. AXIS FILTER\n==================================================\n\nAttivare Stretch solo se:\n\nabs(dx) > touchSlop\nAND\nabs(dx) > abs(dy)\n\nSe il gesto è prevalentemente verticale:\n\nUI-002 non interviene.\n\n==================================================\n10. CENTER SWIPES\n==================================================\n\nSwipe orizzontale iniziato lontano dai bordi:\n\nNO edge Stretch.\n\nQuesto feedback deve essere specifico del bordo.\n\nSe in futuro esisterà un'altra gesture centrale,\ndeve avere un owner separato.\n\n==================================================\n11. RELEASE\n==================================================\n\nAl rilascio:\n\nritorno immediato ma morbido a stato neutro.\n\nNo rimbalzo grande.\n\nNo seconda oscillazione.\n\nNo overshoot evidente.\n\n==================================================\n12. CANCEL\n==================================================\n\nACTION_CANCEL:\n\nritorno allo stato neutro.\n\nNessuna deformazione residua.\n\n==================================================\n13. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nLEFT/RIGHT:\nno haptic.\n\nEdge touch:\nno haptic.\n\nMOVE:\nno haptic.\n\nRelease:\nno haptic.\n\nQuesta patch è feedback VISIVO soltanto.\n\n==================================================\n14. HOME GEOMETRY LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT modify:\n\nHome width\nHome height\nFav\nSearch\nP1\nP2\nDock\ngaps\ncorners\nborders\n\nUI-002 modifica solo il feedback edge.\n\n==================================================\n15. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nPersistence:\nNO\n\nHomeSnapshot:\nUNCHANGED\n\nAppCatalog:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n16. GESTURE OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nEdge horizontal gesture owner:\n1\n\nDuplicate owners:\n0\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n0\n\n==================================================\n17. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nDurante MOVE:\n\nno disk\nno network\nno PackageManager\nno persistence\nno coroutine per event\nno allocation crescente\n\n==================================================\n18. DEV DEBUG FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nAggiornare Debug Status DEV-only:\n\nUI-002\n\n○ Left edge touch\n○ Left Material Stretch\n○ Right edge touch\n○ Right Material Stretch\n○ No edge arrow\n○ No navigation\n○ No center-touch animation\n○ Smooth release\n\nUsare:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ DA SISTEMARE\n○ NON TESTATO\n\n==================================================\n19. DEVICE FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nSul Pixel verificare:\n\nLEFT EDGE\n[ ] tocco bordo non muove subito Home\n[ ] piccolo swipe attiva Stretch\n[ ] origine visiva sinistra\n[ ] nessuna freccia\n[ ] nessun Back\n\nRIGHT EDGE\n[ ] tocco bordo non muove subito Home\n[ ] piccolo swipe attiva Stretch\n[ ] origine visiva destra\n[ ] nessuna freccia\n[ ] nessuna navigazione\n\nCENTER\n[ ] touch normale = nessuna animazione\n[ ] swipe centrale = nessun edge Stretch\n\nRELEASE\n[ ] torna morbido a zero\n[ ] nessun rimbalzo forte\n\n==================================================\n20. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nUpdate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/UI-002.md\n\nRecord:\n\nrevision\nedge-zone width\ntouchSlop\naxis filter\nstretch maximum\nrelease duration/behavior\ndevice feedback\n\n==================================================\n21. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm UI-002 EDGE MATERIAL STRETCH COMPLETE\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nLeft edge zone:\n<dp>\n\nRight edge zone:\n<dp>\n\nTouchSlop:\n<value>\n\nLEFT Stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRIGHT Stretch:\n<YES/NO>\n\nLEFT origin:\n<LEFT_EDGE/OTHER>\n\nRIGHT origin:\n<RIGHT_EDGE/OTHER>\n\nEdge arrow:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nNavigation paths:\n<n>\n\nCenter touch animation:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCenter swipe edge-stretch:\n<NO/YES>\n\nRelease:\n<SMOOTH/OTHER>\n\nHorizontal haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nGesture owners:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n<n>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DRAFT/DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:393:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787373974,"text":"FASE — PATCH 00X MATERIAL STRETCH ENGINE DEBUG/FIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI-00X — MATERIAL STRETCH ENGINE FIX\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT / DEBUG\n\nCORE:\nREAD ONLY / STABLE\n\nPROBLEM\n\nMaterial 3 horizontal stretch is not working on device.\n\nDo NOT retune blindly.\n\nFirst identify the exact failure point, then apply the minimum fix.\n\n==================================================\n1. AUDIT CURRENT GESTURE PATH\n==================================================\n\nTrace exact runtime path:\n\nACTION_DOWN\n→ edge-zone detection\n→ touchSlop\n→ axis lock\n→ horizontal drag accepted\n→ stretch progress update\n→ visual transform applied\n→ release/reset\n\nReport where the chain currently stops.\n\n==================================================\n2. VERIFY EDGE ZONES\n==================================================\n\nReport actual:\n\nleft edge width\nright edge width\n\nConfirm ACTION_DOWN inside edge sets:\n\nedgeCandidate = LEFT or RIGHT\n\nIf not:\nfix detection.\n\n==================================================\n3. VERIFY TOUCH SLOP\n==================================================\n\nUse ViewConfiguration.touchSlop.\n\nReport actual threshold.\n\nConfirm horizontal movement really exceeds it on normal Pixel swipe.\n\nIf threshold logic blocks too aggressively:\nfix only that logic.\n\n==================================================\n4. VERIFY AXIS LOCK\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nabs(dx) > touchSlop\nAND\nabs(dx) > abs(dy)\n\nOnce accepted:\nlock horizontal.\n\nDo not allow vertical owner to steal the gesture after lock.\n\nReport:\n\nhorizontal accepted:\n<YES/NO>\n\n==================================================\n5. VERIFY STRETCH STATE\n==================================================\n\nReport the exact state variable controlling stretch.\n\nRequired:\n\ninitial = 0f\n\nduring accepted drag:\nmust change continuously\n\nrelease/cancel:\nreturns to 0f\n\nIf state remains 0:\nfix state update.\n\n==================================================\n6. VERIFY VISUAL APPLICATION\n==================================================\n\nFind where stretch state is actually applied.\n\nReport whether current code uses:\n\ngraphicsLayer\ndrawWithContent\nlayout transform\nscale\ntranslation\ncustom deformation\nother\n\nCritical:\n\nstate update without a visual consumer = broken.\n\nEnsure one real visual consumer exists.\n\n==================================================\n7. NO SIMPLE TRANSLATION\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT implement stretch as only:\n\ntranslationX\n\nNeed a bounded elastic deformation.\n\nPreferred acceptable approximation:\n\nedge-biased scale/deformation using graphicsLayer with:\n\nLEFT:\ntransformOrigin biased to left edge\n\nRIGHT:\ntransformOrigin biased to right edge\n\nsmall bounded scaleX change\noptional tiny counter-translation if needed\n\nDo NOT move Home across screen.\n\n==================================================\n8. MATERIAL-LIKE RESPONSE\n==================================================\n\nUse non-linear resistance.\n\nConcept:\n\nnormalizedDrag = dragDistance / width\n\nresisted = f(normalizedDrag)\n\nwhere growth slows near max.\n\nClamp hard.\n\nTarget effect:\nsmall/subtle.\n\nDo not exceed a visually strong deformation.\n\n==================================================\n9. EDGE ORIGIN\n==================================================\n\nLEFT:\npivot/origin = left edge\n\nRIGHT:\npivot/origin = right edge\n\nDo not stretch from center.\n\n==================================================\n10. CENTER TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nCenter touch:\nno stretch.\n\nCenter swipe:\nno edge stretch.\n\nOnly accepted edge-origin gesture drives stretch.\n\n==================================================\n11. RELEASE ANIMATION\n==================================================\n\nOn UP/CANCEL:\n\nanimate state back to 0f.\n\nShort duration.\n\nNo large bounce.\n\nNo second oscillation.\n\nIf current reset is instantaneous and invisible:\nuse a short spring/tween only for return.\n\n==================================================\n12. NO HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nHorizontal stretch remains visual only.\n\nHaptic paths:\n0\n\n==================================================\n13. NO EDGE INDICATOR\n==================================================\n\nNo:\nBack arrow\nForward arrow\nChevron\nEdge indicator\n\n==================================================\n14. DEBUG TEMP INSTRUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nIn DEBUG build only, add minimal temporary counters/logging for:\n\nedgeCandidate\nhorizontalAccepted\nmaxStretchReached\nreleaseCount\n\nDo NOT log every MOVE frame verbosely.\n\nRelease build:\ndebug instrumentation absent.\n\n==================================================\n15. DEVICE DEBUG STATUS\n==================================================\n\nUpdate DEV-only status:\n\nUI-002 Material Stretch\n\n[ ] Edge candidate detected\n[ ] Horizontal threshold passed\n[ ] Stretch state changes\n[ ] Visual transform applied\n[ ] Left origin correct\n[ ] Right origin correct\n[ ] Release returns to zero\n\nUse:\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ FIXED/RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n16. GEOMETRY LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT modify:\n\nHome width\nHome height\nFav\nSearch\nP1\nP2\nDock\nspacing\nborders\ncorners\n\n==================================================\n17. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\n==================================================\n18. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm MATERIAL STRETCH ENGINE DEBUG COMPLETE\n\nFailure point:\n<EDGE_DETECTION / TOUCH_SLOP / AXIS_LOCK / STATE_UPDATE / VISUAL_CONSUMER / RELEASE / OTHER>\n\nLeft edge candidate:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRight edge candidate:\n<YES/NO>\n\nTouchSlop:\n<value>\n\nHorizontal accepted:\n<YES/NO>\n\nStretch state changes:\n<YES/NO>\n\nVisual transform applied:\n<YES/NO>\n\nTransform method:\n<value>\n\nLeft origin:\n<LEFT_EDGE/OTHER>\n\nRight origin:\n<RIGHT_EDGE/OTHER>\n\nMax deformation:\n<value>\n\nCenter touch stretch:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCenter swipe stretch:\n<NO/YES>\n\nRelease to zero:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHorizontal haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DEVICE_TEST / FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:394:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787374323,"text":"FASE — UI-00X DISPLAY ADAPTATION / REFERENCE FIT\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI-00X — DISPLAY ADAPTATION\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT / DEVICE_TEST\n\nCORE:\nREAD ONLY / STABLE\n\nREFERENCE:\nuse approved screenshot stored under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/ui-display/\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAdapt the entire Home UI geometry to the actual device display\nwhile preserving the approved visual reference.\n\nDo NOT redesign the UI.\n\nDo NOT modify Core.\n\nDo NOT modify Search behavior.\n\nDo NOT modify gesture behavior.\n\nThis patch owns only:\n\n- responsive sizing\n- safe insets\n- vertical placement\n- horizontal margins\n- container scaling\n- display-fit behavior\n\n==================================================\n1. REFERENCE\n==================================================\n\nUse the approved screenshot as authoritative visual target.\n\nCompare:\n\n- top position\n- Home width\n- Home height\n- Fav size\n- P1 size\n- P2 size\n- Dock size\n- horizontal margins\n- vertical gaps\n- status-bar gap\n- bottom safe-area gap\n\nDo not infer a different design.\n\n==================================================\n2. DISPLAY METRICS\n==================================================\n\nUse actual Compose/Android window constraints.\n\nConsider:\n\n- usable width\n- usable height\n- status bar inset\n- navigation/gesture inset\n- display cutout\n\nDo NOT use hardcoded physical screen coordinates.\n\n==================================================\n3. STATUS BAR\n==================================================\n\nHome starts below status bar.\n\nKeep a small intentional gap.\n\nTarget starting range:\n\n12–20dp after safe top inset.\n\nNo content under clock/signal/battery.\n\n==================================================\n4. HOME WIDTH\n==================================================\n\nHome width must adapt proportionally.\n\nPreferred target:\n\n~92–94% usable display width\n\nor the measured reference ratio.\n\nKeep left/right margins symmetric.\n\nNo full edge-to-edge Home surface.\n\n==================================================\n5. HOME HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nHome height must be content-driven.\n\nDo NOT use:\n\nfillMaxHeight()\nweight(1f)\nlarge screen-relative minHeight\n\nNo giant blank vertical regions.\n\n==================================================\n6. FAV\n==================================================\n\nKeep Fav proportions from reference.\n\nAdapt only width and placement.\n\nDo not stretch Fav vertically unless required by reference.\n\n==================================================\n7. P1 / P2\n==================================================\n\nP1 and P2 remain equal.\n\nRequired:\n\nP1 width == P2 width\nP1 height == P2 height\n\nScale to display without changing slot count.\n\nKeep:\n\nP1 = 8\nP2 = 8\n\n==================================================\n8. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock remains outside Home container.\n\nDock width adapts with Home width.\n\nKeep:\n\n5 slots\none row\n\nDo not attach Dock to bottom system bar.\n\n==================================================\n9. HORIZONTAL MARGINS\n==================================================\n\nMeasure actual usable width.\n\nCompute margins responsively.\n\nTarget:\n\nleft margin == right margin\n\nAvoid arbitrary per-device constants.\n\n==================================================\n10. VERTICAL GAPS\n==================================================\n\nMaintain proportional spacing.\n\nKey gaps:\n\nstatus bar → Home\nFav → Search\nSearch → P1\nP1 → P2\nHome → Dock\nDock → navigation safe area\n\nDo not accumulate duplicate padding + Spacer paths.\n\n==================================================\n11. SMALL / LARGE DISPLAY HANDLING\n==================================================\n\nOn smaller usable heights:\n\nreduce gaps slightly before shrinking P1/P2 content.\n\nOn larger displays:\n\ndo not excessively stretch Home.\n\nKeep Home visually compact.\n\n==================================================\n12. ORIENTATION\n==================================================\n\nPrimary target:\nportrait phone.\n\nIf landscape is unsupported:\nfail gracefully / keep stable layout.\n\nDo not redesign landscape in this patch unless already required.\n\n==================================================\n13. DENSITY\n==================================================\n\nUse dp/sp.\n\nNo px constants for layout geometry.\n\nText respects system font scaling without breaking panel bounds.\n\n==================================================\n14. IME\n==================================================\n\nKeyboard opening must not permanently reflow Home geometry.\n\nPreserve anchored Home layout.\n\nSearch/IME handling remains owned by its existing patch.\n\n==================================================\n15. GESTURE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nMaterial Stretch\nedge handling\nUP reveal\nhaptic\ntouchSlop\naxis lock\n\nDisplay adaptation only.\n\n==================================================\n16. REFERENCE DEBUG\n==================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/UI-DISPLAY.md\n\nRecord:\n\nreference screenshot\ndevice resolution\nusable bounds\nstatus-bar inset\nnavigation inset\nHome width ratio\nHome top gap\nDock bottom gap\ncurrent revision\ndevice feedback\n\n==================================================\n17. DEV STATUS\n==================================================\n\nAdd DEV-only checks:\n\nUI-DISPLAY\n\n○ Status bar gap\n○ Home width\n○ Home vertical fit\n○ P1/P2 equal\n○ Dock outside Home\n○ Dock bottom safe\n○ Margins symmetric\n○ Reference parity\n\nUse:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ DA SISTEMARE\n○ NON TESTATO\n\n==================================================\n18. DEVICE FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nSimplified feedback:\n\nUI-DISPLAY\n\n[ ] Home under status bar correctly\n[ ] Width correct\n[ ] Left/right margins correct\n[ ] Fav size correct\n[ ] P1/P2 size correct\n[ ] Dock size correct\n[ ] Home height correct\n[ ] Bottom safe-area correct\n[ ] No clipping\n[ ] Reference match\n\n==================================================\n19. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nPersistence:\nNO\n\nAppCatalog:\nUNCHANGED\n\nHomeSnapshot:\nUNCHANGED\n\n==================================================\n20. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm UI DISPLAY ADAPTATION COMPLETE\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nReference:\n<path>\n\nDisplay size:\n<value>\n\nUsable width:\n<value>\n\nUsable height:\n<value>\n\nStatus bar inset:\n<value>\n\nNavigation inset:\n<value>\n\nHome width:\n<value>\n\nHome width ratio:\n<percent>\n\nHome top gap:\n<dp>\n\nLeft margin:\n<dp>\n\nRight margin:\n<dp>\n\nMargins symmetric:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFav size:\n<value>\n\nP1 size:\n<value>\n\nP2 size:\n<value>\n\nP1 == P2:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock size:\n<value>\n\nDock outside Home:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock bottom safe gap:\n<dp>\n\nClipping:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nReference parity:\n<MATCH/MINOR_MISMATCH/MAJOR_MISMATCH>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DRAFT/DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:395:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787374725,"text":"FASE — UI-00X SETTINGS SUBCATEGORY SWIPE BACK\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI-00X — SETTINGS NAVIGATION / SWIPE BACK\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT / DEVICE_TEST\n\nCORE:\nREAD ONLY / STABLE\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAdd swipe-back navigation inside Settings subcategories.\n\nBehavior:\n\nSettings root\n→ tap category\n→ open subcategory\n\nInside subcategory:\n\nswipe RIGHT\n→ return to previous Settings level\n\nDo NOT use swipe LEFT for forward navigation.\n\nDo NOT change Home gestures.\n\n==================================================\n1. SETTINGS NAVIGATION STACK\n==================================================\n\nSettings owns one simple navigation stack.\n\nExample:\n\nSettingsRoot\n→ Appearance\n→ Fav Background\n\nBack returns one level at a time.\n\nNo nested Activity.\n\nNo duplicate Settings navigation owner.\n\n==================================================\n2. SWIPE BACK\n==================================================\n\nInside any Settings subcategory:\n\nhorizontal swipe RIGHT\nstarting from left side / left-edge region\n→ Back one Settings level\n\nNo action if already at Settings root.\n\n==================================================\n3. EDGE ZONE\n==================================================\n\nUse a contained left-edge activation region.\n\nSuggested:\n\n24–32dp\n\nDo not make every horizontal swipe inside Settings navigate Back.\n\n==================================================\n4. TOUCH SLOP\n==================================================\n\nUse Android touchSlop.\n\nBefore threshold:\nno navigation.\n\nAccepted when:\n\ndx > touchSlop\nAND\nabs(dx) > abs(dy)\nAND\ngesture direction = RIGHT\n\n==================================================\n5. VISUAL FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nDuring accepted swipe:\n\nsubcategory surface may follow finger slightly.\n\nUse small restrained translation/reveal feedback.\n\nDo NOT use Home Material Stretch here.\n\nSettings Back gesture should feel like navigation,\nnot Home overscroll.\n\n==================================================\n6. RELEASE THRESHOLD\n==================================================\n\nSettle decision:\n\nif drag progress >= ~35–45%\nOR rightward velocity exceeds threshold\n→ Back\n\notherwise\n→ return current subcategory to rest\n\nNever leave half-open page.\n\n==================================================\n7. BACK BUTTON\n==================================================\n\nKeep normal Android Back behavior too.\n\nInside subcategory:\n\nsystem Back\n→ previous Settings level\n\nAt Settings root:\n\nsystem Back\n→ close Settings\n\nSwipe and Back button/system Back must use same navigation owner.\n\n==================================================\n8. SUBCATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nApply to all Settings subcategories, including:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nIcons\nTime\nSystem\nAbout\n\nand any second-level page such as:\n\nAppearance → Fav Background\nAppearance → Status Bar\nSearch → Sources\nIcons → Icon Pack\nTime → Time Zone\n\n==================================================\n9. NO SWIPE ON ROOT\n==================================================\n\nAt Settings root:\n\nright swipe must NOT accidentally dismiss unless that behavior\nis already explicitly approved.\n\nPreferred:\nno subcategory-back gesture when stack depth = 0.\n\n==================================================\n10. VERTICAL SCROLL\n==================================================\n\nSettings lists remain vertically scrollable.\n\nVertical movement must not trigger Back.\n\nAxis lock required.\n\nStrong vertical gesture:\nscroll owner wins.\n\nStrong horizontal-right edge gesture:\nBack owner wins.\n\n==================================================\n11. SWITCH / ROW SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nSwipe-back recognizer must not break:\n\nswitch taps\nrow taps\nsliders\nicon-pack selection\ntimezone selection\n\nFirst touch remains functional.\n\n==================================================\n12. LEFT SWIPE\n==================================================\n\nLEFT swipe inside Settings:\n\nno Forward navigation.\n\nDo not invent page-forward history.\n\nExpected:\nNO ACTION\n\nunless another specific Settings component already owns it.\n\n==================================================\n13. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nNo haptic during MOVE.\n\nOn accepted Back:\noptional one light semantic confirmation only if current worm\nSettings haptic policy requires it.\n\nPreferred first revision:\nno extra haptic.\n\n==================================================\n14. HOME GESTURE ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nWhile Settings is open:\n\nHome LEFT/RIGHT Material Stretch must NOT trigger through Settings.\n\nHome UP reveal must NOT trigger through Settings.\n\nSettings owns interaction within its visible bounds.\n\n==================================================\n15. SINGLE OWNER\n==================================================\n\nSettings navigation owner:\n1\n\nSettings swipe-back owner:\n1\n\nDuplicate BackHandlers:\n0\n\nDuplicate navigation stacks:\n0\n\n==================================================\n16. DEBUG STATUS\n==================================================\n\nUpdate DEV-only debug list:\n\nSETTINGS NAVIGATION\n\n○ Root → subcategory\n○ Left-edge swipe RIGHT\n○ Back one level\n○ System Back one level\n○ Vertical scroll unaffected\n○ Switch first touch\n○ No LEFT forward\n○ Home gestures blocked behind Settings\n\nStatus symbols:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ DA SISTEMARE\n○ NON TESTATO\n\n==================================================\n17. DEVICE FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nSimplified Pixel feedback:\n\nSETTINGS\n\n[ ] Open subcategory\n[ ] Swipe RIGHT returns back\n[ ] Swipe requires intentional edge gesture\n[ ] Vertical scroll works\n[ ] Switches work first touch\n[ ] System Back works\n[ ] LEFT does nothing\n[ ] No Home gesture leak\n[ ] No navigation jump/jank\n\n==================================================\n18. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nNo changes to:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nAppCatalog\nSlotRepository\nSearch engine\nSettings persistence schema\n\nunless a navigation preference already exists, which should not\nbe necessary.\n\n==================================================\n19. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm SETTINGS SWIPE BACK COMPLETE\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSettings navigation owners:\n<n>\n\nSwipe-back owners:\n<n>\n\nLeft edge zone:\n<dp>\n\nTouchSlop:\n<value>\n\nBack progress threshold:\n<value>\n\nVelocity threshold:\n<value>\n\nSubcategory swipe Back:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSettings root swipe dismiss:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSystem Back:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nVertical scroll regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nSwitch first-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nLEFT forward navigation:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nHome gesture leak:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nDuplicate BackHandlers:\n<n>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DRAFT/DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:396:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787375493,"text":"FASE — UI-00X SETTINGS COMPACT REDESIGN\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI-00X — SETTINGS COMPACT REDESIGN\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT / DEVICE_TEST\n\nCORE:\nREAD ONLY / STABLE\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRedesign ONLY the Settings UI so it becomes:\n\n- much more compact\n- cleaner\n- less card-heavy\n- organized by categories / subcategories\n- one glyph per category\n- switches aligned on the right\n- minimal borders\n- native/system-like visual density\n\nDo NOT change Settings functionality unless required\nfor the new visual hierarchy.\n\n==================================================\n1. SETTINGS ROOT\n==================================================\n\nUse a compact root list.\n\nSuggested categories:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nIcons\nTime\nSystem\nAbout\n\nEach category row:\n\nglyph left\ntitle\nshort subtitle optional\nchevron right\n\nNo large cards.\n\nNo oversized category blocks.\n\n==================================================\n2. GLYPHS\n==================================================\n\nEvery category must have one small meaningful glyph.\n\nSuggested:\n\nAppearance → palette/tune\nHome → home\nSearch → search\nIcons → apps/grid\nTime → schedule\nSystem → settings\nAbout → info\n\nGlyphs must be:\n\nsmall\nconsistent\nsingle-color\nDynamic Color aware\n\nNo fake app icons.\n\n==================================================\n3. SUBCATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nTap category:\nopen a compact subcategory page.\n\nExample:\n\nAppearance\n  Dynamic Color\n  Status bar\n  Fav background\n\nSearch\n  Apps\n  Web\n  Shortcuts\n  Hidden apps\n  Work profile\n\nIcons\n  Original icons\n  Icon pack\n\nTime\n  Time zone\n  Time format\n\nSystem\n  Default Home\n  App info\n\nAbout\n  Version\n  Changelog\n\n==================================================\n4. ROW DESIGN\n==================================================\n\nEach option row:\n\nleft:\ntitle\noptional small subtitle\n\nright:\nswitch OR value OR chevron\n\nNo large internal cards.\n\nNo border around every row.\n\nUse spacing/dividers only where useful.\n\n==================================================\n5. SWITCHES\n==================================================\n\nFor boolean settings:\n\nswitch must be on the RIGHT.\n\nExamples:\n\nDynamic Color              [switch]\nSearch apps                [switch]\nWeb results                [switch]\nHidden apps                [switch]\nWork profile               [switch]\nFav visual effect          [switch]\n\nDo not place switch below text.\n\nDo not center switch.\n\n==================================================\n6. NON-BOOLEAN OPTIONS\n==================================================\n\nFor selectable values:\n\nStatus bar                 Auto >\nIcon mode                  Original >\nTime zone                  System >\nTime format                System >\nFav background             Default >\n\nUse value text + chevron right.\n\nNo switch for multi-choice settings.\n\n==================================================\n7. DENSITY\n==================================================\n\nMake Settings significantly more compact.\n\nSuggested row height:\n\n~48–56dp\n\nCategory row:\n~52–60dp\n\nSubtitles:\nsmall / muted\n\nReduce excessive:\n\ntop padding\nbottom padding\ncard padding\nsection gaps\n\n==================================================\n8. BORDERS\n==================================================\n\nRemove most borders.\n\nExpected:\n\nfull-screen Settings surface\n+\nsimple rows\n+\noptional subtle separators\n\nDo NOT put rounded border/card around every option.\n\nUse border only for:\n\nspecial preview/control if genuinely needed.\n\n==================================================\n9. CORNERS\n==================================================\n\nDo not overuse rounded cards.\n\nRoot/subcategory list should feel mostly flat.\n\nIf a grouped surface is used:\n\nsmall number of groups only\nsubtle radius\nno nested card-inside-card design.\n\n==================================================\n10. DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nSettings visual must use Material 3 Dynamic Color when enabled.\n\nUse theme tokens for:\n\nbackground\nsurface\nprimary\nonSurface\nonSurfaceVariant\noutlineVariant\n\nNo hardcoded bright colors.\n\n==================================================\n11. TYPOGRAPHY\n==================================================\n\nUse system/Material typography.\n\nCategory title:\nmedium emphasis\n\nOption title:\nbody/medium\n\nSubtitle:\nsmall and muted\n\nDo not use giant headers.\n\n==================================================\n12. TOP BAR\n==================================================\n\nCompact Settings top bar.\n\nContents:\n\nBack\nSettings\n\nOptional small subtitle only if useful.\n\nNo oversized app branding header.\n\nRespect status bar inset.\n\n==================================================\n13. SUBCATEGORY TITLE\n==================================================\n\nEach subcategory page uses:\n\nBack\nCategory name\n\nExample:\n\n<  Search\n\nRows start soon below header.\n\nAvoid large blank top region.\n\n==================================================\n14. SWIPE BACK\n==================================================\n\nPreserve previous Settings swipe-back behavior.\n\nInside subcategory:\n\nleft-edge swipe RIGHT\n→ previous Settings level\n\nDo not modify Home gestures.\n\n==================================================\n15. SEARCH SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nCompact example:\n\nSearch\n\nApps                    [ON]\nWeb results             [ON]\nShortcuts               [ON]\nHidden apps             [OFF]\nWork profile            [ON]\n\nOne row per option.\n\nNo separate cards.\n\n==================================================\n16. APPEARANCE SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nCompact example:\n\nAppearance\n\nDynamic Color           [ON]\nStatus bar              Auto >\nFav background          Default >\nFav visual effect       [ON]\n\n==================================================\n17. ICON SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nIcons\n\nIcon source             Original >\nIcon pack               None >\n\nIf Icon source = Original:\nIcon pack row may be disabled/hidden.\n\n==================================================\n18. TIME SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nTime\n\nTime zone               System >\nTime format             System >\n\nSelections open compact choice pages/dialogs.\n\n==================================================\n19. SYSTEM SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nSystem\n\nDefault Home            >\nApp info                >\n\nNo fake switches for actions.\n\n==================================================\n20. ABOUT\n==================================================\n\nAbout\n\nVersion                  <runtime value>\nChangelog                >\n\nKeep concise.\n\n==================================================\n21. TOUCH TARGETS\n==================================================\n\nCompact does NOT mean tiny touch targets.\n\nMaintain accessible touch height.\n\nPrefer >= 48dp actionable rows.\n\nSwitch tap area must remain reliable.\n\n==================================================\n22. FIRST TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nrow tap works first touch\nswitch works first touch\nchevron/value row works first touch\nswipe Back does not block switches\n\n==================================================\n23. HOME LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT modify:\n\nHome geometry\nFav\nSearch Home\nP1/P2\nDock\nHome gestures\nMaterial Stretch\nUP reveal\n\nSettings patch only.\n\n==================================================\n24. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT modify stable Core semantics.\n\nAllowed:\nconsume existing Settings state/preferences.\n\nDo not create duplicate SettingsStore.\n\n==================================================\n25. DEV DEBUG STATUS\n==================================================\n\nUpdate DEV-only checklist:\n\nSETTINGS COMPACT\n\n○ Root categories compact\n○ Glyphs\n○ Subcategories\n○ Minimal borders\n○ Switches right aligned\n○ Row density\n○ Dynamic Color\n○ Swipe Back\n○ First touch\n\nUse:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ DA SISTEMARE\n○ NON TESTATO\n\n==================================================\n26. DEVICE FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nSimplified feedback:\n\nSETTINGS\n\n[ ] Compact enough\n[ ] Categories clear\n[ ] Subcategories clear\n[ ] Glyph size correct\n[ ] Too many borders removed\n[ ] Switches aligned right\n[ ] Rows not too tall\n[ ] Dynamic Color correct\n[ ] Swipe Back works\n[ ] First touch works\n\n==================================================\n27. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nUpdate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/SETTINGS-UI.md\n\nRecord:\n\nrevision\ncategory list\nsubcategory list\nrow height\nglyph size\nspacing\ndevice feedback\nstatus\n\n==================================================\n28. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm SETTINGS COMPACT REDESIGN COMPLETE\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSettingsStore owners:\n<n>\n\nRoot categories:\n<n>\n\nSubcategories:\n<n>\n\nGlyphs:\n<YES/NO>\n\nAverage row height:\n<dp>\n\nSwitches right aligned:\n<YES/NO>\n\nPer-row borders:\n<REMOVED/FOUND>\n\nDynamic Color:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSwipe Back preserved:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nHome modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DRAFT/DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:397:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787375850,"text":"FASE — UI-00X EXACT DISPLAY / REFERENCE GEOMETRY\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPATCH:\nUI-00X — EXACT DISPLAY ADAPTATION\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT / DEVICE_TEST\n\nCORE:\nSTABLE / READ ONLY\n\nAUTHORITATIVE REFERENCE:\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/ui-001/home-approved.png\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAdapt worm Home to the current Pixel display so the UI has the\nSAME VISUAL MEASUREMENTS and proportions as the approved screenshot.\n\nThis patch owns ONLY:\n\n- responsive geometry\n- reference scaling\n- display fit\n- system insets\n- margins\n- section sizes\n- section gaps\n\nDo NOT redesign the Home.\n\n==================================================\n1. REFERENCE IS AUTHORITATIVE\n==================================================\n\nThe approved screenshot defines:\n\n- Home outer width\n- Home vertical position\n- Fav size\n- Search size\n- P1 size\n- P2 size\n- Dock size\n- left/right margins\n- gaps\n- border radius proportions\n\nDo NOT choose new dimensions by eye.\n\nMeasure the screenshot proportions first.\n\n==================================================\n2. REFERENCE MEASUREMENT\n==================================================\n\nRead the reference image dimensions.\n\nMeasure normalized ratios for:\n\nHome left\nHome right\nHome top\nHome bottom\n\nFav:\nx / y / width / height\n\nSearch:\nx / y / width / height\n\nP1:\nx / y / width / height\n\nP2:\nx / y / width / height\n\nDock:\nx / y / width / height\n\nRecord ratios relative to:\n\nreference usable width\nreference usable height\n\nDo not use OCR.\n\n==================================================\n3. NORMALIZED GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nConvert reference measurements to normalized values.\n\nConcept:\n\nxRatio = referenceX / referenceWidth\nyRatio = referenceY / referenceHeight\n\nwidthRatio = referenceWidthElement / referenceWidth\nheightRatio = referenceHeightElement / referenceHeight\n\nUse these ratios to reproduce the layout on device.\n\n==================================================\n4. DEVICE USABLE BOUNDS\n==================================================\n\nAt runtime derive:\n\nscreen width\nscreen height\nstatus bar inset\nnavigation/gesture inset\ndisplay cutout\n\nDefine:\n\nusableTop\nusableBottom\nusableWidth\nusableHeight\n\nHome geometry must map reference proportions into usable bounds.\n\n==================================================\n5. STATUS BAR\n==================================================\n\nHome must start below the status bar.\n\nKeep the same visual top gap seen in reference.\n\nDo not hardcode status-bar height.\n\nUse WindowInsets.\n\n==================================================\n6. HOME WIDTH\n==================================================\n\nHome outer width must match the reference ratio.\n\nDo NOT use generic:\n\n90%\n92%\n94%\n\nunless that is what measured reference actually produces.\n\nUse measured reference width ratio.\n\nLeft/right margins must remain symmetric if they are symmetric\nin the reference.\n\n==================================================\n7. HOME VERTICAL POSITION\n==================================================\n\nMatch the reference vertical placement.\n\nDo NOT simply:\n\nCenterVertically\nTop align\nBottom align\n\nunless measurement confirms it.\n\nCompute placement from reference ratio + current usable bounds.\n\n==================================================\n8. FAV GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nFav must match reference:\n\nwidth ratio\nheight ratio\ntop position\ninternal relation to Home\n\nDo not enlarge/reduce independently.\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nSearch must match reference exactly in:\n\nwidth\nheight\ngap from Fav\ngap from P1\n\nKeep current Search visual/functionality unchanged.\n\n==================================================\n10. P1 / P2\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference dimensions.\n\nRequired:\n\nP1 width == P2 width\nP1 height == P2 height\n\nTheir size must come from reference measurement,\nnot remaining available screen space.\n\nNo:\n\nweight(1f)\nfillMaxHeight()\nadaptive vertical stretching\n\n==================================================\n11. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock remains outside Home container.\n\nMatch reference:\n\nwidth\nheight\nHome → Dock gap\nhorizontal alignment\n\nDock must not be resized by remaining vertical space.\n\n==================================================\n12. CORNERS\n==================================================\n\nMeasure/approximate the reference visual corner family.\n\nUse one coherent radius.\n\nDo not change existing style unless current radius visibly differs\nfrom reference.\n\n==================================================\n13. INTERNAL PADDING\n==================================================\n\nMeasure relative content inset from reference where possible.\n\nUse shared tokens.\n\nAvoid duplicated:\n\npadding\nSpacer\ncontentPadding\n\nthat cause geometry drift.\n\n==================================================\n14. DENSITY INDEPENDENCE\n==================================================\n\nReference dimensions are visual proportions.\n\nRuntime implementation must use:\n\ndp\nWindowInsets\nconstraints\n\nDo NOT paste raw screenshot pixel coordinates directly into Compose.\n\n==================================================\n15. FONT SCALE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nGeometry target assumes normal/default font scale.\n\nUI must remain stable with system font scaling.\n\nDo not let larger text silently expand P1/P2/Dock dimensions.\n\nUse sensible text constraints.\n\n==================================================\n16. DISPLAY-SPECIFIC DEBUG\n==================================================\n\nIn DEBUG only, expose measured values:\n\ndisplay usable width\ndisplay usable height\nHome width\nHome height\nHome top\nFav size\nSearch size\nP1 size\nP2 size\nDock size\n\nDo NOT show this in release.\n\n==================================================\n17. REFERENCE OVERLAY DEBUG\n==================================================\n\nOptional DEBUG-only diagnostic:\n\nallow drawing subtle reference bounds/guides for:\n\nHome\nFav\nSearch\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nThis is for device alignment only.\n\nRelease:\nABSENT\n\nNo actual reference bitmap bundled in APK.\n\n==================================================\n18. NO REFERENCE IMAGE IN APK\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nThe screenshot is a development reference only.\n\nDo NOT package:\n\nhome-approved.png\n\ninside:\n\nres/\nassets/\ndrawable/\nmipmap/\n\nReference remains only under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/\n\n==================================================\n19. UI-002 / GESTURE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nMaterial Stretch\nedge gesture behavior\ntouchSlop\naxis lock\nrelease motion\n\n==================================================\n20. SETTINGS LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change Settings.\n\nThis patch affects Home display adaptation only.\n\n==================================================\n21. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nNo changes to:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nAppCatalog\nSlotRepository\nLauncherActions\npersistence\n\n==================================================\n22. DEVICE FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nAdd simplified DEV feedback:\n\nUI-DISPLAY\n\n○ Home size = reference\n○ Home position = reference\n○ Fav size = reference\n○ Search size = reference\n○ P1 size = reference\n○ P2 size = reference\n○ Dock size = reference\n○ Gaps = reference\n○ No clipping\n\nUse:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ DA SISTEMARE\n○ NON TESTATO\n\n==================================================\n23. ACCEPTANCE TOLERANCE\n==================================================\n\nTarget visual difference:\n\n<= ~2–4dp for major edges/spacing\n\nwhere practical on current device density.\n\nDo not chase sub-pixel differences.\n\nMajor geometry mismatch:\nFAIL.\n\n==================================================\n24. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm EXACT DISPLAY ADAPTATION COMPLETE\n\nReference:\n<path>\n\nReference size:\n<px>\n\nDevice usable size:\n<dp/px>\n\nHome reference ratio:\n<value>\n\nHome actual size:\n<value>\n\nHome top:\n<value>\n\nFav reference size:\n<value>\n\nFav actual size:\n<value>\n\nSearch reference size:\n<value>\n\nSearch actual size:\n<value>\n\nP1 reference size:\n<value>\n\nP1 actual size:\n<value>\n\nP2 reference size:\n<value>\n\nP2 actual size:\n<value>\n\nDock reference size:\n<value>\n\nDock actual size:\n<value>\n\nMaximum geometry deviation:\n<dp>\n\nReference image packaged in APK:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nGesture behavior modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nREFERENCE PARITY:\n<MATCH/MINOR_MISMATCH/MAJOR_MISMATCH>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DRAFT/DEVICE_TEST/STABLE>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:398:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787376608,"text":"FASE — worm Alpha+001-debug CONSOLIDATION\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nNEW ACTIVE PATCH:\nAlpha+001-debug\n\nTYPE:\nALPHA / DEBUG / REWRITABLE\n\nCORE:\nSTABLE / PROTECTED\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nConsolidate ALL currently active experimental UI / Option /\nDebug patches into ONE active development baseline:\n\nAlpha+001-debug\n\nThis becomes the only active experimental patch layer.\n\nPrevious individual patches/revisions become historical only.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT merge everything into one giant Kotlin file.\n\n\"One patch\" means:\n\nONE logical development baseline\nONE integration owner\nONE status\nONE rollback boundary\n\nInternally keep clean files/components.\n\n==================================================\n0. SAFETY CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nBefore modification:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl checkpoint pre-alpha-001-debug\n\nIf checkpoint fails:\nSTOP.\n\nRecord exact checkpoint.\n\n==================================================\n1. CONSOLIDATE THESE PATCHES\n==================================================\n\nAbsorb current active behavior from:\n\nUI-001\nUI-002\nUI-003\nUI-004\nUI+OPTION-005\nUI+CORE+OPTION-006\nUI+DEV-007\n\nand subsequent UI-00X fixes concerning:\n\n- Material Stretch\n- display/reference adaptation\n- Settings swipe Back\n- compact Settings redesign\n- reference geometry\n\ninto:\n\nAlpha+001-debug\n\n==================================================\n2. OLD PATCH STATUS\n==================================================\n\nPrevious individual patch identities become:\n\nSUPERSEDED_BY_ALPHA_001_DEBUG\n\nThey must no longer be independent runtime owners.\n\nDo NOT compile multiple historical revisions.\n\nArchive documentation/source revisions where necessary under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/archive/patches/\n\nDo not delete useful history.\n\n==================================================\n3. ACTIVE ARCHITECTURE\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\ncore/\nruntime/\npatches/\nui/\n\nCore:\nstable contracts/data/actions\n\nruntime:\nsingle integration entry\n\npatches:\nONLY current Alpha+001-debug implementation\n\nui:\ngeneric reusable visual components/theme\n\n==================================================\n4. ALPHA DIRECTORY\n==================================================\n\nPreferred active structure:\n\npatches/\n  alpha_001_debug/\n    home/\n    motion/\n    settings/\n    search/\n    onboarding/\n    initialization/\n    debug/\n\nDo NOT create:\n\npatch001/\npatch002/\npatch003/\n...\n\ninside the active runtime.\n\n==================================================\n5. SINGLE ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nRuntime path:\n\nMainActivity\n→ WormRuntime\n→ Alpha+001-debug\n→ Core\n\nMainActivity imports individual patch components:\n0\n\nWormRuntime owns active Alpha selection.\n\nActive experimental patch sets:\n1\n\n==================================================\n6. HOME VISUAL\n==================================================\n\nPreserve current approved Home direction.\n\nHome includes:\n\nFav Apps\nSearch\nP1\nP2\n\nDock remains outside the main Home container.\n\nPreserve:\n\n- widened Home geometry\n- widened Dock\n- reference-based display adaptation\n- compact proportional layout\n- status-bar safe top position\n- P1/P2 equal dimensions\n\n==================================================\n7. REFERENCE GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nKeep approved screenshot under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/\n\nas development reference only.\n\nDo NOT package reference screenshots into APK.\n\nAlpha+001-debug owns current Home geometry implementation.\n\n==================================================\n8. MATERIAL STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nConsolidate latest UI-002 behavior.\n\nLEFT/RIGHT edge gesture:\n\n→ Material 3 / modern Android stretch feedback\n\nRequired:\n\n- edge-origin visual response\n- no Back arrow\n- no Forward indicator\n- no page navigation\n- no haptic\n- no center-touch animation\n- no animation merely from ACTION_DOWN\n- real swipe/touchSlop required\n- smooth release\n\nOne horizontal motion owner.\n\n==================================================\n9. UP REVEAL\n==================================================\n\nPreserve vertical UP behavior.\n\nUP:\n\n→ expand/reveal approximately +25% space\n   between Fav Apps and P1\n\nThe revealed area may remain empty until Search functionality\nuses it.\n\nUP:\nsemantic haptic once when accepted.\n\nUP:\nNO horizontal Material Stretch.\n\nDOWN:\ncollapse to baseline.\n\n==================================================\n10. GESTURE ARBITRATION\n==================================================\n\nOne Home gesture controller preferred.\n\nRequired:\n\nhorizontal owner = 1\nvertical owner = 1\nduplicate pointer owners = 0\nfirst-touch blockers = 0\n\nAxis lock:\ndeterministic.\n\n==================================================\n11. APP ICON / IDENTITY\n==================================================\n\nPreserve worm adaptive application icon:\n\n- hexagonal mark\n- black/dark outer treatment\n- centered X\n- adaptive icon safe\n\nNo legacy Machina icon.\n\n==================================================\n12. FIRST INSTALL\n==================================================\n\nPreserve first-install experience:\n\nfullscreen\nblack base\nworm logo upper/center region\nSet worm as default Home\nContinue\n\nAdd/preserve full-screen particle-network animation.\n\nLayer:\n\nblack\n→ particles\n→ worm logo\n→ controls\n\n==================================================\n13. FIRST INSTALL STATE\n==================================================\n\nOne owner:\n\nfirstInstallCompleted\n\nDo not show onboarding after explicit completion.\n\nNo duplicate onboarding state.\n\n==================================================\n14. DEFAULT HOME\n==================================================\n\nUse supported Android Home-role flow.\n\nPrefer:\n\nRoleManager.ROLE_HOME\n\nDetect already-default state.\n\nNo hidden APIs.\n\n==================================================\n15. SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nConsolidate latest compact Settings design.\n\nSettings:\n\n- compact\n- categories\n- subcategories\n- small glyph per category\n- minimal borders\n- switches right aligned\n- Dynamic Color\n- system typography\n\nDo NOT restore old card-heavy Settings.\n\n==================================================\n16. SETTINGS ROOT\n==================================================\n\nRoot categories:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nIcons\nTime\nSystem\nAbout\n\nKeep concise.\n\n==================================================\n17. SETTINGS NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nSubcategories use one navigation stack.\n\nInside subcategory:\n\nleft-edge swipe RIGHT\n→ previous Settings level\n\nSystem Back:\nsame previous-level behavior.\n\nLEFT swipe:\nno Forward navigation.\n\nHome gestures must not leak through Settings.\n\n==================================================\n18. DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nSettings Dynamic Color:\n\nON/OFF\n\nDefault:\nON\n\nON:\nAndroid Dynamic Color where supported.\n\nOFF:\nworm fallback scheme.\n\nNo custom black Settings wallpaper.\n\n==================================================\n19. STATUS BAR\n==================================================\n\nSetting:\n\nAUTO\nWHITE\nBLACK\n\nAUTO:\nderive light/dark icon appearance from supported wallpaper/system\ncolor information.\n\nNo continuous pixel analysis.\n\n==================================================\n20. SEARCH SHELL\n==================================================\n\nHome Search:\n\nbetween Fav Apps and P1.\n\nVisual:\n\nmagnifier left\ninput/query area\nONE underline\n\nNo oversized filled search card unless current approved device\nfeedback explicitly requires it.\n\n==================================================\n21. SEARCH OPTIONS\n==================================================\n\nSettings → Search:\n\nApps\nWeb\nShortcuts\nHidden apps\nWork profile\n\nBoolean options:\nswitch right aligned.\n\nOnly real supported capability may be enabled.\n\n==================================================\n22. P1 / P2 EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nNo fake app icons.\n\nIf empty:\n\none small glyph\n\n\"No apps\"\n\n\"Add apps from Settings\"\n\nor current approved concise equivalent.\n\n==================================================\n23. INITIAL HOME POPULATION\n==================================================\n\nFirst install only:\n\nP1:\ntop 8 eligible usage-ranked apps\n\nP2:\nnext 8 eligible usage-ranked apps\n\nDock packages excluded.\n\nNo continuous UsageStats monitoring.\n\n==================================================\n24. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock semantic contract:\n\n0 Phone\n1 Messages\n2 Browser\n3 Music\n4 WhatsApp\n\nPhone/Messages/Browser:\nresolve supported default handler/role.\n\nMusic:\nresolve reliable default if available.\n\nWhatsApp:\nexplicit standard WhatsApp package only if installed/launchable.\n\nUnresolved:\nempty.\n\nNo usage-ranked Dock fallback.\n\n==================================================\n25. ICON SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nSettings → Icons:\n\nOriginal/System\nIcon Pack\n\nOriginal:\nnormal app icons.\n\nIcon Pack:\ncompatible installed pack.\n\nMissing pack/resource:\nfallback to original icon.\n\nDo not bundle an icon pack.\n\n==================================================\n26. TIME\n==================================================\n\nSettings → Time:\n\nTime zone:\nSystem or selected ZoneId\n\nTime format:\nSystem\n24-hour\n12-hour AM/PM\n\nUse java.time/system data.\n\n==================================================\n27. FAV BACKGROUND\n==================================================\n\nSettings → Appearance:\n\nFav background\nFav visual effect\n\nSupport lightweight procedural presets.\n\nInclude original worm monochrome/dot-style effect inspired by\nminimal Nothing-like visual language.\n\nDo NOT copy proprietary assets.\n\n==================================================\n28. PARTICLE ENGINE\n==================================================\n\nOne shared engine.\n\nUsed by:\n\nfirst install\nSearch/reveal where enabled\nSettings where enabled\n\nNo duplicate particle implementations.\n\nNo per-particle coroutine.\n\n==================================================\n29. CHANGELOG\n==================================================\n\nSettings → About → Changelog\n\nUser-facing only.\n\nNo:\n\nUI-001\nUI-002\nAlpha internals\nowner\ncheckpoint\nR8\nruntime architecture\n\ninside normal user changelog.\n\n==================================================\n30. DEV DEBUG\n==================================================\n\nAlpha+001-debug includes DEV-only Debug Status.\n\nSettings → Debug\n\nVisible only when:\n\nBuildConfig.DEBUG\n\nRelease:\nABSENT.\n\n==================================================\n31. DEBUG STATUS — SIMPLIFIED\n==================================================\n\nShow compact checklist:\n\nHOME\n○ Container\n○ Fav\n○ Search\n○ P1\n○ P2\n○ Dock\n\nMOTION\n○ Left Stretch\n○ Right Stretch\n○ No edge\n○ Up reveal\n○ Haptic\n\nSETTINGS\n○ Compact\n○ Glyphs\n○ Subcategories\n○ Swipe Back\n○ Dynamic Color\n\nFIRST INSTALL\n○ Logo\n○ Particles\n○ Default Home\n○ Autofill\n\nSYSTEM\n○ Status bar\n○ Icons\n○ Time\n○ Changelog\n\nUse:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ DA SISTEMARE\n○ NON TESTATO\n\n==================================================\n32. DEBUG STATUS POLICY\n==================================================\n\nDo not automatically mark device-dependent tests PASS.\n\nDefault:\n○ NON TESTATO\n\nDebug status:\nno persistence required.\n\nNo filesystem paths.\nNo hashes.\nNo secrets.\n\n==================================================\n33. CORE OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nCore remains stable.\n\nRequired:\n\nHomeSnapshot owner = 1\nAppCatalog owner = 1\nSlotRepository owner = 1\nAppVisuals owner = 1\n\nAlpha must not duplicate these.\n\n==================================================\n34. SETTINGS OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nSettingsStore owner:\n1\n\nFirstInstall owner:\n1\n\nParticle engine:\n1\n\nHome gesture controller:\n1\n\nNo duplicate mutable sources of truth.\n\n==================================================\n35. ARCHIVE OLD PATCHES\n==================================================\n\nAfter successful consolidation:\n\nactive old individual patch runtime refs:\n0\n\nArchive old revision material under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/archive/patches/\n\nDo NOT archive the active Alpha implementation.\n\n==================================================\n36. ACTIVE PATCH STATUS\n==================================================\n\nReplace fragmented status with:\n\nAlpha+001-debug\n\nState:\n\nDRAFT\nDEVICE_TEST\nSTABLE\n\nDuring current phase:\n\nDEVICE_TEST\n\nIndividual superseded patch statuses remain historical only.\n\n==================================================\n37. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/ALPHA-001-DEBUG.md\n\nInclude:\n\n- consolidated capability list\n- Core boundary\n- active owners\n- reference screenshots\n- simplified device checklist\n- known bugs\n- revision\n- status\n\n==================================================\n38. REVISION POLICY\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nAlpha+001-debug-r1\nAlpha+001-debug-r2\nAlpha+001-debug-r3\n...\n\nDo NOT create another numbered patch for every small correction.\n\nRewrite the active Alpha patch until stable.\n\n==================================================\n39. APK SIZE\n==================================================\n\nRelease/R8 target:\n\n<= 7 MB\n\nReference screenshots:\nnot packaged.\n\nDebug UI:\nrelease unreachable/shrunk.\n\nNo bundled icon pack.\n\nNo large raster backgrounds.\n\n==================================================\n40. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n41. CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT create stable checkpoint yet.\n\nAfter Pixel approval later:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl checkpoint alpha-001-stable\n\nUntil then:\nDEVICE_TEST.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm Alpha+001-debug CONSOLIDATION COMPLETE\n\nPre-consolidation checkpoint:\n<path>\n\nActive patch sets:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n1\n\nActive patch:\nAlpha+001-debug\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nOld individual patch runtime refs:\n<n>\n\nArchived revisions:\n<n>\n\nHomeSnapshot owners:\n<n>\n\nAppCatalog owners:\n<n>\n\nSlotRepository owners:\n<n>\n\nSettingsStore owners:\n<n>\n\nHome gesture owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nFirstInstall owners:\n<n>\n\nDebug Status:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDebug Status in release:\n<ABSENT/PRESENT>\n\nReference images packaged:\n<n>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease APK size:\n<value>\n\nRelease <= 7 MB:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DEVICE_TEST/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:399:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787377089,"text":"FASE — worm UNIFIED ALPHA DOCUMENTATION\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nACTIVE DOCUMENT:\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/ALPHA.md\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nUnify all active development Markdown documentation concerning:\n\n- patches\n- debug\n- feedback\n- device tests\n- UI references\n- Alpha revisions\n- known bugs\n- build status\n\ninto ONE canonical active document:\n\ndocs/ALPHA.md\n\nDo NOT modify application runtime code.\n\n==================================================\n1. AUDIT CURRENT DOCS\n==================================================\n\nScan:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/*.md\n\nIdentify documents concerning:\n\nPATCH\nUI-001...\nUI-002...\nUI-00X\nDEBUG\nFEEDBACK\nDEVICE TEST\nREFERENCE\nALPHA\nSTATUS\nmotion\nsettings\ndisplay adaptation\nfirst install\n\nClassify:\n\nMERGE_INTO_ALPHA\nKEEP_SEPARATE_ARCHITECTURE\nARCHIVE_AFTER_MERGE\n\n==================================================\n2. KEEP ONLY ARCHITECTURE DOCS SEPARATE\n==================================================\n\nThese may remain separate if present:\n\nARCHITECTURE.md\nCORE.md\n\nThey describe stable architecture/Core contracts.\n\nEverything specifically related to experimental Alpha UI,\npatches, debug and feedback belongs in ALPHA.md.\n\n==================================================\n3. CREATE ALPHA.md\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/ALPHA.md\n\nHeader:\n\n# worm Alpha\n\nActive development baseline:\nAlpha+001-debug\n\nCurrent revision:\n<actual revision>\n\nStatus:\nDEVICE_TEST\n\n==================================================\n4. ALPHA.md STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nUse this structure:\n\n# worm Alpha\n\n## Current baseline\n\n## Core lock\n\n## Active Alpha capabilities\n\n## UI reference\n\n## Home\n\n## Motion / gestures\n\n## Settings\n\n## Search\n\n## First install\n\n## P1 / P2 / Dock\n\n## Icons\n\n## Time\n\n## Particles\n\n## Debug\n\n## Device feedback\n\n## Known bugs\n\n## Build status\n\n## Revision history\n\n## Stable gate\n\n==================================================\n5. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nRecord concise permanent rule:\n\nCore is stable.\n\nAlpha may consume Core contracts.\n\nAlpha must not duplicate:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nAppCatalog\nSlotRepository\nAppVisuals\n\nCore changes require explicit architectural reason.\n\n==================================================\n6. ACTIVE CAPABILITIES\n==================================================\n\nConsolidate previous patch responsibilities.\n\nDo NOT maintain separate active UI-001/UI-002/etc documents.\n\nInside ALPHA.md describe current Alpha behavior by capability:\n\nHOME\nMOTION\nSETTINGS\nSEARCH\nFIRST INSTALL\nINITIALIZATION\nDEBUG\n\n==================================================\n7. REFERENCE\n==================================================\n\nRecord approved reference images.\n\nExample:\n\ndocs/reference/ui-001/home-approved.png\n\nFor each reference record:\n\npurpose\nstatus\nwhether currently authoritative\n\nReference images remain external files.\n\nDo NOT embed/copy them into ALPHA.md.\n\nDo NOT package them into APK.\n\n==================================================\n8. SIMPLIFIED DEBUG / FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nUse ONE compact checklist.\n\nExample:\n\n## Device feedback\n\n### HOME\n- [ ] Container\n- [ ] Fav Apps\n- [ ] Search\n- [ ] P1\n- [ ] P2\n- [ ] Dock\n- [ ] Display/reference fit\n\n### MOTION\n- [ ] LEFT Material Stretch\n- [ ] RIGHT Material Stretch\n- [ ] No edge indicator\n- [ ] No touch-only animation\n- [ ] UP reveal\n- [ ] UP haptic\n- [ ] DOWN collapse\n\n### SETTINGS\n- [ ] Compact layout\n- [ ] Glyphs\n- [ ] Categories\n- [ ] Subcategories\n- [ ] Switches right\n- [ ] Swipe Back\n- [ ] Dynamic Color\n- [ ] Status bar Auto/White/Black\n\n### SEARCH\n- [ ] Search bar\n- [ ] Apps\n- [ ] Web\n- [ ] Shortcuts\n- [ ] Hidden apps\n- [ ] Work profile\n\n### FIRST INSTALL\n- [ ] worm icon\n- [ ] Fullscreen\n- [ ] Logo\n- [ ] Particles\n- [ ] Default Home\n- [ ] Continue\n- [ ] P1 autofill\n- [ ] P2 autofill\n- [ ] Semantic Dock\n\n### SYSTEM\n- [ ] Original icons\n- [ ] Icon pack\n- [ ] Time zone\n- [ ] 12h/24h\n- [ ] Fav background/effect\n- [ ] Changelog\n\n### BUILD\n- [ ] Debug\n- [ ] R8\n- [ ] Release <= 7 MB\n- [ ] No crash\n- [ ] No regression\n\n==================================================\n9. FEEDBACK STATES\n==================================================\n\nUse simple state notation:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ FIX / RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\nDo not create large matrices.\n\nFeedback must be readable quickly.\n\n==================================================\n10. DEBUG SECTION\n==================================================\n\nDocument DEV-only Debug Status.\n\nKeep same categories as ALPHA.md feedback list.\n\nDebug UI and ALPHA.md should use matching terminology.\n\nDo not duplicate a different status taxonomy.\n\n==================================================\n11. KNOWN BUGS\n==================================================\n\nKeep one concise list.\n\nFormat:\n\n- [BUG] Material Stretch — <description>\n- [BUG] Settings — <description>\n- [RETEST] Display adaptation — <description>\n\nRemove resolved bugs from current list and record them in revision history.\n\n==================================================\n12. BUILD STATUS\n==================================================\n\nKeep latest build only:\n\nDebug:\n<status>\n\nR8:\n<status>\n\nDebug APK:\n<size>\n\nRelease APK:\n<size>\n\nRelease budget:\n<= 7 MB\n\nDo not accumulate every historical build log in ALPHA.md.\n\n==================================================\n13. REVISION HISTORY\n==================================================\n\nKeep concise history:\n\nAlpha+001-debug-r1\n- consolidated previous UI patches\n\nAlpha+001-debug-r2\n- <changes>\n\nAlpha+001-debug-r3\n- <changes>\n\nDo not copy entire old patch specifications into revision history.\n\n==================================================\n14. OLD DOCUMENTS\n==================================================\n\nAfter information has been successfully merged:\n\nmove superseded development docs to:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/archive/docs-alpha-premerge/\n\nDo NOT delete them yet.\n\nPreserve filenames.\n\n==================================================\n15. ACTIVE DOCS AFTER MERGE\n==================================================\n\nPreferred active docs:\n\ndocs/\n  ALPHA.md\n  ARCHITECTURE.md\n  CORE.md\n  reference/\n\nOptional:\nREADME.md if already useful.\n\nAvoid active:\n\nPATCH_STATUS.md\nUI-001.md\nUI-002.md\nUI-003.md\nUI-004.md\nUI-DEV-007.md\nSETTINGS-UI.md\nUI-DISPLAY.md\nmultiple feedback/status docs\n\nafter their content is merged.\n\n==================================================\n16. STATUS SOURCE OF TRUTH\n==================================================\n\nALPHA.md becomes the ONLY source of truth for:\n\nactive Alpha revision\npatch/debug state\ndevice feedback\nknown bugs\nlatest build status\nstable gate\n\nNo competing active status document.\n\n==================================================\n17. RUNTIME DEBUG SYNC\n==================================================\n\nUpdate DEV Debug terminology to match ALPHA.md where necessary.\n\nDo NOT make Android parse ALPHA.md at runtime.\n\nNo filesystem coupling.\n\nNo runtime reading of docs.\n\nOnly terminology/list structure should match.\n\n==================================================\n18. STABLE GATE\n==================================================\n\nALPHA.md must end with:\n\n## Stable gate\n\nRequired before Alpha becomes stable:\n\n- all critical Home feedback ✓\n- gestures ✓\n- Settings critical paths ✓\n- first install ✓\n- no crash\n- no first-touch regression\n- Debug SUCCESS\n- R8 SUCCESS\n- release <= 7 MB\n\nWhen satisfied:\n\nAlpha+001-debug\n→ Alpha+001 STABLE\n\n==================================================\n19. NO APPLICATION CHANGE\n==================================================\n\nApplication runtime source modified:\nNO\n\nException:\nonly DEV Debug labels may be renamed if required to synchronize\nterminology.\n\nNo behavioral changes.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm ALPHA DOCUMENTATION CONSOLIDATION COMPLETE\n\nCanonical document:\n<path>\n\nActive Alpha:\n<value>\n\nMarkdown files scanned:\n<n>\n\nMerged:\n<n>\n\nKept as architecture docs:\n<list>\n\nArchived:\n<n>\n\nActive development status docs remaining:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n1\n\nCanonical status source:\nALPHA.md\n\nReference files preserved:\n<n>\n\nRuntime behavior modified:\nNO\n\nDEV Debug terminology synchronized:\n<YES/NO>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:400:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787377780,"text":"FASE — worm ALPHA/001 FULL CONSOLIDATION\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nACTIVE BASELINE:\nAlpha/001-debug\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST\n\nCORE:\nSTABLE / PROTECTED\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nUnify ALL currently active experimental patches into ONE\ndevelopment baseline:\n\nAlpha/001-debug\n\nAt the same time:\n\n- update the complete Home UI\n- update the complete Settings UI\n- update all motion/animations\n- consolidate options/functions\n- consolidate Debug Status\n- consolidate device feedback\n- remove multiple active patch owners\n\nAfter this phase there must be only:\n\nCORE\n+\nAlpha/001-debug\n\nNo active fragmented UI-001/UI-002/UI-003/... runtime owners.\n\n==================================================\n0. SAFETY CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nBefore modification:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl checkpoint pre-alpha-001-full-consolidation\n\nIf checkpoint fails:\nSTOP.\n\n==================================================\n1. ACTIVE RUNTIME MODEL\n==================================================\n\nRequired runtime path:\n\nMainActivity\n→ WormRuntime\n→ Alpha/001-debug\n→ Core\n\nMainActivity must not import individual experimental patches.\n\nActive Alpha baseline owners:\n1\n\n==================================================\n2. ACTIVE SOURCE STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nPreferred:\n\ncom/worm/\n\ncore/\nruntime/\npatches/\n  alpha/\n    001_debug/\n      home/\n      motion/\n      search/\n      settings/\n      onboarding/\n      initialization/\n      debug/\n\nui/\n  components/\n  theme/\n\nDo NOT create separate active:\n\nUI-001\nUI-002\nUI-003\nUI-004\nUI-005\nUI-006\nUI-007\nUI-00X\n\nThose become historical origins only.\n\n==================================================\n3. OLD PATCH CONSOLIDATION\n==================================================\n\nAbsorb ALL current behavior from previous experimental patches:\n\n- Home reference UI\n- Home width changes\n- display adaptation\n- Material Stretch attempts\n- UP reveal\n- status-bar positioning\n- Search shell\n- Settings visual\n- Settings swipe Back\n- first install\n- app icon\n- particles\n- P1/P2 empty state\n- P1/P2 autofill\n- semantic Dock\n- icon settings\n- timezone/time format\n- Fav effects\n- Debug Status\n\nInto:\n\nAlpha/001-debug\n\n==================================================\n4. OLD PATCHES AFTER MERGE\n==================================================\n\nAll previous individual patch runtime implementations become:\n\nSUPERSEDED\n\nActive runtime references:\n0\n\nArchive old revision source/docs under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/archive/patches/pre-alpha-001/\n\nDo NOT compile archived source.\n\n==================================================\n5. CORE HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore remains owner of stable data/contracts only.\n\nRequired stable owners:\n\nHomeSnapshot = 1\nAppCatalog = 1\nSlotRepository = 1\nLauncherActions = 1\nAppVisuals = 1\n\nAlpha may consume Core.\n\nAlpha must NOT create duplicates.\n\n==================================================\n6. HOME UI — FULL UPDATE\n==================================================\n\nRebuild the active Home UI inside Alpha/001 using the approved\nreference screenshots.\n\nAuthoritative visual principles:\n\n- compact\n- aligned to display\n- wallpaper visible\n- dark rounded surfaces\n- consistent small borders\n- wide Home geometry\n- wide Dock\n- P1/P2 same geometry\n- Dock external\n\n==================================================\n7. HOME STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHOME CONTAINER\n├── Fav Apps\n├── Search / Reveal region\n├── P1\n└── P2\n\nGAP\n\nDOCK\n\nDock MUST remain outside Home container.\n\n==================================================\n8. DISPLAY ADAPTATION\n==================================================\n\nUse approved screenshot reference geometry.\n\nMeasure reference proportions.\n\nMap them responsively to:\n\nusable screen width\nusable screen height\nstatus bar inset\nnavigation inset\n\nDo NOT use arbitrary generic percentages when reference\nmeasurement is available.\n\nTarget major geometry deviation:\n\n<= approximately 2–4dp where practical.\n\n==================================================\n9. HOME TOP POSITION\n==================================================\n\nMove Home near top of usable display.\n\nRequired:\n\nstatus bar\n↓\nsmall safe gap\n↓\nHome\n\nStarting gap:\napproximately 12–20dp\n\nNo overlap with system status bar.\n\n==================================================\n10. HOME WIDTH\n==================================================\n\nPreserve widened Home from previous feedback.\n\nHome and Dock use reference-derived width.\n\nLeft/right margins:\nsymmetric.\n\nNo fullscreen width.\n\n==================================================\n11. FAV APPS\n==================================================\n\nFav contains:\n\nFav Apps\nApps <count>\nSettings glyph right\n\nKeep approved rounded visual.\n\nFav count derives from actual state.\n\nNo hardcoded permanent Apps 0.\n\n==================================================\n12. FAV BACKGROUND\n==================================================\n\nSupport:\n\nDefault\nDynamic\nworm monochrome/dot effect\n\nSetting:\n\nFav visual effect ON/OFF\n\nEffect must be procedural/code-generated.\n\nNo copied proprietary Nothing OS assets.\n\nNo large bitmap.\n\n==================================================\n13. SEARCH POSITION\n==================================================\n\nSearch belongs between:\n\nFav Apps\nand\nP1\n\nVisual:\n\nmagnifier LEFT\nquery/input\nONE underline\n\nNo oversized filled pill.\n\n==================================================\n14. SEARCH REVEAL\n==================================================\n\nUP gesture:\n\nexpand approximately +25% usable region between Fav and P1.\n\nExpanded order:\n\nFav\n↓\nresults / particle region\n↓\nSearchBar\n↓\nP1\n↓\nP2\n\nP1/P2/Dock geometry must remain stable.\n\n==================================================\n15. P1 / P2\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nP1 = 8\nP2 = 8\n\n4 x 2 each.\n\nSame:\n\nwidth\nheight\npadding\nradius\nborder\nicon geometry\n\nP1 == P2:\nmandatory.\n\n==================================================\n16. EMPTY P1/P2\n==================================================\n\nRemove fake app placeholders.\n\nIf empty:\n\none small glyph\n\n\"No apps\"\n\n\"Add apps from Settings\"\n\nor approved equivalent.\n\nNo multiple fake icons.\n\n==================================================\n17. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock:\n\noutside Home\n5 slots\none row\nindependent dark surface\nsame width family as Home\ncompact height\n\n==================================================\n18. MOTION — HORIZONTAL\n==================================================\n\nReplace all failed/conflicting horizontal animation paths with ONE\nowner.\n\nLEFT/RIGHT edge swipe:\n\nMaterial 3 / modern Android elastic stretch feedback.\n\nRequired:\n\n- edge-origin deformation\n- bounded\n- subtle\n- non-linear resistance\n- smooth release\n- no page translation\n- no Back arrow\n- no Forward arrow\n- no navigation action\n\n==================================================\n19. MATERIAL STRETCH DEBUG\n==================================================\n\nVerify exact chain:\n\nACTION_DOWN\n→ edge candidate\n→ touchSlop\n→ horizontal axis lock\n→ stretch state update\n→ visual consumer\n→ release to zero\n\nDo not declare fixed until device test confirms visible deformation.\n\n==================================================\n20. EDGE ZONES\n==================================================\n\nUse contained left/right edge zones.\n\nSuggested starting range:\n\n24–32dp\n\nCenter touch:\nno stretch.\n\nCenter horizontal swipe:\nno edge stretch.\n\n==================================================\n21. NO TOUCH-ONLY ANIMATION\n==================================================\n\nSimple ACTION_DOWN must NOT deform Home.\n\nBefore horizontal threshold:\n\nstretch = 0\n\nOnly actual accepted swipe activates animation.\n\n==================================================\n22. UP MOTION\n==================================================\n\nUP:\n\nNO horizontal Material Stretch.\n\nUP owns:\n\nvertical reveal\n+\none semantic haptic when accepted.\n\nMOVE haptic:\n0\n\n==================================================\n23. DOWN\n==================================================\n\nDOWN from expanded state:\n\ncollapse reveal.\n\nReturn exact collapsed geometry.\n\nNo permanent spacing drift.\n\n==================================================\n24. AXIS ARBITRATION\n==================================================\n\nOne Home motion controller preferred.\n\nHorizontal when:\n\nabs(dx) > touchSlop\nAND\nabs(dx) > abs(dy)\n\nVertical when:\n\nabs(dy) > touchSlop\nAND\nabs(dy) > abs(dx)\n\nOnce locked:\ndo not switch axis mid-gesture.\n\n==================================================\n25. SETTINGS — FULL UPDATE\n==================================================\n\nRebuild Settings as compact Material/System-like UI.\n\nDo NOT use:\n\nlarge cards\nborder around each option\nhuge whitespace\ncustom black Settings wallpaper\n\nUse normal themed/Dynamic Color surface.\n\n==================================================\n26. SETTINGS ROOT\n==================================================\n\nRoot categories:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nIcons\nTime\nSystem\nAbout\n\nEach:\n\nsmall glyph left\ntitle\noptional short subtitle\nchevron/value right\n\n==================================================\n27. SETTINGS SUBCATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nUse compact rows.\n\nBoolean:\n\nlabel                    [switch]\n\nSelection:\n\nlabel                 value >\n\nAction:\n\nlabel                       >\n\nSwitches always aligned RIGHT.\n\n==================================================\n28. SETTINGS BORDERS\n==================================================\n\nRemove almost all per-row borders.\n\nUse:\n\nspacing\noptional subtle divider\nsmall grouped surface only where genuinely useful.\n\n==================================================\n29. SETTINGS GLYPHS\n==================================================\n\nSmall semantic glyph for each category.\n\nAppearance → tune/palette\nHome → home\nSearch → search\nIcons → apps/grid\nTime → schedule\nSystem → settings\nAbout → info\n\nNo decorative fake app glyphs.\n\n==================================================\n30. SETTINGS SWIPE BACK\n==================================================\n\nInside subcategories:\n\nleft-edge swipe RIGHT\n→ previous Settings level\n\nSystem Back:\nsame result.\n\nAt root:\nnormal Settings close/back behavior.\n\nLEFT swipe:\nno Forward navigation.\n\n==================================================\n31. SETTINGS GESTURE ISOLATION\n==================================================\n\nWhile Settings is open:\n\nHome Material Stretch:\nblocked behind Settings\n\nHome UP:\nblocked behind Settings\n\nVertical Settings scroll:\nworks normally.\n\nSwitch first touch:\nworks.\n\n==================================================\n32. DYNAMIC COLOR\n==================================================\n\nSettings:\n\nDynamic Color ON/OFF\n\nDefault:\nON\n\nON:\nsystem Material dynamic scheme where supported.\n\nOFF:\nworm fallback scheme.\n\n==================================================\n33. STATUS BAR SETTING\n==================================================\n\nSettings → Appearance:\n\nStatus bar:\n\nAUTO\nWHITE\nBLACK\n\nAUTO:\nderive supported light/dark system icon appearance from system\nwallpaper colors.\n\nNo continuous screenshot/pixel analysis.\n\n==================================================\n34. SEARCH SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nSettings → Search:\n\nApps\nWeb\nShortcuts\nHidden apps\nWork profile\n\nSwitch right aligned.\n\nOnly functional provider may be active.\n\n==================================================\n35. SEARCH APPS\n==================================================\n\nSearch from in-memory Core AppCatalog.\n\nNo PackageManager scan per character.\n\n==================================================\n36. SEARCH WEB\n==================================================\n\nWeb option:\n\nexternal browser ACTION_VIEW HTTPS action.\n\nNo embedded WebView.\n\nNo worm network search backend in Alpha/001.\n\n==================================================\n37. SEARCH SHORTCUTS\n==================================================\n\nUse supported public shortcut APIs only.\n\nIf unavailable:\nmark unavailable instead of fake switch behavior.\n\n==================================================\n38. HIDDEN APPS\n==================================================\n\nStore user-hidden package identities through one state owner.\n\nSearch option determines whether they appear.\n\nNo hidden/system-package guessing.\n\n==================================================\n39. WORK PROFILE\n==================================================\n\nUse allowed Android profile/launcher APIs.\n\nNo privilege bypass.\n\nIf unavailable:\ndisable/omit functionality safely.\n\n==================================================\n40. SETTINGS ICONS\n==================================================\n\nSettings → Icons:\n\nOriginal/System\nIcon Pack\n\n==================================================\n41. ORIGINAL ICONS\n==================================================\n\nUse original app icon resolved by Core AppVisuals.\n\n==================================================\n42. ICON PACK\n==================================================\n\nSupport selected installed compatible icon pack.\n\nDo not bundle icon packs.\n\nMissing icon:\nfallback to original.\n\nUninstalled pack:\nfallback to original.\n\n==================================================\n43. TIME\n==================================================\n\nSettings → Time:\n\nTime zone:\nSystem or ZoneId\n\nTime format:\nSystem\n24-hour\n12-hour AM/PM\n\nUse java.time/system timezone data.\n\n==================================================\n44. CHANGELOG\n==================================================\n\nSettings → About → Changelog\n\nUser-facing only.\n\nDo not show internal:\n\nAlpha/001\npatch IDs\nowners\nR8\ncheckpoint\ndebug architecture\n\n==================================================\n45. APP ICON\n==================================================\n\nPreserve worm adaptive icon:\n\nhexagonal visual\ndark/black outer treatment\ncentered X\n\nVector/adaptive resources only.\n\n==================================================\n46. FIRST INSTALL\n==================================================\n\nFirst install:\n\nfullscreen black base\n\nfull-screen particle-network animation\n\nworm logo upper-middle\n\nSet worm as default Home\n\nContinue\n\n==================================================\n47. FIRST INSTALL PARTICLES\n==================================================\n\nOne particle engine.\n\nLayer:\n\nblack\n→ particles\n→ logo\n→ controls\n\nParticle count bounded.\n\nNo bitmap animation.\n\nNo per-particle coroutine.\n\n==================================================\n48. FIRST INSTALL STATE\n==================================================\n\nOne owner:\n\nfirstInstallCompleted\n\nAfter explicit completion:\ndo not show again.\n\n==================================================\n49. DEFAULT HOME\n==================================================\n\nUse supported Android Home role/default flow.\n\nDetect already-default state.\n\nNo hidden APIs.\n\n==================================================\n50. INITIAL P1/P2 POPULATION\n==================================================\n\nFirst install only.\n\nIf Usage Access granted:\n\nP1:\ntop 8 eligible usage-ranked apps\n\nP2:\nnext 8\n\nUse bounded deterministic ranking.\n\nNo continuous monitoring.\n\n==================================================\n51. DOCK INITIAL POPULATION\n==================================================\n\nDock contract:\n\n0 Phone\n1 Messages\n2 Browser\n3 Music\n4 WhatsApp\n\nPhone/Messages/Browser:\ndefault supported handler/role.\n\nMusic:\nreliable default resolver only.\n\nWhatsApp:\nstandard WhatsApp only if installed and launchable.\n\nUnresolved:\nempty.\n\n==================================================\n52. DOCK EXCLUSION\n==================================================\n\nResolved Dock packages must be excluded from P1/P2 usage ranking.\n\n==================================================\n53. DEBUG STATUS\n==================================================\n\nKeep Debug Status DEV-only.\n\nSettings → Debug\n\nVisible:\nDEBUG only\n\nRelease:\nABSENT\n\n==================================================\n54. DEBUG STATUS — SIMPLIFIED\n==================================================\n\nUse one list:\n\nHOME\n○ Container\n○ Fav\n○ Search\n○ P1\n○ P2\n○ Dock\n○ Reference fit\n\nMOTION\n○ Left Stretch\n○ Right Stretch\n○ No edge\n○ Up reveal\n○ Up haptic\n○ Down collapse\n\nSETTINGS\n○ Compact\n○ Glyphs\n○ Subcategories\n○ Switches right\n○ Swipe Back\n○ Dynamic Color\n○ Status bar\n\nSEARCH\n○ Apps\n○ Web\n○ Shortcuts\n○ Hidden\n○ Work profile\n\nFIRST INSTALL\n○ Icon\n○ Particles\n○ Default Home\n○ P1 autofill\n○ P2 autofill\n○ Dock\n\nSYSTEM\n○ Icons\n○ Icon Pack\n○ Time\n○ Changelog\n○ Fav effect\n\n==================================================\n55. DEBUG FEEDBACK STATES\n==================================================\n\nUse only:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ FIX / RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\nDevice items default:\n○\n\nDo not auto-mark device tests PASS from static checks.\n\n==================================================\n56. ALPHA.md\n==================================================\n\nUpdate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/ALPHA.md\n\nThis becomes canonical source of truth for:\n\nAlpha revision\nactive capabilities\ndebug checklist\ndevice feedback\nknown bugs\nreference screenshots\nbuild status\nstable gate\n\n==================================================\n57. REFERENCE SCREENSHOTS\n==================================================\n\nKeep screenshots under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/\n\nDevelopment only.\n\nDo NOT package reference PNG/JPG files in APK.\n\n==================================================\n58. OLD DOCUMENTS\n==================================================\n\nArchive superseded patch/debug/feedback docs under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/archive/docs-pre-alpha-001/\n\nActive development status docs:\n1\n\nExpected:\nALPHA.md\n\nArchitecture/Core docs may remain separate.\n\n==================================================\n59. REVISION\n==================================================\n\nSet current:\n\nAlpha/001-debug-r1\n\nFuture fixes:\n\nAlpha/001-debug-r2\nAlpha/001-debug-r3\n...\n\nDo not open a new patch for every bug.\n\nRewrite Alpha/001 until stable.\n\n==================================================\n60. SINGLE OWNER ASSERTIONS\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHomeSnapshot = 1\nAppCatalog = 1\nSlotRepository = 1\nAppVisuals = 1\nSettingsStore = 1\nFirstInstall = 1\nParticle engine = 1\nHome motion controller = 1\nSettings navigation owner = 1\nSearch state owner = 1\n\n==================================================\n61. LEGACY RUNTIME ASSERTIONS\n==================================================\n\nActive runtime references to old:\n\nUI-001\nUI-002\nUI-003\nUI-004\nUI-005\nUI-006\nUI-007\nUI-00X\n\nExpected:\n0\n\nHistorical docs/archive excluded.\n\n==================================================\n62. APK SIZE\n==================================================\n\nRelease/R8 hard target:\n\n<= 7 MB\n\nPreferred:\n4–6 MB\n\nDo not bundle:\n\nreference screenshots\nwallpaper images\nicon packs\nlarge custom fonts\nduplicate animation libraries\n\n==================================================\n63. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\n64. DEVICE STATUS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT mark stable automatically.\n\nAfter consolidation:\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST\n\nPixel feedback required.\n\n==================================================\n65. STABLE GATE\n==================================================\n\nAlpha/001-debug may become:\n\nAlpha/001 STABLE\n\nonly when:\n\nHOME critical feedback = ✓\nMOTION critical feedback = ✓\nSETTINGS critical feedback = ✓\nFIRST INSTALL = ✓\nno crash\nno first-touch regression\nDebug SUCCESS\nR8 SUCCESS\nrelease <= 7 MB\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm ALPHA/001 FULL CONSOLIDATION COMPLETE\n\nCheckpoint:\n<path>\n\nActive baseline:\nAlpha/001-debug\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nActive experimental patch sets:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n1\n\nOld patch runtime refs:\n<n>\n\nArchived old patch revisions:\n<n>\n\nCanonical feedback document:\n<path>\n\nHome UI updated:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSettings UI updated:\n<YES/NO>\n\nAnimations updated:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDisplay adaptation integrated:\n<YES/NO>\n\nMaterial Stretch owner:\n<n>\n\nSettings navigation owner:\n<n>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nSettingsStore owners:\n<n>\n\nFirstInstall owners:\n<n>\n\nSearch state owners:\n<n>\n\nDebug Status:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDebug Status in release:\n<ABSENT/PRESENT>\n\nReference images packaged:\n<n>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSnapshot:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nRelease APK size:\n<value>\n\nRelease <= 7 MB:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSTATUS:\n<DEVICE_TEST/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:401:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787378229,"text":"ALPHA/001 — UPDATE AUTHORITATIVE HOME REFERENCE\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nREFERENCE:\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/alpha-001/home-reference.png\n\nSet this screenshot as the AUTHORITATIVE Home UI reference\nfor Alpha/001-debug.\n\nThe previous Home reference is now historical.\n\nUpdate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/ALPHA.md\n\nwith:\n\nHOME REFERENCE:\ndocs/reference/alpha-001/home-reference.png\n\nSTATUS:\nAUTHORITATIVE\n\nThe reference defines:\n\n- Home overall geometry\n- Home width\n- Home vertical proportions\n- Fav Apps size and position\n- Search position\n- Search single underline\n- P1 size\n- P2 size\n- P1/P2 equal geometry\n- empty-state proportions\n- internal gaps\n- borders\n- corner radii\n- Dock width\n- Dock height\n- Dock outside Home\n- Home → Dock gap\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe wallpaper itself is NOT part of worm UI.\n\nDo NOT package the screenshot.\nDo NOT package the wallpaper.\nDo NOT reproduce status-bar contents.\n\nUse the screenshot only for geometry/visual comparison.\n\nPrevious references:\nHISTORICAL\n\nAlpha/001 reference:\nAUTHORITATIVE\n\nProject source modified:\nNO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:402:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787378607,"text":"FASE — Alpha/002-mod REFERENCE PATCH\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nACTIVE BASELINE:\nAlpha/001-debug\n\nNEW REVISION:\nAlpha/002-mod\n\nAUTHORITATIVE REFERENCE:\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/alpha-001/home-reference.png\n\nSTATUS:\nDRAFT / DEVICE_TEST\n\nCORE:\nSTABLE / READ ONLY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nCreate Alpha/002-mod by adapting the active Home UI to match\nthe authoritative Alpha reference screenshot.\n\nDo NOT redesign from memory.\nDo NOT use older references.\nDo NOT change Core contracts.\n\nAlpha/002-mod is a visual/reference patch of the current Alpha\nbaseline.\n\n==================================================\n1. REFERENCE\n==================================================\n\nUse only:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/alpha-001/home-reference.png\n\nas authoritative Home geometry reference.\n\nPrevious references:\nHISTORICAL / IGNORE FOR CURRENT FIT\n\nThe reference defines:\n\n- Home container size\n- Home position\n- Fav Apps geometry\n- Search position\n- Search underline\n- P1 geometry\n- P2 geometry\n- empty-state scale\n- internal gaps\n- outer margins\n- borders\n- corner radii\n- Dock size\n- Dock position\n- Home → Dock gap\n\nWallpaper/status-bar contents are NOT worm UI.\n\n==================================================\n2. CREATE ALPHA/002-MOD\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT create another fragmented UI-00X owner.\n\nCreate the next active Alpha revision:\n\nAlpha/002-mod\n\nConceptually:\n\nAlpha/001-debug\n→ reference adaptation\n→ Alpha/002-mod\n\nOnly ONE Alpha implementation remains active afterward.\n\n==================================================\n3. PRE-PATCH CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nBefore changes:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl checkpoint alpha-002-mod-pre\n\nIf checkpoint fails:\nSTOP.\n\n==================================================\n4. MEASURE REFERENCE FIRST\n==================================================\n\nBefore editing UI:\n\nmeasure reference image geometry.\n\nReport approximate normalized bounds for:\n\nHome\nFav\nSearch\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nMeasure:\n\nx\ny\nwidth\nheight\ngaps\n\nUse image proportions.\n\nDo NOT use OCR.\n\nDo NOT immediately guess dp values.\n\n==================================================\n5. DISPLAY FIT\n==================================================\n\nMap reference proportions to current usable Pixel display.\n\nRespect:\n\nstatus bar inset\nnavigation/gesture inset\ndisplay cutout\n\nUse Compose constraints / WindowInsets.\n\nDo NOT use raw screenshot px as runtime coordinates.\n\n==================================================\n6. HOME\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference:\n\nwide dark outer container\nrounded corners\nsubtle outline\ncompact vertical composition\n\nHome must NOT:\n\nfill screen\nstretch to remaining height\nuse weight(1f)\n\n==================================================\n7. FAV APPS\n==================================================\n\nMatch exact reference proportions.\n\nContents:\n\nFav. apps\nApps <count>\nsettings glyph right\n\nDo not modify Core count source.\n\nKeep Fav dark rounded surface.\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference exactly:\n\nmagnifier left\nSearch text/query area\nONE line underneath\n\nNo filled Search pill.\n\nNo second outline.\n\nNo additional Search card.\n\n==================================================\n9. P1 / P2\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference dimensions.\n\nRequired:\n\nP1 width == P2 width\nP1 height == P2 height\n\nPreserve current empty-state content unless visual sizing needs\nreference correction.\n\nDo not alter slot contracts.\n\n==================================================\n10. EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nMatch screenshot scale:\n\nsmall cube glyph\nprimary text\nsecondary text\n\nDo not enlarge the empty state.\n\nDo not add fake icons.\n\n==================================================\n11. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock remains OUTSIDE Home.\n\nMatch:\n\nwidth\nheight\nradius\nborder\nhorizontal alignment\nHome → Dock gap\n\nDo not move Dock inside Home.\n\n==================================================\n12. SPACING\n==================================================\n\nReference-derived spacing only.\n\nAudit and eliminate duplicate:\n\npadding\nSpacer\ncontentPadding\nverticalArrangement spacing\n\nif they cause mismatch.\n\n==================================================\n13. MATERIAL STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT redesign Material Stretch in this patch.\n\nPreserve current active motion implementation.\n\nIf geometry changes require transform-origin recalculation,\nadapt only to new measured bounds.\n\nBehavior must remain:\n\nLEFT/RIGHT edge stretch\nno edge arrow\nno navigation\nno touch-only animation\n\n==================================================\n14. UP REVEAL\n==================================================\n\nPreserve current UP reveal contract.\n\nDo not use expanded state while measuring collapsed reference.\n\nCollapsed Alpha/002-mod must match screenshot first.\n\n==================================================\n15. SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT redesign Settings in Alpha/002-mod.\n\nKeep current consolidated Settings.\n\nThis patch is Home-reference adaptation.\n\n==================================================\n16. FIRST INSTALL\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT modify onboarding, particles, default-home flow or autofill.\n\n==================================================\n17. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modifications:\n0\n\nDo not change:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nAppCatalog\nSlotRepository\nAppVisuals\nLauncherActions\n\n==================================================\n18. DEBUG REFERENCE FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nUpdate DEV Debug Status with:\n\nALPHA/002-MOD — REFERENCE\n\n○ Home size\n○ Home position\n○ Fav size\n○ Search position\n○ P1 size\n○ P2 size\n○ Dock size\n○ Gaps\n○ Reference parity\n\nUse:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n19. ALPHA.md\n==================================================\n\nUpdate canonical:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/ALPHA.md\n\nSet:\n\nActive baseline:\nAlpha/002-mod\n\nReference:\ndocs/reference/alpha-001/home-reference.png\n\nPrevious baseline:\nAlpha/001-debug\n\nStatus:\nDEVICE_TEST\n\nAdd concise revision entry describing the reference-fit changes.\n\n==================================================\n20. REFERENCE FILE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT move or duplicate the image into app resources.\n\nReference image packaged in APK:\n0\n\n==================================================\n21. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\nSnapshot = PASS\nSHA-256 = PASS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm Alpha/002-mod REFERENCE PATCH COMPLETE\n\nPre-patch checkpoint:\n<path>\n\nActive baseline:\nAlpha/002-mod\n\nReference:\n<path>\n\nReference size:\n<value>\n\nHome measured ratio:\n<value>\n\nFav measured ratio:\n<value>\n\nSearch measured ratio:\n<value>\n\nP1 measured ratio:\n<value>\n\nP2 measured ratio:\n<value>\n\nDock measured ratio:\n<value>\n\nHome geometry updated:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFav geometry updated:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearch geometry updated:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1/P2 geometry updated:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock geometry updated:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSettings modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nMotion behavior modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nReference image packaged:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nREFERENCE PARITY:\n<MATCH/MINOR_MISMATCH/MAJOR_MISMATCH>\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:403:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787379406,"text":"FASE — Alpha/002-mod DEV DEBUG CONTROL PANEL\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nACTIVE BASELINE:\nAlpha/002-mod\n\nTYPE:\nDEV ONLY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nCreate a developer-only Debug control panel inside Settings.\n\nThe panel must let me inspect every Alpha capability and choose:\n\n- KEEP\n- PATCH\n- DISABLE\n- REMOVE\n- RETEST\n\nEvery item must keep feedback state.\n\nThis is for development only.\n\nRelease:\nDebug panel absent.\n\n==================================================\n1. SETTINGS ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nSettings → Debug\n\nSubtitle:\nAlpha/002 control\n\nVisible only in DEBUG builds.\n\n==================================================\n2. DEBUG ITEM MODEL\n==================================================\n\nEach debug item contains:\n\nname\ngroup\nfeedbackState\nactionState\nnotes\n\nFeedback states:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\nAction states:\n\nKEEP\nPATCH\nDISABLE\nREMOVE\nRETEST\n\n==================================================\n3. ROW LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nCompact row:\n\n[feedback glyph] Feature name\n\nsmall secondary text:\ncurrent action\n\nright:\naction/menu control\n\nExample:\n\n✓ Home container\n   KEEP                         >\n\n! Material Stretch\n   PATCH                        >\n\n○ Work profile\n   RETEST                       >\n\n==================================================\n4. ITEM DETAIL\n==================================================\n\nTap a row:\n\nopen compact detail page.\n\nShow:\n\nFeature\nFeedback\nAction\nShort note\nOwner\nCurrent Alpha revision\n\nControls:\n\nFeedback:\nOK / BUG / RETEST / NOT TESTED\n\nAction:\nKEEP / PATCH / DISABLE / REMOVE / RETEST\n\nOptional:\ndeveloper note text\n\n==================================================\n5. IMPORTANT SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nChanging Debug action must NOT immediately delete source code.\n\nThe panel is a planning/status tool.\n\nREMOVE means:\n\n\"candidate for removal in next Codex patch\"\n\nPATCH means:\n\n\"must be modified in next revision\"\n\nDISABLE means:\n\n\"disable in next revision\"\n\nKEEP means:\n\n\"preserve as-is\"\n\nRETEST means:\n\n\"device validation required\"\n\nNo runtime source deletion from Android UI.\n\n==================================================\n6. GROUP — HOME\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nHome container\nHome position\nHome width\nFav Apps\nSearch shell\nP1\nP2\nDock\nDock outside Home\nReference fit\nDisplay adaptation\nStatus bar gap\n\n==================================================\n7. GROUP — MOTION\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nLEFT Material Stretch\nRIGHT Material Stretch\nEdge detection\nNo edge arrow\nNo navigation\nNo touch-only animation\nTouchSlop\nAxis lock\nUP reveal\nUP +25%\nUP haptic\nDOWN collapse\nDiagonal arbitration\n\n==================================================\n8. GROUP — SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nCompact Settings\nCategories\nSubcategories\nGlyphs\nMinimal borders\nSwitches right\nDynamic Color\nSwipe Back\nSystem Back\nStatus bar Auto\nStatus bar White\nStatus bar Black\nChangelog\n\n==================================================\n9. GROUP — SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nSearch bar\nMagnifier left\nSingle underline\nApps\nWeb\nShortcuts\nHidden apps\nWork profile\nSearch history\nSearch results\n\n==================================================\n10. GROUP — FIRST INSTALL\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nworm icon\nHexagon\nCentered X\nFullscreen onboarding\nLogo\nParticles\nDefault Home\nContinue\nFirst-install completion\nP1 autofill\nP2 autofill\n\n==================================================\n11. GROUP — DOCK\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nPhone\nMessages\nBrowser\nMusic\nWhatsApp\n5 slots\nDock spacing\nDock width\nP1/P2 duplicate exclusion\n\n==================================================\n12. GROUP — ICONS\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nOriginal icons\nIcon pack\nIcon-pack fallback\nIcon shape\nAdaptive worm icon\n\n==================================================\n13. GROUP — TIME\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nSystem timezone\nCustom timezone\nSystem time format\n12h AM/PM\n24h\n\n==================================================\n14. GROUP — APPEARANCE\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nFav background\nFav visual effect\nNothing-like effect\nDynamic Color\nWallpaper-aware status bar\n\n==================================================\n15. GROUP — PARTICLES\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nParticle engine\nFirst-install particles\nSearch particles\nSettings particles\nParticle speed\nParticle lines\nPerformance\n\n==================================================\n16. GROUP — BUILD\n==================================================\n\nItems:\n\nDebug build\nR8\nSnapshot\nSHA-256\nRelease <= 7 MB\nCrash\nFirst-touch regression\nDuplicate owners\nLegacy runtime refs\n\n==================================================\n17. FILTERS\n==================================================\n\nAt top add compact filters:\n\nALL\nBUG\nPATCH\nREMOVE\nRETEST\nNOT TESTED\n\nThis makes the panel useful during development.\n\n==================================================\n18. SUMMARY\n==================================================\n\nTop summary:\n\nAlpha/002-mod\n\nOK: <n>\nBUG: <n>\nPATCH: <n>\nREMOVE: <n>\nRETEST: <n>\nNOT TESTED: <n>\n\n==================================================\n19. DEV PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nPersist Debug feedback/actions locally in DEBUG builds.\n\nUse a dedicated DEV-only store.\n\nDo NOT mix with production SettingsStore.\n\nNo cloud/network sync.\n\n==================================================\n20. RESET\n==================================================\n\nAdd:\n\nReset feedback\n\nReset only DEV feedback/actions.\n\nDo NOT reset:\n\nHome slots\nuser Settings\nfirst-install state\nCore data\n\n==================================================\n21. EXPORT FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nAdd DEV action:\n\nCopy feedback summary\n\nGenerate plain-text summary suitable for pasting into Codex.\n\nFormat example:\n\nAlpha/002-mod feedback\n\nHOME\n✓ Home container — KEEP\n! Fav Apps — PATCH\n○ Search — RETEST\n\nMOTION\n! LEFT Stretch — PATCH\n✓ UP haptic — KEEP\n\nSETTINGS\n~ Dynamic Color — RETEST\n\nREMOVE\n- Work profile\n- Settings particles\n\nThis is the main development workflow.\n\n==================================================\n22. NO CODE EXECUTION\n==================================================\n\nDebug panel must NOT:\n\nrun shell commands\nedit project files\ndelete Kotlin files\ninvoke projectctl\nmodify /opt filesystem\nexecute Codex\n\nIt only records/export feedback.\n\n==================================================\n23. ALPHA.md\n==================================================\n\nUpdate canonical development documentation:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/ALPHA.md\n\nDocument the same groups and action meanings:\n\nKEEP\nPATCH\nDISABLE\nREMOVE\nRETEST\n\nDo NOT make runtime parse ALPHA.md.\n\n==================================================\n24. RELEASE\n==================================================\n\nRelease requirements:\n\nDebug Settings row:\nABSENT\n\nDebug routes:\nUNREACHABLE\n\nDEV feedback store:\nABSENT/unreachable\n\nCopy feedback action:\nABSENT\n\nNo development text visible to users.\n\n==================================================\n25. CORE\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nDebug control panel belongs entirely to DEV UI.\n\n==================================================\n26. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm Alpha/002 DEV CONTROL PANEL COMPLETE\n\nDebug entry:\n<YES/NO>\n\nGroups:\n<n>\n\nFeedback states:\n<list>\n\nAction states:\n<list>\n\nFilters:\n<YES/NO>\n\nEditable:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDEV persistence:\n<YES/NO>\n\nReset:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCopy feedback summary:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCan delete source from app:\nNO\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug panel in release:\n<ABSENT/PRESENT>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:404:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787380514,"text":"FASE — Alpha/002-mod REFERENCE GEOMETRY REBUILD\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nACTIVE BASELINE:\nAlpha/002-mod\n\nAUTHORITATIVE REFERENCE:\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/alpha-001/home-reference.png\n\nSTATUS:\nREFERENCE_FIT_FAILED / REBUILD\n\nCORE:\nREAD ONLY / STABLE\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nThe current Alpha/002-mod Home does NOT match the approved reference.\n\nDo NOT continue with incremental dp tweaks.\n\nRebuild the Home geometry from the reference image measurements.\n\nThe reference is authoritative for:\n\n- overall Home position\n- Home width\n- Home height\n- Fav size\n- Search position\n- Search underline\n- P1 size\n- P2 size\n- Dock size\n- section gaps\n- corner proportions\n- horizontal margins\n\n==================================================\n1. MARK CURRENT FIT FAILED\n==================================================\n\nSet in ALPHA.md:\n\nAlpha/002-mod\nREFERENCE FIT:\nFAILED\n\nReason:\ndevice UI does not visually match authoritative screenshot.\n\nDo NOT mark any Home geometry item validated.\n\n==================================================\n2. MEASURE REFERENCE IMAGE FIRST\n==================================================\n\nBefore editing Compose:\n\nmeasure the screenshot bounds for:\n\nDISPLAY\nHOME OUTER\nFAV\nSEARCH\nP1\nP2\nDOCK\n\nRecord:\n\nx\ny\nwidth\nheight\n\nAlso measure:\n\nstatus bar → Home top\nHome left/right margin\nFav → Search\nSearch → P1\nP1 → P2\nHome → Dock\nDock → bottom safe region\n\nDo NOT OCR.\n\nDo NOT guess generic 90/92/94% values first.\n\n==================================================\n3. NORMALIZED RATIOS\n==================================================\n\nConvert measurements into normalized ratios.\n\nFor every element:\n\nxRatio\nyRatio\nwidthRatio\nheightRatio\n\nrelative to screenshot dimensions.\n\nUse those ratios as the source of truth.\n\n==================================================\n4. DEVICE MAPPING\n==================================================\n\nMap reference proportions to actual usable Pixel bounds.\n\nUse:\n\nWindowInsets.statusBars\nWindowInsets.navigationBars\ndisplay cutout\ncurrent constraints\n\nDo NOT map screenshot pixels directly into runtime px.\n\n==================================================\n5. HOME POSITION\n==================================================\n\nThe target Home is NOT vertically centered.\n\nIt sits in the lower-middle portion of the display with\na large wallpaper area above.\n\nMatch that exact visual placement.\n\nDo NOT move Home near the status bar in this revision.\n\nReference wins over previous top-position experiments.\n\n==================================================\n6. HOME WIDTH\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference width precisely.\n\nHome left/right margins must visually match screenshot.\n\nNo arbitrary extra widening.\n\nNo full-width container.\n\n==================================================\n7. HOME HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference total Home height.\n\nDo NOT let children expand from remaining viewport height.\n\nNo:\n\nfillMaxHeight()\nweight(1f)\nheightIn(min = large)\nscreen-percentage vertical stretching\n\nUse explicit/reference-derived geometry.\n\n==================================================\n8. FAV\n==================================================\n\nFav must match reference:\n\nsame relative width\nsame relative height\nsame left/right inset\nsame top position\n\nContents:\n\nFav. apps\nApps 0\ngear right\n\nDo not vertically enlarge or shrink beyond reference ratio.\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nTarget reference:\n\nmagnifier left\nSearch\nONE underline\n\nNo rounded Search pill.\n\nNo filled Search card.\n\nMatch:\n\nsearch vertical position\nunderline width\nleft inset\ngap below Fav\ngap above P1\n\n==================================================\n10. P1\n==================================================\n\nP1 must match reference panel size.\n\nLarge rounded dark panel.\n\nDo not compress it.\n\nDo not stretch it beyond reference.\n\n==================================================\n11. P2\n==================================================\n\nP2 must exactly match P1.\n\nRequired:\n\nP1 width == P2 width\nP1 height == P2 height\nP1 radius == P2 radius\nP1 internal padding == P2 internal padding\n\n==================================================\n12. EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference scale:\n\ncube glyph\nprimary text\nsecondary text\n\nCenter within panel.\n\nDo not use current alternative compact \"No apps\" text\nif the reference shows the longer copy.\n\nReference text hierarchy wins for Alpha/002-mod.\n\n==================================================\n13. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock remains OUTSIDE Home.\n\nMatch reference:\n\nwidth\nheight\nradius\nhorizontal alignment\nHome→Dock gap\n\nDock is a separate black rounded surface.\n\n==================================================\n14. CORNER RADII\n==================================================\n\nDerive visual radius family from reference.\n\nUse one consistent family for:\n\nHome outer\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nSearch underline has no rounded container.\n\n==================================================\n15. REMOVE CONFLICTING GEOMETRY RULES\n==================================================\n\nAudit active Alpha code for geometry inherited from:\n\nUI-003 width\ntop-position patch\ndisplay adaptation patch\nprevious generic width percentages\n\nIf these conflict with the authoritative screenshot:\n\nAlpha/002 reference geometry wins.\n\nDo not maintain two geometry owners.\n\n==================================================\n16. ONE GEOMETRY OWNER\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHome geometry owner = 1\n\nNo duplicate:\n\nwidth fractions\ntop offsets\nsection heights\nreference adapters\n\nConsolidate into one Alpha/002 Home geometry definition.\n\n==================================================\n17. DEBUG REFERENCE MODE\n==================================================\n\nDEV-only:\n\nadd a compact Reference Fit section showing:\n\nHome width\nHome top\nHome height\nFav size\nSearch Y\nP1 size\nP2 size\nDock size\n\nand per-item state:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n18. OPTIONAL DEBUG BOUNDS\n==================================================\n\nIn DEBUG only, allow temporary outline guides around:\n\nHome\nFav\nSearch\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nfor alignment.\n\nNo reference bitmap overlay required.\n\nRelease:\nguides absent.\n\n==================================================\n19. DO NOT PACKAGE SCREENSHOT\n==================================================\n\nReference remains under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/\n\nAPK reference images:\n0\n\n==================================================\n20. MOTION LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nMaterial Stretch\nUP reveal\nhaptic\nSettings\nfirst install\nSearch backend\n\nThis revision is geometry/reference only.\n\n==================================================\n21. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\n==================================================\n22. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n23. DEVICE VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nAfter installing on Pixel, compare directly against reference.\n\nRequired feedback:\n\nHOME\n[ ] position\n[ ] width\n[ ] height\n\nFAV\n[ ] size\n[ ] position\n\nSEARCH\n[ ] magnifier\n[ ] single underline\n[ ] spacing\n\nP1/P2\n[ ] equal\n[ ] correct height\n[ ] correct width\n\nDOCK\n[ ] width\n[ ] height\n[ ] external\n[ ] gap\n\nREFERENCE\n[ ] visual match\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm Alpha/002-mod REFERENCE GEOMETRY REBUILD COMPLETE\n\nReference:\n<path>\n\nCurrent fit before:\nFAILED\n\nReference image size:\n<px>\n\nMeasured Home bounds:\n<value>\n\nMeasured Fav bounds:\n<value>\n\nMeasured Search bounds:\n<value>\n\nMeasured P1 bounds:\n<value>\n\nMeasured P2 bounds:\n<value>\n\nMeasured Dock bounds:\n<value>\n\nHome geometry owners:\n<n>\n\nConflicting geometry paths removed:\n<n>\n\nHome actual bounds:\n<value>\n\nFav actual bounds:\n<value>\n\nSearch actual bounds:\n<value>\n\nP1 actual bounds:\n<value>\n\nP2 actual bounds:\n<value>\n\nDock actual bounds:\n<value>\n\nMaximum deviation:\n<dp>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST"}
