=================================================\n4. DEVICE MAPPING\n==================================================\n\nMap reference proportions to actual usable Pixel bounds.\n\nUse:\n\nWindowInsets.statusBars\nWindowInsets.navigationBars\ndisplay cutout\ncurrent constraints\n\nDo NOT map screenshot pixels directly into runtime px.\n\n==================================================\n5. HOME POSITION\n==================================================\n\nThe target Home is NOT vertically centered.\n\nIt sits in the lower-middle portion of the display with\na large wallpaper area above.\n\nMatch that exact visual placement.\n\nDo NOT move Home near the status bar in this revision.\n\nReference wins over previous top-position experiments.\n\n==================================================\n6. HOME WIDTH\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference width precisely.\n\nHome left/right margins must visually match screenshot.\n\nNo arbitrary extra widening.\n\nNo full-width container.\n\n==================================================\n7. HOME HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference total Home height.\n\nDo NOT let children expand from remaining viewport height.\n\nNo:\n\nfillMaxHeight()\nweight(1f)\nheightIn(min = large)\nscreen-percentage vertical stretching\n\nUse explicit/reference-derived geometry.\n\n==================================================\n8. FAV\n==================================================\n\nFav must match reference:\n\nsame relative width\nsame relative height\nsame left/right inset\nsame top position\n\nContents:\n\nFav. apps\nApps 0\ngear right\n\nDo not vertically enlarge or shrink beyond reference ratio.\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nTarget reference:\n\nmagnifier left\nSearch\nONE underline\n\nNo rounded Search pill.\n\nNo filled Search card.\n\nMatch:\n\nsearch vertical position\nunderline width\nleft inset\ngap below Fav\ngap above P1\n\n==================================================\n10. P1\n==================================================\n\nP1 must match reference panel size.\n\nLarge rounded dark panel.\n\nDo not compress it.\n\nDo not stretch it beyond reference.\n\n==================================================\n11. P2\n==================================================\n\nP2 must exactly match P1.\n\nRequired:\n\nP1 width == P2 width\nP1 height == P2 height\nP1 radius == P2 radius\nP1 internal padding == P2 internal padding\n\n==================================================\n12. EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference scale:\n\ncube glyph\nprimary text\nsecondary text\n\nCenter within panel.\n\nDo not use current alternative compact \"No apps\" text\nif the reference shows the longer copy.\n\nReference text hierarchy wins for Alpha/002-mod.\n\n==================================================\n13. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock remains OUTSIDE Home.\n\nMatch reference:\n\nwidth\nheight\nradius\nhorizontal alignment\nHome→Dock gap\n\nDock is a separate black rounded surface.\n\n==================================================\n14. CORNER RADII\n==================================================\n\nDerive visual radius family from reference.\n\nUse one consistent family for:\n\nHome outer\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nSearch underline has no rounded container.\n\n==================================================\n15. REMOVE CONFLICTING GEOMETRY RULES\n==================================================\n\nAudit active Alpha code for geometry inherited from:\n\nUI-003 width\ntop-position patch\ndisplay adaptation patch\nprevious generic width percentages\n\nIf these conflict with the authoritative screenshot:\n\nAlpha/002 reference geometry wins.\n\nDo not maintain two geometry owners.\n\n==================================================\n16. ONE GEOMETRY OWNER\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHome geometry owner = 1\n\nNo duplicate:\n\nwidth fractions\ntop offsets\nsection heights\nreference adapters\n\nConsolidate into one Alpha/002 Home geometry definition.\n\n==================================================\n17. DEBUG REFERENCE MODE\n==================================================\n\nDEV-only:\n\nadd a compact Reference Fit section showing:\n\nHome width\nHome top\nHome height\nFav size\nSearch Y\nP1 size\nP2 size\nDock size\n\nand per-item state:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n18. OPTIONAL DEBUG BOUNDS\n==================================================\n\nIn DEBUG only, allow temporary outline guides around:\n\nHome\nFav\nSearch\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nfor alignment.\n\nNo reference bitmap overlay required.\n\nRelease:\nguides absent.\n\n==================================================\n19. DO NOT PACKAGE SCREENSHOT\n==================================================\n\nReference remains under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/\n\nAPK reference images:\n0\n\n==================================================\n20. MOTION LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nMaterial Stretch\nUP reveal\nhaptic\nSettings\nfirst install\nSearch backend\n\nThis revision is geometry/reference only.\n\n==================================================\n21. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\n==================================================\n22. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n23. DEVICE VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nAfter installing on Pixel, compare directly against reference.\n\nRequired feedback:\n\nHOME\n[ ] position\n[ ] width\n[ ] height\n\nFAV\n[ ] size\n[ ] position\n\nSEARCH\n[ ] magnifier\n[ ] single underline\n[ ] spacing\n\nP1/P2\n[ ] equal\n[ ] correct height\n[ ] correct width\n\nDOCK\n[ ] width\n[ ] height\n[ ] external\n[ ] gap\n\nREFERENCE\n[ ] visual match\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm Alpha/002-mod REFERENCE GEOMETRY REBUILD COMPLETE\n\nReference:\n<path>\n\nCurrent fit before:\nFAILED\n\nReference image size:\n<px>\n\nMeasured Home bounds:\n<value>\n\nMeasured Fav bounds:\n<value>\n\nMeasured Search bounds:\n<value>\n\nMeasured P1 bounds:\n<value>\n\nMeasured P2 bounds:\n<value>\n\nMeasured Dock bounds:\n<value>\n\nHome geometry owners:\n<n>\n\nConflicting geometry paths removed:\n<n>\n\nHome actual bounds:\n<value>\n\nFav actual bounds:\n<value>\n\nSearch actual bounds:\n<value>\n\nP1 actual bounds:\n<value>\n\nP2 actual bounds:\n<value>\n\nDock actual bounds:\n<value>\n\nMaximum deviation:\n<dp>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:408:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787382320,"text":"FASE — worm projectctl DEBUG OUTPUT EXPORT FIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nFILE:\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl\n\nMODE:\nBUILD INFRASTRUCTURE ONLY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFix projectctl so every successful Debug build exports:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/project/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n\ninto a timestamped output directory:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/outputs/YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS/app-debug.apk\n\nDo NOT modify application source.\n\n==================================================\n1. CANONICAL PATHS\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nROOT=/opt/Android/worm\nPROJECT=/opt/Android/worm/project\nOUTPUTS=/opt/Android/worm/outputs\n\nKeep current toolchain paths unchanged.\n\n==================================================\n2. DEBUG BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun the existing Debug build path.\n\nRequired Gradle artifact:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/project/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n\nIf Debug build reports success but this APK does not exist:\n\nSTOP\nreport BUILD_ARTIFACT_MISSING\n\nDo not create fake output.\n\n==================================================\n3. OUTPUT SESSION\n==================================================\n\nAfter successful Debug build create:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/outputs/YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS/\n\nDo not overwrite previous sessions.\n\n==================================================\n4. EXPORT APK\n==================================================\n\nCopy:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/project/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n\nto:\n\n<session>/app-debug.apk\n\nUse:\n\ncp -a\n\nor equivalent safe copy.\n\nVerify destination exists and size > 0.\n\n==================================================\n5. BUILD LOG\n==================================================\n\nCapture build output into:\n\n<session>/build.log\n\nThe log must contain the actual Debug build output.\n\nDo not create an empty placeholder log.\n\n==================================================\n6. SHA256\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n<session>/SHA256SUMS\n\nAt minimum include:\n\napp-debug.apk\n\nGenerate hash from the EXPORTED file.\n\nThen verify:\n\nsha256sum -c SHA256SUMS\n\nRequired:\nPASS\n\n==================================================\n7. FAILURE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nIf build fails:\n\ndo not create a successful-looking output session.\n\nIf session directory was already created:\n\neither remove incomplete session\nor mark it explicitly FAILED.\n\nDo not leave:\n\napp-debug.apk\nSHA256SUMS\n\nfrom an older build inside a new failed session.\n\n==================================================\n8. LATEST\n==================================================\n\nIf projectctl has a latest command:\n\nensure:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl latest\n\nreports the newest valid output session containing:\n\napp-debug.apk\n\nDo not point latest to an incomplete session.\n\n==================================================\n9. NO APP CHANGES\n==================================================\n\nAllowed modification:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl\n\nOptional:\ninfrastructure documentation only.\n\nForbidden:\n\napp/src changes\nGradle dependency changes\nUI changes\nCore changes\nAlpha patch changes\n\nApplication source modified:\nNO\n\n==================================================\n10. VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nThen verify:\n\nfind /opt/Android/worm/outputs \\\n  -type f -name 'app-debug.apk' \\\n  -printf '%T@ %p\\n' \\\n  | sort -nr \\\n  | head -1\n\nAlso verify latest session contains:\n\napp-debug.apk\nbuild.log\nSHA256SUMS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm PROJECTCTL DEBUG OUTPUT EXPORT FIX COMPLETE\n\nDebug Gradle APK:\n<path>\n\nDebug Gradle APK size:\n<value>\n\nExport directory:\n<path>\n\nExported Debug APK:\n<path>\n\nDebug exported:\n<YES/NO>\n\nbuild.log:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSHA256SUMS:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSHA256 verification:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nlatest:\n<path/N-A>\n\nApplication source modified:\nNO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:409:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787383112,"text":"FASE — Alpha/002-mod EXACT HOME REFERENCE PATCH\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nACTIVE BASELINE:\nAlpha/002-mod\n\nAUTHORITATIVE REFERENCE:\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/alpha-001/home-reference.png\n\nREFERENCE TARGET:\nthe screenshot with:\n- wallpaper visible\n- Home lower on screen\n- Fav compact\n- Search not rendered as a bordered card\n- P1/P2 empty\n- Dock external\n- wide dark geometry\n- compact overall height\n\nSTATUS:\nREFERENCE_REBUILD\n\nCORE:\nREAD ONLY / STABLE\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nMake the current Home visually match the authoritative reference\nas closely as possible.\n\nDo NOT preserve incorrect geometry from the current build.\n\nDo NOT redesign.\n\nDo NOT compromise between current build and reference.\n\nREFERENCE WINS.\n\n==================================================\n1. CURRENT BUILD IS REJECTED\n==================================================\n\nThe current installed Home layout is NOT accepted.\n\nKnown mismatches:\n\n- Home positioned too high\n- Home too tall\n- Fav too tall\n- Fav surface too inflated\n- Search incorrectly rendered as bordered card\n- P1/P2 geometry differs from reference\n- populated grids must not dictate reference geometry\n- Dock presentation/placement differs\n- wallpaper visibility/proportions differ\n\nMark current reference fit:\n\nFAILED\n\n==================================================\n2. REFERENCE FIRST\n==================================================\n\nBefore changing Compose:\n\nmeasure actual reference image bounds.\n\nMeasure:\n\nHome outer:\nx\ny\nwidth\nheight\n\nFav:\nx\ny\nwidth\nheight\n\nSearch:\nx\ny\nwidth\nheight\n\nP1:\nx\ny\nwidth\nheight\n\nP2:\nx\ny\nwidth\nheight\n\nDock:\nx\ny\nwidth\nheight\n\nAlso measure:\n\ntop wallpaper area\nleft/right margins\nFav → Search gap\nSearch → P1 gap\nP1 → P2 gap\nHome → Dock gap\nDock bottom gap\n\nDo NOT use OCR.\n\n==================================================\n3. ONE GEOMETRY OWNER\n==================================================\n\nAfter this patch:\n\nHome geometry owners = 1\n\nRemove/disable conflicting active geometry logic from previous:\n\nwidth patch\ntop-position patch\ngeneric display adaptation\nold reference fitting\nweight-based sizing\nscreen percentage experiments\n\nDo not keep competing width/height systems.\n\n==================================================\n4. HOME POSITION\n==================================================\n\nMatch the reference.\n\nHome must sit noticeably LOWER than the current build.\n\nThere must be a large wallpaper region above Home.\n\nDo NOT push Home directly below status bar.\n\nDo NOT center generically.\n\nUse reference-derived vertical placement.\n\n==================================================\n5. HOME WIDTH\n==================================================\n\nMatch the reference width exactly/proportionally.\n\nKeep:\n\nleft margin ≈ right margin\n\nDo not make Home narrower or wider based on previous patch rules.\n\n==================================================\n6. HOME HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nReduce current Home height to match reference.\n\nNo:\n\nfillMaxHeight()\nweight(1f)\nremaining-space stretching\n\nHome height comes from reference-derived section geometry.\n\n==================================================\n7. HOME OUTER STYLE\n==================================================\n\nPreserve reference visual family:\n\nvery dark outer container\nrounded corners\nsubtle thin border\n\nDo not create heavy Material card elevation.\n\n==================================================\n8. FAV\n==================================================\n\nFav must match reference size.\n\nRequired:\n\nFav. apps\nApps 0 / actual count source\ngear right\n\nFav:\n\ncompact\nrounded\ndark\n\nCurrent oversized Fav height:\nREMOVE.\n\nDo not use the current large inflated card proportions.\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL.\n\nReference Search is NOT a fully bordered rounded card.\n\nMatch reference presentation:\n\nmagnifier on left\nSearch text\nsingle horizontal underline\n\nNo enclosing rounded border.\n\nNo filled pill.\n\nNo additional card background.\n\nNo double line.\n\n==================================================\n10. SEARCH GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference:\n\nleft inset\nvertical position\nunderline width\ngap above\ngap below\n\nSearch should visually sit in the open region between Fav and P1.\n\n==================================================\n11. P1\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference P1 size exactly/proportionally.\n\nFor REFERENCE FIT mode:\n\nrender reference-compatible empty state geometry.\n\nP1 must not shrink merely because app icons exist.\n\nOuter panel geometry remains fixed.\n\n==================================================\n12. P2\n==================================================\n\nSame as P1.\n\nMandatory:\n\nP1 width == P2 width\nP1 height == P2 height\nP1 radius == P2 radius\nP1 padding == P2 padding\n\n==================================================\n13. EMPTY STATE\n==================================================\n\nReference empty state:\n\nsmall center glyph\n\"No apps in this section\"\n\"Add your favorite apps to access them quickly.\"\n\nMatch:\n\nglyph scale\ntext scale\nvertical placement\n\nDo not use oversized text.\n\n==================================================\n14. DATA VS REFERENCE GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nImportant:\n\nCore app data must NOT control section geometry.\n\nIf P1/P2 have real assigned apps:\n\nsame panel dimensions remain.\n\nDo not let grid content make the panels taller/shorter.\n\nReference geometry is constant.\n\n==================================================\n15. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock remains completely OUTSIDE Home.\n\nMatch reference:\n\nsame approximate width as Home family\ncompact height\nrounded surface\nthin outline\ncorrect vertical gap\n\nCurrent Dock must be repositioned/resized as needed.\n\n==================================================\n16. DOCK DATA\n==================================================\n\nDock state must not affect Dock geometry.\n\nWhether:\n\nempty\npartially populated\nfully populated\n\nouter Dock dimensions stay reference-correct.\n\n==================================================\n17. WALLPAPER\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT bundle the reference wallpaper.\n\nUse actual system wallpaper/environment.\n\nRoot Home background should not obscure it.\n\nReference screenshot wallpaper is geometry/context only.\n\n==================================================\n18. STATUS BAR\n==================================================\n\nKeep system status bar independent.\n\nDo not reproduce screenshot status bar.\n\nDo not overlap it.\n\nBut Home top placement must follow reference visual proportion,\nnot previous \"near status bar\" patch.\n\n==================================================\n19. SYSTEM NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nDock remains safely above navigation gesture area.\n\nMatch reference bottom relation as closely as possible.\n\n==================================================\n20. CORNERS\n==================================================\n\nUse reference-derived consistent corner family for:\n\nHome\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nDo NOT make Search a rounded container.\n\n==================================================\n21. BORDERS\n==================================================\n\nUse subtle border only.\n\nCurrent visible outlines should not become heavier than reference.\n\n==================================================\n22. PADDING\n==================================================\n\nAudit all:\n\npadding()\nSpacer()\ncontentPadding\nArrangement.spacedBy()\n\nRemove stacked spacing causing current oversized layout.\n\nOne spacing owner per relationship.\n\n==================================================\n23. POPULATED GRID SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nWhen app icons render later:\n\nP1:\n4 x 2\n\nP2:\n4 x 2\n\nThey must fit inside reference panel dimensions.\n\nAdjust icon/grid spacing, not panel height.\n\n==================================================\n24. MOTION LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change in this patch:\n\nMaterial Stretch behavior\nedge detection\nUP reveal\nhaptic\naxis lock\n\nOnly adapt transforms if new Home dimensions require updated bounds.\n\n==================================================\n25. SETTINGS LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT redesign Settings.\n\n==================================================\n26. FIRST INSTALL LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nonboarding\nparticles\ndefault Home\nautofill\n\n==================================================\n27. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modifications:\n0\n\nDo not modify:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nAppCatalog\nSlotRepository\nAppVisuals\nLauncherActions\n\n==================================================\n28. DEBUG — REFERENCE FIT\n==================================================\n\nUpdate DEBUG Settings → Alpha/002 feedback:\n\nREFERENCE FIT\n\n○ Home position\n○ Home width\n○ Home height\n○ Fav geometry\n○ Search geometry\n○ Search single underline\n○ P1 geometry\n○ P2 geometry\n○ P1/P2 equality\n○ Dock geometry\n○ Home → Dock gap\n○ Wallpaper visibility\n○ Overall reference match\n\nUse:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n29. DEBUG BOUNDS\n==================================================\n\nOptional DEBUG-only toggle:\n\nShow layout bounds\n\nDraw thin diagnostic outlines for:\n\nHome\nFav\nSearch\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nNo production visibility.\n\n==================================================\n30. ALPHA.md\n==================================================\n\nUpdate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/ALPHA.md\n\nActive baseline:\nAlpha/002-mod\n\nReference fit revision:\nnext rN\n\nSet current geometry feedback:\nRETEST\n\nRecord rejected previous device result.\n\n==================================================\n31. ACCEPTANCE\n==================================================\n\nDevice acceptance target:\n\nmajor geometry deviation:\n<= approximately 2–4dp where practical\n\nMore important:\nvisual proportions must match reference.\n\nDo not chase subpixel differences.\n\n==================================================\n32. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm Alpha/002-mod EXACT REFERENCE PATCH COMPLETE\n\nRevision:\n<value>\n\nReference:\n<path>\n\nPrevious reference fit:\nFAILED\n\nHome geometry owners:\n<n>\n\nConflicting geometry paths removed:\n<n>\n\nHome position:\n<value>\n\nHome size:\n<value>\n\nFav size:\n<value>\n\nSearch presentation:\n<SINGLE_UNDERLINE/OTHER>\n\nSearch bordered container:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1 size:\n<value>\n\nP2 size:\n<value>\n\nP1 == P2:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock size:\n<value>\n\nDock outside Home:\n<YES/NO>\n\nWallpaper visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nMotion modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSettings modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nREFERENCE PARITY:\n<MATCH/MINOR_MISMATCH/MAJOR_MISMATCH>\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:410:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787384611,"text":"FASE — worm RESET TO CORE + PATCH/001 UI\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nACTIVE PATCH:\nPatch/001-UI\n\nREFERENCE:\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/alpha-001/home-reference.png\n\nCORE:\nKEEP / STABLE\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nReset the active worm runtime to the smallest clean baseline:\n\nCORE\n+\nONE UI PATCH\n\nKeep only:\n\nCore\nPatch/001-UI\n\nRemove from ACTIVE runtime everything else.\n\nPatch/001-UI must reproduce the authoritative Home reference\nand nothing more.\n\n==================================================\n0. SAFETY CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nBefore changes:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl checkpoint pre-patch-001-ui-reset\n\nIf checkpoint fails:\nSTOP.\n\n==================================================\n1. FINAL ACTIVE ARCHITECTURE\n==================================================\n\nTarget active runtime:\n\ncom/worm/\n  core/\n  runtime/\n  patches/\n    001_ui/\n  ui/\n    components/\n    theme/\n\nMeaning:\n\ncore/\n= stable data/contracts\n\nruntime/\n= one entry\n\npatches/001_ui/\n= current Home implementation\n\nui/\n= generic reusable visual primitives only\n\n==================================================\n2. REMOVE FROM ACTIVE RUNTIME\n==================================================\n\nRemove/archive all active implementations of:\n\nAlpha/001\nAlpha/002\nUI-002\nUI-003\nUI-004\nUI-005\nUI-006\nUI-007\nUI-00X\n\nAlso remove from active runtime:\n\nSearch functionality\nSettings\nDebug panel\nMaterial Stretch\nUP reveal\ngesture experiments\nparticles\nfirst install\nautofill\nUsageStats\nsemantic Dock initialization\nicon-pack support\ntimezone settings\nstatus-bar options\nFav effects\nchangelog\nwork-profile search\nweb search\nshortcuts\n\nThese may remain in archive/history only.\n\n==================================================\n3. DO NOT DELETE CORE\n==================================================\n\nPreserve stable Core contracts/data.\n\nKeep only genuinely foundational Core owners such as:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nHomeSlot\nAppCatalog\nSlotRepository\nLauncherActions\nAppVisuals\n\nDo NOT rewrite Core because of UI reset.\n\n==================================================\n4. ARCHIVE REMOVED CODE\n==================================================\n\nMove superseded runtime source to:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/archive/pre-patch-001-ui-reset/\n\nDo NOT leave old implementations inside active Android source sets.\n\nDo NOT permanently delete history yet.\n\n==================================================\n5. SINGLE RUNTIME ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nMainActivity\n→ WormRuntime\n→ Patch/001-UI\n→ Core\n\nMainActivity imports individual optional features:\n0\n\nActive UI patch owners:\n1\n\n==================================================\n6. PATCH/001 UI TARGET\n==================================================\n\nPatch/001-UI reproduces ONLY the approved screenshot reference.\n\nVisible target:\n\n- system wallpaper\n- large empty wallpaper space above\n- Home dark outer container\n- Fav Apps panel\n- P1 empty panel\n- P2 empty panel\n- external empty Dock\n\nNothing else.\n\n==================================================\n7. NO SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe authoritative screenshot does NOT contain Search.\n\nTherefore Patch/001-UI must NOT render:\n\nSearch bar\nmagnifier\nunderline\nsearch area\nsearch placeholder\nsearch results\n\nSearch comes later as another patch.\n\n==================================================\n8. HOME POSITION\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference.\n\nHome is positioned in the lower-middle portion of the display.\n\nLarge wallpaper space remains visible above.\n\nDo NOT:\n\ntop-align Home\ncenter it generically\nplace it immediately below status bar\n\nReference determines position.\n\n==================================================\n9. HOME OUTER CONTAINER\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference:\n\nwide\ncompact\ndark\nrounded\nsubtle outline\n\nNo fullscreen panel.\n\nNo fillMaxHeight.\n\nNo weight-based vertical expansion.\n\n==================================================\n10. FAV APPS\n==================================================\n\nRender:\n\nFav. apps\n\nApps 0\n\nSettings glyph on right\n\nFor Patch/001:\n\nSettings glyph is VISUAL ONLY.\n\nDo NOT implement Settings navigation.\n\n==================================================\n11. FAV GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference dimensions.\n\nDo not inflate Fav vertically.\n\nNo animated background.\n\nNo particle background.\n\nPlain dark reference surface only.\n\n==================================================\n12. P1\n==================================================\n\nRender reference empty state.\n\nOne panel.\n\nCentered:\n\nsmall outline glyph\n\nNo apps in this section\n\nAdd your favorite apps to access them quickly.\n\nNo real app grid for device-reference validation.\n\n==================================================\n13. P2\n==================================================\n\nSame component and exact geometry as P1.\n\nRequired:\n\nP1 width == P2 width\nP1 height == P2 height\nP1 radius == P2 radius\nP1 padding == P2 padding\n\n==================================================\n14. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock is OUTSIDE Home container.\n\nRender only the reference external dark Dock surface.\n\nFor Patch/001 validation:\n\nno app icons required.\n\nNo semantic initialization.\n\nNo fake icons.\n\n==================================================\n15. REFERENCE GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nMeasure the actual reference image before implementation.\n\nMeasure:\n\nHome bounds\nFav bounds\nP1 bounds\nP2 bounds\nDock bounds\n\nand gaps:\n\nscreen top → Home\nHome left/right margin\nFav → P1\nP1 → P2\nHome → Dock\nDock → bottom\n\nUse normalized reference geometry.\n\nDo not guess generic 90/92/94% values.\n\n==================================================\n16. ONE GEOMETRY OWNER\n==================================================\n\nPatch/001-UI must have ONE geometry definition.\n\nRemove all active competing:\n\nwidth rules\ntop-position rules\ndisplay adapters\nreference adapters\nold Spacer stacks\nweight-based sizing\n\nHome geometry owners:\n1\n\n==================================================\n17. SYSTEM WALLPAPER\n==================================================\n\nKeep wallpaper visible.\n\nDo NOT bundle screenshot wallpaper.\n\nDo NOT bundle reference image.\n\nRoot background must not become fullscreen opaque black.\n\n==================================================\n18. STATUS BAR\n==================================================\n\nDo not recreate status-bar contents.\n\nRespect system status bar.\n\nDo not implement status-bar color settings yet.\n\n==================================================\n19. NO MOTION\n==================================================\n\nPatch/001 has NO:\n\nMaterial Stretch\nLEFT gesture\nRIGHT gesture\nUP gesture\nDOWN gesture\ncustom haptic\nedge animation\n\nStatic Home only.\n\n==================================================\n20. NO SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nNo Settings screen.\n\nGear may remain inert for visual parity.\n\n==================================================\n21. NO FIRST INSTALL\n==================================================\n\nNo onboarding.\nNo RoleManager flow.\nNo particles.\nNo autofill.\n\n==================================================\n22. NO DEBUG UI\n==================================================\n\nRemove Debug Settings/control panel from active app.\n\nPatch feedback lives in documentation only for now.\n\n==================================================\n23. PATCH FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nCreate one concise feedback section in:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/PATCH-001-UI.md\n\nUse:\n\nPATCH/001 UI\n\n○ Home position\n○ Home width\n○ Home height\n○ Fav size\n○ Fav text\n○ P1 size\n○ P2 size\n○ P1/P2 equal\n○ Empty-state position\n○ Dock size\n○ Dock outside Home\n○ Home → Dock gap\n○ Wallpaper visibility\n○ Reference parity\n\nStates:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n24. REFERENCE\n==================================================\n\nSet the current 822-style screenshot as the ONLY authoritative\nPatch/001 UI reference.\n\nPrevious UI references:\nHISTORICAL\n\nDo not compare against old Alpha experiments.\n\n==================================================\n25. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n26. SIZE\n==================================================\n\nRelease target remains:\n\n<= 7 MB\n\nRemoving experimental code should reduce or preserve size.\n\n==================================================\n27. DEVICE GATE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT add any next feature until Patch/001 UI matches the\nreference on Pixel.\n\nRequired next status:\n\nPATCH_001_UI_DEVICE_TEST\n\nOnly after explicit approval:\n\nPATCH_001_UI_STABLE\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm PATCH/001 UI RESET COMPLETE\n\nCheckpoint:\n<path>\n\nActive architecture:\n<list>\n\nActive UI patches:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n1\n\nActive patch:\nPatch/001-UI\n\nArchived experimental implementations:\n<n>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearch active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSettings active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nParticles active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nFirst install active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nGesture animation active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHome geometry owners:\n<n>\n\nReference:\n<path>\n\nHome position:\n<value>\n\nHome size:\n<value>\n\nFav size:\n<value>\n\nP1 size:\n<value>\n\nP2 size:\n<value>\n\nP1 == P2:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock size:\n<value>\n\nDock outside Home:\n<YES/NO>\n\nReference image packaged:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nPATCH_001_UI_DEVICE_TEST"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:411:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787384952,"text":"FASE — worm projectctl CHECKPOINT SHA256 FIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nFILE:\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl\n\nMODE:\nINFRASTRUCTURE ONLY\n\nPROBLEM\n\nCheckpoint fails with:\n\ncp: cannot stat\n/opt/Android/worm/outputs/<timestamp>/SHA256SUMS.txt\n\nCurrent build output uses:\n\nSHA256SUMS\n\nnot:\n\nSHA256SUMS.txt\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFix projectctl checkpoint logic so it uses the actual build-output\nhash manifest consistently.\n\nDo NOT modify application source.\nDo NOT modify Core.\nDo NOT modify Patch/001 UI.\n\n==================================================\n1. AUDIT SHA FILE NAMING\n==================================================\n\nFind all projectctl references to:\n\nSHA256SUMS\nSHA256SUMS.txt\n\nReport counts and commands using each form.\n\nChoose ONE canonical filename.\n\nPreferred canonical filename:\n\nSHA256SUMS\n\n==================================================\n2. BUILD OUTPUT CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nEvery successful build session should contain:\n\napp-debug.apk\nbuild.log\nSHA256SUMS\n\nand optional release artifacts.\n\nDo not require SHA256SUMS.txt.\n\n==================================================\n3. CHECKPOINT LOGIC\n==================================================\n\nFix checkpoint so it does NOT blindly cp a non-existent\nSHA256SUMS.txt.\n\nPreferred behavior:\n\nif latest output contains SHA256SUMS:\n    copy it into checkpoint metadata if checkpoint contract needs it\n\nif no valid latest SHA256SUMS exists:\n    generate checkpoint's own SHA256 manifest from checkpoint contents\n\nDo not fail merely because an old optional output hash file is absent.\n\n==================================================\n4. CHECKPOINT SHA\n==================================================\n\nCheckpoint should have its OWN hash manifest.\n\nPreferred:\n\n<checkpoint>/SHA256SUMS\n\nGenerate after checkpoint files are copied.\n\nThen verify:\n\nsha256sum -c SHA256SUMS\n\nfrom checkpoint root.\n\n==================================================\n5. NO STALE OUTPUT DEPENDENCY\n==================================================\n\nCheckpoint creation must not require a specific old output session\nfile name if the checkpoint itself can generate hashes.\n\nA checkpoint should remain valid even if:\n\noutputs/ is empty\nlatest output predates current naming\nonly app-debug.apk exists\n\n==================================================\n6. SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nDo not delete:\n\noutputs\nsnapshots\ncheckpoints\nbackups\n\nDo not rewrite existing valid checkpoints.\n\n==================================================\n7. TEST\n==================================================\n\nFirst run:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl status\n\nThen:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl checkpoint test-checkpoint-fix\n\nRequired:\n\ncheckpoint created\ncheckpoint SHA256SUMS created\ncheckpoint SHA verification PASS\n\nThen remove ONLY the test checkpoint if projectctl already has a\nsafe supported way to do so.\n\nIf not, leave it and report its path.\n\n==================================================\n8. RETRY REAL CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nAfter fix succeeds run:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl checkpoint pre-patch-001-ui-reset\n\nRequired:\nSUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm PROJECTCTL CHECKPOINT SHA FIX COMPLETE\n\nSHA256SUMS refs before:\n<n>\n\nSHA256SUMS.txt refs before:\n<n>\n\nCanonical filename:\nSHA256SUMS\n\nCheckpoint depends on output SHA file:\n<NO/YES>\n\nTest checkpoint:\n<path>\n\nTest checkpoint SHA:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nReal checkpoint:\n<path>\n\nApplication source modified:\nNO\n\nCore modified:\nNO\n\nPatch UI modified:\nNO"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:412:{"session_id":"01a02535-6a57-7102-81e0-dcda8679eff4","ts":1787385547,"text":"FASE — worm RESET CORE + UI/001\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nTARGET:\nCORE + UI/001 ONLY\n\nREFERENCE:\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/reference/alpha-001/home-reference.png\n\nSTATUS:\nRESET / DEVICE_TEST\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nReset the active worm application to the minimal stable foundation:\n\n1. CORE\n2. UI/001\n\nRemove all other experimental runtime layers from the active source set.\n\nUI/001 must reproduce only the approved Home reference.\n\n==================================================\n0. CHECKPOINT\n==================================================\n\nFirst run:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl checkpoint pre-core-ui-001-reset\n\nIf checkpoint fails:\nSTOP.\n\nDo not modify source before checkpoint succeeds.\n\n==================================================\n1. FINAL ACTIVE RUNTIME\n==================================================\n\nRequired flow:\n\nMainActivity\n→ WormRuntime\n→ UI/001\n→ Core\n\nOnly one active UI owner.\n\n==================================================\n2. KEEP CORE\n==================================================\n\nKeep only foundational Core responsibilities:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nHomeSlot\nAppCatalog\nSlotRepository\nLauncherActions\nAppVisuals\n\nCore remains independent from UI.\n\nCore must not import Compose UI.\n\n==================================================\n3. REMOVE FROM ACTIVE RUNTIME\n==================================================\n\nArchive/remove from active Android source set:\n\nAlpha/001\nAlpha/002\nUI/002+\nMaterial Stretch\ngesture experiments\nSearch functionality\nSettings\nDebug panel\nparticles\nfirst install\nUsageStats autofill\nsemantic Dock setup\nicon-pack support\ntimezone options\nstatus-bar options\nFav effects\nchangelog\nwork-profile/web/shortcut search\n\nDo not permanently delete history.\n\nArchive under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/archive/pre-core-ui-001-reset/\n\n==================================================\n4. ACTIVE SOURCE TARGET\n==================================================\n\nPreferred active source:\n\napp/src/main/java/com/worm/\n\ncore/\nruntime/\npatches/\n  001_ui/\nui/\n  components/\n  theme/\n\nNo other active patch directories.\n\n==================================================\n5. UI/001 REFERENCE\n==================================================\n\nUI/001 must match the authoritative screenshot.\n\nVisible elements only:\n\n- system wallpaper\n- large wallpaper area above Home\n- dark Home outer container\n- Fav Apps panel\n- P1 empty panel\n- P2 empty panel\n- external empty Dock\n\nNothing else.\n\n==================================================\n6. NO SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nUI/001 must NOT contain:\n\nSearch bar\nmagnifier\nunderline\nquery\nresults\nhistory\n\nSearch comes later.\n\n==================================================\n7. HOME POSITION\n==================================================\n\nMatch reference exactly/proportionally.\n\nHome is lower-middle on screen.\n\nLarge wallpaper area above.\n\nDo not top-align.\n\nDo not center generically.\n\nDo not use previous Alpha display-adaptation rules.\n\n==================================================\n8. HOME WIDTH / HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nReference-derived only.\n\nNo:\n\nfillMaxHeight()\nweight(1f)\ngeneric 90/92/94% width guesses\n\nMeasure the reference and use one geometry owner.\n\n==================================================\n9. FAV\n==================================================\n\nRender:\n\nFav. apps\nApps 0\ngear right\n\nGear is visual only.\n\nNo Settings action.\n\nNo animation.\n\n==================================================\n10. P1 / P2\n==================================================\n\nRender empty state only.\n\nP1 and P2:\n\nsame width\nsame height\nsame radius\nsame padding\n\nText:\n\nNo apps in this section\n\nAdd your favorite apps to access them quickly.\n\nSmall centered outline glyph.\n\n==================================================\n11. DOCK\n==================================================\n\nDock outside Home.\n\nEmpty dark rounded surface only.\n\nNo icons.\nNo autofill.\nNo semantic defaults.\n\n==================================================\n12. WALLPAPER\n==================================================\n\nUse system wallpaper.\n\nDo not bundle reference screenshot.\n\nDo not bundle wallpaper image.\n\nRoot must remain transparent/wallpaper-aware.\n\n==================================================\n13. NO MOTION\n==================================================\n\nUI/001 is static.\n\nNo:\n\nLEFT/RIGHT gesture\nUP/DOWN gesture\nstretch\nhaptic\nedge animation\n\n==================================================\n14. NO SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nSettings active:\nNO\n\nDebug active:\nNO\n\n==================================================\n15. ONE GEOMETRY OWNER\n==================================================\n\nAudit active Home code.\n\nRequired:\n\nHome geometry owners = 1\n\nRemove conflicting:\n\nold width tokens\ntop offsets\nreference adapters\ndisplay-fit logic\nSpacer duplication\nweight-based sizing\n\n==================================================\n16. DOCUMENTATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate/update:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/docs/UI-001.md\n\nKeep only simplified feedback:\n\nUI/001\n\n○ Home position\n○ Home width\n○ Home height\n○ Fav\n○ P1\n○ P2\n○ P1/P2 equal\n○ Dock\n○ Dock outside Home\n○ Wallpaper visibility\n○ Reference parity\n\nStates:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n17. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n18. OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nVerify debug APK exported to:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/outputs/<timestamp>/app-debug.apk\n\n==================================================\n19. FINAL STATUS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT mark stable yet.\n\nExpected:\n\nUI_001_DEVICE_TEST\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm CORE + UI/001 RESET COMPLETE\n\nCheckpoint:\n<path>\n\nActive Core:\n<YES/NO>\n\nActive UI patch count:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n1\n\nActive patch:\nUI/001\n\nSearch active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSettings active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nMotion active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nParticles active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nFirst install active:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHome geometry owners:\n<n>\n\nReference:\n<path>\n\nHome size:\n<value>\n\nFav size:\n<value>\n\nP1 size:\n<value>\n\nP2 size:\n<value>\n\nP1 == P2:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDock outside Home:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nDebug APK:\n<path>\n\nSTATUS:\nUI_001_DEVICE_TEST"}
