ackage imports.\n\n==================================================\n5. GRADLE\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\nnamespace = \"com.worm\"\n\napplicationId = \"com.worm\"\n\nDo not change SDK/dependencies/build types.\n\n==================================================\n6. MANIFEST\n==================================================\n\nUpdate any fully-qualified class references still using:\n\nit.gaetano.machinahome\n\nExpected after migration:\n0\n\nPreserve runtime behavior.\n\n==================================================\n7. OLD SOURCE ROOT\n==================================================\n\nAfter successful migration:\n\napp/src/main/java/it/gaetano/machinahome/\n\nmust not contain active source files.\n\nRemove empty parent directories if safe.\n\nDo not leave two compiled namespaces.\n\n==================================================\n8. CACHE CLEAN\n==================================================\n\nAfter package migration remove generated build state only:\n\nproject/.kotlin\nproject/.gradle\nproject/build\nproject/app/build\n\nDo NOT remove source/config.\n\nThis is required because old compiled classes still reference:\n\nit/gaetano/machinahome/...\n\n==================================================\n9. ACTIVE REF AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nSearch active build/runtime files for:\n\nit.gaetano.machinahome\n\nExclude:\n\narchive\nbackups\nhistorical docs\nPROJECT-TREE.txt\n\nExpected:\n0\n\n==================================================\n10. MACHINA NAMING\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT rename classes such as MachinaCore/MachinaApp in this phase\nunless package migration strictly requires it.\n\nClass/product cleanup is separate.\n\nGoal here:\npackage migration only.\n\n==================================================\n11. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm SOURCE PACKAGE MIGRATION COMPLETE\n\nOld source files before:\n<n>\n\nNew source root:\n<path>\n\nPackage declarations migrated:\n<n>\n\nImports migrated:\n<n>\n\nOld active package refs:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate source trees:\n<n>\n\nnamespace:\n<value>\n\napplicationId:\n<value>\n\nRuntime behavior changed:\nNO\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:417:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787392467,"text":"FASE — worm RESTORE EXACT HOME FROM 19-AUG MACHINA BASELINE\n\nCURRENT ROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nCURRENT PROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nCURRENT PACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nSOURCE BASELINE:\n19-08-2026 device-approved Machina snapshot/checkpoint\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRestore the EXACT Home UI implementation from the validated\n19-08-2026 Machina baseline into the current worm project.\n\nKeep:\n\n- root /opt/Android/worm\n- namespace com.worm\n- applicationId com.worm\n- app label worm\n- current working Gradle/toolchain/projectctl setup\n\nDo NOT redesign the Home.\nDo NOT approximate it.\nDo NOT rebuild it from screenshots.\n\nUse the actual 19-08 source as the source of truth.\n\n==================================================\n1. LOCATE BASELINE SOURCE\n==================================================\n\nFind the exact restored/validated 19-08 Machina source or checkpoint\ncorresponding to:\n\nbaseline-19aug-device-ok\n\nIf the named checkpoint is unavailable inside current worm tree,\nlocate the source from the preserved Machina backup used for the\n19-08 restore.\n\nReport exact source path.\n\nDo NOT modify anything yet.\n\n==================================================\n2. IDENTIFY HOME FILE SET\n==================================================\n\nFrom the 19-08 source identify ALL files required by the Home UI.\n\nInclude only actual dependencies necessary for:\n\n- Home root composable\n- Fav UI\n- P1\n- P2\n- Dock\n- Home geometry\n- Home theme/style used by Home\n- Home-specific interaction helpers if they existed on 19-08\n\nReport exact file list.\n\nDo not pull later 20-08 code.\n\n==================================================\n3. COMPARE CURRENT VS BASELINE\n==================================================\n\nCompare current worm Home files with the 19-08 files.\n\nClassify each:\n\nIDENTICAL_EXCEPT_PACKAGE\nDIFFERENT\nMISSING_CURRENT\nEXTRA_CURRENT\n\nReport differences before replacing source.\n\n==================================================\n4. RESTORE BASELINE HOME\n==================================================\n\nRestore the baseline Home implementation from 19-08.\n\nWhen copying Kotlin source:\n\nchange only package/import namespace:\n\nit.gaetano.machinahome...\n→ com.worm...\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nlayout\ndimensions\nspacing\ncolors\nradii\ngesture behavior\nstate logic\nvisual hierarchy\n\nThe UI source must otherwise remain functionally equivalent\nto the validated 19-08 version.\n\n==================================================\n5. REMOVE CONFLICTING CURRENT HOME\n==================================================\n\nAny current Home implementation introduced after the 19-08\nbaseline that competes with the restored Home must be removed\nfrom the ACTIVE runtime.\n\nTarget:\n\nruntime Home owners = 1\n\nDo not leave current worm experimental Home alongside restored Home.\n\n==================================================\n6. ENTRY POINT\n==================================================\n\nWire MainActivity/current app entry to the restored 19-08 Home.\n\nPreserve:\n\ncom.worm package\nworm app label\n\nDo not restore old package identity.\n\n==================================================\n7. CORE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT replace Core wholesale.\n\nOnly restore a Core file if the 19-08 Home cannot compile or behave\ncorrectly without that exact contract.\n\nIf required, report it explicitly before changing Core.\n\nPreferred:\n\nCore modified = NO\n\n==================================================\n8. STATE\n==================================================\n\nDo not use fresh com.worm state as evidence that UI differs.\n\nThis task concerns exact Home implementation parity.\n\nP1/P2/Dock may be empty on first worm launch because com.worm is a\nnew package; that is acceptable if geometry/behavior matches 19-08.\n\n==================================================\n9. REMOVE LATER UI RESIDUE\n==================================================\n\nAudit active Home/runtime for later experimental code:\n\nui/v3\nAlpha\nworm experiments\nUI-00x\nlater Home redesigns\nlater geometry adapters\n\nIf runtime-reachable and not part of 19-08 baseline:\n\nremove/archive from active runtime.\n\n==================================================\n10. CLEAN GENERATED OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nAfter source restoration remove generated build state:\n\nproject/.kotlin\nproject/.gradle\nproject/build\nproject/app/build\n\nDo not remove source/config.\n\n==================================================\n11. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n12. DEVICE TARGET\n==================================================\n\nThe installed worm Home must visually and behaviorally match the\nvalidated Machina Home from 19-08.\n\nThe ONLY intended differences are:\n\nApp package:\ncom.worm\n\nApp label:\nworm\n\nFresh application data where package identity causes it.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm 19-AUG HOME RESTORE COMPLETE\n\nBaseline source:\n<path>\n\nBaseline Home files:\n<list>\n\nCurrent differing Home files:\n<n>\n\nRestored files:\n<n>\n\nRuntime Home owners:\n<n>\n\nLater UI runtime refs removed:\n<n>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nPackage preserved:\ncom.worm\n\napplicationId preserved:\ncom.worm\n\nApp label preserved:\nworm\n\nHome implementation parity:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nHOME_19AUG_DEVICE_VALIDATION_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:418:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787393538,"text":"FASE — worm RESTORE INTERACTION + SETTINGS + HAPTIC\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nBASELINE:\nrestored 19-08 Home\npackage com.worm\napp label worm\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nPreserve the restored Home exactly as it is now,\nand reintroduce only these missing behaviors:\n\n1. swipe UP reveal\n2. LEFT/RIGHT edge feedback with visible Material 3 stretch\n3. app Settings\n4. Pixel-style semantic haptic feedback\n\nDo NOT redesign Home.\nDo NOT change Home geometry unless strictly required for the UP reveal.\nDo NOT reintroduce later experimental UI.\n\n==================================================\n1. HOME LOCK\n==================================================\n\nKeep current restored Home visual parity.\n\nDo NOT change:\n\n- Home width\n- Home height\n- Fav geometry\n- P1 geometry\n- P2 geometry\n- Dock geometry\n- section gaps\n- colors\n- corner radii\n- wallpaper behavior\n\nThe current restored Home is the visual baseline.\n\n==================================================\n2. SWIPE UP\n==================================================\n\nRestore the previous UP interaction.\n\nGesture:\n\nvertical swipe UP\n→ expand/reveal the region between Fav and P1\n\nTarget behavior:\n\n- smooth drag preview\n- accepted expanded state\n- DOWN collapses\n- no LEFT/RIGHT interference\n- no first-touch blocker\n\nPreserve the earlier approved reveal amount if source/history\ncontains it.\n\nIf no exact value is recoverable:\nstart from +25% reveal relative to collapsed upper region.\n\n==================================================\n3. UP AXIS LOCK\n==================================================\n\nUse touchSlop.\n\nAccept vertical gesture only when:\n\nabs(dy) > touchSlop\nAND\nabs(dy) > abs(dx)\n\nOnce vertical is accepted:\nlock vertical for that pointer sequence.\n\nNo horizontal stretch during UP.\n\n==================================================\n4. LEFT / RIGHT EDGE GESTURES\n==================================================\n\nRestore edge-origin LEFT/RIGHT interaction.\n\nLEFT edge swipe:\nvisual elastic stretch only\n\nRIGHT edge swipe:\nmirrored visual elastic stretch only\n\nNo navigation.\n\nNo page change.\n\nNo Back/Forward action.\n\n==================================================\n5. EDGE VISIBILITY BUG\n==================================================\n\nCurrent defect:\n\nedge/corner feedback does not visibly appear.\n\nAudit exact path:\n\nACTION_DOWN\n→ edge candidate\n→ touchSlop\n→ horizontal lock\n→ stretch state update\n→ visual consumer\n→ release\n\nReport where visibility currently fails.\n\nDo not just tune random values.\n\n==================================================\n6. MATERIAL 3 STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nRestore the previous visible Material 3 / modern Android\nelastic-stretch feel.\n\nRequired:\n\n- originates from touched edge\n- small but clearly visible\n- bounded\n- non-linear resistance\n- smooth return\n- no simple translationX-only effect\n- no permanent deformation\n\nLEFT:\norigin at left edge\n\nRIGHT:\norigin at right edge\n\n==================================================\n7. NO TOUCH-ONLY ANIMATION\n==================================================\n\nSimple touch:\nno stretch.\n\nStretch starts only after real horizontal swipe passes touchSlop.\n\nCenter touch:\nno animation.\n\nCenter swipe:\nno edge stretch.\n\n==================================================\n8. NO EDGE NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nworm must not draw:\n\n- Back arrow\n- Forward arrow\n- chevron\n- edge navigation indicator\n\nHorizontal gesture result:\nvisual stretch only.\n\n==================================================\n9. SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nRestore app Settings.\n\nKeep it separate from Home geometry.\n\nEntry:\ngear in Fav Apps.\n\nTap gear:\nopen Settings.\n\n==================================================\n10. SETTINGS UI\n==================================================\n\nUse the previously approved compact Settings direction.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- compact\n- categories\n- subcategories\n- small glyph per category\n- system font\n- minimal borders\n- switches aligned right\n- Dynamic Color where supported\n\nDo NOT restore card-heavy or fullscreen-black Settings.\n\n==================================================\n11. SETTINGS ROOT\n==================================================\n\nUse concise root categories:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nIcons\nTime\nSystem\nAbout\n\nDo not add debug/experimental categories to release UI.\n\n==================================================\n12. SETTINGS NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nInside subcategories:\n\nleft-edge swipe RIGHT\n→ previous Settings level\n\nSystem Back:\nsame previous-level result.\n\nVertical scroll must remain normal.\n\nSwitch first-touch must work.\n\n==================================================\n13. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nRestore semantic haptic feedback using the Pixel hardware path\nthrough supported Android APIs.\n\nPrefer:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(...)\n\nUse semantic constants appropriate to the action.\n\nDo NOT attempt to reproduce a proprietary motor waveform.\n\n==================================================\n14. HAPTIC POLICY\n==================================================\n\nUP accepted:\n1 short confirmation haptic\n\nDOWN accepted:\n1 short confirmation haptic\n\nLEFT/RIGHT stretch:\nno haptic\n\nMOVE:\nno haptic\n\nsimple touch:\nno haptic\n\nSettings row/switch:\nuse only existing Material/system interaction feedback if needed;\ndo not add repeated custom vibration.\n\n==================================================\n15. PIXEL-LIKE FEEL\n==================================================\n\nTarget haptic character:\n\n- short\n- crisp\n- single pulse\n- semantic\n- not buzzy\n- not repeated\n\nNo raw vibrator waveform unless public semantic haptic APIs are\nproven insufficient.\n\n==================================================\n16. SINGLE INTERACTION OWNER\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHome gesture controller = 1\n\nHorizontal stretch owner = 1\nVertical reveal owner = 1\n\nNo duplicate pointerInput chains competing over Home.\n\n==================================================\n17. SETTINGS OWNER\n==================================================\n\nSettings navigation owner = 1\nSettings preference owner = 1\n\nNo duplicate Settings state.\n\n==================================================\n18. CORE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT replace Core wholesale.\n\nAllowed Core changes only if required for existing Settings\npreferences or stable interaction contracts.\n\nPreferred:\nCore semantics unchanged.\n\n==================================================\n19. DEBUG FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nKeep a concise DEV-only feedback section:\n\nHOME INTERACTION\n\n○ UP reveal\n○ DOWN collapse\n○ LEFT edge visible\n○ RIGHT edge visible\n○ Material Stretch visible\n○ No edge navigation\n○ Axis lock\n○ First touch\n○ UP haptic\n○ DOWN haptic\n\nSETTINGS\n\n○ Opens from gear\n○ Compact UI\n○ Categories\n○ Subcategories\n○ Swipe Back\n○ Switch first touch\n○ Dynamic Color\n\nUse:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n20. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm INTERACTION / SETTINGS RESTORE COMPLETE\n\nHome geometry modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUP reveal:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDOWN collapse:\n<YES/NO>\n\nLEFT edge visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRIGHT edge visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nMaterial Stretch visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nStretch failure point fixed:\n<value>\n\nEdge navigation:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nHome gesture owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings restored:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSettings navigation owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings preference owners:\n<n>\n\nUP haptic:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDOWN haptic:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHaptic API:\n<value>\n\nMOVE haptic paths:\n<n>\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n<n>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:419:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787395407,"text":"FASE — worm HOME INTERACTION + SEARCH REVEAL FIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nBASELINE:\n19-08 restored Home\npackage com.worm\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFix only these confirmed device defects:\n\n1. remove visible edge/corner navigation feedback\n2. restore actual Material 3 elastic stretch on LEFT/RIGHT\n3. make Fav open fully on swipe UP\n4. restore Search bar + particle-network reveal area\n\nDo NOT redesign the restored Home.\nDo NOT change P1/P2/Dock base geometry.\n\n==================================================\n1. EDGE / CORNER DEFECT\n==================================================\n\nCurrent defect:\n\nLEFT/RIGHT swipe still exposes edge/corner system-style feedback.\n\nRequired:\n\n- no Back arrow\n- no Forward arrow\n- no corner/edge chevron\n- no page navigation\n- no custom edge indicator\n\nThe horizontal gesture must produce only worm's elastic stretch.\n\nAudit whether the current gesture starts inside the Android\nsystem navigation edge region.\n\nIf necessary, move worm's own horizontal gesture activation slightly\ninside the content edge while preserving the visual origin at the edge.\n\nUse supported Android APIs only.\n\n==================================================\n2. MATERIAL 3 STRETCH — CURRENTLY MISSING\n==================================================\n\nCurrent defect:\n\nhorizontal gesture exists, but visible Material-style stretch\ndoes not appear.\n\nTrace:\n\npointer down\n→ horizontal candidate\n→ touchSlop\n→ axis lock\n→ drag progress\n→ stretch state\n→ graphics transform\n→ release\n\nFind the exact failure point.\n\nDo NOT fake it with simple translationX.\n\n==================================================\n3. STRETCH VISUAL\n==================================================\n\nImplement one clearly visible but subtle elastic deformation.\n\nLEFT:\nanchored visually to LEFT side\n\nRIGHT:\nanchored visually to RIGHT side\n\nExpected feel:\n\n- Material 3 / modern Android elastic overscroll\n- bounded\n- non-linear\n- resistant near max\n- smooth return\n\nNo large scale.\nNo bounce.\nNo permanent displacement.\n\n==================================================\n4. HORIZONTAL TOUCH RULES\n==================================================\n\nSimple touch:\nno animation.\n\nVertical swipe:\nno horizontal stretch.\n\nHorizontal swipe only:\nstretch.\n\nMOVE haptic:\n0.\n\n==================================================\n5. FAV UP REVEAL DEFECT\n==================================================\n\nCurrent defect:\n\nFav does not fully open.\n\nAudit:\n\ncollapsed state\ndrag progress\nexpanded threshold\nexpanded target height\nrelease settle\n\nConfirm why expanded state stops early.\n\n==================================================\n6. FULL EXPANDED TARGET\n==================================================\n\nOn accepted swipe UP:\n\nFav/Search upper region must reach the full intended expanded state.\n\nDo not stop at partial reveal.\n\nUse one explicit:\n\nCOLLAPSED\nEXPANDED\n\nsettled state.\n\nAfter release:\nnever remain at intermediate height.\n\n==================================================\n7. SEARCH REVEAL AREA\n==================================================\n\nExpanded order must be:\n\nFav\n↓\nParticle Network / Search Results area\n↓\nSearchBar\n↓\nP1\n↓\nP2\n\nCollapsed state keeps this region hidden/minimal.\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH BAR\n==================================================\n\nRestore Search bar only when the reveal is active according to\nthe intended baseline behavior.\n\nVisual target:\n\nmagnifier left\nquery/input\nsingle underline\n\nNo filled pill.\nNo large bordered card.\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH BAR POSITION\n==================================================\n\nSearchBar must sit at the BOTTOM of the expanded Search region,\ndirectly above P1.\n\nResults/history/particles belong ABOVE SearchBar.\n\n==================================================\n10. PARTICLE NETWORK\n==================================================\n\nRestore one network-particle animation in the expanded Search region.\n\nRequired:\n\n- moving dots\n- nearby connection lines\n- fills the available Search reveal area\n- not just a small patch behind the SearchBar\n- no touch interception\n\n==================================================\n11. PARTICLE VISIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nCurrent desired effect:\n\nparticles clearly visible\nlines clearly visible\nmotion slightly lively\n\nDo not make them nearly invisible.\n\nDo not make them excessively fast.\n\n==================================================\n12. PARTICLE ENGINE\n==================================================\n\nOne engine only.\n\nNo duplicate Canvas owner.\nNo per-particle coroutine.\nNo bitmap animation.\n\nUse one frame loop/delta-time update.\n\n==================================================\n13. SEARCH AREA HEIGHT\n==================================================\n\nWhen fully expanded, the Search region must use the complete\navailable space between Fav and P1 according to the previous\napproved interaction.\n\nDo not resize:\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\n==================================================\n14. P1 / P2 / DOCK LOCK\n==================================================\n\nRequired unchanged:\n\nP1 base size\nP2 base size\nDock base size\nP1/P2 equality\nDock external placement\n\nUP reveal must not stretch these sections.\n\n==================================================\n15. DOWN\n==================================================\n\nSwipe DOWN from expanded:\n\ncollapse Search/Fav reveal completely.\n\nHide SearchBar/particle region according to collapsed contract.\n\nReturn to exact restored Home geometry.\n\n==================================================\n16. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nUP accepted:\none short semantic haptic.\n\nDOWN accepted:\none short semantic haptic.\n\nLEFT/RIGHT:\nno haptic.\n\nMOVE:\nno haptic.\n\nUse:\n\nView.performHapticFeedback(...)\n\nwith a supported semantic constant appropriate to the device/API.\n\n==================================================\n17. GESTURE OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHome gesture owner = 1\nhorizontal stretch owner = 1\nvertical reveal owner = 1\n\nNo competing pointerInput layers.\n\n==================================================\n18. DEBUG FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nDEV-only checklist:\n\nHOME INTERACTION\n\n○ No edge/corner indicator\n○ LEFT stretch visible\n○ RIGHT stretch visible\n○ LEFT origin correct\n○ RIGHT origin correct\n○ Fav fully expands\n○ Expanded state settles fully\n○ SearchBar appears\n○ SearchBar at bottom\n○ Particles fill reveal area\n○ Particle lines visible\n○ DOWN fully collapses\n○ UP haptic\n○ DOWN haptic\n○ P1/P2/Dock unchanged\n\nStates:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n19. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm HOME INTERACTION + SEARCH REVEAL FIX COMPLETE\n\nEdge/corner indicator:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nLEFT stretch visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nRIGHT stretch visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nStretch failure point:\n<value>\n\nFav full expanded:\n<YES/NO>\n\nIntermediate settle possible:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearchBar:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSearchBar position:\n<BOTTOM_OF_REVEAL/OTHER>\n\nParticle engine owners:\n<n>\n\nParticles fill reveal area:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticle lines visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDOWN full collapse:\n<YES/NO>\n\nP1 resized:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP2 resized:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock resized:\n<NO/YES>\n\nUP haptic:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDOWN haptic:\n<YES/NO>\n\nGesture owners:\n<n>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:420:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787396214,"text":"FASE — worm SEARCH REVEAL + KEYBOARD PINNING + PARTICLE VISIBILITY FIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nBASELINE:\nrestored 19-08 Home\npackage com.worm\n\nREFERENCE:\ncurrent approved Home + search interaction behavior\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFix only these confirmed issues:\n\n1. restore the previous SearchBar visual style\n2. when keyboard opens, Dock/P1/P2 must remain visually pinned\n3. Search/reveal area must absorb IME height changes\n4. particle-network animation must remain continuously visible\n5. Fav/Search expanded state must remain coherent while typing\n\nDo NOT redesign the restored Home.\nDo NOT change Core ownership.\nDo NOT resize P1/P2/Dock dynamically.\n\n==================================================\n1. SEARCH BAR — RESTORE PREVIOUS STYLE\n==================================================\n\nCurrent SearchBar is wrong because it renders as a large light\nrounded field.\n\nRestore the earlier style:\n\nmagnifier on LEFT\nquery / placeholder text\nONE underline\n\nNo filled pill.\nNo white rounded box.\nNo full border.\nNo card background.\n\nTarget visual:\n\n[search icon] Search\n────────────────────────\n\nUse transparent / Home-surface background.\n\n==================================================\n2. SEARCH BAR POSITION\n==================================================\n\nIn expanded mode:\n\nFav\n↓\nparticle/results area\n↓\nSearchBar\n↓\nP1\n↓\nP2\n\nSearchBar must sit at the BOTTOM of the reveal region,\ndirectly above P1.\n\n==================================================\n3. IME / KEYBOARD CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nWhen keyboard opens:\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nmust remain visually anchored to their approved positions.\n\nThey must NOT:\n\nmove upward\nresize\ncompress\nbe covered\nreflow relative to each other\n\nThe keyboard must consume/reduce only the Search/reveal area.\n\n==================================================\n4. KEYBOARD LAYOUT STRATEGY\n==================================================\n\nAudit current window/Compose IME handling.\n\nDo NOT rely on a parent layout that automatically resizes the\nentire Home stack.\n\nUse one explicit IME-aware layout owner.\n\nThe Home structure should conceptually behave as:\n\nFIXED:\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nFLEXIBLE:\nSearch reveal / results / particles\n\nWhen IME rises:\nreduce flexible reveal area first.\n\n==================================================\n5. DOCK PINNING\n==================================================\n\nDock must remain anchored in the same visual place relative to\nP1/P2 during typing.\n\nDo not translate Dock with keyboard animation.\n\nDo not attach Dock directly to IME inset.\n\n==================================================\n6. P1 / P2 PINNING\n==================================================\n\nP1/P2:\n\nsame width\nsame height\nsame Y relationship\n\nbefore keyboard\nand\nduring keyboard.\n\nNo weight-based compression.\n\nNo height animation caused by IME.\n\n==================================================\n7. SEARCH AREA SHRINK\n==================================================\n\nWhen IME appears:\n\nSearch/reveal area may become shorter.\n\nAllowed to shrink:\n\nparticle/results vertical region\n\nNot allowed to shrink:\n\nFav\nSearchBar height\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nSearchBar stays immediately above P1.\n\n==================================================\n8. IME ANIMATION\n==================================================\n\nUse supported Android/Compose WindowInsets behavior.\n\nKeyboard transition should be smooth.\n\nDo NOT manually animate the whole Home upward.\n\nDo NOT add translationY to P1/P2/Dock.\n\n==================================================\n9. PARTICLE NETWORK — CURRENT DEFECT\n==================================================\n\nCurrent defect:\n\nparticles appear intermittently / disappear.\n\nAudit exact causes:\n\n- particle alpha\n- line alpha\n- clipping\n- Canvas bounds\n- reveal-height changes\n- recomposition/reset\n- animation lifecycle\n- frame-loop cancellation\n- SearchBar/overlay drawing above particles\n\nReport actual cause.\n\n==================================================\n10. PARTICLE ENGINE\n==================================================\n\nThere must be ONE particle engine owner.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- state survives normal recomposition\n- animation loop continues while reveal is visible\n- no reset on each query character\n- no reset on keyboard frame/inset changes\n- no per-particle coroutine\n\nUse stable remembered particle state.\n\n==================================================\n11. PARTICLE CANVAS BOUNDS\n==================================================\n\nParticle Canvas must fill the COMPLETE available reveal area:\n\nbetween Fav\nand\nSearchBar\n\nincluding while keyboard is visible.\n\nCanvas size should update to available area without recreating\nthe entire particle model unnecessarily.\n\n==================================================\n12. PARTICLE VISIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nIncrease visibility enough to be consistently perceived.\n\nTarget:\n\ndots:\nclearly visible but subtle\n\nconnection lines:\nvisible continuously\n\nNo nearly-transparent lines.\n\nNo blinking/flickering caused by random alpha.\n\nDo not use extreme brightness.\n\n==================================================\n13. PARTICLE DENSITY\n==================================================\n\nKeep enough particles for a visible network.\n\nSuggested starting target:\n\n20–30 particles\n\ndepending on actual reveal size.\n\nDo not dramatically reduce count when IME appears.\n\n==================================================\n14. PARTICLE CONNECTIONS\n==================================================\n\nConnect nearby particles using distance threshold.\n\nConnection-line alpha may vary with distance,\nbut must not drop so low that the network effectively disappears.\n\n==================================================\n15. PARTICLE MOTION\n==================================================\n\nMotion:\n\nslow/moderate\ncontinuous\nsmooth\n\nDo not restart velocities on recomposition.\n\nDo not randomize particle list every frame.\n\n==================================================\n16. CLIPPING / DRAW ORDER\n==================================================\n\nRequired draw order:\n\nHome background\n→ particles\n→ results/history\n→ SearchBar\n\nParticles must not be accidentally clipped behind an opaque\nintermediate Search surface.\n\nSearch reveal/result surfaces should remain transparent or\nappropriately translucent where particle visibility is intended.\n\n==================================================\n17. QUERY / TYPING STABILITY\n==================================================\n\nTyping must NOT:\n\nrestart particles\ncollapse Fav\nmove P1/P2/Dock\nchange Home width\nreset expanded state\n\nQuery state is independent from reveal geometry.\n\n==================================================\n18. FAV EXPANDED STATE\n==================================================\n\nIf Home is fully expanded before keyboard:\n\nkeyboard opening must preserve EXPANDED logical state.\n\nIME visibility does not equal collapse.\n\nWhen keyboard closes:\nrestore full expanded reveal height smoothly.\n\n==================================================\n19. COLLAPSED STATE\n==================================================\n\nIf user explicitly collapses:\n\nSearch/reveal hides according to current interaction contract.\n\nKeyboard should dismiss appropriately if Search focus is lost.\n\nDo not collapse merely because IME state changes.\n\n==================================================\n20. GESTURE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT change:\n\nLEFT/RIGHT Material Stretch logic\nedge gesture ownership\nUP/DOWN gesture acceptance\nhaptic policy\n\nexcept where reveal geometry must reference the new flexible area.\n\n==================================================\n21. HAPTIC\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\nUP accepted:\n1 semantic haptic\n\nDOWN accepted:\n1 semantic haptic\n\nLEFT/RIGHT:\n0\n\nMOVE:\n0\n\nNo keyboard haptic added by worm.\n\n==================================================\n22. DEBUG FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nUpdate DEV-only feedback:\n\nSEARCH / IME\n\n○ SearchBar previous style\n○ Magnifier left\n○ Single underline\n○ No pill / no white box\n○ SearchBar above P1\n○ Keyboard opens\n○ P1 pinned\n○ P2 pinned\n○ Dock pinned\n○ Search reveal shrinks\n○ SearchBar remains visible\n○ Expanded state preserved\n○ Keyboard close restores reveal\n\nPARTICLES\n\n○ Particles continuously visible\n○ Lines continuously visible\n○ Full reveal coverage\n○ No flicker\n○ No query reset\n○ No IME reset\n○ Smooth motion\n○ Single particle owner\n\nUse:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n23. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCore modified:\nNO preferred\n\nDo not alter:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nAppCatalog\nSlotRepository\nLauncherActions\nAppVisuals\n\n==================================================\n24. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm SEARCH / IME / PARTICLE FIX COMPLETE\n\nSearchBar style:\n<UNDERLINE_ONLY/OTHER>\n\nSearchBar light pill:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearchBar above P1:\n<YES/NO>\n\nIME layout owner:\n<value>\n\nP1 moves with IME:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP2 moves with IME:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock moves with IME:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1 resizes:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP2 resizes:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock resizes:\n<NO/YES>\n\nReveal area shrinks with IME:\n<YES/NO>\n\nExpanded state preserved:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticle engine owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle disappearance cause:\n<value>\n\nParticles visible continuously:\n<YES/NO>\n\nLines visible continuously:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticle state resets on query:\n<NO/YES>\n\nParticle state resets on IME:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:421:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787397080,"text":"FASE — worm SEARCH EXPANDED UI / IME FIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nBASELINE:\nrestored 19-08 Home\n\nREFERENCE BEHAVIOR:\napproved expanded-search mockup\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFix the current expanded Fav/Search state.\n\nCurrent device defects:\n\n1. SearchBar style is wrong.\n2. Keyboard causes the wrong Home/layout movement.\n3. P1/P2/Dock must remain anchored.\n4. Particle Network is intermittent / too sparse.\n5. Expanded Fav/Search must use the complete available upper area.\n\nDO NOT redesign the restored collapsed Home.\n\n==================================================\n1. SEARCH BAR — RESTORE PREVIOUS STYLE\n==================================================\n\nCurrent wrong implementation:\n\nwhite/filled rounded Search pill.\n\nREMOVE IT.\n\nRequired SearchBar:\n\nmagnifier icon LEFT\n\nplaceholder/query text\n\nONE thin underline\n\ntransparent background\n\nNO pill\nNO filled surface\nNO rounded Search container\nNO enclosing border\n\nVisual concept:\n\n⌕   Search apps...\n────────────────────────\n\n==================================================\n2. SEARCH BAR POSITION\n==================================================\n\nExpanded state hierarchy:\n\nFav Header\n↓\nParticle / Results area\n↓\nSearchBar\n↓\nP1\n↓\nP2\n↓\nDock\n\nSearchBar stays at the BOTTOM of the expanded Search area.\n\nIt must remain directly above P1.\n\n==================================================\n3. KEYBOARD / IME CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nWhen Search receives focus and keyboard opens:\n\nDO NOT move P1 upward.\n\nDO NOT move P2 upward.\n\nDO NOT move Dock upward.\n\nDO NOT resize P1.\n\nDO NOT resize P2.\n\nDO NOT resize Dock.\n\nP1/P2/Dock form the anchored lower Home region.\n\n==================================================\n4. IME RESIZE OWNER\n==================================================\n\nOnly the expandable Search region reacts to IME space.\n\nWhen keyboard rises:\n\nSearch/particle/results region may reduce its available height.\n\nP1/P2/Dock geometry remains unchanged relative to the Home\nlayout contract.\n\nDo not apply imePadding() independently to multiple Home children.\n\nThere must be ONE IME geometry owner.\n\n==================================================\n5. KEYBOARD VISIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nWhen keyboard is visible:\n\nSearchBar remains visible.\n\nP1 remains visible.\n\nP2 remains visible where available according to baseline contract.\n\nDock remains visible and anchored.\n\nKeyboard must not cover Dock if the approved layout reserves\nspace for it.\n\n==================================================\n6. REMOVE GLOBAL IME SHIFT\n==================================================\n\nAudit for:\n\nimePadding()\nnavigationBarsWithImePadding()\nwindowInsetsPadding(WindowInsets.ime)\nbringIntoViewRequester\nadjustPan-like behavior\nglobal Column translation\n\nIf applied to the whole Home:\nremove/restructure it.\n\nIME handling belongs only to the Search expansion/layout owner.\n\n==================================================\n7. EXPANDED SEARCH REGION\n==================================================\n\nSwipe UP must fully open the intended Search region.\n\nUse explicit states:\n\nCOLLAPSED\nEXPANDED\n\nNo partial settled state.\n\nOn accepted UP:\n\nstate = EXPANDED\n\nOn accepted DOWN:\n\nstate = COLLAPSED\n\n==================================================\n8. PARTICLE NETWORK AREA\n==================================================\n\nParticle Network fills ALL available space between:\n\nbottom of Fav Header\nand\ntop of SearchBar\n\nNot just a small strip.\n\nNot behind P1.\n\nNot inside SearchBar.\n\n==================================================\n9. PARTICLES ALWAYS VISIBLE\n==================================================\n\nCurrent defect:\n\nparticles appear/disappear visually.\n\nFix rendering so expanded state continuously displays the network.\n\nRequired:\n\nparticle Canvas remains composed while EXPANDED.\n\nDo not condition rendering on incidental Search query state.\n\nDo not recreate particle state every recomposition.\n\n==================================================\n10. PARTICLE STATE\n==================================================\n\nRemember particle positions across normal recompositions.\n\nUse remember / stable state appropriately.\n\nDo NOT regenerate the complete particle field whenever:\n\nquery changes\nkeyboard changes\nfocus changes\nframe changes\n\n==================================================\n11. PARTICLE DENSITY\n==================================================\n\nCurrent field is too sparse.\n\nIncrease density enough that the network is continuously\nrecognizable.\n\nStarting target:\n\n24–36 particles\n\nadapt count to actual available Search area.\n\nAvoid excessive density.\n\n==================================================\n12. CONNECTION LINES\n==================================================\n\nLines must be clearly visible.\n\nConnect nearby particles using bounded distance threshold.\n\nRequired:\n\nmultiple visible network clusters across the available area.\n\nDo not draw lines so faint that they disappear on device.\n\n==================================================\n13. PARTICLE MOTION\n==================================================\n\nMotion:\n\ncontinuous\nsmooth\nmoderate\nslightly lively\n\nNot extremely slow.\n\nNot chaotic.\n\nUse one frame loop.\n\nUse delta-time movement.\n\nNo coroutine per particle.\n\n==================================================\n14. PARTICLE CLIPPING\n==================================================\n\nClip particles to Search reveal area.\n\nParticles must not draw over:\n\nFav Header\nSearchBar\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\n==================================================\n15. PARTICLES DO NOT INTERCEPT TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nParticle Canvas is presentation only.\n\nPointer input:\nNONE\n\nSearch focus/taps must pass normally.\n\n==================================================\n16. SEARCH RESULTS / HISTORY\n==================================================\n\nSpace above SearchBar is shared conceptually by:\n\nParticle Network\nSearch results/history\n\nWhen no query/results:\nparticles dominate visual area.\n\nWhen results/history exist:\ncontent may overlay/use this region without changing P1/P2/Dock\ngeometry.\n\nDo not introduce a giant bordered results card.\n\n==================================================\n17. UP / DOWN\n==================================================\n\nUP:\n\nfully expands Search area\none short semantic haptic\n\nDOWN:\n\nfully collapses Search area\none short semantic haptic\n\nMOVE:\nno haptic.\n\n==================================================\n18. LEFT / RIGHT STRETCH\n==================================================\n\nPreserve/fix:\n\nLEFT → Material 3 elastic stretch\nRIGHT → Material 3 elastic stretch\n\nNo navigation.\n\nNo system-looking edge/corner indicator generated by worm.\n\nNo horizontal haptic.\n\nDo not mix stretch state with Search expansion state.\n\n==================================================\n19. HOME GEOMETRY LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCollapsed restored 19-08 Home remains unchanged.\n\nDo NOT redesign:\n\nFav collapsed geometry\nP1\nP2\nDock\nHome width\nHome base position\n\n==================================================\n20. SINGLE OWNERS\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHome gesture owner = 1\nSearch expansion owner = 1\nIME geometry owner = 1\nParticle engine = 1\nSearch focus owner = 1\n\nDuplicate owners:\n0\n\n==================================================\n21. DEBUG FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nUpdate DEV feedback:\n\nSEARCH / IME\n\n○ Search underline style\n○ No Search pill\n○ SearchBar above P1\n○ Keyboard opens\n○ P1 anchored\n○ P2 anchored\n○ Dock anchored\n○ Search region resizes for IME\n○ Particles always visible\n○ Particle density\n○ Particle lines\n○ Particle motion\n○ Particle clipping\n○ UP full expand\n○ DOWN full collapse\n\nStates:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n22. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm SEARCH EXPANDED UI / IME FIX COMPLETE\n\nSearch style:\n<UNDERLINE/PILL/OTHER>\n\nSearch enclosing border:\n<NO/YES>\n\nIME geometry owners:\n<n>\n\nP1 moves with IME:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP2 moves with IME:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock moves with IME:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearch region responds to IME:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nParticle count:\n<n>\n\nParticles persistent across recomposition:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticles always visible expanded:\n<YES/NO>\n\nLines visible:\n<YES/NO>\n\nUP full expand:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDOWN full collapse:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCollapsed Home geometry modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:422:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787398672,"text":"FASE — 19-AUG BASELINE PACKAGE RENAME ONLY\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nCURRENT PACKAGE:\nit.gaetano.machinahome\n\nTARGET PACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nCURRENT BASELINE:\n19-08-2026 restored snapshot\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRename ONLY the package/application identity.\n\nPreserve the 19-08 baseline source exactly.\n\nDO NOT:\n- redesign UI\n- change HomeScreen\n- change MachinaCore\n- change LauncherInteractionPatch\n- change geometry\n- change gestures\n- change Settings\n- add V3\n- add Alpha\n- add new patches\n\n==================================================\n1. GRADLE\n==================================================\n\nSet:\n\nnamespace = \"com.worm\"\n\napplicationId = \"com.worm\"\n\nDo not change any other Gradle behavior.\n\n==================================================\n2. SOURCE TREE\n==================================================\n\nMove:\n\napp/src/main/java/it/gaetano/machinahome/\n\nto:\n\napp/src/main/java/com/worm/\n\nPreserve every subdirectory and filename.\n\n==================================================\n3. PACKAGE DECLARATIONS\n==================================================\n\nReplace:\n\npackage it.gaetano.machinahome...\n\nwith:\n\npackage com.worm...\n\nPreserve suffixes exactly.\n\nExample:\n\nit.gaetano.machinahome.ui.home\n→ com.worm.ui.home\n\nit.gaetano.machinahome.core\n→ com.worm.core\n\nit.gaetano.machinahome.patches.launcher_interaction\n→ com.worm.patches.launcher_interaction\n\n==================================================\n4. IMPORTS\n==================================================\n\nReplace all imports:\n\nit.gaetano.machinahome...\n→ com.worm...\n\nNo other source edits.\n\n==================================================\n5. MAINACTIVITY\n==================================================\n\nPreserve existing MainActivity runtime flow exactly.\n\nCurrent expected imports/owners such as:\n\nMachinaCore\nLauncherInteractionPatch\nMachinaTheme\nHomeScreen\n\nmust remain functionally unchanged.\n\nOnly package names change.\n\n==================================================\n6. HOME\n==================================================\n\nHomeScreen.kt must remain source-equivalent except for:\n\npackage declaration\nimports\n\nNo layout changes.\n\nNo spacing changes.\n\nNo new Search.\n\nNo Settings change.\n\n==================================================\n7. CORE\n==================================================\n\nMachinaCore.kt\nHomeSnapshot.kt\nAppCatalog.kt\nLauncherPreferences.kt\nLauncherActions.kt\n\nmust remain source-equivalent except for namespace/import migration.\n\n==================================================\n8. PATCH\n==================================================\n\nLauncherInteractionPatch.kt must remain source-equivalent except\nfor package/import migration.\n\nDo not replace it with newer gesture code.\n\n==================================================\n9. APP LABEL\n==================================================\n\nSet visible app label to:\n\nworm\n\nUse existing string resource mechanism.\n\nDo not change other resources.\n\n==================================================\n10. CLEAN GENERATED FILES\n==================================================\n\nAfter migration remove only generated state:\n\nproject/.kotlin\nproject/.gradle\nproject/build\nproject/app/build\n\nThis avoids stale classes from:\n\nit/gaetano/machinahome\n\n==================================================\n11. AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nSearch active source/build config for:\n\nit.gaetano.machinahome\n\nExpected:\n0\n\nSearch for unintended new source:\n\nui/v3\ncore/v3\nfeatures/\nalpha\nAlpha\n\nExpected:\n0 unless they already existed in the 19-08 snapshot.\n\nDo not create them.\n\n==================================================\n12. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/projectctl build\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm 19-AUG PACKAGE RENAME COMPLETE\n\nOld package refs:\n<n>\n\nNew package:\ncom.worm\n\nnamespace:\ncom.worm\n\napplicationId:\ncom.worm\n\nHomeScreen modified beyond namespace:\n<NO/YES>\n\nMachinaCore modified beyond namespace:\n<NO/YES>\n\nLauncherInteractionPatch modified beyond namespace:\n<NO/YES>\n\nRuntime behavior changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>"}
