son why the network currently occupies only\na thin strip.\n\nDo not change it yet.\n\n==================================================\n5. SEARCH LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nInspect the expanded Home layout hierarchy.\n\nReport exact order:\n\nFav\n<component>\n<component>\nP1\nP2\n\nIdentify:\n\n- first Search render\n- second Search render\n- particle area\n- any results/history area\n- Spacer/weight owners\n\n==================================================\n6. RESTORED BASELINE CHECK\n==================================================\n\nDetermine whether these Search/particle paths were already present\nin the 19-08 snapshot source.\n\nClassify each current Search/particle file:\n\nPRESENT_IN_19AUG\nADDED_AFTER_RESTORE\nMODIFIED_AFTER_RESTORE\n\nDo not infer from timestamps alone where source comparison is possible.\n\n==================================================\n7. DIFF CURRENT VS SNAPSHOT\n==================================================\n\nCompare current files against:\n\n/opt/Android-rebuild-backup-2026-08-21_06-08-10/Machina/snapshots/2026-08-19_23-06-03/project.tar.gz\n\nFor Search/particles/Home interaction files only.\n\nReport:\n\nIDENTICAL_EXCEPT_PACKAGE\nDIFFERENT\nMISSING\nEXTRA\n\n==================================================\n8. NO SOURCE CHANGES\n==================================================\n\nProject modified:\nNO\n\nDo not:\n\nedit\nformat\nmove\ndelete\ngenerate replacement code\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm SEARCH/PARTICLES REVISION AUDIT\n\nSearch runtime owners:\n<n>\n\nSearch owner 1:\n<file/symbol>\n\nSearch owner 2:\n<file/symbol/N-A>\n\nSearch truly duplicated:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticle engine owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle engine:\n<file/symbol>\n\nParticle Canvas sizing:\n<value>\n\nThin-strip cause:\n<value>\n\nExpanded Home order:\n<list>\n\nSearch/particles present in 19-Aug snapshot:\n<YES/NO/PARTIAL>\n\nCurrent vs 19-Aug:\n<summary>\n\nLikely cause:\n<DUPLICATE_RUNTIME_PATH / BASELINE_BEHAVIOR / POST_RESTORE_CHANGE / LAYOUT_CONSTRAINT / OTHER>\n\nProject modified:\nNO\n\nSTATUS:\nREVIEW_COMPLETE"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:427:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787403028,"text":"==================================================\n9. SETTINGS OWNERS\n==================================================\n\nFind every active runtime owner related to Settings.\n\nSearch for:\n\nSettings\nSettingsScreen\nSettingsActivity\nSettingsPreferences\nPreferences\nDynamicColor\nStatusBar\nIconPack\nTimeZone\nChangelog\n\nReport exact:\n\nfile\nsymbol\nruntime path\n\n==================================================\n10. SETTINGS ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nTrace how Settings opens from Home.\n\nExpected path conceptually:\n\nHome/Fav gear\n→ Settings entry\n→ Settings root\n→ subcategory\n\nReport:\n\ngear click owner\nnavigation owner\nSettings root owner\n\nDetermine whether more than one Settings path is active.\n\n==================================================\n11. SETTINGS DUPLICATION\n==================================================\n\nCheck whether there are parallel implementations such as:\n\nold Settings\nV2 Settings\nV3 Settings\nfeature/settings\nui/settings\n\nReport:\n\nSettings runtime owners:\n<n>\n\nDuplicate Settings owners:\n<n>\n\n==================================================\n12. SETTINGS BASELINE CHECK\n==================================================\n\nDetermine which Settings-related files were already present in the\n19-08 snapshot.\n\nClassify each:\n\nPRESENT_IN_19AUG\nADDED_AFTER_RESTORE\nMODIFIED_AFTER_RESTORE\n\n==================================================\n13. SETTINGS CURRENT VS 19-AUG\n==================================================\n\nCompare current Settings-related files against:\n\n/opt/Android-rebuild-backup-2026-08-21_06-08-10/Machina/snapshots/2026-08-19_23-06-03/project.tar.gz\n\nReport:\n\nIDENTICAL_EXCEPT_PACKAGE\nDIFFERENT\nMISSING\nEXTRA\n\n==================================================\n14. SETTINGS STATE OWNERS\n==================================================\n\nReport counts for:\n\nSettings preference owners\nSettings navigation owners\nBackHandler owners\nDynamic Color owners\nstatus-bar setting owners\nicon setting owners\ntime setting owners\n\nDo not modify anything.\n\n==================================================\n15. SETTINGS DEVICE EXPECTATION\n==================================================\n\nBased only on current code, report what Settings should currently\ncontain on device.\n\nDo NOT infer later requested options that are not actually present.\n\nReport actual categories/options only.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT ADDITIONS\n==================================================\n\nSettings runtime owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings root:\n<file/symbol/N-A>\n\nSettings entry owner:\n<file/symbol/N-A>\n\nDuplicate Settings owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings present in 19-Aug snapshot:\n<YES/NO/PARTIAL>\n\nCurrent Settings vs 19-Aug:\n<summary>\n\nSettings preference owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings navigation owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings likely cause:\n<BASELINE_BEHAVIOR / DUPLICATE_RUNTIME_PATH / POST_RESTORE_CHANGE / MISSING_SETTINGS / OTHER>"}
