son why the network currently occupies only\na thin strip.\n\nDo not change it yet.\n\n==================================================\n5. SEARCH LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nInspect the expanded Home layout hierarchy.\n\nReport exact order:\n\nFav\n<component>\n<component>\nP1\nP2\n\nIdentify:\n\n- first Search render\n- second Search render\n- particle area\n- any results/history area\n- Spacer/weight owners\n\n==================================================\n6. RESTORED BASELINE CHECK\n==================================================\n\nDetermine whether these Search/particle paths were already present\nin the 19-08 snapshot source.\n\nClassify each current Search/particle file:\n\nPRESENT_IN_19AUG\nADDED_AFTER_RESTORE\nMODIFIED_AFTER_RESTORE\n\nDo not infer from timestamps alone where source comparison is possible.\n\n==================================================\n7. DIFF CURRENT VS SNAPSHOT\n==================================================\n\nCompare current files against:\n\n/opt/Android-rebuild-backup-2026-08-21_06-08-10/Machina/snapshots/2026-08-19_23-06-03/project.tar.gz\n\nFor Search/particles/Home interaction files only.\n\nReport:\n\nIDENTICAL_EXCEPT_PACKAGE\nDIFFERENT\nMISSING\nEXTRA\n\n==================================================\n8. NO SOURCE CHANGES\n==================================================\n\nProject modified:\nNO\n\nDo not:\n\nedit\nformat\nmove\ndelete\ngenerate replacement code\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm SEARCH/PARTICLES REVISION AUDIT\n\nSearch runtime owners:\n<n>\n\nSearch owner 1:\n<file/symbol>\n\nSearch owner 2:\n<file/symbol/N-A>\n\nSearch truly duplicated:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticle engine owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle engine:\n<file/symbol>\n\nParticle Canvas sizing:\n<value>\n\nThin-strip cause:\n<value>\n\nExpanded Home order:\n<list>\n\nSearch/particles present in 19-Aug snapshot:\n<YES/NO/PARTIAL>\n\nCurrent vs 19-Aug:\n<summary>\n\nLikely cause:\n<DUPLICATE_RUNTIME_PATH / BASELINE_BEHAVIOR / POST_RESTORE_CHANGE / LAYOUT_CONSTRAINT / OTHER>\n\nProject modified:\nNO\n\nSTATUS:\nREVIEW_COMPLETE"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:429:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787403401,"text":"FASE — worm BETA 001 SEARCH/PARTICLES REPAIR\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nBASELINE:\n19-08 restored Home + current post-restore Search/Particles\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_RETEST\n\nCONFIRMED AUDIT:\n\nSearch runtime owners:\n2\n\nParticle engine owners:\n1\n\nHomeScreen.kt:\nMODIFIED_AFTER_RESTORE\n\nMainActivity:\nIDENTICAL_EXCEPT_PACKAGE\n\nLauncherInteractionPatch:\nIDENTICAL_EXCEPT_PACKAGE\n\nROOT CAUSES:\n\n1. SearchBar rendered twice\n2. Particle canvas constrained to residual thin strip\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRepair ONLY Search/Particles inside HomeScreen.kt.\n\nDo NOT modify:\n\nMainActivity\nLauncherInteractionPatch\nCore\nP1\nP2\nDock\ncollapsed Home geometry\ngesture logic\nSettings\n\n==================================================\n1. REMOVE DUPLICATE SEARCHBAR\n==================================================\n\nCurrent expanded stack:\n\nFav\nParticleNetwork\nSearchBar inside SearchRevealArea\nSearchBar again in FavoritesContainer\nP1\nP2\n\nRequired:\n\nFav\nParticleNetwork\nSearchBar\nP1\nP2\n\nVisible SearchBar owners:\n1\n\nRemove the duplicate SearchBar render path from FavoritesContainer\nor equivalent outer path.\n\nKeep ONE SearchBar owned by SearchRevealArea.\n\n==================================================\n2. SEARCHBAR POSITION\n==================================================\n\nThe single SearchBar must remain:\n\nat the bottom of SearchRevealArea\ndirectly above P1\n\nDo not render it twice for layout/input reasons.\n\n==================================================\n3. SEARCH STYLE\n==================================================\n\nKeep current intended style:\n\nmagnifier left\nquery/placeholder\nsingle underline\n\nNo pill.\nNo enclosing rounded card.\nNo duplicate underline.\n\n==================================================\n4. PARTICLE AREA\n==================================================\n\nCurrent:\n\nparticleHeight =\n(height - SearchBarHeight).coerceAtLeast(0.dp)\n\nThis produces a residual thin band.\n\nRefactor SearchRevealArea so layout explicitly allocates:\n\navailable reveal height\nminus one SearchBar\n\nto a dedicated particle/results region.\n\nDo not subtract SearchBar height twice.\n\n==================================================\n5. REQUIRED LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nConceptually:\n\nColumn(\n    height = revealHeight\n) {\n    ParticleNetwork(\n        Modifier\n            .fillMaxWidth()\n            .weight(1f)\n    )\n\n    SearchBar(...)\n}\n\nUse a single SearchBar.\n\nThe particle region should consume all remaining reveal space.\n\nDo NOT apply weight to P1/P2/Home.\n\nWeight is allowed only inside SearchRevealArea for the\nparticle/results region.\n\n==================================================\n6. PARTICLE CANVAS\n==================================================\n\nParticleNetwork Canvas:\n\nfillMaxSize()\n\ninside its allocated particle region.\n\nNo additional small fixed height.\n\nNo heightIn(max = small value).\n\nNo top-strip constraint.\n\n==================================================\n7. PARTICLE DISTRIBUTION\n==================================================\n\nParticle Y coordinates must span the full actual Canvas height.\n\nRequired range:\n\n0 .. canvasHeight\n\nDo not initialize/move particles in a small fixed vertical band.\n\n==================================================\n8. PARTICLE STATE\n==================================================\n\nKeep the single current particle engine.\n\nDo not create a second engine.\n\nParticle positions must survive normal recompositions.\n\nDo not reset on:\n\nquery change\nfocus change\nIME change\nordinary recomposition\n\n==================================================\n9. CONNECTION LINES\n==================================================\n\nKeep dynamic nearby connections.\n\nEnsure distance calculation uses both:\n\ndx\ndy\n\nLines must be visible across the full particle region.\n\n==================================================\n10. COLLAPSED HOME LOCK\n==================================================\n\nCollapsed 19-Aug Home must remain visually unchanged.\n\nDo NOT alter:\n\nFav collapsed height\nP1 geometry\nP2 geometry\nDock geometry\nHome outer geometry\n\n==================================================\n11. P1/P2/DOCK LOCK\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nP1 modified = NO\nP2 modified = NO\nDock modified = NO\n\n==================================================\n12. NO OTHER RESTORE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT restore the full 19-Aug HomeScreen.kt because that would\nremove Search/Particles entirely.\n\nRepair only the post-restore Search/Particles additions.\n\n==================================================\n13. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm BETA 001 SEARCH/PARTICLES REPAIR COMPLETE\n\nSearch runtime owners:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n1\n\nVisible SearchBars:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n1\n\nParticle engine owners:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n1\n\nParticle region sizing:\n<value>\n\nThin-strip constraint removed:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticles use full reveal height:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHomeScreen modified:\n<YES/NO>\n\nMainActivity modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nLauncherInteractionPatch modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP2 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nBETA_001_DEVICE_RETEST"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:430:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787404208,"text":"FASE — worm BETA 002 FULL CORE/PATCH AUDIT + SETTINGS + SEARCH FIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nBASELINE:\n19-08 restored Home + current Search/Particles additions\n\nMODE:\nAUDIT FIRST\nTHEN PATCH ONLY CONFIRMED ISSUES\n\nOBJECTIVES\n\n1. Audit the complete active project runtime:\n   Core\n   Patch layer\n   Home\n   Search\n   Particle engine\n   Settings/storage\n\n2. Fix the defective Search/reveal area shown on device.\n\n3. Add compact Settings with:\n   - black background\n   - white text\n   - Addy.io-style yellow labels/accents\n   - glyph per category\n   - subcategories\n\n4. Add Settings → Debug ONLY in debug builds.\n\nDo NOT redesign the current Home.\nDo NOT modify P1/P2/Dock geometry unless audit proves a runtime defect.\n\n==================================================\nA. COMPLETE ACTIVE-RUNTIME AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nTrace exact runtime path:\n\nMainActivity\n→ Core host\n→ active patch\n→ HomeScreen\n→ Fav\n→ Search/reveal\n→ P1\n→ P2\n→ Dock\n\nReport exact files and symbols.\n\n==================================================\nB. CORE OWNERS\n==================================================\n\nReport exact owner counts for:\n\nMachinaCore/Core host\nHomeSnapshot\nAppCatalog\nLauncherPreferences\nLauncherActions\nAppVisuals\nslot persistence\n\nExpected:\none authoritative owner per responsibility.\n\nDo not modify Core during audit.\n\n==================================================\nC. PATCH OWNERS\n==================================================\n\nEnumerate every active Kotlin file under:\n\npatches/\n\nReport:\n\n- runtime-reachable patches\n- inactive patch files\n- duplicate gesture owners\n- duplicate Home owners\n\nExpected active launcher interaction patch:\n1\n\nDo not count archived/docs files.\n\n==================================================\nD. HOME OWNERS\n==================================================\n\nReport:\n\nHomeScreen owners\nFavoritesContainer owners\nSearch reveal owners\nP1 owners\nP2 owners\nDock owners\n\nExpected:\n1 each.\n\n==================================================\nE. SEARCH AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nKnown previous audit:\n\nSearchBar had been duplicated.\nParticle engine owner = 1.\n\nRe-check current source after latest changes.\n\nReport:\n\nvisible SearchBar owners\nquery state owners\nSearch focus owners\nSearch underline owners\n\nExpected:\n\nVisible SearchBars = 1\nVisible underlines = 1\nQuery state owners = 1\n\n==================================================\nF. PARTICLE AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nCurrent DEVICE defect:\n\nParticle network is compressed into a thin horizontal strip\nnear the top of the expanded Search region.\n\nInspect exact layout constraints.\n\nReport:\n\nParticleNetwork parent\nCanvas modifier\nmeasured height source\nweight/fixed-height usage\nY coordinate generation\nclipping owner\n\nIdentify exact cause before editing.\n\n==================================================\nG. CURRENT SCREEN TARGET\n==================================================\n\nCurrent Home outside Search region is accepted.\n\nDO NOT change:\n\nFav outer geometry\nHome outer geometry\nP1 panel geometry\nP2 panel geometry\nDock geometry\nDock location\nwallpaper behavior\n\nThe defect is localized to the reveal/Search region.\n\n==================================================\nH. SEARCH REVEAL LAYOUT — REQUIRED\n==================================================\n\nExpanded order must become:\n\nFav Header\n↓\nParticle / Results region\n↓\nSearchBar\n↓\nP1\n↓\nP2\n\nDock remains outside Home.\n\nThere must be NO duplicate SearchBar.\n\n==================================================\nI. PARTICLE AREA FIX\n==================================================\n\nThe Particle/Results region must occupy ALL remaining reveal height.\n\nPreferred internal layout:\n\nColumn(\n    height = revealHeight\n) {\n\n    Box(\n        Modifier\n            .fillMaxWidth()\n            .weight(1f)\n    ) {\n        ParticleNetwork(\n            Modifier.fillMaxSize()\n        )\n    }\n\n    SearchBar(...)\n}\n\nWeight is allowed ONLY inside the reveal area.\n\nDo NOT apply weight to:\n\nHome\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\n==================================================\nJ. PARTICLE DISTRIBUTION\n==================================================\n\nParticles must use full Canvas bounds.\n\nX:\n0 .. canvasWidth\n\nY:\n0 .. canvasHeight\n\nCurrent thin-band behavior must disappear.\n\nDo not use a fixed small Y range.\n\n==================================================\nK. PARTICLE NETWORK VISIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nTarget:\n\n- network clearly visible\n- subtle\n- distributed over full reveal region\n- several clusters\n- thin connection lines\n- continuous smooth motion\n\nSuggested starting count:\n24–36 particles\n\nDo not recreate particles on every recomposition.\n\n==================================================\nL. PARTICLE STATE\n==================================================\n\nOne stable engine only.\n\nParticle state must survive:\n\nquery changes\nfocus changes\nIME changes\nordinary recomposition\n\nNo per-particle coroutine.\n\nNo second Canvas engine.\n\n==================================================\nM. SEARCHBAR STYLE\n==================================================\n\nRequired visual:\n\nmagnifier LEFT\nSearch / query text\nONE underline\n\nBackground:\ntransparent\n\nNO:\npill\nfilled card\nrounded search container\nfull border\n\n==================================================\nN. SEARCHBAR POSITION\n==================================================\n\nSearchBar is anchored at the BOTTOM of Search reveal area.\n\nDirectly above P1.\n\nIt must not float in the middle of the particle region.\n\n==================================================\nO. IME / KEYBOARD\n==================================================\n\nWhen Search gains focus:\n\nkeyboard opens.\n\nP1:\ndo not resize.\n\nP2:\ndo not resize.\n\nDock:\ndo not resize.\n\nDo not introduce multiple imePadding owners.\n\nOne Search/reveal IME owner maximum.\n\n==================================================\nP. SETTINGS — NEW BETA 002\n==================================================\n\nAdd actual Settings UI.\n\nEntry:\n\nFav gear\n→ Settings\n\nSingle Settings navigation owner.\n\n==================================================\nQ. SETTINGS VISUAL\n==================================================\n\nAuthoritative palette:\n\nBACKGROUND:\nblack\n\nPRIMARY TEXT:\nwhite\n\nSECONDARY TEXT:\nwhite with reduced alpha\n\nACCENT / LABEL:\nAddy.io-style yellow\n\nDo NOT use Dynamic Color to override this Beta palette.\n\n==================================================\nR. SETTINGS ROOT CATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nUse exactly:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nIcons\nTime\nSystem\nAbout\n\nDEBUG is added separately only for debug builds.\n\n==================================================\nS. CATEGORY GLYPHS\n==================================================\n\nEach category gets one compact glyph:\n\nAppearance → palette/tune\nHome → home\nSearch → search\nIcons → apps/grid\nTime → schedule\nSystem → settings\nAbout → info\n\nGlyphs:\n\nwhite normally\nyellow when selected/active if useful.\n\n==================================================\nT. SETTINGS ROW STYLE\n==================================================\n\nCompact.\n\nTarget row height:\n48–56dp.\n\nBoolean:\n\nTitle                     [switch]\n\nSelectable:\n\nTitle                 Value >\n\nAction:\n\nTitle                       >\n\nNO card around every row.\nNO yellow border around rows.\n\nMinimal separators only.\n\n==================================================\nU. SETTINGS CATEGORY LABELS\n==================================================\n\nUse yellow for compact section labels.\n\nExample:\n\nAPPEARANCE\nSEARCH\nICONS\n\nDo not make the entire row yellow.\n\n==================================================\nV. SWITCH STYLE\n==================================================\n\nOFF:\n\ntrack:\ndark gray\n\nthumb:\nwhite/gray\n\nON:\n\ntrack:\nyellow\n\nthumb:\nblack/dark\n\nSwitch always aligned RIGHT.\n\n==================================================\nW. APPEARANCE SUBCATEGORY\n==================================================\n\nAppearance:\n\nFav background            Default >\nFav visual effect         [switch]\nStatus bar                Auto >\n\nDo not add fake controls.\n\n==================================================\nX. HOME SUBCATEGORY\n==================================================\n\nHome:\n\nFav Apps                  >\nP1                        >\nP2                        >\nDock                      >\n\nOnly expose configuration pages if functionality exists.\n\nOtherwise keep category minimal.\n\n==================================================\nY. SEARCH SUBCATEGORY\n==================================================\n\nSearch:\n\nApps                      [switch]\nWeb results               [switch]\nShortcuts                 [switch]\nHidden apps               [switch]\nWork profile              [switch]\n\nOnly real backend-supported rows may be enabled.\n\nUnsupported rows:\ndisabled or omitted.\n\n==================================================\nZ. ICONS SUBCATEGORY\n==================================================\n\nIcons:\n\nIcon source               Original >\nIcon pack                 None >\n\nNo bundled icon pack.\n\n==================================================\nAA. TIME SUBCATEGORY\n==================================================\n\nTime:\n\nTime zone                 System >\nTime format               System >\n\nChoices:\n\nSystem\n24-hour\n12-hour AM/PM\n\n==================================================\nAB. SYSTEM SUBCATEGORY\n==================================================\n\nSystem:\n\nDefault Home              >\nApp info                  >\n\nActions, not switches.\n\n==================================================\nAC. ABOUT SUBCATEGORY\n==================================================\n\nAbout:\n\nVersion                   <runtime value>\nChangelog                 >\n\nNo internal patch terminology.\n\n==================================================\nAD. SETTINGS NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nSubcategory:\n\nleft-edge swipe RIGHT\n→ previous Settings level\n\nSystem Back:\nsame behavior.\n\nVertical list scroll:\nnormal.\n\nSwitch first-touch:\nmust work.\n\n==================================================\nAE. DEV DEBUG CATEGORY\n==================================================\n\nIn DEBUG builds only add:\n\nDebug\n\nSubtitle:\nBeta feedback\n\nVisible only when:\n\nBuildConfig.DEBUG == true\n\nRelease:\nABSENT.\n\n==================================================\nAF. DEBUG SUBCATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nSettings → Debug should contain compact sections:\n\nCORE\nHOME\nPATCHES\nSEARCH\nPARTICLES\nSETTINGS\nBUILD\n\n==================================================\nAG. DEBUG — CORE\n==================================================\n\nShow:\n\nCore owner count\nHomeSnapshot owners\nAppCatalog owners\nLauncherPreferences owners\nLauncherActions owners\n\nState values:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\nAH. DEBUG — HOME\n==================================================\n\nShow:\n\nHome owner\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\nP1/P2 equality\nDock external\n\n==================================================\nAI. DEBUG — PATCHES\n==================================================\n\nShow:\n\nActive patches\nGesture owners\nDuplicate patch owners\nFirst-touch blockers\n\n==================================================\nAJ. DEBUG — SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nShow:\n\nSearchBar owners\nUnderline owners\nQuery owners\nFocus owners\nIME owners\n\nExpected:\n\nSearchBar = 1\nUnderline = 1\nQuery owner = 1\n\n==================================================\nAK. DEBUG — PARTICLES\n==================================================\n\nShow:\n\nParticle engine owners\nParticle count\nCanvas width\nCanvas height\nFull-height distribution\nPersistent state\n\n==================================================\nAL. DEBUG — SETTINGS\n==================================================\n\nShow:\n\nSettings root owners\nNavigation owners\nPreference owners\nSwipe Back\nFirst-touch\n\n==================================================\nAM. DEBUG — BUILD\n==================================================\n\nShow development metadata only:\n\nDebug build\nR8\nversion\npackage\n\nDo NOT expose:\n\nfilesystem paths\nhashes\nkeys\nprivate logs\n\n==================================================\nAN. DEBUG RELEASE EXCLUSION\n==================================================\n\nRelease requirements:\n\nDebug Settings row:\nABSENT\n\nDebug route:\nUNREACHABLE\n\nDebug-only model:\nshrinkable/absent\n\nNo debug labels in user UI.\n\n==================================================\nAO. SETTINGS STORE\n==================================================\n\nOne preference owner only.\n\nDo not duplicate LauncherPreferences if a separate settings store\nis unnecessary.\n\nIf Settings needs new production preferences:\nuse one dedicated owner.\n\nReport exact ownership decision.\n\n==================================================\nAP. CORE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT rewrite Core to implement Settings UI.\n\nSettings UI should consume stable contracts/state.\n\nCore changes only if a real setting requires a missing stable\ncontract.\n\nReport any Core change explicitly.\n\n==================================================\nAQ. DEVICE FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nUse this simplified checklist:\n\nHOME\n✓ current geometry\n✓ P1\n✓ P2\n✓ Dock\n\nSEARCH\n○ one SearchBar\n○ one underline\n○ Search position\n○ IME behavior\n\nPARTICLES\n! thin-strip defect\n○ full height\n○ full width\n○ visible network\n○ persistent animation\n\nSETTINGS\n○ gear opens Settings\n○ black background\n○ white text\n○ yellow labels\n○ glyphs\n○ categories\n○ subcategories\n○ switches right\n○ swipe Back\n\nDEBUG\n○ visible in Debug\n○ absent in Release\n\n==================================================\nAR. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm BETA 002 AUDIT / SETTINGS / SEARCH FIX COMPLETE\n\nCore owners:\n<summary>\n\nActive patches:\n<n>\n\nHome owners:\n<n>\n\nSearchBar owners:\n<n>\n\nUnderline owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nParticle Canvas:\n<width x height>\n\nThin-strip cause:\n<value>\n\nThin-strip fixed:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticles use full reveal:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSettings root owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings navigation owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings preference owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings palette:\n<BLACK_WHITE_YELLOW/OTHER>\n\nRoot categories:\n<n>\n\nGlyphs:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSubcategories:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDebug category in Debug build:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDebug category in Release:\n<ABSENT/PRESENT>\n\nHome geometry modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP2 modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nBETA_002_DEVICE_TEST"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:431:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787405372,"text":"FASE — worm BETA 003 DEBUG FEEDBACK / HISTORY / CHANGELOG\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nBASELINE:\nBeta 002\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAdd a DEV-only feedback workflow that:\n\n1. provides a free-text feedback box inside Settings → Debug\n2. timestamps every saved feedback using Europe/Rome timezone\n3. stores feedback/history in a dedicated worm development directory\n4. keeps one history entry per app/version revision\n5. exposes a user-facing changelog under Settings → About\n6. allows Codex/ChatGPT to read the development history from disk\n\nDo NOT modify Home geometry.\nDo NOT modify P1/P2/Dock.\nDo NOT change Core behavior unless a tiny interface is required.\n\n==================================================\n1. DEBUG FEEDBACK BOX\n==================================================\n\nInside:\n\nSettings\n→ Debug\n\nadd a section:\n\nFeedback\n\nUI:\n\nmultiline text field\n\nplaceholder:\n\"Write feedback for this build...\"\n\nactions:\n\nSave feedback\nClear\n\nKeep compact.\n\n==================================================\n2. DEBUG ONLY\n==================================================\n\nFeedback editor is DEV-only.\n\nVisible only when:\n\nBuildConfig.DEBUG == true\n\nRelease:\n\nfeedback editor = ABSENT\nDebug category = ABSENT\n\n==================================================\n3. FEEDBACK METADATA\n==================================================\n\nEvery saved feedback entry must include:\n\napp name\npackage\nversionName\nversionCode\nbuild type\ntimestamp\ntimezone\nfeedback text\n\nTimestamp timezone:\n\nEurope/Rome\n\nUse:\n\njava.time.ZoneId.of(\"Europe/Rome\")\n\nDo NOT use device-local timezone implicitly.\n\n==================================================\n4. TIMESTAMP FORMAT\n==================================================\n\nUse a stable human-readable format:\n\nyyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss z\n\nExample:\n\n2026-08-22 15:42:17 CEST\n\nAlso store ISO form if useful:\n\n2026-08-22T15:42:17+02:00[Europe/Rome]\n\n==================================================\n5. DEVELOPMENT DIRECTORY\n==================================================\n\nCreate a dedicated directory outside app source:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/\n\nPreferred structure:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/\n├── README.md\n├── current/\n│   ├── VERSION.md\n│   ├── FEEDBACK.md\n│   └── STATUS.md\n├── history/\n│   ├── beta-001/\n│   ├── beta-002/\n│   └── beta-003/\n└── changelog/\n    └── CHANGELOG.md\n\nThis directory is development-side only.\n\nDo NOT package /opt/Android/worm/dev into the APK.\n\n==================================================\n6. IMPORTANT ANDROID SANDBOX RULE\n==================================================\n\nThe Android app itself cannot directly write to:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/\n\non the development host.\n\nTherefore use a two-layer model:\n\nDEVICE DEBUG STORAGE\n→ app-private debug storage\n\nHOST DEVELOPMENT HISTORY\n→ /opt/Android/worm/dev/\n\nDo NOT attempt to write /opt paths from Android runtime.\n\n==================================================\n7. DEVICE FEEDBACK STORAGE\n==================================================\n\nInside debug app, save feedback locally in app-private storage.\n\nPreferred:\n\ndebug-only JSON/text store\n\nExample record:\n\n{\n  \"versionName\": \"...\",\n  \"versionCode\": ...,\n  \"timestampRome\": \"...\",\n  \"feedback\": \"...\"\n}\n\nKeep implementation tiny.\n\nNo network.\n\n==================================================\n8. EXPORT FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nAdd Debug action:\n\nCopy feedback\n\nand preferably:\n\nShare feedback\n\nGenerate a plain-text block suitable for:\n\nCodex\nChatGPT\nshell paste\n\nFormat:\n\nworm feedback\n\nVersion:\nBeta 003\n\nBuild:\ndebug\n\nTime:\n2026-08-22 15:42:17 CEST\n\nFeedback:\n<text>\n\n==================================================\n9. HOST FEEDBACK FILE\n==================================================\n\nDefine canonical host-side file:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/current/FEEDBACK.md\n\nFormat:\n\n# worm current feedback\n\nVersion: Beta 003\nTimestamp: 2026-08-22 15:42:17 CEST\nTimezone: Europe/Rome\n\n## Feedback\n\n<feedback text>\n\n## Validation\n\n- Home: ...\n- Search: ...\n- Particles: ...\n- Settings: ...\n- Debug: ...\n\n==================================================\n10. CODEX / CHATGPT READ DIRECTORY\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/README.md\n\nExplain:\n\nThis directory is the canonical development handoff area for\nworm.\n\nCodex/ChatGPT should inspect:\n\ncurrent/VERSION.md\ncurrent/STATUS.md\ncurrent/FEEDBACK.md\nchangelog/CHANGELOG.md\nhistory/\n\nbefore modifying the next version.\n\nDo not treat old history as current state.\n\n==================================================\n11. VERSION FILE\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/current/VERSION.md\n\nExample:\n\n# worm version\n\nChannel: Beta\nVersion: 003\nPackage: com.worm\nBaseline: Beta 002\nStatus: DEVICE_TEST\nCreated: 2026-08-22 15:42:17 CEST\nTimezone: Europe/Rome\n\n==================================================\n12. STATUS FILE\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/current/STATUS.md\n\nUse compact format:\n\nHOME\n✓ / ! / ~ / ○\n\nSEARCH\n✓ / ! / ~ / ○\n\nPARTICLES\n✓ / ! / ~ / ○\n\nSETTINGS\n✓ / ! / ~ / ○\n\nDEBUG\n✓ / ! / ~ / ○\n\nBUILD\n✓ / ! / ~ / ○\n\n==================================================\n13. VERSION HISTORY\n==================================================\n\nFor every promoted development version:\n\ncopy the previous current state into:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/history/<version>/\n\nExample:\n\nhistory/beta-002/\n  VERSION.md\n  FEEDBACK.md\n  STATUS.md\n  CHANGES.md\n\nNever overwrite previous history.\n\n==================================================\n14. VERSION PROMOTION SCRIPT\n==================================================\n\nAdd a small host-side helper under:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/versionctl\n\nor:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/shared/scripts/versionctl\n\nPurpose:\n\narchive current version\ncreate next version directory/state\ntimestamp using Europe/Rome\nupdate changelog\n\nDo NOT run inside Android.\n\n==================================================\n15. CHANGELOG — USER FACING\n==================================================\n\nSettings\n→ About\n→ Changelog\n\nThis is RELEASE-visible.\n\nShow user-facing changes only.\n\nDo NOT include:\n\ninternal debug notes\nfilesystem paths\nCodex instructions\nowner counts\nR8 details\ncheckpoint names\nprivate feedback\n\n==================================================\n16. CHANGELOG SOURCE\n==================================================\n\nKeep canonical development changelog:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/changelog/CHANGELOG.md\n\nBut do NOT make the Android app read /opt at runtime.\n\nInstead generate/copy a release-safe changelog resource during build\nor maintain a small app resource generated from current version data.\n\n==================================================\n17. CHANGELOG FORMAT\n==================================================\n\nExample:\n\nBeta 003\n- Added compact Settings\n- Improved Search reveal area\n- Improved particle-network layout\n- Added developer feedback tools\n\nBeta 002\n- Added Settings categories and subcategories\n\nBeta 001\n- Restored stable Home baseline\n\nKeep concise.\n\n==================================================\n18. SETTINGS ABOUT\n==================================================\n\nAbout page:\n\nVersion          Beta 003\nChangelog        >\n\nOptional:\n\nBuild channel    Beta\n\nDo not expose Debug information here.\n\n==================================================\n19. FEEDBACK VERSION ROLLOVER\n==================================================\n\nWhen next version is created:\n\ncurrent/\n→ archived to history/<previous-version>/\n\nThen current/ is regenerated for new version.\n\nFeedback from previous version must remain immutable in history.\n\n==================================================\n20. FEEDBACK UPDATE POLICY\n==================================================\n\nEach version has its own feedback file.\n\nDo NOT append Beta 004 feedback into Beta 003 history.\n\nOne version:\none canonical feedback state.\n\nMultiple feedback entries in same version may be appended with\ntimestamps if needed.\n\n==================================================\n21. DEBUG UI HISTORY\n==================================================\n\nOptional Debug subsection:\n\nFeedback history\n\nShow only app-local feedback records from debug builds.\n\nDo NOT attempt to browse /opt host history from Android.\n\n==================================================\n22. PRIVACY\n==================================================\n\nDo not automatically capture:\n\ndevice identifiers\naccount details\ncontacts\nsearch contents\ninstalled app list\nlogs\n\nOnly save:\n\nexplicit developer feedback\nversion/build metadata\nvalidation states\n\n==================================================\n23. BUILD TYPE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nDebug build:\n\nSettings → Debug visible\nFeedback editor visible\n\nRelease build:\n\nDebug category absent\nFeedback editor absent\ndebug feedback storage code unreachable/shrinkable\n\nChangelog remains visible.\n\n==================================================\n24. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n25. OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm BETA 003 DEBUG FEEDBACK / HISTORY COMPLETE\n\nDebug feedback editor:\n<YES/NO>\n\nEurope/Rome timestamp:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDevice debug storage:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHost dev directory:\n<path>\n\nCurrent version file:\n<path>\n\nCurrent feedback file:\n<path>\n\nCurrent status file:\n<path>\n\nHistory directory:\n<path>\n\nChangelog:\n<path>\n\nSettings changelog:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDebug category in release:\n<ABSENT/PRESENT>\n\nFeedback editor in release:\n<ABSENT/PRESENT>\n\nHome modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearch modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nBETA_003_DEVICE_TEST"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:432:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787406569,"text":"FASE — worm FULL DEBUG EXPORT\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nSTATUS:\nPRE-APPROVAL / FULL AUDIT\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nCreate one complete development debug bundle that can be uploaded\nfor external review.\n\nDo NOT mark any patch approved.\n\nCurrent patch candidates:\n\nPATCH 001 — Launcher Interaction\nPATCH 002 — Search + Particle Reveal\nPATCH 003 — Settings + Debug DEV\n\nAll remain:\n\nNOT_APPROVED\n\n==================================================\n1. READ-ONLY SOURCE AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nAudit active runtime source.\n\nReport exact runtime chain:\n\nMainActivity\n→ CoreHost\n→ HomeScreen\n→ active patches/components\n\nIdentify:\n\n- Core owners\n- Home owner\n- active patches\n- Search owners\n- Particle owners\n- Settings owners\n- persistence owners\n- gesture owners\n- IME owners\n- haptic owners\n\n==================================================\n2. PATCH STATUS\n==================================================\n\nGenerate:\n\nPATCH 001\nStatus: NOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 002\nStatus: NOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 003\nStatus: NOT_APPROVED\n\nDo not infer approval from build success.\n\n==================================================\n3. PATCH 001 AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nLauncher Interaction:\n\nReport:\n\n- source file\n- runtime reachability\n- gesture owners\n- UP/DOWN handling\n- LEFT/RIGHT handling\n- haptic paths\n- edge behavior\n- first-touch blockers\n- differences vs 19-Aug snapshot\n\n==================================================\n4. PATCH 002 AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nSearch + Particle Reveal:\n\nReport:\n\n- SearchBar owners\n- visible SearchBar renders\n- query owners\n- focus owners\n- IME owners\n- reveal state owners\n- Particle engine owners\n- Canvas owners\n- frame-loop owners\n- particle count\n- particle bounds\n- full-height/full-width usage\n- duplicate Search path\n- particle thin-strip issue\n- current expanded layout order\n\n==================================================\n5. PATCH 003 AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nSettings + Debug DEV:\n\nReport whether actually implemented.\n\nCheck:\n\n- Settings root\n- gear entry\n- categories\n- subcategories\n- glyphs\n- palette\n- switches\n- Settings navigation\n- swipe Back\n- Debug category\n- feedback editor\n- DEV-only gating\n- release exclusion\n\nIf absent:\nsay NOT_IMPLEMENTED.\n\nDo not report planned functionality as implemented.\n\n==================================================\n6. CORE AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nReport exact owners for:\n\nHomeSnapshot\nMachinaCore/CoreHost\nAppCatalog\nLauncherPreferences\nLauncherActions\nAppVisuals\n\nReport duplicates.\n\n==================================================\n7. HOMESCREEN AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nReport:\n\nHomeScreen path\nline count\nruntime owners\nFav owner\nP1 owner\nP2 owner\nDock owner\n\nCheck whether HomeScreen contains:\n\nSearch logic\nParticle logic\nSettings logic\ngesture logic\n\nReport what should be extracted/refactored.\n\n==================================================\n8. SOURCE TREE\n==================================================\n\nGenerate active source tree only.\n\nExclude:\n\nbuild/\n.gradle/\n.kotlin/\narchive/\nbackups/\n\nInclude:\n\napp/src/main/java/com/worm\napp/src/main/res\nGradle files\nManifest\n\n==================================================\n9. FILE INVENTORY\n==================================================\n\nList every active Kotlin file with:\n\npath\nline count\npackage\nmain responsibility\n\n==================================================\n10. RELEVANT SOURCE CONTENT\n==================================================\n\nInclude full text of the critical source files in the debug bundle:\n\nMainActivity.kt\n\nHomeScreen.kt\n\nLauncherInteractionPatch.kt\n\nMachinaCore.kt\n\nHomeSnapshot.kt\n\nAppCatalog.kt\n\nLauncherPreferences.kt\n\nLauncherActions.kt\n\nAppVisuals.kt\n\nall Search/Particle files\n\nall Settings files if present\n\nDo NOT include binary files.\n\n==================================================\n11. GRADLE / MANIFEST\n==================================================\n\nInclude:\n\nsettings.gradle.kts\nbuild.gradle.kts\napp/build.gradle.kts\ngradle.properties\nAndroidManifest.xml\nstrings.xml\nthemes.xml\n\nRedact secrets if any.\n\n==================================================\n12. BUILD AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nCapture full logs.\n\nReport:\n\nDebug SUCCESS/FAILED\nRelease SUCCESS/FAILED\nR8 SUCCESS/FAILED\n\n==================================================\n13. APK INFO\n==================================================\n\nReport:\n\ndebug APK path\ndebug APK size\n\nrelease APK path\nrelease APK size\n\nSHA-256 for both if available.\n\nDo NOT include APK binary in the debug bundle unless explicitly\nrequested.\n\n==================================================\n14. DUPLICATE OWNER AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nReport counts:\n\nHome owners\nCore hosts\nHomeSnapshot owners\nAppCatalog owners\nLauncherPreferences owners\nLauncherInteraction owners\nSearchReveal owners\nSearchBar owners\nquery owners\nfocus owners\nIME owners\nParticle engines\nCanvas owners\nSettings roots\nSettings navigation owners\ngesture owners\nhaptic owners\n\n==================================================\n15. DEAD / SUSPICIOUS CODE\n==================================================\n\nReport:\n\nunused Kotlin files\nunreachable composables\nduplicate helpers\nold package refs\nMachina naming leftovers\nV2/V3 refs\nfeatures/ refs\nlegacy patch refs\n\nDo NOT delete anything.\n\n==================================================\n16. DIFFERENCE VS 19-AUG BASELINE\n==================================================\n\nCompare current active source against:\n\n/opt/Android-rebuild-backup-2026-08-21_06-08-10/Machina/snapshots/2026-08-19_23-06-03/project.tar.gz\n\nClassify active files:\n\nIDENTICAL_EXCEPT_PACKAGE\nMODIFIED_AFTER_RESTORE\nNEW_AFTER_RESTORE\nMISSING_FROM_CURRENT\n\nEspecially report:\n\nMainActivity\nHomeScreen\nLauncherInteractionPatch\nCore files\nSearch/Particles\nSettings\n\n==================================================\n17. DEVICE FEEDBACK TEMPLATE\n==================================================\n\nCreate a concise file:\n\nDEVICE-FEEDBACK.md\n\nwith:\n\nPATCH 001 — Launcher Interaction\n○ UP\n○ DOWN\n○ LEFT\n○ RIGHT\n○ Edge behavior\n○ Haptic\n○ First touch\n\nPATCH 002 — Search + Particles\n○ One SearchBar\n○ Search underline\n○ Reveal\n○ IME\n○ Particle full height\n○ Particle full width\n○ Lines visible\n○ Animation stable\n\nPATCH 003 — Settings\n○ Gear opens Settings\n○ Categories\n○ Subcategories\n○ Glyphs\n○ Black/white/yellow palette\n○ Switches right\n○ Swipe Back\n○ Debug DEV-only\n○ Debug absent in Release\n\nGLOBAL\n○ No crash\n○ Debug build\n○ R8\n○ Release <= 7 MB\n\nStates:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n18. EXPORT DIRECTORY\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/debug-export/\n\nThen create timestamped bundle:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/debug-export/YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS/\n\nUse timezone:\n\nEurope/Rome\n\n==================================================\n19. EXPORT CONTENTS\n==================================================\n\nBundle should contain:\n\nSUMMARY.md\nPATCH-STATUS.md\nDEVICE-FEEDBACK.md\nOWNERS.md\nDIFF-19AUG.md\nSOURCE-TREE.txt\nFILE-INVENTORY.txt\nBUILD-DEBUG.log\nBUILD-RELEASE.log\nAPK-INFO.txt\n\nsource/\n  critical Kotlin/config text copies\n\nDo not include:\n\n.gradle\n.kotlin\nbuild intermediates\nAPK binaries\nkeys\ncredentials\nprivate environment variables\n\n==================================================\n20. ZIP/TAR EXPORT\n==================================================\n\nCreate one archive suitable for upload:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/debug-export/\nworm-full-debug-YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS.tar.gz\n\nAlso generate:\n\nworm-full-debug-YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS.tar.gz.sha256\n\n==================================================\n21. FINAL STATUS\n==================================================\n\nNo patch becomes approved.\n\nRequired:\n\nPATCH 001: NOT_APPROVED\nPATCH 002: NOT_APPROVED\nPATCH 003: NOT_APPROVED\n\nApproval happens only after external review + device feedback.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm FULL DEBUG EXPORT COMPLETE\n\nExport directory:\n<path>\n\nArchive:\n<path>\n\nSHA-256:\n<value>\n\nCritical source files included:\n<n>\n\nActive patches found:\n<n>\n\nPATCH 001:\n<IMPLEMENTED/PARTIAL/MISSING>\n\nPATCH 002:\n<IMPLEMENTED/PARTIAL/MISSING>\n\nPATCH 003:\n<IMPLEMENTED/PARTIAL/MISSING>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nPatches approved:\n0\n\nSTATUS:\nREADY_FOR_EXTERNAL_REVIEW"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:434:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787407405,"text":"FASE — worm BETA CONSOLIDATION / SINGLE PATCH FIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nSOURCE OF TRUTH:\nworm-full-debug-2026-08-22_15-50-02\n\nCURRENT VERIFIED STATE:\n\nRuntime:\nMainActivity\n→ MachinaCoreHost\n→ LauncherInteractionPatch.Attach\n→ HomeScreen\n→ SearchRevealArea / ParticleNetwork\n→ SettingsScreen overlay\n\nCore owners:\nHomeSnapshot = 1\nMachinaCore/CoreHost = 1\nAppCatalog = 1\nLauncherPreferences = 1\nLauncherActions = 1\nAppVisuals = 1\n\nCurrent patch candidates:\nPATCH 001 — Launcher Interaction\nPATCH 002 — Search + Particle Reveal\nPATCH 003 — Settings + Debug\n\nALL PATCHES STATUS:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nBuild baseline:\nDebug = SUCCESS\nRelease = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nPerform ONE consolidated refactor/fix pass.\n\nGoals:\n\n1. preserve stable 19-Aug Core and Home geometry\n2. keep one HomeScreen\n3. reduce HomeScreen.kt complexity\n4. separate Search/Particles cleanly\n5. separate Settings/Debug cleanly\n6. fix Search reveal/particle layout\n7. keep Settings compact black/white/yellow\n8. keep Debug DEV-only\n9. create versioned feedback/history handoff\n10. keep all owners single\n11. preserve build success\n12. do NOT mark patches approved\n\n==================================================\n1. HARD CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nThe following files are considered stable and currently\nIDENTICAL_EXCEPT_PACKAGE versus 19-Aug:\n\nMainActivity.kt\ncore/HomeSnapshot.kt\ncore/MachinaCore.kt\ncatalog/AppCatalog.kt\nstorage/LauncherPreferences.kt\nactions/LauncherActions.kt\nui/common/AppVisuals.kt\nui/design/MachinaDesign.kt\nmodel/LaunchableApp.kt\npatches/launcher_interaction/LauncherInteractionPatch.kt\n\nDo NOT rewrite them unless compilation requires a minimal import/API\nadjustment caused by this refactor.\n\nExpected:\n\nCore behavior changed = NO\nLauncherInteractionPatch behavior changed = NO\n\n==================================================\n2. ONE HOMESCREEN ONLY\n==================================================\n\nKeep exactly one runtime Home:\n\napp/src/main/java/com/worm/ui/home/HomeScreen.kt\n\nExpected runtime Home owners:\n1\n\nHomeScreen remains the single composition/integration point between:\n\nCore state\nUI\nPatch 001\nPatch 002\nPatch 003 entry\n\nDo NOT create:\n\nHomeV2\nHomeV3\nWormHome2\nAlphaHome\nBetaHome\n\n==================================================\n3. HOMESCREEN RESPONSIBILITY AFTER REFACTOR\n==================================================\n\nHomeScreen should own only:\n\n- read/receive current HomeSnapshot\n- Fav composition\n- P1\n- P2\n- Dock\n- overall Home geometry\n- invoke SearchRevealPatch once\n- open Settings once\n- vertical reveal integration if it is truly Home-level\n\nMove implementation details OUT of HomeScreen:\n\nParticleFieldState\nParticleNetwork\ndrawParticleField\nSearchBar implementation\nSearch reveal internals\nSettings implementation\nDebug implementation\n\n==================================================\n4. TARGET PATCH STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nUse exactly these 3 active capability patches:\n\npatches/\n  launcher_interaction/\n    LauncherInteractionPatch.kt\n\n  search_reveal/\n    SearchRevealPatch.kt\n    SearchBar.kt\n    ParticleNetwork.kt\n    SearchRevealState.kt\n\n  settings/\n    SettingsPatch.kt\n    SettingsScreen.kt\n    SettingsNavigation.kt\n    DebugScreen.kt\n\nDo NOT make Home itself another patch.\n\nExpected active patch count:\n3\n\n==================================================\n5. PATCH 001 — KEEP\n==================================================\n\nLauncherInteractionPatch is already verified against 19-Aug as:\n\nIDENTICAL_EXCEPT_PACKAGE\n\nPreserve it.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- horizontal launcher interaction layer\n- existing gesture attach behavior\n- current integration contract\n\nDo NOT put Search or Settings logic into PATCH 001.\n\n==================================================\n6. PATCH 002 — EXTRACT FROM HOMESCREEN\n==================================================\n\nCurrent Search/Particle logic lives in:\n\nui/home/HomeScreen.kt\n\nExtract it into:\n\npatches/search_reveal/\n\nPreserve one owner each:\n\nSearchRevealArea = 1\nSearchBar = 1\nquery state = 1\nfocus owner = 1\nIME owner = 1\nParticleFieldState = 1\nParticle Canvas = 1\nframe loop = 1\n\n==================================================\n7. SEARCHBAR FIX\n==================================================\n\nCurrent debug bundle reports:\n\nvisible SearchBar renders = 1\n\nKeep it that way.\n\nRequired visual:\n\nmagnifier LEFT\nquery/placeholder\nONE underline\ntransparent background\n\nNO:\n\nfilled pill\nrounded Search card\nduplicate Search field\nduplicate underline\n\nExpected:\n\nSearchBar owners = 1\nVisible SearchBars = 1\nVisible underlines = 1\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH REVEAL LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nThe device defect to fix is the Search/particle space.\n\nExpanded layout must be:\n\nFav\n↓\nParticle / Results region\n↓\nSearchBar\n↓\nP1\n↓\nP2\n\nDock stays outside Home.\n\nSearchBar remains directly above P1.\n\n==================================================\n9. PARTICLE THIN-STRIP FIX\n==================================================\n\nCurrent known problem:\n\nParticle Canvas receives a residual/small reveal height and visually\nappears as a thin strip.\n\nFix layout ownership.\n\nPreferred internal SearchReveal layout:\n\nColumn(\n    modifier = Modifier.height(revealHeight)\n) {\n\n    Box(\n        modifier = Modifier\n            .fillMaxWidth()\n            .weight(1f)\n    ) {\n        ParticleNetwork(\n            modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize()\n        )\n    }\n\n    SearchBar(...)\n}\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nweight is allowed inside SearchReveal only.\n\nDo NOT apply weight to:\n\nHome\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\n==================================================\n10. PARTICLE ENGINE\n==================================================\n\nKeep exactly one engine.\n\nMove to:\n\npatches/search_reveal/ParticleNetwork.kt\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- particle model\n- stable particle state\n- frame loop\n- Canvas\n- lines\n- movement\n\nDo NOT put Search state or Home geometry here.\n\n==================================================\n11. PARTICLE STATE\n==================================================\n\nParticle state must not reset because of:\n\nquery changes\nfocus changes\nIME changes\nordinary recomposition\n\nUse stable remembered state.\n\nNo per-particle coroutine.\n\nOne frame loop only.\n\n==================================================\n12. PARTICLE DISTRIBUTION\n==================================================\n\nParticles must use full actual Canvas bounds.\n\nX:\n0 .. width\n\nY:\n0 .. height\n\nNo small fixed vertical Y band.\n\nParticles must visually occupy the full reveal region.\n\n==================================================\n13. PARTICLE NETWORK VISIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nTarget:\n\n24–36 particles as a reasonable starting range\n\nvisible but subtle connection lines\n\nmoderate motion\n\nconnections based on full 2D distance:\n\ndx + dy distance logic\n\nNo almost-invisible network.\n\nNo excessive dense mesh.\n\n==================================================\n14. PARTICLE TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nParticle layer is visual only.\n\nPointer input:\nNONE\n\nIt must not intercept:\n\nSearch taps\nkeyboard focus\nHome gesture handling\n\n==================================================\n15. IME / KEYBOARD\n==================================================\n\nUse one IME geometry owner.\n\nWhen Search opens keyboard:\n\nSearch/reveal region may adapt.\n\nDo NOT create multiple imePadding owners.\n\nDo not let Search implementation independently push:\n\nP1\nP2\nDock\n\nPreserve current approved Home geometry where practical.\n\nReport actual behavior after refactor.\n\n==================================================\n16. PATCH 003 — SETTINGS EXTRACTION\n==================================================\n\nCurrent files:\n\nui/settings/SettingsScreen.kt\nstorage/SettingsPreferences.kt\nstorage/DebugFeedbackStore.kt\n\nMove/organize Settings UI under:\n\npatches/settings/\n\nSettingsPreferences may remain under storage if it is the single\nproduction settings persistence owner.\n\nDebugFeedbackStore may remain storage/debug-related, but must remain\nDEV-oriented and not become a second production SettingsStore.\n\n==================================================\n17. SETTINGS ROOT\n==================================================\n\nRequired root categories:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nIcons\nTime\nSystem\nAbout\n\nDebug:\nDEBUG BUILD ONLY\n\n==================================================\n18. SETTINGS VISUAL SYSTEM\n==================================================\n\nAuthoritative Settings palette:\n\nBACKGROUND:\nBLACK\n\nPRIMARY TEXT:\nWHITE\n\nSECONDARY:\nWHITE reduced alpha\n\nACCENT / SECTION LABELS:\nADDY-style YELLOW\n\nDo NOT use Dynamic Color to override this palette in this version.\n\n==================================================\n19. SETTINGS DESIGN\n==================================================\n\nCompact list.\n\nNo card-heavy interface.\n\nRows:\n\nBoolean:\nTitle                     [switch]\n\nSelectable:\nTitle                 Value >\n\nAction:\nTitle                       >\n\nTarget actionable row height:\napproximately 48–56dp\n\nNo border around every row.\n\n==================================================\n20. SETTINGS GLYPHS\n==================================================\n\nOne compact semantic glyph per category:\n\nAppearance → palette/tune\nHome → home\nSearch → search\nIcons → apps/grid\nTime → schedule\nSystem → settings\nAbout → info\n\nWhite normally.\n\nYellow for active/selected state if appropriate.\n\n==================================================\n21. SETTINGS SUBCATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nAppearance:\n- Fav background\n- Fav visual effect\n- Status bar\n\nHome:\n- Fav Apps\n- P1\n- P2\n- Dock\n\nSearch:\n- Apps\n- Web results\n- Shortcuts\n- Hidden apps\n- Work profile\n\nIcons:\n- Icon source\n- Icon pack\n\nTime:\n- Time zone\n- Time format\n\nSystem:\n- Default Home\n- App info\n\nAbout:\n- Version\n- Changelog\n\nOnly enable options with real backend support.\n\nDo not fake functionality.\n\n==================================================\n22. SETTINGS NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nUse one navigation owner.\n\nSubcategory:\n\nleft-edge swipe RIGHT\n→ previous Settings level\n\nSystem Back:\nsame previous level\n\nVertical scroll:\nmust remain functional.\n\nNo forward navigation gesture.\n\n==================================================\n23. SETTINGS ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nFav gear:\n\n→ SettingsPatch.open / SettingsScreen\n\nSingle gear click owner.\n\nSettings must not be duplicated as another Activity unless already\nrequired by architecture.\n\n==================================================\n24. DEBUG — DEV ONLY\n==================================================\n\nSettings → Debug\n\nVisible only when:\n\nBuildConfig.DEBUG\n\nRelease:\nDebug category ABSENT\nDebug screen unreachable\n\nNo release navigation path to Debug.\n\n==================================================\n25. DEBUG SECTIONS\n==================================================\n\nUse compact sections:\n\nCORE\nHOME\nPATCHES\nSEARCH\nPARTICLES\nSETTINGS\nBUILD\nFEEDBACK\n\n==================================================\n26. DEBUG OWNER STATUS\n==================================================\n\nShow concise runtime state:\n\nCORE\n- HomeSnapshot owners\n- CoreHost owners\n- AppCatalog owners\n- LauncherPreferences owners\n\nHOME\n- HomeScreen owners\n- Fav owners\n- P1 owners\n- P2 owners\n- Dock owners\n\nPATCHES\n- active patch count\n- LauncherInteraction owners\n- SearchReveal owners\n- Settings owners\n\nSEARCH\n- SearchBar owners\n- query owners\n- focus owners\n- IME owners\n\nPARTICLES\n- engine owners\n- Canvas owners\n- particle count\n- Canvas dimensions\n\nSETTINGS\n- root owners\n- navigation owners\n- preference owners\n\n==================================================\n27. DEBUG FEEDBACK EDITOR\n==================================================\n\nAdd/keep a compact multiline feedback field.\n\nFields:\n\nFeedback text\n\nActions:\n\nSave\nClear\nCopy summary\n\nFeedback states:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n28. FEEDBACK TIMESTAMP\n==================================================\n\nEvery saved feedback entry must use:\n\nZoneId.of(\"Europe/Rome\")\n\nHuman-readable format:\n\nyyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss z\n\nAlso store ISO timestamp if practical.\n\nDo not rely on arbitrary device timezone.\n\n==================================================\n29. DEBUG FEEDBACK METADATA\n==================================================\n\nStore:\n\napp = worm\npackage = com.worm\nversionName\nversionCode\nbuildType\ntimestampEuropeRome\nfeedback\nvalidation states\n\nDo NOT automatically collect:\n\ndevice identifiers\naccounts\ncontacts\nsearch terms\ninstalled-app inventory\n\n==================================================\n30. HOST DEV HANDOFF DIRECTORY\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/\n\nStructure:\n\ndev/\n├── README.md\n├── current/\n│   ├── VERSION.md\n│   ├── STATUS.md\n│   └── FEEDBACK.md\n├── history/\n└── changelog/\n    └── CHANGELOG.md\n\nThis directory is for Codex/ChatGPT/developer handoff.\n\nIt is NOT part of Android runtime.\n\n==================================================\n31. DEV README\n==================================================\n\nREADME.md must explain:\n\nBefore modifying worm, inspect:\n\ndev/current/VERSION.md\ndev/current/STATUS.md\ndev/current/FEEDBACK.md\ndev/changelog/CHANGELOG.md\n\nhistory/ is historical only.\n\nDo not treat previous history as current state.\n\n==================================================\n32. DEVICE/HOST SEPARATION\n==================================================\n\nAndroid app must NOT attempt to write:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/\n\nDevice Debug feedback:\napp-private debug storage\n\nHost history:\ndev/ directory\n\nProvide Copy feedback summary so the developer can paste/export\ndevice feedback into host workflow.\n\n==================================================\n33. VERSION HISTORY\n==================================================\n\nFor each future version:\n\narchive prior current state into:\n\ndev/history/<version>/\n\nInclude:\n\nVERSION.md\nSTATUS.md\nFEEDBACK.md\nCHANGES.md\n\nNever overwrite previous version history.\n\n==================================================\n34. CHANGELOG\n==================================================\n\nCanonical host changelog:\n\ndev/changelog/CHANGELOG.md\n\nSettings → About → Changelog must show a release-safe user-facing\nversion.\n\nDo NOT show:\n\nfilesystem paths\ndebug notes\nCodex instructions\nR8 internals\nowner counts\nprivate feedback\n\n==================================================\n35. CURRENT PATCH STATUS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT approve anything.\n\nSet:\n\nPATCH 001 — IMPLEMENTED / NOT_APPROVED\nPATCH 002 — IMPLEMENTED / DEVICE_RETEST / NOT_APPROVED\nPATCH 003 — IMPLEMENTED / DEVICE_TEST / NOT_APPROVED\n\nApproval count:\n0\n\n==================================================\n36. CODE REDUCTION\n==================================================\n\nCurrent known large files:\n\nHomeScreen.kt ≈ 945 lines\nSettingsScreen.kt ≈ 954 lines\n\nReduce responsibilities.\n\nTarget concept:\n\nHomeScreen.kt:\norchestration/layout only\n\nSearchRevealPatch.kt:\nSearch reveal orchestration\n\nSearchBar.kt:\nSearch field only\n\nParticleNetwork.kt:\nparticle engine only\n\nSettingsScreen.kt:\nSettings root/navigation shell\n\nSettings components:\nrows/categories/subcategory content\n\nDebugScreen.kt:\nDEV-only debug/feedback UI\n\nDo not chase arbitrary line counts if readability suffers.\n\n==================================================\n37. DEAD CODE AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nAfter extraction, identify and remove only proven:\n\nunused imports\nduplicate Search helpers\nobsolete particle helpers\nunreachable composables\nduplicate constants\ndead post-restore experimental paths\n\nDo NOT delete archive/history.\n\n==================================================\n38. NAMING CLEANUP\n==================================================\n\nDo not perform a broad product rename refactor.\n\nOld \"Machina\" class/resource names may remain if they are stable internal\nidentifiers and changing them introduces risk.\n\nPackage/app identity remains:\n\ncom.worm\nworm\n\nNo runtime old package:\nit.gaetano.machinahome\n\n==================================================\n39. OWNER ASSERTIONS\n==================================================\n\nRequired after refactor:\n\nHomeScreen owners = 1\nCoreHost owners = 1\nHomeSnapshot owners = 1\nAppCatalog owners = 1\nLauncherPreferences owners = 1\nLauncherInteraction owners = 1\n\nSearchReveal owners = 1\nSearchBar owners = 1\nquery owners = 1\nfocus owners = 1\nIME owners = 1\n\nParticle engines = 1\nParticle Canvas owners = 1\nframe loops = 1\n\nSettings root owners = 1\nSettings navigation owners = 1\nSettings production preference owners = 1\nDebug feedback stores = 1\n\n==================================================\n40. HOME VISUAL LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT alter accepted Home geometry outside Search reveal.\n\nRequired unchanged:\n\nHome outer geometry\nFav base geometry\nP1 geometry\nP2 geometry\nDock geometry\nDock external placement\n\nReport any unavoidable change.\n\n==================================================\n41. PATCH BEHAVIOR LOCK\n==================================================\n\nPATCH 001:\nbehavior unchanged\n\nPATCH 002:\nbehavior unchanged except:\n- particle thin-strip defect fixed\n- code extracted/cleaned\n\nPATCH 003:\nbehavior preserved/improved structurally\n- Settings compact\n- Debug DEV-only\n- feedback/history integration\n\n==================================================\n42. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew clean assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nRelease = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n43. APK SIZE\n==================================================\n\nReport:\n\nDebug size\n\nRelease size\n\nCurrent reference release:\n~2.0 MB\n\nHard gate:\nRelease <= 7 MB\n\nDo not add heavy dependencies.\n\n==================================================\n44. FULL POST-REFACTOR AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nGenerate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/current/STATUS.md\n\nInclude:\n\nPATCH 001\nPATCH 002\nPATCH 003\n\nand simplified feedback:\n\nPATCH 001 — Launcher Interaction\n○ gestures\n○ edge behavior\n○ haptic\n○ first touch\n\nPATCH 002 — Search / Particles\n○ SearchBar\n○ underline\n○ reveal\n○ IME\n○ particles full width\n○ particles full height\n○ lines\n○ animation\n\nPATCH 003 — Settings / Debug\n○ gear\n○ categories\n○ subcategories\n○ glyphs\n○ black/white/yellow\n○ switches right\n○ swipe Back\n○ Debug visible in debug\n○ Debug absent in release\n○ feedback save\n○ Europe/Rome timestamp\n○ changelog\n\n==================================================\n45. NO AUTO APPROVAL\n==================================================\n\nBuild success does NOT approve patches.\n\nAfter this phase:\n\napproved patches = 0\n\nDevice test required.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm BETA CONSOLIDATION COMPLETE\n\nRuntime chain:\n<value>\n\nActive patch count:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n3\n\nPATCH 001:\n<IMPLEMENTED/FAILED>\nApproval:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 002:\n<IMPLEMENTED/FAILED>\nApproval:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 003:\n<IMPLEMENTED/FAILED>\nApproval:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nHomeScreen owners:\n<n>\n\nHomeScreen lines before:\n<n>\n\nHomeScreen lines after:\n<n>\n\nSearchReveal owners:\n<n>\n\nSearchBar owners:\n<n>\n\nQuery owners:\n<n>\n\nFocus owners:\n<n>\n\nIME owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nParticle Canvas owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle full reveal:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSettings root owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings navigation owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings preference owners:\n<n>\n\nDebug feedback stores:\n<n>\n\nDebug category in Debug:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDebug category in Release:\n<ABSENT/PRESENT>\n\nEurope/Rome feedback timestamp:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHost dev directory:\n<path>\n\nChangelog:\n<path>\n\nDead code removed:\n<n files / n lines>\n\nCore behavior changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nLauncherInteraction behavior changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHome geometry outside Search changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nDebug APK size:\n<value>\n\nRelease APK size:\n<value>\n\nRelease <= 7 MB:\n<YES/NO>\n\nApproved patches:\n0\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_TEST_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:435:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787408830,"text":"FASE — worm BETA HOTFIX 001\nCRASH + SEARCH + IME + INITIAL APP POPULATION\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nCURRENT STATUS:\nDEVICE TEST FAILED\n\nPATCH 001:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 002:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 003:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nCONFIRMED DEVICE BUGS:\n\nCRITICAL\n- Debug build crashes\n\nBUG 1\n- SearchBar / Search reveal / particle animation defective\n\nBUG 2\n- Opening keyboard moves the entire Home container upward\n\nBUG 3\n- P1 and P2 contain no apps\n\nBUG 4\n- No initial app arrangement/population on installation\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFix these confirmed device failures in ONE controlled revision.\n\nDo NOT redesign the accepted collapsed Home.\n\nDo NOT approve any patch.\n\n==================================================\n1. CRASH FIRST\n==================================================\n\nBefore changing behavior, reproduce/capture the Debug crash.\n\nFind the FIRST real runtime exception.\n\nCollect:\n\nexception type\nmessage\nfirst com.worm stack frame\nActivity/Composable involved\ntrigger action\n\nDetermine whether crash belongs to:\n\nSettings/Debug\nSearch\nParticles\nIME\nCore\nLauncherPreferences\ninitialization\nother\n\nDo NOT guess.\n\n==================================================\n2. CRASH FIX\n==================================================\n\nFix only the confirmed root cause.\n\nRequired after fix:\n\ncold launch:\nPASS\n\nHome launch:\nPASS\n\nopen Settings:\nPASS\n\nopen Debug:\nPASS\n\nopen Search:\nPASS\n\nkeyboard open:\nPASS\n\nNo broad try/catch swallowing errors.\n\n==================================================\n3. SEARCH — SINGLE STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nRequired expanded hierarchy:\n\nFav\n↓\nParticle/Search-results area\n↓\nONE SearchBar\n↓\nP1\n↓\nP2\n\nDock remains external.\n\nRequired owners:\n\nSearchReveal = 1\nSearchBar = 1\nQuery = 1\nFocus = 1\nIME = 1\nParticle engine = 1\n\n==================================================\n4. SEARCHBAR\n==================================================\n\nRequired style:\n\nmagnifier LEFT\nquery/placeholder\nONE underline\ntransparent background\n\nRemove:\n\nduplicate SearchBar\nduplicate underline\nfilled pill\nrounded enclosing Search card\n\n==================================================\n5. PARTICLE REGION\n==================================================\n\nParticleNetwork must fill all available reveal space above SearchBar.\n\nNo thin strip.\n\nPreferred internal layout:\n\nColumn {\n    Box(\n        Modifier\n            .fillMaxWidth()\n            .weight(1f)\n    ) {\n        ParticleNetwork(\n            Modifier.fillMaxSize()\n        )\n    }\n\n    SearchBar(...)\n}\n\nWeight is allowed ONLY inside SearchReveal.\n\n==================================================\n6. PARTICLE ENGINE\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\none engine\none Canvas\none frame loop\n\nParticles distributed across:\n\nX = full Canvas width\nY = full Canvas height\n\nState must survive:\n\nquery changes\nfocus\nIME\nrecomposition\n\nDo not recreate field constantly.\n\n==================================================\n7. PARTICLE VISIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nTarget:\n\n24–36 particles\nvisible thin connection lines\nmoderate continuous motion\n\nParticles:\npresentation only\n\nPointer input:\nNONE\n\n==================================================\n8. IME BUG\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT DEFECT:\n\nkeyboard opening raises the entire Home container.\n\nThis is NOT allowed.\n\nAudit all active:\n\nimePadding()\nwindowInsetsPadding(WindowInsets.ime)\nnavigationBarsWithImePadding()\nbringIntoViewRequester\nadjustResize interactions\nroot Column/Box IME modifiers\n\nFind the actual owner causing global Home displacement.\n\n==================================================\n9. IME REQUIRED BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nWhen keyboard opens:\n\nHome outer position:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP1:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP2:\nUNCHANGED\n\nDock:\nUNCHANGED\n\nFav:\nUNCHANGED\n\nOnly Search/reveal region may shrink/adapt.\n\nSearchBar must remain visible.\n\n==================================================\n10. ONE IME OWNER\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nIME geometry owners = 1\n\nApply keyboard/inset adaptation ONLY to SearchReveal.\n\nDo NOT apply IME padding to:\n\nHome root\nFavoritesContainer\nP1/P2 parent\nDock parent\n\n==================================================\n11. P1/P2 EMPTY BUG\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT DEFECT:\n\nP1 = no apps\nP2 = no apps\n\nAudit why.\n\nTrace:\n\nAppCatalog\n→ launchable apps\n→ persisted HomeSnapshot\n→ initial assignment\n→ P1/P2 rendering\n\nReport exact failure point.\n\n==================================================\n12. APP CATALOG VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nAt launch verify AppCatalog returns actual launchable apps.\n\nReport:\n\ncatalog app count\n\nIf:\n0\n\nfix catalog/package query visibility/runtime issue first.\n\nDo NOT fabricate applications.\n\n==================================================\n13. FIRST INSTALL INITIALIZATION\n==================================================\n\nImplement/re-enable one initial arrangement owner.\n\nOnly when:\n\nthere is no existing saved Home assignment\n\nDo NOT overwrite an already configured Home.\n\n==================================================\n14. USAGE ACCESS\n==================================================\n\nIf UsageStats permission/access is available:\n\nrank eligible launchable apps using recent local usage.\n\nUse public:\n\nUsageStatsManager\n\nSuggested window:\n30 days\n\nRanking may combine:\n\nforeground usage\nrecency\n\nDeterministic tie-break.\n\n==================================================\n15. FALLBACK WITHOUT USAGE ACCESS\n==================================================\n\nIf Usage Access is unavailable:\n\nDO NOT leave P1/P2 permanently empty.\n\nUse a deterministic safe fallback based on launchable apps.\n\nPreferred:\n\nstable alphabetical/catalog ordering\n\nafter excluding Dock apps.\n\nThis is first-install fallback only.\n\n==================================================\n16. P1 POPULATION\n==================================================\n\nP1:\n\nfirst 8 eligible apps\n\nPriority:\n\nusage-ranked if available\n\notherwise deterministic fallback.\n\n==================================================\n17. P2 POPULATION\n==================================================\n\nP2:\n\nnext 8 eligible apps\n\nNo duplicates with P1.\n\n==================================================\n18. DOCK INITIALIZATION\n==================================================\n\nUse exactly 5 semantic slots:\n\n0 Phone\n1 Messages\n2 Browser\n3 Music\n4 WhatsApp\n\nResolve using supported public Android APIs where possible.\n\n==================================================\n19. PHONE\n==================================================\n\nResolve current default Phone/Dialer.\n\nIf unavailable:\nempty.\n\n==================================================\n20. MESSAGES\n==================================================\n\nResolve current default SMS app.\n\nIf unavailable:\nempty.\n\n==================================================\n21. BROWSER\n==================================================\n\nResolve current default web browser / HTTPS handler.\n\nIf unavailable:\nempty.\n\n==================================================\n22. MUSIC\n==================================================\n\nResolve a reliable default audio/music handler.\n\nIf no reliable resolver:\nempty.\n\nDo NOT assign random usage-ranked app.\n\n==================================================\n23. WHATSAPP\n==================================================\n\nIf standard WhatsApp is installed and launchable:\nassign it.\n\nOtherwise:\nempty.\n\nDo not substitute another messaging app.\n\n==================================================\n24. DOCK EXCLUSION\n==================================================\n\nAny package placed in Dock must be excluded from:\n\nP1\nP2\n\nRequired duplicates:\n0\n\n==================================================\n25. INITIALIZATION ONCE\n==================================================\n\nInitial automatic arrangement happens only when:\n\nsaved layout does not exist\n\nAfter initialization:\n\npersist HomeSnapshot\n\nSubsequent launches:\ndo not reorder automatically.\n\nManual future edits always win.\n\n==================================================\n26. FRESH com.worm PACKAGE\n==================================================\n\nRemember:\n\ncom.worm is a new applicationId.\n\nTherefore old Machina preferences do NOT automatically exist.\n\nInitialization must correctly handle a completely fresh install.\n\nDo not assume migrated state exists.\n\n==================================================\n27. PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nUse existing:\n\nLauncherPreferences\n\nas the single Home persistence owner.\n\nDo NOT create a second slot persistence system.\n\nRequired:\n\nLauncherPreferences owners = 1\n\n==================================================\n28. HOMESCREEN\n==================================================\n\nHomeScreen reads actual snapshot.\n\nDo not hardcode empty P1/P2.\n\nP1/P2 rendering must use:\n\nHomeSnapshot.p1\nHomeSnapshot.p2\n\nor current equivalent.\n\n==================================================\n29. SETTINGS / DEBUG\n==================================================\n\nPreserve Patch 003.\n\nBut because Debug currently crashes:\n\ntest explicitly:\n\nSettings gear\n→ Settings\n→ Debug\n\nDebug must be visible only in debug build.\n\nRelease:\nABSENT.\n\n==================================================\n30. DEBUG FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nUpdate Debug device checklist:\n\nCRITICAL\n○ Cold launch\n○ Settings open\n○ Debug open\n○ No crash\n\nSEARCH\n○ One SearchBar\n○ One underline\n○ Full particle area\n○ Particles continuous\n○ Search focus\n\nIME\n○ Keyboard opens\n○ Home fixed\n○ P1 fixed\n○ P2 fixed\n○ Dock fixed\n○ Search remains visible\n\nINITIALIZATION\n○ AppCatalog > 0\n○ First-install detected\n○ P1 populated\n○ P2 populated\n○ Dock initialized\n○ No duplicates\n○ Persistence survives relaunch\n\n==================================================\n31. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew clean assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nRelease = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n32. DEVICE TEST STATUS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT approve patches from static/build checks.\n\nAll remain:\n\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nuntil device validation.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm BETA HOTFIX 001 COMPLETE\n\nCRASH\nRoot cause:\n<value>\n\nFirst failing frame:\n<value>\n\nCrash fixed:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCold launch:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSettings open:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nDebug open:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\n\nSEARCH\n\nSearchReveal owners:\n<n>\n\nSearchBar owners:\n<n>\n\nUnderline owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nParticle Canvas owners:\n<n>\n\nParticles full reveal:\n<YES/NO>\n\nParticle count:\n<n>\n\n\nIME\n\nIME owners:\n<n>\n\nGlobal Home IME padding removed:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHome moves with keyboard:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1 moves:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP2 moves:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock moves:\n<NO/YES>\n\n\nINITIALIZATION\n\nAppCatalog count:\n<n>\n\nInitial-layout owners:\n<n>\n\nUsage access:\n<AVAILABLE/UNAVAILABLE>\n\nRanking:\n<USAGE/FALLBACK>\n\nP1 apps:\n<n>/8\n\nP2 apps:\n<n>/8\n\nDock Phone:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY>\n\nDock Messages:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY>\n\nDock Browser:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY>\n\nDock Music:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY>\n\nDock WhatsApp:\n<RESOLVED/EMPTY>\n\nDuplicate packages:\n<n>\n\nLauncherPreferences owners:\n<n>\n\nLayout persists after relaunch:\n<YES/NO>\n\n\nBUILD\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease APK size:\n<value>\n\nApproved patches:\n0\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_RETEST_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:436:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787410261,"text":"FASE — worm SETTINGS REBUILD / BUGFIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nSCOPE:\nSETTINGS ONLY\n\nCURRENT STATUS:\nDEVICE TEST FAILED / VARIOUS SETTINGS BUGS\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nRebuild the Settings UI cleanly and remove the current bugs.\n\nDo NOT modify:\n\n- Home geometry\n- Search reveal\n- Particle engine\n- P1\n- P2\n- Dock\n- Core behavior\n- LauncherInteractionPatch\n- first-install/autofill logic\n\n==================================================\n1. REBUILD SETTINGS STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nReplace the current oversized/buggy Settings implementation with\na compact single-owner Settings architecture.\n\nTarget:\n\npatches/settings/\n  SettingsPatch.kt\n  SettingsScreen.kt\n  SettingsNavigation.kt\n  SettingsComponents.kt\n  SettingsSections.kt\n  DebugScreen.kt\n\nKeep persistence separate.\n\n==================================================\n2. SINGLE OWNERS\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nSettings root owners = 1\nSettings navigation owners = 1\nSettings preference owners = 1\nDebug feedback stores = 1\n\nNo duplicate BackHandler.\nNo duplicate Settings overlay.\nNo duplicate navigation stack.\n\n==================================================\n3. SETTINGS ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nFav gear\n→ Settings\n\nOne click owner only.\n\nOpening Settings must not alter Home state.\n\n==================================================\n4. VISUAL STYLE\n==================================================\n\nAuthoritative palette:\n\nBACKGROUND:\nBLACK\n\nPRIMARY TEXT:\nWHITE\n\nSECONDARY TEXT:\nWHITE at reduced alpha\n\nACCENT / SECTION LABELS:\nADDY-style YELLOW\n\nNo Dynamic Color override for this version.\n\nNo gray wallpaper.\nNo large colored cards.\n\n==================================================\n5. ROOT CATEGORIES\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\nAppearance\nHome\nSearch\nIcons\nTime\nSystem\nAbout\n\nDebug:\nDEBUG builds only\n\nEach row:\n\nglyph left\ntitle\noptional subtitle\nvalue/chevron right\n\n==================================================\n6. GLYPHS\n==================================================\n\nAppearance → tune/palette\nHome → home\nSearch → search\nIcons → apps/grid\nTime → schedule\nSystem → settings\nAbout → info\nDebug → bug/developer glyph\n\nSmall, monochrome, consistent.\n\n==================================================\n7. ROW DESIGN\n==================================================\n\nBoolean:\n\nTitle                      [switch]\n\nSelectable:\n\nTitle                  Value >\n\nAction:\n\nTitle                        >\n\nTarget height:\n48–56dp\n\nNo card around each row.\n\nNo yellow border around rows.\n\n==================================================\n8. SWITCH STYLE\n==================================================\n\nOFF:\ndark gray track\nwhite/gray thumb\n\nON:\nyellow track\nblack/dark thumb\n\nSwitch always on RIGHT.\n\nSwitch tap must work first touch.\n\n==================================================\n9. APPEARANCE\n==================================================\n\nAppearance:\n\nFav background            Default >\nFav visual effect         [switch]\nStatus bar                Auto >\n\nOnly real controls.\n\n==================================================\n10. HOME\n==================================================\n\nHome:\n\nFav Apps                  >\nP1                        >\nP2                        >\nDock                      >\n\nIf no real configuration page exists:\ndo not invent fake controls.\n\n==================================================\n11. SEARCH\n==================================================\n\nSearch:\n\nApps                      [switch]\nWeb results               [switch]\nShortcuts                 [switch]\nHidden apps               [switch]\nWork profile              [switch]\n\nUnsupported backend:\ndisable or omit row.\n\n==================================================\n12. ICONS\n==================================================\n\nIcons:\n\nIcon source               Original >\nIcon pack                 None >\n\nMissing pack:\nfallback to original.\n\n==================================================\n13. TIME\n==================================================\n\nTime:\n\nTime zone                 System >\nTime format               System >\n\nChoices:\n\nSystem\n24-hour\n12-hour AM/PM\n\n==================================================\n14. SYSTEM\n==================================================\n\nSystem:\n\nDefault Home              >\nApp info                  >\n\nThese are actions, not switches.\n\n==================================================\n15. ABOUT\n==================================================\n\nAbout:\n\nVersion                   <runtime value>\nChangelog                 >\n\nNo debug/internal patch names in About.\n\n==================================================\n16. SETTINGS NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nUse one navigation stack.\n\nRoot\n→ subcategory\n→ optional nested page\n\nSystem Back:\nprevious level\n\nleft-edge swipe RIGHT:\nprevious level\n\nAt root:\nBack closes Settings\n\nLEFT swipe:\nno Forward navigation\n\n==================================================\n17. SWIPE BACK BUG SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nSwipe Back must not steal:\n\nswitch taps\nrow taps\nvertical scroll\n\nUse touchSlop + axis lock.\n\nVertical movement:\nscroll wins.\n\nIntentional rightward edge swipe:\nBack wins.\n\n==================================================\n18. SCROLL\n==================================================\n\nAll long subcategory lists must scroll vertically.\n\nNo nested scroll conflict.\n\nNo page clipping.\n\n==================================================\n19. STATUS BAR\n==================================================\n\nSettings must respect status-bar inset.\n\nNo content under signal/battery/time.\n\nDo not alter Home status-bar behavior.\n\n==================================================\n20. DEBUG CATEGORY\n==================================================\n\nDebug visible only when:\n\nBuildConfig.DEBUG == true\n\nRelease:\nDebug row absent\nDebug route unreachable\n\n==================================================\n21. DEBUG SECTIONS\n==================================================\n\nDebug screen:\n\nCORE\nHOME\nPATCHES\nSEARCH\nPARTICLES\nSETTINGS\nBUILD\nFEEDBACK\n\nCompact rows only.\n\n==================================================\n22. DEBUG FEEDBACK EDITOR\n==================================================\n\nInclude:\n\nmultiline feedback field\nSave\nClear\nCopy summary\n\nTimestamp:\nEurope/Rome\n\nUse:\n\nZoneId.of(\"Europe/Rome\")\n\n==================================================\n23. DEBUG FEEDBACK STATE\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\nNo automatic device PASS from build success.\n\n==================================================\n24. SETTINGS PERSISTENCE\n==================================================\n\nUse one production settings store.\n\nDo not create duplicate preferences.\n\nDebug feedback storage:\nseparate DEV-only store.\n\n==================================================\n25. RELEASE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nVerify release:\n\nDebug category = ABSENT\nDebugScreen unreachable\nDebug feedback editor absent\nNo dev labels visible\n\n==================================================\n26. REMOVE BUGGY/DEAD SETTINGS CODE\n==================================================\n\nAfter rebuild identify:\n\nduplicate composables\nunused settings rows\ndead navigation code\nduplicate BackHandlers\nunused imports\nold Settings helpers\nobsolete debug paths\n\nRemove only proven dead code.\n\n==================================================\n27. HOMESCREEN LOCK\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nHome modified = NO\nSearch modified = NO\nParticles modified = NO\nP1 modified = NO\nP2 modified = NO\nDock modified = NO\n\n==================================================\n28. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew clean assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nRelease = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm SETTINGS REBUILD COMPLETE\n\nSettings root owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings navigation owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings preference owners:\n<n>\n\nDebug feedback stores:\n<n>\n\nRoot categories:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n7\n\nDebug category in Debug:\n<YES/NO>\n\nDebug category in Release:\n<ABSENT/PRESENT>\n\nGlyphs:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSubcategories:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSwitches right aligned:\n<YES/NO>\n\nSwipe Back:\n<YES/NO>\n\nVertical scroll:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nFirst-touch regression:\n<NONE/FOUND>\n\nDuplicate BackHandlers:\n<n>\n\nDead Settings code removed:\n<n files / n lines>\n\nHome modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearch modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nParticles modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nSETTINGS_DEVICE_RETEST_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:437:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787410796,"text":"FASE — worm SEARCH / IME GEOMETRY HOTFIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nSCOPE:\nSEARCH + IME ONLY\n\nCONFIRMED DEVICE BUGS:\n\n1. Keyboard opening shifts/layouts Search incorrectly\n2. Cursor/pointer is not aligned with the Search field\n3. Search reveal space has no clear gap rules\n4. Search reveal space has no defined background ownership\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFix Search geometry and IME behavior without modifying:\n\n- Home outer geometry\n- Fav base geometry\n- P1\n- P2\n- Dock\n- Core\n- Settings\n- LauncherInteractionPatch\n\n==================================================\n1. SINGLE SEARCH GEOMETRY OWNER\n==================================================\n\nCreate one SearchReveal geometry owner.\n\nIt must define:\n\n- reveal height\n- top gap\n- bottom gap\n- SearchBar height\n- SearchBar baseline\n- particle/results area\n- background\n- IME adaptation\n\nRemove competing layout calculations.\n\nExpected Search geometry owners:\n1\n\n==================================================\n2. EXPANDED SEARCH STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nRequired hierarchy:\n\nFav\n↓\nTOP GAP\n↓\nParticle / Results area\n↓\nBOTTOM GAP\n↓\nSearchBar\n↓\nGAP\n↓\nP1\n\nUse explicit shared tokens.\n\nNo accidental spacing from stacked Spacer + padding + Arrangement.\n\n==================================================\n3. GAP RULES\n==================================================\n\nDefine deterministic gaps.\n\nStarting values:\n\nFav → Search area:\n8–12dp\n\nParticle/results → SearchBar:\n6–10dp\n\nSearchBar → P1:\n8–12dp\n\nUse one token owner.\n\nDo not let IME or available height arbitrarily change these gaps.\n\n==================================================\n4. SEARCH REVEAL BACKGROUND\n==================================================\n\nDefine one background owner for the expanded Search region.\n\nRequired:\n\n- transparent or very dark subtle surface\n- no random inherited background\n- no white/gray block\n- no card around SearchBar\n- Particle Network rendered above this background\n\nPrefer transparent background if wallpaper/particle presentation\nalready provides the intended look.\n\n==================================================\n5. SEARCHBAR VISUAL\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nmagnifier LEFT\neditable text\nONE underline\ntransparent background\n\nNo pill.\nNo enclosing rounded card.\n\n==================================================\n6. SEARCHBAR INTERNAL LAYOUT\n==================================================\n\nUse one Row/Box layout with explicit vertical alignment.\n\nMagnifier:\ncenter vertically to text field content.\n\nText field:\nstable fixed/min height.\n\nUnderline:\ndrawn independently below content.\n\nDo not use a TextField style that adds hidden internal padding if it\nbreaks cursor alignment.\n\n==================================================\n7. CURSOR / POINTER BUG\n==================================================\n\nCurrent defect:\n\ntext cursor/pointer is visually not in the correct Search field position.\n\nAudit:\n\n- text field contentPadding\n- baseline\n- line height\n- vertical alignment\n- graphicsLayer/translation\n- parent offset\n- SearchBar animation offset\n- density conversion\n\nFind the real cause before changing numbers.\n\n==================================================\n8. CURSOR TARGET\n==================================================\n\nWhen Search receives focus:\n\ncursor must start immediately after the query/placeholder start position.\n\nCursor Y must align with text baseline.\n\nNo vertical floating cursor.\n\nNo cursor rendered above/below underline.\n\n==================================================\n9. REMOVE ANIMATED OFFSET FROM INPUT\n==================================================\n\nDo not animate/translate the actual editable text field independently.\n\nSearch reveal may animate its container height.\n\nThe input/cursor itself must remain geometrically stable inside SearchBar.\n\nNo graphicsLayer translation on BasicTextField/TextField unless required\nand proven safe.\n\n==================================================\n10. IME OWNER\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nIME geometry owners = 1\n\nIME handling belongs to SearchReveal.\n\nAudit/remove global:\n\nimePadding()\nWindowInsets.ime padding\nnavigationBarsWithImePadding()\nbringIntoViewRequester\n\nfrom Home root or P1/P2/Dock parents.\n\n==================================================\n11. KEYBOARD OPEN BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nWhen keyboard opens:\n\nHome outer container:\nMUST NOT MOVE\n\nFav:\nMUST NOT MOVE\n\nP1:\nMUST NOT MOVE\n\nP2:\nMUST NOT MOVE\n\nDock:\nMUST NOT MOVE\n\nOnly the Search reveal's available particle/results height may reduce.\n\n==================================================\n12. SEARCHBAR WITH IME\n==================================================\n\nSearchBar remains pinned directly above P1.\n\nIt must not jump upward with keyboard.\n\nIt must not be covered by keyboard.\n\nIf available vertical space becomes smaller:\n\nshrink Particle/Results area first.\n\nDo NOT move P1/P2/Dock.\n\n==================================================\n13. PARTICLE AREA MINIMUM\n==================================================\n\nDefine:\n\nparticleAreaHeight =\navailableRevealHeight - fixed SearchBar/gaps\n\nClamp:\n\nmin = 0dp\n\nNever use negative layout height.\n\nWhen IME reduces available Search area:\nparticles may reduce/disappear temporarily,\nbut SearchBar position remains deterministic.\n\n==================================================\n14. FOCUS\n==================================================\n\nSingle focus owner.\n\nTap SearchBar:\nfocus input\nopen IME\n\nTap outside:\nuse existing intended dismissal behavior.\n\nNo duplicate FocusRequester.\n\n==================================================\n15. POINTER INPUT SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nParticle Canvas:\npointer input = NONE\n\nSearchBar:\nreceives touch directly\n\nHome gesture layer must not steal first tap inside Search input.\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n0\n\n==================================================\n16. DEBUG METRICS\n==================================================\n\nIn DEBUG only add compact diagnostics for:\n\nSearch reveal height\nParticle area height\nSearchBar Y\nSearchBar height\nP1 Y\nIME height\ncursor/input bounds\n\nDo not show in release.\n\n==================================================\n17. DEVICE FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nSEARCH / IME\n\n○ Keyboard opens\n○ Home stays fixed\n○ Fav stays fixed\n○ P1 stays fixed\n○ P2 stays fixed\n○ Dock stays fixed\n○ Cursor aligned\n○ SearchBar fixed above P1\n○ Top gap correct\n○ Bottom gap correct\n○ Background correct\n○ One underline\n○ Particle region resizes only\n\nUse:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n18. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew clean assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nRelease = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm SEARCH / IME GEOMETRY HOTFIX COMPLETE\n\nSearch geometry owners:\n<n>\n\nIME owners:\n<n>\n\nFocus owners:\n<n>\n\nSearchBar Y:\n<value>\n\nSearchBar height:\n<value>\n\nP1 Y:\n<value>\n\nTop gap:\n<dp>\n\nBottom gap:\n<dp>\n\nSearch background:\n<value>\n\nCursor alignment cause:\n<value>\n\nCursor aligned:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHome moves with IME:\n<NO/YES>\n\nFav moves:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP1 moves:\n<NO/YES>\n\nP2 moves:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDock moves:\n<NO/YES>\n\nParticle area adapts to IME:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFirst-touch blockers:\n<n>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSettings modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nSEARCH_IME_DEVICE_RETEST_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:438:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787411501,"text":"FASE — worm PRE-CLEAN-CODE ARCHIVE\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nMODE:\nARCHIVE ONLY\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nCreate a complete pre-clean-code archive of the current worm project\nbefore any refactor.\n\nDo NOT modify application behavior.\nDo NOT clean code yet.\nDo NOT approve patches.\n\n==================================================\n1. TIMESTAMP\n==================================================\n\nUse timezone:\n\nEurope/Rome\n\nTimestamp format:\n\nYYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS\n\n==================================================\n2. ARCHIVE DIRECTORY\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/archive/pre-clean-code/<timestamp>/\n\n==================================================\n3. COPY CURRENT STATE\n==================================================\n\nArchive:\n\nproject/\ndev/\ndocs/\nprojectctl if present\n\nAlso preserve:\n\ncurrent patch/status documentation\ncurrent feedback\ncurrent changelog\n\nExclude generated/cache directories:\n\nproject/.gradle\nproject/.kotlin\nproject/build\nproject/app/build\n\n==================================================\n4. PATCH STATE\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nPATCH-STATE.md\n\nRecord:\n\nPATCH 001 — Launcher Interaction\nSTATUS: NOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 002 — Search + Particle Reveal\nSTATUS: NOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 003 — Settings + Debug\nSTATUS: NOT_APPROVED\n\n==================================================\n5. BUILD STATE\n==================================================\n\nRecord current:\n\nDebug result\nRelease result\nR8 result\nDebug APK size\nRelease APK size\n\nDo not rebuild unless needed only to obtain current status.\n\n==================================================\n6. SOURCE HASH\n==================================================\n\nGenerate SHA-256 manifest for archived source/config files.\n\nCreate:\n\nSHA256SUMS\n\nVerify:\n\nsha256sum -c SHA256SUMS\n\n==================================================\n7. TAR ARCHIVE\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/archive/\nworm-pre-clean-code-<timestamp>.tar.gz\n\nDo not include:\n\nAPK\nAAB\nGradle caches\nprivate keys\nkeystores\ncredentials\n\n==================================================\n8. CLEAN CODE GATE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT begin clean-code patch until archive verification passes.\n\nRequired:\n\nArchive created = YES\nSHA = PASS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm PRE-CLEAN-CODE ARCHIVE COMPLETE\n\nArchive directory:\n<path>\n\nTar archive:\n<path>\n\nSHA-256:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nPATCH 001:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 002:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 003:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nApplication source modified:\nNO\n\nSTATUS:\nREADY_FOR_CLEAN_CODE"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:439:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787411696,"text":"FASE — worm FULL DEBUG ARCHIVE FOR REVIEW\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nMODE:\nAUDIT + EXPORT\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo NOT modify application behavior.\nDo NOT fix bugs during this phase.\nDo NOT approve patches.\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nCreate ONE complete debug archive for external code review.\n\nThe archive must contain enough source/configuration/audit information\nto review:\n\n- Core\n- HomeScreen\n- PATCH 001 Launcher Interaction\n- PATCH 002 Search + Particles\n- PATCH 003 Settings + Debug\n- Search geometry\n- IME behavior\n- particle animation\n- first-install/app population\n- Settings navigation\n- Debug feedback\n- build configuration\n- current known bugs\n\n==================================================\n1. EXPORT DIRECTORY\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/debug-export/\n\nTimestamp using:\n\nEurope/Rome\n\nFormat:\n\nYYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS\n\nCreate working directory:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/debug-export/<timestamp>/\n\n==================================================\n2. SOURCE TREE\n==================================================\n\nExport active source tree listing for:\n\nproject/app/src/main/java/com/worm\nproject/app/src/main/res\n\nAlso include:\n\nproject/settings.gradle.kts\nproject/build.gradle.kts\nproject/app/build.gradle.kts\nproject/gradle.properties\nproject/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml\n\nExclude:\n\n.gradle/\n.kotlin/\nbuild/\narchive/\nbackups/\n\nWrite:\n\nSOURCE-TREE.txt\n\n==================================================\n3. COMPLETE ACTIVE KOTLIN SOURCE\n==================================================\n\nCopy ALL active:\n\n*.kt\n\nunder:\n\nproject/app/src/main/java/com/worm/\n\ninto:\n\nsource/java/\n\nPreserve directory hierarchy.\n\nDo not include compiled classes.\n\n==================================================\n4. ANDROID RESOURCES\n==================================================\n\nCopy text-based active resources required for review:\n\nAndroidManifest.xml\n\nres/values/*.xml\nres/drawable/*.xml\nres/mipmap-anydpi*/*.xml\nres/xml/*.xml\n\nDo not include unnecessary binary/raster resources unless they are\nrequired to understand current UI.\n\nStore under:\n\nsource/android/\n\n==================================================\n5. GRADLE CONFIG\n==================================================\n\nCopy:\n\nsettings.gradle.kts\nbuild.gradle.kts\napp/build.gradle.kts\ngradle.properties\ngradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties\n\nDo NOT include:\n\ngradle-wrapper.jar\n\nStore under:\n\nsource/gradle/\n\n==================================================\n6. CORE REPORT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nCORE.md\n\nReport exact active files and owners for:\n\nMachinaCore/CoreHost\nHomeSnapshot\nAppCatalog\nLauncherPreferences\nLauncherActions\nAppVisuals\n\nReport duplicate owners.\n\n==================================================\n7. PATCH REPORT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nPATCHES.md\n\nReport all runtime-reachable patches.\n\nFor each:\n\nname\npath\nresponsibility\nruntime entry\nowner count\ncurrent status\n\nExpected logical patches:\n\nPATCH 001 — Launcher Interaction\nPATCH 002 — Search + Particle Reveal\nPATCH 003 — Settings + Debug\n\nApproval for all:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\n==================================================\n8. HOMESCREEN REPORT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nHOME.md\n\nReport:\n\nHomeScreen path\nline count\nFav owner\nSearch insertion\nP1 owner\nP2 owner\nDock owner\n\nReport which responsibilities remain directly inside HomeScreen.kt.\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH / IME REPORT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nSEARCH-IME.md\n\nReport exact current implementation:\n\nSearchReveal owners\nSearchBar owners\nquery owners\nfocus owners\nIME geometry owners\nSearchBar layout\nSearchBar Y ownership\ngap owners\nbackground owner\n\nAudit for:\n\nimePadding\nWindowInsets.ime\nnavigationBarsWithImePadding\nbringIntoViewRequester\ngraphicsLayer\noffset\ntranslation\nfocusRequester\n\nReport every matching active source location.\n\n==================================================\n10. PARTICLE REPORT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nPARTICLES.md\n\nReport:\n\nParticle engine owners\nCanvas owners\nframe-loop owners\nparticle count\nparticle state owner\nCanvas sizing\nX range\nY range\nconnection threshold\nrecomposition behavior\n\nReport exact layout hierarchy:\n\nFav\n→ particle/results area\n→ SearchBar\n→ P1\n\n==================================================\n11. SETTINGS REPORT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nSETTINGS.md\n\nReport:\n\nSettings root owner\nnavigation owner\npreference owner\nDebug owner\nfeedback store owner\n\nList actual implemented categories/subcategories.\n\nReport:\n\nglyph implementation\npalette\nswitch implementation\nBack handling\nswipe Back\nvertical scrolling\nDebug gating\n\nDo NOT report planned functionality as implemented.\n\n==================================================\n12. INITIALIZATION / APP POPULATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nINITIALIZATION.md\n\nTrace:\n\nAppCatalog\n→ HomeSnapshot\n→ LauncherPreferences\n→ P1\n→ P2\n→ Dock\n\nReport whether a fresh com.worm installation has an automatic\ninitialization path.\n\nReport:\n\ninitialization owners\nUsageStats usage\nfallback ranking\nP1 assignment\nP2 assignment\nDock assignment\npersistence\n\nThis is important because current device feedback reports no apps\nin P1/P2.\n\n==================================================\n13. OWNER REPORT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nOWNERS.md\n\nReport counts:\n\nCore hosts\nHomeSnapshot\nAppCatalog\nLauncherPreferences\nHomeScreen\nLauncherInteraction\nSearchReveal\nSearchBar\nquery\nfocus\nIME\nParticle engine\nParticle Canvas\nSettings root\nSettings navigation\nSettings preferences\nDebug feedback store\ninitialization\ngesture\nhaptic\n\n==================================================\n14. KNOWN DEVICE BUGS\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nDEVICE-BUGS.md\n\nRecord current reported bugs exactly:\n\n1. Debug/app crash observed during previous device testing\n2. Search/reveal/particle behavior defective\n3. Keyboard opening moves entire Home/container\n4. Search cursor/pointer position incorrect\n5. Search area gap/background rules incorrect\n6. P1/P2 empty on fresh installation\n7. No automatic initial arrangement on fresh installation\n8. Settings has various device bugs\n\nDo NOT mark fixed unless current device feedback explicitly confirms it.\n\n==================================================\n15. DEVICE FEEDBACK TEMPLATE\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nDEVICE-FEEDBACK.md\n\nUse:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\nSections:\n\nPATCH 001 — INTERACTION\n○ LEFT\n○ RIGHT\n○ UP\n○ DOWN\n○ Edge behavior\n○ Haptic\n○ First touch\n\nPATCH 002 — SEARCH\n○ SearchBar\n○ Cursor\n○ Underline\n○ Reveal\n○ Gaps\n○ Background\n○ IME\n○ P1 fixed\n○ P2 fixed\n○ Dock fixed\n\nPARTICLES\n○ Full width\n○ Full height\n○ Lines\n○ Animation\n○ Persistent state\n\nPATCH 003 — SETTINGS\n○ Gear\n○ Root\n○ Categories\n○ Subcategories\n○ Glyphs\n○ Black/white/yellow\n○ Switches\n○ Swipe Back\n○ Debug\n○ Feedback\n\nINITIALIZATION\n○ AppCatalog\n○ P1 population\n○ P2 population\n○ Dock population\n○ Persistence\n\nBUILD\n○ Debug\n○ Release\n○ R8\n○ Release <= 7 MB\n\n==================================================\n16. DEV DIRECTORY\n==================================================\n\nCopy current development handoff files if present:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/current/\n/opt/Android/worm/dev/changelog/CHANGELOG.md\n\nStore under:\n\ndev/\n\nDo NOT include entire history unless small.\n\nInstead create:\n\nDEV-HISTORY-LIST.txt\n\nlisting available historical versions.\n\n==================================================\n17. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nCapture complete output separately:\n\nBUILD-DEBUG.log\nBUILD-RELEASE.log\n\nDo not modify source to make build pass.\n\n==================================================\n18. APK INFO\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nAPK-INFO.txt\n\nInclude:\n\ndebug APK path\ndebug APK bytes\ndebug APK SHA-256\n\nrelease APK path\nrelease APK bytes\nrelease APK SHA-256\n\nrelease <= 7 MB:\nYES/NO\n\nDo NOT put APK binaries into archive.\n\n==================================================\n19. SUMMARY\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nSUMMARY.md\n\nInclude concise current state:\n\npackage\nversion\nruntime chain\nactive patches\nowner summary\nbuild results\nknown bugs\nfiles requiring review\npatch approval count\n\nPatch approval count:\n0\n\n==================================================\n20. SECURITY / EXCLUSIONS\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT include:\n\n*.apk\n*.aab\n*.jks\n*.keystore\nprivate keys\nSSH keys\ncredentials\ntokens\nenvironment dumps\nlocal.properties\nGradle caches\ncompiled classes\nbuild intermediates\n\nScan archive staging directory before packaging for obvious secrets.\n\n==================================================\n21. CREATE ARCHIVE\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n/opt/Android/worm/debug-export/\nworm-review-<timestamp>.tar.gz\n\nThe archive root should contain:\n\nSUMMARY.md\nCORE.md\nPATCHES.md\nHOME.md\nSEARCH-IME.md\nPARTICLES.md\nSETTINGS.md\nINITIALIZATION.md\nOWNERS.md\nDEVICE-BUGS.md\nDEVICE-FEEDBACK.md\nSOURCE-TREE.txt\nAPK-INFO.txt\nBUILD-DEBUG.log\nBUILD-RELEASE.log\nDEV-HISTORY-LIST.txt\nsource/\ndev/\n\n==================================================\n22. SHA\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nworm-review-<timestamp>.tar.gz.sha256\n\nVerify:\n\nsha256sum -c\n\nRequired:\nPASS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm REVIEW ARCHIVE COMPLETE\n\nArchive:\n<absolute path>\n\nArchive size:\n<value>\n\nSHA-256:\n<value>\n\nSHA verification:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nKotlin files included:\n<n>\n\nReports included:\n<n>\n\nActive patches:\n<n>\n\nApproved patches:\n0\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nREADY_FOR_UPLOAD"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:440:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787412232,"text":"FASE — worm SETTINGS EXIT / BACK HOTFIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nSCOPE:\nSETTINGS NAVIGATION ONLY\n\nCONFIRMED DEVICE BUG:\n\nCannot exit Settings.\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nFix Settings so the user can always return to Home.\n\nDo NOT modify:\n- Home geometry\n- Search\n- Particles\n- P1/P2\n- Dock\n- Core\n- initialization\n\n==================================================\n1. TRACE CURRENT SETTINGS STATE\n==================================================\n\nIdentify:\n\nSettings root visibility state\nSettings navigation stack\nBackHandler owner\nswipe-back owner\nHome overlay owner\ncloseSettings callback\n\nReport exact runtime path:\n\nFav gear\n→ Settings open\n→ Settings root\n→ subcategory\n→ Back/close\n\n==================================================\n2. SINGLE SETTINGS VISIBILITY OWNER\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nSettings visibility owner = 1\n\nUse one state such as:\n\nsettingsOpen = true/false\n\nor current equivalent.\n\nDo not maintain multiple overlay visibility flags.\n\n==================================================\n3. SYSTEM BACK\n==================================================\n\nRequired behavior:\n\nIf inside nested Settings page:\nBack\n→ previous Settings level\n\nIf at Settings root:\nBack\n→ close Settings\n→ return to Home\n\nNo Back lock.\n\nNo no-op at root.\n\n==================================================\n4. BACKHANDLER\n==================================================\n\nUse ONE BackHandler for Settings.\n\nConcept:\n\nif settingsStack has parent:\n    pop()\nelse:\n    closeSettings()\n\nExpected BackHandler owners:\n1\n\nRemove duplicate handlers if present.\n\n==================================================\n5. SWIPE BACK\n==================================================\n\nInside subcategory:\n\nleft-edge swipe RIGHT\n→ previous Settings level\n\nAt Settings root:\n\nleft-edge swipe RIGHT\n→ close Settings\n→ return Home\n\nUse same navigation owner as system Back.\n\nDo not create a second independent back stack.\n\n==================================================\n6. TOP BAR BACK\n==================================================\n\nIf Settings header has Back glyph:\n\ninside subcategory:\n→ previous level\n\nat root:\n→ close Settings\n\nUse same callback as system Back.\n\n==================================================\n7. HOME RESTORE\n==================================================\n\nWhen Settings closes:\n\nHome becomes visible immediately.\n\nDo NOT recreate Core.\n\nDo NOT reset HomeSnapshot.\n\nDo NOT reload P1/P2/Dock unnecessarily.\n\nSettings close is UI navigation only.\n\n==================================================\n8. STATE CLEANUP\n==================================================\n\nOn close:\n\nclear transient Settings navigation stack to root\n\nDo NOT clear production settings/preferences.\n\nNext Settings open:\nstart at Settings root.\n\n==================================================\n9. OVERLAY / TOUCH\n==================================================\n\nWhen Settings is closed:\n\nSettings overlay must be removed from composition or non-interactive.\n\nNo invisible layer may block Home first touch.\n\nExpected first-touch blockers after close:\n0\n\n==================================================\n10. DEBUG FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nAdd/update:\n\nSETTINGS NAVIGATION\n\n○ Open Settings\n○ Open subcategory\n○ System Back one level\n○ Swipe Back one level\n○ Top Back one level\n○ Root Back closes Settings\n○ Root swipe closes Settings\n○ Home visible after close\n○ Home first touch after close\n\n==================================================\n11. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nRelease = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm SETTINGS EXIT HOTFIX COMPLETE\n\nSettings visibility owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings navigation owners:\n<n>\n\nBackHandler owners:\n<n>\n\nSystem Back from subcategory:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSystem Back from root:\n<CLOSES_SETTINGS/FAIL>\n\nSwipe Back from subcategory:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nSwipe Back from root:\n<CLOSES_SETTINGS/FAIL>\n\nTop Back:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nHome restored:\n<YES/NO>\n\nFirst-touch blockers after close:\n<n>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHome modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nSETTINGS_EXIT_DEVICE_RETEST_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:441:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787412780,"text":"FASE — worm SEARCH FOCUS / AUTO-IME FIX\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nSCOPE:\nSEARCH FOCUS + KEYBOARD ONLY\n\nCONFIRMED TARGET\n\nWhen Search is revealed:\n\n- cursor must already be positioned inside the SearchBar\n- keyboard must open automatically\n- Dock must NOT move\n- P1 must NOT move\n- P2 must NOT move\n- Home must NOT deform\n- Search reveal geometry must remain stable\n\nDo NOT modify:\nCore\nSettings\nP1\nP2\nDock\nHome base geometry\nParticle layout unless required only for focus safety\n\n==================================================\n1. AUTO FOCUS ON REVEAL\n==================================================\n\nWhen reveal state becomes EXPANDED:\n\nautomatically focus the Search input.\n\nUse exactly one FocusRequester.\n\nConcept:\n\nif revealState == EXPANDED:\n    requestFocus()\n\nDo not create multiple focus owners.\n\n==================================================\n2. AUTO KEYBOARD\n==================================================\n\nAfter focus is granted:\n\nopen IME automatically.\n\nUse supported Compose/Android APIs.\n\nPreferred:\n\nLocalSoftwareKeyboardController\n\nRequired:\n\nUP reveal\n→ Search expands\n→ cursor appears in SearchBar\n→ keyboard opens automatically\n\nNo extra user tap required.\n\n==================================================\n3. CURSOR POSITION\n==================================================\n\nCursor must be placed at the Search input text position.\n\nFor empty query:\ncursor appears at normal text-start location after the magnifier.\n\nFor existing query:\ncursor goes to the end of the query unless current product behavior\nexplicitly requires restoring selection.\n\nNo cursor floating above/below field.\n\nNo cursor offset outside SearchBar.\n\n==================================================\n4. SEARCHBAR INPUT GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nUse stable input bounds.\n\nPreferred:\n\nBasicTextField or current input implementation with explicit:\n\n- height\n- verticalAlignment\n- content padding\n- baseline\n- cursor position\n\nDo NOT animate the editable text field independently.\n\nNo graphicsLayer/offset/translation on the text input.\n\n==================================================\n5. HOME MUST NOT MOVE\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL.\n\nWhen IME opens:\n\nHome outer container:\nUNCHANGED\n\nFav:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP1:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP2:\nUNCHANGED\n\nDock:\nUNCHANGED\n\nNo vertical translation.\n\nNo scaling.\n\nNo resizing.\n\nNo re-centering.\n\n==================================================\n6. P1 / P2 / DOCK HARD LOCK\n==================================================\n\nRequired while keyboard is visible:\n\nP1 bounds before IME == P1 bounds after IME\n\nP2 bounds before IME == P2 bounds after IME\n\nDock bounds before IME == Dock bounds after IME\n\nAllow tolerance only for sub-pixel rounding.\n\nNo dp geometry change.\n\n==================================================\n7. NO GLOBAL IME RESIZE\n==================================================\n\nAudit and remove/avoid any root-level:\n\nimePadding()\nWindowInsets.ime\nnavigationBarsWithImePadding()\nadjustResize-driven layout behavior\nbringIntoViewRequester on Home\nglobal vertical offset\n\nThe entire Home must not react geometrically to the IME.\n\n==================================================\n8. WINDOW IME MODE\n==================================================\n\nChoose Activity/window configuration that prevents the keyboard\nfrom resizing or panning the entire launcher Home.\n\nAudit current soft-input mode.\n\nUse the safest public Android behavior that keeps Home fixed.\n\nDo NOT solve this by moving P1/P2/Dock manually.\n\n==================================================\n9. SEARCH REVEAL WITH IME\n==================================================\n\nSearch reveal stays in its expanded geometry.\n\nDo NOT collapse or compress the Home because IME appears.\n\nSearchBar stays in its defined expanded position.\n\nIf keyboard overlaps lower content at system level, do not compensate\nby shifting Home.\n\nThe requested contract is fixed launcher geometry.\n\n==================================================\n10. NO DEFORMATION\n==================================================\n\nOpening keyboard must not trigger:\n\nMaterial Stretch\nscaleX\nscaleY\ntranslationX\ntranslationY\nanimated height change\nspring/bounce\n\nIME and gesture animation states must be independent.\n\n==================================================\n11. REVEAL / FOCUS ORDER\n==================================================\n\nRequired order:\n\n1. UP accepted\n2. reveal settles EXPANDED\n3. Search input becomes focused\n4. cursor becomes visible\n5. IME opens\n\nAvoid racing focus before SearchBar has valid layout bounds.\n\nIf required, request focus after the expanded SearchBar is composed\nand positioned.\n\n==================================================\n12. SINGLE FOCUS OWNER\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nFocusRequester owners = 1\nfocus state owners = 1\nkeyboard controller owners = 1\n\nNo duplicate LaunchedEffect requesting focus.\n\n==================================================\n13. KEYBOARD CLOSE\n==================================================\n\nWhen keyboard closes:\n\nHome geometry remains identical.\n\nSearch may remain EXPANDED according to current interaction contract.\n\nDo NOT automatically collapse Search merely because IME closed.\n\n==================================================\n14. DOWN COLLAPSE\n==================================================\n\nIf user performs accepted DOWN collapse:\n\nclear Search focus\nhide keyboard\ncollapse Search\n\nOrder should avoid layout jump.\n\nP1/P2/Dock remain fixed throughout.\n\n==================================================\n15. PARTICLES\n==================================================\n\nParticle animation must not control focus or IME.\n\nParticles continue according to current expanded-state behavior.\n\nNo layout deformation due to keyboard.\n\n==================================================\n16. DEBUG METRICS\n==================================================\n\nDEV-only report:\n\nReveal state\nSearch input focused\nCursor visible\nKeyboard visible\n\nP1 bounds before/after IME\nP2 bounds before/after IME\nDock bounds before/after IME\nHome bounds before/after IME\n\nExpected deltas:\n0dp\n\n==================================================\n17. DEVICE FEEDBACK\n==================================================\n\nSEARCH AUTO-IME\n\n○ UP expands Search\n○ Cursor appears automatically\n○ Cursor inside SearchBar\n○ Keyboard opens automatically\n○ No extra tap required\n○ Home does not move\n○ Fav does not move\n○ P1 does not move\n○ P2 does not move\n○ Dock does not move\n○ No deformation\n○ Closing keyboard does not move Home\n○ DOWN hides keyboard cleanly\n\nStates:\n\n✓ OK\n! BUG\n~ RETEST\n○ NOT TESTED\n\n==================================================\n18. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew clean assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nRelease = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm SEARCH AUTO-IME FIX COMPLETE\n\nFocusRequester owners:\n<n>\n\nFocus state owners:\n<n>\n\nKeyboard controller owners:\n<n>\n\nAuto focus on expanded:\n<YES/NO>\n\nAuto keyboard:\n<YES/NO>\n\nCursor inside SearchBar:\n<YES/NO>\n\nHome delta with IME:\n<dp>\n\nFav delta with IME:\n<dp>\n\nP1 delta with IME:\n<dp>\n\nP2 delta with IME:\n<dp>\n\nDock delta with IME:\n<dp>\n\nMaterial deformation on IME:\n<NO/YES>\n\nGlobal IME layout resize:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSettings modified:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nSEARCH_AUTO_IME_DEVICE_RETEST_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:442:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787413606,"text":"FASE — worm CLEAN-CODE\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nMODE:\nREFACTOR ONLY\n\nCURRENT VERIFIED OWNERS:\n\nHomeScreen owners: 1\nSearchReveal owners: 1\nSearchBar owners: 1\nIME owners: 1\nParticle engine owners: 1\nSettings root owners: 1\nSettings navigation owners: 1\nCore owners: 1\n\nPATCH STATUS:\n\nPATCH 001 — Launcher Interaction\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 002 — Search + Particle Reveal\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 003 — Settings + Debug\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nClean and reduce the current codebase without changing runtime behavior.\n\nDo NOT add features.\nDo NOT redesign UI.\nDo NOT change Home geometry.\nDo NOT change Core behavior.\nDo NOT approve patches.\n\n==================================================\n1. HARD BEHAVIOR LOCK\n==================================================\n\nThe following behavior must remain unchanged:\n\n- Home visual geometry\n- Fav geometry\n- P1 geometry\n- P2 geometry\n- Dock geometry\n- launcher interaction\n- Search reveal behavior\n- SearchBar behavior\n- particle behavior\n- Settings behavior\n- Debug behavior\n- initialization behavior\n\nThis phase is source organization only.\n\n==================================================\n2. CORE LOCK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT refactor stable Core unless required for import cleanup.\n\nKeep existing:\n\nMachinaCore\nHomeSnapshot\nAppCatalog\nLauncherPreferences\nLauncherActions\nAppVisuals\n\nNo new Core abstraction.\n\nNo new repository.\n\nNo duplicate state owner.\n\n==================================================\n3. ONE HOMESCREEN\n==================================================\n\nKeep exactly one runtime:\n\nui/home/HomeScreen.kt\n\nHomeScreen remains the only Home composition owner.\n\nDo not create:\n\nHomeV2\nHomeV3\nWormHome\nBetaHome\nHomePatch\n\n==================================================\n4. HOMESCREEN REDUCTION\n==================================================\n\nHomeScreen.kt should contain only Home-level orchestration and layout.\n\nKeep:\n\n- Home outer layout\n- Fav integration\n- P1 integration\n- P2 integration\n- Dock integration\n- SearchReveal insertion\n- Settings entry\n- callbacks to Core/patches\n\nMove implementation details out.\n\n==================================================\n5. HOME COMPONENT EXTRACTION\n==================================================\n\nIf currently embedded in HomeScreen.kt, extract reusable presentation\ncomponents into:\n\nui/home/FavoritesHeader.kt\nui/home/AppSection.kt\nui/home/Dock.kt\nui/home/HomeLayout.kt\n\nOnly extract when it reduces responsibility cleanly.\n\nDo not change modifiers or geometry values while moving code.\n\n==================================================\n6. PATCH 001\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\npatches/launcher_interaction/LauncherInteractionPatch.kt\n\nBehavior must remain identical.\n\nDo not rename or rewrite it just for aesthetics.\n\nRemove only:\n\nunused imports\ndead helpers\nobvious duplicate constants\n\n==================================================\n7. PATCH 002 STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nTarget:\n\npatches/search_reveal/\n  SearchRevealPatch.kt\n  SearchRevealState.kt\n  SearchBar.kt\n  ParticleNetwork.kt\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nSearchRevealPatch.kt\n- orchestration only\n\nSearchRevealState.kt\n- reveal/focus/query transient state only\n\nSearchBar.kt\n- input UI only\n\nParticleNetwork.kt\n- particle model/animation/drawing only\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH OWNER LOCK\n==================================================\n\nRequired after clean-code:\n\nSearchReveal owners = 1\nSearchBar owners = 1\nQuery owners = 1\nFocus owners = 1\nIME owners = 1\n\nNo behavior changes.\n\n==================================================\n9. PARTICLE OWNER LOCK\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nParticle engine owners = 1\nCanvas owners = 1\nframe-loop owners = 1\n\nDo not split particle animation into multiple helpers that create new\nstate owners.\n\nPure math/drawing helpers are allowed.\n\n==================================================\n10. PATCH 003 STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nTarget:\n\npatches/settings/\n  SettingsPatch.kt\n  SettingsScreen.kt\n  SettingsNavigation.kt\n  SettingsComponents.kt\n  SettingsSections.kt\n  DebugScreen.kt\n\nDo not keep one ~900-line Settings file if responsibilities can be\nseparated safely.\n\n==================================================\n11. SETTINGS ROOT\n==================================================\n\nSettingsScreen.kt should own:\n\n- Settings root shell\n- current category/page\n- navigation connection\n\nMove row/category implementations to SettingsComponents.kt.\n\nMove individual category content to SettingsSections.kt or small files.\n\n==================================================\n12. SETTINGS NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nSettingsNavigation.kt owns:\n\n- current page\n- back stack\n- pop/close behavior\n\nExpected navigation owners:\n1\n\nDo not create multiple BackHandler owners.\n\n==================================================\n13. DEBUG\n==================================================\n\nDebugScreen.kt owns only DEV UI:\n\n- owner counters\n- validation state\n- feedback editor\n- copy/reset actions\n\nDebugFeedbackStore stays separate.\n\nRelease behavior:\nunchanged.\n\n==================================================\n14. PRODUCTION SETTINGS STORAGE\n==================================================\n\nKeep one production settings persistence owner.\n\nDo not combine DebugFeedbackStore with production settings storage.\n\nRequired:\n\nSettings preference owners = 1\nDebug feedback stores = 1\n\n==================================================\n15. IMPORT CLEANUP\n==================================================\n\nRemove all proven unused imports.\n\nDo not use wildcard imports unless project already consistently does so.\n\n==================================================\n16. DEAD CODE\n==================================================\n\nFind and remove only proven unreachable/dead code:\n\n- unused composables\n- duplicate Search helpers\n- duplicate particle helpers\n- obsolete Settings components\n- stale old package aliases\n- unused constants\n- unreachable debug paths\n- old temporary instrumentation\n\nDo NOT remove archive/history/docs.\n\n==================================================\n17. CONSTANT CONSOLIDATION\n==================================================\n\nAudit repeated layout/style constants.\n\nReuse existing design tokens when semantically identical.\n\nDo NOT move every number into a token file.\n\nOnly consolidate genuine duplicates.\n\n==================================================\n18. STATE CLEANUP\n==================================================\n\nRemove duplicated derived state where possible.\n\nPrefer:\n\nsingle source state\n+\nderived values\n\nAvoid parallel booleans representing the same condition.\n\nDo NOT change persistence semantics.\n\n==================================================\n19. COMPOSABLE SIZE\n==================================================\n\nSplit composables when they own multiple independent responsibilities.\n\nDo not create dozens of tiny one-line wrapper composables.\n\nGoal:\nreadability, not file-count inflation.\n\n==================================================\n20. NAMING\n==================================================\n\nKeep stable internal class names where rename adds risk.\n\nPackage remains:\n\ncom.worm\n\nApp remains:\n\nworm\n\nNo broad Machina→Worm internal rename in this patch.\n\n==================================================\n21. COMMENTS\n==================================================\n\nRemove stale comments that describe old behavior.\n\nKeep comments only when they explain:\n\n- non-obvious state ownership\n- gesture arbitration\n- IME/window behavior\n- lifecycle constraints\n\nDo not add obvious comments for every line.\n\n==================================================\n22. LOGGING\n==================================================\n\nRemove obsolete temporary debug logging.\n\nKeep only necessary DEBUG diagnostics.\n\nNo verbose frame-by-frame logs.\n\n==================================================\n23. NO NEW DEPENDENCIES\n==================================================\n\nDo not add libraries.\n\nDo not add architecture frameworks.\n\nUse current Kotlin/Compose stack.\n\n==================================================\n24. SOURCE METRICS BEFORE\n==================================================\n\nBefore edits report:\n\nKotlin files:\n<n>\n\nTotal Kotlin lines:\n<n>\n\nHomeScreen.kt lines:\n<n>\n\nSettingsScreen.kt lines:\n<n>\n\nSearch patch lines:\n<n>\n\nParticleNetwork lines:\n<n>\n\n==================================================\n25. SOURCE METRICS AFTER\n==================================================\n\nAfter edits report same metrics.\n\nDo not force total line count lower if extraction improves clarity.\n\nPrimary target:\nlower complexity / smaller multipurpose files.\n\n==================================================\n26. OWNER AUDIT AFTER\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nCoreHost = 1\nHomeSnapshot = 1\nAppCatalog = 1\nLauncherPreferences = 1\n\nHomeScreen = 1\nLauncherInteraction = 1\n\nSearchReveal = 1\nSearchBar = 1\nQuery = 1\nFocus = 1\nIME = 1\n\nParticle engine = 1\nParticle Canvas = 1\nFrame loop = 1\n\nSettings root = 1\nSettings navigation = 1\nSettings preferences = 1\nDebug feedback store = 1\n\n==================================================\n27. DIFF SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nReview final diff and classify every changed file as:\n\nMOVE_ONLY\nEXTRACTION_ONLY\nIMPORT_CLEANUP\nDEAD_CODE_REMOVAL\nMINIMAL_GLUE_CHANGE\n\nIf a changed file contains behavioral modification:\nSTOP and report it.\n\n==================================================\n28. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew clean assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nRelease = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n29. SIZE\n==================================================\n\nReport:\n\nDebug APK size\nRelease APK size\n\nRelease target:\n<= 7 MB\n\nNo size regression from new dependencies.\n\n==================================================\n30. PATCH APPROVAL\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT approve anything.\n\nAfter clean-code:\n\nPATCH 001:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 002:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\nPATCH 003:\nNOT_APPROVED\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm CLEAN-CODE COMPLETE\n\nKotlin files before:\n<n>\n\nKotlin files after:\n<n>\n\nTotal Kotlin lines before:\n<n>\n\nTotal Kotlin lines after:\n<n>\n\nHomeScreen lines before:\n<n>\n\nHomeScreen lines after:\n<n>\n\nSettingsScreen lines before:\n<n>\n\nSettingsScreen lines after:\n<n>\n\nDead code removed:\n<n files / n lines>\n\nUnused imports removed:\n<n>\n\nActive patch count:\n<n>\n\nExpected:\n3\n\nCore owners:\n<summary>\n\nHomeScreen owners:\n<n>\n\nSearchReveal owners:\n<n>\n\nSearchBar owners:\n<n>\n\nIME owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nSettings root owners:\n<n>\n\nSettings navigation owners:\n<n>\n\nBehavioral changes detected:\n<NO/YES>\n\nCore behavior changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nHome geometry changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSearch behavior changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nSettings behavior changed:\n<NO/YES>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease APK size:\n<value>\n\nApproved patches:\n0\n\nSTATUS:\nCLEAN_CODE_DEVICE_RETEST_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:443:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787414986,"text":"FASE — worm ANDROID 16/17 SEARCH PANEL + IME PATCH\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nTARGET PLATFORM:\nAndroid 16 / API 36\nAndroid 17 / API 37\n\nSCOPE:\nSEARCH PANEL\nSEARCH INPUT\nPARTICLE NETWORK\nIME / KEYBOARD\n\nDO NOT MODIFY:\n\nCore\nFav\nP1\nP2\nDock\nSettings\nLauncherInteractionPatch\ninitial app arrangement\ncollapsed Home geometry\n\n==================================================\nREFERENCE PLATFORM RULES\n==================================================\n\nAndroid 16:\n\n- edge-to-edge is enforced for targetSdk 36\n- do NOT attempt to opt out of edge-to-edge\n- use WindowInsets APIs correctly\n- windowSoftInputMode=adjustResize is retained so IME insets are\n  available to Compose\n- DO NOT apply IME padding to the launcher Home\n\nAndroid 17:\n\n- preserve explicit focus/IME control\n- do not depend on implicit IME visibility restoration\n\n==================================================\n1. MANIFEST\n==================================================\n\nVerify MainActivity uses:\n\nandroid:windowSoftInputMode=\"adjustResize\"\n\nDo NOT use:\n\nadjustPan\n\nDo NOT use deprecated programmatic SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE calls.\n\nDo NOT attempt to disable Android 16 edge-to-edge.\n\n==================================================\n2. MAINACTIVITY\n==================================================\n\nUse normal edge-to-edge setup.\n\nPreferred:\n\nenableEdgeToEdge()\n\nDo not add IME padding to the Activity/root Home.\n\nDo not perform manual translation when keyboard opens.\n\nDo not resize Home based on IME height.\n\n==================================================\n3. HOME MUST IGNORE IME FOR GEOMETRY\n==================================================\n\nHomeScreen geometry must use stable display/window constraints.\n\nDO NOT use:\n\nModifier.imePadding()\n\nModifier.windowInsetsPadding(WindowInsets.ime)\n\nWindowInsets.ime.asPaddingValues()\n\nwindowInsetsBottomHeight(WindowInsets.ime)\n\non:\n\nHomeScreen\nHome outer container\nFav\nP1/P2 parent\nDock parent\n\n==================================================\n4. MATERIAL / SCAFFOLD INSETS\n==================================================\n\nAudit Scaffold and Material 3 components.\n\nIf Home uses Scaffold:\n\nensure the launcher content is NOT receiving automatic IME/content\npadding indirectly.\n\nFor the launcher shell use explicit content insets as appropriate,\nfor example empty content insets where the shell itself must remain\nedge-to-edge/fixed.\n\nDo NOT stack:\n\nScaffold padding\n+\nsafeDrawingPadding\n+\nimePadding\n\non the same Home hierarchy.\n\n==================================================\n5. SYSTEM BAR INSETS\n==================================================\n\nStatus/navigation bar handling and IME handling must remain separate.\n\nHome may respect:\n\nstatusBars\nnavigationBars\ndisplayCutout\n\naccording to current baseline.\n\nIt must NOT treat IME as a Home layout inset.\n\n==================================================\n6. NEW SEARCH REVEAL PANEL\n==================================================\n\nReplace the current visually undefined Search reveal area with ONE\ndedicated panel.\n\nStructure:\n\nFav\n\n<fixed gap>\n\nSearchRevealPanel\n\n<fixed gap>\n\nP1\nP2\n\n==================================================\n7. SEARCH PANEL SHAPE\n==================================================\n\nSearchRevealPanel must be approximately square.\n\nTarget:\n\naspectRatio(1f)\n\nBUT:\n\ndo not exceed the existing available reveal space.\n\nUse a constrained square:\n\nwidth determined by Home internal width\nheight normally = width\n\nIf current device height requires a slightly shorter panel to avoid\nchanging P1/P2/Dock baseline geometry, clamp height rather than move\nP1/P2/Dock.\n\nHome geometry wins.\n\n==================================================\n8. SEARCH PANEL STYLE\n==================================================\n\nBackground:\n\nvery near black\n\nStarting token:\n\nColor(0xFF0A0A0A)\n\nor adjust slightly to match existing Home surfaces.\n\nPanel must remain visually distinct from Home outer background.\n\nCorner radius:\n\nuse same visual family as existing panels.\n\nSuggested:\n20–24dp\n\nNo strong elevation.\nNo bright border.\n\nOptional subtle outline only if consistent with Home.\n\n==================================================\n9. PANEL OUTER GAPS\n==================================================\n\nDefine ONE spacing owner.\n\nStarting tokens:\n\nFav → SearchPanel:\n12dp\n\nSearchPanel → P1:\n12dp\n\nHorizontal inset inside Home:\nsame as existing P1/Fav internal alignment\n\nDo not combine Spacer + parent padding for the same gap.\n\n==================================================\n10. PANEL INTERNAL STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\nSearchRevealPanel:\n\nBox/Column\nwith internal padding:\n\n12–16dp\n\nRequired order INSIDE PANEL:\n\nParticleNetwork region\n↓\n8–12dp gap\n↓\nSearchBar\n\nSearchBar is INSIDE the square panel at its bottom.\n\n==================================================\n11. PARTICLE REGION\n==================================================\n\nParticleNetwork occupies all panel space above SearchBar.\n\nConcept:\n\nColumn(\n    Modifier\n        .fillMaxSize()\n        .padding(16.dp)\n) {\n\n    Box(\n        Modifier\n            .fillMaxWidth()\n            .weight(1f)\n    ) {\n        ParticleNetwork(\n            Modifier.fillMaxSize()\n        )\n    }\n\n    Spacer(Modifier.height(8.dp))\n\n    SearchBar(...)\n}\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nweight allowed only inside SearchRevealPanel.\n\nNever apply this weight to Home/P1/P2/Dock.\n\n==================================================\n12. PARTICLES\n==================================================\n\nKeep:\n\nparticle engine owners = 1\nCanvas owners = 1\nframe loops = 1\n\nParticles must cover:\n\nfull particle Box width\nfull particle Box height\n\nX range:\n0..canvasWidth\n\nY range:\n0..canvasHeight\n\nDo not compress to a horizontal strip.\n\n==================================================\n13. PARTICLE BACKGROUND\n==================================================\n\nParticle Canvas itself should remain transparent.\n\nThe near-black color belongs to SearchRevealPanel.\n\nDo not give ParticleNetwork a second competing background.\n\n==================================================\n14. SEARCHBAR STYLE\n==================================================\n\nSearchBar sits INSIDE the panel bottom.\n\nRequired:\n\nmagnifier left\neditable query\ncursor\none underline\n\nNo pill.\nNo filled Search field.\nNo rounded SearchBar card.\n\nSearch panel is the enclosing surface.\n\n==================================================\n15. SEARCHBAR INTERNAL GAP\n==================================================\n\nSearchBar must NOT touch panel edges.\n\nPanel internal horizontal padding:\n16dp target\n\nBottom inset:\n12–16dp\n\nParticle → Search:\n8–12dp\n\n==================================================\n16. SEARCH INPUT\n==================================================\n\nUse ONE BasicTextField if current TextField introduces internal\ncursor/baseline problems.\n\nExpected:\n\neditable inputs = 1\n\nFocusRequesters = 1\n\nKeyboardControllers = 1\n\n==================================================\n17. CURSOR\n==================================================\n\nWhen expanded:\n\nrequest Search focus once AFTER SearchBar is actually placed.\n\nEmpty query:\ncursor starts at text-start immediately after magnifier.\n\nExisting query:\ncursor at query end unless existing selection state says otherwise.\n\nNo manual cursor offset.\n\nNo graphicsLayer on BasicTextField.\n\n==================================================\n18. AUTO KEYBOARD\n==================================================\n\nRequired interaction:\n\nUP accepted\n→ Search panel becomes expanded\n→ SearchBar completes layout\n→ requestFocus()\n→ cursor visible\n→ keyboard show()\n\nNo user tap required.\n\nDo not request focus repeatedly on every recomposition.\n\n==================================================\n19. ANDROID 17 IME VISIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nDo not rely on system restoration of previous IME state.\n\nSearch reveal explicitly owns the desired focus/keyboard request.\n\nAfter configuration recreation:\n\nonly reopen IME when Search state contract actually requires it.\n\n==================================================\n20. IME STATE IS NOT LAYOUT STATE\n==================================================\n\nKeep independent:\n\nrevealState\nfocusState\nimeVisible\n\nDo not define expanded panel height as:\n\navailableHeight - imeHeight\n\nDo not change SearchPanel dimensions because IME opens.\n\n==================================================\n21. KEYBOARD OVERLAY CONTRACT\n==================================================\n\nWhen keyboard opens:\n\nHome bounds:\nUNCHANGED\n\nFav:\nUNCHANGED\n\nSearchRevealPanel:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP1:\nUNCHANGED\n\nP2:\nUNCHANGED\n\nDock:\nUNCHANGED\n\nThe keyboard may visually overlay the lower portion of the launcher.\n\nThat is intentional for worm.\n\nDo NOT shift launcher content upward to expose Dock.\n\n==================================================\n22. NO IME GAP ON HOME\n==================================================\n\nDo not apply:\n\nimePadding()\nfitInside(IME)\n\nto the entire Home.\n\nNOTE:\n\nAndroid documentation normally recommends fitting interactive\ncontent to IME.\n\nworm deliberately keeps launcher geometry fixed, so IME adaptation\nis localized to Search input behavior rather than Home layout.\n\n==================================================\n23. SEARCH PANEL + KEYBOARD\n==================================================\n\nKeyboard opening must NOT:\n\nresize square\nchange panel aspect ratio\nreduce particles\nmove SearchBar\nmove Fav\nmove P1/P2\nmove Dock\n\nParticle animation continues behind/above keyboard normally.\n\n==================================================\n24. DOWN COLLAPSE\n==================================================\n\nDOWN accepted:\n\nkeyboardController.hide()\nfocusManager.clearFocus()\nSearch state → COLLAPSED\n\nThen return to existing collapsed Home.\n\nNo intermediate geometry deformation.\n\n==================================================\n25. SETTINGS / BACK\n==================================================\n\nDo not touch Settings in this patch.\n\n==================================================\n26. DEBUG METRICS\n==================================================\n\nDEBUG only record before and after IME:\n\nHome bounds\nSearchPanel bounds\nSearchBar bounds\nP1 bounds\nP2 bounds\nDock bounds\n\nAlso:\n\nfocus state\nIME visible\nparticle frame loop active\n\nExpected bounds deltas with IME:\n\nHome = 0\nSearchPanel = 0\nP1 = 0\nP2 = 0\nDock = 0\n\n==================================================\n27. OWNER AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nRequired:\n\nSearchReveal owners = 1\nSearch geometry owners = 1\nSearchBar owners = 1\neditable inputs = 1\nFocusRequester owners = 1\nKeyboardController owners = 1\nIME layout owners on Home = 0\nParticle engines = 1\nCanvas owners = 1\nframe loops = 1\n\n==================================================\n28. BUILD\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\n./gradlew clean assembleDebug\n./gradlew assembleRelease\n\nRequired:\n\nDebug = SUCCESS\nRelease = SUCCESS\nR8 = SUCCESS\n\n==================================================\n29. DEVICE TEST\n==================================================\n\nSEARCH PANEL\n\n○ square/near-square panel\n○ near-black background\n○ outer gap from Fav\n○ outer gap from P1\n○ internal padding\n○ particles full panel\n○ SearchBar at bottom\n○ SearchBar one underline\n\nIME\n\n○ UP expands\n○ cursor visible\n○ keyboard automatic\n○ Home does not move\n○ panel does not move\n○ P1 does not move\n○ P2 does not move\n○ Dock does not move\n○ particles continue\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nworm ANDROID 16/17 SEARCH + IME PATCH COMPLETE\n\ntargetSdk:\n<value>\n\nEdge-to-edge:\n<value>\n\nwindowSoftInputMode:\n<value>\n\nHome IME padding owners:\n<n>\n\nSearch panel aspect:\n<value>\n\nSearch panel background:\n<value>\n\nFav→panel gap:\n<dp>\n\nPanel→P1 gap:\n<dp>\n\nPanel internal padding:\n<dp>\n\nParticle→Search gap:\n<dp>\n\nSearchReveal owners:\n<n>\n\nSearchBar owners:\n<n>\n\nFocusRequester owners:\n<n>\n\nKeyboardController owners:\n<n>\n\nParticle engines:\n<n>\n\nHome delta IME:\n<value>\n\nSearchPanel delta IME:\n<value>\n\nP1 delta IME:\n<value>\n\nP2 delta IME:\n<value>\n\nDock delta IME:\n<value>\n\nDebug:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nRelease:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nR8:\n<SUCCESS/FAILED>\n\nSTATUS:\nANDROID_16_17_DEVICE_RETEST_REQUIRED"}
/root/.codex/history.jsonl:444:{"session_id":"01a028ac-a922-71c0-a1e8-5a6a45b32a97","ts":1787416042,"text":"FASE — worm PATCH 001 / LAUNCHER INTERACTION\n\nROOT:\n/opt/Android/worm\n\nPROJECT:\n/opt/Android/worm/project\n\nPACKAGE:\ncom.worm\n\nTARGET:\nAndroid 16 / API 36\nAndroid 17 / API 37\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nConsolidate launcher gesture handling without changing Home geometry.\n\nRequired:\n\n- exactly 1 launcher gesture owner\n- UP / DOWN handled by worm\n- LEFT / RIGHT worm stretch does NOT perform Back navigation\n- Settings uses supported Back APIs\n- no KEYCODE_BACK interception\n- no Activity.onBackPressed override\n- no duplicate BackHandler\n\nANDROID 16 RULE\n\nPredictive Back is enabled by default for targetSdk 36.\n\nDo not globally intercept Back at MainActivity root unless required,\nbecause root interception disables normal back-to-home system animation.\n\nSETTINGS\n\nInside Settings:\nBackHandler or PredictiveBackHandler may navigate one level back.\n\nAt Settings root:\nBack closes Settings.\n\nHome itself:\ndo not intercept normal system Back unless launcher UX explicitly needs it.\n\nWORM HORIZONTAL GESTURES\n\nLEFT / RIGHT:\nworm visual interaction only.\n\nDo not turn horizontal launcher swipe into Android Back.\n\nDo not draw custom back chevrons/arrows.\n\nGESTURE ARBITRATION\n\nUse touchSlop.\n\nHorizontal:\nabs(dx) > touchSlop && abs(dx) > abs(dy)\n\nVertical:\nabs(dy) > touchSlop && abs(dy) > abs(dx)\n\nOnce locked:\ndo not switch axis until pointer sequence ends.\n\nOWNER REQUIREMENTS\n\nLauncher gesture owners = 1\nSettings back owners = 1\nRoot Back interception owners = 0 preferred\n\nBUILD:\nDebug SUCCESS\nRelease SUCCESS\nR8 SUCCESS\n\nSTATUS:\nDEVICE_RETEST_REQUIRED"}
